translate chinese strings:

    old "Tomorrow night, the city will defend itself and fight for survival. But tonight, things are quiet and peaceful."
    new "Tomorrow night, the city will defend itself and fight for survival. But tonight, things are quiet and peaceful.\n明晚，这座城市将自我保卫、为生存而战。但今晚，一切宁静而平和。"

    old "I walk until I reach the town's outskirts. I pass several of the cities workshops, located here on the edge of town, downwind of the rest of the city to prevent their chimneys from showering the rest of the city in soot."
    new "I walk until I reach the town's outskirts. I pass several of the cities workshops, located here on the edge of town, downwind of the rest of the city to prevent their chimneys from showering the rest of the city in soot.\n我一直走到镇子外围。我经过几座城里的工坊，它们就设在镇子边缘，位于整座城市的下风处，免得烟囱把煤灰撒到城里其他地方。"

    old "Any other time of day, I'd expect to hear the clanging of hammers on anvils, but right now, I hear only the sound of the wind as it sweeps through the desolate workshop district."
    new "Any other time of day, I'd expect to hear the clanging of hammers on anvils, but right now, I hear only the sound of the wind as it sweeps through the desolate workshop district.\n换作一天中的其他任何时候，我本该听到铁锤敲打铁砧的叮当声，可此刻，我只听到风扫过这片荒凉工坊区的声音。"

    old "At the edge of town, I pause for a moment. Nobody should be out here, and I've heard no footsteps or any other sign that some other person might be here at the edge of town. And yet I feel the growing sensation that I'm being watched."
    new "At the edge of town, I pause for a moment. Nobody should be out here, and I've heard no footsteps or any other sign that some other person might be here at the edge of town. And yet I feel the growing sensation that I'm being watched.\n在镇子边缘，我停下片刻。这里本不该有人，我既没听到脚步声，也没察觉任何其他人可能来到镇边的迹象。然而我却越来越强烈地感到，有人在注视着我。"

    old "I look behind me."
    new "I look behind me.\n我回头看去。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. I suppose I should know by now that it's impossible to sneak up on you."
    new "Ah, [protag]. I suppose I should know by now that it's impossible to sneak up on you.\n啊，[protag]。我想我早该知道，想悄悄靠近你是不可能的。"

    old "Impossible!"
    new "Impossible!\n不可能！"

    old "And what purpose might you have for sneaking up on me?"
    new "And what purpose might you have for sneaking up on me?\n那你悄悄靠近我，又有什么目的？"

    old "For sneaking up on you? Simply to test your abilities. You seem to have some kind of uncanny sixth sense."
    new "For sneaking up on you? Simply to test your abilities. You seem to have some kind of uncanny sixth sense.\n悄悄靠近你？只是想试试你的本事。你似乎有种超乎寻常的第六感。"

    old "A truly uncanny sixth sense."
    new "A truly uncanny sixth sense.\n一种真正不可思议的第六感。"

    old "I merely wanted to talk."
    new "I merely wanted to talk.\n我不过是想和你谈谈。"

    old "Just to talk?"
    new "Just to talk?\n只是想谈谈？"

    old "I wouldn't say it's 'just' to talk. We have so much to talk about."
    new "I wouldn't say it's 'just' to talk. We have so much to talk about.\n我可不会说这只是谈谈。我们可谈的事情多得很。"

    old "And so little time to do it!"
    new "And so little time to do it!\n而留给我们的时间却又这么少！"

    old "Indeed. The invasion looms on the horizon. Do you suppose that Grimoire is ready?"
    new "Indeed. The invasion looms on the horizon. Do you suppose that Grimoire is ready?\n的确。入侵已近在眼前。你觉得 Grimoire 准备好了吗？"

    old "Yes, they are. I'm sure of it."
    new "Yes, they are. I'm sure of it.\n是的，他们准备好了。我确信。"

    old "My, my, such confidence. I've always appraised you to be a person confident in their own abilities. But a city's ability to defend itself goes far beyond the capabilities of a single person. I must wonder how it is that you're able to be so confident about the abilities of others."
    new "My, my, such confidence. I've always appraised you to be a person confident in their own abilities. But a city's ability to defend itself goes far beyond the capabilities of a single person. I must wonder how it is that you're able to be so confident about the abilities of others.\n哎呀呀，真是自信。我一直认为你是个对自己能力很有信心的人。但一座城市自卫的能力，远远超出单个人的本领。我倒很想知道，你怎么能对别人的能力也如此笃定。"

    old "I'm confident in myself, and I'm confident in my ability to correctly estimate the abilities of others. In fact, I consider those to be one and the same: in order to know that you're the best, you need to appraise both yourself and others. I've appraised Grimoire, and I think that they're ready to defend against whatever invasion N'Mar can mount."
    new "I'm confident in myself, and I'm confident in my ability to correctly estimate the abilities of others. In fact, I consider those to be one and the same: in order to know that you're the best, you need to appraise both yourself and others. I've appraised Grimoire, and I think that they're ready to defend against whatever invasion N'Mar can mount.\n我对自己有信心，也对我准确判断他人能力的能力有信心。事实上，我认为这两者是一回事：要想知道自己是最强的，就必须同时衡量自己和他人。我衡量过 Grimoire，我认为他们已准备好抵挡 N'Mar 发动的任何入侵。"

    old "Ah, but there lies the hidden unknown in all of this. You know that you and your companions are capable combatants, and you consider the city of Grimoire to be strong, but can you really assess Grimoire's readiness in comparison to a threat that you yourself have not yet faced?"
    new "Ah, but there lies the hidden unknown in all of this. You know that you and your companions are capable combatants, and you consider the city of Grimoire to be strong, but can you really assess Grimoire's readiness in comparison to a threat that you yourself have not yet faced?\n啊，但这其中正藏着未知。你知道你和你的同伴都是能征善战之人，也认为 Grimoire 城很强，但面对一个连你自己都尚未遭遇的威胁，你真能评估出 Grimoire 的准备程度吗？"

    old "N'Mar's invasion force will be like nothing you've ever seen before. It seems odd to say you're ready for them, when you don't entirely know what it is that you're ready for."
    new "N'Mar's invasion force will be like nothing you've ever seen before. It seems odd to say you're ready for them, when you don't entirely know what it is that you're ready for.\nN'Mar 的入侵大军将是你前所未见的。在你并不完全清楚自己究竟准备好面对什么的时候，就说你已经准备好了，这听起来有些奇怪。"

    old "I think I have a pretty good idea. Vampires, and their undead cohorts."
    new "I think I have a pretty good idea. Vampires, and their undead cohorts.\n我想我心里有数。Vampires，还有他们的亡灵同类。"

    old "Yes, but if you believe that the vampires you've faced so far are the strongest that N'Mar has to offer, you may find yourself sorely mistaken."
    new "Yes, but if you believe that the vampires you've faced so far are the strongest that N'Mar has to offer, you may find yourself sorely mistaken.\n是啊，但如果你以为迄今交过手的那些 Vampires 就是 N'Mar 能派出的最强力量，那你恐怕会大错特错。"

    old "I'm not sure."
    new "I'm not sure.\n我不太确定。"

    old "And yet you're still here. The attack from N'Mar may succeed, you know."
    new "And yet you're still here. The attack from N'Mar may succeed, you know.\n可你还是留在这里。N'Mar 的进攻也许会得手，你知道的。"

    old "And it may just as easily fail."
    new "And it may just as easily fail.\n它也同样可能轻易落空。"

    old "So, two possible outcomes. One of which may end with you being killed. Are you willing to gamble with your life?"
    new "So, two possible outcomes. One of which may end with you being killed. Are you willing to gamble with your life?\n那么，两种可能的结局。其中之一，可能以你的死告终。你愿意拿性命去赌吗？"

    old "No, they're not ready."
    new "No, they're not ready.\n不，他们还没准备好。"

    old "Interesting. And yet here you are, in the city that you yourself consider to be unprepared for the attack."
    new "Interesting. And yet here you are, in the city that you yourself consider to be unprepared for the attack.\n有意思。可你却待在这里，待在这座连你自己都认为尚未做好迎战准备的城市里。"

    old "I have my reasons."
    new "I have my reasons.\n我有我的理由。"

    old "No doubt. But I wonder whether those reasons are really so compelling that you're willing to stay here in Grimoire and risk your own life."
    new "No doubt. But I wonder whether those reasons are really so compelling that you're willing to stay here in Grimoire and risk your own life.\n毫无疑问。但我想知道，那些理由是否真的有力到让你愿意留在 Grimoire，冒着性命之忧。"

    old "It sounds like you're trying to talk me out of staying in Grimoire."
    new "It sounds like you're trying to talk me out of staying in Grimoire.\n听起来你像是想劝我别留在 Grimoire。"

    old "I am simply pointing out that the possibility exists for you to simply disappear before then."
    new "I am simply pointing out that the possibility exists for you to simply disappear before then.\n我只是在指出一种可能：你可以在那之前就悄悄消失。"

    old "That would be treasonous, and my absence will certainly be noticed."
    new "That would be treasonous, and my absence will certainly be noticed.\n那是叛逃，而我的缺席一定会被人察觉。"

    old "No doubt. But even in the event that Grimoire is mostly successful in repelling the invasion, people will die. There will be chaos. Many people may disappear, their bodies to be undiscovered by the survivors. Who's to say you can't be one of them?"
    new "No doubt. But even in the event that Grimoire is mostly successful in repelling the invasion, people will die. There will be chaos. Many people may disappear, their bodies to be undiscovered by the survivors. Who's to say you can't be one of them?\n毫无疑问。但即便 Grimoire 大体上成功击退了入侵，仍会有人死去，仍会一片混乱。许多人可能就此消失，尸体也不会被幸存者发现。谁又能说你不能成为其中之一呢？"

    old "You're suggesting that I slip out and leave others to deal with the invasion."
    new "You're suggesting that I slip out and leave others to deal with the invasion.\n你是在暗示我悄悄溜走，把入侵留给别人去应付。"

    old "I'm only putting it forward as a possibility."
    new "I'm only putting it forward as a possibility.\n我只是把它作为一种可能提出来。"

    old "I find this odd, coming from you. I thought you wanted to see N'Mar crumble."
    new "I find this odd, coming from you. I thought you wanted to see N'Mar crumble.\n这话从你嘴里说出来，我觉得很奇怪。我还以为你盼着看到 N'Mar 土崩瓦解。"

    old "Not the castle, I'd prefer if that remained intact. But yes, I would like to see the vampire heirarchy brought to its knees."
    new "Not the castle, I'd prefer if that remained intact. But yes, I would like to see the vampire heirarchy brought to its knees.\n不是城堡，我倒希望城堡完好无损。不过没错，我确实想看到 Vampires 的统治阶层跪倒在地。"

    old "And yet you encourage me to leave. Why not encourage me to stay and fight the vampires of N'Mar, if you hate them so much?"
    new "And yet you encourage me to leave. Why not encourage me to stay and fight the vampires of N'Mar, if you hate them so much?\n可你却鼓励我离开。既然你这么恨他们，为什么不鼓励我留下来，与 N'Mar 的 Vampires 一战？"

    old "[protag], you've already done so much. You've sown much chaos, and regardless of who wins tomorrow night, the vampires will certainly find themselves battered and weakened in the aftermath."
    new "[protag], you've already done so much. You've sown much chaos, and regardless of who wins tomorrow night, the vampires will certainly find themselves battered and weakened in the aftermath.\n[protag]，你已经做了很多。你搅起了不小的乱局，无论明晚谁胜谁负，Vampires 在事后都必定会发现自己元气大伤、实力削弱。"

    old "Who ultimately wins is not so important to me as the fact that battles will happen, and there will be losses and casualties on both sides. Besides, hundreds of people will be fighting. Maybe thousands."
    new "Who ultimately wins is not so important to me as the fact that battles will happen, and there will be losses and casualties on both sides. Besides, hundreds of people will be fighting. Maybe thousands.\n对我来说，谁最终获胜并不那么重要，重要的是战斗一定会发生，双方都会有所损失、有所伤亡。况且，参战的将有数百人，也许是数千人。"

    old "If you happen to disappear, will it really be such a great loss? It seems the height of hubris to assume that your participation in the battle will be what makes or breaks Grimoire's chances of survival."
    new "If you happen to disappear, will it really be such a great loss? It seems the height of hubris to assume that your participation in the battle will be what makes or breaks Grimoire's chances of survival.\n若你碰巧消失了，那真的会是多大的损失吗？认定你的参战将决定 Grimoire 生死存亡的成败，这未免太过自负了。"

    old "So why encourage me to leave?"
    new "So why encourage me to leave?\n那为什么要劝我离开？"

    old "Again, I'm not encouraging you to leave. I merely wish to ensure that you've considered it as a possibility. But if you have to know why, it's that I see potential in you, [protag]."
    new "Again, I'm not encouraging you to leave. I merely wish to ensure that you've considered it as a possibility. But if you have to know why, it's that I see potential in you, [protag].\n我再重申一次，我不是在劝你离开。我只是想确认你把它当作一种可能考虑过了。不过你若一定要知道原因，那就是我看中了你的潜力，[protag]。"

    old "Potential?"
    new "Potential?\n潜力？"

    old "Potential."
    new "Potential.\n潜力。"

    old "It's time to do away with old blood. If the vampires are vanquished, we'll need new blood to replace them. A younger generation of vampires."
    new "It's time to do away with old blood. If the vampires are vanquished, we'll need new blood to replace them. A younger generation of vampires.\n是时候淘汰旧血了。若 Vampires 被剿灭，我们就需要新血来接替他们——更年轻的一代 Vampires。"

    old "Vampires like Valery."
    new "Vampires like Valery.\n像 Valery 那样的 Vampires。"

    old "And Zachary!"
    new "And Zachary!\n还有 Zachary！"

    old "And you."
    new "And you.\n还有你。"

    old "Me?"
    new "Me?\n我？"

    old "Zachary chuckles."
    new "Zachary chuckles.\nZachary 轻声笑了。"

    old "I wouldn't take you against your will. But yes, if you wanted to join me as part of the new brood, I'd be glad to bring you along for the ride."
    new "I wouldn't take you against your will. But yes, if you wanted to join me as part of the new brood, I'd be glad to bring you along for the ride.\n我不会强迫你。不过没错，如果你想作为新血族的一员加入我，我很乐意带你一起上路。"

    old "You want me to abandon the fight at Grimoire so that I can become a vampire."
    new "You want me to abandon the fight at Grimoire so that I can become a vampire.\n你想让我放弃在 Grimoire 的战斗，好让自己变成 Vampire。"

    old "If you want, you could do that. But the two aren't mutually exclusive. You could undergo initiation as a vampire, and still stay with Grimoire for assault from N'Mar."
    new "If you want, you could do that. But the two aren't mutually exclusive. You could undergo initiation as a vampire, and still stay with Grimoire for assault from N'Mar.\n只要你愿意，你可以这么做。但这两件事并不互相排斥。你可以接受初拥成为 Vampire，同时仍留在 Grimoire 应对 N'Mar 的进攻。"

    old "I don't think that my companions would take too kindly to being led into battle by a vampire."
    new "I don't think that my companions would take too kindly to being led into battle by a vampire.\n我觉得我的同伴们大概不会乐意被一个 Vampire 领上战场。"

    old "You might be surprised how loyal certain followers can be, [protag]. But you needn't worry about them recognizing you as a vampire right away. The vampires that I initiate take nearly a full moon to mature."
    new "You might be surprised how loyal certain followers can be, [protag]. But you needn't worry about them recognizing you as a vampire right away. The vampires that I initiate take nearly a full moon to mature.\n你也许会惊讶，某些追随者能有多忠诚，[protag]。但你无需担心他们马上认出你是 Vampire。经我初拥的 Vampires 要将近一个月圆才会成熟。"

    old "I mean that if you choose to become one of the children of the night, you won't fully turn until a month from now."
    new "I mean that if you choose to become one of the children of the night, you won't fully turn until a month from now.\n我的意思是，如果你选择成为黑夜之子的一员，要一个月后才会完全转化。"

    old "I think I need a moment to process the fact that you seem to have just offered to make me a vampire."
    new "I think I need a moment to process the fact that you seem to have just offered to make me a vampire.\n我想我需要缓一缓，好好消化一下你似乎刚刚提出要让我变成 Vampire 这件事。"

    old "Well, think about it, but don't think too long. Valery and I are quite busy, and we have things to attend to before tomorrow."
    new "Well, think about it, but don't think too long. Valery and I are quite busy, and we have things to attend to before tomorrow.\n那么，好好想想，但别想太久。Valery 和我都很忙，明天之前还有事要处理。"

    old "What would it even mean for me to become a vampire?"
    new "What would it even mean for me to become a vampire?\n我变成 Vampire，究竟意味着什么？"

    old "Well, for one thing, you'd be leaving your old life completely behind. After you'd turned, of course, which would be a month from now, or thereabouts. It's not as if you could walk around a city like Grimoire and participate in normal society as a vampire."
    new "Well, for one thing, you'd be leaving your old life completely behind. After you'd turned, of course, which would be a month from now, or thereabouts. It's not as if you could walk around a city like Grimoire and participate in normal society as a vampire.\n首先，你将彻底抛下过去的生活。当然，那是在你转化之后——也就是一个月左右之后。你总不可能以 Vampire 的身份，在 Grimoire 这样的城市里四处走动、照常融入社会。"

    old "And you couldn't go much of anywhere during the day."
    new "And you couldn't go much of anywhere during the day.\n而且白天你哪儿也去不了多少。"

    old "I wouldn't say that."
    new "I wouldn't say that.\n我不会这么说。"

    old "But it is more difficult to move during the day. You need to stick to places where the sun doesn't shine. Not that you'd be instantly killed like in those stupid folk tales."
    new "But it is more difficult to move during the day. You need to stick to places where the sun doesn't shine. Not that you'd be instantly killed like in those stupid folk tales.\n不过白天确实更难行动。你得待在阳光照不到的地方。倒不是说你会像那些愚蠢的民间故事里说的那样，一照阳光就立刻毙命。"

    old "Simply it's... painful. One scream, and people would notice you. And... you don't want to be noticed."
    new "Simply it's... painful. One scream, and people would notice you. And... you don't want to be noticed.\n只是会……痛苦。一声尖叫，人们就会注意到你。而……你不会想被人注意的。"

    old "Those seem like significant drawbacks. Why would I want to become a vampire?"
    new "Those seem like significant drawbacks. Why would I want to become a vampire?\n这些听起来都是不小的缺陷。我为什么还想变成 Vampire？"

    old "Perhaps Valery can tell you. So many of the advantages of being a vampire are things I take for granted."
    new "Perhaps Valery can tell you. So many of the advantages of being a vampire are things I take for granted.\n也许 Valery 能告诉你。做 Vampire 的许多好处，都是我早已习以为常的。"

    old "Oh, where do I even begin? It is utterly indescribable. You couldn't possibly understand it."
    new "Oh, where do I even begin? It is utterly indescribable. You couldn't possibly understand it.\n哦，我该从哪儿说起呢？那完全无法形容。你根本不可能理解。"

    old "I don't see how I could reasonably agree to something that I can't possibly understand. What if I turn, and find every moment of existence to be torment?"
    new "I don't see how I could reasonably agree to something that I can't possibly understand. What if I turn, and find every moment of existence to be torment?\n我不明白，我怎么能理智地答应一件自己根本无法理解的事。万一我转化之后，发现活着的每一刻都是折磨呢？"

    old "But you won't. When you're a vampire...when I turned, I felt limber. Young. I could move, and jump, and dance, all effortlessly, all without tiring."
    new "But you won't. When you're a vampire...when I turned, I felt limber. Young. I could move, and jump, and dance, all effortlessly, all without tiring.\n你不会的。当你成为 Vampire……我转化的时候，感觉身体轻盈，青春焕发。我可以活动、跳跃、起舞，一切都毫不费力，而且不知疲倦。"

    old "Yes, vampires do have an increased stamina."
    new "Yes, vampires do have an increased stamina.\n没错，Vampires 的耐力确实更强。"

    old "So much stamina! I could go for days or weeks without sleeping, simply enjoying all of the pleasures of this world. And so pleasurable they are! Nothing you can do as a [prace] can compare to the pleasure of drinking fresh blood, right from the artery."
    new "So much stamina! I could go for days or weeks without sleeping, simply enjoying all of the pleasures of this world. And so pleasurable they are! Nothing you can do as a [prace] can compare to the pleasure of drinking fresh blood, right from the artery.\n何止是耐力！我可以几天甚至几周不睡觉，尽情享受这世间的种种欢愉。而那些欢愉又是多么美妙啊！作为 [prace]，你所做的一切，都比不上从动脉直接啜饮新鲜血液的快感。"

    old "Drinking fresh blood doesn't sound too appealing to me."
    new "Drinking fresh blood doesn't sound too appealing to me.\n喝新鲜的血，对我来说可没那么有吸引力。"

    old "But it will become appealing, once you turn."
    new "But it will become appealing, once you turn.\n但一旦你转化，它就会变得诱人。"

    old "I'm not sure that I like the idea of coming to enjoy drinking blood."
    new "I'm not sure that I like the idea of coming to enjoy drinking blood.\n我不太喜欢那种将来会渐渐爱上喝血的想法。"

    old "Oh, I had the same concern. But all of my inhibitions surrounding it completely went away. Now, I feel only the pure enjoyment of drinking fresh blood, with none of the concern that plagued me before. For that pleasure alone, the transformation would be worth it. You'll come to love it."
    new "Oh, I had the same concern. But all of my inhibitions surrounding it completely went away. Now, I feel only the pure enjoyment of drinking fresh blood, with none of the concern that plagued me before. For that pleasure alone, the transformation would be worth it. You'll come to love it.\n哦，我也曾有过同样的顾虑。但我心中围绕此事的种种顾虑全都烟消云散了。如今，我只感受到啜饮新鲜血液的纯粹欢愉，再也没有从前那些烦扰。单单为了这份欢愉，转化也值了。你会爱上它的。"

    old "I guess I'll have to take your word for it. But it would be a disconcerting thing to become a vampire and then suddenly not have a taste for blood."
    new "I guess I'll have to take your word for it. But it would be a disconcerting thing to become a vampire and then suddenly not have a taste for blood.\n我想我只好相信你的话了。但要是变成了 Vampire，却突然对血提不起兴趣，那可就让人心里发毛了。"

    old "You'll change once you're turned. Everyone changes."
    new "You'll change once you're turned. Everyone changes.\n一旦转化，你就会改变。人人都会改变。"

    old "The novelty seems like it might wear off after awhile. It might be fun for a few weeks, or years, but what about centuries?"
    new "The novelty seems like it might wear off after awhile. It might be fun for a few weeks, or years, but what about centuries?\n新鲜感似乎过一阵子就会消退。几周、几年或许很有趣，可几个世纪之后呢？"

    old "Some people think immortality is a curse. Well, for one thing, vampires are not immortal, strictly speaking. But tell me. Do you know of anyone who wants to live a shorter life? Anyone who wants a shorter life for their children?"
    new "Some people think immortality is a curse. Well, for one thing, vampires are not immortal, strictly speaking. But tell me. Do you know of anyone who wants to live a shorter life? Anyone who wants a shorter life for their children?\n有些人觉得永生是种诅咒。不过首先，严格来说 Vampires 并非永生不死。但你告诉我，你认识谁想活得更短？谁想让自己的孩子寿命更短？"

    old "Some people live lives of great pain and long to be put out of their misery."
    new "Some people live lives of great pain and long to be put out of their misery.\n有些人活在巨大的痛苦中，只求早日解脱。"

    old "Well, I doubt you would encounter such an existence as a vampire. Ailments and disease are nothing to a vampire's constitution. And the benefits of old age are, well, somewhat indescribable, as Valery put it. But so incredibly worth it."
    new "Well, I doubt you would encounter such an existence as a vampire. Ailments and disease are nothing to a vampire's constitution. And the benefits of old age are, well, somewhat indescribable, as Valery put it. But so incredibly worth it.\n不过，我想你成为 Vampire 后不会遇到那种境况。疾病对 Vampire 的体质来说根本不算什么。而年长的好处，正如 Valery 所说，多少有些难以言传。但绝对物超所值。"

    old "It is something truly special to be able to watch the rise and fall of world powers, to observe legacies as they spring up and vanish. You have not experienced the world as I have, [protag]. I wish you could. And you can."
    new "It is something truly special to be able to watch the rise and fall of world powers, to observe legacies as they spring up and vanish. You have not experienced the world as I have, [protag]. I wish you could. And you can.\n能够目睹世界强权的兴衰，观察那些功业如何兴起又消逝，这确实非同寻常。你没有像我这样见识过这个世界，[protag]。我希望你能。而且你可以。"

    old "What's most important to you, [protag]?"
    new "What's most important to you, [protag]?\n对你来说最重要的是什么，[protag]？"

    old "Myself, of course. Nothing else matters if I'm not here to experience it."
    new "Myself, of course. Nothing else matters if I'm not here to experience it.\n当然是我自己。若我不在这里去经历，其他一切都不重要。"

    old "Then experience the world, [protag]. Extend the life of the person who's most important to you: yourself."
    new "Then experience the world, [protag]. Extend the life of the person who's most important to you: yourself.\n那就去经历这个世界吧，[protag]。延长那个对你最重要的人的生命：你自己。"

    old "My friends. Life means nothing without companionship."
    new "My friends. Life means nothing without companionship.\n我的朋友。没有同伴，生命毫无意义。"

    old "[protag], the best friendships are those that last a lifetime, don't you agree? There is a certain kind of special friendship that can only be formed over a long period of time. Bonds that require decades to fully foment."
    new "[protag], the best friendships are those that last a lifetime, don't you agree? There is a certain kind of special friendship that can only be formed over a long period of time. Bonds that require decades to fully foment.\n[protag]，最好的友谊是相伴一生的，你同意吗？有一种特殊的友谊，只有经过漫长岁月才能建立。那种羁绊需要几十年才能完全酝酿成形。"

    old "Do you have anyone like that?"
    new "Do you have anyone like that?\n你身边有这样的人吗？"

    old "Most people only get a few chances to have friendships like those. If you grow up in one area, and then move, you miss out on the opportunity for life-long friendship. You seem like someone who moves around a lot. You don't strike me as the sort of person who has had the chance to form bonds that last for decades."
    new "Most people only get a few chances to have friendships like those. If you grow up in one area, and then move, you miss out on the opportunity for life-long friendship. You seem like someone who moves around a lot. You don't strike me as the sort of person who has had the chance to form bonds that last for decades.\n大多数人只有寥寥几次机会能拥有那样的友谊。你若在一个地方长大，后来又搬走，就会错过建立终生友谊的机会。你看起来是个四处漂泊的人。你不像是那种有机会结下延续数十年羁绊的人。"

    old "And you're saying that you do?"
    new "And you're saying that you do?\n你是说你有这样的机会？"

    old "When you live for centuries, a friendship that lasts for eighty years is something you have many chances to form. And yet it's just as strong a bond as one shared between two mortals who grow up, age, and die together."
    new "When you live for centuries, a friendship that lasts for eighty years is something you have many chances to form. And yet it's just as strong a bond as one shared between two mortals who grow up, age, and die together.\n当你活上几个世纪，一段维系八十年的友谊，你有大把机会去建立。而且，它的牢固程度，丝毫不亚于两个凡人之间那种一起长大、一起变老、一起死去的羁绊。"

    old "I'm not sure that just you two would make for ample companionship over several centuries."
    new "I'm not sure that just you two would make for ample companionship over several centuries.\n我不太确定，几个世纪下来，仅你们两位是否足以称得上是充实的陪伴。"

    old "If you want to know what true companionship is, join us. We're forming a new brood, [protag]. You won't be the first new vampire, and you won't be the last."
    new "If you want to know what true companionship is, join us. We're forming a new brood, [protag]. You won't be the first new vampire, and you won't be the last.\n若你想知道何为真正的陪伴，就加入我们吧。我们正在组建新的血族，[protag]。你不会是第一个新 Vampire，也不会是最后一个。"

    old "I believe in the greater good. It's why I fight for Grimoire. I'm just one individual who is part of a city. And that one city is part of a nation. And that one nation is part of an entire continent."
    new "I believe in the greater good. It's why I fight for Grimoire. I'm just one individual who is part of a city. And that one city is part of a nation. And that one nation is part of an entire continent.\n我信仰更大的善。这正是我为 Grimoire 而战的原因。我不过是一个个体，隶属一座城市；而那座城市隶属一个国家；那个国家又隶属整片大陆。"

    old "So, you wish to strive for the greater good. That sounds nice, but what does the greater good really mean to you, [protag]? Do you simply care about the people who are around now? What about your children? What about their children?"
    new "So, you wish to strive for the greater good. That sounds nice, but what does the greater good really mean to you, [protag]? Do you simply care about the people who are around now? What about your children? What about their children?\n那么，你想为更大的善而奋斗。这话听起来不错，但对你而言，更大的善究竟意味着什么，[protag]？你只关心眼下身边的人吗？你的孩子呢？你孩子的孩子呢？"

    old "Of course they matter as well. One of the reasons we try to preserve things larger than ourselves, things like institutions and a fertile land, is so that they can be enjoyed by future generations as well."
    new "Of course they matter as well. One of the reasons we try to preserve things larger than ourselves, things like institutions and a fertile land, is so that they can be enjoyed by future generations as well.\n他们当然也同样重要。我们努力守护比自身更宏大的东西——比如制度、肥沃的土地——原因之一，就是为了让后世也能享有它们。"

    old "But what better way to ensure the well-being of future generations than to preside over them? Suppose a greater threat arises two centuries from now. Wouldn't it be good if you were around to help deal with it?"
    new "But what better way to ensure the well-being of future generations than to preside over them? Suppose a greater threat arises two centuries from now. Wouldn't it be good if you were around to help deal with it?\n但要想确保后世的福祉，还有什么比亲自守护他们更好的办法？假设两百年后出现更大的威胁。若那时你仍在，能帮忙应对，岂不更好？"

    old "You're suggesting that I accept immortality in undeath just for the hypothetical case that I might be of greater help to future generations?"
    new "You're suggesting that I accept immortality in undeath just for the hypothetical case that I might be of greater help to future generations?\n你是在建议我接受不死之身，只为了那种假想的情形——或许我能对后世更有帮助？"

    old "A century or two is a long time, [protag]. This isn't the first time the human empire has gone to war, and it won't be the last."
    new "A century or two is a long time, [protag]. This isn't the first time the human empire has gone to war, and it won't be the last.\n一两个世纪是很长的时间，[protag]。人类帝国开战不是头一回了，也不会是最后一回。"

    old "It's an interesting offer."
    new "It's an interesting offer.\n这是个有意思的提议。"

    old "No doubt the most interesting offer you've received today. Quite possibly the most interesting offer you've received, or will ever receive, in an entire lifetime."
    new "No doubt the most interesting offer you've received today. Quite possibly the most interesting offer you've received, or will ever receive, in an entire lifetime.\n无疑是你今天收到的最有意思的提议。也很可能是你这一生中，已经收到、或将会收到的最有意思的提议。"

    old "But I need an answer."
    new "But I need an answer.\n但我需要一个答复。"

    old "When?"
    new "When?\n什么时候？"

    old "By tomorrow night. We can perform the ceremony exactly one day from now."
    new "By tomorrow night. We can perform the ceremony exactly one day from now.\n明晚之前。从现在起整整一天后，我们就能举行仪式。"

    old "This doesn't give me very much time to think about it."
    new "This doesn't give me very much time to think about it.\n这可没给我多少考虑的时间。"

    old "If you need more than a day to think about it, then you're not ready to be a vampire. So tell me, are you ready to be initiated?"
    new "If you need more than a day to think about it, then you're not ready to be a vampire. So tell me, are you ready to be initiated?\n如果你想这件事都要想上不止一天，那你还没准备好成为 Vampire。那么告诉我，你准备好接受初拥了吗？"

    old "I feel obliged to ask if there's a particular reason that you're coming to me right now."
    new "I feel obliged to ask if there's a particular reason that you're coming to me right now.\n我觉得有必要问一句，你此刻来找我，是不是有什么特别的原因？"

    old "Tomorrow night will be a full moon. And the ritual tends to work best under the conditions of a full moon."
    new "Tomorrow night will be a full moon. And the ritual tends to work best under the conditions of a full moon.\n明晚将是满月。而这种仪式在满月之时效果最佳。"

    old "I'll be a bit busy tomorrow night, as you might imagine."
    new "I'll be a bit busy tomorrow night, as you might imagine.\n明晚我恐怕会有点忙，你也能想象得到。"

    old "I imagine that your business will be the least of your concerns when it comes to a topic this important. Come now. The ritual won't take but a few minutes."
    new "I imagine that your business will be the least of your concerns when it comes to a topic this important. Come now. The ritual won't take but a few minutes.\n我想，面对如此重要的话题，你的那些事务将是你最不必操心的事。来吧。仪式不过几分钟而已。"

    old "A few minutes aren't going to come between you and the most important decision of your life."
    new "A few minutes aren't going to come between you and the most important decision of your life.\n几分钟时间，绝不会耽误你做出这一生最重要的决定。"

    old "You'll have plenty of time to return to Grimoire after the ritual is completed. You can even help your friends, if you so desire."
    new "You'll have plenty of time to return to Grimoire after the ritual is completed. You can even help your friends, if you so desire.\n仪式完成后，你将有充裕的时间返回 Grimoire。若你愿意，甚至还能帮上你的朋友们。"

    old "Yes. Even if you initiate tomorrow, you'll have a full month before you turn. That should be more than enough time to complete whatever duties you have to attend to for Grimoire, shouldn't it?"
    new "Yes. Even if you initiate tomorrow, you'll have a full month before you turn. That should be more than enough time to complete whatever duties you have to attend to for Grimoire, shouldn't it?\n是的。就算你明天接受初拥，离完全转化也还有整整一个月。这段时间足够你完成在 Grimoire 该尽的职责了，不是吗？"

    old "Besides, even before you fully turn, you'll start to experience little...advantages."
    new "Besides, even before you fully turn, you'll start to experience little...advantages.\n况且，即便在你完全转化之前，你就会开始体验到一些小小的……好处。"

    old "I wouldn't want to completely spoil the surprise. Let's just say that after the initiation, you'll get a small taste of what vampiric strength and resilience feels like. By the time the next full moon comes and you fully turn, you'll be more than ready to face what's on the other side of the transformation."
    new "I wouldn't want to completely spoil the surprise. Let's just say that after the initiation, you'll get a small taste of what vampiric strength and resilience feels like. By the time the next full moon comes and you fully turn, you'll be more than ready to face what's on the other side of the transformation.\n我可不想把惊喜完全说破。这么说吧，初拥之后，你会稍稍尝到 Vampire 的力量与韧性是什么滋味。等到下一个满月来临、你完全转化时，你早就准备好面对转化彼岸的一切了。"

    old "You'll experience increased health and stamina regeneration while you fight."
    new "You'll experience increased health and stamina regeneration while you fight.\n战斗时，你会感到生命与耐力的恢复都有所提升。"

    old "So only advantages? No bad side effects?"
    new "So only advantages? No bad side effects?\n这么说只有好处？没有副作用？"

    old "For example, I know for certain that healing potions harm undead. What if I use one while I'm in the process of getting transformed?"
    new "For example, I know for certain that healing potions harm undead. What if I use one while I'm in the process of getting transformed?\n比如说，我确知治疗药剂会伤害亡灵。要是我在转化过程中用上一瓶，会怎样？"

    old "Until you completely turn, you won't be harmed by them. However, the potion's healing effect will be greatly reduced. Like even down to half."
    new "Until you completely turn, you won't be harmed by them. However, the potion's healing effect will be greatly reduced. Like even down to half.\n在你完全转化之前，它们不会伤害你。不过药剂的治疗效果会大大减弱，甚至可能减到一半。"

    old "In that case, I can give you an answer right now."
    new "In that case, I can give you an answer right now.\n那样的话，我现在就能给你答复。"

    old "Save your answer for tomorrow night."
    new "Save your answer for tomorrow night.\n把你的答复留到明晚吧。"

    old "See that little grove? Out there, at the edge of that knoll, right where the mist is rolling in. If you decide to take us up on the offer, meet us there."
    new "See that little grove? Out there, at the edge of that knoll, right where the mist is rolling in. If you decide to take us up on the offer, meet us there.\n看到那片小树林了吗？就在外面，那座小丘的边缘，雾气正滚滚涌来的地方。若你决定接受我们的提议，就到那里来找我们。"

    old "I think I need some time to think about it."
    new "I think I need some time to think about it.\n我想我需要些时间考虑一下。"

    old "We'll be out tomorrow night. See that little grove? Out there, at the edge of that knoll, right where the mist is rolling in. If you decide to take us up on the offer, meet us there."
    new "We'll be out tomorrow night. See that little grove? Out there, at the edge of that knoll, right where the mist is rolling in. If you decide to take us up on the offer, meet us there.\n明晚我们会在外面。看到那片小树林了吗？就在外面，那座小丘的边缘，雾气正滚滚涌来的地方。若你决定接受我们的提议，就到那里来找我们。"

    old "With that, Zachary and Valery receed into the mist, leaving me to contemplate the consequences of choosing to become a vampire."
    new "With that, Zachary and Valery receed into the mist, leaving me to contemplate the consequences of choosing to become a vampire.\n说完，Zachary 和 Valery 便退入雾中，留下我独自思索选择成为 Vampire 的后果。"

    old "Another thing that Zachary said sticks with me: the idea that perhaps now is not the time for me to stay and fight. It's a question that I haven't pondered much recently, but one way or another, I'll be facing it tomorrow."
    new "Another thing that Zachary said sticks with me: the idea that perhaps now is not the time for me to stay and fight. It's a question that I haven't pondered much recently, but one way or another, I'll be facing it tomorrow.\nZachary 说的另一句话一直萦绕在我心头：也许眼下并不是我留下来战斗的时候。这个问题我近来没怎么细想过，但无论如何，明天我都将面对它。"

    old "I step into the mists, locating the knoll that Zachary and Valery told me of. For a moment, I consider whether this might be some sort of trap, but if their goal really was to isolate and kill me, this is the most roundabout way they could possible do it."
    new "I step into the mists, locating the knoll that Zachary and Valery told me of. For a moment, I consider whether this might be some sort of trap, but if their goal really was to isolate and kill me, this is the most roundabout way they could possible do it.\n我步入雾中，找到 Zachary 和 Valery 所说的那座小丘。有那么一瞬，我怀疑这会不会是某种陷阱，但如果他们的目的真是把我孤立起来杀掉，这恐怕是他们能做到的最迂回的方式了。"

    old "Though there's a breeze, I hear a voice in my ear, beckoning me."
    new "Though there's a breeze, I hear a voice in my ear, beckoning me.\n虽有微风拂过，我却听到一个声音在耳边召唤我。"

    old "Closer..."
    new "Closer...\n再近些……"

    old "The voice speaks directly into my ear, as though it's coming from someone directly over my shoulder, and I spin around, but see no one beside or behind me. The voice speaks again."
    new "The voice speaks directly into my ear, as though it's coming from someone directly over my shoulder, and I spin around, but see no one beside or behind me. The voice speaks again.\n那声音径直传入我耳中，仿佛有人就紧贴在我肩后说话，我猛地转身，却不见身边或身后有人。那声音再次响起。"

    old "Come, closer..."
    new "Come, closer...\n来，再近些……"

    old "I walk past the knoll and find a secluded area surrounded by several small trees. As I step past the first tree, the fog around me seems to thicken, and then envelops me entirely as Zachary and Valery fade into view."
    new "I walk past the knoll and find a secluded area surrounded by several small trees. As I step past the first tree, the fog around me seems to thicken, and then envelops me entirely as Zachary and Valery fade into view.\n我走过小丘，找到一处被几棵小树环绕的僻静之地。刚走过第一棵树，四周的雾仿佛变浓了，随即将我完全笼罩，Zachary 和 Valery 的身影也渐渐浮现。"

    old "So, you've come."
    new "So, you've come.\n看来，你来了。"

    old "You're joining us!"
    new "You're joining us!\n你要加入我们了！"

    old "Yes, I've come to accept your proposal."
    new "Yes, I've come to accept your proposal.\n是的，我来接受你们的提议。"

    old "Ooh, this is going to be fun!"
    new "Ooh, this is going to be fun!\n哦，这下可好玩了！"

    old "So, is this going to be like the time that you drew blood?"
    new "So, is this going to be like the time that you drew blood?\n那么，这会像你上次取血那样吗？"

    old "How does this work, exactly?"
    new "How does this work, exactly?\n这到底是怎么进行的？"

    old "I need you to turn around and face the moon."
    new "I need you to turn around and face the moon.\n我需要你转过身去，面向月亮。"

    old "I turn my back to Zachary and Valery, casting my gaze skyward."
    new "I turn my back to Zachary and Valery, casting my gaze skyward.\n我背对 Zachary 和 Valery，把目光投向天空。"

    old "I see the moon. Now what—"
    new "I see the moon. Now what—\n我看到月亮了。现在呢——"

    old "I feel a blunt force on the back of my head, followed by a stinging sensation in my neck. The silhouettes of Zachary and Valery against the moonlight are all that I remember before I lose consciousness."
    new "I feel a blunt force on the back of my head, followed by a stinging sensation in my neck. The silhouettes of Zachary and Valery against the moonlight are all that I remember before I lose consciousness.\n我后脑遭到一记钝击，紧接着脖颈传来一阵刺痛。我失去意识前所记得的，只有月光下 Zachary 和 Valery 的剪影。"

    old "I feel pain. It's not a sharp pain that I can trace to any point in my body. It's more a throbbing pain that comes from inside. From within me."
    new "I feel pain. It's not a sharp pain that I can trace to any point in my body. It's more a throbbing pain that comes from inside. From within me.\n我感到疼痛。那不是我能在身上指出位置的锐痛，而更像一种从内部、从我的体内涌出的阵阵抽痛。"

    old "It's almost as if the pain itself is coursing through my limbs, through my chest, through my heart, and seeping into every part of my body. I hear voices above me faintly."
    new "It's almost as if the pain itself is coursing through my limbs, through my chest, through my heart, and seeping into every part of my body. I hear voices above me faintly.\n那疼痛仿佛顺着我的四肢、胸膛、心脏奔流，渗进我身体的每一个角落。我隐约听到上方有人声。"

    old "Is [heshe] awake?"
    new "Is [heshe] awake?\n[heshe] 醒了吗？"

    old "For [hisher] sake, I hope not."
    new "For [hisher] sake, I hope not.\n看在 [hisher] 的份上，我希望没有。"

    old "Maybe [heshe] needs another bite to sleep well."
    new "Maybe [heshe] needs another bite to sleep well.\n也许 [heshe] 需要再被咬一口，才能睡得安稳。"

    old "Perhaps it's best not to—"
    new "Perhaps it's best not to—\n也许最好别——"

    old "Too late!"
    new "Too late!\n太迟了！"

    old "I feel a sharp pain in my neck again. This time, the sharp pain is almost a relief, as it overwhelms the dull, throbbing pain all over my body, and I again find myself losing awareness."
    new "I feel a sharp pain in my neck again. This time, the sharp pain is almost a relief, as it overwhelms the dull, throbbing pain all over my body, and I again find myself losing awareness.\n我脖颈上又是一阵锐痛。这一次，这锐痛近乎一种解脱，盖过了遍布全身的沉闷抽痛，于是我再次渐渐失去意识。"

    old "What's happening? Why hasn't [heshe] woken up yet?"
    new "What's happening? Why hasn't [heshe] woken up yet?\n出什么事了？为什么 [heshe] 还没醒过来？"

    old "This is quite interesting. Look, [hisher] body is fighting it."
    new "This is quite interesting. Look, [hisher] body is fighting it.\n这倒是挺有意思。看，[hisher] 的身体在抵抗它。"

    old "No, it will still work, just with a great deal more pain involved. But to think, the amount of power [heshe] has exhibited so far...I've never seen someone last this long."
    new "No, it will still work, just with a great deal more pain involved. But to think, the amount of power [heshe] has exhibited so far...I've never seen someone last this long.\n不，它仍会生效，只是会伴随更多的痛苦。但想一想，[heshe] 迄今展现出的力量……我还从没见过有人能撑这么久。"

    old "Perhaps [heshe] will become one to challenge even you."
    new "Perhaps [heshe] will become one to challenge even you.\n也许 [heshe] 会成为连你都要正视的对手。"

    old "Ohoho. I wouldn't go that far, Valery. Getting a grasp of that kind of power will take decades of learning. And natural talent can only carry someone so far."
    new "Ohoho. I wouldn't go that far, Valery. Getting a grasp of that kind of power will take decades of learning. And natural talent can only carry someone so far.\n哦呵呵。我可不会说到那个份上，Valery。要掌握那种力量，得花上几十年的钻研。而天赋只能把人带到一定程度。"

    old "Oh, it looks like [heshe] is starting to fade again."
    new "Oh, it looks like [heshe] is starting to fade again.\n哦，看来 [heshe] 又开始失去意识了。"

    old "Good, hopefully this will be the last one."
    new "Good, hopefully this will be the last one.\n好，希望这是最后一次。"

    old "I blink awake, with Zachary and Valery standing above me. However, despite having a feeling of clearly just coming awake, I feel no grogginess. I immediately stand up, fully alert."
    new "I blink awake, with Zachary and Valery standing above me. However, despite having a feeling of clearly just coming awake, I feel no grogginess. I immediately stand up, fully alert.\n我眨眨眼醒了过来，Zachary 和 Valery 站在我身旁。然而，尽管我分明是刚刚醒来，却毫无昏沉之感。我立刻站起身，头脑完全清醒。"

    old "You took that surprisingly well."
    new "You took that surprisingly well.\n你撑过来了，真是出人意料地好。"

    old "What did you do to me?"
    new "What did you do to me?\n你们对我做了什么？"

    old "The ritual, of course. That's what you came here for, isn't it?"
    new "The ritual, of course. That's what you came here for, isn't it?\n当然是仪式。这不正是你来此的目的吗？"

    old "I wasn't expecting to be beating over the head and left unconscious for the ritual."
    new "I wasn't expecting to be beating over the head and left unconscious for the ritual.\n我可没想到仪式是要被敲昏过去、失去知觉。"

    old "It's easiest to knock someone out when they're not expecting it, and you certainly did not want to be awake for the ritual. It is an incredibly painful experience."
    new "It's easiest to knock someone out when they're not expecting it, and you certainly did not want to be awake for the ritual. It is an incredibly painful experience.\n在人毫无防备时，最容易将其击昏，而你肯定不想在仪式过程中保持清醒。那是一种极其痛苦的经历。"

    old "We drained away most of your blood."
    new "We drained away most of your blood.\n我们抽干了你大部分的血。"

    old "You drained me of my blood?"
    new "You drained me of my blood?\n你们抽干了我的血？"

    old "I squeeze my fingers together, forming a fist, then release my fingers, testing my ability to form a grip. I flex, and my entire arm reacts, almost as if the muscle in other parts of my body is amplifying the strength of my hand."
    new "I squeeze my fingers together, forming a fist, then release my fingers, testing my ability to form a grip. I flex, and my entire arm reacts, almost as if the muscle in other parts of my body is amplifying the strength of my hand.\n我把手指攥拢成拳，又松开，试探自己握力的恢复。我一发力，整条手臂便随之响应，仿佛身体其他部位的肌肉都在放大我手掌的力量。"

    old "How do you feel?"
    new "How do you feel?\n你感觉如何？"

    old "I feel...powerful."
    new "I feel...powerful.\n我感觉……充满力量。"

    old "You've gotten only the slightest taste of power so far."
    new "You've gotten only the slightest taste of power so far.\n你迄今只是浅尝了力量的一丝滋味。"

    old "I feel...strange. There's something deep within me that feels different. My heart is still beating, but with each pulse, I feel something within me, almost as if my body is somehow changing with every breath I take, and every beat of the heart."
    new "I feel...strange. There's something deep within me that feels different. My heart is still beating, but with each pulse, I feel something within me, almost as if my body is somehow changing with every breath I take, and every beat of the heart.\n我感觉……很奇怪。我内心深处有某种东西变得不同了。我的心仍在跳动，但每一次脉搏，我都感到体内有某种东西在涌动，仿佛我的身体正随着每一次呼吸、每一次心跳而悄然改变。"

    old "A bit confused. I know a change has happened in my body, but I'm not quite sure what's happened."
    new "A bit confused. I know a change has happened in my body, but I'm not quite sure what's happened.\n有点困惑。我知道身体发生了变化，却不太确定究竟是什么。"

    old "The fact that I seem to have a greater sense of strength despite losing most of my blood is especially confusing. If you had drained most of my blood, I'd expect to be in a dazed, weakened state, and yet I feel alert. But the heightened sense of awareness is doing nothing to dispel my confusion, so maybe you can give me some answers."
    new "The fact that I seem to have a greater sense of strength despite losing most of my blood is especially confusing. If you had drained most of my blood, I'd expect to be in a dazed, weakened state, and yet I feel alert. But the heightened sense of awareness is doing nothing to dispel my confusion, so maybe you can give me some answers.\n我明明失掉了大半的血，却反而感到更有力量，这一点尤其让我困惑。若你们抽干了我大部分的血，我本该神志恍惚、虚弱无力，可我却头脑清醒。不过这份清醒的警觉丝毫无助于消解我的困惑，所以也许你们能给我些答案。"

    old "Most of your blood is gone, but we've replaced it with something much stronger. Now, a mixture of blood and vitus courses through your veins. Over the next month, the vitus will grow stronger and stronger, until it fully overwhelms the last drop of living blood in your body and you fully turn under the cover of the next full moon."
    new "Most of your blood is gone, but we've replaced it with something much stronger. Now, a mixture of blood and vitus courses through your veins. Over the next month, the vitus will grow stronger and stronger, until it fully overwhelms the last drop of living blood in your body and you fully turn under the cover of the next full moon.\n你大部分的血已经没了，但我们用更强大的东西取而代之。如今，血液与维图斯的混合物正流淌在你的血管里。未来一个月里，维图斯会越来越强，直到彻底压过你体内最后一滴活血，你将在下一个满月的笼罩下完全转化。"

    old "What does the vitus do for me right now?"
    new "What does the vitus do for me right now?\n维图斯现在能为我做什么？"

    old "Until you change form, not too much. You will find yourself slightly stronger. You may find yourself able to sustain blows with less chance of injury, or recover faster from your injuries. Your ability to engage in physical combat may see a small improvement. But over the course of the coming month, you may find yourself in possession of new abilities."
    new "Until you change form, not too much. You will find yourself slightly stronger. You may find yourself able to sustain blows with less chance of injury, or recover faster from your injuries. Your ability to engage in physical combat may see a small improvement. But over the course of the coming month, you may find yourself in possession of new abilities.\n在你改变形态之前，作用还不大。你会发现自己略强壮了些。你或许能承受打击而更不易受伤，或从伤势中恢复得更快。你参与近身战斗的能力可能会略有提升。但在接下来一个月里，你或许会发现自己拥有新的能力。"

    old "What kind of abilities?"
    new "What kind of abilities?\n什么样的能力？"

    old "Zachary shrugs and smiles."
    new "Zachary shrugs and smiles.\nZachary 耸耸肩，笑了。"

    old "I wish I could tell you, but everyone is unique. No one's body reacts to vitus the same way, and what kinds of transformations you'll see will partly be determined by what your body wants to do."
    new "I wish I could tell you, but everyone is unique. No one's body reacts to vitus the same way, and what kinds of transformations you'll see will partly be determined by what your body wants to do.\n我倒是想告诉你，可每个人都是独一无二的。没有谁的身体对维图斯的反应完全相同，你将会看到怎样的转化，一部分取决于你的身体想要做什么。"

    old "What my body...wants to do?"
    new "What my body...wants to do?\n我的身体……想要做什么？"

    old "You may, in some cases, be able to control how your abilities develop, in a somewhat indirect manner. It could be that simple aspects of your behavior affect the way that the vitus transforms your body. But I wouldn't worry about it too much."
    new "You may, in some cases, be able to control how your abilities develop, in a somewhat indirect manner. It could be that simple aspects of your behavior affect the way that the vitus transforms your body. But I wouldn't worry about it too much.\n在某些情况下，你或许能以一种较为间接的方式，掌控自己能力的发展方向。也许你行为中的一些细微之处，会影响维图斯改造你身体的方式。不过也不必太为此操心。"

    old "Now, if I'm not mistaken, there's a city that's waiting for you to defend it."
    new "Now, if I'm not mistaken, there's a city that's waiting for you to defend it.\n那么，如果我没弄错的话，有座城市正等着你去守护。"

    old "I look over my shoulder, and suddenly find my abilities able to pierce the fog and see the city walls. The shapes are mostly indistinct, but the fact that I can see anything through this opaque mist must be one of the new powers Zachary was talking about. The vision lasts only a moment before it fades, though."
    new "I look over my shoulder, and suddenly find my abilities able to pierce the fog and see the city walls. The shapes are mostly indistinct, but the fact that I can see anything through this opaque mist must be one of the new powers Zachary was talking about. The vision lasts only a moment before it fades, though.\n我回头望去，忽然发现自己的目力能穿透浓雾、望见城墙。那些轮廓大多模糊不清，但能透过这不透光的雾看见东西，这想必就是 Zachary 所说的新能力之一。不过这景象只维持了一瞬便消散了。"

    old "How much time was I out for?"
    new "How much time was I out for?\n我昏迷了多久？"

    old "Not long. Perhaps half of one hour."
    new "Not long. Perhaps half of one hour.\n没多久。大约半个钟头。"

    old "That's a long time for me to be unconscious."
    new "That's a long time for me to be unconscious.\n对我而言，昏迷这么久可不短。"

    old "You're not going to be late to your little battle."
    new "You're not going to be late to your little battle.\n你不会赶不上你那场小战斗的。"

    old "I was thinking more about the amount of time that I was completely vulnerable for."
    new "I was thinking more about the amount of time that I was completely vulnerable for.\n我更在意的是，有这么久我完全任人摆布。"

    old "That doesn't make any sense, [protag]. When you talk about 'complete vulnerability,' there aren't varying degrees to speak of. If you're unconscious for even a short time, your enemies can kill you."
    new "That doesn't make any sense, [protag]. When you talk about 'complete vulnerability,' there aren't varying degrees to speak of. If you're unconscious for even a short time, your enemies can kill you.\n这话没道理，[protag]。你说到完全无防备，这本来就没什么程度之分。哪怕只昏迷一小会儿，你的敌人都能杀了你。"

    old "The idea of just lying here for half an hour as you did things to my body still makes me feel quite vulnerable."
    new "The idea of just lying here for half an hour as you did things to my body still makes me feel quite vulnerable.\n一想到我躺在这里半个小时，任你们对我的身体动手脚，我还是觉得相当无防备。"

    old "Well, you won't be vulnerable much longer, [protag]. I hope you'll forgive me for knocking you unconscious unexpectedly, but the truth is that this little ritual should increase your independence."
    new "Well, you won't be vulnerable much longer, [protag]. I hope you'll forgive me for knocking you unconscious unexpectedly, but the truth is that this little ritual should increase your independence.\n不过，你这种无防备的状态不会持续太久了，[protag]。希望你原谅我出其不意把你击昏，但事实上，这场小小的仪式应当能增强你的独立性。"

    old "It'll increase your independence!"
    new "It'll increase your independence!\n它会增强你的独立性！"

    old "...Valery's words don't do much to reassure me."
    new "...Valery's words don't do much to reassure me.\n……Valery 的话并不能让我安心多少。"

    old "It felt much longer than that. I'm surprised it happened so quickly."
    new "It felt much longer than that. I'm surprised it happened so quickly.\n感觉比那长得多。我惊讶的是它竟进行得如此之快。"

    old "How could you know, though? You were unconscious for most of it."
    new "How could you know, though? You were unconscious for most of it.\n可你怎么会知道？大半时间里你都昏迷着。"

    old "I felt parts of it. I...I don't know. It just felt longer than that."
    new "I felt parts of it. I...I don't know. It just felt longer than that.\n我断断续续感觉到了一些。我……我不知道。就是感觉比那更久。"

    old "The ritual doesn't take tremendously long, [protag]. It takes very little time to completely drain a person's body of blood, and only slightly more time to replace it with vitus."
    new "The ritual doesn't take tremendously long, [protag]. It takes very little time to completely drain a person's body of blood, and only slightly more time to replace it with vitus.\n仪式并不需要太长时间，[protag]。把一个人体内的血完全抽干，用不了多少工夫，再用维图斯取而代之，也不过稍多一点时间。"

    old "We should be going, too."
    new "We should be going, too.\n我们也该动身了。"

    old "You said you replaced most of my blood with 'vitus.' Is that what runs through a vampire's veins"
    new "You said you replaced most of my blood with 'vitus.' Is that what runs through a vampire's veins\n你说你们用维图斯取代了我大部分的血。那就是 Vampire 血管里流淌的东西吗？"

    old "Vampires have no beating heart pumping anything—blood or vitus—through our veins. Our bodies work in fundamentally different ways, despite looking similar."
    new "Vampires have no beating heart pumping anything—blood or vitus—through our veins. Our bodies work in fundamentally different ways, despite looking similar.\nVampires 并没有跳动的心脏把任何东西——无论血液还是维图斯——泵进我们的血管。尽管外表相似，我们的身体运作方式却截然不同。"

    old "What can you tell me about vitus, since it's apparently already in me?"
    new "What can you tell me about vitus, since it's apparently already in me?\n既然维图斯显然已经在我体内了，你们能告诉我些什么关于它的事？"

    old "It's like I said. It will start to rebuild and transform your body. You'll find yourself growing stronger and maybe gaining new abilities. The fact that the vitus helps you recover from wounds more rapidly is just a side effect."
    new "It's like I said. It will start to rebuild and transform your body. You'll find yourself growing stronger and maybe gaining new abilities. The fact that the vitus helps you recover from wounds more rapidly is just a side effect.\n就像我说的。它会开始重塑、改造你的身体。你会发现自己越来越强，也许还会获得新的能力。维图斯能让你更快地从伤口中恢复，那不过是附带效果罢了。"

    old "I'd like to know more about my powers."
    new "I'd like to know more about my powers.\n我想多了解一些我的能力。"

    old "The vitus in your veins is slowly rebuilding your body. It will also help with repairing any wounds your body sustains."
    new "The vitus in your veins is slowly rebuilding your body. It will also help with repairing any wounds your body sustains.\n你血管里的维图斯正在慢慢重塑你的身体。它也会帮助你修复身体所受到的任何创伤。"

    old "So I'll start to regenerate? Is that normal for vampires?"
    new "So I'll start to regenerate? Is that normal for vampires?\n这么说我会开始自我再生？对 Vampires 来说这正常吗？"

    old "The effect that it has on your body is very different from someone whose body has no blood. You still have a beating heart. You are, in most respects, still a living being."
    new "The effect that it has on your body is very different from someone whose body has no blood. You still have a beating heart. You are, in most respects, still a living being.\n它对你身体产生的影响，与那些体内没有血液的人大不相同。你仍有一颗跳动的心脏。在大多数方面，你依然是个活生生的存在。"

    old "I wish I could go into more detail, but there isn't much point in spending a lot of time to teach you things about your body that will only apply for the next month. You'll learn to adapt to the changes in your body soon enough."
    new "I wish I could go into more detail, but there isn't much point in spending a lot of time to teach you things about your body that will only apply for the next month. You'll learn to adapt to the changes in your body soon enough.\n我也想讲得更详细些，但花大量时间教你那些只适用于接下来一个月的身体知识，实在没多大意义。你很快就会学会适应身体的变化。"

    old "I'd like to leave Grimoire and go with you."
    new "I'd like to leave Grimoire and go with you.\n我想离开 Grimoire，跟你们一起走。"

    old "Zachary raises an eyebrow."
    new "Zachary raises an eyebrow.\nZachary 挑了挑眉。"

    old "Abandoning Grimoire in their hour of need?"
    new "Abandoning Grimoire in their hour of need?\n在 Grimoire 最需要你的时候弃它而去？"

    old "You said it yourself. I'm only one [manwoman]. If the city is really ready to survive, they can survive without me."
    new "You said it yourself. I'm only one [manwoman]. If the city is really ready to survive, they can survive without me.\n这是你自己说的。我不过是一个 [manwoman]。若这座城市真的做好了生存的准备，没有我也能挺过去。"

    old "Besides, I've already decided to leave the land of the living behind. I know I won't fully turn until a month from now, but I may as well get started now."
    new "Besides, I've already decided to leave the land of the living behind. I know I won't fully turn until a month from now, but I may as well get started now.\n况且，我已经决定告别生者的世界。我知道要一个月后才会完全转化，但不如现在就启程。"

    old "What do you think, Valery? Should we let [himher]?"
    new "What do you think, Valery? Should we let [himher]?\n你怎么看，Valery？我们该让 [himher] 吗？"

    old "I'm surprised you have to ask. It would be the highest of pleasures to have [protag] join us so early."
    new "I'm surprised you have to ask. It would be the highest of pleasures to have [protag] join us so early.\n我很惊讶你竟然还要问。[protag] 这么早就加入我们，那会是莫大的乐趣。"

    old "You've thought this through, [protag]? You're really ready to leave all of this behind? Though I certainly don't envy mortals, this is your chance to make history. If you join us now, your story will not be one for the history books."
    new "You've thought this through, [protag]? You're really ready to leave all of this behind? Though I certainly don't envy mortals, this is your chance to make history. If you join us now, your story will not be one for the history books.\n你想清楚了吗，[protag]？你真的准备好把这一切都抛下？我固然不羡慕凡人，但这是你名留青史的机会。若你现在加入我们，你的故事就不会再属于史书了。"

    old "Yes, I'm ready. This chapter of my life is over. I'm more interested in what lies ahead."
    new "Yes, I'm ready. This chapter of my life is over. I'm more interested in what lies ahead.\n是的，我准备好了。我人生的这一章已经结束。我更期待前方的一切。"

    old "Very well, [protag]. In that case, we'll do what we were going to do: leave this place. But Valery and I will move slowly enough for you to keep up."
    new "Very well, [protag]. In that case, we'll do what we were going to do: leave this place. But Valery and I will move slowly enough for you to keep up.\n很好，[protag]。既然如此，我们就去做原本要做的事：离开此地。不过我和 Valery 会放慢速度，好让你跟得上。"

    old "In what seems like the blink of an eye, Zachary and Valery seem to vanish, but as I blink again, I can see their forms faintly through the fog, receeding. I take after them running."
    new "In what seems like the blink of an eye, Zachary and Valery seem to vanish, but as I blink again, I can see their forms faintly through the fog, receeding. I take after them running.\n仿佛只在一眨眼间，Zachary 和 Valery 似乎消失不见，但我再一眨眼，又能透过雾气隐约看见他们远去的身影。我拔腿追赶上去。"

    old "With the amount of distance that's between us already, there's no way that I should be able to keep up. And the old me wouldn't have been able to."
    new "With the amount of distance that's between us already, there's no way that I should be able to keep up. And the old me wouldn't have been able to.\n以我们之间已经拉开的那段距离，我本绝无可能跟得上。而过去的我也确实做不到。"

    old "But something in my legs gives me an added strength, an added swiftness, that allows me to close the distance between us faster than I ever would have imagined possible. Within moments, I find myself running alongside them."
    new "But something in my legs gives me an added strength, an added swiftness, that allows me to close the distance between us faster than I ever would have imagined possible. Within moments, I find myself running alongside them.\n但我双腿中有某种东西赋予我额外的力量与迅捷，让我以超乎想象的速度缩短了彼此的距离。片刻之间，我发现自己已与他们并肩奔跑。"

    old "So good of you to join us!"
    new "So good of you to join us!\n你肯加入我们，真是太好了！"

    old "I wouldn't miss it for the world."
    new "I wouldn't miss it for the world.\n无论如何我都不会错过。"

    old "As I speak, I realize how absurd it is for me to be able to form the words at all—I should be out of breath, wheezing, and yet as I run I can speak to them just as easily as if we were sitting down to talk."
    new "As I speak, I realize how absurd it is for me to be able to form the words at all—I should be out of breath, wheezing, and yet as I run I can speak to them just as easily as if we were sitting down to talk.\n说话间，我意识到自己竟能如此从容地吐字，实在荒谬——我本该气喘吁吁、上气不接下气，可奔跑之中我同他们说话，竟像坐下来交谈一样轻松。"

    old "I've never run through the mists like this. For the past month, the mists have been something that held danger. Even without the risk of encountering a ghoul, I'd be too worried about running into a large rock or a tree, or stumbling over uneven ground."
    new "I've never run through the mists like this. For the past month, the mists have been something that held danger. Even without the risk of encountering a ghoul, I'd be too worried about running into a large rock or a tree, or stumbling over uneven ground.\n我从未这样在雾中奔跑过。过去一个月里，这片雾一直是危险的所在。即便不提撞上食尸鬼的风险，我也要时刻担心撞上大石或树木，或是在崎岖不平的地面上绊倒。"

    old "Yet we seem to navigate through the mists without any sense of hesitation, as Zachary leads us somewhere."
    new "Yet we seem to navigate through the mists without any sense of hesitation, as Zachary leads us somewhere.\n然而，我们穿行于雾中，似乎没有一丝迟疑，由 Zachary 领着我们前往某处。"

    old "I look at his face, which wears a slight grin and a look of determination. I'm not sure what this vampire has in store, but whatever it is, it's bound to be an experience unlike any other."
    new "I look at his face, which wears a slight grin and a look of determination. I'm not sure what this vampire has in store, but whatever it is, it's bound to be an experience unlike any other.\n我看向他的脸，那上面挂着一丝浅笑和一副坚定的神情。我不知道这个 Vampire 心里打着什么算盘，但无论是什么，都注定是一番前所未有的经历。"

    old "For a moment, I look over my shoulder toward Grimoire, but we're already so far away that I can't even make out the shape of it, even with my apparently improved vision. Still, I feel no sadness in leaving it behind."
    new "For a moment, I look over my shoulder toward Grimoire, but we're already so far away that I can't even make out the shape of it, even with my apparently improved vision. Still, I feel no sadness in leaving it behind.\n有那么一瞬，我回头朝 Grimoire 望去，但我们已走得那么远，即便视力明显增强了，我也分辨不出它的轮廓。尽管如此，我对抛下它并不感到悲伤。"

    old "In the past month, I've met many new people, and for a moment it occurs to me that whatever adventures I embark on will probably be unknown to all of them. It may be a hundred years or more before I show myself in the world of the living, and even then, only a few individuals will ever know this new version of me."
    new "In the past month, I've met many new people, and for a moment it occurs to me that whatever adventures I embark on will probably be unknown to all of them. It may be a hundred years or more before I show myself in the world of the living, and even then, only a few individuals will ever know this new version of me.\n过去一个月里，我结识了许多新的人。有那么一瞬，我突然想到，无论我踏上怎样的冒险，他们大概都无从知晓。也许要过上一百多年，我才会再度现身于生者的世界，而即便那时，也只有寥寥数人会认识这个全新的我。"

    old "But why should I care about that? The idea of being written about in some history book, of being talked about by gossiping townsfolk or politicians in the chambers of Grimoire's council, pales in comparison to the life I'm about to live."
    new "But why should I care about that? The idea of being written about in some history book, of being talked about by gossiping townsfolk or politicians in the chambers of Grimoire's council, pales in comparison to the life I'm about to live.\n可我又何必在意这些？被写进某本史书，被爱嚼舌根的镇民或 Grimoire 议会厅里的政客们谈论——这一切，与我即将开始的生活相比，都黯然失色。"

    old "They'll never know what it's like. But I don't need for them to know."
    new "They'll never know what it's like. But I don't need for them to know.\n他们永远不会知道那是什么滋味。但我也无需他们知道。"

    old "Goodbye, to the only life I've ever known. You won't be missed."
    new "Goodbye, to the only life I've ever known. You won't be missed.\n再见了，我唯一熟悉的人生。我不会怀念你。"

    old "You know what? Maybe I will spend one last night among the living, making history."
    new "You know what? Maybe I will spend one last night among the living, making history.\n你知道吗？也许我会在生者之中度过最后一个夜晚，创造一段历史。"

    old "Just be careful not to over-extend yourself. You may be slightly more resilient than the average mortal, but you are, at your core, still just a [prace]."
    new "Just be careful not to over-extend yourself. You may be slightly more resilient than the average mortal, but you are, at your core, still just a [prace].\n只是别过度逞强。你或许比一般凡人稍显坚韧，但骨子里，你终究只是一个 [prace]。"

    old "It's time for us to part ways. Until we meet again, [protag]."
    new "It's time for us to part ways. Until we meet again, [protag].\n我们该分道扬镳了。后会有期，[protag]。"

    old "Until next time."
    new "Until next time.\n下次见。"

    old "Zachary and Valery vanish into the night, and I head back to the city."
    new "Zachary and Valery vanish into the night, and I head back to the city.\nZachary 和 Valery 消失在夜色中，我则返回城中。"

    old "Tonight, I find myself having trouble sleeping. It's not the first time this has happened. The N'Mar threat does weigh on my mind, but it's not the thing that weighs on my heart."
    new "Tonight, I find myself having trouble sleeping. It's not the first time this has happened. The N'Mar threat does weigh on my mind, but it's not the thing that weighs on my heart.\n今晚，我辗转难眠。这已不是第一次了。N'Mar 的威胁确实压在心头，但它并不是真正让我揪心的那件事。"

    old "At this point, I'm not even sure if it's right to say that it weighs on my heart. I'm sure by now, the blood that runs through my heart has mostly been replaced with the 'vitus' that Zachary spoke of. Soon, my heart may be no more. But these feelings are real."
    new "At this point, I'm not even sure if it's right to say that it weighs on my heart. I'm sure by now, the blood that runs through my heart has mostly been replaced with the 'vitus' that Zachary spoke of. Soon, my heart may be no more. But these feelings are real.\n事到如今，我甚至不确定说它压在心头是否恰当。我确信此刻，流经我心脏的血大多已被 Zachary 所说的维图斯取代。也许不久，我的心将不复存在。但这些感受是真实的。"

    old "I worry about the others. What will happen when, or if, they discover what I've done? What I've chosen to become?"
    new "I worry about the others. What will happen when, or if, they discover what I've done? What I've chosen to become?\n我担心其他人。当他们发现——或者说如果发现——我做了什么、我选择变成了什么时，会怎样？"

    old "We've spent so long fighting vampires. For them to find out that they now serve under a vampire...it seems like it would be the ultimate betrayal."
    new "We've spent so long fighting vampires. For them to find out that they now serve under a vampire...it seems like it would be the ultimate betrayal.\n我们与 Vampires 战斗了这么久。若他们发现自己如今竟听命于一个 Vampire……那似乎会是彻头彻尾的背叛。"

    old "When I accepted Zachary's offer, I was focused on myself. But when I consider the cost to others, was it really worth the price?"
    new "When I accepted Zachary's offer, I was focused on myself. But when I consider the cost to others, was it really worth the price?\n当初接受 Zachary 的提议时，我只顾着自己。可当我想到这会给他人带来的代价时，它真的值这个价吗？"

    old "These people have pledged loyalty to me, and I can no longer think of them as pawns, as a simple means to an end."
    new "These people have pledged loyalty to me, and I can no longer think of them as pawns, as a simple means to an end.\n这些人曾向我宣誓效忠，我不能再把他们当作棋子，当作达成目的的简单工具。"

    old "Respect is a two-way street: if I want them to respect me, then I must respect them. Do I respect them enough to let them know of what I've become?"
    new "Respect is a two-way street: if I want them to respect me, then I must respect them. Do I respect them enough to let them know of what I've become?\n尊重是相互的：若我想让他们尊重我，就必须尊重他们。我是否足够尊重他们，以至于愿意让他们知道我变成了什么？"

    old "The day soon approaches when this reveal may be unavoidable."
    new "The day soon approaches when this reveal may be unavoidable.\n真相大白、无从回避的那一天，正日益临近。"

    old "I worry about [chosen_romance]. What will happen when [che] finds out what I have done? That I've chosen to become a vampire?"
    new "I worry about [chosen_romance]. What will happen when [che] finds out what I have done? That I've chosen to become a vampire?\n我担心 [chosen_romance]。当 [che] 发现我所做的一切、发现我选择成为 Vampire 时，会怎样？"

    old "Should I tell [chim]? No, I can't tell [chim] now. Not before the final assault on N'Mar, it could compromise the whole operation."
    new "Should I tell [chim]? No, I can't tell [chim] now. Not before the final assault on N'Mar, it could compromise the whole operation.\n我应该告诉 [chim] 吗？不，现在我不能告诉 [chim]。在对 N'Mar 的最后总攻之前不行，那可能危及整个行动。"

    old "But what will happen when I finally tell [chim]? I am not sure if [che] will still want to be with me."
    new "But what will happen when I finally tell [chim]? I am not sure if [che] will still want to be with me.\n但当我最终告诉 [chim] 时会怎样？我不确定 [che] 是否还愿意和我在一起。"

    old "I feel like I'm betraying [chim] by not telling [chosen_romance] the truth. But I don't know what to do either."
    new "I feel like I'm betraying [chim] by not telling [chosen_romance] the truth. But I don't know what to do either.\n不向 [chosen_romance] 说出真相，让我觉得自己在背叛 [chim]。但我也不知道该怎么办。"

    old "Damn it! I accepted Zachary's deal, but the costs are greater than I considered. At the time, I didn't feel so close to [chosen_romance]. I only saw [chim] as friend, as a worthy ally, and nothing more. I would have never imagined to fall in love with [chim]."
    new "Damn it! I accepted Zachary's deal, but the costs are greater than I considered. At the time, I didn't feel so close to [chosen_romance]. I only saw [chim] as friend, as a worthy ally, and nothing more. I would have never imagined to fall in love with [chim].\n该死！我接受了 Zachary 的交易，代价却比我想象的更重。当时我还不觉得与 [chosen_romance] 那么亲近。我只把 [chim] 当作朋友、当作值得信赖的盟友，仅此而已。我从没想过自己会爱上 [chim]。"

    old "I feel like I'm betraying both Enok and Sylrissa at the same time by not telling them the truth. But I don't know what to do either."
    new "I feel like I'm betraying both Enok and Sylrissa at the same time by not telling them the truth. But I don't know what to do either.\n同时瞒着 Enok 和 Sylrissa 不说出真相，让我觉得自己同时背叛了他们两个。但我也不知道该怎么办。"

    old "Damn it! I accepted Zachary's deal, but the costs are greater than I considered. At the time, I didn't feel so close to [chosen_romance]. I only saw them as friends, as worthy allies, and nothing more. I would have never imagined to fall in love with them."
    new "Damn it! I accepted Zachary's deal, but the costs are greater than I considered. At the time, I didn't feel so close to [chosen_romance]. I only saw them as friends, as worthy allies, and nothing more. I would have never imagined to fall in love with them.\n该死！我接受了 Zachary 的交易，代价却比我想象的更重。当时我还不觉得与 [chosen_romance] 那么亲近。我只把他们当作朋友、当作值得信赖的盟友，仅此而已。我从没想过自己会爱上他们。"

    old "I only hope that when this is over and I become...a vampire, there will still be a way to stay together, a way or another."
    new "I only hope that when this is over and I become...a vampire, there will still be a way to stay together, a way or another.\n我只希望当这一切结束、我变成……一个 Vampire 之后，我们仍能找到一种方式长相厮守，无论以何种方式。"

    old "The night before the battle, I feel my body...change. When I look down at my hands, I see the hands of a [prace]. But it's almost as if I'm surprised to see a [prace]'s hands, as opposed to the pale flesh of a vampire."
    new "The night before the battle, I feel my body...change. When I look down at my hands, I see the hands of a [prace]. But it's almost as if I'm surprised to see a [prace]'s hands, as opposed to the pale flesh of a vampire.\n决战前夜，我感到自己的身体……在变化。我低头看自己的双手，看到一双 [prace] 的手。可我几乎感到惊讶，映入眼帘的竟是一双 [prace] 的手，而非 Vampire 苍白的肌肤。"

    old "I feel my teeth. Still [prace] teeth, but it's as if my body is already prepared to be something else. It's as if this [prace] is some kind of 'other' form, and my true self is about to be born."
    new "I feel my teeth. Still [prace] teeth, but it's as if my body is already prepared to be something else. It's as if this [prace] is some kind of 'other' form, and my true self is about to be born.\n我摸摸自己的牙齿。仍是 [prace] 的牙齿，但仿佛我的身体已经准备好变成别的什么。仿佛这个 [prace] 的形态只是某种他物，而我真正的自我即将诞生。"

    old "Zachary told me that the vitus would eventually overwhelm the blood in my veins. It was a transformation that would take a month to complete, and that was one moon ago. I have no inkling of what is happening in my body, yet it feels like the transformation could occur at any moment. Is that feeling in the pit of my stomach the feeling of something changing within me, or mere anxiety?"
    new "Zachary told me that the vitus would eventually overwhelm the blood in my veins. It was a transformation that would take a month to complete, and that was one moon ago. I have no inkling of what is happening in my body, yet it feels like the transformation could occur at any moment. Is that feeling in the pit of my stomach the feeling of something changing within me, or mere anxiety?\nZachary 告诉过我，维图斯终将压过我血管中的血液。那场转化需要一个月才能完成，而那已是一个月前的事了。我对体内正在发生的一切毫无头绪，却感觉转化随时可能发生。我心底那股感觉，究竟是体内某种东西在改变的征兆，还是仅仅只是焦虑？"

    old "For my allies to see me transform before their very eyes, in the heat of battle, would be quite a disaster. No matter how accepting they might be of my choice, finding out in the midst of a conflict would be a difficult time for them to learn it."
    new "For my allies to see me transform before their very eyes, in the heat of battle, would be quite a disaster. No matter how accepting they might be of my choice, finding out in the midst of a conflict would be a difficult time for them to learn it.\n若我的盟友在激战之中、众目睽睽之下亲眼目睹我转化，那将是场十足的灾难。无论他们对我的选择多么包容，在战事正酣之际得知此事，对他们来说都是个难以接受的时刻。"

    old "And if it happened at an inopportune moment, they might mistakenly believe me to be possessed by the enemy. If we went in to confront the vampires of N'Mar, and I immediately began transforming into a vampire before their very eyes, what other conclusion could they draw?"
    new "And if it happened at an inopportune moment, they might mistakenly believe me to be possessed by the enemy. If we went in to confront the vampires of N'Mar, and I immediately began transforming into a vampire before their very eyes, what other conclusion could they draw?\n而若它发生在不凑巧的关头，他们或许会误以为我被敌人附了身。倘若我们前去对抗 N'Mar 的 Vampires，我却在众人眼前立刻开始变成 Vampire，他们又能得出什么别的结论？"

    old "An explanation seems like the most prudent course of action. And, prudence aside, it's what I owe them. They deserve to know who and what it is that I truly am, before they follow me into battle for the last time."
    new "An explanation seems like the most prudent course of action. And, prudence aside, it's what I owe them. They deserve to know who and what it is that I truly am, before they follow me into battle for the last time.\n向他们解释，似乎是最稳妥的做法。而且抛开稳妥不谈，这也是我欠他们的。在他们最后一次随我上战场之前，他们有权知道我究竟是谁、是什么。"

    old "I can only hope that they understand my reasons for doing what I did. Perhaps this is the ultimate test of their trust in me."
    new "I can only hope that they understand my reasons for doing what I did. Perhaps this is the ultimate test of their trust in me.\n我只能希望他们理解我这么做的理由。也许，这是对他们对我信任的终极考验。"

    old "I asked you to come here tonight to talk, but it's not only about the final assault on N'Mar. There's something vital I need to share with you."
    new "I asked you to come here tonight to talk, but it's not only about the final assault on N'Mar. There's something vital I need to share with you.\n我请你们今晚前来谈话，但内容不止是关于对 N'Mar 的最后总攻。有件至关重要的事，我必须告诉你们。"

    old "What is it? From the tone of your voice and the look on your face, it looks serious."
    new "What is it? From the tone of your voice and the look on your face, it looks serious.\n什么事？从你的语气和神情来看，似乎很严重。"

    old "You all remember the battle of Grimoire. Before the battle, I was visited upon by two vampires. Not vampires such as the one's we've battled, mind you. Vampires who consider those dwelling in castle N'Mar as rivals. Zachary and Valery are their names."
    new "You all remember the battle of Grimoire. Before the battle, I was visited upon by two vampires. Not vampires such as the one's we've battled, mind you. Vampires who consider those dwelling in castle N'Mar as rivals. Zachary and Valery are their names.\n你们都记得 Grimoire 之战。开战前，有两个 Vampires 来找过我。注意，他们可不是我们一直交战的那种 Vampires。他们视居住在 N'Mar 城堡里的那些人为对手。他们名叫 Zachary 和 Valery。"

    old "My companions look at me with stunned silence. For them to hear that their leader has been consorting with vampires is one thing, but the bitter truth I must reveal is far, far more grave."
    new "My companions look at me with stunned silence. For them to hear that their leader has been consorting with vampires is one thing, but the bitter truth I must reveal is far, far more grave.\n我的同伴们震惊地望着我，一片沉默。听说自己的领袖一直与 Vampires 往来已够让他们吃惊，但我必须道出的苦痛真相，还要严重得多得多。"

    old "I actually met them way before that night, some of you already know about it. I was only vague about the details."
    new "I actually met them way before that night, some of you already know about it. I was only vague about the details.\n其实早在那一夜之前，我就见过他们了，你们中有些人已经知道。只是我一直对细节含糊其辞。"

    old "Zachary and Valery have their own reasons for aiding me—for aiding us—in our mission to defeat the vampires of N'Mar."
    new "Zachary and Valery have their own reasons for aiding me—for aiding us—in our mission to defeat the vampires of N'Mar.\nZachary 和 Valery 帮助我们——帮助我们——完成击败 N'Mar Vampires 的使命，自有他们的理由。"

    old "These two vampires made me an offer. They told me that they could make me a vampire, a being with greater strength, greater powers. A greater capability to defeat our enemies. And I accepted their offer."
    new "These two vampires made me an offer. They told me that they could make me a vampire, a being with greater strength, greater powers. A greater capability to defeat our enemies. And I accepted their offer.\n这两个 Vampires 向我提出一个条件。他们说，他们能把我变成 Vampire，一个拥有更强力量、更强能力的生灵，一个更能击败我们敌人的存在。而我接受了他们的提议。"

    old "I expect to hear murmurs open delivering this revelation. Instead, I hear only a few gasps. Some of their mouths are agape in shock, but they say nothing."
    new "I expect to hear murmurs open delivering this revelation. Instead, I hear only a few gasps. Some of their mouths are agape in shock, but they say nothing.\n我本以为道出这真相时，会听到一片窃窃私语。可我却只听到几声倒抽冷气。有些人惊得张大了嘴，却一言不发。"

    old "I imagine that some of you may be thinking that perhaps these vampires were lying to me. Perhaps this was some sort of trap. Believe me, this possibility occurred to me as well."
    new "I imagine that some of you may be thinking that perhaps these vampires were lying to me. Perhaps this was some sort of trap. Believe me, this possibility occurred to me as well.\n我想，你们中有些人或许会认为，那些 Vampires 是在骗我，也许这根本是个陷阱。相信我，我自己也想过这种可能。"

    old "Even now, I'm not sure that I fully trust Zachary and Valery. But every step of this journey that we've taken together has been one of calculated risks. Even if this might be a trap, the benefits seemed to great to pass up."
    new "Even now, I'm not sure that I fully trust Zachary and Valery. But every step of this journey that we've taken together has been one of calculated risks. Even if this might be a trap, the benefits seemed to great to pass up.\n即便现在，我也不确定自己是否完全信任 Zachary 和 Valery。但我们共同走过的这段旅程，每一步都伴随着精打细算的风险。就算这可能是陷阱，其好处也实在太诱人，令人难以拒绝。"

    old "I saw an opportunity to gain an advantage in our fight against N'Mar's vampires, and I took it. So on that night, hours before the undead came knocking at the Grimoire city gates, I allowed them to give me a bite which started the process."
    new "I saw an opportunity to gain an advantage in our fight against N'Mar's vampires, and I took it. So on that night, hours before the undead came knocking at the Grimoire city gates, I allowed them to give me a bite which started the process.\n我看到一个机会，能在与 N'Mar Vampires 的战斗中占得先机，便抓住了它。于是在那一夜，亡灵敲响 Grimoire 城门前的几个小时，我让他们咬了我一口，由此开启了这一过程。"

    old "The changes in me were gradual. You may have already noticed some of them yourselves. I've become physically sturdier and more resilient to damage. My powers have grown over time, and I've gained abiliities that allow me to fight better than before."
    new "The changes in me were gradual. You may have already noticed some of them yourselves. I've become physically sturdier and more resilient to damage. My powers have grown over time, and I've gained abiliities that allow me to fight better than before.\n我的变化是渐进的。你们中也许有人已经察觉到了一些。我的体格变得更结实，更能承受伤害。我的力量随时间增长，也获得了让我比以前更能战斗的能力。"

    old "The transformation is not yet complete, but it may be imminent."
    new "The transformation is not yet complete, but it may be imminent.\n转化尚未完成，但或许已迫在眉睫。"

    old "I can tell from looking at each of you that this revelation comes as a shock. I understand how wrong this must seem to some of you: how I could choose to become a vampire myself, when vampires are our enemies. I can only say that I had my reasons. But I fully understand if you disagree with those reasons."
    new "I can tell from looking at each of you that this revelation comes as a shock. I understand how wrong this must seem to some of you: how I could choose to become a vampire myself, when vampires are our enemies. I can only say that I had my reasons. But I fully understand if you disagree with those reasons.\n从你们每个人的神情，我看得出这真相令你们震惊。我理解这在你们有些人看来有多离谱：当 Vampires 是我们的敌人时，我怎能选择自己变成 Vampire。我只能说，我有我的理由。但若你们不认同那些理由，我完全理解。"

    old "If you want to talk, I am here. Please, each of you, take the time to think upon this. Take as much time as you need. I'll personally meet with each of you in turn when you are ready to give me your thoughts."
    new "If you want to talk, I am here. Please, each of you, take the time to think upon this. Take as much time as you need. I'll personally meet with each of you in turn when you are ready to give me your thoughts.\n若你们想谈谈，我就在这里。请你们每个人都花时间好好想想。想多久都行。等你们准备好告诉我你们的想法时，我会逐一与你们单独见面。"

    old "You've taken an incredible step, [protag]. You've entered a world that you can never leave. I hope you thought about it carefully, [protag]."
    new "You've taken an incredible step, [protag]. You've entered a world that you can never leave. I hope you thought about it carefully, [protag].\n你迈出了惊人一步，[protag]。你踏入了一个再也无法离开的世界。我希望你经过了慎重考虑，[protag]。"

    old "While I don't like you keeping this secret from us, I must say that I had noticed your battle skills were greatly improved in the recent times. If this choice can help us win this war, that's fine by me."
    new "While I don't like you keeping this secret from us, I must say that I had noticed your battle skills were greatly improved in the recent times. If this choice can help us win this war, that's fine by me.\n虽然我不喜欢你把这件事瞒着我们，但我必须承认，我注意到近来你的战斗本领大有长进。如果这个选择能帮我们打赢这场战争，那我没意见。"

    old "I do hope you'll forgive me if I find myself a bit more reluctant to turn my back on you from now on. It's unavoidable."
    new "I do hope you'll forgive me if I find myself a bit more reluctant to turn my back on you from now on. It's unavoidable.\n从今往后，若我发现自己在背向你时会多几分迟疑，还望你见谅。这也在所难免。"

    old "[protag], I have no objection to what you did."
    new "[protag], I have no objection to what you did.\n[protag]，我不反对你所做的事。"

    old "Yes. While I would have preferred if you didn't, I know a leader sometimes needs to sacrifice [himher]self in order to achieve victory, to achieve peace. That's what you did: you decided that the sacrifice of one was worth to save many. You have my respect for this."
    new "Yes. While I would have preferred if you didn't, I know a leader sometimes needs to sacrifice [himher]self in order to achieve victory, to achieve peace. That's what you did: you decided that the sacrifice of one was worth to save many. You have my respect for this.\n是的。虽说我更希望你没有这么做，但我知道，领袖有时需要牺牲 [himher]self，才能赢得胜利、赢得和平。你正是这么做的：你认定牺牲一人，值得拯救众人。为此我敬重你。"

    old "That said, if you turned into a vampire and you started being a threat to me or my companions... I would have no hesitation to strike you down, [protag]."
    new "That said, if you turned into a vampire and you started being a threat to me or my companions... I would have no hesitation to strike you down, [protag].\n话虽如此，若你变成 Vampire 后开始威胁到我或我的同伴……我会毫不犹豫地将你击倒，[protag]。"

    old "Yes, I understand Larik. Let's hope it doesn't come to that."
    new "Yes, I understand Larik. Let's hope it doesn't come to that.\n是的，我明白，Larik。但愿不会走到那一步。"

    old "Hmpf. I really didn't expect this from you."
    new "Hmpf. I really didn't expect this from you.\n哼。我真没料到你会做出这种事。"

    old "Have I disappointed you, Galan?"
    new "Have I disappointed you, Galan?\n我让你失望了吗，Galan？"

    old "A bit. Though, considering who I am, what I did in the past... I'm the last one who can judge you for your choices, [protag]."
    new "A bit. Though, considering who I am, what I did in the past... I'm the last one who can judge you for your choices, [protag].\n有一点。不过，想想我是谁、我过去做过什么……我才是最没资格评判你选择的人，[protag]。"

    old "I only hope that it was really worth it. I guess we'll see in the coming battle tomorrow."
    new "I only hope that it was really worth it. I guess we'll see in the coming battle tomorrow.\n我只希望这一切真的值得。我想，明天的大战自会揭晓。"

    old "So you'll be on my side, Galan?"
    new "So you'll be on my side, Galan?\n那么你会站在我这边，Galan？"

    old "You bet. I wouldn't miss it for anything in the world."
    new "You bet. I wouldn't miss it for anything in the world.\n那当然。世上没什么能让我错过它。"

    old "Dasyra approaches me, with a sad face, and wet eyes. Is she crying?"
    new "Dasyra approaches me, with a sad face, and wet eyes. Is she crying?\nDasyra 走到我面前，神情哀伤，眼眶湿润。她哭了吗？"

    old "Dasyra, you don't need to worry. I won't be a threat for you, I promise."
    new "Dasyra, you don't need to worry. I won't be a threat for you, I promise.\nDasyra，你不必担心。我不会威胁到你，我保证。"

    old "You don't understand, [protag]. I'm sad for you. For what you'll become after this is over. What will happen to you? You'll end up like one of them, hunted by the law, always hiding in the darkness of the night. What kind of life is that?"
    new "You don't understand, [protag]. I'm sad for you. For what you'll become after this is over. What will happen to you? You'll end up like one of them, hunted by the law, always hiding in the darkness of the night. What kind of life is that?\n你不明白，[protag]。我是为你难过。为这一切结束后你将变成的模样而难过。你会怎样呢？你会沦落到和他们一样，被法律追捕，永远躲藏在黑夜的阴影里。那算是什么样的生活？"

    old "A life I chose to live to save you all."
    new "A life I chose to live to save you all.\n为了拯救你们所有人，我选择去过的一种生活。"

    old "I will be on your side tomorrow, [protag]. You can count on me."
    new "I will be on your side tomorrow, [protag]. You can count on me.\n明天我会站在你这边，[protag]。你可以信赖我。"

    old "What have you done, [protag]? You embraced the darkness, the same darkness that we're fighting!?"
    new "What have you done, [protag]? You embraced the darkness, the same darkness that we're fighting!?\n你都做了什么，[protag]？你拥抱了黑暗，正是我们一直在与之战斗的那片黑暗！？"

    old "Yes, I embraced it to become as strong as our enemies! It was an opportunity given to me, and I chose to take it!"
    new "Yes, I embraced it to become as strong as our enemies! It was an opportunity given to me, and I chose to take it!\n没错，我拥抱了它，只为变得和我们的敌人一样强大！那是一个送到我面前的机会，而我选择抓住它！"

    old "I'm only asking you to follow me until the end of our mission. Nothing else."
    new "I'm only asking you to follow me until the end of our mission. Nothing else.\n我只求你跟随我，直到我们使命的终点。仅此而已。"

    old "How could you do this to me!? You... you're a monster!"
    new "How could you do this to me!? You... you're a monster!\n你怎么能这样对我！？你……你是个怪物！"

    old "Nuala, I did what I thought was best—"
    new "Nuala, I did what I thought was best—\nNuala，我只是做了我认为最该做的事——"

    old "No more! I won't listen to you anymore! I'm done with this! I'm heading back to the desert!"
    new "No more! I won't listen to you anymore! I'm done with this! I'm heading back to the desert!\n够了！我再也不要听你说了！我受够了！我要回沙漠去了！"

    old "I don't care. I don't want to stay close to [himher] a minute longer!"
    new "I don't care. I don't want to stay close to [himher] a minute longer!\n我不管。我一分钟都不想再待在 [himher] 身边！"

    old "I get close to Nuala and I hug her. She tries to fight back at first by punching my chest, but then she gives up and starts crying, moving her head near mine."
    new "I get close to Nuala and I hug her. She tries to fight back at first by punching my chest, but then she gives up and starts crying, moving her head near mine.\n我走近 Nuala，将她拥入怀中。起初她挥拳捶打我的胸口试图挣扎，但随后放弃了，放声哭了起来，把头靠向我。"

    old "What about us? The moments that we shared together? The many moments I hoped we would continue to share? What will happen once you turn into...oh god. Into a vampire?!"
    new "What about us? The moments that we shared together? The many moments I hoped we would continue to share? What will happen once you turn into...oh god. Into a vampire?!\n那我们呢？我们曾共同度过的那些时光呢？我原以为还能继续共度的那么多时光呢？等你变成……天哪，变成一个 Vampire 之后，会怎样？！"

    old "I will still be myself. I will learn to control it. We can go hunt animals together. I won't feed from people. And I won't leave you alone, Nuala."
    new "I will still be myself. I will learn to control it. We can go hunt animals together. I won't feed from people. And I won't leave you alone, Nuala.\n我仍会是我自己。我会学着控制它。我们可以一起去猎捕动物。我不会以人为食。而且我也不会抛下你，Nuala。"

    old "I... I'm not sure this will work. I need some time to think."
    new "I... I'm not sure this will work. I need some time to think.\n我……我不确定这样行不行。我需要些时间想想。"

    old "She pushes me away, and runs out of the room, tears falling from her eyes."
    new "She pushes me away, and runs out of the room, tears falling from her eyes.\n她一把推开我，跑出了房间，泪水从她眼中滑落。"

    old "Don't worry [protag]. I know her. She will be on our side tomorrow's night. After that though... I don't know."
    new "Don't worry [protag]. I know her. She will be on our side tomorrow's night. After that though... I don't know.\n别担心，[protag]。我了解她。明晚她会站在我们这边。不过在那之后……我就不知道了。"

    old "I... will do it. Then, I don't want to see you again."
    new "I... will do it. Then, I don't want to see you again.\n我……会照做的。只是之后，我不想再见到你。"

    old "I'm sorry. I'm sorry to you all. I just...this is wrong. I don't want to be part of this anymore. Go ahead without me."
    new "I'm sorry. I'm sorry to you all. I just...this is wrong. I don't want to be part of this anymore. Go ahead without me.\n对不起。我对你们所有人都很抱歉。我只是……这是不对的。我不想再参与这件事了。没有我，你们继续吧。"

    old "Nuala runs out of the room, like if she saw already a monster in me and wanted to get away from me as fast as possible. I guess we'll have to do without her."
    new "Nuala runs out of the room, like if she saw already a monster in me and wanted to get away from me as fast as possible. I guess we'll have to do without her.\nNuala 跑出房间，仿佛她早已在我身上看到了一个怪物，只想尽快逃离。我想，我们只能没有她地上路了。"

    old "So, finally [protag] reveals [himher]self for what [heshe] really is: an egoist."
    new "So, finally [protag] reveals [himher]self for what [heshe] really is: an egoist.\n那么，[protag] 终于露出了 [himher]self 的真面目：[heshe] 其实是个自私自利的人。"

    old "How is it what I've done selfish?"
    new "How is it what I've done selfish?\n我所做的一切，怎么算自私了？"

    old "You're even asking?! After what has been between us? You threw everything away! We had a whole life ahead of us and you... you just threw it away."
    new "You're even asking?! After what has been between us? You threw everything away! We had a whole life ahead of us and you... you just threw it away.\n你竟然还问？！在我们经历了那么多之后？你把一切都毁了！我们本有着大好人生在前方，而你……你却把它一把扔掉了。"

    old "Jasper's gaze falls on the ground. He really looks broken."
    new "Jasper's gaze falls on the ground. He really looks broken.\nJasper 的目光垂向地面。他看起来真的心碎欲绝。"

    old "Jasper. I still love you. The fact that shortly I'll become...something else, might be troubling. I understand. But nothing will ever change this truth: that I love you."
    new "Jasper. I still love you. The fact that shortly I'll become...something else, might be troubling. I understand. But nothing will ever change this truth: that I love you.\nJasper，我仍然爱你。不久后我将变成……别的什么，这或许令人不安，我明白。但有一件事永远不会改变：我爱你。"

    old "Then why did you do this!"
    new "Then why did you do this!\n那你为什么还要这么做！"

    old "I did it to ensure we could win. That we could have a future together. Even this meant I would live this future as a vampire myself."
    new "I did it to ensure we could win. That we could have a future together. Even this meant I would live this future as a vampire myself.\n我这么做，是为了确保我们能赢，确保我们能一起拥有未来。即便这意味着，我将以 Vampire 之身去过这段未来。"

    old "You... you might be right, but still..."
    new "You... you might be right, but still...\n你……你也许是对的，但……"

    old "I move closer to him and put a finger on his mouth, silencing him. He looks at me, with a sad face, but then he nods and says:"
    new "I move closer to him and put a finger on his mouth, silencing him. He looks at me, with a sad face, but then he nods and says:\n我走近他，把一根手指按在他唇上，示意他噤声。他看着我，神情哀伤，但随即点点头，说道："

    old "I will join you on this mission, my love. That's all I can say for now."
    new "I will join you on this mission, my love. That's all I can say for now.\n我会加入这次行动，我的爱人。眼下我只能说这么多。"

    old "You didn't think about us? What would happen if you suddenly turned while we are on mission?"
    new "You didn't think about us? What would happen if you suddenly turned while we are on mission?\n你就没为我们想想吗？要是在执行任务途中你突然转化了，该怎么办？"

    old "They assured me that it wouldn't happen until the full moon was upon us."
    new "They assured me that it wouldn't happen until the full moon was upon us.\n他们向我保证，不到满月降临，是不会发生的。"

    old "Yeah, like vampires can be trusted. Pah, [protag] sometimes I wonder how it is that the council put so much trust on you, when clearly you're such an ingenuous person. Vampires are liars."
    new "Yeah, like vampires can be trusted. Pah, [protag] sometimes I wonder how it is that the council put so much trust on you, when clearly you're such an ingenuous person. Vampires are liars.\n是啊，说得好像 Vampires 可以信任似的。呸，[protag]，有时候我真纳闷，议会怎么会如此信任你，明明你就是个这么天真的人。Vampires 都是骗子。"

    old "Are you coming or not?"
    new "Are you coming or not?\n你到底来不来？"

    old "I am. But only because I want to make sure that this threat is stopped, once for all. I don't think we'll see each other after this."
    new "I am. But only because I want to make sure that this threat is stopped, once for all. I don't think we'll see each other after this.\n我去。但只是为了确保这威胁被一劳永逸地铲除。我想，此事过后我们不会再见。"

    old "You know what? I won't. You didn't trust us, so why I should trust you? Sorry, but you'll have to do it without me. I'm getting back to my ship. I'll be safe there, no matter what happens tomorrow."
    new "You know what? I won't. You didn't trust us, so why I should trust you? Sorry, but you'll have to do it without me. I'm getting back to my ship. I'll be safe there, no matter what happens tomorrow.\n你知道吗？我不去了。你都不信任我们，我又凭什么信任你？抱歉，你们得在没有我的情况下去了。我要回我的船上去。不管明天发生什么，我在那里都会是安全的。"

    old "Leena looks at me in the eyes, her light blue eyes piercing through me like a spear, as if she wanted to understand what I am really thinking, what's going on in my head. I wish I could know what's she thinking as well."
    new "Leena looks at me in the eyes, her light blue eyes piercing through me like a spear, as if she wanted to understand what I am really thinking, what's going on in my head. I wish I could know what's she thinking as well.\nLeena 直视着我的双眼，她浅蓝色的眼眸如长矛般穿透我，仿佛想弄明白我究竟在想什么、我脑中到底有什么。我也希望能知道她在想什么。"

    old "You're... silent. What do you think? I mean, about the fact that you'll be with me?"
    new "You're... silent. What do you think? I mean, about the fact that you'll be with me?\n你……一直沉默。你在想什么？我是说，关于你将要和我在一起这件事。"

    old "When I walked into this room, I supposed you wanted to warn us that this could have been some kind of suicide mission. But I was ready. I would have given my life for you, [protag]."
    new "When I walked into this room, I supposed you wanted to warn us that this could have been some kind of suicide mission. But I was ready. I would have given my life for you, [protag].\n我走进这房间时，本猜想你是想警告我们，这可能是某种自杀式任务。但我已经准备好了。我原愿为你献出生命，[protag]。"

    old "This? This I was unprepared for. I don't even know what to think."
    new "This? This I was unprepared for. I don't even know what to think.\n这个？这个我却毫无准备。我甚至不知道该作何感想。"

    old "You hate me?"
    new "You hate me?\n你恨我吗？"

    old "I don't. But...I can't keep but wondering: what future do we have now?"
    new "I don't. But...I can't keep but wondering: what future do we have now?\n我不恨。但……我仍忍不住想：我们现在还有什么未来可言？"

    old "I thought to bring you with me at the Citadel. Karen would have gladly accepted you. I could have married you. I imagined how could have been the rest of my life with you."
    new "I thought to bring you with me at the Citadel. Karen would have gladly accepted you. I could have married you. I imagined how could have been the rest of my life with you.\n我本想着带你一起去 Citadel。Karen 一定会欣然接纳你。我本可以娶你。我甚至想象过与你共度余生的样子。"

    old "Now? I can't imagine anything. All I see after tomorrow's night is darkness."
    new "Now? I can't imagine anything. All I see after tomorrow's night is darkness.\n现在？我什么也想象不出了。明晚之后，我眼前只有一片黑暗。"

    old "Her words hurt, but deep in my heart I think that she's right."
    new "Her words hurt, but deep in my heart I think that she's right.\n她的话刺痛了我，但在我内心深处，我想她说得对。"

    old "She comes near me and takes my hand."
    new "She comes near me and takes my hand.\n她走近我，握住我的手。"

    old "I will fight with you tomorrow, [protag]. After that? I guess we'll need to see what happens to you."
    new "I will fight with you tomorrow, [protag]. After that? I guess we'll need to see what happens to you.\n明天我会与你并肩作战，[protag]。在那之后？我想我们得看看你会变成什么样。"

    old "I will. But make no mistake, [protag]: I'm only coming to ensure that the evil lurking in N'Mar is defeated once and for all. After that, you better not try to even come close the amazon territory. You'll be killed on sight."
    new "I will. But make no mistake, [protag]: I'm only coming to ensure that the evil lurking in N'Mar is defeated once and for all. After that, you better not try to even come close the amazon territory. You'll be killed on sight.\n我会去的。但别会错意，[protag]：我来，只为确保潜伏在 N'Mar 的邪恶被一劳永逸地铲除。在那之后，你最好连靠近 Amazon 领地都别想。一旦现身，格杀勿论。"

    old "I won't. If you told me sooner, maybe I could have forgiven you. But you kept this hidden for so long. I can't trust you anymore. I will also inform queen Karen about this. You're a threat to the amazons now: don't even try to come closer to our territory again."
    new "I won't. If you told me sooner, maybe I could have forgiven you. But you kept this hidden for so long. I can't trust you anymore. I will also inform queen Karen about this. You're a threat to the amazons now: don't even try to come closer to our territory again.\n我不会的。你若早点告诉我，也许我还能原谅你。可你把这件事藏了这么久。我再也无法信任你了。我也会把此事禀告 Karen 女王。如今你对 Amazons 是个威胁：别再试图靠近我们的领地了。"

    old "She leaves the room, stomping her feet. She really looked angry at me."
    new "She leaves the room, stomping her feet. She really looked angry at me.\n她跺着脚离开了房间。她看上去真的对我怒不可遏。"

    old "What have you done, [protag]? This is wrong!"
    new "What have you done, [protag]? This is wrong!\n你都做了什么，[protag]？这是错的！"

    old "Of all people, I thought you could be the one who would understand what I did more than others, Vaeril!"
    new "Of all people, I thought you could be the one who would understand what I did more than others, Vaeril!\n在所有人当中，我本以为你会是比别人更能理解我所作所为的那一个，Vaeril！"

    old "How? Because I am a fallen druid? I didn't chose this life. You deliberately chose it! You chose to turn yourself into a monster. For what?"
    new "How? Because I am a fallen druid? I didn't chose this life. You deliberately chose it! You chose to turn yourself into a monster. For what?\n凭什么？就因为我是一个堕落的德鲁伊？我并没有选择这样的生活。而你是故意选择的！你选择把自己变成怪物。为了什么？"

    old "To make sure we would win this battle, Vaeril! That's why!"
    new "To make sure we would win this battle, Vaeril! That's why!\n是为了确保我们能打赢这场仗，Vaeril！就是这个原因！"

    old "The battle, yes. The mission. The council. They were always your priorities, didn't they? I was never one."
    new "The battle, yes. The mission. The council. They were always your priorities, didn't they? I was never one.\n战斗，没错。使命。议会。这些永远是你的优先考虑，不是吗？我却从来都不是其中之一。"

    old "No! Don't say this, you know it's not true, Vaeril. I still care about you."
    new "No! Don't say this, you know it's not true, Vaeril. I still care about you.\n不！别这么说，你知道这不是真的，Vaeril。我依然在乎你。"

    old "Then why you kept such a secret hidden from me for so long, eh?"
    new "Then why you kept such a secret hidden from me for so long, eh?\n那你为什么把这样一个秘密瞒了我这么久，嗯？"

    old "I... I didn't know what you'd say... and maybe if you told the others... there was too much at stake..."
    new "I... I didn't know what you'd say... and maybe if you told the others... there was too much at stake...\n我……我不知道你会怎么说……而且万一你告诉了其他人……事关重大，牵扯太多了……"

    old "I will come to N'Mar tomorrow and make sure you don't harm anyone, in case you turn. That's it."
    new "I will come to N'Mar tomorrow and make sure you don't harm anyone, in case you turn. That's it.\n明天我会去 N'Mar，确保你万一转化，不会伤害任何人。仅此而已。"

    old "He looks at me in the eyes. I don't see hate, but his expression is fierce. He probably isn't ready to forgive me for what I've done."
    new "He looks at me in the eyes. I don't see hate, but his expression is fierce. He probably isn't ready to forgive me for what I've done.\n他注视着我的眼睛。我看不到恨意，但他的神情十分凶狠。他大概还没准备好原谅我的所作所为。"

    old "Thank you, Vaeril. I hope that won't be the last time we meet, though."
    new "Thank you, Vaeril. I hope that won't be the last time we meet, though.\n谢谢你，Vaeril。不过，我希望那不是我们最后一次相见。"

    old "I... I don't want to..."
    new "I... I don't want to...\n我……我不想……"

    old "He doesn't finish the phrase, and leaves the room. I hope we can still be together after all of this."
    new "He doesn't finish the phrase, and leaves the room. I hope we can still be together after all of this.\n他没有把话说完，便离开了房间。我希望这一切过后，我们仍能在一起。"

    old "Well, then you better make sure we'll win it. Because this will be the last time that you and I fight together, understood?"
    new "Well, then you better make sure we'll win it. Because this will be the last time that you and I fight together, understood?\n那么，你最好确保我们能赢下这一仗。因为这将是你我最后一次并肩作战，明白吗？"

    old "Understood."
    new "Understood.\n明白。"

    old "Oh, [protag]. How foolish you are. Don't you see that by yielding to them, you have already lost the battle? You've already become one of them, even if technically you're still [prace]."
    new "Oh, [protag]. How foolish you are. Don't you see that by yielding to them, you have already lost the battle? You've already become one of them, even if technically you're still [prace].\n哦，[protag]。你多么愚蠢啊。难道你看不出，一旦向他们屈服，你就已经输了这场战斗吗？即便严格说来你仍是个 [prace]，可你早已成了他们中的一员。"

    old "I am done following you, [protag]. Don't expect me to help you tomorrow night."
    new "I am done following you, [protag]. Don't expect me to help you tomorrow night.\n我不再追随你了，[protag]。别指望明晚我会帮你。"

    old "[protag]...I was thinking about a joke to make, but I can't find any."
    new "[protag]...I was thinking about a joke to make, but I can't find any.\n[protag]……我本想说个笑话，可一个也找不出来。"

    old "I guess this was too much even for you, right?"
    new "I guess this was too much even for you, right?\n我想，这对你来说也太过了，对吧？"

    old "I would be lying if I said that I am not shocked by the news. However, who am I to judge you? Most people on Aravorn consider us nagas bloodthirsty monsters. Yet, not all of us are."
    new "I would be lying if I said that I am not shocked by the news. However, who am I to judge you? Most people on Aravorn consider us nagas bloodthirsty monsters. Yet, not all of us are.\n若说我对这个消息毫不震惊，那我就是在撒谎。然而，我有什么资格评判你呢？Aravorn 上的大多数人，都把我们 Nagas 视作嗜血的怪物。可我们并非全都如此。"

    old "What are you getting at?"
    new "What are you getting at?\n你想说什么？"

    old "Even if you become a vampire... we could still be together. I know you won't be an evil vampire, you know."
    new "Even if you become a vampire... we could still be together. I know you won't be an evil vampire, you know.\n即便你变成 Vampire……我们仍可以在一起。我知道，你不会是邪恶的 Vampire，你知道的。"

    old "How can you say it?"
    new "How can you say it?\n你怎么能这么说？"

    old "Because I know you. You will turn into something different, yes. But deep down there will still be you. The person who loves me, the person I love. The person who will be able to control the most visceral impulses and choose to act with mercy."
    new "Because I know you. You will turn into something different, yes. But deep down there will still be you. The person who loves me, the person I love. The person who will be able to control the most visceral impulses and choose to act with mercy.\n因为我了解你。你会变成不一样的存在，没错。但内心深处，仍然会是你。那个爱我的人，那个我爱的人。那个能够克制最本能的冲动、选择心怀仁慈行事的人。"

    old "Ssh... Come here."
    new "Ssh... Come here.\n嘘……过来。"

    old "Sylrissa comes near me and kisses me. Everyone else left in the room looks surprised by what she's doing. I guess nobody would ever think about kissing me right now, huh?"
    new "Sylrissa comes near me and kisses me. Everyone else left in the room looks surprised by what she's doing. I guess nobody would ever think about kissing me right now, huh?\nSylrissa 走到我面前，吻了我。房间里剩下的人都惊讶地看着她的举动。我想，此刻谁也不会想到要吻我吧，嗯？"

    old "Tomorrow we go kick some asses, and then...we'll find a solution. Trust me."
    new "Tomorrow we go kick some asses, and then...we'll find a solution. Trust me.\n明天我们去狠狠教训他们一顿，然后……我们再想办法。相信我。"

    old "Well, I guess after what happened, I won't be the only one speaking with a forked tongue."
    new "Well, I guess after what happened, I won't be the only one speaking with a forked tongue.\n好吧，我想经此一事，我就不再是唯一一个说话吐着分叉舌头的人了。"

    old "You found a way to make me smile even now. Impressive."
    new "You found a way to make me smile even now. Impressive.\n你总能想办法让我笑，即便此刻也是如此。真了不起。"

    old "So, see you tomorrow I guess. After that? Who knows, maybe you'll start to enjoy the swamps as well. It's a nice place when you're hunted on sight from most races, you know?"
    new "So, see you tomorrow I guess. After that? Who knows, maybe you'll start to enjoy the swamps as well. It's a nice place when you're hunted on sight from most races, you know?\n那么，我想明天见吧。在那之后？谁知道呢，也许你也会开始喜欢上沼泽。当你被大多数种族一见即猎杀时，那里可是个好去处，你明白吧？"

    old "I must say I don't like much the idea."
    new "I must say I don't like much the idea.\n我得说，我不太喜欢这个主意。"

    old "Yes, this was really too much. But don't misunderstand, [protag]. I won't coming with you tomorrow, because I don't want to become like you."
    new "Yes, this was really too much. But don't misunderstand, [protag]. I won't coming with you tomorrow, because I don't want to become like you.\n是的，这确实太过分了。但别误会，[protag]。明天我不会跟你去，因为我不想变得像你一样。"

    old "Like me?"
    new "Like me?\n像我一样？"

    old "I told you several times I don't care what happens to the Empire. I was doing this only for you, because you were kind to me, you were different from most people."
    new "I told you several times I don't care what happens to the Empire. I was doing this only for you, because you were kind to me, you were different from most people.\n我跟你说过好几次，我根本不在乎帝国会怎样。我做这些只是为了你，因为你待我很和善，你和大多数人都不一样。"

    old "Tomorrow you'll turn into a savage monster. I don't want to stay near you. It's too risky for me. It could be too easy for me to... fall back into temptation. I don't want to risk becoming a monster too. Sorry. I hope you understand."
    new "Tomorrow you'll turn into a savage monster. I don't want to stay near you. It's too risky for me. It could be too easy for me to... fall back into temptation. I don't want to risk becoming a monster too. Sorry. I hope you understand.\n明天你就会变成一头凶残的怪物。我不想待在你身边。那对我太冒险了。我太容易……再次沉沦于诱惑。我也不想冒险变成怪物。对不起。希望你能理解。"

    old "She moves out of the room before I have a chance to say anything in reply. But even if she had given me a chance to respond, I'm not sure I would have known what to say."
    new "She moves out of the room before I have a chance to say anything in reply. But even if she had given me a chance to respond, I'm not sure I would have known what to say.\n她在我还没来得及开口回应之前就走出了房间。但即便她给了我回应的机会，我也不确定自己知道该说什么。"

    old "Enok comes closer to me, shaking his head in disapproval."
    new "Enok comes closer to me, shaking his head in disapproval.\nEnok 走近我，不以为然地摇着头。"

    old "Why have you done it, [protag]? There was no need of any extra power. Our team is already strong enough as it is."
    new "Why have you done it, [protag]? There was no need of any extra power. Our team is already strong enough as it is.\n你为什么要这么做，[protag]？根本不需要什么额外的力量。我们的队伍本就足够强大了。"

    old "Especially after what happened between us. How could you do it?"
    new "Especially after what happened between us. How could you do it?\n尤其是在我们之间发生了那些事之后。你怎么能这么做？"

    old "I felt bad every day I was on your side, believe me. I just couldn't risk you knowing about it before it was time."
    new "I felt bad every day I was on your side, believe me. I just couldn't risk you knowing about it before it was time.\n我待在你身边的每一天都觉得愧疚，相信我。我只是不能冒险让你在时机成熟之前知道。"

    old "Why? You really trust me so little?"
    new "Why? You really trust me so little?\n为什么？你就这么不信任我？"

    old "No! I trust you with my life. That's why I'm asking you to come with me. I need you, Enok."
    new "No! I trust you with my life. That's why I'm asking you to come with me. I need you, Enok.\n不！我以性命信任你。所以我才请求你跟我一起。我需要你，Enok。"

    old "Yet you didn't tell me anything."
    new "Yet you didn't tell me anything.\n可你什么都没告诉我。"

    old "It was a sudden decision. The vampires who turned me asked me to choose quickly. There was no time to discuss it with you. I had to make a choice, and I choose. Then, I didn't tell you anything because I feared how you might react."
    new "It was a sudden decision. The vampires who turned me asked me to choose quickly. There was no time to discuss it with you. I had to make a choice, and I choose. Then, I didn't tell you anything because I feared how you might react.\n那是个仓促的决定。让我转化的那些 Vampires 要求我尽快选择。没有时间跟你商量。我必须做出抉择，而我也做了。之后，我什么都没告诉你，是因为我害怕你的反应。"

    old "I was afraid of losing you."
    new "I was afraid of losing you.\n我害怕失去你。"

    old "[protag]...well. That was very sweet of you, all things considered."
    new "[protag]...well. That was very sweet of you, all things considered.\n[protag]……好吧。考虑到这一切，你这话倒十分贴心。"

    old "I will come with you tomorrow. Then we'll need to talk about your life choices."
    new "I will come with you tomorrow. Then we'll need to talk about your life choices.\n明天我会跟你去。之后，我们得好好谈谈你的人生抉择。"

    old "Thank you, Enok."
    new "Thank you, Enok.\n谢谢你，Enok。"

    old "You need to put yourself in my shoes, Enok. I was offered this opportunity. I only had a brief moment to think about it. I needed to decide fast, and even if the choice I made was wrong, there's nothing that can be done about it now."
    new "You need to put yourself in my shoes, Enok. I was offered this opportunity. I only had a brief moment to think about it. I needed to decide fast, and even if the choice I made was wrong, there's nothing that can be done about it now.\n你得设身处地为我想想，Enok。这个机会摆到了我面前。我只有片刻时间考虑。我必须当机立断，即便我做出的选择是错的，如今也已无可挽回了。"

    old "Well, on this you're right. The damage is done. I don't think even with dark magic I could undo a vampire transmutation."
    new "Well, on this you're right. The damage is done. I don't think even with dark magic I could undo a vampire transmutation.\n好吧，这点你说得对。伤害已经造成。我想即便动用黑暗魔法，我也无法逆转 Vampire 的转化。"

    old "I will follow you in this final battle, but I'll keep an eye on you, [protag]."
    new "I will follow you in this final battle, but I'll keep an eye on you, [protag].\n这最后一战我会跟随你，但我会盯着你的，[protag]。"

    old "No 'buts'. I am sorry but I don't want to come with you anymore. I admit that at first, when I joined you, I did it because I didn't know what to do. To get a purpose."
    new "No 'buts'. I am sorry but I don't want to come with you anymore. I admit that at first, when I joined you, I did it because I didn't know what to do. To get a purpose.\n没什么可但是的。抱歉，我不想再跟你去了。我承认，当初加入你时，我那么做是因为我不知道该做什么，想给自己找个目标。"

    old "But as we fought together, I started to believe that we were doing it for something bigger. A greater good. Something like that."
    new "But as we fought together, I started to believe that we were doing it for something bigger. A greater good. Something like that.\n但随着我们并肩作战，我开始相信，我们这么做是为了某种更宏大的东西。一种更大的善。诸如此类。"

    old "Now I see that it was all about you. You wanted more power, and since you couldn't get it other ways... you decided to take the vampires' offer."
    new "Now I see that it was all about you. You wanted more power, and since you couldn't get it other ways... you decided to take the vampires' offer.\n现在我看清了，这一切都只是为了你自己。你想要更多力量，而既然无法通过其他途径得到……你就决定接受 Vampires 的提议。"

    old "What? No it's not-"
    new "What? No it's not-\n什么？不，不是——"

    old "Don't try to convince me otherwise. And you know this is the truth. Good bye, [protag]. Has been nice while it lasted."
    new "Don't try to convince me otherwise. And you know this is the truth. Good bye, [protag]. Has been nice while it lasted.\n别试图说服我。你知道这就是事实。再见了，[protag]。这段日子以来，还是不错的。"

    old "Everyone has left. I'm alone in my room now. I spend a moment in isolation, but the moment is gone when two familiar vampire faces appear in front of me."
    new "Everyone has left. I'm alone in my room now. I spend a moment in isolation, but the moment is gone when two familiar vampire faces appear in front of me.\n所有人都离开了。如今我独自待在房里。我享受了片刻的独处，但当两张熟悉的 Vampire 面孔出现在我面前时，那一刻便结束了。"

    old "That was an interesting show, wasn't it, Valery?"
    new "That was an interesting show, wasn't it, Valery?\n刚才那场戏挺有意思，对吧，Valery？"

    old "An interesting show indeed."
    new "An interesting show indeed.\n确实是一场有意思的戏。"

    old "You look surprised, [protag]. What, did you really think that nobody would object about your life-changing choice? Did you really expect all of them to come with you, like nothing happened?"
    new "You look surprised, [protag]. What, did you really think that nobody would object about your life-changing choice? Did you really expect all of them to come with you, like nothing happened?\n你看起来很惊讶，[protag]。怎么，你真以为没有人会反对你那个改变一生的选择吗？你真以为他们全都会跟着你，仿佛什么都没发生？"

    old "I... might have not thought about it fully."
    new "I... might have not thought about it fully.\n我……也许没有想得太周全。"

    old "Still, with your new powers and the allies you have left, we believe you could still finish your job."
    new "Still, with your new powers and the allies you have left, we believe you could still finish your job.\n不过，凭你的新力量和剩下的盟友，我们相信你仍能完成你的任务。"

    old "Finish your job. For us."
    new "Finish your job. For us.\n完成你的任务。为了我们。"

    old "Well, I might be that I'm getting old, but I really don't understand normal people anymore. How could they all still follow you, after you dropped that bomb on them?"
    new "Well, I might be that I'm getting old, but I really don't understand normal people anymore. How could they all still follow you, after you dropped that bomb on them?\n嗯，也许是我老了，但我真是越来越看不懂普通人了。你朝他们投下那样的重磅炸弹之后，他们怎么还会跟着你？"

    old "They're really loyal followers. After you turn, you should consider transforming them all into vampires as well. You could become a formidable force. I've never seen more obedient people."
    new "They're really loyal followers. After you turn, you should consider transforming them all into vampires as well. You could become a formidable force. I've never seen more obedient people.\n他们真是忠心的追随者。你转化之后，应该考虑把他们都变成 Vampires。你就能成为一股令人生畏的力量。我从没见过这么听话的人。"

    old "Don't you dare, Zachary. They only follow me because they trust me, and even now their loyalty is being tested to its ultimate limit. Some stated clearly that it will be the last mission they'll do with me."
    new "Don't you dare, Zachary. They only follow me because they trust me, and even now their loyalty is being tested to its ultimate limit. Some stated clearly that it will be the last mission they'll do with me.\n你敢，Zachary。他们跟着我，只因为他们信任我，而即便现在，他们的忠诚也正被考验到极限。有些人已明确表示，这将是他们与我共同执行的最后一次任务。"

    old "Of course, of course. But you know, people don't always say exactly what they're thinking, and people's minds can be changed. You could still convince them, you know."
    new "Of course, of course. But you know, people don't always say exactly what they're thinking, and people's minds can be changed. You could still convince them, you know.\n当然，当然。但你知道，人并不总把心中所想原原本本说出来，人的想法也是可以改变的。你仍可以说服他们，你知道的。"

    old "Please leave."
    new "Please leave.\n请离开。"

    old "Come Valery. Looks like our friend needs some time alone."
    new "Come Valery. Looks like our friend needs some time alone.\n走吧，Valery。看来我们的朋友需要独处一会儿。"

    old "They leave. I am alone in my empty room again. I feel a shiver down my spine, because..."
    new "They leave. I am alone in my empty room again. I feel a shiver down my spine, because...\n他们离开了。我又独自待在空荡荡的房里。我感到一阵寒意顺着脊背窜下，因为……"

    old "...finally, tomorrow will be the day I turn into a vampire. And nobody will be able to stop me anymore. In the past weeks I could already feel it, but today I feel an immense power flowing in my veins."
    new "...finally, tomorrow will be the day I turn into a vampire. And nobody will be able to stop me anymore. In the past weeks I could already feel it, but today I feel an immense power flowing in my veins.\n……终于，明天就是我变成 Vampire 的日子。再没有人能阻止我了。过去几周里我已有所察觉，但今天，我感到一股巨大的力量在血管中奔涌。"

    old "Tomorrow couldn't come sooner enough."
    new "Tomorrow couldn't come sooner enough.\n明天真是来得再快也不够。"

    old "...I wonder if by accepting the vampires' proposal I didn't make the biggest mistake of my life."
    new "...I wonder if by accepting the vampires' proposal I didn't make the biggest mistake of my life.\n……我怀疑，接受 Vampires 的提议，是否让我犯下了这一生最大的错误。"

    old "I am terrified by what will happen tomorrow. Of course, the danger that lurks within castle N'Mar weighs heavy on my mind. But what lies inside of that castle does not terrify me as much as what lies inside of me. Tomorrow, my life will change forever."
    new "I am terrified by what will happen tomorrow. Of course, the danger that lurks within castle N'Mar weighs heavy on my mind. But what lies inside of that castle does not terrify me as much as what lies inside of me. Tomorrow, my life will change forever.\n我对明天将要发生的事感到恐惧。诚然，潜伏在 N'Mar 城堡内的危险沉甸甸地压在我心头。但城堡内的事物，远不如我体内的事物更令我恐惧。明天，我的人生将永远改变。"

    old "{i}Review your party setup before proceeding.{/i}"
    new "{i}Review your party setup before proceeding.{/i}\n{i}出发前请先检查你的队伍配置。{/i}"

    old "party.gui_selected_char [party.gui_selected_char]"
    new "party.gui_selected_char [party.gui_selected_char]\nparty.gui_selected_char [party.gui_selected_char]"

    old "party.guiTree [party.guiTree]"
    new "party.guiTree [party.guiTree]\nparty.guiTree [party.guiTree]"

    old "Your tricks don't work with me anymore! You hurt Diego and you must pay for it!"
    new "Your tricks don't work with me anymore! You hurt Diego and you must pay for it!\n你的花招对我再也没用了！你伤了 Diego，必须为此付出代价！"

    old "Oh, no no no no! I'm done listening to you! Save your breath!"
    new "Oh, no no no no! I'm done listening to you! Save your breath!\n哦，不不不不！我听够你的话了！省省口水吧！"

    old "We still have [ship_cannons] cannon(s) which can fire. Where should we aim to?"
    new "We still have [ship_cannons] cannon(s) which can fire. Where should we aim to?\n我们还有 [ship_cannons] 门大炮可以开火。我们该瞄准哪里？"

    old "Fire!"
    new "Fire!\n开火！"

    old "Watch out! He's moving one of its tentacles towards us!"
    new "Watch out! He's moving one of its tentacles towards us!\n小心！它正把一根触手伸向我们！"

    old "That was the last cannon! It destroyed our last cannon!"
    new "That was the last cannon! It destroyed our last cannon!\n那是最后一门炮了！它毁掉了我们最后一门炮！"

    old "This means we need to finish it ourselves. Stand back!"
    new "This means we need to finish it ourselves. Stand back!\n这意味着我们得亲手了结它。退后！"

    old "Damn one of our cannons was destroyed!"
    new "Damn one of our cannons was destroyed!\n该死，我们的一门炮被毁了！"

    old "It was worth it, we inflicted serious damage on the Kraken!"
    new "It was worth it, we inflicted serious damage on the Kraken!\n值了，我们给 Kraken 造成了重创！"

    old "You...didn't kill me. I can't die! Not now, that I'm so close to my goal! My loyal minions will take care of you while I regain my forces."
    new "You...didn't kill me. I can't die! Not now, that I'm so close to my goal! My loyal minions will take care of you while I regain my forces.\n你……没能杀掉我。我不能死！现在不行，我离目标如此之近！趁我重整力量之际，我忠心的爪牙会好好招呼你们的。"

    old "Hahaha! Do you think I'm stupid? I know your strategy! Save your breath, your trick don't work against me!"
    new "Hahaha! Do you think I'm stupid? I know your strategy! Save your breath, your trick don't work against me!\n哈哈哈！你以为我傻吗？我早看穿你的策略了！省省口水吧，你的花招对我没用！"

    old "Looks like I need to beat him only by force."
    new "Looks like I need to beat him only by force.\n看来我只能靠武力击败他了。"

    old "No... this can't be..."
    new "No... this can't be...\n不……这不可能……"

    old "All the zombies around him collapse on the ground."
    new "All the zombies around him collapse on the ground.\n他周围所有的僵尸都倒在了地上。"

    old "You reached the end of the demo. We hope you enjoyed it and you decide to continue your quest by purchasing the full version!"
    new "You reached the end of the demo. We hope you enjoyed it and you decide to continue your quest by purchasing the full version!\n你已经到达试玩版的结尾。希望你玩得愉快，并决定购买完整版，继续你的冒险之旅！"

    old "BATTLE"
    new "BATTLE\n战斗"

    old "Level UP! Your party gained 1000XP. Enemy base level is: [lvl]"
    new "Level UP! Your party gained 1000XP. Enemy base level is: [lvl]\n升级！你的队伍获得 1000 经验。敌方基础等级为：[lvl]"

    old "Game mission: you must choose up to 6 reserves whenever you leave your hq. In battle maximum 4 characters can fight, no auto-heal after each fight. Only the characters left in reserve will fully heal after each fight."
    new "Game mission: you must choose up to 6 reserves whenever you leave your hq. In battle maximum 4 characters can fight, no auto-heal after each fight. Only the characters left in reserve will fully heal after each fight.\n游戏说明：每当你离开总部时，必须选择至多 6 名后备队员。战斗中最多有 4 名角色参战，每场战斗结束后不会自动回血。只有留在后备中的角色才会在每场战斗后完全恢复。"

    old "First wave: 6 skeleton scouts! Each one level +1 from left to right."
    new "First wave: 6 skeleton scouts! Each one level +1 from left to right.\n第一波：6 个 Skeleton Scout！从左到右，每个的等级 +1。"

    old "Second wave: 3 skeletons, 1 skeleton warrior. If you swap injured characters they will be fully recovered on the third and final fight!"
    new "Second wave: 3 skeletons, 1 skeleton warrior. If you swap injured characters they will be fully recovered on the third and final fight!\n第二波：3 个骷髅，1 个 Skeleton Warrior。如果你换下受伤的角色，他们将在第三场、也是最后一场战斗中完全恢复！"

    old "Third wave: 3 different skeletons including a spellcaster (the skeleton warden)."
    new "Third wave: 3 different skeletons including a spellcaster (the skeleton warden).\n第三波：3 种不同的骷髅，其中包括一名施法者（Skeleton Warden）。"

    old "OK that's enough for now! :-D"
    new "OK that's enough for now! :-D\n好了，暂时就到这里！:-D"

    old "We step into the circular room and begin ascending the spiral staircase."
    new "We step into the circular room and begin ascending the spiral staircase.\n我们踏入圆形房间，开始攀上螺旋楼梯。"

    old "Do you think there's anything waiting for us at the top?"
    new "Do you think there's anything waiting for us at the top?\n你觉得楼梯顶端会有什么等着我们吗？"

    old "If there is, we're about to find out."
    new "If there is, we're about to find out.\n如果有，我们马上就知道了。"

    old "We'll be at a height disadvantage if there's someone at the top of the stairs."
    new "We'll be at a height disadvantage if there's someone at the top of the stairs.\n如果楼梯顶端有人，我们就会处于高处不利的位置。"

    old "Yes, but I get the feeling that if anyone is up there, they're probably outside on the battlements, not watching the top of the spiral staircase and waiting for someone to come clamoring up."
    new "Yes, but I get the feeling that if anyone is up there, they're probably outside on the battlements, not watching the top of the spiral staircase and waiting for someone to come clamoring up.\n没错，但我有种感觉，就算上面有人，他们多半也在外面的城垛上，而不是盯着螺旋楼梯口，等着谁闹闹哄哄地爬上来。"

    old "What if they hear us coming up?"
    new "What if they hear us coming up?\n要是他们听到我们上来呢？"

    old "In that situation, I think it would be wise to have your hands on your weapon."
    new "In that situation, I think it would be wise to have your hands on your weapon.\n那种情况下，我想把手按在武器上才是明智之举。"

    old "We reach the top of the staircase without incident, and we make our way onto the battlements atop the castle wall. I briefly peer over the edge."
    new "We reach the top of the staircase without incident, and we make our way onto the battlements atop the castle wall. I briefly peer over the edge.\n我们一路无事地到达楼梯顶端，走上城堡墙顶的城垛。我朝边缘外匆匆瞥了一眼。"

    old "Careful. You wouldn't want to have a stumble from this height."
    new "Careful. You wouldn't want to have a stumble from this height.\n小心。在这个高度，你可不想失足跌倒。"

    old "It's rather incredible, isn't it? Look at how dense the fog is. I can't even see the ground from up here. We might as well be in the clouds."
    new "It's rather incredible, isn't it? Look at how dense the fog is. I can't even see the ground from up here. We might as well be in the clouds.\n实在不可思议，不是吗？看看这雾有多浓。从这里我甚至看不见地面。我们简直就像置身云中。"

    old "That's good. It means that we shouldn't be visible from other parts of the castle. Even if there are things patrolling the other balconies, they likely can't see us from here."
    new "That's good. It means that we shouldn't be visible from other parts of the castle. Even if there are things patrolling the other balconies, they likely can't see us from here.\n这是好事。这意味着城堡其他部分应该看不见我们。即便有其他东西在别的露台上巡逻，从这里它们多半也看不见我们。"

    old "You might think that, but don't get too cocky. You and I can't see through this fog, but who knows what powers of sight our foes possess? I wouldn't underestimate the eyesight of a vampire under the moonlight. Their vision is likely impeded by the fog, but all the same, it's probably best to keep our heads down."
    new "You might think that, but don't get too cocky. You and I can't see through this fog, but who knows what powers of sight our foes possess? I wouldn't underestimate the eyesight of a vampire under the moonlight. Their vision is likely impeded by the fog, but all the same, it's probably best to keep our heads down.\n你也许会这么想，但别太得意。你我都看不透这雾，可谁知道我们的敌人拥有怎样的目力？我可不会低估月光下 Vampire 的视力。他们的视线多半也会被雾遮挡，但即便如此，我们还是最好压低身子。"

    old "What exactly are we looking for here?"
    new "What exactly are we looking for here?\n我们在这里究竟要找什么？"

    old "I want to figure out how defensible this castle is. What would happen if we were to try and assault it with an army? Does this castle have traditional defenses? That's what we're here to find out."
    new "I want to figure out how defensible this castle is. What would happen if we were to try and assault it with an army? Does this castle have traditional defenses? That's what we're here to find out.\n我想弄清这座城堡的防御能力如何。如果我们试图用军队强攻，会怎样？这座城堡有没有传统的防御工事？这正是我们要来查明的事。"

    old "For example, at the top of the staircase we just came from, I would have expected to find something. If this were a traditional castle, inside the tower at the top of the staircase would be a logical place to store projectile weapons like bows and arrows, the kinds of things that soldiers on the balcony could use in a defense."
    new "For example, at the top of the staircase we just came from, I would have expected to find something. If this were a traditional castle, inside the tower at the top of the staircase would be a logical place to store projectile weapons like bows and arrows, the kinds of things that soldiers on the balcony could use in a defense.\n例如，在我们刚走过的那段楼梯顶端，我本以为会找到点什么。若这是一座传统城堡，楼梯顶端的塔楼里理应存放弓箭之类的投射武器，正是阳台上的士兵守城时用得上的东西。"

    old "I didn't see a single crossbow in there. In fact, the tower seemed completely barren."
    new "I didn't see a single crossbow in there. In fact, the tower seemed completely barren.\n那里面连一把弩都没有。事实上，那座塔楼看上去空空如也。"

    old "Exactly. Are all of the other towers like that? And if we did assault the castle, how much time would it take them to prepare to defend it?"
    new "Exactly. Are all of the other towers like that? And if we did assault the castle, how much time would it take them to prepare to defend it?\n正是如此。其他塔楼也都是这样吗？而若我们真的强攻城堡，他们需要多久才能做好防守准备？"

    old "Part of me wonders whether undead soldiers like walking skeletons are even capable of using projectile weapons like bows."
    new "Part of me wonders whether undead soldiers like walking skeletons are even capable of using projectile weapons like bows.\n我心里有些疑惑，像行尸走肉般的骷髅这类亡灵士兵，是否真有能力使用弓箭之类的投射武器。"

    old "They can swing swords, why wouldn't they be able to use bows and arrows?"
    new "They can swing swords, why wouldn't they be able to use bows and arrows?\n他们能挥剑，为何就不能用弓箭？"

    old "Still, these battlements must be here for a reason."
    new "Still, these battlements must be here for a reason.\n不过，这些城垛立在这里，必有原因。"

    old "I poke my head through one of the gaps in the battlements. It's the kind of gap that an architect would have placed here with an archer in mind."
    new "I poke my head through one of the gaps in the battlements. It's the kind of gap that an architect would have placed here with an archer in mind.\n我把头探进城垛上的一个垛口。这种垛口，正是建筑师为弓箭手设计的。"

    old "See? This is exactly the kind of place to put a row of archers. There's no other reason for these battlements to be here."
    new "See? This is exactly the kind of place to put a row of archers. There's no other reason for these battlements to be here.\n看到了吗？这里正是布置一排弓箭手的地方。这些城垛没有别的存在理由。"

    old "Vampires didn't build these walls, though. An architect did intend for these gaps to be used as vantage points for archers, but the castle's original occupants are long gone."
    new "Vampires didn't build these walls, though. An architect did intend for these gaps to be used as vantage points for archers, but the castle's original occupants are long gone.\n不过，这些城墙并非 Vampires 所建。建筑师确实打算把这些垛口用作弓箭手的射击位，但城堡最初的主人早已不在了。"

    old "Where did they go to, I wonder?"
    new "Where did they go to, I wonder?\n他们去了哪儿呢，我想知道。"

    old "That's a question that we can ponder another day. Right now our job is to observe and collect information."
    new "That's a question that we can ponder another day. Right now our job is to observe and collect information.\n这个问题我们可以改日再想。眼下，我们的任务是观察并收集情报。"

    old "We begin marching to the opposite end of the battlements."
    new "We begin marching to the opposite end of the battlements.\n我们开始朝城垛的另一端行进。"

    old "I hear the sound of flapping wings, and I motion for everyone to get down and stay quiet. A hush falls over the battlements, and for a moment, I hear nothing but the sound of the wind. Moments later, a group of crows begins flying overhead, and their cawing breaks the silence."
    new "I hear the sound of flapping wings, and I motion for everyone to get down and stay quiet. A hush falls over the battlements, and for a moment, I hear nothing but the sound of the wind. Moments later, a group of crows begins flying overhead, and their cawing breaks the silence.\n我听到扑扇翅膀的声音，便示意大家蹲下，保持安静。城垛上一片寂静，一时间，我耳边只有风声。片刻之后，一群乌鸦从头顶飞过，它们的聒噪打破了沉寂。"

    old "Looks like it's just a flock of crows."
    new "Looks like it's just a flock of crows.\n看来只是一群乌鸦。"

    old "Not a flock. A murder."
    new "Not a flock. A murder.\n不是群。是谋杀。"

    old "Murder?"
    new "Murder?\n谋杀？"

    old "A group of crows is called a murder."
    new "A group of crows is called a murder.\n一群乌鸦，被称为谋杀。"

    old "Chilling. As if the sound of crows on a foggy night above an undead fortress wasn't eerie enough."
    new "Chilling. As if the sound of crows on a foggy night above an undead fortress wasn't eerie enough.\n令人毛骨悚然。仿佛雾气弥漫的夜里，乌鸦在不死堡垒上空啼叫，还不够阴森似的。"

    old "Just be thankful it's not some vampire."
    new "Just be thankful it's not some vampire.\n你该庆幸，那不是某个 Vampire。"

    old "Can vampires fly?"
    new "Can vampires fly?\nVampires 会飞吗？"

    old "Not that I know of. There are blood-sucking bats that have vampire-like qualities, and obviously, bats can fly. But I've learned nothing about flying vampires."
    new "Not that I know of. There are blood-sucking bats that have vampire-like qualities, and obviously, bats can fly. But I've learned nothing about flying vampires.\n据我所知不会。有些吸血蝙蝠具有 Vampire 般的特质，而蝙蝠当然会飞。但我从未听说过会飞的 Vampires。"

    old "Maybe tonight is the night we learn about the existence of flying vampires. You did say we're here to learn new things."
    new "Maybe tonight is the night we learn about the existence of flying vampires. You did say we're here to learn new things.\n也许今晚，就是我们得知存在会飞的 Vampires 的夜晚。你不是说我们是来学新东西的吗。"

    old "No use speculating. Let's keep going."
    new "No use speculating. Let's keep going.\n猜来猜去也没用。继续走吧。"

    old "Eventually, we reach the end of the battlements, and find a locked steel door at the end of it. No, not locked—it's actually just a flat sheet of metal with no handle, as if the person who put it there never intended for it to be opened from this side."
    new "Eventually, we reach the end of the battlements, and find a locked steel door at the end of it. No, not locked—it's actually just a flat sheet of metal with no handle, as if the person who put it there never intended for it to be opened from this side.\n最终，我们走到城垛尽头，发现尽头有一扇锁着的铁门。不，不是锁着——那其实只是一块没有把手的平板金属，仿佛放置它的人从一开始就没打算让它从这一侧打开。"

    old "Any way for us to get through?"
    new "Any way for us to get through?\n我们有办法过去吗？"

    old "I don't think so. I think whoever built this place wanted the doors on the battlements to work one way only. You can use the door to get from the inside tower to the outside battlements, but not the other way around."
    new "I don't think so. I think whoever built this place wanted the doors on the battlements to work one way only. You can use the door to get from the inside tower to the outside battlements, but not the other way around.\n我想没有。我想，建造此地的人，是想让城垛上的门只能单向通行。你可以用这扇门从内侧塔楼走到外面的城垛，却无法反着来。"

    old "That's smart architecture. It lets the defenders access the battlements to defend the castle, but if an enemy climbs onto the battlements, they can't enter the towers."
    new "That's smart architecture. It lets the defenders access the battlements to defend the castle, but if an enemy climbs onto the battlements, they can't enter the towers.\n这是巧妙的建筑。它让守军能登上城垛守城，但若敌人爬上了城垛，也无法进入塔楼。"

    old "But if an attacker has already scaled the battlements, then they can just jump down into the courtyard."
    new "But if an attacker has already scaled the battlements, then they can just jump down into the courtyard.\n但若攻击者已经爬上了城垛，他们大可以直接跳进庭院。"

    old "You want to try jumping into the courtyard from here? Be my guest, but I wouldn't expect you to survive that jump with any of your bones intact."
    new "You want to try jumping into the courtyard from here? Be my guest, but I wouldn't expect you to survive that jump with any of your bones intact.\n你想试试从这里跳进庭院？请便，不过我可不敢指望你跳下去后还能保全任何一根骨头。"

    old "Maybe we can break our way through the door."
    new "Maybe we can break our way through the door.\n也许我们能破门而入。"

    old "When it comes to a contest of brute strength against a steel door set in rock, I'd put my money on the door. But if you want to try your strength against it, be my guest."
    new "When it comes to a contest of brute strength against a steel door set in rock, I'd put my money on the door. But if you want to try your strength against it, be my guest.\n要说蛮力与嵌在岩石里的铁门较量，我会押铁门赢。但你若想试试自己的力气，请便。"

    old "Very well. Rahhh!"
    new "Very well. Rahhh!\n那好。喝啊！"

    old "I hear the sound of a steel weapon striking the door, but the weapon bounces off harmlessly, landing at the edge of the battlements."
    new "I hear the sound of a steel weapon striking the door, but the weapon bounces off harmlessly, landing at the edge of the battlements.\n我听到钢制武器击打铁门的声音，但那武器被无害地弹开，落在城垛边缘。"

    old "Careful. You wouldn't want to lose that off the edge."
    new "Careful. You wouldn't want to lose that off the edge.\n小心。你可不想让它从边缘掉下去。"

    old "I guess there's no way breaking our way through."
    new "I guess there's no way breaking our way through.\n我想，我们是没法破门而入了。"

    old "Wait. Do you feel that? It feels like the floor is shaking."
    new "Wait. Do you feel that? It feels like the floor is shaking.\n等等。你感觉到了吗？地面似乎在震动。"

    old "I hear the sound of a low rumble, which grows more and more intense. I hear the screeching groan of steel rubbing against rock, and I watch as the steel door opens in front of us."
    new "I hear the sound of a low rumble, which grows more and more intense. I hear the screeching groan of steel rubbing against rock, and I watch as the steel door opens in front of us.\n我听到一阵低沉的轰鸣，越来越响。接着是钢铁摩擦岩石的刺耳声响，我看着眼前的铁门缓缓打开。"

    old "Hah! I guess might can solve these kinds of problems."
    new "Hah! I guess might can solve these kinds of problems.\n哈！看来蛮力也能解决这类问题。"

    old "I'm not sure if your striking the door is what opened it. Or rather, it doesn't seem like you forced it open."
    new "I'm not sure if your striking the door is what opened it. Or rather, it doesn't seem like you forced it open.\n我不确定是不是你敲那一下把门打开的。或者更确切地说，它不像是被你强行撞开的。"

    old "How do you suppose it opened, then?"
    new "How do you suppose it opened, then?\n那依你之见，它是怎么开的？"

    old "Maybe someone opened the door from the inside. They heard a knock, so they opened the door to see what was on the other side."
    new "Maybe someone opened the door from the inside. They heard a knock, so they opened the door to see what was on the other side.\n也许有人从里面把门打开了。他们听到敲门声，便打开门，想看看另一侧是什么。"

    old "I poke my head through the doorway."
    new "I poke my head through the doorway.\n我把头探进门里。"

    old "Well, I don't see anyone. Let's step in and take a look around, shall we?"
    new "Well, I don't see anyone. Let's step in and take a look around, shall we?\n嗯，我没看到任何人。我们进去四处看看吧，如何？"

    old "We enter the tower, and I drop a staff at the door to serve as a door-stop, just in case the door decides to take on a mind of its own and close behind us."
    new "We enter the tower, and I drop a staff at the door to serve as a door-stop, just in case the door decides to take on a mind of its own and close behind us.\n我们进入塔楼，我把一根木杖卡在门边当作门挡，以防这扇门自作主张，在我们身后合上。"

    old "Are there any stairs leading down?"
    new "Are there any stairs leading down?\n有通往下方的楼梯吗？"

    old "Doesn't seem like it. I see several racks for weapons, but no actual weapons. I think the only way to access this tower is from the battlements."
    new "Doesn't seem like it. I see several racks for weapons, but no actual weapons. I think the only way to access this tower is from the battlements.\n似乎没有。我看到几个武器架，却没有真正的武器。我想，进入这座塔楼的唯一途径就是从城垛上来。"

    old "I look up toward the source of the noise, and see the hole in the roof just in time to see a figure drop down from it."
    new "I look up toward the source of the noise, and see the hole in the roof just in time to see a figure drop down from it.\n我抬头望向声响的来源，恰好看到屋顶上的那个洞，也恰好看到一个人影从那里落下。"

    old "Visitors! Have you come to play?"
    new "Visitors! Have you come to play?\n访客！你们是来玩的吗？"

    old "I hear the sound of weapons being drawn behind me."
    new "I hear the sound of weapons being drawn behind me.\n我听到身后响起拔出兵器的声音。"

    old "Already drawing weapons? But we haven't even had a proper introduction yet! I'm Zephyr. Won't you tell me your name?"
    new "Already drawing weapons? But we haven't even had a proper introduction yet! I'm Zephyr. Won't you tell me your name?\n这就拔兵器了？可我们连个像样的自我介绍都还没做呢！我是 Zephyr。你不打算告诉我你的名字吗？"

    old "At a glance, we would appear to have the advantage. I see only one vampire before me. And yet, I can't help but feel that we might be at a disadvantage."
    new "At a glance, we would appear to have the advantage. I see only one vampire before me. And yet, I can't help but feel that we might be at a disadvantage.\n乍一看，我们似乎占着上风。我眼前只有一个 Vampire。然而，我却不禁觉得，我们或许反而处于劣势。"

    old "After all, he caught us unawares. He approached us. Why would he do that if we in some way threatened him? Something about this doesn't feel right."
    new "After all, he caught us unawares. He approached us. Why would he do that if we in some way threatened him? Something about this doesn't feel right.\n毕竟，是他趁我们不备抓住了我们。是他主动接近了我们。若我们在某方面威胁到他，他为何还要这么做？这事有些不对劲。"

    old "What should I do? Is it best to attack now, or can I talk my way out of this one?"
    new "What should I do? Is it best to attack now, or can I talk my way out of this one?\n我该怎么办？是现在就动手最好，还是能靠嘴皮子脱身？"

    old "Maybe I can talk my way out of this one. At the very least, I should try to fish for more information."
    new "Maybe I can talk my way out of this one. At the very least, I should try to fish for more information.\n也许我能靠言语脱身。至少，我该试着套取更多信息。"

    old "My name's [protag]."
    new "My name's [protag].\n我叫 [protag]。"

    old "[protag], it's nice to meet you. I heard someone was traipsing about on the battlements, and I thought I'd see who it was."
    new "[protag], it's nice to meet you. I heard someone was traipsing about on the battlements, and I thought I'd see who it was.\n[protag]，很高兴认识你。我听说有人在城垛上闲逛，就想来看看是谁。"

    old "Who notified you?"
    new "Who notified you?\n是谁通知你的？"

    old "A crow whispered it in my ear."
    new "A crow whispered it in my ear.\n一只乌鸦在我耳边低语。"

    old "Zephyr grins, and I'm not sure whether his statement was meant literally or not. Does Zephyr really have the ability to commune with the crows?"
    new "Zephyr grins, and I'm not sure whether his statement was meant literally or not. Does Zephyr really have the ability to commune with the crows?\nZephyr 咧嘴一笑，我不确定他这话是字面意思还是别的。Zephyr 真的有与乌鸦交流的能力吗？"

    old "Your crows seem to be very attentive. I didn't realize we were being watched."
    new "Your crows seem to be very attentive. I didn't realize we were being watched.\n你的乌鸦们似乎十分警觉。我倒没意识到，我们一直被盯着。"

    old "Oh, they're not my crows. I don't own them, and I don't think anyone ever could. There's not much you can do to keep a crow in one place, besides caging it, and that just seems so cruel. No, these crows are loyal to me only for as long as I give them flesh to feast on."
    new "Oh, they're not my crows. I don't own them, and I don't think anyone ever could. There's not much you can do to keep a crow in one place, besides caging it, and that just seems so cruel. No, these crows are loyal to me only for as long as I give them flesh to feast on.\n哦，它们不是我的乌鸦。我不拥有它们，我想也没人能拥有。除了把它关进笼子，你没法把乌鸦留在原地，而那未免太残忍了。不，这些乌鸦只在我供给它们血肉享用的时候，才会忠于我。"

    old "You know, I was thinking of going out to night, finding some new carrion for them to dine on. But then you all were nice enough to come and deliver yourselves to me."
    new "You know, I was thinking of going out to night, finding some new carrion for them to dine on. But then you all were nice enough to come and deliver yourselves to me.\n你知道吗，我本打算今晚出去，给它们找些新鲜的腐肉吃。可你们就这么好心，把自己送上门来了。"

    old "I must admit, though, you are no ordinary prey. You've got an aura about you. It's so aggressive. I can appreciate the assertive attitude, but please, don't be cold about it."
    new "I must admit, though, you are no ordinary prey. You've got an aura about you. It's so aggressive. I can appreciate the assertive attitude, but please, don't be cold about it.\n不过我得承认，你们可不是寻常的猎物。你们周身有种气势。太有攻击性了。我欣赏这份强势的姿态，但请别那么冷淡嘛。"

    old "Why is this vampire so self-assured? There seems to be only one way out of this room, and that's the door behind us. We outnumber him, it seems he has nowhere to flee. Does he really think so little of us that he doesn't fear us in the least?"
    new "Why is this vampire so self-assured? There seems to be only one way out of this room, and that's the door behind us. We outnumber him, it seems he has nowhere to flee. Does he really think so little of us that he doesn't fear us in the least?\n这个 Vampire 为何如此自信？这房间似乎只有一条出路，就是我们身后的门。我们人数占优，他似乎无处可逃。他真的这么小看我们，丝毫不怕我们吗？"

    old "I notice Zephyr cast a glance upward toward the hole in the roof, the same one that he dropped through. Now, why would he be eying that? Could someone like him jump up through that hole? For an ordinary man, I'd say it's impossible, but for a vampire...he must be planning his exit."
    new "I notice Zephyr cast a glance upward toward the hole in the roof, the same one that he dropped through. Now, why would he be eying that? Could someone like him jump up through that hole? For an ordinary man, I'd say it's impossible, but for a vampire...he must be planning his exit.\n我注意到 Zephyr 朝屋顶上的那个洞瞥了一眼，正是他落下来的那个洞。他为何要盯着那儿？像他这样的人，能跳上那个洞吗？对普通人来说，我会说绝无可能，但对一个 Vampire 来说……他一定是在盘算退路。"

    old "He might not have a plan to kill us, but he doesn't need one. He already has an exit strategy. But maybe that means he can be negotiated with."
    new "He might not have a plan to kill us, but he doesn't need one. He already has an exit strategy. But maybe that means he can be negotiated with.\n他也许没有杀我们的计划，但他也不需要。他早有了脱身之策。不过，这或许意味着可以与他谈判。"

    old "You are Zephyr? Your friends told me about you, but I didn't realize you'd look so...scrawny. We've killed all the other vampires so far. You'll be the last one."
    new "You are Zephyr? Your friends told me about you, but I didn't realize you'd look so...scrawny. We've killed all the other vampires so far. You'll be the last one.\n你就是 Zephyr？你的朋友们跟我提起过你，但我没料到你看上去这么……瘦弱。迄今我们已经杀光了其他所有 Vampires。你将是最后一个。"

    old "What? No, you haven't. There's no way that you could have already..."
    new "What? No, you haven't. There's no way that you could have already...\n什么？不，你们没有。你们不可能已经……"

    old "I sense a moment of hesitation in his denial, and make another calculated bluff. I can see him starting to doubt himself."
    new "I sense a moment of hesitation in his denial, and make another calculated bluff. I can see him starting to doubt himself.\n我察觉到他否认时有一瞬的迟疑，便又虚张声势地使出一招。我能看出，他开始怀疑起自己来了。"

    old "We burned their bodies, so I'm afraid that there's no evidence for me to show that I'm telling you the truth. But search the castle as much as you like, you won't find them."
    new "We burned their bodies, so I'm afraid that there's no evidence for me to show that I'm telling you the truth. But search the castle as much as you like, you won't find them.\n我们烧掉了他们的尸体，所以恐怕我拿不出证据来证明我说的是实话。但你尽管搜遍城堡，也找不到他们。"

    old "That's impossible."
    new "That's impossible.\n这不可能。"

    old "Unlikely? Yes. Impossible? No. I'm sure that you've gotten used to killing defenseless wanderers who find themselves somehow stuck in the wastes, but tell me, how many of those lost wanderers found their way into this castle?"
    new "Unlikely? Yes. Impossible? No. I'm sure that you've gotten used to killing defenseless wanderers who find themselves somehow stuck in the wastes, but tell me, how many of those lost wanderers found their way into this castle?\n不太可能？是的。不可能？不是。我相信，你早已习惯了杀害那些莫名其妙被困在荒地里、毫无还手之力的流浪者，但告诉我，那些迷路的流浪者里，有多少人找到路进了这座城堡？"

    old "We didn't come here by accident. We came here to invade this castle. We came here to kill vampires. We came here to kill you."
    new "We didn't come here by accident. We came here to invade this castle. We came here to kill vampires. We came here to kill you.\n我们不是碰巧来的。我们是来入侵这座城堡的。我们是来杀 Vampires 的。我们是来杀你的。"

    old "I take a step forward, and Zephyr flinches. I flash a toothy grin."
    new "I take a step forward, and Zephyr flinches. I flash a toothy grin.\n我上前一步，Zephyr 瑟缩了一下。我咧嘴一笑，露出牙齿。"

    old "You came here trying to intimidate a vampire? You've got guts, I'll give you that."
    new "You came here trying to intimidate a vampire? You've got guts, I'll give you that.\n你来这里，是想吓唬一个 Vampire？你倒是有胆量，这点我承认。"

    old "Zephyr crouches to the floor, then looks up and leaps through the hole in the ceiling."
    new "Zephyr crouches to the floor, then looks up and leaps through the hole in the ceiling.\nZephyr 蹲下身，随即抬头一望，纵身跃过天花板上的洞。"

    old "Where did he go!?"
    new "Where did he go!?\n他去哪儿了！？"

    old "I'm not sure but we shouldn't waste any more time in this room. It's a dead end for us, let's go back the way we came."
    new "I'm not sure but we shouldn't waste any more time in this room. It's a dead end for us, let's go back the way we came.\n我不确定，但我们不该再在这个房间浪费时间了。它对我们来说是个死胡同，我们原路返回吧。"

    old "Zephyr, eh? Your friends told me about you. You're the annoying one that nobody likes, right?"
    new "Zephyr, eh? Your friends told me about you. You're the annoying one that nobody likes, right?\nZephyr，是吗？你的朋友们跟我提起过你。你就是那个没人喜欢的讨厌鬼，对吧？"

    old "I'm not sure what you've heard about me, but what you're saying about me sounds completely false."
    new "I'm not sure what you've heard about me, but what you're saying about me sounds completely false.\n我不知道你听说了什么关于我的事，但你刚才说的那些，听起来完全是无稽之谈。"

    old "Maybe you're right. You seem like a perfectly reasonable person. I mean, you're a vampire and I'm a [prace], so that's a bit of a problem, but if we had met under better circumstances, I think you and I would be able to get along just fine. I'm not sure why the other vampires seem to disparage you so much."
    new "Maybe you're right. You seem like a perfectly reasonable person. I mean, you're a vampire and I'm a [prace], so that's a bit of a problem, but if we had met under better circumstances, I think you and I would be able to get along just fine. I'm not sure why the other vampires seem to disparage you so much.\n也许你说得对。你看上去是个相当通情达理的人。我是说，你是 Vampire，而我是 [prace]，所以这多少有点问题，但若我们是在更好的境遇下相遇，我想你我会相处得不错。我不太明白，为什么其他 Vampires 似乎那么瞧不起你。"

    old "Zephyr's eyebrow begins to twitch."
    new "Zephyr's eyebrow begins to twitch.\nZephyr 的眉毛开始抽搐。"

    old "I see what you're trying to do. You're trying to get under my skin."
    new "I see what you're trying to do. You're trying to get under my skin.\n我看穿你的意图了。你想惹恼我。"

    old "Maybe I am. Maybe I'm not."
    new "Maybe I am. Maybe I'm not.\n也许我是，也许我不是。"

    old "You're trying hard, but you can't beat us."
    new "You're trying hard, but you can't beat us.\n你很卖力，但你打不过我们。"

    old "Don't you see that what are you doing is pointless? Think about it."
    new "Don't you see that what are you doing is pointless? Think about it.\n你难道看不出，你所做的一切毫无意义吗？好好想想吧。"

    old "You look tired. You should stop before we kill you."
    new "You look tired. You should stop before we kill you.\n你看起来累了。趁我们还没杀你，住手吧。"

    old "You look tired. I'm a bit tired too. Shall we take a break to talk?"
    new "You look tired. I'm a bit tired too. Shall we take a break to talk?\n你看起来很累。我也有些累了。我们歇一歇，谈一谈如何？"

    old "Hmpf."
    new "Hmpf.\n哼。"

    old "What's the matter, Zephyr? You look tense. Can you keep up this fight?"
    new "What's the matter, Zephyr? You look tense. Can you keep up this fight?\n怎么了，Zephyr？你看上去很紧张。这场战斗，你还撑得住吗？"

    old "Me, tense? Why do you think I'd be tense?"
    new "Me, tense? Why do you think I'd be tense?\n我，紧张？你凭什么觉得我会紧张？"

    old "Because you know that we have the power to beat you."
    new "Because you know that we have the power to beat you.\n因为你知道，我们有打败你的实力。"

    old "That's the kind of can-do spirit I like to see! Maybe you and your friends could beat me. But what happens when I decide to bring my friends along for the fight, I wonder?"
    new "That's the kind of can-do spirit I like to see! Maybe you and your friends could beat me. But what happens when I decide to bring my friends along for the fight, I wonder?\n我就喜欢看到这种干劲十足的精神！也许你和你的朋友们真能打败我。不过，等我决定把我的朋友们也带来参战时，又会怎样呢？我真好奇。"

    old "What do you suppose he meant by that?"
    new "What do you suppose he meant by that?\n你觉得他这话是什么意思？"

    old "I think it means we shouldn't waste any more time in this room. It's a dead end for us, let's go back the way we came."
    new "I think it means we shouldn't waste any more time in this room. It's a dead end for us, let's go back the way we came.\n我想，那意味着我们不该再在这个房间浪费时间了。它对我们来说是个死胡同，我们原路返回吧。"

    old "We step onto the battlements and begin trekking back to the tower we first climbed up."
    new "We step onto the battlements and begin trekking back to the tower we first climbed up.\n我们走上城垛，开始返回我们最初爬上来的那座塔楼。"

    old "As we walk, I notice that the crows appear to be perched on the walls of the battlements, sitting completely still, as if poised and watching us. I feel a chill run down my spine, and my pace becomes more even and deliberate."
    new "As we walk, I notice that the crows appear to be perched on the walls of the battlements, sitting completely still, as if poised and watching us. I feel a chill run down my spine, and my pace becomes more even and deliberate.\n走着走着，我注意到乌鸦们似乎栖落在城垛的墙头，一动不动地坐着，仿佛蓄势待发地注视着我们。我感到一股寒意沿脊背窜下，脚步也变得愈发沉稳而谨慎。"

    old "Be careful. There's something deeply unsettling about these crows."
    new "Be careful. There's something deeply unsettling about these crows.\n小心。这些乌鸦身上，有种令人深感不安的东西。"

    old "I feel a gust of wind, and suddenly, the crows begin cawing. They begin flying in front of us, forming a wall of black feathers, as if trying to block our way forward—and then just as quickly, they disperse, leaving a lone figure in their wake. It's Zephyr."
    new "I feel a gust of wind, and suddenly, the crows begin cawing. They begin flying in front of us, forming a wall of black feathers, as if trying to block our way forward—and then just as quickly, they disperse, leaving a lone figure in their wake. It's Zephyr.\n我感到一阵狂风，突然，乌鸦们聒噪起来。它们飞到我们面前，聚成一堵黑色羽毛之墙，仿佛要挡住我们的去路——随即又迅速散开，留下一个孤零零的身影。是 Zephyr。"

    old "I must admit, I found that cramped little room to be quite stifling. But out here, I think I can show you what I'm really made of."
    new "I must admit, I found that cramped little room to be quite stifling. But out here, I think I can show you what I'm really made of.\n我得承认，那间狭小的屋子让我觉得憋闷。但到了外面，我想我可以让你们看看我真正的本事。"

    old "I'm going to cut you to shreds and feed your flesh to the crows. The birds usually prefer carrion, but they've been known to feast on the flesh of the living if they get a whiff of blood in the air. I guess that's why crows and I get along so well. That bloodlust is in our nature."
    new "I'm going to cut you to shreds and feed your flesh to the crows. The birds usually prefer carrion, but they've been known to feast on the flesh of the living if they get a whiff of blood in the air. I guess that's why crows and I get along so well. That bloodlust is in our nature.\n我要把你们剁成碎片，喂给乌鸦。这些鸟通常更喜欢腐肉，但据说只要闻到空气中的血腥味，它们也会大啖活人的血肉。我想，这正是乌鸦和我如此投缘的原因。嗜血是刻在我们骨子里的天性。"

    old "Zephyr takes several steps back. He wears a grin on his face, but he's breathing quickly. I don't know if vampires get winded, but he certainly doesn't like he's prepared to keep fighting."
    new "Zephyr takes several steps back. He wears a grin on his face, but he's breathing quickly. I don't know if vampires get winded, but he certainly doesn't like he's prepared to keep fighting.\nZephyr 后退了几步。他脸上挂着笑，呼吸却急促起来。我不知道 Vampires 会不会气喘，但他显然不像是做好了继续战斗的准备。"

    old "Why? Why are you here?"
    new "Why? Why are you here?\n为什么？你们为什么在这里？"

    old "We're here to kill vampires. And I see a vampire standing in front of me right now."
    new "We're here to kill vampires. And I see a vampire standing in front of me right now.\n我们是来杀 Vampires 的。而我眼前就站着一个 Vampire。"

    old "Very well, if that's what you want!"
    new "Very well, if that's what you want!\n很好，如果这是你们想要的！"

    old "He looks exhausted and injured. This time should be an easier fight."
    new "He looks exhausted and injured. This time should be an easier fight.\n他看上去精疲力尽、伤痕累累。这一次，战斗应该会轻松些。"

    old "We've come to rescue a friend."
    new "We've come to rescue a friend.\n我们是来救一位朋友的。"

    old "A friend? A captive, perhaps? Let's parley. I can tell you where to find your friend."
    new "A friend? A captive, perhaps? Let's parley. I can tell you where to find your friend.\n一位朋友？或许是个俘虏？我们来谈谈条件吧。我可以告诉你去哪里找你的朋友。"

    old "And what do you expect in exchange?"
    new "And what do you expect in exchange?\n那你想要什么作为交换？"

    old "Once you find your friend, leave this place."
    new "Once you find your friend, leave this place.\n找到你的朋友后，离开这里。"

    old "You tell us, and we'll spare your life. You'll disappear from this castle. Next time we encounter you, we'll kill you. Or you still think you can defeat us?"
    new "You tell us, and we'll spare your life. You'll disappear from this castle. Next time we encounter you, we'll kill you. Or you still think you can defeat us?\n你告诉我们，我们就饶你一命。你会从这座城堡消失。下次再遇上你，我们必取你性命。还是说，你仍觉得自己能打败我们？"

    old "Zephyr stays silent for a few seconds, then he speaks."
    new "Zephyr stays silent for a few seconds, then he speaks.\nZephyr 沉默了几秒，然后开口了。"

    old "Very well. I'll take your deal."
    new "Very well. I'll take your deal.\n很好。我接受你们的条件。"

    old "I believe this is what you wanted."
    new "I believe this is what you wanted.\n我想，这正是你们想要的。"

    old "I see Zephyr throwing something on the ground before disappearing into the mist."
    new "I see Zephyr throwing something on the ground before disappearing into the mist.\n我看到 Zephyr 往地上扔了样东西，随即消失在雾中。"

    old "How about we beat you to a pulp, and then you tell us?"
    new "How about we beat you to a pulp, and then you tell us?\n不如我们把你揍个半死，你再告诉我们？"

    old "Why would I tell you why we came here?"
    new "Why would I tell you why we came here?\n我凭什么告诉你，我们为什么来这里？"

    old "Maybe I know something. Maybe I can help you."
    new "Maybe I know something. Maybe I can help you.\n也许我知道些什么。也许我能帮上你们。"

    old "And why would you help us?"
    new "And why would you help us?\n你又为什么要帮我们？"

    old "Because maybe you can offer me something in return."
    new "Because maybe you can offer me something in return.\n因为，也许你们能给我点什么作为回报。"

    old "What is it that you plan to offer us?"
    new "What is it that you plan to offer us?\n你打算给我们什么？"

    old "You came here looking for something. Is it wealth? You came to plunder this castle? Because these battlements seem like an odd place to look for riches."
    new "You came here looking for something. Is it wealth? You came to plunder this castle? Because these battlements seem like an odd place to look for riches.\n你们来这里是为了找什么东西。是财富吗？你们来洗劫这座城堡？毕竟，在城垛上找财宝，可真是个奇怪的地方。"

    old "Or did you come here looking for someone?"
    new "Or did you come here looking for someone?\n还是说，你们是来找人的？"

    old "Let's stop talking, shall we?"
    new "Let's stop talking, shall we?\n我们别谈了吧，好吗？"

    old "Wait. I know! The amazon prisoners. I have the prison key! Here, take it!"
    new "Wait. I know! The amazon prisoners. I have the prison key! Here, take it!\n等等。我知道了！是那些 Amazon 囚犯。我有监狱的钥匙！来，拿去吧！"

    old "Spare me. I will go away. You'll never hear from me again."
    new "Spare me. I will go away. You'll never hear from me again.\n饶了我吧。我会离开的。你们再也不会听到我的消息。"

    old "I will! I didn't even like it here, to be honest. Too humid for my tastes."
    new "I will! I didn't even like it here, to be honest. Too humid for my tastes.\n我会的！老实说，我甚至不喜欢这里。对我来说太潮湿了。"

    old "You... you'll regret this!"
    new "You... you'll regret this!\n你们……你们会后悔的！"

    old "Haha...to think it would end like this..."
    new "Haha...to think it would end like this...\n哈哈……没想到会以这种方式收场……"

    old "Zephyr looks up. His skin seems to melt away and crumble under the moonlight, until all that remains of him is a cloak."
    new "Zephyr looks up. His skin seems to melt away and crumble under the moonlight, until all that remains of him is a cloak.\nZephyr 抬头望天。他的皮肤似乎在月光下融化、崩解，直到最后，他身上剩下的只有一件斗篷。"

    old "Good riddance."
    new "Good riddance.\n总算清净了。"

    old "I look on the ground, and I see a key."
    new "I look on the ground, and I see a key.\n我看向地面，看到一把钥匙。"

    old "This must be the prison key! Let's get back to the main hall!"
    new "This must be the prison key! Let's get back to the main hall!\n这一定就是监狱的钥匙！我们回主厅去！"

    old "We step into the library. I breath in, and I detect the musty odor of old paper."
    new "We step into the library. I breath in, and I detect the musty odor of old paper.\n我们走进图书馆。我深吸一口气，闻到旧纸张的霉味。"

    old "Here we are. The library. A place of learning."
    new "Here we are. The library. A place of learning.\n我们到了。图书馆。一处求学的所在。"

    old "This doesn't look like a place of learning per se. It seems more like an archive."
    new "This doesn't look like a place of learning per se. It seems more like an archive.\n这里本身并不太像求学之地。它更像一个档案馆。"

    old "Well, for one thing, some of these books have layers of glass in front of them. Normal libraries don't put up glass to prevent you from accessing their materials."
    new "Well, for one thing, some of these books have layers of glass in front of them. Normal libraries don't put up glass to prevent you from accessing their materials.\n首先，这些书里有些前面挡着一层层玻璃。普通图书馆可不会用玻璃挡住你，不让你取阅它们的藏书。"

    old "Not all of the books are covered. Look, this shelf is open."
    new "Not all of the books are covered. Look, this shelf is open.\n不是所有书都被挡着。你看，这个书架是敞开的。"

    old "I pick a book off the shelf and try skimming through the pages, but they're written in some kind of arcane language."
    new "I pick a book off the shelf and try skimming through the pages, but they're written in some kind of arcane language.\n我从书架上取下一本书，试着快速翻阅，可书页上写的却是某种奥术文字。"

    old "Can you read this?"
    new "Can you read this?\n你能读懂这个吗？"

    old "It doesn't look like anything to me."
    new "It doesn't look like anything to me.\n在我看来，什么都不是。"

    old "I can't read any of this."
    new "I can't read any of this.\n这些我一个字都读不懂。"

    old "Sadly, it's beyond my capability to decipher this."
    new "Sadly, it's beyond my capability to decipher this.\n可惜，这超出了我能破译的能力范围。"

    old "In all my years of study, I've never encountered text like this. Though, the shapes do somewhat resemble what I once saw in an old preserved demonic text. I wonder, is this simply a record of some kind, or some kind of sinister spellbook?"
    new "In all my years of study, I've never encountered text like this. Though, the shapes do somewhat resemble what I once saw in an old preserved demonic text. I wonder, is this simply a record of some kind, or some kind of sinister spellbook?\n在我多年的求学生涯里，从未见过这样的文字。不过，这些字形倒有些像我在一部保存完好的古老恶魔文献中见过的东西。我很好奇，这仅仅是某种记录，还是某种邪恶的咒术书？"

    old "It looks like all of these books are printed in the same script. I can't read any of this."
    new "It looks like all of these books are printed in the same script. I can't read any of this.\n看起来这些书都是用同一种文字印制的。这些我一点也看不懂。"

    old "Let's look further. These books look old and quite dusty. Maybe there are newer books that are written in a more contemporary language."
    new "Let's look further. These books look old and quite dusty. Maybe there are newer books that are written in a more contemporary language.\n我们再往里看看吧。这些书看上去又旧又积满灰尘。也许有较新的书，是用更现代的语言写成的。"

    old "I step past the next bookshelf."
    new "I step past the next bookshelf.\n我走过下一个书架。"

    old "Halt. Step no further."
    new "Halt. Step no further.\n站住。别再往前走了。"

    old "If you had eyes to read the door before you walked in, you would know that this is Adede's library. And I just so happen to be Adede. So you'll understand if I seem cross at your intrusion."
    new "If you had eyes to read the door before you walked in, you would know that this is Adede's library. And I just so happen to be Adede. So you'll understand if I seem cross at your intrusion.\n若你进门之前有眼睛看清门上的字，就会知道这是 Adede 的图书馆。而我恰好就是 Adede。所以，若我看上去对你们的闯入颇为不悦，也请你理解。"

    old "So, tell me, interlopers. What are you doing in my library?"
    new "So, tell me, interlopers. What are you doing in my library?\n那么，告诉我，闯入者们。你们在我的图书馆里做什么？"

    old "We came here seeking information."
    new "We came here seeking information.\n我们来这里是为了寻找情报。"

    old "Ah, you seek knowledge? Well, a library is a good place to find it. If only you had eyes to see what my eyes can see!"
    new "Ah, you seek knowledge? Well, a library is a good place to find it. If only you had eyes to see what my eyes can see!\n啊，你们寻求知识？那么，图书馆正是寻找它的好地方。但愿你们有眼，能看到我这双眼所看到的一切！"

    old "I come here to learn. But did you? I sense other motives in you. Looking at your armor and weapons, it seems you came here to do more than just read."
    new "I come here to learn. But did you? I sense other motives in you. Looking at your armor and weapons, it seems you came here to do more than just read.\n我来这里是为了学习。可你们是吗？我察觉到你们另有所图。看看你们的铠甲和武器，你们来这里，似乎不止是为了读书。"

    old "We're on a rescue mission. We came here looking for our friends."
    new "We're on a rescue mission. We came here looking for our friends.\n我们是在执行救援任务。我们是来找朋友的。"

    old "And so you came searching for them in the library? How curious. How do you suppose your friends might come to be trapped inside a place such as this?"
    new "And so you came searching for them in the library? How curious. How do you suppose your friends might come to be trapped inside a place such as this?\n于是你们就到图书馆里来找他们？真稀奇。你们的朋友怎么会被困在这样一个地方呢？"

    old "We came to kill you."
    new "We came to kill you.\n我们是来杀你的。"

    old "You came here to kill Adede? I did not realize that my name was known outside these castle walls. Curious..."
    new "You came here to kill Adede? I did not realize that my name was known outside these castle walls. Curious...\n你们来这里，是为了杀 Adede？我竟不知道，我的名字在城堡墙外也有人知晓。稀奇……"

    old "Could it be that you did not really come here to kill me specifically? It seems more likely that you simply have malicious intent, and you just so happened to encounter me. Do you intend to take that out on me? Well, it won't be happening."
    new "Could it be that you did not really come here to kill me specifically? It seems more likely that you simply have malicious intent, and you just so happened to encounter me. Do you intend to take that out on me? Well, it won't be happening.\n莫非你们并非专程来杀我的？更可能的情况是，你们只是心怀恶意，恰好撞见了我。你们打算把这股恶意撒在我身上？哼，那可不会如你们所愿。"

    old "If you draw weapons, I'll have to defend myself."
    new "If you draw weapons, I'll have to defend myself.\n若你们拔出武器，我就不得不自卫了。"

    old "Oh? And just how do you intend to do that?"
    new "Oh? And just how do you intend to do that?\n哦？你打算怎么自卫？"

    old "This is my place of study. I wish to be left alone. But you had to come and ruin that."
    new "This is my place of study. I wish to be left alone. But you had to come and ruin that.\n这里是我研习的地方。我只想独自待着。可你们偏要来，毁了这份清静。"

    old "We step into the abandoned chapel."
    new "We step into the abandoned chapel.\n我们走进废弃的小教堂。"

    old "This was once a place of prayer."
    new "This was once a place of prayer.\n这里曾是祈祷之所。"

    old "A place for the pious to gather and ward of evil. Now, it's surrounded by fields that harbor evil. How ironic."
    new "A place for the pious to gather and ward of evil. Now, it's surrounded by fields that harbor evil. How ironic.\n一个供虔诚之人聚集、驱避邪恶的地方。如今，它却被藏匿邪恶的田地所环绕。多么讽刺。"

    old "This place looks like it's seen better days."
    new "This place looks like it's seen better days.\n这地方看起来昔日的风光早已不再。"

    old "The core architecture of the building is still intact, but apart from that, it seems to be a mess. Vines cover the walls, cobwebs cover every corner and every nook that's visible, and a thick layer of dust covers the floor. Except...near the window, I see a place where the dust seems to have been disturbed. There seems to be dirt staining the floor."
    new "The core architecture of the building is still intact, but apart from that, it seems to be a mess. Vines cover the walls, cobwebs cover every corner and every nook that's visible, and a thick layer of dust covers the floor. Except...near the window, I see a place where the dust seems to have been disturbed. There seems to be dirt staining the floor.\n建筑的主体结构仍完好无损，但除此之外，这里一片狼藉。藤蔓爬满墙壁，蛛网覆盖着每一个看得见的角落和缝隙，地板上则积着一层厚厚的灰尘。只是……在窗边，我看到一处灰尘像是被人动过。地板上似乎沾着污迹。"

    old "I walk over to the floor, and as I get closer, I see that what I thought was dirt is actually streaks of blood that has just begun to dry. The blood streaks form a pattern, something that looks intentionally drawn."
    new "I walk over to the floor, and as I get closer, I see that what I thought was dirt is actually streaks of blood that has just begun to dry. The blood streaks form a pattern, something that looks intentionally drawn.\n我走到那处地板前，走近一看，才发现我以为是污迹的东西，其实是刚开始干涸的血痕。这些血痕构成某种图案，看上去是刻意画出来的。"

    old "How perverse, for a place that was once considered holy to be tainted by these profane markings."
    new "How perverse, for a place that was once considered holy to be tainted by these profane markings.\n一个曾被视为神圣的地方，竟被这些亵渎的印记玷污，实在令人作呕。"

    old "Is this what remains of some vampire's blood ritual?"
    new "Is this what remains of some vampire's blood ritual?\n这就是某个 Vampire 血之仪式的残留吗？"

    old "Whatever it is, it can't be good. Luckily, we came prepared."
    new "Whatever it is, it can't be good. Luckily, we came prepared.\n不管这是什么，都不会是好事。幸好，我们有备而来。"

    old "I reach for the bag of salt that Captain Thomas provided."
    new "I reach for the bag of salt that Captain Thomas provided.\n我伸手去拿 Thomas 船长提供的那袋盐。"

    old "Will salting a stone floor work the same way that salting the earth would?"
    new "Will salting a stone floor work the same way that salting the earth would?\n给石头地面撒盐，会和给土地撒盐有同样的效果吗？"

    old "Stone comes from the earth, you know. It's carved and polished, but it's still stone."
    new "Stone comes from the earth, you know. It's carved and polished, but it's still stone.\n你要知道，石头本就出自大地。它虽经雕琢打磨，可终究还是石头。"

    old "Hmm, for all the disrepair this chapel has suffered, this area seems to be in good shape. Look, a sort of library. And some books seem to have survived. Scriptures, perhaps?"
    new "Hmm, for all the disrepair this chapel has suffered, this area seems to be in good shape. Look, a sort of library. And some books seem to have survived. Scriptures, perhaps?\n嗯，这教堂虽破败不堪，这一带看上去却保存良好。看，像是个小藏书处。而且有些书似乎留存了下来。也许是经文？"

    old "Hold on. Those books don't look old and worn. They look like someone brought them here recently."
    new "Hold on. Those books don't look old and worn. They look like someone brought them here recently.\n等等。那些书看起来既不旧也不破。倒像是有人最近才带过来的。"

    old "Who would bring books to a place like this?"
    new "Who would bring books to a place like this?\n谁会带书到这种地方来？"

    old "I'm guessing it's whoever drew these patterns from blood. Maybe they aren't the kind of drawings that you make from memory."
    new "I'm guessing it's whoever drew these patterns from blood. Maybe they aren't the kind of drawings that you make from memory.\n我猜，就是用血画出这些图案的人。也许这些图案，不是单凭记忆就能画出来的。"

    old "I guess even vampires need a reference manual every now and then, huh?"
    new "I guess even vampires need a reference manual every now and then, huh?\n看来，就算 Vampires 也偶尔需要一本参考手册，对吧？"

    old "Then why so many books?"
    new "Then why so many books?\n那为什么有这么多书？"

    old "A bookworm vampire, perhaps?"
    new "A bookworm vampire, perhaps?\n也许是个书虫 Vampire？"

    old "Now's not the time for jokes."
    new "Now's not the time for jokes.\n现在不是开玩笑的时候。"

    old "Agreed. There's no reason for us to linger any longer. Let's get moving."
    new "Agreed. There's no reason for us to linger any longer. Let's get moving.\n同意。我们没有理由再逗留了。动身吧。"

    old "If you had eyes to read the circle you just destroyed, you would know that it was made by Adede. And I just so happen to be Adede. So you'll understand if I seem cross at your intrusion."
    new "If you had eyes to read the circle you just destroyed, you would know that it was made by Adede. And I just so happen to be Adede. So you'll understand if I seem cross at your intrusion.\n若你有眼睛看清你们刚刚毁掉的那个圆圈，就会知道它是 Adede 所画。而我恰好就是 Adede。所以，若我看上去对你们的闯入颇为不悦，也请你理解。"

    old "You've made quite a mess of things here. Why, it will take me weeks to reconstruct the ritual summoning grounds that you've just salted. All of my work, undone so quickly."
    new "You've made quite a mess of things here. Why, it will take me weeks to reconstruct the ritual summoning grounds that you've just salted. All of my work, undone so quickly.\n你们把这里搅得一团糟。哎呀，要重建你们刚刚撒盐毁掉的仪式召唤法阵，我得花上好几周。我所有的努力，就这样被你们瞬间化为乌有。"

    old "So, tell me, interlopers. What are you doing here?"
    new "So, tell me, interlopers. What are you doing here?\n那么，告诉我，闯入者们。你们在这里做什么？"

    old "We're explorers."
    new "We're explorers.\n我们是探险者。"

    old "Exploring, on a night such as this? I always doubt the words of a [prace], and now I have reason to doubt them even more. You have other motives, I'm sure. You wouldn't have destroyed my ritual otherwise."
    new "Exploring, on a night such as this? I always doubt the words of a [prace], and now I have reason to doubt them even more. You have other motives, I'm sure. You wouldn't have destroyed my ritual otherwise.\n在这样一个夜晚探险？我一直都对 [prace] 的话心存怀疑，如今我更有理由怀疑了。我敢肯定，你们另有所图。否则你们也不会毁掉我的仪式。"

    old "You came here to kill Adede? I did not realize that my name was known outside the walls of castle N'Mar. Curious..."
    new "You came here to kill Adede? I did not realize that my name was known outside the walls of castle N'Mar. Curious...\n你们来这里，是为了杀 Adede？我竟不知道，我的名字在 N'Mar 城堡的墙外也有人知晓。稀奇……"

    old "This is where I have come to practice my rituals. I wish to be left alone. But you had to come and ruin that."
    new "This is where I have come to practice my rituals. I wish to be left alone. But you had to come and ruin that.\n这里是我来演练仪式的地方。我只想独自待着。可你们偏要来，毁了这份清静。"

    old "Yet...you haven't attacked me. What could be motivating that, I wonder? Are you scared? Or could you be...hmm."
    new "Yet...you haven't attacked me. What could be motivating that, I wonder? Are you scared? Or could you be...hmm.\n然而……你们还没有攻击我。这会是什么原因呢，我很好奇。你们害怕了？还是说，你们可能……嗯。"

    old "Adede seems unalarmed by our appearance. It seems like a mix of disinterest and a feeling of confident superiority. Almost as if we're not a big enough threat to be worried about. Strange. I would normally expect undead to desire an end to us, but Adede seems to be more thoughtful, almost as if waiting for a reason to act."
    new "Adede seems unalarmed by our appearance. It seems like a mix of disinterest and a feeling of confident superiority. Almost as if we're not a big enough threat to be worried about. Strange. I would normally expect undead to desire an end to us, but Adede seems to be more thoughtful, almost as if waiting for a reason to act.\nAdede 对我们的出现似乎毫不惊慌。那神情像是漠不关心与自信优越感的混合。仿佛我们还不构成足以让她担忧的威胁。奇怪。我本以为亡灵会急于置我们于死地，可 Adede 似乎更深思熟虑，几乎像是在等待一个动手的理由。"

    old "I'm afraid I can't let you leave this place. It won't do to have interlopers traipsing about the castle."
    new "I'm afraid I can't let you leave this place. It won't do to have interlopers traipsing about the castle.\n恐怕我不能放你们离开这里。让闯入者在城堡里四处游荡，可不成体统。"

    old "I'm afraid I can't let you leave this place. Not on a night like tonight. Your journey ends here."
    new "I'm afraid I can't let you leave this place. Not on a night like tonight. Your journey ends here.\n恐怕我不能放你们离开这里。至少，在今晚这样的夜晚不行。你们的旅程到此为止。"

    old "My powers have waned with age, but they should be more than enough to deal with the likes of you."
    new "My powers have waned with age, but they should be more than enough to deal with the likes of you.\n我的力量已随岁月衰退，但要对付你们这等货色，应当绰绰有余。"

    old "Wait. Maybe we can find a peaceful solution to all this. As proof of my good faith, I have a valuable gift for you. Here, take it."
    new "Wait. Maybe we can find a peaceful solution to all this. As proof of my good faith, I have a valuable gift for you. Here, take it.\n等等。也许我们能为这一切找到和平的解决之道。作为我诚意的证明，我有份珍贵的礼物送你。来，拿去吧。"

    old "Adede takes the vial in her hands, she looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness."
    new "Adede takes the vial in her hands, she looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness.\nAdede 接过小瓶，神情困惑，被我的好意弄得措手不及。"

    old "Sniff...blood? I am so thirsty..."
    new "Sniff...blood? I am so thirsty...\n嗅嗅……是血？我好渴……"

    old "It should taste great. It's my own blood."
    new "It should taste great. It's my own blood.\n味道应该很好。那是我自己的血。"

    old "Unable to resist, Adede swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as she finishes though, she starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal."
    new "Unable to resist, Adede swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as she finishes though, she starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal.\nAdede 无法抗拒，一口吞下了瓶中的全部内容。然而刚一喝完，她便开始感到不适。Zachary 和 Valery 说过，这毒应当是致命的。"

    old "Gurbl...you...bwurghl...!"
    new "Gurbl...you...bwurghl...!\n咕噜……你……呕噜……！"

    old "Adede collapses to the floor. No, it would be more accurate to say that Adede's clothes collapse as Adede's body fades away into a fine dust."
    new "Adede collapses to the floor. No, it would be more accurate to say that Adede's clothes collapse as Adede's body fades away into a fine dust.\nAdede 倒在地上。不，更准确地说，是 Adede 的衣服瘫倒下来，因为她的身体化作了细细的尘土。"

    old "What was that, [protag]?"
    new "What was that, [protag]?\n那是什么，[protag]？"

    old "I poisoned her using a trick!"
    new "I poisoned her using a trick!\n我用计毒死了她！"

    old "Smart! But... was that really your blood?"
    new "Smart! But... was that really your blood?\n聪明！不过……那真的是你的血吗？"

    old "They don't need to know the whole truth. It would be a bit weird to explain them that I did a blood ritual with two vampires."
    new "They don't need to know the whole truth. It would be a bit weird to explain them that I did a blood ritual with two vampires.\n他们不需要知道全部真相。跟他们解释我和两个 Vampires 做过血之仪式，会有点怪。"

    old "Perhaps this doesn't need to end in a fight. You seem bothered by our presence."
    new "Perhaps this doesn't need to end in a fight. You seem bothered by our presence.\n也许这事未必非要兵戎相见。我们的出现，似乎让你很困扰。"

    old "Bothered, yes."
    new "Bothered, yes.\n困扰，没错。"

    old "Were it all the same to you, you would probably rather not have encountered us in the first place."
    new "Were it all the same to you, you would probably rather not have encountered us in the first place.\n如果由你决定，你大概宁愿一开始就没遇见我们。"

    old "Yes, that would have been ideal."
    new "Yes, that would have been ideal.\n是的，那样就再好不过了。"

    old "What if you hadn't found us?"
    new "What if you hadn't found us?\n要是你根本没找到我们呢？"

    old "But I did find you."
    new "But I did find you.\n可我的确找到了你们。"

    old "Yes, but what if you acted as though you hadn't found us? That would solve your problem, would it not? You could act oblivious to our presence, and we would no longer be your problem."
    new "Yes, but what if you acted as though you hadn't found us? That would solve your problem, would it not? You could act oblivious to our presence, and we would no longer be your problem.\n是的，但要是你装作没找到我们呢？那不就解决了你的烦恼吗？你可以对我们的存在佯装不知，我们也就不再是你的麻烦了。"

    old "Hmm. That is not a bad point."
    new "Hmm. That is not a bad point.\n嗯。这倒不失为一个好主意。"

    old "It's as I thought. Adede seems to be more wrapped up with the library and studying than with the welfare of the actual castle. For all Adede cares, we could probably ransack this place."
    new "It's as I thought. Adede seems to be more wrapped up with the library and studying than with the welfare of the actual castle. For all Adede cares, we could probably ransack this place.\n正如我所料。比起城堡本身的安危，Adede 似乎更醉心于图书馆和研习。以 Adede 的心思，我们就算把这里洗劫一空，她大概也不在乎。"

    old "We'll leave, then. We just need one thing from you."
    new "We'll leave, then. We just need one thing from you.\n那我们这就离开。我们只需要你给一样东西。"

    old "The prisoners. We can't very well leave without them."
    new "The prisoners. We can't very well leave without them.\n那些囚犯。没有他们，我们可没法就这样离开。"

    old "Then...take this key."
    new "Then...take this key.\n那么……拿上这把钥匙。"

    old "Promise us you'll go away as soon as possible. You shouldn't stay here any longer."
    new "Promise us you'll go away as soon as possible. You shouldn't stay here any longer.\n答应我们，尽快离开。你不该再留在这里了。"

    old "Away? Why I should? This library has a lot of books. Lots of resources. Perfect place for my studies."
    new "Away? Why I should? This library has a lot of books. Lots of resources. Perfect place for my studies.\n离开？我为什么要离开？这图书馆有大量藏书，资源丰富。是我研习的绝佳之地。"

    old "Look, we're trying to help you. There are many more like us that will come here."
    new "Look, we're trying to help you. There are many more like us that will come here.\n听着，我们是在帮你。还会有更多像我们这样的人来这里。"

    old "What? More intruders like you?"
    new "What? More intruders like you?\n什么？更多像你们这样的闯入者？"

    old "Yes. And you don't know when they'll come. It could be tomorrow, in two days, in a week. They'll suddenly show up, and interrupt your studies again like we did."
    new "Yes. And you don't know when they'll come. It could be tomorrow, in two days, in a week. They'll suddenly show up, and interrupt your studies again like we did.\n是的。而且你不知道他们何时会来。可能是明天、两天后，或一周后。他们会突然出现，像我们一样，再次打断你的研习。"

    old "No. This is too much. You're right. I need to find a quiet place for my studies. Yes, I'll grab my stuff and leave. Thanks for telling me."
    new "No. This is too much. You're right. I need to find a quiet place for my studies. Yes, I'll grab my stuff and leave. Thanks for telling me.\n不。这太过分了。你说得对。我得找个安静的地方继续研习。是的，我收拾东西离开。谢谢你告诉我。"

    old "Incredible. She really didn't care at all about the castle or other vampires. All she cared about was her books and studying. Unexpected, but welcome."
    new "Incredible. She really didn't care at all about the castle or other vampires. All she cared about was her books and studying. Unexpected, but welcome.\n难以置信。她真的一点都不在乎这座城堡，也不在乎其他 Vampires。她在乎的只有她的书和研习。出乎意料，但令人欣慰。"

    old "Yes, that would have been ideal. Though it would have been more ideal had you not disturbed my ritual in progress."
    new "Yes, that would have been ideal. Though it would have been more ideal had you not disturbed my ritual in progress.\n是的，那样就再好不过了。不过，要是你们没有打扰我进行中的仪式，那就更理想了。"

    old "You said you would need several weeks to reconstruct your rituals. Why don't we leave you alone, so that you can repair the damage?"
    new "You said you would need several weeks to reconstruct your rituals. Why don't we leave you alone, so that you can repair the damage?\n你说过，重建你的仪式需要好几周。我们不如就此离开，好让你修复损伤？"

    old "There would be no point, anyway. These rituals are not something one performs on a whim."
    new "There would be no point, anyway. These rituals are not something one performs on a whim.\n反正也没什么意义。这些仪式并非心血来潮就能举行的东西。"

    old "Well, whatever you plan to do with that time, we can leave you to it."
    new "Well, whatever you plan to do with that time, we can leave you to it.\n好吧，无论你打算用那段时间做什么，我们都可以留给你自行处理。"

    old "Hmm. I see. You wouldn't come to disturb me again?"
    new "Hmm. I see. You wouldn't come to disturb me again?\n嗯。我明白了。你们不会再来打扰我了吧？"

    old "It's as I thought. Adede seems to be more preoccupied with being left alone than actually helping the rest of the vampires with the invasion of Grimoire."
    new "It's as I thought. Adede seems to be more preoccupied with being left alone than actually helping the rest of the vampires with the invasion of Grimoire.\n正如我所料。比起真正帮助其他 Vampires 入侵 Grimoire，Adede 似乎更惦记着独处清静。"

    old "We'll leave, then. But I must warn you, this is not a region where you want to stay."
    new "We'll leave, then. But I must warn you, this is not a region where you want to stay.\n那我们这就离开。但我必须警告你，这里可不是你想久留的地方。"

    old "And why would that be?"
    new "And why would that be?\n那是为什么？"

    old "Well, let's just say that we're not the only ones who are walking these plains. If you want to remain undisturbed, this is the wrong area to be."
    new "Well, let's just say that we're not the only ones who are walking these plains. If you want to remain undisturbed, this is the wrong area to be.\n这么说吧，在这些平原上游荡的，可不止我们这一拨。你若想不被打扰，这里可不是该待的地方。"

    old "Yes. And you don't know when they'll come. It could be tomorrow, in two days, in a week. They'll suddenly show up, and interrupt your business like we just did."
    new "Yes. And you don't know when they'll come. It could be tomorrow, in two days, in a week. They'll suddenly show up, and interrupt your business like we just did.\n是的。而且你不知道他们何时会来。可能是明天、两天后，或一周后。他们会突然出现，像我们刚才那样打断你的事。"

    old "No. This is too much. You're right. I need to find a quiet place for my rituals. Yes, I'll grab my stuff and leave. Thanks for telling me."
    new "No. This is too much. You're right. I need to find a quiet place for my rituals. Yes, I'll grab my stuff and leave. Thanks for telling me.\n不。这太过分了。你说得对。我得找个安静的地方举行我的仪式。是的，我收拾东西离开。谢谢你告诉我。"

    old "Perhaps we can find a mutually beneficial solution, based on our interests."
    new "Perhaps we can find a mutually beneficial solution, based on our interests.\n也许，基于我们各自的利益，我们能找到一个互利共赢的解决办法。"

    old "You want to be left alone in your library. You'd rather study than deal with a fight, wouldn't you? We don't want a fight, either."
    new "You want to be left alone in your library. You'd rather study than deal with a fight, wouldn't you? We don't want a fight, either.\n你想独自待在图书馆里。你宁愿研习，也不愿应付一场战斗，对吧？我们也不想打。"

    old "However, I'm afraid that even if we go away, or if you managed to kill us, that wouldn't matter."
    new "However, I'm afraid that even if we go away, or if you managed to kill us, that wouldn't matter.\n然而，恐怕即便我们离开，或你设法杀了我们，也无济于事。"

    old "Why? With you gone, I can enjoy some peace and quiet."
    new "Why? With you gone, I can enjoy some peace and quiet.\n为什么？你们一走，我就能享受些许安宁了。"

    old "We're just one of the many teams sent to investigate. Another one will come. And then, in a few hours, tomorrow, in a few days, another one will come again."
    new "We're just one of the many teams sent to investigate. Another one will come. And then, in a few hours, tomorrow, in a few days, another one will come again.\n我们只是被派来调查的众多小队之一。还会有另一队来。然后，几小时后、明天、几天后，又会再来一队。"

    old "What?! This is unacceptable! How I am supposed to complete any of my rituals or do any research if I am constantly interrupted?"
    new "What?! This is unacceptable! How I am supposed to complete any of my rituals or do any research if I am constantly interrupted?\n什么？！这太不可接受了！若我不断被打扰，还怎么完成任何仪式、做任何研究？"

    old "See? I'm taking your interests seriously, I only want to help you."
    new "See? I'm taking your interests seriously, I only want to help you.\n看到了吗？我是在认真对待你的利益，我只想帮你。"

    old "Hmm. Very well, thank you for your advice. You can go. And I'll go too from this place. Just a moment to take some supplies with me."
    new "Hmm. Very well, thank you for your advice. You can go. And I'll go too from this place. Just a moment to take some supplies with me.\n嗯。很好，谢谢你的建议。你们可以走了。我也要离开这个地方。稍等片刻，我带些补给。"

    old "It seems to have worked! I wonder of Apolimesho would believe this story if I told him what just happened. We exit the chapel while Adede is preparing to leave."
    new "It seems to have worked! I wonder of Apolimesho would believe this story if I told him what just happened. We exit the chapel while Adede is preparing to leave.\n似乎奏效了！我在想，若我把刚才发生的事告诉 Apolimesho，他会不会相信。趁 Adede 准备离开之际，我们走出小教堂。"

    old "Yes, but you must be dealt with."
    new "Yes, but you must be dealt with.\n是的，但必须把你们解决掉。"

    old "What would constitute 'dealing' with us?"
    new "What would constitute 'dealing' with us?\n所谓解决我们，是指什么？"

    old "You'd need to leave."
    new "You'd need to leave.\n你们得离开。"

    old "Then we'll do that. We just need one thing."
    new "Then we'll do that. We just need one thing.\n那我们就照做。我们只需要一样东西。"

    old "And what might that be?"
    new "And what might that be?\n那会是什么？"

    old "The prisoners. We're not leaving this castle without them."
    new "The prisoners. We're not leaving this castle without them.\n那些囚犯。不带上他们，我们绝不离开这座城堡。"

    old "You're just giving it to us?"
    new "You're just giving it to us?\n你就这样给我们了？"

    old "Yes, provided that you leave."
    new "Yes, provided that you leave.\n是的，只要你们离开。"

    old "Why? With you gone, I can resume my studies."
    new "Why? With you gone, I can resume my studies.\n为什么？你们一走，我就能继续研习了。"

    old "We're just one of the many teams sent to the castle. Another one will come. And then, in a few hours, tomorrow, in a few days, another one will come again."
    new "We're just one of the many teams sent to the castle. Another one will come. And then, in a few hours, tomorrow, in a few days, another one will come again.\n我们只是被派来城堡的众多小队之一。还会有另一队来。然后，几小时后、明天、几天后，又会再来一队。"

    old "What?! This is unacceptable! How I am supposed to study if I get constantly interrupted?"
    new "What?! This is unacceptable! How I am supposed to study if I get constantly interrupted?\n什么？！这太不可接受了！若我不断被打扰，还怎么研习？"

    old "Hmm. Very well, thank you for your advice. You can go. And I'll go too. Just a moment to take some books with me."
    new "Hmm. Very well, thank you for your advice. You can go. And I'll go too. Just a moment to take some books with me.\n嗯。很好，谢谢你的建议。你们可以走了。我也要离开。稍等片刻，我带几本书。"

    old "It seems to have worked! When I'll tell this to Apolimesho, he won't believe me. I head back to the main hall while Adede is preparing to leave."
    new "It seems to have worked! When I'll tell this to Apolimesho, he won't believe me. I head back to the main hall while Adede is preparing to leave.\n似乎奏效了！等我把这事告诉 Apolimesho，他准不会相信。趁 Adede 准备离开之际，我返回主厅。"

    old "Adede, we didn't come to this place to yield the first time we encountered a monster like you."
    new "Adede, we didn't come to this place to yield the first time we encountered a monster like you.\nAdede，我们来到此地，可不是为了第一次遇到你这样的怪物就退缩。"

    old "You've already ruined several of my books. Haven't you done enough?"
    new "You've already ruined several of my books. Haven't you done enough?\n你们已经毁掉我好些书了。你们做得还不够吗？"

    old "By the time we're done with you, you're going to wish that having your reading collection ruined was the worst thing that happened to you."
    new "By the time we're done with you, you're going to wish that having your reading collection ruined was the worst thing that happened to you.\n等我们收拾完你，你会巴不得自己遇到的最糟的事，不过是藏书被毁。"

    old "You've already ruined my ritual. Haven't you done enough?"
    new "You've already ruined my ritual. Haven't you done enough?\n你们已经毁掉我的仪式了。你们做得还不够吗？"

    old "By the time we're done with you, you're going to wish that having your little blood drawings ruined was the worst thing that happened to you."
    new "By the time we're done with you, you're going to wish that having your little blood drawings ruined was the worst thing that happened to you.\n等我们收拾完你，你会巴不得自己遇到的最糟的事，不过是那些小小的血画被毁。"

    old "If you have no intention of backing down, then I suppose I have no choice. Prepare to die."
    new "If you have no intention of backing down, then I suppose I have no choice. Prepare to die.\n若你们无意退让，那我想我也别无选择了。准备受死吧。"

    old "How many nice books are there. A pity if they got damaged somehow."
    new "How many nice books are there. A pity if they got damaged somehow.\n这里的好书可真多。要是它们不知怎地受损了，那多可惜。"

    old "It's dangerous to keep fighting. The books might get damaged."
    new "It's dangerous to keep fighting. The books might get damaged.\n继续打下去很危险。这些书可能会受损。"

    old "Those books looks very interesting. I understand now why you care so much about them."
    new "Those books looks very interesting. I understand now why you care so much about them.\n那些书看起来很有意思。我现在明白，你为什么这么在乎它们了。"

    old "You look tired. Why don't we take a break to talk again?"
    new "You look tired. Why don't we take a break to talk again?\n你看起来很累。我们何不再歇一歇，谈一谈？"

    old "Adede glares at me."
    new "Adede glares at me.\nAdede 怒视着我。"

    old "You. You've really ruined things here. It's unforgivable."
    new "You. You've really ruined things here. It's unforgivable.\n你。你真的把这里的一切都毁了。这不可原谅。"

    old "You can't keep up this fight, Adede. We'll win."
    new "You can't keep up this fight, Adede. We'll win.\n这场战斗你撑不下去了，Adede。我们会赢的。"

    old "I can defeat you. I just need a little help. Little ones! Come out!"
    new "I can defeat you. I just need a little help. Little ones! Come out!\n我能打败你们。我只需要一点小小的帮助。小家伙们！出来吧！"

    old "I see what appears to be a wave of black cascading from the bookcase, and for a moment it seems like a wave of darkness sweeping through the library before I realize what is really happening."
    new "I see what appears to be a wave of black cascading from the bookcase, and for a moment it seems like a wave of darkness sweeping through the library before I realize what is really happening.\n我看到一片黑色浪潮从书架上倾泻而下，有那么一瞬，它仿佛一股席卷图书馆的黑暗之潮，随后我才意识到究竟发生了什么。"

    old "I see what appears to be a wave of black cascading from the corners of the room. The numerous cobwebs that I ignored upon entering now seem much more menacing as I realize just what this wave of cascading darkness is."
    new "I see what appears to be a wave of black cascading from the corners of the room. The numerous cobwebs that I ignored upon entering now seem much more menacing as I realize just what this wave of cascading darkness is.\n我看到一片黑色浪潮从房间四角倾泻而出。我进门时没当回事的无数蛛网，此刻显得狰狞许多，因为我终于看清这股倾泻而下的黑暗究竟是什么。"

    old "Spiders!"
    new "Spiders!\n蜘蛛！"

    old "Spiders crawl from the many nooks and crannies amongst the bookcases, covering the floor around us. The way the spiders move in waves, it seems like they almost bend directly to Adede's will, puppeting them much in the way a necromancer might puppet dead flesh."
    new "Spiders crawl from the many nooks and crannies amongst the bookcases, covering the floor around us. The way the spiders move in waves, it seems like they almost bend directly to Adede's will, puppeting them much in the way a necromancer might puppet dead flesh.\n蜘蛛从书架间的众多缝隙和角落里爬出，铺满了我们周围的地面。这些蜘蛛如浪潮般涌动的姿态，仿佛几乎完全听命于 Adede 的意志，正像一个死灵法师操控死尸那般，把它们当作傀儡。"

    old "Now, prepare to die a death by a thousand venomous bites. Have at you!"
    new "Now, prepare to die a death by a thousand venomous bites. Have at you!\n现在，准备迎接千次毒咬之死吧。看招！"

    old "There's no way we can fight those spiders, they're too small to hit. We'll have to quickly defeat Adede who seems to be controlling them somehow!"
    new "There's no way we can fight those spiders, they're too small to hit. We'll have to quickly defeat Adede who seems to be controlling them somehow!\n我们没法跟那些蜘蛛打，它们太小，根本打不中。我们得尽快击败 Adede，她似乎正以某种方式操控它们！"

    old "Not even your spiders can slow us down!"
    new "Not even your spiders can slow us down!\n连你的蜘蛛也拖不住我们！"

    old "The spiders was an interesting trick. A pity that it didn't work. You noticed it, right?"
    new "The spiders was an interesting trick. A pity that it didn't work. You noticed it, right?\n那蜘蛛是记有趣的把戏。可惜没奏效。你注意到了吧？"

    old "The spiders magic was really interesting. Did you read it in those precious books? Maybe I should give you another chance to leave peacefully."
    new "The spiders magic was really interesting. Did you read it in those precious books? Maybe I should give you another chance to leave peacefully.\n那蜘蛛魔法真有意思。你是在那些珍贵的书里学到的吗？也许我该再给你一次和平离开的机会。"

    old "Please, we don't want to hurt your spider friends. Talk to us face to face, let's find a solution."
    new "Please, we don't want to hurt your spider friends. Talk to us face to face, let's find a solution.\n拜托，我们不想伤害你的蜘蛛朋友。面对面和我们谈谈吧，我们一起想个办法。"

    old "Adede seems to be growing weary, and the spiders around us seem to be moving less decisively and less confidently. It seems like they really are tied to Adede's will. And if the spiders are growing weaker, that must mean..."
    new "Adede seems to be growing weary, and the spiders around us seem to be moving less decisively and less confidently. It seems like they really are tied to Adede's will. And if the spiders are growing weaker, that must mean...\nAdede 似乎愈发疲惫，而我们周围的蜘蛛，动作也渐渐不再果断、不再自信。看来它们真的与 Adede 的意志相连。若蜘蛛们越来越虚弱，那就意味着……"

    old "It's over for you, Adede. You're on the verge of collapse."
    new "It's over for you, Adede. You're on the verge of collapse.\n你完了，Adede。你就快倒下了。"

    old "Hah. And what exactly do you intend to do about it?"
    new "Hah. And what exactly do you intend to do about it?\n哈。那你究竟打算怎么做？"

    old "You've walked this earth for too long, Adede. Your journey comes to an end now."
    new "You've walked this earth for too long, Adede. Your journey comes to an end now.\n你在这世间行走太久了，Adede。你的旅程到此结束。"

    old "Very well. I won't hold back this time, I'll use all the magic spells I've learned from these books. And your trick won't work with me anymore!"
    new "Very well. I won't hold back this time, I'll use all the magic spells I've learned from these books. And your trick won't work with me anymore!\n很好。这次我不会再留手了，我要使出从这些书中学到的所有魔法。而你的把戏，对我再也行不通了！"

    old "{i}Adede looks furious. My social talents won't work against her this time.{/i}"
    new "{i}Adede looks furious. My social talents won't work against her this time.{/i}\n{i}Adede 怒不可遏。这一次，我的社交技巧对她不会再起作用了。{/i}"

    old "Adede collapses to the floor. No, it would be more accurate to say that Adede's clothes collapse as Adede's body fades away into a fine dust. The crowd of remaining spiders disperses, going off to hide away in whatever nook or cranny they came from, and I go over to inspect Adede's remains."
    new "Adede collapses to the floor. No, it would be more accurate to say that Adede's clothes collapse as Adede's body fades away into a fine dust. The crowd of remaining spiders disperses, going off to hide away in whatever nook or cranny they came from, and I go over to inspect Adede's remains.\nAdede 倒在地上。不，更准确地说，是 Adede 的衣服瘫倒下来，因为她的身体化作了细细的尘土。剩下的蜘蛛群四散而去，躲回它们各自来的缝隙角落，我则走过去查看 Adede 的遗骸。"

    old "That looks like a key, if my eyes don't deceive me."
    new "That looks like a key, if my eyes don't deceive me.\n那看起来像把钥匙，若我的眼睛没骗我的话。"

    old "Anything useful on her?"
    new "Anything useful on her?\n她身上有什么有用的东西吗？"

    old "Nothing. Let's get back to the main hall."
    new "Nothing. Let's get back to the main hall.\n没有。我们回主厅吧。"

    old "We'll spare you, if you leave these plains immediately."
    new "We'll spare you, if you leave these plains immediately.\n若你立即离开这些平原，我们就饶你一命。"

    old "But where will I go? My books..."
    new "But where will I go? My books...\n可我能去哪儿呢？我的书……"

    old "You'll find another place to set up shop. Or you can take some books with you, I don't care. As long as you leave this place immediately. Unless you want to die."
    new "You'll find another place to set up shop. Or you can take some books with you, I don't care. As long as you leave this place immediately. Unless you want to die.\n你会另找个地方安顿下来。或者你也可以带上几本书，我无所谓。只要你立刻离开这里。除非你想死。"

    old "No! Let me take this, and this."
    new "No! Let me take this, and this.\n不！让我带上这本，还有这本。"

    old "Adede grabs a stack of books and puts them in a bag. I watch her, and when she's finished, I tell her:"
    new "Adede grabs a stack of books and puts them in a bag. I watch her, and when she's finished, I tell her:\nAdede 抓起一摞书，塞进袋子里。我看着她，待她收拾完，我对她说："

    old "Good. Now leave. If we see you again, next time we'll kill you."
    new "Good. Now leave. If we see you again, next time we'll kill you.\n很好。现在走吧。若再见到你，下次我们必取你性命。"

    old "We'll spare you, if you can assist with our mission."
    new "We'll spare you, if you can assist with our mission.\n若你能协助我们的任务，我们就饶你一命。"

    old "Mission? What would that be?"
    new "Mission? What would that be?\n任务？那是什么？"

    old "We came here to rescue the prisoners being kept in your dungeon. Help us rescue the prisoners, and you can walk free."
    new "We came here to rescue the prisoners being kept in your dungeon. Help us rescue the prisoners, and you can walk free.\n我们是来营救关押在地牢里的囚犯的。帮我们救出囚犯，你就能自由离开。"

    old "Very well. If giving you the dungeon key will make you leave this place, then I'll give it to you."
    new "Very well. If giving you the dungeon key will make you leave this place, then I'll give it to you.\n很好。若把地牢钥匙交给你们，能让你们离开此地，那我就给你们。"

    old "Adede tosses the key toward us, and it clatters to the floor as the spiders make way."
    new "Adede tosses the key toward us, and it clatters to the floor as the spiders make way.\nAdede 把钥匙朝我们扔来，蜘蛛们让开去路，钥匙叮当作响地落在地上。"

    old "I trust we're done here."
    new "I trust we're done here.\n我想我们的事就此了结了。"

    old "Adede ducks behind one of the bookcases, and I don't make a move to pursue."
    new "Adede ducks behind one of the bookcases, and I don't make a move to pursue.\nAdede 闪身躲到一座书架后面，我没有上前追赶。"

    old "Let's get out of here."
    new "Let's get out of here.\n我们离开这里吧。"

    old "We'll spare you, if you leave the castle immediately."
    new "We'll spare you, if you leave the castle immediately.\n若你立即离开城堡，我们就饶你一命。"

    old "But where I'll go? This library... all the books in it..."
    new "But where I'll go? This library... all the books in it...\n可我能去哪儿呢？这图书馆……里面所有的书……"

    old "You'll find another one. Or you can take some books with you, I don't care. As long as you leave this place immediately. Unless you want to die."
    new "You'll find another one. Or you can take some books with you, I don't care. As long as you leave this place immediately. Unless you want to die.\n你会另找一个图书馆。或者你也可以带上几本书，我无所谓。只要你立刻离开这里。除非你想死。"

    old "Adede grabs a few books from the library and puts them in a bag. I watch her, and when she's finished, I tell her:"
    new "Adede grabs a few books from the library and puts them in a bag. I watch her, and when she's finished, I tell her:\nAdede 从图书馆里抓了几本书，塞进袋子里。我看着她，待她收拾完，我对她说："

    old "I take the key and head back to the main hall. I hear Adede talking to herself as I leave."
    new "I take the key and head back to the main hall. I hear Adede talking to herself as I leave.\n我拿起钥匙，返回主厅。离开时，我听到 Adede 在自言自语。"

    old "Too much noise. I can't concentrate on my studies. Hmm. I should move to another place. Yes, I should. I need to be alone, I need silence."
    new "Too much noise. I can't concentrate on my studies. Hmm. I should move to another place. Yes, I should. I need to be alone, I need silence.\n太吵了。我没法专心研习。嗯。我该搬到别处去。是的，我该搬。我需要独处，需要安静。"

    old "Well if she decides to leave this place, I won't be the one stopping her."
    new "Well if she decides to leave this place, I won't be the one stopping her.\n好吧，若她决定离开这里，我可不会去拦她。"

    old "We head to the barren wastes."
    new "We head to the barren wastes.\n我们朝荒芜的废土进发。"

    old "What exactly are we looking for? There's...nothing here."
    new "What exactly are we looking for? There's...nothing here.\n我们究竟在找什么？这里……什么都没有。"

    old "No grass, no trees, no sign of any sort of life...I wonder if all of the plains will eventually become like this."
    new "No grass, no trees, no sign of any sort of life...I wonder if all of the plains will eventually become like this.\n没有草，没有树，没有任何生命的迹象……我在想，是否所有平原最终都会变成这样。"

    old "Not all barren areas are that way due to the corruption. N'Mar's plains have always had some barren areas, especially near Hammerhands, places where the soil just isn't hospitable to plant life."
    new "Not all barren areas are that way due to the corruption. N'Mar's plains have always had some barren areas, especially near Hammerhands, places where the soil just isn't hospitable to plant life.\n并非所有荒芜之地都是因腐化所致。N'Mar 的平原一直都有一些荒芜地带，尤其是 Hammerhands 附近，那里的土壤本就不适宜植物生长。"

    old "So what are we doing here, anyway? The fog seems even thicker than normal over these wastes. I can't see anything."
    new "So what are we doing here, anyway? The fog seems even thicker than normal over these wastes. I can't see anything.\n那我们到底来这里做什么？这片废土上的雾，似乎比平常还要浓。我什么都看不见。"

    old "I think it's less that the fog is thicker and more that it's hard to judge distance when there isn't anything around. Ordinarily, we might have trees, or other landmarks to guide us. Here, it's nothing but flat ground."
    new "I think it's less that the fog is thicker and more that it's hard to judge distance when there isn't anything around. Ordinarily, we might have trees, or other landmarks to guide us. Here, it's nothing but flat ground.\n我想，与其说是雾更浓，不如说是四周空无一物，难以判断距离。通常，我们还能靠树木或其他地标来辨认方向。而这里，只有一片平地。"

    old "I hope this isn't a waste of time."
    new "I hope this isn't a waste of time.\n希望这不是在浪费时间。"

    old "If this circle is what I think it is, then no, it wasn't a waste of time to come here. Come look at this."
    new "If this circle is what I think it is, then no, it wasn't a waste of time to come here. Come look at this.\n若这个圆圈正是我想的那样，那么不，来这一趟不算浪费时间。过来看看这个。"

    old "I examine the circle. It's just an empty circle on the ground, drawn in what I can only assume is blood."
    new "I examine the circle. It's just an empty circle on the ground, drawn in what I can only assume is blood.\n我端详起这个圆圈。它只是地上一个空荡荡的圆，我只能猜测是用血画的。"

    old "Blood ritual. Is this what's summoning the undead? It looks so...well, plain."
    new "Blood ritual. Is this what's summoning the undead? It looks so...well, plain.\n血之仪式。召唤亡灵的就是这个吗？它看上去如此……嗯，平平无奇。"

    old "I can't imagine why else this would be here. Why would there be a circle of blood, so perfectly drawn? Someone did this on purpose, and whatever that purpose was, hopefully this salt will help to foil it."
    new "I can't imagine why else this would be here. Why would there be a circle of blood, so perfectly drawn? Someone did this on purpose, and whatever that purpose was, hopefully this salt will help to foil it.\n我想不出它还能有什么别的用途。为什么会有一个画得如此规整的血圈？定是有人故意为之，而无论那目的是什么，希望这些盐能帮忙挫败它。"

    old "I reach into the bag and toss enough salt over the ground to cover the circle."
    new "I reach into the bag and toss enough salt over the ground to cover the circle.\n我把手伸进袋子，撒出足够的盐，覆盖住地上的圆圈。"

    old "Now can we get out of these wastes?"
    new "Now can we get out of these wastes?\n现在我们可以离开这片废土了吗？"

    old "Yes, I think our work here is done."
    new "Yes, I think our work here is done.\n可以了，我想我们在这里的事已经办完。"

    old "We turn around and begin retracing our steps."
    new "We turn around and begin retracing our steps.\n我们转过身，开始沿原路折返。"

    old "We exit the castle's interior, spilling out into the inner courtyard."
    new "We exit the castle's interior, spilling out into the inner courtyard.\n我们走出城堡内部，涌入内院。"

    old "I can't see a damn thing through the fog. How is it that the fog is so thick, even here?"
    new "I can't see a damn thing through the fog. How is it that the fog is so thick, even here?\n透过这雾，我什么都看不见。这雾怎么这么浓，连这里都是？"

    old "Technically, we are outdoors. In fact, the way that this castle is designed, a significant portion of the N'Mar territory contained within the castle walls is exposed to the open air."
    new "Technically, we are outdoors. In fact, the way that this castle is designed, a significant portion of the N'Mar territory contained within the castle walls is exposed to the open air.\n严格来说，我们现在在户外。事实上，按这座城堡的设计，城堡墙内包含的大片 N'Mar 领地，都暴露在露天之下。"

    old "It doesn't seem like there's anyone wandering out here, though. That's a good thing."
    new "It doesn't seem like there's anyone wandering out here, though. That's a good thing.\n不过，这里似乎没有人在游荡。这是件好事。"

    old "If there's no one out here, how can we hope to get good information?"
    new "If there's no one out here, how can we hope to get good information?\n若这里没有人，我们怎么能指望获得有用的情报？"

    old "For one thing, we may be able to get a lay of the land. The fog is thick, but we can at least make out the general layout of the castle."
    new "For one thing, we may be able to get a lay of the land. The fog is thick, but we can at least make out the general layout of the castle.\n首先，我们也许能摸清这里的地形。雾虽浓，但至少能辨认出城堡的大致布局。"

    old "What do we hope to divine from that?"
    new "What do we hope to divine from that?\n我们又想从这当中推测出什么？"

    old "We don't know yet. That's what we're here to find out. Keep your eyes open and tell me what you see. Don't forget to check above us. These are high castle walls, and we don't know what could be looking down at us."
    new "We don't know yet. That's what we're here to find out. Keep your eyes open and tell me what you see. Don't forget to check above us. These are high castle walls, and we don't know what could be looking down at us.\n现在还不知道。这正是我们要来查明的。睁大眼睛，把你看到的告诉我。别忘了检查我们上方。这些城堡墙很高，我们不知道会有什么东西正从上面俯视我们。"

    old "We move slowly through the courtyard. I keep my eyes mostly focused on the ground level."
    new "We move slowly through the courtyard. I keep my eyes mostly focused on the ground level.\n我们缓慢穿过庭院。我的目光大多停留在贴近地面的高度。"

    old "There are gargoyles mounted on the spire."
    new "There are gargoyles mounted on the spire.\n尖塔上安着石像鬼。"

    old "What? Gargoyles? Does it look like they're poised to attack?"
    new "What? Gargoyles? Does it look like they're poised to attack?\n什么？石像鬼？它们看起来像是蓄势待发要攻击吗？"

    old "As far as I can tell, they're just stone decorations."
    new "As far as I can tell, they're just stone decorations.\n就我所见，它们只是石雕装饰。"

    old "Oh. Well, that still is rather disconcerting."
    new "Oh. Well, that still is rather disconcerting.\n哦。嗯，那也还是挺让人心里发毛的。"

    old "Less commentary on the architecture, unless it's relevant to our mission somehow."
    new "Less commentary on the architecture, unless it's relevant to our mission somehow.\n少对建筑评头论足，除非它和我们的任务有什么关系。"

    old "I hear the howl of a dog in the distance."
    new "I hear the howl of a dog in the distance.\n我听到远处传来一声狗嚎。"

    old "Some kind of dog, obviously."
    new "Some kind of dog, obviously.\n显然是某种狗。"

    old "Dog? What if it's a wolf?"
    new "Dog? What if it's a wolf?\n狗？万一是狼呢？"

    old "Wolves don't bark like that. Wolves howl to communicate with their kin. You seldom hear only one wolf. Yet I hear only one howl. It's a dog."
    new "Wolves don't bark like that. Wolves howl to communicate with their kin. You seldom hear only one wolf. Yet I hear only one howl. It's a dog.\n狼不会那样叫。狼嚎叫是为了与同类交流。你很少只听到一头狼。可我只听到一声嚎叫。那是狗。"

    old "Why would a dog howl if it's alone?"
    new "Why would a dog howl if it's alone?\n狗若独自一个，为什么要嚎叫？"

    old "Dogs sometimes howl to communicate with their masters. Wolves can be tamed, but they'll only howl like that when another wolf is around."
    new "Dogs sometimes howl to communicate with their masters. Wolves can be tamed, but they'll only howl like that when another wolf is around.\n狗有时会嚎叫，是为了与主人沟通。狼可以被驯服，但只有附近有另一头狼时，它们才会那样嚎叫。"

    old "I hear the howl again, closer this time."
    new "I hear the howl again, closer this time.\n我又听到那声嚎叫，这次更近了。"

    old "Are there attack dogs out here?"
    new "Are there attack dogs out here?\n这里有攻击犬吗？"

    old "I told you, it's only one dog."
    new "I told you, it's only one dog.\n我告诉过你，只有一条狗。"

    old "I look around, but I can't identify the source of the noise."
    new "I look around, but I can't identify the source of the noise.\n我环顾四周，却无法辨明声音的来源。"

    old "This seems like it could be bad news. We should get out back to the castle interior until we can figure out what's doing on out here."
    new "This seems like it could be bad news. We should get out back to the castle interior until we can figure out what's doing on out here.\n这看起来可能是个坏消息。在我们弄清这里究竟发生了什么之前，还是先退回城堡内部为妙。"

    old "There's a door right over there. Should we try it?"
    new "There's a door right over there. Should we try it?\n那边就有一扇门。我们要试试吗？"

    old "We don't know what's behind that door. It would be bad if trying to avoid an encounter in the courtyard led to us running into even greater danger out of recklessness. Let's go back the way we came."
    new "We don't know what's behind that door. It would be bad if trying to avoid an encounter in the courtyard led to us running into even greater danger out of recklessness. Let's go back the way we came.\n我们不知道那扇门后有什么。若为了避开庭院里的遭遇，却因鲁莽而陷入更大的危险，那可就糟了。我们原路返回吧。"

    old "We turn around and head back in the direction of the door that we entered the courtyard through. As we cut through the fog, I see a large figure looming in the mist. No, wait—two figures."
    new "We turn around and head back in the direction of the door that we entered the courtyard through. As we cut through the fog, I see a large figure looming in the mist. No, wait—two figures.\n我们转过身，朝进入庭院时经过的那扇门方向走去。穿行于雾中时，我看到雾里浮现出一个庞大的身影。不，等等——是两个。"

    old "This seems like it could be bad news. Let's stop talking and start walking."
    new "This seems like it could be bad news. Let's stop talking and start walking.\n这看起来可能是个坏消息。别说话了，快走吧。"

    old "I hope nothing followed us here."
    new "I hope nothing followed us here.\n希望没有什么东西跟在我们身后。"

    old "As we cut through the fog, I see a large figure looming in the mist. No, wait—two figures."
    new "As we cut through the fog, I see a large figure looming in the mist. No, wait—two figures.\n穿行于雾中时，我看到雾里浮现出一个庞大的身影。不，等等——是两个。"

    old "Look, Diego. There are four of them."
    new "Look, Diego. There are four of them.\n看，Diego。他们有四个。"

    old "A woman stands before us, with a large beast looming behind her. The beast begins growling. I motion for my followers to stand by."
    new "A woman stands before us, with a large beast looming behind her. The beast begins growling. I motion for my followers to stand by.\n一个女人站在我们面前，一头庞大的野兽在她身后若隐若现。那野兽开始低吼。我示意同伴们原地待命。"

    old "The woman's appearance is unlike anything I've ever seen, but from the sickly pale color of her skin, there can be no mistaking it: she's a vampire."
    new "The woman's appearance is unlike anything I've ever seen, but from the sickly pale color of her skin, there can be no mistaking it: she's a vampire.\n这女人的模样我前所未见，但从她皮肤那病态的苍白颜色来看，绝不会错：她是个 Vampire。"

    old "Hush, Diego. Don't look at them. Look at Malone."
    new "Hush, Diego. Don't look at them. Look at Malone.\n嘘，Diego。别看着他们。看着 Malone。"

    old "Malone? Is that your name?"
    new "Malone? Is that your name?\nMalone？这是你的名字吗？"

    old "What? They can speak? Oh, of course they can speak. But how is it that they can understand us? What do you think, Diego?"
    new "What? They can speak? Oh, of course they can speak. But how is it that they can understand us? What do you think, Diego?\n什么？他们会说话？哦，他们当然会说话。但他们怎么能听懂我们的话呢？你觉得呢，Diego？"

    old "Diego. That must be the name of her beast companion. The woman—who I assume is Malone—doesn't seem to be completely lucid. It's almost as if she's carrying on a conversation with the dog, barely aware of our presence."
    new "Diego. That must be the name of her beast companion. The woman—who I assume is Malone—doesn't seem to be completely lucid. It's almost as if she's carrying on a conversation with the dog, barely aware of our presence.\nDiego。那一定是她野兽同伴的名字。这女人——我猜就是 Malone——神志似乎并不完全清醒。她几乎像是一直在和那条狗对话，对我们的存在几乎毫无察觉。"

    old "Don't worry, Diego. Malone will protect you."
    new "Don't worry, Diego. Malone will protect you.\n别担心，Diego。Malone 会保护你的。"

    old "I take a step toward the two of them, and Malone shrinks back. The dog begins whimpering, as if mirroring the hesitation of its master."
    new "I take a step toward the two of them, and Malone shrinks back. The dog begins whimpering, as if mirroring the hesitation of its master.\n我朝他们俩走近一步，Malone 向后缩了缩。那条狗呜咽起来，仿佛在应和它主人的迟疑。"

    old "She seems...almost fearful of our presence. As if she doesn't want a fight, and is having trouble deciding on the best course of action."
    new "She seems...almost fearful of our presence. As if she doesn't want a fight, and is having trouble deciding on the best course of action.\n她似乎……对我们的出现近乎恐惧。仿佛她不想打架，又拿不定主意该采取怎样的行动。"

    old "I take a step forward, and Malone seems to relax a bit, with her hold on the beast's leash loosening a bit. The beast seems less tense as well."
    new "I take a step forward, and Malone seems to relax a bit, with her hold on the beast's leash loosening a bit. The beast seems less tense as well.\n我又上前一步，Malone 似乎放松了些，她抓着野兽皮带的力道也松了几分。那野兽看起来也不那么紧绷了。"

    old "I'm not sure about this one, Diego. Let's see if [heshe] is nice."
    new "I'm not sure about this one, Diego. Let's see if [heshe] is nice.\n我不太确定这个，Diego。我们看看 [heshe] 是不是好人。"

    old "Hmm. She seems guarded, and potentially hostile, but not aggressive. Perhaps I can parley my way out of a fight."
    new "Hmm. She seems guarded, and potentially hostile, but not aggressive. Perhaps I can parley my way out of a fight.\n嗯。她似乎戒备着，也可能怀有敌意，但并不具有攻击性。也许我能靠谈判避免一场战斗。"

    old "Hush, Diego. Malone will keep you safe."
    new "Hush, Diego. Malone will keep you safe.\n嘘，Diego。Malone 会保你平安。"

    old "She seems like she's still trying to figure out what we are. She's definitely not ready for a fight. Maybe we could catch her off guard..."
    new "She seems like she's still trying to figure out what we are. She's definitely not ready for a fight. Maybe we could catch her off guard...\n她似乎仍在琢磨我们是什么人。她显然还没做好战斗的准备。也许我们能趁其不备……"

    old "Your dog looks hungry, but I can help. I have a treat for him. Here, take it."
    new "Your dog looks hungry, but I can help. I have a treat for him. Here, take it.\n你的狗看起来饿了，不过我能帮忙。我给它带了点吃的。来，拿着。"

    old "Malone takes the vial in her hands, she looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness."
    new "Malone takes the vial in her hands, she looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness.\nMalone 接过小瓶，神情困惑，被我的好意弄得措手不及。"

    old "Sniff...blood? Diego, look! Fresh blood for you!"
    new "Sniff...blood? Diego, look! Fresh blood for you!\n嗅嗅……是血？Diego，看！给你送来了新鲜的血！"

    old "Diego sniffs the vial, but refuses to drink from it. Malone looks pissed and says:"
    new "Diego sniffs the vial, but refuses to drink from it. Malone looks pissed and says:\nDiego 嗅了嗅小瓶，却不肯喝。Malone 一脸恼怒，说道："

    old "Malone doesn't like your treat!"
    new "Malone doesn't like your treat!\nMalone 不喜欢你的款待！"

    old "I'm sorry. But maybe, you'd like it?"
    new "I'm sorry. But maybe, you'd like it?\n抱歉。不过，也许你会喜欢？"

    old "I...am so thirsty...just a little sip."
    new "I...am so thirsty...just a little sip.\n我……好渴……就喝一小口。"

    old "After trying it, she is unable to resist, and she swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as she finishes though, she starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal."
    new "After trying it, she is unable to resist, and she swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as she finishes though, she starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal.\n尝过之后，她再也无法抗拒，一口吞下了瓶中的全部内容。然而刚一喝完，她便开始感到不适。Zachary 和 Valery 说过，这毒应当是致命的。"

    old "Malone's form starts to crumble, until she's reduced to nothing but dust that's swept away by the wind, and her beast companion seems to fade from existence."
    new "Malone's form starts to crumble, until she's reduced to nothing but dust that's swept away by the wind, and her beast companion seems to fade from existence.\nMalone 的身躯开始崩解，直到她化作尘土，被风卷走，而她的野兽同伴也仿佛从世上消失无踪。"

    old "Malone, you want to keep Diego safe, don't you?"
    new "Malone, you want to keep Diego safe, don't you?\nMalone，你想让 Diego 平安无事，对吧？"

    old "Yes. I always keep Diego safe and by my side."
    new "Yes. I always keep Diego safe and by my side.\n是的。我总是让 Diego 平安，把他留在身边。"

    old "This isn't a safe place for Diego to be. There might be intruders out here."
    new "This isn't a safe place for Diego to be. There might be intruders out here.\n这里对 Diego 来说并不安全。外面可能有入侵者。"

    old "Intruders? You. You're an intruder."
    new "Intruders? You. You're an intruder.\n入侵者？你。你就是个入侵者。"

    old "Indeed. So you see, this area has already been invaded. Clearly, this is a dangerous place for someone like Diego, isn't it?"
    new "Indeed. So you see, this area has already been invaded. Clearly, this is a dangerous place for someone like Diego, isn't it?\n确实。所以你看，这片区域已经遭到了入侵。显然，这对 Diego 这样的存在来说是个危险的地方，不是吗？"

    old "You should take Diego away from here. Some place safe. Some place far away."
    new "You should take Diego away from here. Some place safe. Some place far away.\n你该带 Diego 离开这里。去个安全的地方。去个遥远的地方。"

    old "Some place...far away..."
    new "Some place...far away...\n某个地方……遥远的地方……"

    old "Malone, we have no quarrel with you. You and Diego can be on your way, and we'll be on our way."
    new "Malone, we have no quarrel with you. You and Diego can be on your way, and we'll be on our way.\nMalone，我们与你无冤无仇。你和 Diego 可以上路了，我们也要继续赶路。"

    old "But what is it that you're doing here?"
    new "But what is it that you're doing here?\n可你们在这里做什么？"

    old "I could ask the same of you. What are you doing here? We all have our reasons for being out tonight. We won't ask questions if you won't."
    new "I could ask the same of you. What are you doing here? We all have our reasons for being out tonight. We won't ask questions if you won't.\n我也正想问你同样的问题。你在这里做什么？我们今晚出来，各有各的理由。你若不说，我们也不问。"

    old "Hmm. That seems fair."
    new "Hmm. That seems fair.\n嗯。这似乎很公平。"

    old "Why are you doing this? You're upsetting Diego. I've never heard him like this."
    new "Why are you doing this? You're upsetting Diego. I've never heard him like this.\n你们为什么要这么做？你们惹得 Diego 不安了。我从没听他这样过。"

    old "It's quite simple, Malone. You're a vampire."
    new "It's quite simple, Malone. You're a vampire.\n这很简单，Malone。你是个 Vampire。"

    old "I'm a vampire? Oh yes, that's right. I am a vampire."
    new "I'm a vampire? Oh yes, that's right. I am a vampire.\n我是 Vampire？哦，是啊，没错。我是 Vampire。"

    old "Right now, Grimoire is under assault, and there's no reason for you to be here unless you're involved with that attack. So you see, we really have no choice but to get rid of you."
    new "Right now, Grimoire is under assault, and there's no reason for you to be here unless you're involved with that attack. So you see, we really have no choice but to get rid of you.\n眼下 Grimoire 正遭围攻，而你没有理由待在这里，除非你与那场进攻有关。所以你看，我们实在别无选择，只能除掉你。"

    old "Right now, this castle and the vampires in it have been causing a lot of problems for us. So you see, we really have no choice but to get rid of you."
    new "Right now, this castle and the vampires in it have been causing a lot of problems for us. So you see, we really have no choice but to get rid of you.\n眼下，这座城堡和里面的 Vampires 给我们带来了许多麻烦。所以你看，我们实在别无选择，只能除掉你。"

    old "Get rid...of me?"
    new "Get rid...of me?\n除掉……我？"

    old "You. You're making me very upset. And when I become upset, Diego becomes upset. You're going to wish you hadn't done that."
    new "You. You're making me very upset. And when I become upset, Diego becomes upset. You're going to wish you hadn't done that.\n你。你让我非常生气。而我一生气，Diego 也会生气。你会后悔这么做的。"

    old "Surrender, you're no match for my team!"
    new "Surrender, you're no match for my team!\n投降吧，你不是我们队伍的对手！"

    old "Can't you see? You have no chances to win if you keep fighting like this."
    new "Can't you see? You have no chances to win if you keep fighting like this.\n你难道看不出吗？你再这样打下去，根本没有胜算。"

    old "Clock is ticking, Malone. More of us will be here soon."
    new "Clock is ticking, Malone. More of us will be here soon.\n时间不等人，Malone。我们的人很快就会赶到。"

    old "If you don't care about being killed, at least think about Diego."
    new "If you don't care about being killed, at least think about Diego.\n若你不在乎自己被杀，至少也为 Diego 想想。"

    old "Malone looks at us with sad eyes."
    new "Malone looks at us with sad eyes.\nMalone 用悲伤的眼神看着我们。"

    old "The bond between me and Diego. I can feel it weakening. It only weakens when I weaken. Why is this happening? You're...you're hurting me."
    new "The bond between me and Diego. I can feel it weakening. It only weakens when I weaken. Why is this happening? You're...you're hurting me.\n我和 Diego 之间的羁绊。我能感觉到它在变弱。只有我变弱时，它才会变弱。为什么会这样？你们……你们在伤害我。"

    old "Why are you doing this to me? To Diego?"
    new "Why are you doing this to me? To Diego?\n你们为什么要这样对我？对 Diego？"

    old "You pause for a moment and ponder what to say. This vampire looks different from all the others. She doesn't seem to realize what's really going on. And she's showing at least some sort of feeling towards her undead companion Diego."
    new "You pause for a moment and ponder what to say. This vampire looks different from all the others. She doesn't seem to realize what's really going on. And she's showing at least some sort of feeling towards her undead companion Diego.\n你停顿片刻，斟酌着该说些什么。这个 Vampire 看上去和其他所有 Vampires 都不一样。她似乎并不清楚究竟发生了什么。而且，她至少对自己那亡灵同伴 Diego 表现出了某种感情。"

    old "On the other hand, sparing the life of a crazy creature like this might have consequences later."
    new "On the other hand, sparing the life of a crazy creature like this might have consequences later.\n另一方面，饶过这样一个疯癫的怪物一命，日后也许会招来后果。"

    old "Look, you don't want us to hurt Diego anymore, right? He is innocent."
    new "Look, you don't want us to hurt Diego anymore, right? He is innocent.\n听着，你不想让我们再伤害 Diego 了吧？它是无辜的。"

    old "Yes. He did nothing bad! He's a good dog. My beloved Diego..."
    new "Yes. He did nothing bad! He's a good dog. My beloved Diego...\n是的。它什么坏事都没做！它是条好狗。我心爱的 Diego……"

    old "You can go. But if we ever see you again here, we'll hurt you and your... dog. Hurt badly, very badly."
    new "You can go. But if we ever see you again here, we'll hurt you and your... dog. Hurt badly, very badly.\n你们可以走了。但若我们再在这里见到你，我们就会伤害你和你的……狗。狠狠伤害，非常狠。"

    old "No. We vanish. We'll never be seen again. Come, Diego."
    new "No. We vanish. We'll never be seen again. Come, Diego.\n不。我们会消失的。再也不会被你们看见。来吧，Diego。"

    old "Malone steps back, receding into the mist, and her beast companion seems to vanish with her."
    new "Malone steps back, receding into the mist, and her beast companion seems to vanish with her.\nMalone 后退几步，退入雾中，她的野兽同伴也仿佛随她一同消失。"

    old "Sorry, Malone. You're on the wrong side of this conflict. We have to deal with you some way, and it might as well be now."
    new "Sorry, Malone. You're on the wrong side of this conflict. We have to deal with you some way, and it might as well be now.\n抱歉，Malone。你站在这场冲突错误的一边。我们总得想办法对付你，不如就趁现在。"

    old "Stand back, Diego! I'll deal with them myself! I won't let them hurt you again!"
    new "Stand back, Diego! I'll deal with them myself! I won't let them hurt you again!\n退后，Diego！我自己来对付他们！我不会让他们再伤害你！"

    old "Your friends hurt our friends, Malone."
    new "Your friends hurt our friends, Malone.\n你的朋友们伤害了我们的朋友，Malone。"

    old "Your...friends? Do you mean the women who were captured?"
    new "Your...friends? Do you mean the women who were captured?\n你的……朋友们？你是说那些被抓起来的女人？"

    old "I...I know them. There was a little girl with them, wasn't there? Are those your friends?"
    new "I...I know them. There was a little girl with them, wasn't there? Are those your friends?\n我……我认识她们。她们当中是不是还有个小女孩？那些是你的朋友吗？"

    old "Yes, Malone."
    new "Yes, Malone.\n是的，Malone。"

    old "I have a key that you could use. I can let you get to your friends, if you leave me and Diego alone in the courtyard."
    new "I have a key that you could use. I can let you get to your friends, if you leave me and Diego alone in the courtyard.\n我有一把你们用得上的钥匙。若你们让我和 Diego 在这庭院里安生待着，我就能让你们去救你们的朋友。"

    old "It seems like Malone is offering a deal. We did come to rescue the Amazons. But...if she really has that key, maybe we could just defeat her and take it."
    new "It seems like Malone is offering a deal. We did come to rescue the Amazons. But...if she really has that key, maybe we could just defeat her and take it.\n看来 Malone 是在提出交易。我们确实是来救 Amazons 的。但……若她真有那把钥匙，也许我们大可直接打败她，把钥匙夺过来。"

    old "Is it better to strike a deal with a vampire, or deal with them permanently? Hmm..."
    new "Is it better to strike a deal with a vampire, or deal with them permanently? Hmm...\n是和 Vampire 达成交易好，还是干脆把他们彻底解决掉好？嗯……"

    old "Alright, Malone. We'll leave you alone if you give us the key."
    new "Alright, Malone. We'll leave you alone if you give us the key.\n好吧，Malone。只要你给我们钥匙，我们就不打扰你。"

    old "Come on, Diego. Let's go. Let's find another place for us, here is too dangerous."
    new "Come on, Diego. Let's go. Let's find another place for us, here is too dangerous.\n来吧，Diego。我们走。我们另找个地方，这里太危险了。"

    old "Malone steps back, receding into the mist, and her beast companion seems to vanish with her. I hear the soft 'tink' of metal hitting the ground."
    new "Malone steps back, receding into the mist, and her beast companion seems to vanish with her. I hear the soft 'tink' of metal hitting the ground.\nMalone 后退几步，退入雾中，她的野兽同伴也仿佛随她一同消失。我听到金属落地的轻微叮当声。"

    old "I hear the soft 'tink' of metal hitting the ground, and I walk up to where Malone stood to get a closer look at what's happening."
    new "I hear the soft 'tink' of metal hitting the ground, and I walk up to where Malone stood to get a closer look at what's happening.\n我听到金属落地的轻微叮当声，便走到 Malone 方才站立之处，想看清发生了什么。"

    old "Malone turns around and begins receding into the mists."
    new "Malone turns around and begins receding into the mists.\nMalone 转过身，开始退入雾中。"

    old "Poor woman. She seems to be barely aware of what's happening around her. Without that beast companion, she would probably be completely vulnerable. At least we managed to avoid a fight."
    new "Poor woman. She seems to be barely aware of what's happening around her. Without that beast companion, she would probably be completely vulnerable. At least we managed to avoid a fight.\n可怜的女人。她似乎几乎觉察不到周围正在发生什么。没有那个野兽同伴，她大概会完全不堪一击。至少，我们设法避免了一场战斗。"

    old "On the ground, I can see the shimmering glint of moonlight reflected on a small piece of metal. A key."
    new "On the ground, I can see the shimmering glint of moonlight reflected on a small piece of metal. A key.\n在地面上，我看见月光映在一小块金属上，泛着微光。是一把钥匙。"

    old "Does it seem like it matches the door we saw in the main hall?"
    new "Does it seem like it matches the door we saw in the main hall?\n它看起来和我们在主厅看到的那扇门相配吗？"

    old "Let's find out, shall we?"
    new "Let's find out, shall we?\n我们去验证一下吧，如何？"

    old "We head to the shaded glen. The trees here look dark and menacing, and the way the moonlight dances off of them almost makes them look alive, even as their shape suggests that the life has been drained out of them by the corruption of the soil."
    new "We head to the shaded glen. The trees here look dark and menacing, and the way the moonlight dances off of them almost makes them look alive, even as their shape suggests that the life has been drained out of them by the corruption of the soil.\n我们朝阴翳的幽谷走去。这里的树木看上去黝黑而狰狞，月光在树间跃动，几乎让它们显得有了生气，尽管它们的形态暗示着，其生命力早已被土壤的腐化抽干。"

    old "This place was once fertile ground. Now it stinks of rot and decay."
    new "This place was once fertile ground. Now it stinks of rot and decay.\n这地方曾是肥沃的土地。如今却弥漫着腐坏与衰败的恶臭。"

    old "I hear a whistling sound sweep through the glen, and I feel the wind at our backs."
    new "I hear a whistling sound sweep through the glen, and I feel the wind at our backs.\n我听到一阵呼啸声掠过幽谷，感到风从我们背后吹来。"

    old "The wind is troubled tonight."
    new "The wind is troubled tonight.\n今夜的风，不太平静。"

    old "Don't let it get to you."
    new "Don't let it get to you.\n别让它搅乱你的心神。"

    old "Another draft comes. But this time, the wind his me in the face. I close my eyes reflexively until the wind has passed."
    new "Another draft comes. But this time, the wind his me in the face. I close my eyes reflexively until the wind has passed.\n又一阵风袭来。但这一次，风直扑我的面门。我下意识地闭上眼，直到风过去。"

    old "This is no ordinary wind."
    new "This is no ordinary wind.\n这不是寻常的风。"

    old "Indeed. The wind is coming from multiple directions."
    new "Indeed. The wind is coming from multiple directions.\n的确。这风来自四面八方。"

    old "Something tells me we're not alone here."
    new "Something tells me we're not alone here.\n有某种感觉告诉我，这里并非只有我们。"

    old "Freeze. Listen closely."
    new "Freeze. Listen closely.\n别动。仔细听。"

    old "We all wait in place, not making a sound, and I feel a slight trembling in my feet. At first, it feels like my body is shaking with fright, but I suddenly realize that the ground is actually trembling beneath us."
    new "We all wait in place, not making a sound, and I feel a slight trembling in my feet. At first, it feels like my body is shaking with fright, but I suddenly realize that the ground is actually trembling beneath us.\n我们都原地等待，不发出一点声音，我感到脚下有轻微的震颤。起初，我以为是自己吓得发抖，但我忽然意识到，颤抖的其实是脚下的地面。"

    old "Tremors!"
    new "Tremors!\n震颤！"

    old "And just as quickly as the ground started moving, it stops."
    new "And just as quickly as the ground started moving, it stops.\n而地面开始晃动得有多快，停得就有多快。"

    old "We're not alone in here. Weapons ready, people. I don't know if we've walked into a fight, but I don't want to take the chance."
    new "We're not alone in here. Weapons ready, people. I don't know if we've walked into a fight, but I don't want to take the chance.\n我们在这里并不孤单。大家准备好武器。我不知道我们是否已经撞进了一场战斗，但我不想冒这个险。"

    old "I begin inching slowly forward through the hall, with my followers behind me, when I spot a tree stump with several streaks on it. They look like blood markings."
    new "I begin inching slowly forward through the hall, with my followers behind me, when I spot a tree stump with several streaks on it. They look like blood markings.\n我带着身后的同伴，开始缓缓向前挪动，这时我发现一个树桩，上面有几道条纹。它们看起来像是血痕。"

    old "Is that an enchantment, that someone drew to make these woods so spooky?"
    new "Is that an enchantment, that someone drew to make these woods so spooky?\n那是一种魔法吗？有人画出来，好让这片树林变得如此诡异？"

    old "I don't think so. Why would someone specifically enchant this glen to make the ground quiver slightly and for the wind to behave strangely? No, these seem more like side-effects. It might be a ritual or enchantment, but it had some other purpose in mind."
    new "I don't think so. Why would someone specifically enchant this glen to make the ground quiver slightly and for the wind to behave strangely? No, these seem more like side-effects. It might be a ritual or enchantment, but it had some other purpose in mind.\n我想不是。谁会特意给这片幽谷施法，只为让地面轻轻颤动、让风变得怪异？不，这些更像是副作用。它也许是某种仪式或魔法，但本意另有所图。"

    old "Sounds like something we ought to deal with."
    new "Sounds like something we ought to deal with.\n听起来是我们该处理的事。"

    old "Indeed. Luckily we came prepared."
    new "Indeed. Luckily we came prepared.\n没错。幸好我们有备而来。"

    old "I reach for my bag and pour salt over the tree stump until it's covered completely. As the salt neutralizes the enchantment, I feel the wind stop."
    new "I reach for my bag and pour salt over the tree stump until it's covered completely. As the salt neutralizes the enchantment, I feel the wind stop.\n我伸手拿过背包，把盐倒在树桩上，直到把它完全覆盖。随着盐中和掉魔法，我感到风停了。"

    old "Looks like a success to me."
    new "Looks like a success to me.\n在我看来，是成功了。"

    old "Let's get out. This place gives me the creeps."
    new "Let's get out. This place gives me the creeps.\n我们出去吧。这地方让我毛骨悚然。"

    old "I turn around and find myself confronted by the sight of a clown."
    new "I turn around and find myself confronted by the sight of a clown.\n我转过身，迎面撞见一个小丑。"

    old "The hall seems to contain what looks like an ornate dining table, but a moment's inspection reveals that the table is covered by a thick layer of dust. This table hasn't been used for dining in quite some time."
    new "The hall seems to contain what looks like an ornate dining table, but a moment's inspection reveals that the table is covered by a thick layer of dust. This table hasn't been used for dining in quite some time.\n大厅里似乎摆着一张华丽的餐桌，但稍一查看便发现，桌上积着厚厚一层灰。这张餐桌已许久不曾用来进餐了。"

    old "Where should we begin searching?"
    new "Where should we begin searching?\n我们该从哪里开始搜查？"

    old "Any area that's covered in dust is a place hasn't been disturbed recently. The prisoners were locked up just a day ago, so focus on the parts of the room that don't have dust."
    new "Any area that's covered in dust is a place hasn't been disturbed recently. The prisoners were locked up just a day ago, so focus on the parts of the room that don't have dust.\n凡是积灰的地方，都是近来无人动过的。囚犯们是一天前才被关起来的，所以把注意力放在房间里没有灰尘的部分。"

    old "Good call."
    new "Good call.\n好主意。"

    old "I open my mouth to say something, but I hear a chilling wind pass through the room."
    new "I open my mouth to say something, but I hear a chilling wind pass through the room.\n我张嘴想说什么，却听到一阵阴风穿过房间。"

    old "Just a draft."
    new "Just a draft.\n不过是穿堂风。"

    old "A draft indoors? Where could it be coming from?"
    new "A draft indoors? Where could it be coming from?\n室内哪来的穿堂风？它会是从哪儿来的？"

    old "It's a large hall. That could be normal here."
    new "It's a large hall. That could be normal here.\n这是个大礼堂。在这里，这也许很正常。"

    old "Something's not right. If drafty winds pass through here regularly, then why would there be so much settled dust here?"
    new "Something's not right. If drafty winds pass through here regularly, then why would there be so much settled dust here?\n有些不对劲。若穿堂风经常从这里吹过，这里又怎会积起这么多灰尘？"

    old "I hear a deep sound, almost like a groan, that lasts only for a moment."
    new "I hear a deep sound, almost like a groan, that lasts only for a moment.\n我听到一声低沉的声响，几乎像呻吟，只持续了一瞬。"

    old "We all wait in place, not making a sound, and I hear the sound of the table vibrating against the floor."
    new "We all wait in place, not making a sound, and I hear the sound of the table vibrating against the floor.\n我们都原地等待，不发出一点声音，我听到桌子贴地颤动的声响。"

    old "I begin inching slowly forward through the hall, with my followers behind me, when I'm struck by a flash that blinds me for a moment. When my eyes blink and adjust to the room's dim light, I see a clown standing in front of me."
    new "I begin inching slowly forward through the hall, with my followers behind me, when I'm struck by a flash that blinds me for a moment. When my eyes blink and adjust to the room's dim light, I see a clown standing in front of me.\n我带着身后的同伴，开始缓缓向前挪动，忽然一道闪光袭来，让我一瞬间目不能视。待我眨眨眼，适应了房间里昏暗的光线，便看到一个小丑站在我面前。"

    old "Hello, visitors, and welcome to the blood hall! I, Nootau, will be your host this evening."
    new "Hello, visitors, and welcome to the blood hall! I, Nootau, will be your host this evening.\n你们好，各位来宾，欢迎来到血之大厅！我，Nootau，将是今晚招待你们的主人。"

    old "Ah, what's this? You're not on the guest list for tonight! Perhaps you've come to rest upon the dining table, rather than sit around it? You're all looking very...appetizing tonight. Why, I can't wait to sink my fangs into your juicy flesh!"
    new "Ah, what's this? You're not on the guest list for tonight! Perhaps you've come to rest upon the dining table, rather than sit around it? You're all looking very...appetizing tonight. Why, I can't wait to sink my fangs into your juicy flesh!\n啊，这是怎么回事？你们今晚可不在宾客名单上！也许你们是来躺上餐桌，而不是围桌而坐的吧？你们今晚看上去真是……美味诱人。哎呀，我简直等不及要把我的獠牙扎进你们多汁的肉里了！"

    old "I don't think you'll be consuming anyone's flesh tonight."
    new "I don't think you'll be consuming anyone's flesh tonight.\n我想今晚你不会吃到任何人的肉。"

    old "Ohoho! You intend to put up a fight? I suppose that would explain the weapons you brought with you."
    new "Ohoho! You intend to put up a fight? I suppose that would explain the weapons you brought with you.\n哦呵呵！你们打算反抗？我想，这倒能解释你们为何随身带着武器。"

    old "Hello, visitors, and welcome to the bloody woods! I, Nootau, will be your guide for this evening."
    new "Hello, visitors, and welcome to the bloody woods! I, Nootau, will be your guide for this evening.\n你们好，各位来宾，欢迎来到血色树林！我，Nootau，将是今晚为你们领路的向导。"

    old "Ah, what's this? These woods, something's wrong...what have you done to the blood? Now they're not blood woods at all! I need fresh blood! And...how convenient, I have you right in front of me. Carrying plenty of blood. Please, give it to me."
    new "Ah, what's this? These woods, something's wrong...what have you done to the blood? Now they're not blood woods at all! I need fresh blood! And...how convenient, I have you right in front of me. Carrying plenty of blood. Please, give it to me.\n啊，这是怎么回事？这片树林，有什么不对劲……你们对血做了什么？如今它们根本算不上血色树林了！我需要新鲜的血！而……多方便啊，你们就站在我面前。带着满满的血。求求你们，把它给我吧。"

    old "If you want to have our blood, you'll need to drain it from our cold, dead bodies."
    new "If you want to have our blood, you'll need to drain it from our cold, dead bodies.\n若你想要我们的血，就得从我们冰冷的尸体上取。"

    old "Good idea. I intend to do exactly that. Except, I wouldn't wait for your bodies to get cold. Oh no. Blood is best when it's at its freshest."
    new "Good idea. I intend to do exactly that. Except, I wouldn't wait for your bodies to get cold. Oh no. Blood is best when it's at its freshest.\n好主意。我正打算这么做。只不过，我不会等你们的尸体变冷。哦，不。血啊，还是最新鲜的时候最好。"

    old "A battle would suit me just fine. But perhaps you have designs beyond a spar with me, no?"
    new "A battle would suit me just fine. But perhaps you have designs beyond a spar with me, no?\n打一场，我求之不得。不过，也许你们的目的不只是和我过招，对吧？"

    old "I can tell from the look of you that you didn't stumble in here without knowing what you were getting into. What could you be planning, I wonder?"
    new "I can tell from the look of you that you didn't stumble in here without knowing what you were getting into. What could you be planning, I wonder?\n从你们的神情我能看出，你们不是不知深浅就闯进来的。我很好奇，你们究竟在盘算什么？"

    old "But did you really come here with hostile intentions? You seem so nice, such tender eyes! Why, I almost feel guilty about the fact that I'm about to make a meal out of you. Ah well, at least I'll have you all to myself. It almost enough to make up for the fact that they're making me stay inside tonight."
    new "But did you really come here with hostile intentions? You seem so nice, such tender eyes! Why, I almost feel guilty about the fact that I'm about to make a meal out of you. Ah well, at least I'll have you all to myself. It almost enough to make up for the fact that they're making me stay inside tonight.\n可你们真的是带着敌意来的吗？你们看上去那么和善，眼神那么温柔！哎呀，一想到我就要把你们做成一顿美餐，我几乎有些内疚了。唉，不过至少，我能独占你们。这几乎足以弥补他们今晚逼我待在屋里这件事了。"

    old "He's being forced to stay inside, hmm? Maybe he could be persuaded to leave..."
    new "He's being forced to stay inside, hmm? Maybe he could be persuaded to leave...\n他是被迫待在屋里的，嗯？也许可以说服他离开……"

    old "But did you really come here with hostile intentions? You seem so nice, such tender eyes! Why, I almost feel guilty about the fact that I'm about to take your blood. Ah well, at least I'll have you all to myself. It almost enough to make up for the fact that I'm stuck with the task of summoning."
    new "But did you really come here with hostile intentions? You seem so nice, such tender eyes! Why, I almost feel guilty about the fact that I'm about to take your blood. Ah well, at least I'll have you all to myself. It almost enough to make up for the fact that I'm stuck with the task of summoning.\n可你们真的是带着敌意来的吗？你们看上去那么和善，眼神那么温柔！哎呀，一想到我就要取走你们的血，我几乎有些内疚了。唉，不过至少，我能独占你们。这几乎足以弥补我被困在召唤仪式这活儿上这件事了。"

    old "He's being forced to be here, hmm? Maybe he could be persuaded to abandon his duties..."
    new "He's being forced to be here, hmm? Maybe he could be persuaded to abandon his duties...\n他是被迫待在这里的，嗯？也许可以说服他抛下自己的职责……"

    old "Should I bother trying to parley with this clown?"
    new "Should I bother trying to parley with this clown?\n我该不该费心去和这个小丑谈判？"

    old "I came in peace. As proof of my good faith, I have a valuable gift for you. Here take it."
    new "I came in peace. As proof of my good faith, I have a valuable gift for you. Here take it.\n我是带着和平来的。作为我诚意的证明，我有份珍贵的礼物送你。来，拿着。"

    old "Nootau takes the vial in his hands, he looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness."
    new "Nootau takes the vial in his hands, he looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness.\nNootau 接过小瓶，神情困惑，被我的好意弄得措手不及。"

    old "Sniff...blood? It looks so inviting..."
    new "Sniff...blood? It looks so inviting...\n嗅嗅……是血？看上去真是诱人……"

    old "Unable to resist, Nootau swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as he finishes though, he starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal."
    new "Unable to resist, Nootau swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as he finishes though, he starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal.\nNootau 无法抗拒，一口吞下了瓶中的全部内容。然而刚一喝完，他便开始感到不适。Zachary 和 Valery 说过，这毒应当是致命的。"

    old "Nootau lets out a final shriek, and in a moment, he vanishes. His clothes, now empty, crumple to the floor in a pile, and the balls he was juggling fall to the floor harmlessly."
    new "Nootau lets out a final shriek, and in a moment, he vanishes. His clothes, now empty, crumple to the floor in a pile, and the balls he was juggling fall to the floor harmlessly.\nNootau 发出最后一声尖啸，转瞬之间便消失了。他空荡荡的衣服瘫作一堆落在地上，而他方才抛接的彩球也无害地滚落在地。"

    old "I poisoned him using a trick!"
    new "I poisoned him using a trick!\n我用计毒死了他！"

    old "You're right. We'd be fools to come here without a plan, and as you may have surmised, we're no fools."
    new "You're right. We'd be fools to come here without a plan, and as you may have surmised, we're no fools.\n你说得对。毫无计划就来这里，那我们就是傻瓜了，而正如你或许已经猜到的那样，我们可不是傻瓜。"

    old "Nootau, you seem like a nice fellow, so I'll share a bit of information with you. We're the first wave of people invading your castle. Get it? The second wave will be here shortly. If you value your skin, you won't be here when they arrive."
    new "Nootau, you seem like a nice fellow, so I'll share a bit of information with you. We're the first wave of people invading your castle. Get it? The second wave will be here shortly. If you value your skin, you won't be here when they arrive.\nNootau，你看上去是个不错的家伙，所以我就跟你分享点消息吧。我们是入侵你城堡的第一波人马。懂了吗？第二波很快就到。你若珍惜自己的小命，他们到时可别还留在这里。"

    old "Nootau, you seem like a nice fellow, so I'll share a bit of information with you. We're the first wave of people invading these plains. Get it? The second wave will be here shortly. If you value your skin, you won't be here when they arrive."
    new "Nootau, you seem like a nice fellow, so I'll share a bit of information with you. We're the first wave of people invading these plains. Get it? The second wave will be here shortly. If you value your skin, you won't be here when they arrive.\nNootau，你看上去是个不错的家伙，所以我就跟你分享点消息吧。我们是入侵这片平原的第一波人马。懂了吗？第二波很快就到。你若珍惜自己的小命，他们到时可别还留在这里。"

    old "So, why are you telling me this?"
    new "So, why are you telling me this?\n那么，你为什么告诉我这些？"

    old "Because we didn't come here to kill vampires, Nootau. You'd be a distraction. If you leave now, you'll be doing both of us a favor. We save the time of dealing with you and waiting for our friends to show up, and you don't get a stake through the heart. Sound fair?"
    new "Because we didn't come here to kill vampires, Nootau. You'd be a distraction. If you leave now, you'll be doing both of us a favor. We save the time of dealing with you and waiting for our friends to show up, and you don't get a stake through the heart. Sound fair?\n因为我们不是来杀 Vampires 的，Nootau。你只会让我们分心。若你现在离开，对我们双方都是好事。我们省下对付你的时间，也不必等朋友们到场，而你也不会被木桩刺穿心脏。听起来公平吗？"

    old "Feh! I was going to stick around and perform some tricks for you, but you wouldn't appreciate them. You'd better watch yourself."
    new "Feh! I was going to stick around and perform some tricks for you, but you wouldn't appreciate them. You'd better watch yourself.\n呸！我本打算留下来，给你们露几手戏法，可你们不会懂得欣赏。你们最好当心点。"

    old "Someone as skilled as you could surely deal with us alone."
    new "Someone as skilled as you could surely deal with us alone.\n像你这么有本事的人，肯定能独自对付我们。"

    old "No doubt, no doubt! It would be effortless, of that I'm sure."
    new "No doubt, no doubt! It would be effortless, of that I'm sure.\n毫无疑问，毫无疑问！那简直不费吹灰之力，这点我确信。"

    old "So, why is it that you're stuck in this castle, cavorting with other vampires? Clearly, you're someone who needs no assistance to get the job done."
    new "So, why is it that you're stuck in this castle, cavorting with other vampires? Clearly, you're someone who needs no assistance to get the job done.\n那么，你为何被困在这城堡里，和其他 Vampires 厮混呢？显然，你是个无需任何人协助就能成事的人。"

    old "So, why is it that you're stuck in these gloomy-looking woods, acting as someone's mere assistant? Surely you should be the star of this show."
    new "So, why is it that you're stuck in these gloomy-looking woods, acting as someone's mere assistant? Surely you should be the star of this show.\n那么，你为何被困在这片阴森的树林里，仅仅充当某个人的助手呢？你理应成为这出戏的主角才对。"

    old "Quite true! I always win with style and grace, something that the others sorely lack in."
    new "Quite true! I always win with style and grace, something that the others sorely lack in.\n一点没错！我总是以风度和优雅取胜，这正是其他人所严重欠缺的。"

    old "So why work with them? Why not leave this place, and find someone to dazzle with your talents? It's a full moon, and yet you're spending it here, alone. What a waste!"
    new "So why work with them? Why not leave this place, and find someone to dazzle with your talents? It's a full moon, and yet you're spending it here, alone. What a waste!\n那又何必和他们共事呢？何不离开此地，去找个能让你大展才华的人？今夜满月，你却独自待在这里度过。多浪费啊！"

    old "A waste indeed. A full moon. Heh. The last full moon, several dozen human soldiers were slaughtered. What an event that must have been!"
    new "A waste indeed. A full moon. Heh. The last full moon, several dozen human soldiers were slaughtered. What an event that must have been!\n确实是浪费。满月。嘿嘿。上一次满月，有几十个人类士兵惨遭屠杀。那该是多么盛大的场面啊！"

    old "A waste indeed. A full moon. Heh. Two full moons ago, several dozen human soldiers were slaughtered. What an event that must have been!"
    new "A waste indeed. A full moon. Heh. Two full moons ago, several dozen human soldiers were slaughtered. What an event that must have been!\n确实是浪费。满月。嘿嘿。两个月前的满月，有几十个人类士兵惨遭屠杀。那该是多么盛大的场面啊！"

    old "And yet you missed out on it, didn't you? You'll never have the opportunity to experience that full moon again. But you can experience this one."
    new "And yet you missed out on it, didn't you? You'll never have the opportunity to experience that full moon again. But you can experience this one.\n可你却错过了那一次，不是吗？你永远没有机会再经历那个满月了。但你可以经历这一个。"

    old "Nootau looks at me with a glint in his eye, grinning like a madman."
    new "Nootau looks at me with a glint in his eye, grinning like a madman.\nNootau 眼中闪过一丝光芒，像个疯子般咧嘴笑着看我。"

    old "The moon is full! What a night this will be. Oh, you'll still be here when I return, won't you? Yes, yes, the fields yearn for me. I am on my way!"
    new "The moon is full! What a night this will be. Oh, you'll still be here when I return, won't you? Yes, yes, the fields yearn for me. I am on my way!\n月正圆满！这将是多么美妙的一夜。哦，等我回来时你们还会在这里的，对吧？是的，是的，原野在召唤我。我这就上路！"

    old "With a flourish of fabric, Nootau vanishes as quickly as he appeared."
    new "With a flourish of fabric, Nootau vanishes as quickly as he appeared.\n随着衣袂一扬，Nootau 消失得和他出现时一样快。"

    old "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of leaves. As the leaves settle, I see he's gone."
    new "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of leaves. As the leaves settle, I see he's gone.\nNootau 身后留下一阵狂风，掀起一小片枯叶。待落叶落定，我发现他已经不见了。"

    old "Was it really alright to let him go like that?"
    new "Was it really alright to let him go like that?\n就这样放他走，真的没问题吗？"

    old "I get the feeling that Nootau will behave differently when he's staring at the wrong end of a dozen spears. Someone like him will be easily overwhelmed by numbers. I wouldn't be surprised if he simply leaves when he sees how well-prepared Grimoire's defenses are."
    new "I get the feeling that Nootau will behave differently when he's staring at the wrong end of a dozen spears. Someone like him will be easily overwhelmed by numbers. I wouldn't be surprised if he simply leaves when he sees how well-prepared Grimoire's defenses are.\n我有种感觉，当 Nootau 面对十几支长矛的矛尖时，他的表现会大不一样。像他那样的人，很容易被人多势众压垮。等他看到 Grimoire 的防御准备得有多充分，就算直接跑掉，我也不会意外。"

    old "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of dust. As the dust settles, I see something that he's left behind."
    new "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of dust. As the dust settles, I see something that he's left behind.\nNootau 身后留下一阵狂风，扬起一小片尘土。待尘埃落定，我看见他留下了什么东西。"

    old "Is that...a key?"
    new "Is that...a key?\n那是……一把钥匙？"

    old "A key? Do you suppose he meant to leave it?"
    new "A key? Do you suppose he meant to leave it?\n钥匙？你觉得他是有意留下的吗？"

    old "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of dust. As the dust settles, I see he's gone."
    new "Nootau leaves behind a gust of wind, a small tempest that creates a small cloud of dust. As the dust settles, I see he's gone.\nNootau 身后留下一阵狂风，扬起一小片尘土。待尘埃落定，我发现他已经不见了。"

    old "Where did he go? Will he come back later?"
    new "Where did he go? Will he come back later?\n他去哪儿了？他之后会回来吗？"

    old "Who can say? If he's abandoning his post, his intentions could be anything."
    new "Who can say? If he's abandoning his post, his intentions could be anything.\n谁能说得准呢？若他是在擅离职守，那他的意图可就难说了。"

    old "He seemed to be almost possessed with madness. Do you suppose it's the full moon that made him that way, or his he usually so unhinged?"
    new "He seemed to be almost possessed with madness. Do you suppose it's the full moon that made him that way, or his he usually so unhinged?\n他看上去几乎被疯狂附体了。你觉得是满月让他变成那样，还是他平日里就这般疯癫？"

    old "Perhaps we'll never know. Let's hurry up and take advantage of the fact that he's gone."
    new "Perhaps we'll never know. Let's hurry up and take advantage of the fact that he's gone.\n也许我们永远不会知道。趁着他离开，我们抓紧时间利用这个机会吧。"

    old "This is all you got? Ha!"
    new "This is all you got? Ha!\n你就这点本事？哈！"

    old "Don't you see? You can't hit us with your bombs. You're too slow."
    new "Don't you see? You can't hit us with your bombs. You're too slow.\n你难道看不出吗？你的炸弹打不中我们。你太慢了。"

    old "Careful with those bombs! You might hurt yourself."
    new "Careful with those bombs! You might hurt yourself.\n当心你的炸弹！你可能会伤到自己。"

    old "You're good! Why are you wasting your time here, with us? You should take part to more epic battles."
    new "You're good! Why are you wasting your time here, with us? You should take part to more epic battles.\n你真厉害！为什么在这里跟我们一起浪费时间？你该去参加更宏大的战斗才是。"

    old "Ohoho! You really are quite something. But I wonder if you can keep up this fight."
    new "Ohoho! You really are quite something. But I wonder if you can keep up this fight.\n哦呵呵！你还真是有两下子。不过，我很好奇你还能不能把这场战斗撑下去。"

    old "You see, indoors, I use weaker explosives. This is an old castle, and its stone walls can only take so much, so I try to restrain myself. But I can see that you, you're something stronger. An enemy of your caliber deserves to see my true powers. I hope the others will forgive me if the furniture gets caught in the blast radius..."
    new "You see, indoors, I use weaker explosives. This is an old castle, and its stone walls can only take so much, so I try to restrain myself. But I can see that you, you're something stronger. An enemy of your caliber deserves to see my true powers. I hope the others will forgive me if the furniture gets caught in the blast radius...\n你看，在室内，我用的都是威力较弱的炸药。这是一座古老的城堡，它的石墙承受力有限，所以我尽量克制自己。但我看得出，你，你更强大。像你这种级别的敌人，理应见识我真正的力量。只希望若家具被卷入爆炸范围，其他人能原谅我……"

    old "You see, with all these dead trees around, I use weaker explosives. It would be inconvenient if I started a fire, so I try to restrain myself. But I can see that you, you're something stronger. An enemy of your caliber deserves to see my true powers. I hope the others will forgive me if I set things ablaze..."
    new "You see, with all these dead trees around, I use weaker explosives. It would be inconvenient if I started a fire, so I try to restrain myself. But I can see that you, you're something stronger. An enemy of your caliber deserves to see my true powers. I hope the others will forgive me if I set things ablaze...\n你看，四周都是枯树，我用的都是威力较弱的炸药。要是不慎引发大火，那可不妙，所以我尽量克制自己。但我看得出，你，你更强大。像你这种级别的敌人，理应见识我真正的力量。只希望若我把一切付之一炬，其他人能原谅我……"

    old "{i}Nootau's explosive and plague balls gain AOE (Area Of Effect)!{/i}"
    new "{i}Nootau's explosive and plague balls gain AOE (Area Of Effect)!{/i}\n{i}Nootau 的 Explosive Ball 与 Plague Ball 获得了 AOE（范围效果）！{/i}"

    old "Heh. Who would have thought mortal flesh could show such strength. Who would have thought I'd be reduced to this..."
    new "Heh. Who would have thought mortal flesh could show such strength. Who would have thought I'd be reduced to this...\n嘿。谁会想到，凡人的血肉竟能展现如此力量。谁又会想到，我竟会沦落到这般田地……"

    old "He's taken quite a beating, but Nootau looks fatigued now. We could put an end to him, once and for all."
    new "He's taken quite a beating, but Nootau looks fatigued now. We could put an end to him, once and for all.\n他挨了不少打，不过此刻 Nootau 看上去已疲惫不堪。我们可以一劳永逸地了结他。"

    old "If you want me to beg for mercy, you're not going to see it. But...I am not above bargaining to survive another day. So, what say you. Let me leave now, and I won't tell the others you're here. You can leave peacefully."
    new "If you want me to beg for mercy, you're not going to see it. But...I am not above bargaining to survive another day. So, what say you. Let me leave now, and I won't tell the others you're here. You can leave peacefully.\n若你想看我求饶，那你是看不到了。不过……为了多活一天，我倒不介意讨价还价。那么，你们意下如何？现在放我离开，我就不把你们在这里的事告诉其他人。你们可以和平离去。"

    old "We came here for a reason, Nootau. And we're not going to leave until we've fulfilled it."
    new "We came here for a reason, Nootau. And we're not going to leave until we've fulfilled it.\n我们来这里是有目的的，Nootau。不达目的，我们绝不离开。"

    old "What, you came here to kill me? Ha!"
    new "What, you came here to kill me? Ha!\n怎么，你们是来杀我的？哈！"

    old "A friend sent us here to rescue someone."
    new "A friend sent us here to rescue someone.\n一位朋友派我们来救人。"

    old "Oh, the prisoners? I was wondering if anyone would come for them. You won't leave without the prisoners, then?"
    new "Oh, the prisoners? I was wondering if anyone would come for them. You won't leave without the prisoners, then?\n哦，那些囚犯？我还纳闷会不会有人来救他们。这么说，不带走囚犯，你们就不走喽？"

    old "You're crazy if you think we'd just walk out of here without trying to rescue them."
    new "You're crazy if you think we'd just walk out of here without trying to rescue them.\n你若以为我们会不设法救他们就一走了之，那你可真是疯了。"

    old "Fine! I'll let you take the prisoners with you! Just leave!"
    new "Fine! I'll let you take the prisoners with you! Just leave!\n好！我让你们把囚犯带走！只要你们离开！"

    old "Hmm. Should I take his offer? This could be a chance to deal with Nootau permanently..."
    new "Hmm. Should I take his offer? This could be a chance to deal with Nootau permanently...\n嗯。我该接受他的提议吗？这也许是个彻底解决 Nootau 的机会……"

    old "We didn't come here to fight you, Nootau. If you can give us the prisoners, we'd have no reason to fight you."
    new "We didn't come here to fight you, Nootau. If you can give us the prisoners, we'd have no reason to fight you.\n我们不是来跟你打的，Nootau。若你能把囚犯交给我们，我们就没有理由和你动手。"

    old "Fine!"
    new "Fine!\n行！"

    old "Nootau pulls out a key and tosses it into the air, so high it almost touches the ceiling. It falls down, and he snatches it out of the air, then tosses it to me."
    new "Nootau pulls out a key and tosses it into the air, so high it almost touches the ceiling. It falls down, and he snatches it out of the air, then tosses it to me.\nNootau 掏出一把钥匙，高高抛起，几乎碰到天花板。钥匙落下时，他一把接住，又把它抛给了我。"

    old "Give them my regards, won't you?"
    new "Give them my regards, won't you?\n替我向他们问好，好吗？"

    old "Nootau makes a hasty retreat through a door at the opposite end of the hall."
    new "Nootau makes a hasty retreat through a door at the opposite end of the hall.\nNootau 从大厅对面的一扇门仓皇退去。"

    old "Let's make use of this key, shall we? Back to the main hall, everyone."
    new "Let's make use of this key, shall we? Back to the main hall, everyone.\n我们把这把钥匙派上用场吧，如何？大家回主厅去。"

    old "We didn't come here to fight you, Nootau. If you leave this fight, we'll spare you."
    new "We didn't come here to fight you, Nootau. If you leave this fight, we'll spare you.\n我们不是来跟你打的，Nootau。若你退出这场战斗，我们就饶你一命。"

    old "Me? Leave?"
    new "Me? Leave?\n我？离开？"

    old "Yes. You need to leave NOW."
    new "Yes. You need to leave NOW.\n是的。你必须现在就走。"

    old "Make no mistakes though: next time we encounter you, you're dead."
    new "Make no mistakes though: next time we encounter you, you're dead.\n不过别搞错了：下次我们再遇上你，你就死定了。"

    old "Dead! What a waste! No no no, I'm going to Zoltar. Yes, there they'll appreciate my talents."
    new "Dead! What a waste! No no no, I'm going to Zoltar. Yes, there they'll appreciate my talents.\n死！多浪费啊！不不不，我要去 Zoltar。对，在那里，他们会赏识我的才华。"

    old "Nootau makes a hasty retreat and vanishes in the darkness."
    new "Nootau makes a hasty retreat and vanishes in the darkness.\nNootau 仓皇退去，消失在黑暗中。"

    old "Do you really think he'll keep his promise?"
    new "Do you really think he'll keep his promise?\n你真的觉得他会信守承诺吗？"

    old "I don't know, but he seemed genuinely scared."
    new "I don't know, but he seemed genuinely scared.\n我不知道，但他看起来真的吓坏了。"

    old "Sorry, Nootau. You don't seem like the type to show mercy, and turnabout seems like fair play to me. You've been beaten. Now, we just need to make it official."
    new "Sorry, Nootau. You don't seem like the type to show mercy, and turnabout seems like fair play to me. You've been beaten. Now, we just need to make it official.\n抱歉了，Nootau。你看起来可不像是会手下留情的人，而以牙还牙在我看来很公平。你已经输了，现在我们只需要让这事正式敲定。"

    old "Nootau lets out a shriek and pulls out several balls. Time to fight..."
    new "Nootau lets out a shriek and pulls out several balls. Time to fight...\nNootau发出一声尖叫，掏出几个球。该开打了……"

    old "Upon closer inspection, it seems that his clothes are filled with a fine powder, almost like dust. It's all that remains of Nootau."
    new "Upon closer inspection, it seems that his clothes are filled with a fine powder, almost like dust. It's all that remains of Nootau.\n仔细一看，他的衣服里似乎装满了细粉末，几乎像灰尘一样。这就是Nootau所剩下的一切。"

    old "The tragic clown."
    new "The tragic clown.\n那个悲惨的小丑。"

    old "Look at that."
    new "Look at that.\n看看那个。"

    old "I inspect the clothing, and find a metal key inside."
    new "I inspect the clothing, and find a metal key inside.\n我检查了那件衣服，在里面找到一把金属钥匙。"

    old "Do you suppose it matches the door in the main hall?"
    new "Do you suppose it matches the door in the main hall?\n你觉得它能打开正厅的那扇门吗？"

    old "Let's find out."
    new "Let's find out.\n我们去找找看。"

    old "Let's get back to the main hall."
    new "Let's get back to the main hall.\n我们回正厅去吧。"

    old "You're trying to play tricks with my mind? But my mind is already tricked!"
    new "You're trying to play tricks with my mind? But my mind is already tricked!\n你想跟我耍花招？可我的脑子早就被耍过了！"

    old "Uh oh. Doesn't look like my talents will work anymore with him now. We need to beat him down to win the fight."
    new "Uh oh. Doesn't look like my talents will work anymore with him now. We need to beat him down to win the fight.\n糟了。看来我的能力现在对他不管用了。我们得把他打倒才能赢下这场战斗。"

    old "We head to the clifftop. It's near the northern part of the plains."
    new "We head to the clifftop. It's near the northern part of the plains.\n我们朝悬崖顶进发。它就在平原北部附近。"

    old "This terrain is starting to get pretty rocky."
    new "This terrain is starting to get pretty rocky.\n这里的地形开始变得相当多岩石了。"

    old "Some historians believe that several thousand years ago, the sea levels were higher. This clifftop might have once overlooked the sea."
    new "Some historians believe that several thousand years ago, the sea levels were higher. This clifftop might have once overlooked the sea.\n一些历史学家认为，几千年前海平面更高，这个悬崖顶也许曾经俯瞰过大海。"

    old "It still seems odd that there's a jagged outcropping out here. Most of these plains are flat and barren."
    new "It still seems odd that there's a jagged outcropping out here. Most of these plains are flat and barren.\n这里冒出这么一块嶙峋的凸岩，还是很奇怪。这片平原大多平坦而荒芜。"

    old "That's what makes this a potentially strategic location for the vampires who are coordinating the attack."
    new "That's what makes this a potentially strategic location for the vampires who are coordinating the attack.\n正因如此，这里才可能成为正在协调这场进攻的吸血鬼们的战略要地。"

    old "Do you really think we'll find something here?"
    new "Do you really think we'll find something here?\n你真的觉得我们会在这里找到什么吗？"

    old "Something, or someone. It could be anything. That's why we need to be ready for a fight."
    new "Something, or someone. It could be anything. That's why we need to be ready for a fight.\n是东西，或是人，什么都可能。所以我们得做好战斗准备。"

    old "If it's something that can be resolved with a fight, we should count that as a blessing. Fights are straightforward."
    new "If it's something that can be resolved with a fight, we should count that as a blessing. Fights are straightforward.\n如果能用一场战斗解决，那我们就该谢天谢地了。战斗至少直截了当。"

    old "Watch your footing."
    new "Watch your footing.\n小心脚下。"

    old "We reach the clifftop. I walk up to the edge and peer over it."
    new "We reach the clifftop. I walk up to the edge and peer over it.\n我们到达了悬崖顶。我走到边缘，朝下面张望。"

    old "Are you sure you want to be that close to the edge?"
    new "Are you sure you want to be that close to the edge?\n你确定要离边缘那么近吗？"

    old "Just checking to see what's down there. Doesn't look like there's anything."
    new "Just checking to see what's down there. Doesn't look like there's anything.\n只是想看看下面有什么。看起来什么都没有。"

    old "On the plus side, that means that anyone out here probably can't see us, right?"
    new "On the plus side, that means that anyone out here probably can't see us, right?\n好的一面是，这意味着外面的人大概也看不见我们，对吧？"

    old "You might think that, but don't get too cocky. You and I can't see through this fog, but who knows what powers of sight our foes possess? I wouldn't underestimate the eyesight of a vampire under the moonlight. Their vision is likely impeded by the fog, but all the same, anyone we try to sneak up on might see us before we see them."
    new "You might think that, but don't get too cocky. You and I can't see through this fog, but who knows what powers of sight our foes possess? I wouldn't underestimate the eyesight of a vampire under the moonlight. Their vision is likely impeded by the fog, but all the same, anyone we try to sneak up on might see us before we see them.\n你可能会这么想，但别太得意。你我虽然看不透这片雾，可谁知道敌人拥有怎样的视力？我可不会低估月光下吸血鬼的眼力。他们的视线多半会被雾挡住，但即便如此，我们想偷袭的任何目标，可能都会比我们先一步看见我们。"

    old "So what are we looking for?"
    new "So what are we looking for?\n那我们到底在找什么？"

    old "Officially, anything unusual, but the main thing I'm concerned about is the possibility of vampires conducting summoning rituals."
    new "Officially, anything unusual, but the main thing I'm concerned about is the possibility of vampires conducting summoning rituals.\n按任务要求，任何不寻常的东西都行，但我最担心的是吸血鬼可能在举行召唤仪式。"

    old "Summoning rituals?"
    new "Summoning rituals?\n召唤仪式？"

    old "Yes. They might involve hexes or markings on the ground."
    new "Yes. They might involve hexes or markings on the ground.\n对。仪式可能会用到地面上的符咒或标记。"

    old "You mean markings like this?"
    new "You mean markings like this?\n你是说像这样的标记吗？"

    old "My, my. Is that a circle drawn in blood?"
    new "My, my. Is that a circle drawn in blood?\n哎呀呀。那是一个用血画成的圈吗？"

    old "Looks like it. Fresh, too."
    new "Looks like it. Fresh, too.\n看起来是的，而且血还是新鲜的。"

    old "I think this may be exactly the reason that Captain Thomas sent us with salt."
    new "I think this may be exactly the reason that Captain Thomas sent us with salt.\n我想，这大概正是Thomas队长派我们带盐来的原因。"

    old "You think this circle of blood is a sign that some blood ritual is being conducted here? What if the ritual is already complete?"
    new "You think this circle of blood is a sign that some blood ritual is being conducted here? What if the ritual is already complete?\n你觉得这个血圈说明这里正在举行某种血祭仪式？要是仪式已经完成了怎么办？"

    old "It almost looks as if this circle was hastily-drawn, and then abandoned."
    new "It almost looks as if this circle was hastily-drawn, and then abandoned.\n看起来这个圈像是匆忙画下，然后就被弃置了。"

    old "Well, if someone abandoned it mid-ritual, let's not give them a circle of blood to come back to."
    new "Well, if someone abandoned it mid-ritual, let's not give them a circle of blood to come back to.\n好吧，如果有人中途放弃了仪式，那我们就别留个血圈让他回来接着用。"

    old "I take a bag of salt and spread it over the pool of blood."
    new "I take a bag of salt and spread it over the pool of blood.\n我取出一袋盐，撒在那滩血上。"

    old "If someone abandoned this ritual, they might still be around here. Maybe they abandoned this spot for the ritual because they found a better location."
    new "If someone abandoned this ritual, they might still be around here. Maybe they abandoned this spot for the ritual because they found a better location.\n如果有人放弃了这个仪式，他们可能还在附近。也许他们放弃这个地方，是因为找到了更好的仪式地点。"

    old "In that case, we'd better be extra careful."
    new "In that case, we'd better be extra careful.\n那样的话，我们最好格外小心。"

    old "As if we were only being somewhat careful before."
    new "As if we were only being somewhat careful before.\n说得好像我们之前只是稍微小心了一点似的。"

    old "We might have interrupted whoever drew that circle in blood. Keep your eyes peeled for any sort of motion."
    new "We might have interrupted whoever drew that circle in blood. Keep your eyes peeled for any sort of motion.\n我们可能打断了那个用血画圈的人。睁大眼睛，留意任何动静。"

    old "I continue walking along the clifftop. We've almost reached the furthest point of the rocky protrusion."
    new "I continue walking along the clifftop. We've almost reached the furthest point of the rocky protrusion.\n我继续沿着悬崖顶往前走。我们几乎已经到了这块凸岩最远的一端。"

    old "I hear the sound of flapping wings, and I motion for everyone to get down and stay quiet. For a moment, I hear nothing but the sound of the wind. Moments later, a group of crows flies overhead, and their cawing breaks the silence."
    new "I hear the sound of flapping wings, and I motion for everyone to get down and stay quiet. For a moment, I hear nothing but the sound of the wind. Moments later, a group of crows flies overhead, and their cawing breaks the silence.\n我听到拍打翅膀的声音，便示意所有人趴下并保持安静。有那么一会儿，我耳边只有风声。片刻之后，一群乌鸦从头顶飞过，它们的呱叫打破了寂静。"

    old "Chilling. As if the sound of crows on a foggy night above a circle of blood wasn't eerie enough."
    new "Chilling. As if the sound of crows on a foggy night above a circle of blood wasn't eerie enough.\n真瘆人。雾夜里，血圈上方传来乌鸦的叫声，这还不够诡异吗。"

    old "Maybe tonight is the night we learn about the existence of flying vampires."
    new "Maybe tonight is the night we learn about the existence of flying vampires.\n也许今晚，我们就会知道是否存在会飞的吸血鬼了。"

    old "No use speculating. Let's backtrack to where we found the circle."
    new "No use speculating. Let's backtrack to where we found the circle.\n瞎猜也没用。我们回到发现那个圈的地方去。"

    old "We retrace our steps. The circle seems to have vanished. I feel a chill run down my spine."
    new "We retrace our steps. The circle seems to have vanished. I feel a chill run down my spine.\n我们沿原路返回。那个圈似乎消失了。我感到一阵寒意顺着脊背蹿下去。"

    old "I've got a bad feeling about this."
    new "I've got a bad feeling about this.\n我有种不好的预感。"

    old "Visitors! Always with the interruptions! Have you come to play?"
    new "Visitors! Always with the interruptions! Have you come to play?\n来客！总是来打扰！你们是来玩的吗？"

    old "Vampire!"
    new "Vampire!\n吸血鬼！"

    old "At a glance, we would appear to have the advantage. I see only one vampire before me. And yet, I can't help but feel that there might be some hidden danger, lurking just out of sight."
    new "At a glance, we would appear to have the advantage. I see only one vampire before me. And yet, I can't help but feel that there might be some hidden danger, lurking just out of sight.\n乍一看，我们似乎占了上风。我面前只有一个吸血鬼。然而，我还是忍不住觉得，也许有什么隐蔽的危险，正潜伏在视线之外。"

    old "[protag], I heard that someone had disturbed my circle, and now I know who it is. So nice to see you face to face."
    new "[protag], I heard that someone had disturbed my circle, and now I know who it is. So nice to see you face to face.\n[protag]，我听说有人动过我的圈，现在我知道是谁了。能和你面对面相见，真是太好了。"

    old "You heard us?"
    new "You heard us?\n你听见我们了？"

    old "You know, I was thinking of joining the fight at the city gates, finding some new carrion for them to dine on. But then you all were nice enough to come and deliver yourselves to me."
    new "You know, I was thinking of joining the fight at the city gates, finding some new carrion for them to dine on. But then you all were nice enough to come and deliver yourselves to me.\n你知道吗，我本来想着去城门加入战斗，给它们找点新鲜腐肉吃。结果你们倒好，自己送上门来了。"

    old "Why is this vampire so self-assured? We have him outnumbered, and despite all his bravado, I doubt that he's spoiling for a fight. I don't think the vampires expected to encounter anyone this far away from Grimoire's defenses. They were supposed to be the aggressors, not us."
    new "Why is this vampire so self-assured? We have him outnumbered, and despite all his bravado, I doubt that he's spoiling for a fight. I don't think the vampires expected to encounter anyone this far away from Grimoire's defenses. They were supposed to be the aggressors, not us.\n这个吸血鬼为什么这么自信？我们人数占优，尽管他虚张声势，我仍怀疑他未必真想打这一仗。我想吸血鬼们没料到，在远离Grimoire防线这么远的地方会遇到人。本应是他们来进攻，而不是我们。"

    old "I notice Zephyr cast a glance upward toward the edge of the cliff. Could it be that he's planning his exit? Does jumping off of a cliff really constitute an exit strategy for this vampire? Powers of flight, or levitation, perhaps? There's no way to know for certain, but I don't think he would have started talking to us without a plan."
    new "I notice Zephyr cast a glance upward toward the edge of the cliff. Could it be that he's planning his exit? Does jumping off of a cliff really constitute an exit strategy for this vampire? Powers of flight, or levitation, perhaps? There's no way to know for certain, but I don't think he would have started talking to us without a plan.\n我注意到Zephyr朝悬崖边缘上方瞥了一眼。他会不会是在盘算退路？对这个吸血鬼来说，跳下悬崖真的算一种脱身之计吗？也许他会飞，或能悬浮？无法确定，但我想，要不是心里有打算，他是不会跟我们开口搭话的。"

    old "He might not have a plan to kill us, but he doesn't need one if he has an exit strategy. But maybe that means he can be negotiated with."
    new "He might not have a plan to kill us, but he doesn't need one if he has an exit strategy. But maybe that means he can be negotiated with.\n他也许没有杀我们的打算，但如果他有脱身之计，也就不需要了。不过，这也许意味着可以和他谈条件。"

    old "Zephyr takes the vial in his hands, he looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness."
    new "Zephyr takes the vial in his hands, he looks confused, caught by surprise from my kindness.\nZephyr把瓶子接在手里，一脸困惑，被我的善意弄得措手不及。"

    old "Unable to resist, Zephyr swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as he finishes though, he starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal."
    new "Unable to resist, Zephyr swallows the vial content all at once. As soon as he finishes though, he starts to feel bad. Zachary and Valery said the poison should be lethal.\nZephyr无法抗拒，一口气吞下了瓶里的东西。然而刚一吞下，他就开始感到不适。Zachary和Valery说过，这毒应当致命。"

    old "You are Zephyr? Your friends told me about you, but I didn't realize you'd look so...scrawny. Your friends are losing the fight at Grimoire's gates, and badly. In fact, it wouldn't surprise me if they're all dead by now. You'll be the last one."
    new "You are Zephyr? Your friends told me about you, but I didn't realize you'd look so...scrawny. Your friends are losing the fight at Grimoire's gates, and badly. In fact, it wouldn't surprise me if they're all dead by now. You'll be the last one.\n你就是Zephyr？你的朋友们跟我提过你，但我没想到你看起来这么……瘦弱。你的朋友们在Grimoire城门前的战斗节节败退，而且败得很惨。说实话，就算他们现在全死了，我也不会惊讶。你会是最后一个。"

    old "Look, we just came from the city gates. Do you really think that we'd be here if that wasn't the case? If your side was winning, we'd be defending the city to protect its survival. The only reason that we came out here to hunt you down is that our victory at the city gates is so certain. You'll be the last vampire to fall."
    new "Look, we just came from the city gates. Do you really think that we'd be here if that wasn't the case? If your side was winning, we'd be defending the city to protect its survival. The only reason that we came out here to hunt you down is that our victory at the city gates is so certain. You'll be the last vampire to fall.\n听着，我们刚从城门那边过来。要不是这样，你觉得我们会在这里吗？如果你们占了上风，我们早该守着城、保护它的存亡了。我们之所以跑到这里来追捕你，是因为我们在城门前的胜利已经板上钉钉。你会是最后一个倒下的吸血鬼。"

    old "Impossible? No. You've severely underestimated Grimoire's defenses. Do you know who we are? We're the same ones who walked right into your castle a month ago and walked out with several prisoners. We put the spook in some of your friends, too. You should be quaking in your boots right now."
    new "Impossible? No. You've severely underestimated Grimoire's defenses. Do you know who we are? We're the same ones who walked right into your castle a month ago and walked out with several prisoners. We put the spook in some of your friends, too. You should be quaking in your boots right now.\n不可能？不。是你严重低估了Grimoire的防御。你知道我们是谁吗？一个月前，正是我们径直走进你们的城堡，又带着几名俘虏走了出来。我们还把你的几个同伴吓得不轻。你现在本该吓得浑身发抖才对。"

    old "I've had lots of chances to practice killing the undead. I've gotten a few chances to kill vampires, too. I think I'm going to enjoy dealing with you."
    new "I've had lots of chances to practice killing the undead. I've gotten a few chances to kill vampires, too. I think I'm going to enjoy dealing with you.\n我有很多机会练习杀不死生物，也有过几次杀吸血鬼的机会。我想，对付你应该会让我很享受。"

    old "Zephyr turns to the edge of the cliff, then takes a running leap and disappears over the edge."
    new "Zephyr turns to the edge of the cliff, then takes a running leap and disappears over the edge.\nZephyr转向悬崖边缘，助跑一跃，消失在了崖边之外。"

    old "Oh, come on. Why do you think they left you to deal with things here, at the edge of this clifftop? I can see it in your eyes. You'd rather be on the frontlines. You deserve glory. But they won't let you have it. What reason would they have for doing that, other than simply not liking you?"
    new "Oh, come on. Why do you think they left you to deal with things here, at the edge of this clifftop? I can see it in your eyes. You'd rather be on the frontlines. You deserve glory. But they won't let you have it. What reason would they have for doing that, other than simply not liking you?\n哦，得了吧。你觉得他们为什么把你留在这里、留在这个悬崖顶边上处理这些事？我从你的眼神里看得出来，你更想上前线。你配得上荣耀，可他们不让你得到。除了单纯不喜欢你之外，他们还能有什么理由这么做？"

    old "I think it means that we shouldn't spend time waiting to see if he returns."
    new "I think it means that we shouldn't spend time waiting to see if he returns.\n我觉得这意味着，我们不该浪费时间等他回不回来。"

    old "He mentioned 'friends' of his. Are there other vampires lurking about?"
    new "He mentioned 'friends' of his. Are there other vampires lurking about?\n他提到了他的“朋友”。附近还潜伏着别的吸血鬼吗？"

    old "I'm not sure. It's a possibility, but this is no ordinary vampire..."
    new "I'm not sure. It's a possibility, but this is no ordinary vampire...\n我不确定。有这种可能，但这家伙可不是普通吸血鬼……"

    old "We begin heading back to the plains."
    new "We begin heading back to the plains.\n我们开始返回平原。"

    old "As we walk, I notice that several crows are perched at the cliff's edge, sitting completely still, as if poised and watching us. A feeling of discomfort wells within me, and I try to avoid looking too closely into the crows' eyes as my pace becomes more even and deliberate."
    new "As we walk, I notice that several crows are perched at the cliff's edge, sitting completely still, as if poised and watching us. A feeling of discomfort wells within me, and I try to avoid looking too closely into the crows' eyes as my pace becomes more even and deliberate.\n走着走着，我注意到有几只乌鸦栖息在悬崖边缘，一动不动地坐着，仿佛正蓄势盯着我们。我心里涌起一阵不安，随着脚步变得愈发平稳而谨慎，我尽量避免去直视乌鸦的眼睛。"

    old "I hope you didn't think you'd seen the last of me. And I think I can show you what I'm really made of."
    new "I hope you didn't think you'd seen the last of me. And I think I can show you what I'm really made of.\n希望你别以为再也见不到我了。而且，我想我可以让你看看我真正的本事。"

    old "I'm going to cut you to shreds and feed your flesh to the crows. The birds usually prefer carrion, but they've been known to feast on the flesh of the living if they get a whiff of blood in the air. I guess that's why crows and I get along so well. That kind of bloodlust is in our nature."
    new "I'm going to cut you to shreds and feed your flesh to the crows. The birds usually prefer carrion, but they've been known to feast on the flesh of the living if they get a whiff of blood in the air. I guess that's why crows and I get along so well. That kind of bloodlust is in our nature.\n我要把你剁成碎片，把你的肉喂给乌鸦。这些鸟平时更爱吃腐肉，但据说只要闻到空气里有血腥味，它们也会大啖活人的肉。我想，这正是我和乌鸦如此投缘的原因。那种嗜血的欲望，是我们天性里就有的。"

    old "It's simple. There are undead attacking Grimoire. You're undead. And if that summoning circle we saw earlier was your work, getting rid of you will greatly aid our allies."
    new "It's simple. There are undead attacking Grimoire. You're undead. And if that summoning circle we saw earlier was your work, getting rid of you will greatly aid our allies.\n很简单。有不死生物正在攻打Grimoire，而你也是不死生物。如果之前我们看到的那个召唤圈是你画的，那么除掉你，就能大大帮助我们的盟友。"

    old "I don't think you need me to explain any of this to you. This only ends in one way."
    new "I don't think you need me to explain any of this to you. This only ends in one way.\n我想这些不用我向你解释。这件事只有一种结局。"

    old "I raise my weapon."
    new "I raise my weapon.\n我举起武器。"

    old "Wait! What if I surrender?"
    new "Wait! What if I surrender?\n等等！如果我投降呢？"

    old "Not good enough."
    new "Not good enough.\n那可不够。"

    old "I'll leave. I swear it. This wasn't my fight to begin with, anyway."
    new "I'll leave. I swear it. This wasn't my fight to begin with, anyway.\n我会离开的，我发誓。而且这场战斗本来就不关我的事。"

    old "Zephyr turns to the cliff's face. He might be looking to get away. If he really does leave the fields, that could serve our purposes..."
    new "Zephyr turns to the cliff's face. He might be looking to get away. If he really does leave the fields, that could serve our purposes...\nZephyr转向崖壁。他可能是在找机会脱身。如果他真的离开这片战场，那对我们也有好处……"

    old "Yes! Thanks. I'll go. I'll go now. This is not my fight!"
    new "Yes! Thanks. I'll go. I'll go now. This is not my fight!\n好！多谢。我这就走。我这就走。这场战斗不关我的事！"

    old "He's gone."
    new "He's gone.\n他走了。"

    old "I wonder why he said that's 'not his fight'?"
    new "I wonder why he said that's 'not his fight'?\n我在想，他为什么说那“不是他的战斗”呢？"

    old "Maybe we'll find out. Let's go back now."
    new "Maybe we'll find out. Let's go back now.\n也许我们以后会知道。现在我们回去吧。"

    old "I visit Apolimesho in the council chambers in the early evening, several hours before nightfall."
    new "I visit Apolimesho in the council chambers in the early evening, several hours before nightfall.\n傍晚时分，在入夜前几小时，我去议会厅拜访了Apolimesho。"

    old "[protag]. I trust you are ready for tonight's mission?"
    new "[protag]. I trust you are ready for tonight's mission?\n[protag]，我相信你已经为今晚的任务做好了准备？"

    old "I've had weeks to prepare. During that time, being ready for tonight has been a single-minded obsession of mine. Yes, of course I'm ready."
    new "I've had weeks to prepare. During that time, being ready for tonight has been a single-minded obsession of mine. Yes, of course I'm ready.\n我已经准备了好几个星期。这段时间里，为今晚做好准备一直是我心无旁骛的执念。是的，我当然准备好了。"

    old "Very good, [protag]. Though, I do hope that you don't grow too obsessed."
    new "Very good, [protag]. Though, I do hope that you don't grow too obsessed.\n很好，[protag]。不过，我还是希望你别太过执着。"

    old "That seems like an odd thing to say. Isn't this mission what's most important?"
    new "That seems like an odd thing to say. Isn't this mission what's most important?\n这话听起来有点奇怪。这任务难道不是最重要的吗？"

    old "What's important is for you to be the most effective leader you can be. And sometimes that requires a bit of self-care."
    new "What's important is for you to be the most effective leader you can be. And sometimes that requires a bit of self-care.\n重要的是，你要成为你能成为的最出色的领袖。而有时候，这需要一点自我照顾。"

    old "Don't worry, Apolimesho. I do what's necessary, but never beyond what I'm capable of."
    new "Don't worry, Apolimesho. I do what's necessary, but never beyond what I'm capable of.\n别担心，Apolimesho。我做该做的事，但绝不超出自己的能力。"

    old "That's good. Take care of yourself, [protag]. It won't do for you to get killed out there."
    new "That's good. Take care of yourself, [protag]. It won't do for you to get killed out there.\n那就好。照顾好自己，[protag]。你要是在外面送了命，可就不妙了。"

    old "Would you take any answer besides 'yes?' At this point, I don't believe that backing down is much of an option."
    new "Would you take any answer besides 'yes?' At this point, I don't believe that backing down is much of an option.\n除了“是”，你还会接受别的回答吗？事到如今，我觉得打退堂鼓已经不是个选项了。"

    old "Do not be so arrogant as to presume that the council does not have contingencies prepared."
    new "Do not be so arrogant as to presume that the council does not have contingencies prepared.\n别那么傲慢，以为议会没有准备应急方案。"

    old "You're ready to replace me?"
    new "You're ready to replace me?\n你已经准备好取代我了？"

    old "Replace you? No. But during the time that you've had time to prepare for your mission, the council has had time to prepare for the eventuality that your mission would not succeed."
    new "Replace you? No. But during the time that you've had time to prepare for your mission, the council has had time to prepare for the eventuality that your mission would not succeed.\n取代你？不。只是在你为任务做准备的时间里，议会也为你的任务可能不会成功这种情况做了准备。"

    old "So, you're saying I could back out if I wanted to."
    new "So, you're saying I could back out if I wanted to.\n所以，你是说只要我想，我就可以退出。"

    old "No, I would not advise that at all. The council has prepared other measures. However, their contingencies are, in my estimation, woefully inadequate."
    new "No, I would not advise that at all. The council has prepared other measures. However, their contingencies are, in my estimation, woefully inadequate.\n不，我绝不会建议你这么做。议会确实准备了其他措施，但依我估计，他们的应急方案实在是糟糕透顶，远远不够。"

    old "That's awfully pessimistic."
    new "That's awfully pessimistic.\n这话也太悲观了。"

    old "I am just saying that even a less-than-excellent performance from you would far exceed what the council would be capable of providing in your absence. Take it as a word of encouragement, [protag]."
    new "I am just saying that even a less-than-excellent performance from you would far exceed what the council would be capable of providing in your absence. Take it as a word of encouragement, [protag].\n我只是想说，即便你的表现不算出色，也远胜过你缺席时议会所能提供的。就当作一句鼓励的话吧，[protag]。"

    old "I'm not sure that I should find it encouraging that the council's alternatives to trusting me seem to be so dire, but I suppose I shouldn't be surprised."
    new "I'm not sure that I should find it encouraging that the council's alternatives to trusting me seem to be so dire, but I suppose I shouldn't be surprised.\n我不太确定，议会不信任我时的备选方案竟如此不堪，这到底算不算值得欣慰，但我想我也不该感到意外。"

    old "I have faith in your ability to complete this mission, [protag]. Were it up to me, all of the resources that the council spent coming up with contingency options would be spent instead on supporting you in your mission. I had to take it upon myself to begin amassing what additional resources I could. In secret, of course."
    new "I have faith in your ability to complete this mission, [protag]. Were it up to me, all of the resources that the council spent coming up with contingency options would be spent instead on supporting you in your mission. I had to take it upon myself to begin amassing what additional resources I could. In secret, of course.\n我相信你有能力完成这个任务，[protag]。要是由我做主，议会用来拟定应急方案的全部资源，都会转而用来支援你的任务。我不得不自己动手，开始尽可能多地积攒额外资源。当然，是秘密进行的。"

    old "I collected a small cache of sundries for your mission tonight. Healing items, the sort that might prove useful in battle."
    new "I collected a small cache of sundries for your mission tonight. Healing items, the sort that might prove useful in battle.\n我为今晚的任务收集了一小批杂项物资。都是治疗用品，在战斗中可能会派上用场。"

    old "Ah, good. Items to cure injuries."
    new "Ah, good. Items to cure injuries.\n啊，太好了。是治疗伤势的物品。"

    old "Or inflict them. Forget not, [protag]. You are facing undead of many sorts. And the holy and curative properties that cause some items to heal wounds in the living can be used to craft 'healing bombs' that cause to rend and assail the flesh of the undead."
    new "Or inflict them. Forget not, [protag]. You are facing undead of many sorts. And the holy and curative properties that cause some items to heal wounds in the living can be used to craft 'healing bombs' that cause to rend and assail the flesh of the undead.\n或者造成伤势。别忘了，[protag]。你要面对的是各种各样的不死生物。那些能让某些物品治愈活人伤口的神圣与治疗之力，也可以用来制造“healing bombs”，去撕裂、侵袭不死生物的血肉。"

    old "That's a good thing to keep in mind, Apolimesho. I'll be sure not to forget it."
    new "That's a good thing to keep in mind, Apolimesho. I'll be sure not to forget it.\n这倒是值得记在心里，Apolimesho。我一定会记住的。"

    old "Tell me, [protag]. I'm curious. What do you think was your biggest talent so far? How did you convince all your teammates to join you in this dangerous mission? What's been most essential in helping you overcome all the challenges thrown at you along the path?"
    new "Tell me, [protag]. I'm curious. What do you think was your biggest talent so far? How did you convince all your teammates to join you in this dangerous mission? What's been most essential in helping you overcome all the challenges thrown at you along the path?\n告诉我，[protag]，我很好奇。你觉得迄今为止，你最大的才能是什么？你是怎样说服所有队友加入这场危险任务的？在帮你克服沿途所有挑战的过程中，什么最重要？"

    old "Using force, eh?"
    new "Using force, eh?\n靠武力，是吗？"

    old "Not necessarily. But you do have to show that you're willing to go to extreme lengths to achieve your goal."
    new "Not necessarily. But you do have to show that you're willing to go to extreme lengths to achieve your goal.\n不一定。但你确实得让人看到，你愿意为实现目标而拼尽全力。"

    old "That sounds like intimidation to me."
    new "That sounds like intimidation to me.\n在我看来，这听起来像是恐吓。"

    old "Intimidation is part of it. But you can intimidate people with more than just violence. Displaying determination, focus, and dedication can sometimes inspire both fear and admiration in others. Even if you never pick up a weapon."
    new "Intimidation is part of it. But you can intimidate people with more than just violence. Displaying determination, focus, and dedication can sometimes inspire both fear and admiration in others. Even if you never pick up a weapon.\n恐吓是其中一部分。但你不必只靠暴力来震慑人。展现出决心、专注与投入，有时也能让别人既敬畏又佩服，哪怕你从不拿起武器。"

    old "I suppose so, but you need a lot of talent to be able to do this."
    new "I suppose so, but you need a lot of talent to be able to do this.\n我想也是，不过要做到这点，需要很高的才能。"

    old "If you face a determined foe who fights better than you, be they faster, stronger, or more skilled with a weapon than you are, it can be effective to challenge them on a mental level instead."
    new "If you face a determined foe who fights better than you, be they faster, stronger, or more skilled with a weapon than you are, it can be effective to challenge them on a mental level instead.\n如果你面对一个意志坚定、打起来比你强的敌人，无论对方是更快、更强，还是使武器更娴熟，改从精神层面挑战他们，反而可能更有效。"

    old "Sometimes it's as simple as saying something that instills doubt. Make them question their motivations. Sometimes, you can make someone question something they were previously confident about through the subtle power of persuasion."
    new "Sometimes it's as simple as saying something that instills doubt. Make them question their motivations. Sometimes, you can make someone question something they were previously confident about through the subtle power of persuasion.\n有时候简单到只需说一句能埋下怀疑种子的话。让他们质疑自己的动机。有时，你可以凭借微妙的说服力，让某人对原本笃信的事情产生怀疑。"

    old "In the same way, if you make people think about what they're doing, why they're doing it, why they made certain choices...sometimes it's easier to have them join you. Some people just naturally want to be followers, but they don't realize it until you make them question their previously-held beliefs."
    new "In the same way, if you make people think about what they're doing, why they're doing it, why they made certain choices...sometimes it's easier to have them join you. Some people just naturally want to be followers, but they don't realize it until you make them question their previously-held beliefs.\n同样，如果你让人们思考自己在做什么、为什么要做、当初为何做出某些选择……有时让他们加入你就会更容易。有些人天生就想当追随者，只是直到你让他们质疑自己一直以来的信念之前，他们自己都没意识到。"

    old "I see what you mean. Very clever."
    new "I see what you mean. Very clever.\n我明白你的意思了。很高明。"

    old "Yes, not everyone can keep cold blood under pressure."
    new "Yes, not everyone can keep cold blood under pressure.\n是啊，不是每个人都能在压力下保持冷静。"

    old "For obvious reasons, if you put pressure on a target, they'll fight worse. But the same can work also if you need to persuade others you're right."
    new "For obvious reasons, if you put pressure on a target, they'll fight worse. But the same can work also if you need to persuade others you're right.\n显而易见，如果你给目标施压，他们就会打得更差。但同样，当你需要说服别人你是对的时，这一招也能奏效。"

    old "Some people tend to delay their decisions, to ponder them for too long. Unfortunately, the urgency of our mission doesn't afford us that luxury. So I had to put a bit of pressure on them as well."
    new "Some people tend to delay their decisions, to ponder them for too long. Unfortunately, the urgency of our mission doesn't afford us that luxury. So I had to put a bit of pressure on them as well.\n有些人总爱拖延决定，琢磨太久。可惜，我们任务的紧迫性不允许我们享受这种奢侈。所以我也只好给他们施加一点压力。"

    old "It seems it worked well."
    new "It seems it worked well.\n看来效果不错。"

    old "Symphathize with the enemies?"
    new "Symphathize with the enemies?\n同情敌人吗？"

    old "Yes. Very few of them expect this when they enter the fight. It's an unorthodox approach, I'll admit. But the fact that it's unexpected is part of what can make it so effective."
    new "Yes. Very few of them expect this when they enter the fight. It's an unorthodox approach, I'll admit. But the fact that it's unexpected is part of what can make it so effective.\n没错。很少有人会在进入战斗时料到这一手。我承认，这是种非常规的做法。但正因为它出人意料，才格外有效。"

    old "Sympathy isn't just about showing compassion and kindness for people. It's about understanding what it is that's really driving them. Even if you don't particularly like someone, even if they're your enemy on the battlefield, a bit of sympathy can go a long way toward building a bridge of understanding."
    new "Sympathy isn't just about showing compassion and kindness for people. It's about understanding what it is that's really driving them. Even if you don't particularly like someone, even if they're your enemy on the battlefield, a bit of sympathy can go a long way toward building a bridge of understanding.\n同情不只是对人表示怜悯与善意，而是要理解真正驱动他们的是什么。即使你不怎么喜欢一个人，即使他是战场上的敌人，一点同情也能在搭建理解的桥梁上发挥很大作用。"

    old "Though some people think the best way to gain respect is by appearing strong and intimidating, I often find that sympathizing with them can be just as effective at winning their respect and trust."
    new "Though some people think the best way to gain respect is by appearing strong and intimidating, I often find that sympathizing with them can be just as effective at winning their respect and trust.\n虽然有些人认为赢得尊重的最好方式是表现得强势而慑人，但我常常发现，同情他们同样能有效地赢得他们的尊重与信任。"

    old "It seems to have paid off for you. Your allies seems to really trust you."
    new "It seems to have paid off for you. Your allies seems to really trust you.\n看来这对你颇有成效。你的盟友们似乎真的很信任你。"

    old "So this is how I got here, with a full team ready to face any danger inside N'Mar."
    new "So this is how I got here, with a full team ready to face any danger inside N'Mar.\n就这样，我来到了这里，带着一支完整的队伍，随时准备面对N'Mar内部的任何危险。"

    old "Oh I almost forgot. The elves sent me a gift as well. They won't be directly involved in the mission for political reasons, but they wanted to show support by sending an enchanted item for you to use."
    new "Oh I almost forgot. The elves sent me a gift as well. They won't be directly involved in the mission for political reasons, but they wanted to show support by sending an enchanted item for you to use.\n哦，我差点忘了。精灵们也送来了一份礼物。出于政治原因，他们不会直接参与任务，但想通过送你一件附魔物品来表达支持。"

    old "Send them my thanks, this will be an invaluable help!"
    new "Send them my thanks, this will be an invaluable help!\n请代我向他们致谢，这将是无比珍贵的帮助！"

    old "The dwarves have sent something as well. Nothing enchanted in this case, just an ordinary but very well crafted sword."
    new "The dwarves have sent something as well. Nothing enchanted in this case, just an ordinary but very well crafted sword.\n矮人们也送来了东西。这次没有附魔，只是一把普通但做工极其精良的剑。"

    old "Such a beautiful craftsmanship. This will be helpful too."
    new "Such a beautiful craftsmanship. This will be helpful too.\n这工艺真漂亮。它也会派上用场的。"

    old "Excellent. Tonight, at nightfall, the city guard will be amassing at the city gates, just in case any undead decide to wander close to the city. However, it will be up to you to gather your forces and infiltrate the castle."
    new "Excellent. Tonight, at nightfall, the city guard will be amassing at the city gates, just in case any undead decide to wander close to the city. However, it will be up to you to gather your forces and infiltrate the castle.\n好极了。今晚入夜时分，城卫队会集结在城门处，以防有不死生物游荡到城市附近。不过，集结你的队伍、潜入城堡，就要靠你自己了。"

    old "Any last-minute bits of advice?"
    new "Any last-minute bits of advice?\n还有什么最后的建议吗？"

    old "Do not allow your ambitions for this mission to grow too great. Remember, there is a reason that we are sending you along with a small group, rather than an entire regiment of soldiers. Obviously, you will encounter enemies along the way, and some amount of fighting is inevitable, but don't forget, you are there to investigate, not wage war."
    new "Do not allow your ambitions for this mission to grow too great. Remember, there is a reason that we are sending you along with a small group, rather than an entire regiment of soldiers. Obviously, you will encounter enemies along the way, and some amount of fighting is inevitable, but don't forget, you are there to investigate, not wage war.\n别让对这任务的雄心变得过大。记住，我们派你带一支小队去，而不是整团士兵，是有原因的。显然，你沿途会遇到敌人，某些战斗在所难免，但别忘了，你去那里是为了调查，而不是开战。"

    old "That being said...if opportunity presents itself, and you find yourself poised to strike a crippling blow before leaving with your findings and information, perhaps it would be wise to seize that opportunity. But I would do this only if you are acting from a position of great confidence. I would think it best to avoid any unneccesary risks."
    new "That being said...if opportunity presents itself, and you find yourself poised to strike a crippling blow before leaving with your findings and information, perhaps it would be wise to seize that opportunity. But I would do this only if you are acting from a position of great confidence. I would think it best to avoid any unneccesary risks.\n话虽如此……如果机会出现，而你发现自己在带着发现与情报离开之前，正好有机会发动致命一击，那么抓住这个机会或许是明智的。但只有在你有十足把握的情况下，我才会这么做。我认为最好还是避免任何不必要的风险。"

    old "Alright. With any luck, I'll be back in Grimoire before daybreak."
    new "Alright. With any luck, I'll be back in Grimoire before daybreak.\n好的。运气好的话，我会在天亮前回到Grimoire。"

    old "Good night, [protag]. May the winds of fortune be in your favor."
    new "Good night, [protag]. May the winds of fortune be in your favor.\n晚安，[protag]。愿幸运之风眷顾你。"

    old "We get close to the castle, we can spot it from one of the hills nearby, despite the heavy fog."
    new "We get close to the castle, we can spot it from one of the hills nearby, despite the heavy fog.\n我们靠近了城堡，尽管浓雾弥漫，仍能从附近的一座山丘上望见它。"

    old "This is both a scary yet majestic view."
    new "This is both a scary yet majestic view.\n这景象既骇人，又壮丽。"

    old "We must proceed with caution. The fog should hide our movements, so actually helping us to sneak inside."
    new "We must proceed with caution. The fog should hide our movements, so actually helping us to sneak inside.\n我们必须谨慎前进。这雾应当能掩盖我们的行动，实际上是在帮我们潜入其中。"

    old "I'm surprised we found nobody on our path so far."
    new "I'm surprised we found nobody on our path so far.\n让我惊讶的是，到目前为止，我们路上一个人都没遇到。"

    old "Don't push our luck. Come, let's get closer."
    new "Don't push our luck. Come, let's get closer.\n别得寸进尺。来，我们再靠近一点。"

    old "With the fog, it takes us much longer to walk even the smallest distances. However, after half hour we're almost there."
    new "With the fog, it takes us much longer to walk even the smallest distances. However, after half hour we're almost there.\n有这雾，哪怕最短的一段路，我们也要花上长得多的时间。不过，半小时后，我们差不多就到了。"

    old "Woah! Look at their size!"
    new "Woah! Look at their size!\n哇！看它们个头有多大！"

    old "Vampires! I mean, bats!"
    new "Vampires! I mean, bats!\n吸血鬼！我是说，蝙蝠！"

    old "More likely, vampire bats. They're just animals, but better kill them, we don't want to attract unwanted attention."
    new "More likely, vampire bats. They're just animals, but better kill them, we don't want to attract unwanted attention.\n更可能是吸血蝙蝠。它们只是动物，但最好还是杀掉，我们可不想引来不必要的注意。"

    old "Good, there seems to be no more of them. Let's get inside the castle."
    new "Good, there seems to be no more of them. Let's get inside the castle.\n好，似乎没有更多了。我们进城堡吧。"

    old "We arrive in the castle. As we enter, I hear a faint but chilling sound of voices, just beyond a door at the end of the hall."
    new "We arrive in the castle. As we enter, I hear a faint but chilling sound of voices, just beyond a door at the end of the hall.\n我们抵达城堡。刚走进去，我就听到一阵微弱却令人毛骨悚然的说话声，就在大厅尽头的一扇门后。"

    old "Are those the moans of the undead?"
    new "Are those the moans of the undead?\n那是不死生物的呻吟声吗？"

    old "Wait a minute. Listen more closely."
    new "Wait a minute. Listen more closely.\n等一下，再仔细听听。"

    old "I approach the door and place my ear to it."
    new "I approach the door and place my ear to it.\n我走近那扇门，把耳朵贴了上去。"

    old "Careful! It might be some kind of trap."
    new "Careful! It might be some kind of trap.\n小心！可能是某种陷阱。"

    old "We are already inside the castle's main hall. If they intended to spring any sort of trap on us, they would have done it by now. Likely, they didn't expect anyone to come this far. That would explain why the place is completely vacated."
    new "We are already inside the castle's main hall. If they intended to spring any sort of trap on us, they would have done it by now. Likely, they didn't expect anyone to come this far. That would explain why the place is completely vacated.\n我们已经身在城堡的主厅里了。如果他们想给我们设什么陷阱，早就动手了。他们大概没料到会有人走到这么深。这也能解释为什么这里空无一人。"

    old "Then where are those sounds coming from?"
    new "Then where are those sounds coming from?\n那那些声音是从哪里传来的？"

    old "Quiet, let me listen."
    new "Quiet, let me listen.\n安静，让我听听。"

    old "I close my eyes, trying to better make out the sound. It sounds like the sobbing of a child."
    new "I close my eyes, trying to better make out the sound. It sounds like the sobbing of a child.\n我闭上眼睛，想把那声音听得更清楚。听起来像是一个孩子的啜泣声。"

    old "I hear a child crying."
    new "I hear a child crying.\n我听到一个孩子在哭。"

    old "What? How can that be?"
    new "What? How can that be?\n什么？这怎么可能？"

    old "The vampires may have taken prisoners. An Amazon girl went missing less than two days ago. It would not surprise me if it's her sobs we're now hearing."
    new "The vampires may have taken prisoners. An Amazon girl went missing less than two days ago. It would not surprise me if it's her sobs we're now hearing.\n吸血鬼们可能抓了俘虏。不到两天前，有一个Amazon女孩失踪了。如果我们现在听到的是她的啜泣声，我一点也不惊讶。"

    old "They take children as prisoners? They truly are evil manifest."
    new "They take children as prisoners? They truly are evil manifest.\n他们连孩子都抓来当俘虏？真是邪恶的化身。"

    old "Let's break down that door, then."
    new "Let's break down that door, then.\n那我们就砸开那扇门吧。"

    old "Breaking down the door would make a lot of sound. And if we get caught in this main hall, I think that things will go very badly for us. I see four different doors that potential enemies could come through. We would be very quickly surrounded."
    new "Breaking down the door would make a lot of sound. And if we get caught in this main hall, I think that things will go very badly for us. I see four different doors that potential enemies could come through. We would be very quickly surrounded.\n砸门会弄出很大声响。而如果我们在这主厅里被发现，我想情况会变得非常糟糕。我看到有四扇门，潜在敌人都可能从那里冲进来。我们很快就会被包围。"

    old "We have to do something, though."
    new "We have to do something, though.\n但我们总得做点什么。"

    old "Yes, we should get to the other side of this door. But I'm more interested in finding the key that fits it than trying to muster the force to break it down."
    new "Yes, we should get to the other side of this door. But I'm more interested in finding the key that fits it than trying to muster the force to break it down.\n是啊，我们该到这门后面去。但比起费力气砸开它，我更想找到能打开它的钥匙。"

    old "Let's find that key, then."
    new "Let's find that key, then.\n那我们就去找那把钥匙。"

    old "Unfortunately, I doubt a key to the castle's prison is the sort of thing that they would leave lying around. We should continue with our original course of action: investigate."
    new "Unfortunately, I doubt a key to the castle's prison is the sort of thing that they would leave lying around. We should continue with our original course of action: investigate.\n可惜，我怀疑城堡监狱的钥匙不会是他们随手乱放的东西。我们还是按原计划行事：继续调查。"

    old "Where shall we investigate first?"
    new "Where shall we investigate first?\n我们先调查哪里？"

    old "I eye the four doors I called out earlier."
    new "I eye the four doors I called out earlier.\n我打量着先前提到的那四扇门。"

    old "Let's go to the castle's inner courtyard. We may be able to more easily navigate around the castle from there."
    new "Let's go to the castle's inner courtyard. We may be able to more easily navigate around the castle from there.\n我们去城堡的内院吧。从那里也许能更方便地摸清城堡的布局。"

    old "I'm nervous at the prospect of stepping out into the moonlight again on a night like this...but I can't deny it's a good place to begin a search."
    new "I'm nervous at the prospect of stepping out into the moonlight again on a night like this...but I can't deny it's a good place to begin a search.\n在这样一个夜晚再次走进月光下，让我有些紧张……但我不得不承认，那里是个开始搜索的好地方。"

    old "I see what looks like indications of a spiral staircase. Based on what we saw from the castle's exterior, it should lead us up to the battlements."
    new "I see what looks like indications of a spiral staircase. Based on what we saw from the castle's exterior, it should lead us up to the battlements.\n我看到似乎有螺旋楼梯的迹象。根据我们从城堡外面看到的，它应该能带我们上到城垛。"

    old "The battlements, eh? Well, if nothing else, it should give us a good vantage."
    new "The battlements, eh? Well, if nothing else, it should give us a good vantage.\n城垛，嗯？好吧，就算没别的，也该能给我们一个好视野。"

    old "To the dining hall."
    new "To the dining hall.\n去宴会厅。"

    old "The dining hall? What do you hope to find there?"
    new "The dining hall? What do you hope to find there?\n宴会厅？你想在那里找到什么？"

    old "Places of festivity are often places where things are forgotten. How many people have forgotten a valuable item at a party? If the vampires are as hedonistic as I imagine them to be, a dining hall seems like the sort of place where they might forget something like a key. Or at the very least, something to give us a clue."
    new "Places of festivity are often places where things are forgotten. How many people have forgotten a valuable item at a party? If the vampires are as hedonistic as I imagine them to be, a dining hall seems like the sort of place where they might forget something like a key. Or at the very least, something to give us a clue.\n寻欢作乐的地方，常常是东西被遗忘的地方。有多少人在聚会上落下过贵重物品？如果吸血鬼真如我想象的那般纵情享乐，宴会厅就正是他们可能落下钥匙之类东西的地方。至少，也会留下点线索。"

    old "I shudder to think of what a 'dining hall' looks like for vampires..."
    new "I shudder to think of what a 'dining hall' looks like for vampires...\n一想到吸血鬼的“宴会厅”是什么样子，我就不寒而栗……"

    old "Relax. It's a full moon. If there are any vampires feeding, they're doing it outside."
    new "Relax. It's a full moon. If there are any vampires feeding, they're doing it outside.\n放轻松。今晚是满月。如果真有吸血鬼在进食，他们也会在外面。"

    old "Down this corridor, to the library. That's where I'd keep secrets if I had them."
    new "Down this corridor, to the library. That's where I'd keep secrets if I had them.\n沿着这条走廊，去图书馆。要是换了我有秘密，就会藏在那里。"

    old "The library. An excellent place to gather intelligence."
    new "The library. An excellent place to gather intelligence.\n图书馆。搜集情报的好地方。"

    old "We rush back to the main hall, key in hand. To my relief, the key fits the door that the crying we heard was coming from."
    new "We rush back to the main hall, key in hand. To my relief, the key fits the door that the crying we heard was coming from.\n我们手握钥匙，匆匆赶回主厅。让我松了口气的是，这把钥匙正好能打开那扇传来哭声的门。"

    old "We step into the dungeon."
    new "We step into the dungeon.\n我们走进地牢。"

    old "Hush, all of you. We're rescuing you, but you need to stay quiet."
    new "Hush, all of you. We're rescuing you, but you need to stay quiet.\n嘘，你们所有人。我们是来救你们的，但你们得保持安静。"

    old "We step into the prison. Just as Karen described, there are four adult Amazons, with a child among them, wrapped in the arms of a woman who I can only presume is her mother."
    new "We step into the prison. Just as Karen described, there are four adult Amazons, with a child among them, wrapped in the arms of a woman who I can only presume is her mother.\n我们走进牢房。正如Karen所说，那里有四个成年Amazon，其中还有一个孩子，被一个女人搂在怀里，我只能猜想那是她的母亲。"

    old "As I unlock the cell, the Amazons step through, each whispering 'thank you' in turn. The girl is the last to leave the cell, led by her mother."
    new "As I unlock the cell, the Amazons step through, each whispering 'thank you' in turn. The girl is the last to leave the cell, led by her mother.\n我打开牢门后，Amazon们依次走出来，每个人都低声说了句“谢谢”。那个女孩最后一个离开牢房，由她的母亲牵着。"

    old "Hello, little one. What's your name?"
    new "Hello, little one. What's your name?\n你好，小家伙。你叫什么名字？"

    old "I'm Breza. Thank you for rescuing us."
    new "I'm Breza. Thank you for rescuing us.\n我叫Breza。谢谢你救了我们。"

    old "The young girl stands in front of me. To my surprise, I see not fear in her eyes, but a look of determination. If she was crying earlier, she seems more angry than scared now."
    new "The young girl stands in front of me. To my surprise, I see not fear in her eyes, but a look of determination. If she was crying earlier, she seems more angry than scared now.\n这个小女孩站在我面前。让我惊讶的是，我在她眼里看到的不是恐惧，而是坚定的神情。如果说她先前哭过，那么现在她更像是愤怒多过害怕。"

    old "I'm okay, but the vampires need to pay for what they did to us. They denied us everything. No food, no water."
    new "I'm okay, but the vampires need to pay for what they did to us. They denied us everything. No food, no water.\n我没事，但吸血鬼们必须为他们对我们做的事付出代价。他们什么都不给我们，没有食物，没有水。"

    old "They were going to let you starve?"
    new "They were going to let you starve?\n他们打算让你们活活饿死？"

    old "They offered us blood instead of food or water. They're disgusting."
    new "They offered us blood instead of food or water. They're disgusting.\n他们不给食物和水，反倒给我们血喝。真恶心。"

    old "Now, we make them pay for what they did to us."
    new "Now, we make them pay for what they did to us.\n现在，我们要让他们为对我们做的事付出代价。"

    old "Hush, child. Now is not the time."
    new "Hush, child. Now is not the time.\n嘘，孩子。现在还不是时候。"

    old "Now is exactly the time to take the fight to the vampires. We're here, aren't we? And you have weapons."
    new "Now is exactly the time to take the fight to the vampires. We're here, aren't we? And you have weapons.\n现在正是把战斗带到吸血鬼面前的时候。我们不是到了这里吗？而且你们有武器。"

    old "I'm afraid that you all are in no condition to fight. Battling vampires is hard enough in good health, and harder still when you haven't had anything to eat or drink in several days. You'd best leave now and try to avoid notice."
    new "I'm afraid that you all are in no condition to fight. Battling vampires is hard enough in good health, and harder still when you haven't had anything to eat or drink in several days. You'd best leave now and try to avoid notice.\n恐怕你们现在的状态不适合战斗。身体健康时与吸血鬼搏斗已经够难了，几天没吃没喝就更难了。你们最好现在就离开，尽量避免被人发现。"

    old "But you can fight, right? That's why you came here."
    new "But you can fight, right? That's why you came here.\n但你们能战斗，对吧？你们就是为此而来的。"

    old "We came here with two objectives. To rescue you, which you can thank Karen for. And to gather intel, on behalf of Grimoire."
    new "We came here with two objectives. To rescue you, which you can thank Karen for. And to gather intel, on behalf of Grimoire.\n我们来这里有两个目的。一是救你们，这你们可以感谢Karen；二是代表Grimoire搜集情报。"

    old "You were sent here by Grimoire? Of the human empire?"
    new "You were sent here by Grimoire? Of the human empire?\n你们是被Grimoire派来的？人类帝国的Grimoire？"

    old "I overheard the vampires talking. They plan to attack Grimoire. They know it's the Empire headquarters, probably they want to create chaos."
    new "I overheard the vampires talking. They plan to attack Grimoire. They know it's the Empire headquarters, probably they want to create chaos.\n我无意中听到了吸血鬼们的谈话。他们计划攻打Grimoire。他们知道那里是帝国总部，大概是想要制造混乱。"

    old "They're invading now?"
    new "They're invading now?\n他们现在就要入侵了吗？"

    old "No, not now, but they made it sound soon. One of them, one with particularly cruel-looking claws, expressed he was upset that the invasion had to be delayed until the next full moon. Apparently the corruption has not been spreading as quickly as they hoped."
    new "No, not now, but they made it sound soon. One of them, one with particularly cruel-looking claws, expressed he was upset that the invasion had to be delayed until the next full moon. Apparently the corruption has not been spreading as quickly as they hoped.\n不，不是现在，但听他们的意思，很快了。其中一个爪子看起来格外残忍的家伙表示，他很恼火入侵不得不推迟到下个满月。显然，腐化蔓延的速度没有他们希望的那么快。"

    old "This is...very serious. We should bring you to Grimoire so that the council can be briefed on what you heard."
    new "This is...very serious. We should bring you to Grimoire so that the council can be briefed on what you heard.\n这……非常严重。我们该把你们带回Grimoire，好让议会听取你们所听到的情况。"

    old "We'll go to Grimoire gladly, then. Anywhere is better than being trapped in this castle."
    new "We'll go to Grimoire gladly, then. Anywhere is better than being trapped in this castle.\n那我们很乐意去Grimoire。总比被困在这座城堡里强。"

    old "It seems that we got the information that we came for. However, we did leave some areas of the castle unexplored."
    new "It seems that we got the information that we came for. However, we did leave some areas of the castle unexplored.\n看来我们拿到了想要的情报。不过，城堡里还有一些区域我们没有探索。"

    old "You all should leave now."
    new "You all should leave now.\n你们现在都该离开了。"

    old "But you're staying, right?"
    new "But you're staying, right?\n但你们要留下，对吧？"

    old "You and your friends. While we escape, you and your friends will stay at the castle and continue to fight the vampires. Right?"
    new "You and your friends. While we escape, you and your friends will stay at the castle and continue to fight the vampires. Right?\n你和你的朋友们。在我们逃走的时候，你和你的朋友们会留在城堡里，继续和吸血鬼战斗。对吗？"

    old "We've already achieved all of our objectives here in the castle. However, we still seem to be here, undetected, and inside the castle at a moment when the vampires are at their most vulnerable. We may not have another opportunity like this again."
    new "We've already achieved all of our objectives here in the castle. However, we still seem to be here, undetected, and inside the castle at a moment when the vampires are at their most vulnerable. We may not have another opportunity like this again.\n我们在城堡里的所有目标都已经达成了。然而，我们此刻仍然没被发现，而且正处于吸血鬼最脆弱的时刻、身处城堡内部。这样的机会，我们可能不会再有第二次。"

    old "We could leave with the prisoners and the information that they obtained...but we could stay around, and perhaps try to deal a crippling blow to the vampires when they least suspect it."
    new "We could leave with the prisoners and the information that they obtained...but we could stay around, and perhaps try to deal a crippling blow to the vampires when they least suspect it.\n我们可以带着俘虏和他们得到的情报离开……但也可以留下来，也许趁吸血鬼最不防备的时候，给他们以致命一击。"

    old "If we do stay, we may face powerful enemies, similar in caliber to the one that we recovered the key from."
    new "If we do stay, we may face powerful enemies, similar in caliber to the one that we recovered the key from.\n如果我们留下，可能要面对强大的敌人，实力与我们取回钥匙时对付的那个不相上下。"

    old "We got what we came for. Let's be content with that."
    new "We got what we came for. Let's be content with that.\n我们拿到了想要的东西。就满足于此吧。"

    old "We group up with the prisoners and make our way back to Grimoire without incident."
    new "We group up with the prisoners and make our way back to Grimoire without incident.\n我们和俘虏们会合，一路平安无事地返回Grimoire。"

    old "We're going to stay and continue to explore the castle. But you are in no condition to fight."
    new "We're going to stay and continue to explore the castle. But you are in no condition to fight.\n我们要留下来继续探索城堡。但你们现在没有战斗的条件。"

    old "I think we can find our way to Grimoire from here. They left our weapons in that bin in the corner. We may not have much strength, but we still have enough fight in us to beat any ghouls that stand between us and the city."
    new "I think we can find our way to Grimoire from here. They left our weapons in that bin in the corner. We may not have much strength, but we still have enough fight in us to beat any ghouls that stand between us and the city.\n我想我们能从这里找到去Grimoire的路。他们把我们的武器留在了角落里那个箱子里。我们也许没多少力气，但体内的斗志还足够击败任何挡在我们和城市之间的食尸鬼。"

    old "Then make your exit. I wish you safe travels."
    new "Then make your exit. I wish you safe travels.\n那就动身吧。祝你们一路平安。"

    old "The Amazons leave the castle, looking strong in spirit, if a bit weary for their time in the castle's prison. I turn my attention back to the hall."
    new "The Amazons leave the castle, looking strong in spirit, if a bit weary for their time in the castle's prison. I turn my attention back to the hall.\nAmazon们离开了城堡，虽然因在城堡监狱里待了些时日而略显疲惫，但精神依然抖擞。我把注意力转回大厅。"

    old "We arrive in Grimoire. The Amazon prisoners are escorted to the council chambers to provide testimony."
    new "We arrive in Grimoire. The Amazon prisoners are escorted to the council chambers to provide testimony.\n我们抵达Grimoire。Amazon俘虏们被护送到议会厅去作证。"

    old "We arrive in Grimoire. It seems the Amazon prisoners have already made their way to the council chambers, I presume to provide testimony about what they saw."
    new "We arrive in Grimoire. It seems the Amazon prisoners have already made their way to the council chambers, I presume to provide testimony about what they saw.\n我们抵达Grimoire。看来Amazon俘虏们已经自己前往议会厅了，我猜想是去就他们所见作证。"

    old "[protag], it is such a relief to see you."
    new "[protag], it is such a relief to see you.\n[protag]，见到你真是让我松了一口气。"

    old "I assure you that your relief at seeing me is far exceeded by my relief at being out of that castle."
    new "I assure you that your relief at seeing me is far exceeded by my relief at being out of that castle.\n我向你保证，你见到我的宽慰，远比不上我离开那座城堡后的宽慰。"

    old "Quite true. We've been tense waiting for you, but you were the one who actually had to step into the fray and do the work. And it seems that your efforts have been rewarded. I don't think we could have hoped for a better outcome."
    new "Quite true. We've been tense waiting for you, but you were the one who actually had to step into the fray and do the work. And it seems that your efforts have been rewarded. I don't think we could have hoped for a better outcome.\n千真万确。我们等你的这段时间一直提心吊胆，但真正要踏入险境、动手做事的人是你。看来你的努力得到了回报。我想，我们再也想不出比这更好的结果了。"

    old "The way you say you're relieved makes it sound like you were worrying about me. You shouldn't worry, not when you leave someone like me in charge."
    new "The way you say you're relieved makes it sound like you were worrying about me. You shouldn't worry, not when you leave someone like me in charge.\n你说你松了口气，听那口气就好像你在为我担心。你不必担心，尤其当你把重任交给像我这样的人时。"

    old "You're quite cocksure, [protag]. Ordinarily, I'd caution against being overconfident, but given the success of your mission, I'd say you've earned the right to boast."
    new "You're quite cocksure, [protag]. Ordinarily, I'd caution against being overconfident, but given the success of your mission, I'd say you've earned the right to boast.\n你倒是自信得很，[protag]。通常我会劝人别太自负，但鉴于你任务的成功，我得说你已经赢得了夸耀的资格。"

    old "We managed to gather some information that I think will prove to be most valuable."
    new "We managed to gather some information that I think will prove to be most valuable.\n我们设法搜集到了一些情报，我想这些情报会证明价值非凡。"

    old "Indeed. [protag], you probably are already aware of this, but prior to your mission, the council's support was far from unanimous. Many of the council members doubted that your mission would turn up anything of interest."
    new "Indeed. [protag], you probably are already aware of this, but prior to your mission, the council's support was far from unanimous. Many of the council members doubted that your mission would turn up anything of interest.\n确实。[protag]，你大概已经知道了，但在你执行任务之前，议会的支持远非一致。许多议员怀疑，你的任务不会查出任何有价值的东西。"

    old "I didn't realize."
    new "I didn't realize.\n这我倒没意识到。"

    old "I wouldn't take their doubts personally. It's just politics as usual. However, if it is true that the vampires are on the verge of invading the city, I think that the information you've gathered will prove to be quite the unifying force."
    new "I wouldn't take their doubts personally. It's just politics as usual. However, if it is true that the vampires are on the verge of invading the city, I think that the information you've gathered will prove to be quite the unifying force.\n我不会把他们的怀疑当成针对你个人。那不过是寻常的政治罢了。不过，如果吸血鬼确实濒临入侵城市，我想你搜集到的情报将会成为一股相当有力的凝聚力量。"

    old "Hopefully the testimony of the prisoners should erase any doubts."
    new "Hopefully the testimony of the prisoners should erase any doubts.\n希望俘虏们的证词能消除任何疑虑。"

    old "I'm just glad that we were able to rescue the captives being held in the castle."
    new "I'm just glad that we were able to rescue the captives being held in the castle.\n我只是很高兴我们能救出被关在城堡里的俘虏。"

    old "Indeed, indeed. With a child among them, as well. For a girl of her age to experience captivity at the hands of vampires, and spend days trapped, unsure of whether help would ever come...it is difficult to think about. You're a hero to that girl, [protag]."
    new "Indeed, indeed. With a child among them, as well. For a girl of her age to experience captivity at the hands of vampires, and spend days trapped, unsure of whether help would ever come...it is difficult to think about. You're a hero to that girl, [protag].\n确实，确实。其中还有个孩子。像她这个年纪的女孩，却要经历被吸血鬼囚禁，被困数日，不知救援是否会到来……想想都令人难受。对那个女孩来说，你就是英雄，[protag]。"

    old "However, it seems the council has taken far more interest in the information that your mission turned up. There's quite a bit to process."
    new "However, it seems the council has taken far more interest in the information that your mission turned up. There's quite a bit to process.\n不过，议会似乎对你任务查出的情报产生了浓厚得多的兴趣。需要处理的内容相当多。"

    old "I was surprised to see the Amazon prisoners taken in for questioning so immediately. Shouldn't someone be looking after their health? From what I hear, they haven't had food or water in several days."
    new "I was surprised to see the Amazon prisoners taken in for questioning so immediately. Shouldn't someone be looking after their health? From what I hear, they haven't had food or water in several days.\n看到Amazon俘虏们这么快就被带去问话，我很惊讶。难道不该有人先照顾一下他们的身体吗？据我所知，他们已经好几天没吃没喝了。"

    old "The council is at least aware that healthy subjects provide more accurate testimony. They'll be taken care of, [protag]. Even if they're only being supplied with food and water for the cynical reason that they can provide information."
    new "The council is at least aware that healthy subjects provide more accurate testimony. They'll be taken care of, [protag]. Even if they're only being supplied with food and water for the cynical reason that they can provide information.\n议会至少明白，健康的证人能提供更准确的证词。会有人照顾他们的，[protag]。即便给他们食物和水，只是出于他们能提供情报这种功利的理由。"

    old "We should be joining the session shortly."
    new "We should be joining the session shortly.\n我们很快就要参加会议了。"

    old "I follow Apolimesho into the council chamber. I stand before the council, and a long line of questioning follows as I report on what I saw in the castle."
    new "I follow Apolimesho into the council chamber. I stand before the council, and a long line of questioning follows as I report on what I saw in the castle.\n我跟着Apolimesho走进议会厅。我站在议会面前，在我汇报城堡中所见时，一连串冗长的提问接踵而至。"

    old "For several moments during the questioning, my thoughts turn to my conversation with Karen and her desire to keep the information about the captured prisoners from the council."
    new "For several moments during the questioning, my thoughts turn to my conversation with Karen and her desire to keep the information about the captured prisoners from the council.\n在问话的间隙，有好几次我的思绪飘回了与Karen的谈话，以及她想把被俘囚犯的消息瞒着议会的心愿。"

    old "However, the council never questions me about how the prisoners came to be trapped in the castle, or whether I had any knowledge about them prior to setting foot in the castle."
    new "However, the council never questions me about how the prisoners came to be trapped in the castle, or whether I had any knowledge about them prior to setting foot in the castle.\n然而，议会始终没有问我，囚犯们是如何被困在城堡里的，也没有问我踏进城堡之前是否对她们有所了解。"

    old "The questioning continues for almost an hour before Apolimesho intercedes on my behalf."
    new "The questioning continues for almost an hour before Apolimesho intercedes on my behalf.\n问话持续了将近一个小时，Apolimesho才出面替我解围。"

    old "Gentlemen and ladies of the council, I believe we have heard enough of [protag]'s testimony to at least corroborate what we heard from the Amazon prisoners."
    new "Gentlemen and ladies of the council, I believe we have heard enough of [protag]'s testimony to at least corroborate what we heard from the Amazon prisoners.\n各位议员先生和女士，我相信，[protag]的证词我们已经听得足够多了，至少足以印证我们从Amazon俘虏那里听到的内容。"

    old "I know that any information that we can glean about the castle's interior and the behavior of the vampires will prove valuable, but it is late, and I believe everyone in this chamber requires rest. "
    new "I know that any information that we can glean about the castle's interior and the behavior of the vampires will prove valuable, but it is late, and I believe everyone in this chamber requires rest. \n我知道，任何关于城堡内部和吸血鬼行径的情报都会很有价值，但时候不早了，我相信这间厅里的每个人都需要休息。"

    old "Will it do to resume questioning at a later date?"
    new "Will it do to resume questioning at a later date?\n改日再继续问话，可以吗？"

    old "No objections."
    new "No objections.\n没有异议。"

    old "No objections here. I could use some sleep."
    new "No objections here. I could use some sleep.\n我这里没有异议。我是该睡上一觉了。"

    old "Indeed, we are only a few hours from sunrise."
    new "Indeed, we are only a few hours from sunrise.\n确实，离日出只剩几个小时了。"

    old "The council's presiding officer adjourns the meeting, and Apolimesho escorts me from the council chambers. We walk outside, where we find Karen, standing with several of the Amazons I rescued. Karen notices me and takes me aside."
    new "The council's presiding officer adjourns the meeting, and Apolimesho escorts me from the council chambers. We walk outside, where we find Karen, standing with several of the Amazons I rescued. Karen notices me and takes me aside.\n议会的主持官宣布休会，Apolimesho护送我离开议会厅。我们走到外面，在那里遇到了Karen，她正和我救出的几个Amazon站在一起。Karen注意到我，把我拉到一旁。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. I owe you many thanks for rescuing my people."
    new "Ah, [protag]. I owe you many thanks for rescuing my people.\n啊，[protag]。你救了我的子民，我欠你许多感谢。"

    old "They were able to provide useful information, so it seems that the rescue was to our mutual benefit."
    new "They were able to provide useful information, so it seems that the rescue was to our mutual benefit.\n她们提供了有用的情报，所以看来这次营救对我们双方都有好处。"

    old "I wish that my people could be a bit more effusive with their thanks to you. Amazons are usually not in the position of being rescued, particularly by a [prace]. I hope you take no offense if their gratitude isn't as forthcoming as you surely deserve."
    new "I wish that my people could be a bit more effusive with their thanks to you. Amazons are usually not in the position of being rescued, particularly by a [prace]. I hope you take no offense if their gratitude isn't as forthcoming as you surely deserve.\n我希望我的子民能更热情地向你道谢。Amazon通常不会落到被人搭救的境地，尤其是被一个[prace]搭救。如果她们的感激没有你应得的那般爽快，还望你不要见怪。"

    old "They have been through quite a lot, Karen. Seeing them led to safety is thanks enough."
    new "They have been through quite a lot, Karen. Seeing them led to safety is thanks enough.\n她们经历了太多，Karen。看到她们被带到安全的地方，就已经是最好的感谢了。"

    old "That is a nice sentiment, but words are cheap. You deserve a reward for the work you've done. Come to the citadel when you have the opportunity, and I'll be sure to thank you properly."
    new "That is a nice sentiment, but words are cheap. You deserve a reward for the work you've done. Come to the citadel when you have the opportunity, and I'll be sure to thank you properly.\n这份心意很好，但话毕竟不值钱。你做的这些事，理应得到奖赏。有机会时来Citadel一趟，我一定会好好答谢你。"

    old "By the way, in the council's questioning of me, the topic of the Amazon prisoners and how they came to be trapped in the castle never came up. Did you tell them anything?"
    new "By the way, in the council's questioning of me, the topic of the Amazon prisoners and how they came to be trapped in the castle never came up. Did you tell them anything?\n顺便问一句，议会盘问我的时候，Amazon俘虏以及她们如何被困在城堡里的话题始终没有提及。你有跟他们说过什么吗？"

    old "I did not have occasion to provide them with that sort of information, and if they are not interested in prying into it, I am not inclined to provide answers to questions that they didn't ask. You can choose to divulge the information if you choose, or keep it to yourself. I would not try to bind you to secrecy about something like that."
    new "I did not have occasion to provide them with that sort of information, and if they are not interested in prying into it, I am not inclined to provide answers to questions that they didn't ask. You can choose to divulge the information if you choose, or keep it to yourself. I would not try to bind you to secrecy about something like that.\n我没有机会向他们提供那类信息，而如果他们无意深究，我也不愿去回答他们没问过的问题。你可以选择透露这消息，也可以选择藏在心里。我不会因为这种事硬要你守口如瓶。"

    old "Karen turns to leave, and I return to the council steps to part ways with Apolimesho as we watch the Amazons leave."
    new "Karen turns to leave, and I return to the council steps to part ways with Apolimesho as we watch the Amazons leave.\nKaren转身离开，我回到议会台阶上，与Apolimesho道别，一起目送Amazon们离去。"

    old "I'm sure that the rescued prisoners are glad to be living the city with their queen. I don't think they could ask for a more prestigious escort."
    new "I'm sure that the rescued prisoners are glad to be living the city with their queen. I don't think they could ask for a more prestigious escort.\n我相信获救的俘虏们很高兴能和她们的女王一起离开这座城市。我想她们再也找不到比她更尊贵的护卫了。"

    old "To be honest, I'm a bit surprised that Karen came out to escort them back herself. Even more puzzling was the fact that she arrived in Grimoire prior to the prisoners being returned. I wonder if she had some ulterior motive in coming to Grimoire."
    new "To be honest, I'm a bit surprised that Karen came out to escort them back herself. Even more puzzling was the fact that she arrived in Grimoire prior to the prisoners being returned. I wonder if she had some ulterior motive in coming to Grimoire.\n老实说，我有点惊讶Karen会亲自出来护送她们回去。更令人费解的是，她竟在俘虏们被送回之前就抵达了Grimoire。我怀疑她来Grimoire是否另有隐情。"

    old "Would you happen to know anything about this, [protag]?"
    new "Would you happen to know anything about this, [protag]?\n这件事你碰巧知道些什么吗，[protag]？"

    old "If you want to know why Karen came to Grimoire, you'll have to ask her yourself."
    new "If you want to know why Karen came to Grimoire, you'll have to ask her yourself.\n如果你想知道Karen为什么来Grimoire，就得亲自去问她。"

    old "I suppose so. Well, good night, [protag]. Take the opportunity to rest, please."
    new "I suppose so. Well, good night, [protag]. Take the opportunity to rest, please.\n我想也是。那好，晚安，[protag]。请趁机好好休息。"

    old "Karen knew that there were Amazon prisoners being held in castle N'Mar."
    new "Karen knew that there were Amazon prisoners being held in castle N'Mar.\nKaren知道有Amazon俘虏被关押在N'Mar城堡里。"

    old "In fact, she told me about them shortly after I left Grimoire."
    new "In fact, she told me about them shortly after I left Grimoire.\n事实上，她是在我离开Grimoire后不久告诉我的。"

    old "Why did she not come to the council with this information?"
    new "Why did she not come to the council with this information?\n她为什么不带着这个情报去找议会？"

    old "As I told you, she intercepted me after I had left Grimoire and was on my way to N'Mar. She had to come directly to me. If she had gone to the council, the message wouldn't have made it to me before I made it to the castle."
    new "As I told you, she intercepted me after I had left Grimoire and was on my way to N'Mar. She had to come directly to me. If she had gone to the council, the message wouldn't have made it to me before I made it to the castle.\n正如我跟你说过的，她是在我离开Grimoire、前往N'Mar的途中拦住我的。她必须直接来找我。如果她去的是议会，那么在我抵达城堡之前，这消息根本到不了我手上。"

    old "That doesn't explain why she didn't tell the council after delivering the message to you, however."
    new "That doesn't explain why she didn't tell the council after delivering the message to you, however.\n然而，这并不能解释为什么她把消息带给你之后，也没去告诉议会。"

    old "To be honest, I am not surprised that Karen was intentionally withholding information from the council. She doesn't fully trust them. But actions like this make it difficult for the council to trust her."
    new "To be honest, I am not surprised that Karen was intentionally withholding information from the council. She doesn't fully trust them. But actions like this make it difficult for the council to trust her.\n老实说，Karen故意向议会隐瞒情报，我并不惊讶。她并不完全信任他们。但这样的举动，也会让议会难以信任她。"

    old "She was afraid that the council would begin meddling with the mission if they were presented with more information."
    new "She was afraid that the council would begin meddling with the mission if they were presented with more information.\n她担心，如果议会得到更多信息，就会开始插手干预任务。"

    old "Is that so? Well, I can hardly blame her. One of the reasons we vested you with so much autonomy was to avoid the council micro-managing every one of your decisions. Having the council try to plan and execute the rescue would have been a disaster."
    new "Is that so? Well, I can hardly blame her. One of the reasons we vested you with so much autonomy was to avoid the council micro-managing every one of your decisions. Having the council try to plan and execute the rescue would have been a disaster.\n是这样吗？好吧，我几乎没法怪她。我们之所以赋予你这么大的自主权，其中一个原因就是避免议会对你每一个决定都事无巨细地管束。要是让议会来筹划并执行这次营救，那会是一场灾难。"

    old "And knowing the council, there's a good chance that a number of them would have voted to cancel the mission if they knew that you would be distracted by the task of rescuing the prisoners."
    new "And knowing the council, there's a good chance that a number of them would have voted to cancel the mission if they knew that you would be distracted by the task of rescuing the prisoners.\n而且以我对议会的了解，如果他们知道你会被营救俘虏的任务分心，他们中有不少人很可能就会投票取消任务。"

    old "I wish Karen were a bit more forthright, but perhaps it's for the best that she went to you with the information directly. [protag], you proved tonight that you know how to act on your own while still keeping the council's interest in mind."
    new "I wish Karen were a bit more forthright, but perhaps it's for the best that she went to you with the information directly. [protag], you proved tonight that you know how to act on your own while still keeping the council's interest in mind.\n我倒希望Karen能更坦率些，但也许她直接把情报交给你，才是最好的做法。[protag]，你今晚证明了，你既懂得独自行动，又时刻把议会的利益放在心上。"

    old "But I'm glad that you decided to tell me about it afterward. I believe that you did the right thing, both by going ahead with the rescue without informing the council ahead of time, and by telling me afterward. To be honest, I myself am torn about whether to present this bit of information to the council."
    new "But I'm glad that you decided to tell me about it afterward. I believe that you did the right thing, both by going ahead with the rescue without informing the council ahead of time, and by telling me afterward. To be honest, I myself am torn about whether to present this bit of information to the council.\n不过我很高兴你事后决定把这件事告诉我。我相信你做得对，既在没有事先告知议会的情况下继续营救，又能在事后告诉我。老实说，我自己也拿不定主意，要不要把这条信息呈报给议会。"

    old "But that is for me to worry about. Right now, you need only concern yourself with getting sleep. You've earned it."
    new "But that is for me to worry about. Right now, you need only concern yourself with getting sleep. You've earned it.\n但那是我该操心的事。现在，你只需要专心去睡觉。这是你应得的。"

    old "I took the liberty of reserving a room for you at the travelers inn just outside the city perimeter. It's away from the heart of the city, and I thought you might want a place to sleep in without worry of being woken up in the early morning by the hustle and bustle of the city."
    new "I took the liberty of reserving a room for you at the travelers inn just outside the city perimeter. It's away from the heart of the city, and I thought you might want a place to sleep in without worry of being woken up in the early morning by the hustle and bustle of the city.\n我自作主张，在城外不远处的旅行者客栈为你订了间房。那里远离市中心，我想你也许想要一个能安心睡觉的地方，不用大清早被城市的喧闹吵醒。"

    old "Thank you, Apolimesho. After the events of tonight, I think a long sleep is exactly what I need."
    new "Thank you, Apolimesho. After the events of tonight, I think a long sleep is exactly what I need.\n谢谢你，Apolimesho。经历了今晚这些事，我想我正需要好好睡上一大觉。"

    old "Before going to sleep, I decide to talk with every party member who came with me on the mission."
    new "Before going to sleep, I decide to talk with every party member who came with me on the mission.\n睡觉之前，我决定和随我一同执行任务的每位队友都聊一聊。"

    old "Hey [protag], thanks for bringing me with you. It was fun."
    new "Hey [protag], thanks for bringing me with you. It was fun.\n嘿，[protag]，谢谢你带上我。很有意思。"

    old "You're welcome? Heh. If that's what you consider 'fun', I forsee us having a lot more fun together in the future."
    new "You're welcome? Heh. If that's what you consider 'fun', I forsee us having a lot more fun together in the future.\n不客气？呵。如果这就是你所谓的“有意思”，那我预感到我们将来还会有更多乐子。"

    old "Good night for now, [protag]. I'm going to go ahead and head back to the swamp."
    new "Good night for now, [protag]. I'm going to go ahead and head back to the swamp.\n那就先道晚安了，[protag]。我先回沼泽去了。"

    old "You not staying at the inn? It's okay, you know. People know who we are now so nobody is going to think twice about it."
    new "You not staying at the inn? It's okay, you know. People know who we are now so nobody is going to think twice about it.\n你不住客栈吗？没关系的，你知道的。现在大家都知道我们是谁了，没人会多想。"

    old "Truly? Hmm. Well, I've never tried sleeping in a normal bed before..."
    new "Truly? Hmm. Well, I've never tried sleeping in a normal bed before...\n真的吗？嗯。好吧，我还从没试过睡在普通的床上……"

    old "Then come! After that boring N'Mar infiltration mission, you deserve the exciting adventure of sleeping in a normal bed!"
    new "Then come! After that boring N'Mar infiltration mission, you deserve the exciting adventure of sleeping in a normal bed!\n那就来吧！经历了那趟无聊的N'Mar潜入任务，你值得享受一次睡普通床的刺激冒险！"

    old "Haha. I will give it a try then. Thanks, [protag]."
    new "Haha. I will give it a try then. Thanks, [protag].\n哈哈。那我就试试看。谢谢你，[protag]。"

    old "Leena? I thought you followed Karen back to the Citadel."
    new "Leena? I thought you followed Karen back to the Citadel.\nLeena？我还以为你跟着Karen回Citadel去了。"

    old "Queen Karen and the others were kind enough to wait up for me. I wanted to see you before I left to... Well, I just wanted to thank you."
    new "Queen Karen and the others were kind enough to wait up for me. I wanted to see you before I left to... Well, I just wanted to thank you.\nKaren女王和其他人好心留下来等我。我想在离开前见你一面，好……嗯，我只是想谢谢你。"

    old "Thank me? For what?"
    new "Thank me? For what?\n谢我？谢什么？"

    old "For picking me for the mission. It seems like I've earned your trust."
    new "For picking me for the mission. It seems like I've earned your trust.\n谢谢你选我参加任务。看来我赢得了你的信任。"

    old "Indeed you have. You've been very useful, Leena."
    new "Indeed you have. You've been very useful, Leena.\n你确实赢得了。你帮了很大的忙，Leena。"

    old "I'd better get going now. Anyway, be sure to come visit me at the Citadel sometime."
    new "I'd better get going now. Anyway, be sure to come visit me at the Citadel sometime.\n我现在得走了。总之，有空一定要来Citadel看看我。"

    old "Hey Jasper, you look happy. It feels good to be home, eh?"
    new "Hey Jasper, you look happy. It feels good to be home, eh?\n嘿，Jasper，你看起来很开心。回到家的感觉不错吧？"

    old "Yes, especially after a successful mission like this one!"
    new "Yes, especially after a successful mission like this one!\n是啊，尤其是经历了这样一次成功的任务之后！"

    old "[protag]! My heart is still beating from all of the excitement."
    new "[protag]! My heart is still beating from all of the excitement.\n[protag]！我的心还在因为激动怦怦直跳。"

    old "Nuala grabs my hand and places it on her chest."
    new "Nuala grabs my hand and places it on her chest.\nNuala抓住我的手，放到她的胸口上。"

    old "You hear it? My heart?"
    new "You hear it? My heart?\n你听到了吗？我的心跳？"

    old "Ehm, yes I hear it very clearly. Are you heading back to the desert now?"
    new "Ehm, yes I hear it very clearly. Are you heading back to the desert now?\n呃，是的，我听得很清楚。你现在要回沙漠去了吗？"

    old "Yes, but don't worry. I'll take the safest routes, away from the fog."
    new "Yes, but don't worry. I'll take the safest routes, away from the fog.\n是的，不过别担心。我会走最安全的路，远离那片雾。"

    old "We killed a few undead, didn't we?"
    new "We killed a few undead, didn't we?\n我们杀了好几个不死生物，对吧？"

    old "Indeed we did! It was great to have you on my team, Larik."
    new "Indeed we did! It was great to have you on my team, Larik.\n确实！能把你招进我的队伍，真是太好了，Larik。"

    old "It was my pleasure. Take care, [protag]."
    new "It was my pleasure. Take care, [protag].\n这是我的荣幸。保重，[protag]。"

    old "That place... I could feel the evil surrounding it."
    new "That place... I could feel the evil surrounding it.\n那个地方……我能感觉到它四周环绕的邪恶。"

    old "You could feel it? Like, as a sort of sixth sense or something?"
    new "You could feel it? Like, as a sort of sixth sense or something?\n你能感觉到？就像某种第六感之类的？"

    old "Yes, with my magic. I could almost 'taste' the evil. There's still a lot of work to do to purge it from the castle."
    new "Yes, with my magic. I could almost 'taste' the evil. There's still a lot of work to do to purge it from the castle.\n是的，用我的魔法。我几乎能“尝”到那股邪恶。要想把邪恶从城堡里清除干净，还有很长的路要走。"

    old "I know. Nevertheless, our victory today is a start."
    new "I know. Nevertheless, our victory today is a start.\n我知道。尽管如此，我们今天的胜利已经是个开端。"

    old "Thanks for you help by the way."
    new "Thanks for you help by the way.\n顺便说一句，谢谢你的帮助。"

    old "Thank you for bringing me with you. It was good to feel useful."
    new "Thank you for bringing me with you. It was good to feel useful.\n谢谢你带上我。能感觉自己派上用场，真好。"

    old "That was a well executed plan, [protag]. All that's left now is for us to have a good rest before the next inevitable battle."
    new "That was a well executed plan, [protag]. All that's left now is for us to have a good rest before the next inevitable battle.\n这计划执行得很漂亮，[protag]。现在剩下的，就是在下一场不可避免的战斗来临前好好休息。"

    old "Hey Kusho, are you going back to Grandtree?"
    new "Hey Kusho, are you going back to Grandtree?\n嘿，Kusho，你要回GrandTree去了吗？"

    old "You bet. I can't stay in cities for long before I start missing the trees."
    new "You bet. I can't stay in cities for long before I start missing the trees.\n当然。我在城市里待不长，久了就会想念那些树。"

    old "[protag]! We did great tonight, didn't we?"
    new "[protag]! We did great tonight, didn't we?\n[protag]！我们今晚干得漂亮，对吧？"

    old "We did, Galan, we did. And a good part of that is thanks to your contribution."
    new "We did, Galan, we did. And a good part of that is thanks to your contribution.\n是啊，Galan，是啊。而其中很大一部分功劳，都要归功于你的付出。"

    old "Haha. Anytime."
    new "Haha. Anytime.\n哈哈。随时效劳。"

    old "Dasyra? You look serious. Aren't you happy about our mission's success?"
    new "Dasyra? You look serious. Aren't you happy about our mission's success?\nDasyra？你看上去很严肃。任务成功，你不开心吗？"

    old "Oh, sorry, [protag]. Of course I am happy about that."
    new "Oh, sorry, [protag]. Of course I am happy about that.\n哦，抱歉，[protag]。我当然为那开心。"

    old "But I couldn't stop thinking about those amazon prisoners. That young girl... Breza was her name? I can't begin to imagine all of the horrible things she must have gone through."
    new "But I couldn't stop thinking about those amazon prisoners. That young girl... Breza was her name? I can't begin to imagine all of the horrible things she must have gone through.\n但我一直忍不住想那些Amazon俘虏。那个年轻女孩……她是叫Breza吗？我根本无法想象她一定经历过的那些可怕事情。"

    old "True, but remember how determined she was. As bad as it was, I think she'll use this experience to forge her character. She'll become a tough woman when she grows up."
    new "True, but remember how determined she was. As bad as it was, I think she'll use this experience to forge her character. She'll become a tough woman when she grows up.\n没错，但别忘了她有多么坚定。虽然遭遇很糟，但我想她会利用这段经历来锤炼自己的品格。她长大后会成为一个坚强的女人。"

    old "Yes, I think so too."
    new "Yes, I think so too.\n是的，我也这么想。"

    old "Some time later, I stir awake to the sound of voices beside me."
    new "Some time later, I stir awake to the sound of voices beside me.\n过了些时候，我被身旁的说话声吵醒了。"

    old "Hush, Valery. You'll scare [himher]."
    new "Hush, Valery. You'll scare [himher].\n嘘，Valery。你会把[himher]吓到的。"

    old "I sit up and see two familiar figures standing in my room. I feel my pulse quicken."
    new "I sit up and see two familiar figures standing in my room. I feel my pulse quicken.\n我坐起身，看到两个熟悉的身影站在我的房间里。我感到脉搏加快了。"

    old "Oh good, you're awake."
    new "Oh good, you're awake.\n哦，太好了，你醒了。"

    old "What are you two doing in my room?"
    new "What are you two doing in my room?\n你们两个在我房间里做什么？"

    old "[protag], I hope you'll forgive my lack of manners. I know that waking up to visitors unexpectedly in your room is never a welcome occurrence."
    new "[protag], I hope you'll forgive my lack of manners. I know that waking up to visitors unexpectedly in your room is never a welcome occurrence.\n[protag]，希望你能原谅我的失礼。我知道，醒来时发现房间里有不速之客，从来都不是件让人高兴的事。"

    old "Even when the visitors happen to be such a charming couple?"
    new "Even when the visitors happen to be such a charming couple?\n即便这两位访客恰好是这么有魅力的一对？"

    old "We wanted to talk to you privately, and finding you in your room seemed preferable to trying to trying to catch you elsewhere, since you're so often with others when you're out and about."
    new "We wanted to talk to you privately, and finding you in your room seemed preferable to trying to trying to catch you elsewhere, since you're so often with others when you're out and about.\n我们想私下和你谈谈，而在你的房间里找到你，似乎比去别处堵你更好，毕竟你在外面走动时，总是和别人在一起。"

    old "How did you get into my room?"
    new "How did you get into my room?\n你们是怎么进到我房间里的？"

    old "It was easy to sneak in! You're by the outskirts of town, there's hardly anyone out here!"
    new "It was easy to sneak in! You're by the outskirts of town, there's hardly anyone out here!\n溜进来很容易的！你住在镇子边上，这里几乎没人！"

    old "Indeed. No paved roads, and though there were a few city patrols watching the area, they were easy to get past at night."
    new "Indeed. No paved roads, and though there were a few city patrols watching the area, they were easy to get past at night.\n确实。这里没有铺好的道路，虽然有几支城巡队盯着这一带，但夜里很容易绕过去。"

    old "You put on a good show last night."
    new "You put on a good show last night.\n你昨晚演了一出好戏。"

    old "Last night? Don't you mean tonight?"
    new "Last night? Don't you mean tonight?\n昨晚？你该不是想说今晚吧？"

    old "That was yesterday, [protag]. You slept the entire day away. After what the vampires at N'Mar put you through, I can hardly blame you."
    new "That was yesterday, [protag]. You slept the entire day away. After what the vampires at N'Mar put you through, I can hardly blame you.\n那是昨天的事了，[protag]。你睡了整整一天。经历了N'Mar那些吸血鬼给你带来的磨难，我完全不会怪你。"

    old "If I went to bed just before sunrise, and you two came to wake me up after nightfall, then it seems I really did sleep the day away."
    new "If I went to bed just before sunrise, and you two came to wake me up after nightfall, then it seems I really did sleep the day away.\n如果我在日出前才上床，而你们俩是在天黑后才来叫醒我，那看来我确实睡了一整天。"

    old "Ooh, you're becoming nocturnal! Just like us!"
    new "Ooh, you're becoming nocturnal! Just like us!\n哦，你变得昼伏夜出了！就像我们一样！"

    old "It probably won't become a habit, Valery. Don't get too excited."
    new "It probably won't become a habit, Valery. Don't get too excited.\n这大概不会成为习惯的，Valery。别太兴奋。"

    old "I owe you a personal debt of gratitude, [protag]. That's why I came here. To thank you."
    new "I owe you a personal debt of gratitude, [protag]. That's why I came here. To thank you.\n我欠你一份个人的恩情，[protag]。这就是我来的原因。为了谢谢你。"

    old "Also..."
    new "Also...\n还有……"

    old "Thank you for dealing with our enemies!"
    new "Thank you for dealing with our enemies!\n谢谢你替我们收拾了敌人！"

    old "You know, with skills like yours, you could go on to do great things. Who knows..."
    new "You know, with skills like yours, you could go on to do great things. Who knows...\n你知道，凭你这样的身手，将来一定能成就一番大事。谁知道呢……"

    old "Zachary's voice trails off as he looks away with a wistful expression."
    new "Zachary's voice trails off as he looks away with a wistful expression.\nZachary的声音渐渐低了下去，他带着若有所思的神情望向别处。"

    old "I didn't kill those vampires because I wanted your thanks or approval. I dealt with them because they're enemies of Grimoire."
    new "I didn't kill those vampires because I wanted your thanks or approval. I dealt with them because they're enemies of Grimoire.\n我杀那些吸血鬼，不是想要你的感谢或认可。我收拾他们，是因为他们是Grimoire的敌人。"

    old "Well, in my book, the enemy of my enemy is my friend. It's unfortunate if that friendship is one-sided. For the time being I suppose we'll have to be fine with that, but in the future, I hope we can become something more."
    new "Well, in my book, the enemy of my enemy is my friend. It's unfortunate if that friendship is one-sided. For the time being I suppose we'll have to be fine with that, but in the future, I hope we can become something more.\n好吧，在我看来，敌人的敌人就是朋友。只可惜，这友谊若是单方面的就遗憾了。眼下我想我们只能先这样，但将来，我希望我们能成为更进一步的关系。"

    old "We can become something more!"
    new "We can become something more!\n我们能成为更进一步的关系！"

    old "Anyway. I'm sorry to run off so quickly after saying hello, but Valery and I have important business to attend to. You've created quite a power vacuum, and we're not about to let that opportunity slip away."
    new "Anyway. I'm sorry to run off so quickly after saying hello, but Valery and I have important business to attend to. You've created quite a power vacuum, and we're not about to let that opportunity slip away.\n总之。很抱歉刚打过招呼就要匆匆离开，但我和Valery还有要事去办。你制造了一个相当大的权力真空，我们可不会让这个机会溜走。"

    old "We won't let it slip away!"
    new "We won't let it slip away!\n我们不会让它溜走的！"

    old "Good night, [protag]. Or since you just woke up, perhaps I should say, good morning."
    new "Good night, [protag]. Or since you just woke up, perhaps I should say, good morning.\n晚安，[protag]。不过既然你刚醒，也许我该说，早安。"

    old "Good morning, [protag]! And goodbye!"
    new "Good morning, [protag]! And goodbye!\n早安，[protag]！还有，再见！"

    old "Last night, you dealt with Nootau. I was never very fond of him."
    new "Last night, you dealt with Nootau. I was never very fond of him.\n昨晚，你对付了Nootau。我从来都不怎么喜欢他。"

    old "Not fond of him at all! That Nootau, always so ostentatious! No sense of class! No sense of style."
    new "Not fond of him at all! That Nootau, always so ostentatious! No sense of class! No sense of style.\n一点也不喜欢他！那个Nootau，总是那么爱炫耀！没一点格调！没一点品味。"

    old "That, and he thinks very highly of himself. Very opinionated. He can never consider the possibility that he might be wrong about anything."
    new "That, and he thinks very highly of himself. Very opinionated. He can never consider the possibility that he might be wrong about anything.\n而且他还自视甚高，固执己见。他从不愿考虑自己在任何事上可能出错。"

    old "Is there some kind of internal feud between you two?"
    new "Is there some kind of internal feud between you two?\n你们俩之间是不是有什么内部恩怨？"

    old "He and I got into an argument several decades ago, and that argument never ended. Let's leave it at that."
    new "He and I got into an argument several decades ago, and that argument never ended. Let's leave it at that.\n他和我几十年前有过一场争执，那争执一直没完。就说这么多吧。"

    old "Anyway. With Nootau out of the picture, I took the liberty of helping myself to one of his personal stashes. It seemed only right that I should share the spoils with you."
    new "Anyway. With Nootau out of the picture, I took the liberty of helping myself to one of his personal stashes. It seemed only right that I should share the spoils with you.\n总之。既然Nootau已经不在了，我便自作主张，从他的私藏里取了一份。我想，把战利品分你一份才算公道。"

    old "What kind of spoils are we talking about?"
    new "What kind of spoils are we talking about?\n我们说的是什么战利品？"

    old "Bombs. You can throw them at people, and they cause explosions."
    new "Bombs. You can throw them at people, and they cause explosions.\n炸弹。你可以朝人扔出去，它们会引发爆炸。"

    old "They make things go boom!"
    new "They make things go boom!\n它们能让东西砰地炸开！"

    old "I'm surprised you need to ask, [protag]. I'm sure you saw plenty of these during your encounter with Nootau."
    new "I'm surprised you need to ask, [protag]. I'm sure you saw plenty of these during your encounter with Nootau.\n我很惊讶你还需要问，[protag]。你和Nootau交手时，肯定见过不少这东西。"

    old "Yes. Not the most elegant of weapons, but when you need force, they'll do in a pinch."
    new "Yes. Not the most elegant of weapons, but when you need force, they'll do in a pinch.\n是啊。不是最优雅的武器，但当你需要蛮力时，它们在紧要关头很管用。"

    old "In a pinch."
    new "In a pinch.\n紧要关头很管用。"

    old "Last night, you dealt with Zephyr. I must admit, it warms my heart to see that young ruffian put in his place."
    new "Last night, you dealt with Zephyr. I must admit, it warms my heart to see that young ruffian put in his place.\n昨晚，你对付了Zephyr。我必须承认，看到那个年轻莽汉被好好教训一顿，我心里很痛快。"

    old "Put him in his place!"
    new "Put him in his place!\n好好教训他一顿！"

    old "Zephyr never had the proper respect for his elders, so to see you take him down a notch is something I find quite edifying."
    new "Zephyr never had the proper respect for his elders, so to see you take him down a notch is something I find quite edifying.\nZephyr从来不肯对长辈怀有应有的敬意，所以看到你让他收敛几分，我觉得相当解气。"

    old "When you call him a youngster, how young are we talking?"
    new "When you call him a youngster, how young are we talking?\n你叫他年轻人，那他到底有多年轻？"

    old "When you have lifespans that are measured in centuries, anyone turned in the past hundred years is a whippersnapper. But Zephyr had problems apart from his age. Most young bloods learn their place quickly."
    new "When you have lifespans that are measured in centuries, anyone turned in the past hundred years is a whippersnapper. But Zephyr had problems apart from his age. Most young bloods learn their place quickly.\n当你的寿命以百年计算时，过去一百年里才转化的人都是乳臭未干的小子。但Zephyr的问题不只在年龄。大多数年轻血族很快就会学会自己的本分。"

    old "Zephyr thought himself above the advice of his elders, simply because he happened to be a strong fighter. Well, I'd say you showed him the error of his ways."
    new "Zephyr thought himself above the advice of his elders, simply because he happened to be a strong fighter. Well, I'd say you showed him the error of his ways.\nZephyr自认为高居于长辈的劝告之上，只因为他碰巧是个很强的战士。嗯，我看你已经让他明白了自己的错处。"

    old "Zephyr liked killing, and he made a habit of collecting trophies from his kills. Mostly, he stuck to hunting animals, so it was just a collection of skulls and other bones. But he did also take trophies from a number of travelers who were unfortunate enough to cross through N'Mar while he was out. Personal effects."
    new "Zephyr liked killing, and he made a habit of collecting trophies from his kills. Mostly, he stuck to hunting animals, so it was just a collection of skulls and other bones. But he did also take trophies from a number of travelers who were unfortunate enough to cross through N'Mar while he was out. Personal effects.\nZephyr喜欢杀戮，而且习惯从猎物身上收集战利品。大多数时候他只猎杀动物，所以那只是一堆头骨和其他骨头。但他也确实从一些不幸的旅行者那里取过战利品——那些人在他外出时倒霉地途经N'Mar。都是些随身物品。"

    old "Unfortunate!"
    new "Unfortunate!\n真倒霉！"

    old "Unfortunate to them, but perhaps ultimately fortunate for you. [protag], items of this sort were meant to be worn by mortals, not taken by the undead as trophies."
    new "Unfortunate to them, but perhaps ultimately fortunate for you. [protag], items of this sort were meant to be worn by mortals, not taken by the undead as trophies.\n对他们来说是不幸，但对你来说，最终也许是幸运。[protag]，这类物品本就该由凡人佩戴，而不是被不死生物拿去当战利品。"

    old "I know it might seem in poor taste to wear a ring that was originally looted from a corpse, but it's better off in your hands than Zephyr's. I hope you can wear it proudly."
    new "I know it might seem in poor taste to wear a ring that was originally looted from a corpse, but it's better off in your hands than Zephyr's. I hope you can wear it proudly.\n我知道，戴上一枚原本从尸体上搜刮来的戒指，可能显得不太体面，但它在你手里总比在Zephyr手里强。希望你能骄傲地戴上它。"

    old "Wear it proudly!"
    new "Wear it proudly!\n骄傲地戴上它！"

    old "It seems you gave old Adede the what for. And I have to admit, I was quite pleased to find out."
    new "It seems you gave old Adede the what for. And I have to admit, I was quite pleased to find out.\n看来你给了老Adede一点颜色瞧瞧。而且我必须承认，得知此事我相当高兴。"

    old "Quite pleased to find out!"
    new "Quite pleased to find out!\n得知此事相当高兴！"

    old "That senile old woman would have been better off dying as a mortal. Her undead flesh has persisted longer than her sanity. That woman is creepier than the spiders that act at her beck and call."
    new "That senile old woman would have been better off dying as a mortal. Her undead flesh has persisted longer than her sanity. That woman is creepier than the spiders that act at her beck and call.\n那个老糊涂女人当初还不如以凡人之身死去。她那不死之躯比她残存的理智活得还久。那女人比她呼来唤去的蜘蛛还要瘆人。"

    old "Creepier than a spider!"
    new "Creepier than a spider!\n比蜘蛛还瘆人！"

    old "I'm a bit surprised to hear a vampire describing others as 'creepy.'"
    new "I'm a bit surprised to hear a vampire describing others as 'creepy.'\n听到一个吸血鬼把别人形容成“瘆人”，我有点惊讶。"

    old "[protag], you should know what I'm talking about if you talked with her for more than a few minutes. There's something about that woman that is...not right."
    new "[protag], you should know what I'm talking about if you talked with her for more than a few minutes. There's something about that woman that is...not right.\n[protag]，如果你和她多聊过几分钟，就该明白我在说什么。那个女人身上有某种……不对劲的地方。"

    old "The problem with people like that is that they are always unpredictable. And trying to usurp control of a territory is always difficult when you have wild cards like that in the mix. So, it's quite beneficial for me to see that you were able to take care of her."
    new "The problem with people like that is that they are always unpredictable. And trying to usurp control of a territory is always difficult when you have wild cards like that in the mix. So, it's quite beneficial for me to see that you were able to take care of her.\n这种人问题就在于总是难以捉摸。当你身边混着这样的变数时，想要夺取一片领地的控制权总是困难重重。所以，看到你能除掉她，对我来说相当有利。"

    old "I took the liberty of invading one of the supply caches she keeps. Lots of poisons, yes, but also a few antidotes."
    new "I took the liberty of invading one of the supply caches she keeps. Lots of poisons, yes, but also a few antidotes.\n我自作主张，闯进了她藏匿的一处补给点。里面有很多毒药，但也有几瓶解药。"

    old "Why would a vampire brew antidotes for poisons?"
    new "Why would a vampire brew antidotes for poisons?\n一个吸血鬼为什么要炼制毒药的解药？"

    old "Who can say? They were probably the result of failed experiments. Or maybe she was testing the antidotes, trying to see if she could create a stronger poison that they couldn't cure. But, you know, that woman is a pack rat. Never throws anything away."
    new "Who can say? They were probably the result of failed experiments. Or maybe she was testing the antidotes, trying to see if she could create a stronger poison that they couldn't cure. But, you know, that woman is a pack rat. Never throws anything away.\n谁说得清呢？它们大概是她实验失败的产物。又或许她在测试这些解药，想看看自己能否造出它们解不了的更强毒药。不过，你知道的，那女人是个囤积狂，什么都舍不得扔。"

    old "So her collection of potions is now mine, and I figured that part of what's mine should also be yours. You'll make better use of it than I would, I'm sure."
    new "So her collection of potions is now mine, and I figured that part of what's mine should also be yours. You'll make better use of it than I would, I'm sure.\n所以她那批药剂现在归我了，而我想，属于我的东西也该有你一份。我敢肯定，你会比我更懂得利用它。"

    old "I'm sure!"
    new "I'm sure!\n我敢肯定！"

    old "I heard Diego's howls as you were fighting Malone. I'm glad that bitch is gone. And her dog, too."
    new "I heard Diego's howls as you were fighting Malone. I'm glad that bitch is gone. And her dog, too.\n你与Malone交战时，我听到了Diego的嚎叫。我很高兴那个贱人死了，还有她的狗也是。"

    old "You don't like dogs?"
    new "You don't like dogs?\n你不喜欢狗？"

    old "Quite the contrary. As living beasts go, dogs are among the best. Which is why it's such a shame that Malone forced that creature to fight for her, protecting her in a state of perpetual undeath."
    new "Quite the contrary. As living beasts go, dogs are among the best. Which is why it's such a shame that Malone forced that creature to fight for her, protecting her in a state of perpetual undeath.\n恰恰相反。论起活着的野兽，狗算是最好的之一了。正因如此，Malone强迫那生物为她战斗、以永久不死的状态守护她，才更令人惋惜。"

    old "There is a reason that dogs live shorter lives than humans. They were meant to live for awhile, and pass on from this earth. For her to keep a dog around like that for centuries strikes me as cruel."
    new "There is a reason that dogs live shorter lives than humans. They were meant to live for awhile, and pass on from this earth. For her to keep a dog around like that for centuries strikes me as cruel.\n狗的寿命比人类短，是有原因的。它们本应活上一阵子，然后离开这个世界。她把一条狗那样留了几个世纪，在我看来实在残忍。"

    old "That animal should have gone onto the afterlife, not left to linger around attached to Malone. She doesn't deserve that creature's loyalty."
    new "That animal should have gone onto the afterlife, not left to linger around attached to Malone. She doesn't deserve that creature's loyalty.\n那动物本该前往来世，而不是被留下，依附在Malone身边徘徊。她不配得到那生物如此忠诚。"

    old "She doesn't deserve that loyalty!"
    new "She doesn't deserve that loyalty!\n她不配得到那样的忠诚！"

    old "Not only that, but Diego couldn't have asked for a worse master. Truth be told, the only reason that Malone grew so attached to that animal is that she has no friends of her own kind. Not in life, and not in undeath. She is a rotten, misanthropic hermit."
    new "Not only that, but Diego couldn't have asked for a worse master. Truth be told, the only reason that Malone grew so attached to that animal is that she has no friends of her own kind. Not in life, and not in undeath. She is a rotten, misanthropic hermit.\n不仅如此，Diego也找不到比她更糟糕的主人了。说真的，Malone之所以对那动物如此依恋，唯一的原因就是她没有同类朋友，生前没有，死后也没有。她是个腐烂、厌世的隐士。"

    old "Rotten misanthrope!"
    new "Rotten misanthrope!\n腐烂的厌世者！"

    old "That's an awfully uncharitable description."
    new "That's an awfully uncharitable description.\n这描述也太刻薄了。"

    old "[protag], if you want any proof that Malone was trouble, you should know what I found hiding amongst her personal effects."
    new "[protag], if you want any proof that Malone was trouble, you should know what I found hiding amongst her personal effects.\n[protag]，如果你想要任何证明Malone是个祸害的证据，就该知道我在她的私人物品里发现了什么。"

    old "He tosses me a bottle of something, and I catch it."
    new "He tosses me a bottle of something, and I catch it.\n他朝我扔来一瓶东西，我接住了。"

    old "Holy water. That conniving sadist had holy water. Blessed by the God Tayrion himself!"
    new "Holy water. That conniving sadist had holy water. Blessed by the God Tayrion himself!\n圣水。那个工于心计的虐待狂居然有圣水，还是由Tayrion神亲自祝福过的！"

    old "Holy water! Disgusting!"
    new "Holy water! Disgusting!\n圣水！真恶心！"

    old "Why would a vampire have such a powerful holy water?"
    new "Why would a vampire have such a powerful holy water?\n一个吸血鬼为什么会有这么强大的圣水？"

    old "It's like I said: she never fit in amongst her own kind. Not in life, and not in undeath. Perhaps she hated her peers so much that she wanted a strategy to deal with them if she needed to."
    new "It's like I said: she never fit in amongst her own kind. Not in life, and not in undeath. Perhaps she hated her peers so much that she wanted a strategy to deal with them if she needed to.\n就像我说的：她从来都融不进自己的同类，生前如此，死后也如此。也许她太恨自己的同辈，所以想要留一手，以备必要时对付他们。"

    old "But aren't you also conspiring against your fellow vampires? Isn't it a little hypocritical for you to be cross with Malone for doing the same?"
    new "But aren't you also conspiring against your fellow vampires? Isn't it a little hypocritical for you to be cross with Malone for doing the same?\n但你不也在暗中对付你的吸血鬼同胞吗？你对Malone做同样的事却大加指责，是不是有点虚伪了？"

    old "My intentions are different. I want to build something grander. Selfish, I know, but I've got more in plan than wanton destruction. Malone...she just wants the ability to hurt those who are close to her. Being a traitor is one thing, but being a traitor with no goal other than hurting others is quite another."
    new "My intentions are different. I want to build something grander. Selfish, I know, but I've got more in plan than wanton destruction. Malone...she just wants the ability to hurt those who are close to her. Being a traitor is one thing, but being a traitor with no goal other than hurting others is quite another.\n我的意图不同。我想建立起更宏大的东西。我知道这很自私，但我的计划远不止肆意破坏。而Malone……她只想获得伤害身边人的能力。当叛徒是一回事，当叛徒却除了伤害他人外别无目的，就完全是另一回事了。"

    old "So, good riddance to Malone. And you can hold onto that holy water. I'm sure we won't be needing it."
    new "So, good riddance to Malone. And you can hold onto that holy water. I'm sure we won't be needing it.\n所以，Malone算是死得好。那瓶圣水你留着吧，我确信我们用不上。"

    old "A bit dazed and confused from my encounter with Zachary and Valery, I compose myself and step out of the inn. Since I'm in Grimoire and left a sort of inquisition by the council before Apolimesho rescued me and sent me off to bed, perhaps I should find him and see if the council has any further questions."
    new "A bit dazed and confused from my encounter with Zachary and Valery, I compose myself and step out of the inn. Since I'm in Grimoire and left a sort of inquisition by the council before Apolimesho rescued me and sent me off to bed, perhaps I should find him and see if the council has any further questions.\n和Zachary、Valery的会面让我有些恍惚，我定了定神，走出客栈。既然人在Grimoire，之前在Apolimesho出面解围、打发我去睡觉之前，议会的盘问还未了结，也许我该去找他，看看议会是否还有更多问题。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Good to see you. I trust you slept well?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Good to see you. I trust you slept well?\n啊，[protag]。见到你真好。我想你睡得很好吧？"

    old "Yes. Looking at the time of day, perhaps I slept a bit too long."
    new "Yes. Looking at the time of day, perhaps I slept a bit too long.\n是的。看这时间，也许我睡得有点久了。"

    old "Nonsense. You deserve it. Besides, the council spent most of the afternoon in emergency meetings after reconvening, and you would have been barred from most of those meetings anyway."
    new "Nonsense. You deserve it. Besides, the council spent most of the afternoon in emergency meetings after reconvening, and you would have been barred from most of those meetings anyway.\n胡说。这是你应得的。况且，议会在复会后，一下午大部分时间都在开紧急会议，而那些会议大多你本就没资格参加。"

    old "So, it looks like I managed to sleep through the boring parts."
    new "So, it looks like I managed to sleep through the boring parts.\n所以看来，我正好睡过了那些无聊的部分。"

    old "Indeed. In fact, if you're ready to meet with the council now, you're right on time."
    new "Indeed. In fact, if you're ready to meet with the council now, you're right on time.\n确实。事实上，如果你现在准备好见议会，时间正合适。"

    old "Alright, let's go to meet the council, then."
    new "Alright, let's go to meet the council, then.\n好，那我们去见议会吧。"

    old "That's bothersome. It sounds like important meetings have been happening all afternoon, and I wasn't invited."
    new "That's bothersome. It sounds like important meetings have been happening all afternoon, and I wasn't invited.\n这有点烦人。听起来整个下午都在开重要会议，而我却没被邀请。"

    old "I hope you don't take it personally, [protag]. Matters of this level of secrecy and importance are always discussed internally before they're discussed with external parties."
    new "I hope you don't take it personally, [protag]. Matters of this level of secrecy and importance are always discussed internally before they're discussed with external parties.\n希望你别往心里去，[protag]。这种级别的机密要事，总是先内部讨论，之后才与外部各方沟通。"

    old "And I'm still an external party?"
    new "And I'm still an external party?\n而我还算外部一方？"

    old "You're not part of the council."
    new "You're not part of the council.\n你不是议会成员。"

    old "Even though I represent their interests."
    new "Even though I represent their interests.\n尽管我代表着他们的利益。"

    old "That's just the way it works, [protag]. The council isn't excluding you, specifically. They tend to be very opaque. In fact, you're seeing the inside of the council chambers more than anyone else in this city, council members excluded of course."
    new "That's just the way it works, [protag]. The council isn't excluding you, specifically. They tend to be very opaque. In fact, you're seeing the inside of the council chambers more than anyone else in this city, council members excluded of course.\n事情就是这样运作的，[protag]。议会并不是专门把你排除在外。他们一向很不透明。事实上，这座城市里，除了议员本身，你进出议会厅的次数比任何人都多。"

    old "Well, it looks like I'll be visiting those council chambers yet again."
    new "Well, it looks like I'll be visiting those council chambers yet again.\n好吧，看来我又要去那议会厅一趟了。"

    old "Ah, Apolimesho. I see you've returned with the emissary. Have you discussed the contents of our afternoon meetings with [himher] yet?"
    new "Ah, Apolimesho. I see you've returned with the emissary. Have you discussed the contents of our afternoon meetings with [himher] yet?\n啊，Apolimesho。我看你带着使者回来了。你已经和[himher]讨论过我们下午会议的内容了吗？"

    old "No, I did not tell [protag] anything beyond the fact that [hisher] presence was requested."
    new "No, I did not tell [protag] anything beyond the fact that [hisher] presence was requested.\n没有，除了告知[protag]是应要求出席之外，我什么也没说。"

    old "Good, good. [protag], after discussing the results of last night internally, and reviewing the testimony of the women that you rescued, it would seem that the forces that hide within the castle of N'Mar represent a threat to the existence of the human empire. Grimoire is menaced by a very clear and present danger."
    new "Good, good. [protag], after discussing the results of last night internally, and reviewing the testimony of the women that you rescued, it would seem that the forces that hide within the castle of N'Mar represent a threat to the existence of the human empire. Grimoire is menaced by a very clear and present danger.\n好，好。[protag]，在内部讨论过昨晚的结果、并审阅了你所救妇女们的证词之后，看来潜伏在N'Mar城堡中的势力，已对人类帝国的存续构成威胁。Grimoire正面临一个十分明确而迫在眉睫的危险。"

    old "I'm glad that the council sees it that way. I had come to the same conclusion myself."
    new "I'm glad that the council sees it that way. I had come to the same conclusion myself.\n我很高兴议会也这么看。我自己也得出了同样的结论。"

    old "Further intelligence reports indicate that the vampires planned to act on the first available full moon. Obviously, they didn't attack us last night, which leads us to believe that next full moon, they will be bringing the fight to our city gates."
    new "Further intelligence reports indicate that the vampires planned to act on the first available full moon. Obviously, they didn't attack us last night, which leads us to believe that next full moon, they will be bringing the fight to our city gates.\n进一步的情报显示，吸血鬼们计划在最近的满月动手。显然，他们昨晚没有进攻我们，这让我们相信，下个满月，他们会把战火带到我们的城门前。"

    old "We intend to be prepared for that attack when it comes, and we have already begun assembling forces within our borders to meet the attackers in one month's time."
    new "We intend to be prepared for that attack when it comes, and we have already begun assembling forces within our borders to meet the attackers in one month's time.\n我们打算在那场进攻来临时做好准备，并且已经开始在境内集结兵力，以便一个月后迎击来犯之敌。"

    old "This conflict seems to be quickly growing beyond what one person, or one small group of fighters, might be able to deal with. However, we believe that your services would be of further use to the council, if you're in a position to offer them."
    new "This conflict seems to be quickly growing beyond what one person, or one small group of fighters, might be able to deal with. However, we believe that your services would be of further use to the council, if you're in a position to offer them.\n这场冲突的规模似乎正迅速超出一个人、或一小队战士所能应付的范围。不过，我们相信，如果你愿意，你的效劳对议会还会有更多用处。"

    old "What kind of services do you speak of?"
    new "What kind of services do you speak of?\n你说的是什么效劳？"

    old "You would still bear the title of emissary, and we have need of a diplomatic representative to attend to certain duties critical to preparing for N'Mar's assault on the city. You could attend to them."
    new "You would still bear the title of emissary, and we have need of a diplomatic representative to attend to certain duties critical to preparing for N'Mar's assault on the city. You could attend to them.\n你仍将保留使者的头衔，而我们需要一位外交代表，去处理对备战N'Mar攻城至关重要的若干事务。你可以去办这些事。"

    old "You just want me to be a diplomat?"
    new "You just want me to be a diplomat?\n你们只是想让我当个外交官？"

    old "We are hoping that you could be a bit more than a diplomat. You proved last night that you're an effective leader in combat situations. If you can lead a strike force, then we'd like you to do the same during the next full moon."
    new "We are hoping that you could be a bit more than a diplomat. You proved last night that you're an effective leader in combat situations. If you can lead a strike force, then we'd like you to do the same during the next full moon.\n我们希望你做的，不止于外交官。你昨晚证明了，在战斗中你是位出色的领袖。如果你能率领一支突击队，那么我们希望你在下个满月时也这么做。"

    old "You want me to help defend the city?"
    new "You want me to help defend the city?\n你们想让我帮忙守城？"

    old "Your role would not be so simple as defending the city gates. Every battle has strategic objectives."
    new "Your role would not be so simple as defending the city gates. Every battle has strategic objectives.\n你的职责不会只是守城门那么简单。每场战斗都有战略目标。"

    old "Based on what we've learned of the undead, it seems that these vampires act as commanders of sort, with many ghouls, skeletons and zombies acting as their puppets."
    new "Based on what we've learned of the undead, it seems that these vampires act as commanders of sort, with many ghouls, skeletons and zombies acting as their puppets.\n根据我们对不死生物的了解，这些吸血鬼似乎充当着某种指挥官，而许多食尸鬼、骷髅和僵尸则充当他们的傀儡。"

    old "While a significant portion of the battle will consist of defending the city from the legions of undead, we have reason to believe that a more effective plan would involve sending smaller strike teams to deal with the vampire commanders."
    new "While a significant portion of the battle will consist of defending the city from the legions of undead, we have reason to believe that a more effective plan would involve sending smaller strike teams to deal with the vampire commanders.\n虽然战斗的相当一部分将是抵御不死军团的攻城，但我们有理由相信，更有效的方案是派遣小股突击队去对付吸血鬼指挥官。"

    old "Like trying to take out officers. Kill the general, and force his army to flee."
    new "Like trying to take out officers. Kill the general, and force his army to flee.\n就像是设法干掉军官。杀掉将军，逼他的军队溃逃。"

    old "That is the idea, yes."
    new "That is the idea, yes.\n正是这个思路。"

    old "The council leader pauses for a moment, letting the room linger in silence as I consider the proposition."
    new "The council leader pauses for a moment, letting the room linger in silence as I consider the proposition.\n议会领袖停顿片刻，让我在考虑这个提议时，满屋陷入沉默。"

    old "You would, of course, be paid. The council is prepared to increase your income, both to cover your expenses, and to compensate you for your services."
    new "You would, of course, be paid. The council is prepared to increase your income, both to cover your expenses, and to compensate you for your services.\n你当然会得到报酬。议会准备提高你的俸禄，既用于贴补你的开销，也作为对你效劳的酬谢。"

    old "I consider the offer. Of course, there's more at stake here than just the material reward. I've become part of something important."
    new "I consider the offer. Of course, there's more at stake here than just the material reward. I've become part of something important.\n我思量着这个提议。当然，这里牵涉的远不止物质报酬。我已成为某件大事的一部分。"

    old "I encountered many new allies and led them into battle. I could lead them into battle once more, and perhaps even have the opportunity to encounter even more allies. The connections that I would form by working for the council alone could be worth more than whatever money they're getting ready to pay me."
    new "I encountered many new allies and led them into battle. I could lead them into battle once more, and perhaps even have the opportunity to encounter even more allies. The connections that I would form by working for the council alone could be worth more than whatever money they're getting ready to pay me.\n我结识了许多新盟友，并带领他们投入战斗。我可以再次带领他们出征，甚至可能有机会结识更多盟友。单是为议会效力所结下的人脉，其价值就可能超过他们准备付给我的任何酬劳。"

    old "I'm sorry, but I must decline."
    new "I'm sorry, but I must decline.\n很抱歉，但我必须拒绝。"

    old "I'm glad to have provided valuable information to the council. And it seems that you are now prepared to act on that information. But I'm afraid you'll have to find someone else to be your messenger and fight your battles for you."
    new "I'm glad to have provided valuable information to the council. And it seems that you are now prepared to act on that information. But I'm afraid you'll have to find someone else to be your messenger and fight your battles for you.\n我很高兴能向议会提供有价值的情报。看来你们现在也准备依据这情报采取行动了。但恐怕你们得另找他人来当你们的信使、替你们打仗了。"

    old "I intend no disrespect, but it would be irresponsible for me to agree to a task I cannot commit myself to fully."
    new "I intend no disrespect, but it would be irresponsible for me to agree to a task I cannot commit myself to fully.\n我无意冒犯，但若同意一项我无法全身心投入的任务，那是不负责任的。"

    old "Understood. No disrespect taken, [protag]. We wish you the best of luck in your future endeavors."
    new "Understood. No disrespect taken, [protag]. We wish you the best of luck in your future endeavors.\n明白了。没有冒犯，[protag]。祝你在未来的事业中好运。"

    old "I'm pleased to continue serving as the council's emissary."
    new "I'm pleased to continue serving as the council's emissary.\n我很乐意继续担任议会的使者。"

    old "Excellent. I think that concludes our meeting. There are several action items for you to consider, but Apolimesho can brief you on them later. You're dismissed, [protag]."
    new "Excellent. I think that concludes our meeting. There are several action items for you to consider, but Apolimesho can brief you on them later. You're dismissed, [protag].\n很好。我想我们的会议到此结束。有几项行动事项需要你考虑，Apolimesho稍后会向你说明。你可以退下了，[protag]。"

    old "I turn to leave the council chamber."
    new "I turn to leave the council chamber.\n我转身离开议会厅。"

    old "Oh, and [protag]?"
    new "Oh, and [protag]?\n哦，还有，[protag]？"

    old "Thank you for your service. We know that you could be doing many other things with your time and resources. I speak for many of us when I say that we're glad you've chosen to continue acting as the council's emissary."
    new "Thank you for your service. We know that you could be doing many other things with your time and resources. I speak for many of us when I say that we're glad you've chosen to continue acting as the council's emissary.\n感谢你的效力。我们知道，你的时间和资源本可以用来做许多别的事。我代表我们中的许多人说一句：我们很高兴你选择继续担任议会的使者。"

    old "'Many,' not all. It sounds like the council is still not unanimous. But at least the majority has chosen to support me."
    new "'Many,' not all. It sounds like the council is still not unanimous. But at least the majority has chosen to support me.\n“许多人”，而不是所有人。听起来议会仍未达成一致。但至少多数人选择支持我。"

    old "Thank you. It's an honor to serve as your representative."
    new "Thank you. It's an honor to serve as your representative.\n谢谢。能担任你们的代表，是我的荣幸。"

    old "In my mission, I've found and killed four vampire...commanders. Lieutenants, however you want to call them."
    new "In my mission, I've found and killed four vampire...commanders. Lieutenants, however you want to call them.\n在这次任务中，我找到并杀死了四个吸血鬼……指挥官。随你怎么叫，副官之类的。"

    old "And you believe they're all of them?"
    new "And you believe they're all of them?\n而你相信这就是全部了？"

    old "I don't know, but I couldn't find anyone else in the castle."
    new "I don't know, but I couldn't find anyone else in the castle.\n我不知道，但我在城堡里找不到其他人了。"

    old "Exactly, you don't know. [protag], you did really well but I would caution you about being excessively confident."
    new "Exactly, you don't know. [protag], you did really well but I would caution you about being excessively confident.\n正是，你并不知道。[protag]，你做得非常好，但我要提醒你，别过度自信。"

    old "They're right, [protag]. Sure, maybe you defeated all the vampire lieutenants you could find in the castle, but who knows who else might show up? If they're still planning to attack Grimoire, means that someone else will be in charge of leading the undead army."
    new "They're right, [protag]. Sure, maybe you defeated all the vampire lieutenants you could find in the castle, but who knows who else might show up? If they're still planning to attack Grimoire, means that someone else will be in charge of leading the undead army.\n他们说得对，[protag]。不错，也许你击败了城堡里能找到的所有吸血鬼副官，但谁知道还会有谁冒出来？如果他们仍计划攻打Grimoire，那就意味着会有别人来统领那支不死大军。"

    old "Sorry, you're right. I shouldn't presume that I killed every vampire leader. Some might have been out since it was a full moon."
    new "Sorry, you're right. I shouldn't presume that I killed every vampire leader. Some might have been out since it was a full moon.\n抱歉，你说得对。我不该认定自己杀光了所有吸血鬼头目。那天是满月，有些可能外出了。"

    old "We all wish it was so easy. But sadly, probably it's not."
    new "We all wish it was so easy. But sadly, probably it's not.\n我们都希望事情这么简单。但可惜，恐怕并非如此。"

    old "Still, defeating four of them was a formidable feat. I can speak for everyone in the council when I say that I am very impressed."
    new "Still, defeating four of them was a formidable feat. I can speak for everyone in the council when I say that I am very impressed.\n尽管如此，击败其中四个仍是一项了不起的壮举。我可以代表议会全体说一句：我印象非常深刻。"

    old "Impressed eh? Maybe they'll be more genereous with their monetary efforts now..."
    new "Impressed eh? Maybe they'll be more genereous with their monetary efforts now...\n印象深刻，嗯？也许他们现在在钱财上会更慷慨些了……"

    old "The council leader said something about action items."
    new "The council leader said something about action items.\n议会领袖提到了什么行动事项。"

    old "Yes. The first order of business would be for you to deliver this news to Karen, as well as serve her an invitation to meet with the council again to plan out details."
    new "Yes. The first order of business would be for you to deliver this news to Karen, as well as serve her an invitation to meet with the council again to plan out details.\n是的。第一件事，是让你把这个消息带给Karen，同时向她发出邀请，请她再次与议会会面，商定细节。"

    old "Ah, so they haven't told Karen yet?"
    new "Ah, so they haven't told Karen yet?\n啊，所以他们还没告诉Karen？"

    old "Well, they did decide just this afternoon. And as for delivering messages, that's what emissaries do, [protag]. I'd advise you to meet with Karen without much further delay."
    new "Well, they did decide just this afternoon. And as for delivering messages, that's what emissaries do, [protag]. I'd advise you to meet with Karen without much further delay.\n嗯，他们也是今天下午才决定的。至于传话，那正是使者的本分，[protag]。我建议你尽快去见Karen，别再耽搁。"

    old "Of course, of course. You know, I think Karen will be quite pleased to hear that the council is taking the vampire threat more seriously. If I recall correctly, the first time I met her, she made quite an impassioned plea for them to do something about the encroaching fog around N'Mar."
    new "Of course, of course. You know, I think Karen will be quite pleased to hear that the council is taking the vampire threat more seriously. If I recall correctly, the first time I met her, she made quite an impassioned plea for them to do something about the encroaching fog around N'Mar.\n当然，当然。你知道吗，我想Karen听到议会更认真对待吸血鬼威胁的消息，会非常高兴。如果我没记错，我第一次见她时，她曾慷慨陈词，恳求他们对N'Mar周围不断蔓延的雾采取行动。"

    old "Yes. I suppose the council is acting later than she would have liked, but a late response is better than none at all."
    new "Yes. I suppose the council is acting later than she would have liked, but a late response is better than none at all.\n是的。我想议会的行动比她期望的要迟，但迟来的回应总好过毫无回应。"

    old "Come to think of it, Karen also promised me a reward the next time I stopped by the citadel. I should find time to visit her..."
    new "Come to think of it, Karen also promised me a reward the next time I stopped by the citadel. I should find time to visit her...\n说起来，Karen还答应过，等我下次到Citadel去时给我一份奖赏。我该找时间去看看她……"

    old "There are also other tasks the council would like you to take care of, but we can discuss them after you've delivered the news to Karen."
    new "There are also other tasks the council would like you to take care of, but we can discuss them after you've delivered the news to Karen.\n议会还希望你处理其他一些事务，不过我们可以等你把消息带给Karen之后再谈。"

    old "Alright. Thank you, Apolimesho."
    new "Alright. Thank you, Apolimesho.\n好的。谢谢你，Apolimesho。"

    old "No, [protag]. I should be the one thanking you."
    new "No, [protag]. I should be the one thanking you.\n不，[protag]。该道谢的人是我。"

    old "Apolimesho requested a meeting, so I reach him in his chambers."
    new "Apolimesho requested a meeting, so I reach him in his chambers.\nApolimesho请我前去会面，我便到他的房间去找他。"

    old "[protag], thank you for stopping by."
    new "[protag], thank you for stopping by.\n[protag]，谢谢你过来一趟。"

    old "Any important news?"
    new "Any important news?\n有什么重要消息吗？"

    old "No, but I thought a check-in was in order, given how close the full moon is. I hope you're already at the point where you have a good idea of who you want to be directly assisting you."
    new "No, but I thought a check-in was in order, given how close the full moon is. I hope you're already at the point where you have a good idea of who you want to be directly assisting you.\n没有，只是考虑到满月将近，我觉得该和你碰个头。希望你现在已经心里有数，想让谁来直接协助你。"

    old "I think I have a pretty good idea."
    new "I think I have a pretty good idea.\n我想我已经想得相当清楚了。"

    old "I also wanted to meet with you now because I won't be meeting with you directly on the night of the attack. I'm afraid I can't stay too close to the front lines."
    new "I also wanted to meet with you now because I won't be meeting with you directly on the night of the attack. I'm afraid I can't stay too close to the front lines.\n我现在想见你，也是因为进攻当晚我无法与你直接碰面。恐怕我不能离前线太近。"

    old "Where will you be?"
    new "Where will you be?\n你会在哪里？"

    old "I'll be with the rest of the council, waiting at the strategic headquarters. Every member of the council will be located there, including me."
    new "I'll be with the rest of the council, waiting at the strategic headquarters. Every member of the council will be located there, including me.\n我会和议会其他人一起，在战略指挥部待命。议会的每位成员都会在那里，包括我。"

    old "So, none of the council's active members will actually be close to the battle?"
    new "So, none of the council's active members will actually be close to the battle?\n那么，议会中没有一个在任成员会真正靠近战场？"

    old "That's correct. Honestly, were it up to me, I'd be closer to the front lines, but they won't make an exception in my case."
    new "That's correct. Honestly, were it up to me, I'd be closer to the front lines, but they won't make an exception in my case.\n没错。老实说，要是我做主，我会离前线更近些，但他们不会为我破例。"

    old "I hope you forgive me for saying this, but the council's decision to place themselves away from the actual consequences of the attack seems cowardly."
    new "I hope you forgive me for saying this, but the council's decision to place themselves away from the actual consequences of the attack seems cowardly.\n希望你能原谅我这么说，但议会决定让自己远离攻击的实际后果，这显得很懦弱。"

    old "They'll give the orders to have others rally to the city's defense. Meanwhile, they themselves are isolated from the front lines."
    new "They'll give the orders to have others rally to the city's defense. Meanwhile, they themselves are isolated from the front lines.\n他们会下令让其他人集结起来保卫城市，而自己则与前线隔绝。"

    old "And what would you have them do otherwise, [protag]?"
    new "And what would you have them do otherwise, [protag]?\n那不然你要他们怎么做呢，[protag]？"

    old "I guess that is necessary. The lives of those who govern the city are too valuable to risk in combat, or anywhere near it."
    new "I guess that is necessary. The lives of those who govern the city are too valuable to risk in combat, or anywhere near it.\n我想这是必要的。那些治理城市的人，其性命太过宝贵，不能冒险投入战斗，甚至不能靠近战场。"

    old "That does make some sense. There's no reason for the city leadership to be located by the battle."
    new "That does make some sense. There's no reason for the city leadership to be located by the battle.\n这确实有些道理。城市的领导层没有理由置身战场。"

    old "The truth is that the council probably won't be directly involved in the city's defense at all on the night of the attack. Remember, the council represents Grimoire's civilian leadership. Their job is to decide whether battles are fought. It's not their job to actually direct those battles. That task relies in the hands of military leadership."
    new "The truth is that the council probably won't be directly involved in the city's defense at all on the night of the attack. Remember, the council represents Grimoire's civilian leadership. Their job is to decide whether battles are fought. It's not their job to actually direct those battles. That task relies in the hands of military leadership.\n真相是，进攻当晚，议会很可能根本不会直接参与守城。记住，议会代表的是Grimoire的文职领导层。他们的职责是决定打不打仗，而不是实际指挥战斗。指挥战斗的任务掌握在军事领导手中。"

    old "A politician's place is in the safety of the city, and a military officer's place is on the battlefield. Such is the way of things. It is a reality that often leaves me uncomfortable, and I can't help but feel as though it gives the impression of some sort of class divide between those who govern and those who are governed."
    new "A politician's place is in the safety of the city, and a military officer's place is on the battlefield. Such is the way of things. It is a reality that often leaves me uncomfortable, and I can't help but feel as though it gives the impression of some sort of class divide between those who govern and those who are governed.\n政客的位置在安全的城市里，军官的位置在战场上。世事如此。这个现实常常让我不安，我忍不住觉得，它给人一种统治者与被统治者之间某种阶级鸿沟的印象。"

    old "Since I won't be working with you on the night of the city's defense, what should I do? My understanding is that the council wanted me to be part of the defense, but I think I'm going to need more specific instructions."
    new "Since I won't be working with you on the night of the city's defense, what should I do? My understanding is that the council wanted me to be part of the defense, but I think I'm going to need more specific instructions.\n既然守城之夜我不会与你并肩作战，那我该做什么？我的理解是，议会希望我参与防御，但我想我需要更具体的指示。"

    old "Indeed. Instead of working with me, you'll be working with the ranking military officers who are overseeing the city's defense directly. It will be up to them to decide how you navigate the battlefield."
    new "Indeed. Instead of working with me, you'll be working with the ranking military officers who are overseeing the city's defense directly. It will be up to them to decide how you navigate the battlefield.\n确实。你不是与我合作，而是与直接统领城防的高级军官们合作。如何调遣你、让你如何在战场上行动，将由他们决定。"

    old "Will I have any choice in the matter?"
    new "Will I have any choice in the matter?\n这件事上我还能有选择吗？"

    old "You probably will not have full autonomy. You bear many responsibilities, [protag]. Over the past two months, it feels as though you've borne the burden of not only executing your own tasks, but deciding what those tasks should be."
    new "You probably will not have full autonomy. You bear many responsibilities, [protag]. Over the past two months, it feels as though you've borne the burden of not only executing your own tasks, but deciding what those tasks should be.\n你恐怕不会有完全的自主权。你肩负着许多责任，[protag]。过去两个月里，感觉你不仅承担了执行任务的重担，还承担了决定该做什么任务的重担。"

    old "I wouldn't exactly call that a burden. It feels more like freedom."
    new "I wouldn't exactly call that a burden. It feels more like freedom.\n我倒不觉得那是重担。那感觉更像自由。"

    old "It can be quite a burden. There are times when I've found myself not quite sure of what to do, sometimes paralyzed by indecision as I try to determine the best use of my time."
    new "It can be quite a burden. There are times when I've found myself not quite sure of what to do, sometimes paralyzed by indecision as I try to determine the best use of my time.\n那可能确实是种重担。有时我会发现自己不太确定该做什么，偶尔在试图确定如何最好地利用时间时，因犹豫不决而陷入僵局。"

    old "I've spoken to several of the leading officers, and they intend to include you in the decision-making process. However, when it comes to things like gathering intelligence, you'll defer to them. Let them determine which points around the battlefield are most ripe for exploitation, then go in and strike decisively when they discover potential weaknesses."
    new "I've spoken to several of the leading officers, and they intend to include you in the decision-making process. However, when it comes to things like gathering intelligence, you'll defer to them. Let them determine which points around the battlefield are most ripe for exploitation, then go in and strike decisively when they discover potential weaknesses.\n我和几位主要军官谈过，他们打算让你参与决策过程。不过，在搜集情报这类事情上，你要听从他们。让他们判断战场上哪些位置最值得利用，等他们发现潜在弱点后，你再果断出击。"

    old "Potential weaknesses?"
    new "Potential weaknesses?\n潜在弱点？"

    old "Or potential strong points in the enemy lines where they need to break through. I must confess, I'm not a military man, so if you're expecting me to give you a perfect picture of what the battle will be like, I'm sorely unqualified."
    new "Or potential strong points in the enemy lines where they need to break through. I must confess, I'm not a military man, so if you're expecting me to give you a perfect picture of what the battle will be like, I'm sorely unqualified.\n或是敌军阵线上需要突破的潜在强点。我必须坦白，我不是军人，所以你若指望我把战斗的情形描绘得面面俱到，那我实在不够格。"

    old "That's alright, Apolimesho. I'll meet with the high-ranking officers and get my marching orders when the night comes."
    new "That's alright, Apolimesho. I'll meet with the high-ranking officers and get my marching orders when the night comes.\n没关系，Apolimesho。我会去和高级军官们碰面，等夜晚降临时领受我的行军命令。"

    old "In the meantime, think carefully about how you'll spend your remaining time, especially if there are any tasks you've been putting off. Oh, and I've brought another cache of supplies. Hopefully this will help."
    new "In the meantime, think carefully about how you'll spend your remaining time, especially if there are any tasks you've been putting off. Oh, and I've brought another cache of supplies. Hopefully this will help.\n与此同时，仔细想想你剩下的时间要怎么安排，尤其是那些你一直拖延的事情。哦，我还带来了一批补给。希望这能帮上忙。"

    old "And more gifts from the elves and dwarves."
    new "And more gifts from the elves and dwarves.\n还有精灵和矮人们送来的更多礼物。"

    old "Wow, a health-regenerating ring!"
    new "Wow, a health-regenerating ring!\n哇，一枚回复生命值的戒指！"

    old "The dwarves as usual are sending a more practical item. A very sturdy piece of armor. I'm sure you'll find it as useful as the ring."
    new "The dwarves as usual are sending a more practical item. A very sturdy piece of armor. I'm sure you'll find it as useful as the ring.\n矮人们照旧送来更实用的东西。一件非常结实的护甲。我肯定你会觉得它和那枚戒指一样有用。"

    old "Thank you. I guess I might not see you again until after the mission, but I'll be sure to report in when the night is over."
    new "Thank you. I guess I might not see you again until after the mission, but I'll be sure to report in when the night is over.\n谢谢。我想可能要等任务结束才能再见到你，但夜里结束后我一定会来汇报。"

    old "Here's hoping we'll both still be around to make it to that post-battle report."
    new "Here's hoping we'll both still be around to make it to that post-battle report.\n希望我们俩都能活到做那份战后汇报的时候。"

    old "The full moon has arrived. This should be the night of the attack."
    new "The full moon has arrived. This should be the night of the attack.\n满月已至。今晚应该就是进攻之夜。"

    old "All of the shops and residences around Grimoire seem to have boarded-up windows. I'm not sure what use that protection will be if the undead manage to breach the city perimeter, but I suppose there are people who feel the need to do something so that they don't feel completely defenseless."
    new "All of the shops and residences around Grimoire seem to have boarded-up windows. I'm not sure what use that protection will be if the undead manage to breach the city perimeter, but I suppose there are people who feel the need to do something so that they don't feel completely defenseless.\nGrimoire周边所有的店铺和住宅似乎都钉上了窗板。如果不死生物真突破了城市外围，我不知道这防护能有什么用，但我想，总有人觉得必须做点什么，才不至于感到彻底无助。"

    old "Standing at the edge of the city and facing the plains of N'Mar, the city does actually look to be ready for combat. Rows of soldiers are lined up, and they look alert and ready for battle."
    new "Standing at the edge of the city and facing the plains of N'Mar, the city does actually look to be ready for combat. Rows of soldiers are lined up, and they look alert and ready for battle.\n站在城市边缘，面朝N'Mar平原，这座城市看上去确实已为战斗做好了准备。一排排士兵列队站好，个个警觉，随时准备开战。"

    old "Some are telling jokes and trying to kill the tension with a bit of levity, while others wear steely gazes with furrowed brows, but one thing that I don't see in their eyes is fear. They're prepared for whatever this night holds."
    new "Some are telling jokes and trying to kill the tension with a bit of levity, while others wear steely gazes with furrowed brows, but one thing that I don't see in their eyes is fear. They're prepared for whatever this night holds.\n有的在讲笑话，想用几分轻松冲淡紧张，有的则眉头紧锁、目光如铁，但我在他们眼中看不到一样东西——恐惧。无论今晚发生什么，他们都已准备好面对。"

    old "As I look at the rows upon rows of soldiers, I find myself overwhelmed by the sheer immensity of the city's defenses. I suppose it shouldn't surprise me to see that a city of Grimoire's size has such a substantial self-defense force."
    new "As I look at the rows upon rows of soldiers, I find myself overwhelmed by the sheer immensity of the city's defenses. I suppose it shouldn't surprise me to see that a city of Grimoire's size has such a substantial self-defense force.\n望着那一排又一排的士兵，我不禁被这座城市防御之庞大所震撼。我想，看到Grimoire这样规模的城市拥有如此雄厚的自卫力量，本也不该令我惊讶。"

    old "And I did encounter scores of soldiers out in the fields during my first vampire encounter that led to me becoming a representative of Grimoire. In a way, tonight seems to mirror that experience from two months ago, but in reverse: this time, the vampires are coming to our territory, and I'm thinking that the city's defenses will be able to punish them."
    new "And I did encounter scores of soldiers out in the fields during my first vampire encounter that led to me becoming a representative of Grimoire. In a way, tonight seems to mirror that experience from two months ago, but in reverse: this time, the vampires are coming to our territory, and I'm thinking that the city's defenses will be able to punish them.\n而在我第一次遭遇吸血鬼、并因此成为Grimoire代表的那晚，我确实在旷野里遇到过大批士兵。从某种意义上说，今晚仿佛是两个月前那次经历的倒影，只是反了过来：这一次，是吸血鬼来到我们的地盘，而我想，这座城市的防御足以狠狠教训他们。"

    old "Then again, it probably won't be an easy victory. The vampires are, above all, unpredictable. Not only do they have nearly limitless ranks of undead ghouls under their command, but a single powerful enemy could wreak untold destruction among the ranks of Grimoire's soldiers."
    new "Then again, it probably won't be an easy victory. The vampires are, above all, unpredictable. Not only do they have nearly limitless ranks of undead ghouls under their command, but a single powerful enemy could wreak untold destruction among the ranks of Grimoire's soldiers.\n不过话说回来，这场胜利恐怕不会轻松。吸血鬼最是难以捉摸。他们麾下不仅有近乎无穷无尽的不死食尸鬼，而且单是一个强大的敌人，就可能在Grimoire的士兵阵列中造成难以估量的破坏。"

    old "I start to think about my role in all of this. In a way, it feels like I'm only a small part of Grimoire's defense, and yet everyone I've talked to seems to think my role is important. Is it really necessary for me to lead a squad?"
    new "I start to think about my role in all of this. In a way, it feels like I'm only a small part of Grimoire's defense, and yet everyone I've talked to seems to think my role is important. Is it really necessary for me to lead a squad?\n我开始思考自己在这一切中的角色。某种程度上，我感觉自己只是Grimoire防御中微不足道的一环，可我交谈过的每个人似乎都认为我的角色很重要。真的有必要让我率领一支小队吗？"

    old "Whether it's necessary is beside the point, I suppose. It's my duty and obligation, and it's something I've agreed to do. If I'm going to make good by the promises I've made, now's the time for me to step up to the plate."
    new "Whether it's necessary is beside the point, I suppose. It's my duty and obligation, and it's something I've agreed to do. If I'm going to make good by the promises I've made, now's the time for me to step up to the plate.\n我想，有没有必要并不重要。这是我的职责与义务，也是我答应要做的事。如果我要兑现许下的承诺，现在正是我挺身而出的时候。"

    old "My mind turns to my recent conversation with Zachary and Valery. I suppose compared to the prospect of becoming a vampire, this battle might not be the most significant thing to happen in my life. I could become a vampire, and leave all of this behind."
    new "My mind turns to my recent conversation with Zachary and Valery. I suppose compared to the prospect of becoming a vampire, this battle might not be the most significant thing to happen in my life. I could become a vampire, and leave all of this behind.\n我的思绪转向了不久前与Zachary和Valery的谈话。我想，与变成吸血鬼的前景相比，这场战斗也许并不是我一生中最重要的事。我可以变成吸血鬼，把这一切都抛在身后。"

    old "Or perhaps I might accept their offer, and continue to fight for Grimoire. Odd as it might seem, it could be possible for me to both join the ranks of the vampires while continuing to assist Grimoire in their fight against N'Mar's vampires."
    new "Or perhaps I might accept their offer, and continue to fight for Grimoire. Odd as it might seem, it could be possible for me to both join the ranks of the vampires while continuing to assist Grimoire in their fight against N'Mar's vampires.\n又或许我可以接受他们的提议，同时继续为Grimoire而战。听上去虽怪，但我确实有可能既加入吸血鬼的行列，又继续协助Grimoire对抗N'Mar的吸血鬼。"

    old "Then again, the decision to actually be initiated as a vampire isn't one I should make flippantly. It it something I'm really ready for?"
    new "Then again, the decision to actually be initiated as a vampire isn't one I should make flippantly. It it something I'm really ready for?\n不过话说回来，真正接受转化成为吸血鬼的决定，我不该草率做出。我当真准备好了吗？"

    old "...whether it's something I'm ready for or not is less important than whether it's something I want to do. And I know it's something that I want to do."
    new "...whether it's something I'm ready for or not is less important than whether it's something I want to do. And I know it's something that I want to do.\n……我是否准备好，远不如我是否想做这件事来得重要。而我知道，这正是我想做的事。"

    old "I turn in the direction of the fields and head out to meet with Zachary and Valery."
    new "I turn in the direction of the fields and head out to meet with Zachary and Valery.\n我转向旷野的方向，前去与Zachary和Valery会面。"

    old "As much as I might like to play with the idea, it's just not something I have it in me to go through with."
    new "As much as I might like to play with the idea, it's just not something I have it in me to go through with.\n尽管我可能很想玩玩这个念头，但我终究没有那个心性去真的付诸实施。"

    old "In a way, I feel like I've already given Grimoire more than I owe it. I've risked my life once already. Actually, probably more than once. I could have died on many occasions during my journey."
    new "In a way, I feel like I've already given Grimoire more than I owe it. I've risked my life once already. Actually, probably more than once. I could have died on many occasions during my journey.\n从某种意义上说，我觉得自己为Grimoire付出的，已经超出了我亏欠它的。我早已冒过一次生命危险。实际上，恐怕不止一次。旅途中我本可能死上很多回。"

    old "The council tells me I'm needed...but do they really have my best interests at heart? I doubt very much that the balance of power is so fragile that the participation of a single person could turn the tide of battle in one direction or another."
    new "The council tells me I'm needed...but do they really have my best interests at heart? I doubt very much that the balance of power is so fragile that the participation of a single person could turn the tide of battle in one direction or another.\n议会说他们需要我……但他们真的把我的切身利益放在心上吗？我很怀疑，力量的平衡会脆弱到单凭一人的参与，就能左右战局的走向。"

    old "And if the city falls, why should I stay around to be part of its defeat? Whatever the odds may be, I'm not ready to die here. I've ignored my own self-interest for far too long."
    new "And if the city falls, why should I stay around to be part of its defeat? Whatever the odds may be, I'm not ready to die here. I've ignored my own self-interest for far too long.\n而如果城市陷落，我又何必留在这里，成为它溃败的一部分？无论胜算几何，我都没准备好死在这里。我已经忽视自己的切身利益太久了。"

    old "Now feels like the worst possible time for me to leave, and yet I can't help but feel that this might actually be the ideal time to leave. It's time for this city to learn that it can survive without my help. It's time for me to start taking care of myself and my own safety first."
    new "Now feels like the worst possible time for me to leave, and yet I can't help but feel that this might actually be the ideal time to leave. It's time for this city to learn that it can survive without my help. It's time for me to start taking care of myself and my own safety first.\n现在离开，感觉时机糟透了，可我又忍不住觉得，这也许恰恰是离开的最佳时机。是时候让这座城市学会，没有我的帮助它也能存活下去。是时候让我开始优先照顾自己、顾及自己的安危了。"

    old "I move away from my companions with an excuse. I feel sorry for abandoning them, but I have a bad feeling about this."
    new "I move away from my companions with an excuse. I feel sorry for abandoning them, but I have a bad feeling about this.\n我找了个借口，从同伴们身边走开。为抛下他们，我感到抱歉，但我对此有种不好的预感。"

    old "I turn away from the city walls and start walking south. Away from N'Mar, away from Grimoire, away from the attack."
    new "I turn away from the city walls and start walking south. Away from N'Mar, away from Grimoire, away from the attack.\n我转身离开城墙，开始向南走去。远离N'Mar，远离Grimoire，远离这场进攻。"

    old "It's time for me to stop dawdling and get on with business."
    new "It's time for me to stop dawdling and get on with business.\n我该停止磨蹭，去办正事了。"

    old "At the city gates, I spot the ranking officers standing by the banner bearing the city's emblem. One of them seems to recognize me and trots over."
    new "At the city gates, I spot the ranking officers standing by the banner bearing the city's emblem. One of them seems to recognize me and trots over.\n在城门处，我看到几位高级军官站在绘有城市徽记的旗帜旁。其中一人似乎认出了我，小跑着迎上前来。"

    old "[protag]! I was told you'd be joining us. It's good to see you again. It's been quite awhile."
    new "[protag]! I was told you'd be joining us. It's good to see you again. It's been quite awhile.\n[protag]！我听说你会加入我们。很高兴再见到你。已经好一阵子没见了。"

    old "It's good to see you too, Sergeant Thomas. I haven't seen you since...well, since the night I started working for the Grimoire council."
    new "It's good to see you too, Sergeant Thomas. I haven't seen you since...well, since the night I started working for the Grimoire council.\n我也很高兴见到你，Thomas中士。自打……嗯，自打我刚开始为Grimoire议会效力的那个夜晚，我就再没见过你。"

    old "Indeed, indeed. Though, it's actually Captain Thomas now."
    new "Indeed, indeed. Though, it's actually Captain Thomas now.\n确实，确实。不过，现在其实该叫Thomas队长了。"

    old "I'm sorry, I don't recall when we last met."
    new "I'm sorry, I don't recall when we last met.\n抱歉，我不记得我们上次见面是什么时候了。"

    old "It was a night quite like this one. You might not remember me, but I certainly remember you. You helped get my men home safely through the field."
    new "It was a night quite like this one. You might not remember me, but I certainly remember you. You helped get my men home safely through the field.\n那是一个和今晚十分相似的夜晚。你也许不记得我，但我肯定记得你。是你帮我的人安全穿过旷野回了家。"

    old "Ah, yes. That first night when Grimoire learned just what kinds of dangers N'Mar held."
    new "Ah, yes. That first night when Grimoire learned just what kinds of dangers N'Mar held.\n啊，是的。就是Grimoire第一次领教N'Mar藏有何等危险的那个夜晚。"

    old "Indeed. I was surprised to learn that you became so closely tied to the council's affairs after that night, but I don't think they could have picked someone better for the task."
    new "Indeed. I was surprised to learn that you became so closely tied to the council's affairs after that night, but I don't think they could have picked someone better for the task.\n确实。得知那晚之后你与议会的事务联系得如此紧密，我很惊讶，但我想，他们再也挑不出比你更合适的人选了。"

    old "They've been quickly adapting to the new threat. Assembling a defense force of this size is no small task."
    new "They've been quickly adapting to the new threat. Assembling a defense force of this size is no small task.\n他们一直在迅速适应这新的威胁。集结起这么大规模的防御力量，可不是件小事。"

    old "Indeed. I myself was a bit surprised to find myself quickly promoted to the rank of captain."
    new "Indeed. I myself was a bit surprised to find myself quickly promoted to the rank of captain.\n确实。我自己都有点惊讶，竟这么快就被提拔成了队长。"

    old "Weren't you a sergeant before?"
    new "Weren't you a sergeant before?\n你以前不是中士吗？"

    old "Yes, I was."
    new "Yes, I was.\n是的，我以前是。"

    old "My, my. That's quite a fast promotion."
    new "My, my. That's quite a fast promotion.\n哎呀呀。这升迁可真是快。"

    old "These are trying times for the city, and ever since the night I watched so many men die on that field, I've fully dedicated myself to ensuring the city's combat readiness."
    new "These are trying times for the city, and ever since the night I watched so many men die on that field, I've fully dedicated myself to ensuring the city's combat readiness.\n这座城市正处在艰难时期，而自从那晚我眼睁睁看着那么多人在那片旷野上死去，我便全身心投入到确保城市做好战斗准备这件事上。"

    old "It seems you've done much to earn your rank, then. Most of the time, promotions just seem to happen through seniority."
    new "It seems you've done much to earn your rank, then. Most of the time, promotions just seem to happen through seniority.\n这么说，你的军衔是靠自己挣来的。大多数时候，晋升似乎都只是论资排辈。"

    old "Well, you've certainly earned your title. Though...I must confess, I don't know exactly what that is."
    new "Well, you've certainly earned your title. Though...I must confess, I don't know exactly what that is.\n嗯，你的头衔也肯定是挣来的。不过……我得承认，我不太清楚那到底是什么头衔。"

    old "I'm the council's emissary."
    new "I'm the council's emissary.\n我是议会的使者。"

    old "Ah, not a military title, then. And yet you're fighting with us tonight."
    new "Ah, not a military title, then. And yet you're fighting with us tonight.\n啊，那不是军职头衔了。可你今晚还是来和我们并肩作战。"

    old "It's...complicated."
    new "It's...complicated.\n这……说来话长。"

    old "Haha! No doubt, no doubt. Well, I don't mean to get bogged down on the technicalities of rank and such. What's important is tonight's mission. You have some trusted followers who will accompany you, correct? You're essentially commanding a small unit?"
    new "Haha! No doubt, no doubt. Well, I don't mean to get bogged down on the technicalities of rank and such. What's important is tonight's mission. You have some trusted followers who will accompany you, correct? You're essentially commanding a small unit?\n哈哈！那是自然，那是自然。嗯，我也不想在这些军衔之类的细枝末节上纠缠。重要的是今晚的任务。你有一些信得过的追随者会随行，对吧？你基本上是在指挥一支小队？"

    old "Based on what we've observed, we expect that the invasion will come in the form of lesser undead. Zombies, ghouls, perhaps skeleton warriors and the like. Certainly nothing to trifle with, but they won't be sending their best. The nature of these undead is that they can attack us with numbers, and simply fending that off will be quite an ordeal."
    new "Based on what we've observed, we expect that the invasion will come in the form of lesser undead. Zombies, ghouls, perhaps skeleton warriors and the like. Certainly nothing to trifle with, but they won't be sending their best. The nature of these undead is that they can attack us with numbers, and simply fending that off will be quite an ordeal.\n根据我们的观察，我们预计入侵会以低等不死生物的形式到来。僵尸、食尸鬼，也许还有骷髅战士之类。当然绝非可以掉以轻心的东西，但他们不会派出精锐。这些不死生物的本质就是靠数量压人，单是挡住这一波波的冲击，就够我们苦战一场。"

    old "That being said, we've established a perimeter in such a way that it will take more than sheer numbers to break us. We'll be constantly replacing men on the front line with a consistent rotation, and we've been running drills for several days to ensure that everyone knows how to deal with slow-moving threats like the lesser undead."
    new "That being said, we've established a perimeter in such a way that it will take more than sheer numbers to break us. We'll be constantly replacing men on the front line with a consistent rotation, and we've been running drills for several days to ensure that everyone knows how to deal with slow-moving threats like the lesser undead.\n话虽如此，我们布设的防线，也不是光靠人海就能冲破的。我们会用轮换不断更替前线的士兵，而且已经操练了数日，确保每个人都懂得如何应对低等不死生物这类行动迟缓的威胁。"

    old "The council told me that you already disposed of the four vampire lieutenants you found in the castle. I must say, I'm impressed."
    new "The council told me that you already disposed of the four vampire lieutenants you found in the castle. I must say, I'm impressed.\n议会告诉我，你已经除掉了在城堡里找到的那四个吸血鬼副官。我得说，我很佩服。"

    old "That will be a big help for tonight's battle. Without their lieutenants, we believe that someone else is leading the forces. Another vampire, or perhaps this time something bigger. We don't know yet. But there's only one way to find out."
    new "That will be a big help for tonight's battle. Without their lieutenants, we believe that someone else is leading the forces. Another vampire, or perhaps this time something bigger. We don't know yet. But there's only one way to find out.\n这对今晚的战斗是极大的帮助。没了那些副官，我们相信统领这支部队的另有其人。是另一个吸血鬼，又或许这次是更厉害的东西。我们还不知道。但要想弄清楚，只有一个办法。"

    old "We will have you assume a defensive posture with us at the city perimeter. You'd be fighting many ranks of undead enemies. For someone as skilled as you, they probably wouldn't pose much of a challenge."
    new "We will have you assume a defensive posture with us at the city perimeter. You'd be fighting many ranks of undead enemies. For someone as skilled as you, they probably wouldn't pose much of a challenge.\n我们会让你和我们在城市外围采取防守姿态。你将与成排的不死敌人作战。以你的身手，它们大概构不成什么威胁。"

    old "And that's until the real enemy leader shows up."
    new "And that's until the real enemy leader shows up.\n而这一切会持续到真正的敌方首领现身为止。"

    old "Yes. After seeing you, maybe whoever is leading this attack will show up."
    new "Yes. After seeing you, maybe whoever is leading this attack will show up.\n是的。看到你之后，也许这次进攻的统领者就会现身。"

    old "From envoy of Grimoire, to bait of Grimoire. Doesn't sound like a great career improvement."
    new "From envoy of Grimoire, to bait of Grimoire. Doesn't sound like a great career improvement.\n从Grimoire的使者，到Grimoire的诱饵。这职业发展听着可不怎么样。"

    old "Haha. Worry not, while it's true that you might act as a sort of bait, my men and I will be vigilant and offer you help whenever you need it. You're not alone in this fight, [protag]."
    new "Haha. Worry not, while it's true that you might act as a sort of bait, my men and I will be vigilant and offer you help whenever you need it. You're not alone in this fight, [protag].\n哈哈。别担心，你固然可能充当某种诱饵，但我和我的弟兄们会保持警惕，随时在你需要时伸出援手。这场战斗里你不是孤身一人，[protag]。"

    old "Good work, [protag]. You've really helped to thin out their ranks. We just need to keep up this fight."
    new "Good work, [protag]. You've really helped to thin out their ranks. We just need to keep up this fight.\n干得漂亮，[protag]。你真的帮我们削薄了他们的阵线。我们只需把这场战斗继续下去。"

    old "More undead incoming! Get ready!"
    new "More undead incoming! Get ready!\n更多不死生物来袭！做好准备！"

    old "Now, we could have you assume a defensive posture with us at the city perimeter. You'd be fighting many ranks of undead enemies. For someone as skilled as you, they probably wouldn't pose much of a challenge, but that's certainly an option, if you'd choose to take it."
    new "Now, we could have you assume a defensive posture with us at the city perimeter. You'd be fighting many ranks of undead enemies. For someone as skilled as you, they probably wouldn't pose much of a challenge, but that's certainly an option, if you'd choose to take it.\n那么，我们可以让你和我们在城市外围采取防守姿态。你将与成排的不死敌人作战。以你的身手，它们大概构不成什么威胁，但如果你愿意，这当然是个选择。"

    old "However...there is also an option which is a bit more ambitious."
    new "However...there is also an option which is a bit more ambitious.\n然而……还有一个更有雄心的选择。"

    old "Decapitation."
    new "Decapitation.\n斩首行动。"

    old "You mean dismembering the zombies?"
    new "You mean dismembering the zombies?\n你是说肢解僵尸？"

    old "No, no. I'm talking about decapitating the enemy army. It's a military approach that involves targeting the enemy's leaders with the assumption that, if their leader is killed, the lesser soldieres will retreat. We think it might be possible here."
    new "No, no. I'm talking about decapitating the enemy army. It's a military approach that involves targeting the enemy's leaders with the assumption that, if their leader is killed, the lesser soldieres will retreat. We think it might be possible here.\n不，不。我说的是给敌军“斩首”。这是一种军事策略，以敌方首领为目标，假定首领一死，底下的士兵就会溃退。我们觉得在这里也许行得通。"

    old "For the undead of N'Mar's plains to all suddenly rise up and attack the city isn't natural. They must be under the influence of some more powerful undead. Undead such as the vampires we saw a while ago. The vampires can control the lesser undead, but the range of their powers is somewhat limited. They'll probably have to leave the castle."
    new "For the undead of N'Mar's plains to all suddenly rise up and attack the city isn't natural. They must be under the influence of some more powerful undead. Undead such as the vampires we saw a while ago. The vampires can control the lesser undead, but the range of their powers is somewhat limited. They'll probably have to leave the castle.\nN'Mar平原上的不死生物突然全数涌起、攻打城市，这并不自然。它们必定处于某个更强大不死生物的影响之下。就像我们之前见过的吸血鬼那样。吸血鬼能控制低等不死生物，但他们力量的作用范围相当有限。他们很可能不得不离开城堡。"

    old "If you were to go out into the field, away from the main fight, and dispatch those vampires that are remotely controlling the zombies and other shambling monsters, it would likely cause portions of their army to stop advancing, or simply vanish altogether. It would certainly decrease the number of waves our army would need to fend off."
    new "If you were to go out into the field, away from the main fight, and dispatch those vampires that are remotely controlling the zombies and other shambling monsters, it would likely cause portions of their army to stop advancing, or simply vanish altogether. It would certainly decrease the number of waves our army would need to fend off.\n如果你能深入旷野，远离主战场，去干掉那些远程操控僵尸和其他蹒跚怪物的吸血鬼，那么他们军队的一部分很可能会停止推进，甚至直接消失。这无疑会减少我们军队需要抵挡的进攻波次。"

    old "I see. So my options are to stay and fight weaker enemies, or venture out in the pursuit of stronger foes."
    new "I see. So my options are to stay and fight weaker enemies, or venture out in the pursuit of stronger foes.\n我明白了。所以我的选择，要么是留下与较弱的敌人作战，要么是冒险外出，去追击更强的敌人。"

    old "We've actually scouted out several locations where we think vampires might be hiding. Parts of the plains that are somewhat secluded, but close enough to the city that a vampire could hide their and have their influence extend to our gates. If you decide to check out one of those locations, be sure to come back once you're done."
    new "We've actually scouted out several locations where we think vampires might be hiding. Parts of the plains that are somewhat secluded, but close enough to the city that a vampire could hide their and have their influence extend to our gates. If you decide to check out one of those locations, be sure to come back once you're done.\n我们其实已经侦察出几处我们认为吸血鬼可能藏身的地点。那是平原上几处有些隐蔽的地方，但离城市够近，吸血鬼可以藏身其中，让自己的影响延伸到我们的城门。如果你决定去查看其中一处，完成后一定要回来。"

    old "Hmm traveling to each location will take some time. Even by horse, with the fog, it will be hard to move fast."
    new "Hmm traveling to each location will take some time. Even by horse, with the fog, it will be hard to move fast.\n嗯，前往每个地点都要花些时间。即便骑马，有这雾，也很难快速移动。"

    old "Oh the council didn't inform you? We got an unexpected help from the Grand Mogul of Dingirra. He offered to let us use their magic portals."
    new "Oh the council didn't inform you? We got an unexpected help from the Grand Mogul of Dingirra. He offered to let us use their magic portals.\n哦，议会没告诉你吗？我们得到了Dingirra大君主意外的帮助。他提出让我们使用他们的魔法传送门。"

    old "With them, you'll be able to instantly teleport in any of those locations and come back after you're done."
    new "With them, you'll be able to instantly teleport in any of those locations and come back after you're done.\n有了它们，你就能瞬间传送到任何一个地点，办完事后再回来。"

    old "Won't be risky to have the portals open? What if a horde of undead moves through it?"
    new "Won't be risky to have the portals open? What if a horde of undead moves through it?\n让传送门开着不会有风险吗？要是有大群不死生物穿过来怎么办？"

    old "Apparently, doesn't work for them. I am not sure why exactly, but the Grand Mogul assured us that the undead who try to pass through the portal will be instantly destroyed. Apolimesho confirmed that he was saying the truth."
    new "Apparently, doesn't work for them. I am not sure why exactly, but the Grand Mogul assured us that the undead who try to pass through the portal will be instantly destroyed. Apolimesho confirmed that he was saying the truth.\n显然，那对它们不奏效。我不太清楚具体原因，但大君主向我们保证，试图穿过传送门的不死生物会瞬间被摧毁。Apolimesho也证实他说的是实话。"

    old "Nice. Why help us though?"
    new "Nice. Why help us though?\n不错。不过他们为什么要帮我们？"

    old "For obvious reasons. If Grimoire was to be overrun by undead, who you think would buy the precious Dingirran goods? It's their interest that the Empire's biggest town remains safe."
    new "For obvious reasons. If Grimoire was to be overrun by undead, who you think would buy the precious Dingirran goods? It's their interest that the Empire's biggest town remains safe.\n原因显而易见。如果Grimoire被不死生物攻陷，你觉得还有谁会买Dingirra那些贵重的货物？帝国最大的城市保持安全，才符合他们的利益。"

    old "Right. I forgot about this detail."
    new "Right. I forgot about this detail.\n对。我倒是忘了这茬。"

    old "But it's not just that. Speaking of Dingirra, while I suppose you already equipped yourself properly for the battle, some of their merchants conveniently set up some temporary shops nearby the gates. Just in case you need something."
    new "But it's not just that. Speaking of Dingirra, while I suppose you already equipped yourself properly for the battle, some of their merchants conveniently set up some temporary shops nearby the gates. Just in case you need something.\n但还不止如此。说到Dingirra，我想你既然已为战斗备好了装备，他们的一些商人还是顺势在城门附近搭起了临时商铺，以防你需要什么。"

    old "Ha. Now I understand why they 'helped' us. Always trying to make a profit from every situation, even an undead invasion."
    new "Ha. Now I understand why they 'helped' us. Always trying to make a profit from every situation, even an undead invasion.\n哈。现在我明白他们为什么“帮”我们了。总是想从每一种局面里牟利，连不死生物入侵都不放过。"

    old "Heh, you'll see they're very reasonable with their prices. Besides, they're risking their lives by staying out here: I think they deserve it, after all."
    new "Heh, you'll see they're very reasonable with their prices. Besides, they're risking their lives by staying out here: I think they deserve it, after all.\n呵，你会发现他们的价格十分公道。况且，他们留在这里是冒着生命危险的：我想他们终究受之无愧。"

    old "Now, let's get to work [protag]. Decide what to do next."
    new "Now, let's get to work [protag]. Decide what to do next.\n好了，[protag]，我们开始干活吧。决定下一步做什么。"

    old "Amazing fight, [protag]. We're lucky to have your help in this battle."
    new "Amazing fight, [protag]. We're lucky to have your help in this battle.\n打得太精彩了，[protag]。这场战斗能有你相助，我们真是幸运。"

    old "Look out, [protag]. They seem to be launching a powerful attack on the front gate! The next undead wave will be tough."
    new "Look out, [protag]. They seem to be launching a powerful attack on the front gate! The next undead wave will be tough.\n当心，[protag]。他们似乎正在对前门发动猛烈攻击！下一波不死生物会很难对付。"

    old "The undead are retreating! [protag], let's teach them a lesson they won't forget soon!"
    new "The undead are retreating! [protag], let's teach them a lesson they won't forget soon!\n不死生物在撤退了！[protag]，让我们给他们一个久久难忘的教训！"

    old "Get back, [protag]. We'll take care of them. Get to cover and heal yourself for the next fight."
    new "Get back, [protag]. We'll take care of them. Get to cover and heal yourself for the next fight.\n退后，[protag]。这里交给我们。去找掩护，为下一场战斗治疗自己。"

    old "{i}You take a rest before the next fight. All party members have regained 50%% of their total HP/SP! (Members in reserve will still heal fully like before){/i}"
    new "{i}You take a rest before the next fight. All party members have regained 50%% of their total HP/SP! (Members in reserve will still heal fully like before){/i}\n{i}你在下一场战斗前稍作休息。所有队友都恢复了总HP/SP的50%%！（后备成员仍会像之前一样完全恢复）{/i}"

    old "Best of luck. Oh, one more thing, [protag]. Take this with you."
    new "Best of luck. Oh, one more thing, [protag]. Take this with you.\n祝你好运。哦，还有一件事，[protag]。把这个带上。"

    old "It's a bag of salt."
    new "It's a bag of salt.\n这是一袋盐。"

    old "I can see that. I'm wondering what its purpose is."
    new "I can see that. I'm wondering what its purpose is.\n我看得出来。我只是在想它有什么用途。"

    old "One of Grimoire's most prominent researchers speculates that salting the earth might be an effective counter-measure against certain rituals designed to summon the undead, or exert influence over them."
    new "One of Grimoire's most prominent researchers speculates that salting the earth might be an effective counter-measure against certain rituals designed to summon the undead, or exert influence over them.\nGrimoire最杰出的研究者之一推测，用盐撒地，也许是对抗某些旨在召唤不死生物、或对其施加影响的仪式的有效对策。"

    old "If that's true, then why not salt the entire plains?"
    new "If that's true, then why not salt the entire plains?\n如果这是真的，那为什么不给整片平原都撒上盐？"

    old "Because it requires a large quantity of salt to effectively cover a very small area. As a preventative measure, covering the plains in salt just isn't possible. But if you encounter a ritual in progress, you may be able to halt it by spreading salt over the area where the ritual is being conducted."
    new "Because it requires a large quantity of salt to effectively cover a very small area. As a preventative measure, covering the plains in salt just isn't possible. But if you encounter a ritual in progress, you may be able to halt it by spreading salt over the area where the ritual is being conducted.\n因为要有效覆盖很小一块区域，就需要大量盐。作为预防措施，用盐覆盖整片平原根本不可能。但如果你撞见正在进行的仪式，也许可以通过把盐撒在仪式举行的区域上来中止它。"

    old "You seem to have become quite an expert on this topic, Captain Thomas."
    new "You seem to have become quite an expert on this topic, Captain Thomas.\n你似乎已经成了这个话题的行家，Thomas队长。"

    old "It's a topic that's consumed most of my attention as of late."
    new "It's a topic that's consumed most of my attention as of late.\n最近这个话题占据了我绝大部分的注意力。"

    old "Could this be the key to stopping the creation of new undead?"
    new "Could this be the key to stopping the creation of new undead?\n这会不会是阻止新不死生物被制造出来的关键？"

    old "Unlikely. This method of salting the earth only seems to be effective in the case of blood rituals. Some vampires are apparently able to exert their powers through other means, like incantations and other methods we have yet to understand. This method has fairly narrow applications."
    new "Unlikely. This method of salting the earth only seems to be effective in the case of blood rituals. Some vampires are apparently able to exert their powers through other means, like incantations and other methods we have yet to understand. This method has fairly narrow applications.\n不太可能。这种撒盐的方法似乎只在血祭仪式上有效。有些吸血鬼显然能通过其他手段施展力量，比如咒语，以及其他我们尚未了解的方法。这种方法的适用范围相当窄。"

    old "Well, we'll take several bags of salt, just in case."
    new "Well, we'll take several bags of salt, just in case.\n好吧，我们多带几袋盐，以防万一。"

    old "Please do."
    new "Please do.\n请务必带上。"

    old "Excellent work, [protag]. The undead are growing less and less numerous."
    new "Excellent work, [protag]. The undead are growing less and less numerous.\n干得漂亮，[protag]。不死生物越来越少了。"

    old "Let's not celebrate too early."
    new "Let's not celebrate too early.\n别高兴得太早。"

    old "Of course, of course. We don't want to be punished for a moment of carelessness. Let's stay vigilant."
    new "Of course, of course. We don't want to be punished for a moment of carelessness. Let's stay vigilant.\n当然，当然。我们可不想因一时疏忽而受惩罚。保持警惕吧。"

    old "It's not just that. If the undead were planning to break off their attack, don't you think they would have done it by now? It's obvious that our side is winning. They're not going to penetrate the city by continuing to fling lesser zombies at us."
    new "It's not just that. If the undead were planning to break off their attack, don't you think they would have done it by now? It's obvious that our side is winning. They're not going to penetrate the city by continuing to fling lesser zombies at us.\n还不止如此。如果不死生物打算中止进攻，你不觉得他们早就该这么做了吗？显然是我们这边在占上风。他们光靠不断朝我们抛来低等僵尸，是攻不进城的。"

    old "So why do they persist in their attack? It makes no sense for them to continue unless they think they have some way of punching a hole in our defenses."
    new "So why do they persist in their attack? It makes no sense for them to continue unless they think they have some way of punching a hole in our defenses.\n那他们为什么还坚持进攻？除非他们认为自己有办法在防线上撕开个口子，否则继续下去毫无道理。"

    old "I see what you mean. Could it be that they're simply growing desperate?"
    new "I see what you mean. Could it be that they're simply growing desperate?\n我明白你的意思。会不会他们只是变得狗急跳墙了？"

    old "Desperation is not a term I'd expect most vampires to be familiar with. Undead creatures that live for hundreds of years don't feel much sense of urgency. If they thought they were losing this fight, they could break it off, and then try again in a month. Or a year, in fact."
    new "Desperation is not a term I'd expect most vampires to be familiar with. Undead creatures that live for hundreds of years don't feel much sense of urgency. If they thought they were losing this fight, they could break it off, and then try again in a month. Or a year, in fact.\n“狗急跳墙”这个词，我可不认为大多数吸血鬼会熟悉。活了几百年的不死生物，没有多少紧迫感。如果他们觉得自己打不赢，大可以收兵，过一个月再试，甚至一年之后再试。"

    old "Based on the information available to us directly, we think that we're winning the battle. But for their attack to continue like this, they must think that they're winning the battle. I imagine we've come to different conclusions because we have different sets of information. So the question is, what do they know that we don't?"
    new "Based on the information available to us directly, we think that we're winning the battle. But for their attack to continue like this, they must think that they're winning the battle. I imagine we've come to different conclusions because we have different sets of information. So the question is, what do they know that we don't?\n根据我们直接掌握的信息，我们认为我们正赢得这场战斗。但他们的进攻能这样持续下去，说明他们必定认为自己才是在赢。我想，我们得出不同结论，是因为我们掌握的信息不同。那么问题来了：他们知道些什么我们不知道的？"

    old "You think they have a trick up their sleeve."
    new "You think they have a trick up their sleeve.\n你觉得他们还有后手。"

    old "Yes, I'm all but certain of it."
    new "Yes, I'm all but certain of it.\n是的，我几乎可以肯定。"

    old "In that case, you and your party should stay close to the city in case they spring some kind of surprise on us."
    new "In that case, you and your party should stay close to the city in case they spring some kind of surprise on us.\n那样的话，你和你的队伍应该待在城市附近，以防他们给我们来个突然袭击。"

    old "I think that 'surprise' may already be arriving."
    new "I think that 'surprise' may already be arriving.\n我想那个“突袭”可能已经来了。"

    old "I look at the horizon. For a moment, it appears that there's a break in the ranks of the undead shambling across the plains to the city gates. But now, it becomes apparent that the undead are still coming. Only now, they're rising from the ground."
    new "I look at the horizon. For a moment, it appears that there's a break in the ranks of the undead shambling across the plains to the city gates. But now, it becomes apparent that the undead are still coming. Only now, they're rising from the ground.\n我望向地平线。有那么一刻，似乎蹒跚穿过平原涌向城门的不死大军出现了缺口。但现在，显而易见，不死生物仍在涌来。只是这一次，它们是从地底升起来的。"

    old "Tighten the perimeter!"
    new "Tighten the perimeter!\n收紧防线！"

    old "I spot a figure brandishing a metal blade. There's no mistake: it's a vampire. Maybe even the same vampire that is dragging the waves of undead from the ground."
    new "I spot a figure brandishing a metal blade. There's no mistake: it's a vampire. Maybe even the same vampire that is dragging the waves of undead from the ground.\n我发现一个挥舞着金属利刃的身影。没错，那是个吸血鬼。也许正是那个把一波波不死生物从地底拖出来的吸血鬼。"

    old "That vampire must be their commander. If they even have commanders."
    new "That vampire must be their commander. If they even have commanders.\n那个吸血鬼一定就是他们的指挥官——如果他们真有指挥官的话。"

    old "[protag], do you think that you can fight her directly?"
    new "[protag], do you think that you can fight her directly?\n[protag]，你觉得你能直接和她对战吗？"

    old "I'll try. But I'll need your men to spread out and deal with the undead around us. The worst possible thing would be for me to confront her and then get flanked."
    new "I'll try. But I'll need your men to spread out and deal with the undead around us. The worst possible thing would be for me to confront her and then get flanked.\n我试试。但我需要你的弟兄们散开，去对付我们周围的不死生物。最糟的情况，就是我正面对上她，然后被人从侧翼包抄。"

    old "Done. Squadrons A and D, enter formation two!"
    new "Done. Squadrons A and D, enter formation two!\n完毕。A、D中队，进入二号编队！"

    old "The soldiers surround us, forming a sort of protective barrier around my group."
    new "The soldiers surround us, forming a sort of protective barrier around my group.\n士兵们把我们围在中间，在我方队伍四周形成一道保护屏障。"

    old "Captain Thomas. If this vampire commander is responsible for summoning these waves of undead, then their power must surely be finite. I'm not sure when it will run out, but this battle may simply prove to be a test of survival."
    new "Captain Thomas. If this vampire commander is responsible for summoning these waves of undead, then their power must surely be finite. I'm not sure when it will run out, but this battle may simply prove to be a test of survival.\nThomas队长。如果这个吸血鬼指挥官正是召唤这一波波不死生物的人，那他们的力量必定是有限的。我不确定它何时会耗尽，但这场战斗或许终究只是一场生存考验。"

    old "Attrition."
    new "Attrition.\n消耗战。"

    old "This could be a battle of attrition, or I might be able to find an opening and end it quickly. But be aware that you may have to have your men protecting me for quite awhile."
    new "This could be a battle of attrition, or I might be able to find an opening and end it quickly. But be aware that you may have to have your men protecting me for quite awhile.\n这可能是一场消耗战，也可能我能找到破绽，迅速结束战斗。但你要有心理准备，你的弟兄们可能得保护我相当长一段时间。"

    old "Don't worry. Leave that to us. You concentrate on the vampire."
    new "Don't worry. Leave that to us. You concentrate on the vampire.\n别担心。交给我们。你专心对付那个吸血鬼。"

    old "I step forward to confront the vampire commander directly."
    new "I step forward to confront the vampire commander directly.\n我上前一步，直接迎向那个吸血鬼指挥官。"

    old "It's you."
    new "It's you.\n是你。"

    old "You're the one who was at the castle last moon. You've been quite a pain in my side."
    new "You're the one who was at the castle last moon. You've been quite a pain in my side.\n你就是上个月圆时闯进城堡的那个人。你一直让我很头疼。"

    old "In fact, I think you're the one to blame for the disappearance of [i] of my lieutenants."
    new "In fact, I think you're the one to blame for the disappearance of [i] of my lieutenants.\n事实上，我想我的[i]个副官的失踪，都得算在你头上。"

    old "I guess that would make you the captain, then."
    new "I guess that would make you the captain, then.\n那我猜，你就是他们的队长了。"

    old "Are we exchanging names? I was a bit curious to find out who it was exactly that was making my life difficult. And in case you're curious as to who it is that's about to end your pitiful life, I'm Captain Hersilia."
    new "Are we exchanging names? I was a bit curious to find out who it was exactly that was making my life difficult. And in case you're curious as to who it is that's about to end your pitiful life, I'm Captain Hersilia.\n我们这是在互通姓名吗？我倒是有点好奇，究竟是哪个家伙让我的日子这么难过。而万一你想知道，即将结束你这条可怜小命的究竟是谁——我是Hersilia队长。"

    old "Well, Captain Hersilia, I'm [protag], emissary of Grimoire, and if you think I'm the one who will be dead at the end of this encounter, I think you're in for a rude awakening."
    new "Well, Captain Hersilia, I'm [protag], emissary of Grimoire, and if you think I'm the one who will be dead at the end of this encounter, I think you're in for a rude awakening.\n好吧，Hersilia队长，我是[protag]，Grimoire的使者。如果你以为这场交锋结束时倒下的人会是我，那我想，你可得好好被惊醒一次了。"

    old "Know your place, mortal. We could talk all day, but I think once we start trading blows, you'll regret your insolence."
    new "Know your place, mortal. We could talk all day, but I think once we start trading blows, you'll regret your insolence.\n认清你的本分吧，凡人。我们可以聊上一整天，但我想，一旦我们开始交手，你就会为自己的无礼后悔。"

    old "Not bad, [protag], not bad. I didn't expect you to last so long. But you can't go on forever!"
    new "Not bad, [protag], not bad. I didn't expect you to last so long. But you can't go on forever!\n不错嘛，[protag]，不错嘛。我没想到你能撑这么久。但你可没法永远撑下去！"

    old "Hersilia laughs as more undead rise from the ground! She has much more power than I thought."
    new "Hersilia laughs as more undead rise from the ground! She has much more power than I thought.\nHersilia大笑起来，更多不死生物从地底升起！她的力量远超我的想象。"

    old "However, I notice that takes a lot of efforts for her to summon the undead. She looks...weaker. The undead look weaker too. Maybe we can still win this fight."
    new "However, I notice that takes a lot of efforts for her to summon the undead. She looks...weaker. The undead look weaker too. Maybe we can still win this fight.\n不过，我注意到她召唤不死生物颇为吃力。她看起来……更虚弱了。那些不死生物看起来也变弱了。也许这场战斗我们仍有胜算。"

    old "Suddenly, I remember about the Valery's blood vial I have with me. According to Zachary and Valery, it's very pure and undead will be attracted to it like bees on honey."
    new "Suddenly, I remember about the Valery's blood vial I have with me. According to Zachary and Valery, it's very pure and undead will be attracted to it like bees on honey.\n突然，我想起身上还带着那瓶Valery的血。据Zachary和Valery说，那血十分纯净，不死生物会像蜜蜂扑向蜂蜜一样被它吸引。"

    old "I grab the vial and throw it on the ground, away from Hersilia. Zachary was right: all the undead around her start running towards it, unable to resist the call of pure blood."
    new "I grab the vial and throw it on the ground, away from Hersilia. Zachary was right: all the undead around her start running towards it, unable to resist the call of pure blood.\n我抓起瓶子，把它扔在远离Hersilia的地上。Zachary说得没错：她身边所有的不死生物都开始朝它冲去，无法抗拒纯净血液的召唤。"

    old "What there was in that vial!? How did you do it?!"
    new "What there was in that vial!? How did you do it?!\n那瓶子里装的是什么？！你是怎么做到的？！"

    old "I'm a [manwoman] full of surprises. Now, die!"
    new "I'm a [manwoman] full of surprises. Now, die!\n我是个浑身是惊喜的[manwoman]。现在，去死吧！"

    old "<screech>"
    new "<screech>\n<screech>"

    old "Hersilia lets out a scream as her body starts to dissolve. In an instant, the undead around us—ghouls, zombies, and skeletons alike—all seem to collapse to the ground, motionless sacks of flesh and bones."
    new "Hersilia lets out a scream as her body starts to dissolve. In an instant, the undead around us—ghouls, zombies, and skeletons alike—all seem to collapse to the ground, motionless sacks of flesh and bones.\n随着身体开始消解，Hersilia发出一声尖叫。刹那间，我们周围的不死生物——食尸鬼、僵尸、骷髅，全都瘫倒在地，成了一堆堆了无生气的血肉与骸骨。"

    old "Is it over?"
    new "Is it over?\n结束了吗？"

    old "Cheers erupt from around us as men raise their weapons over their heads in triumph. It seems the battle is won."
    new "Cheers erupt from around us as men raise their weapons over their heads in triumph. It seems the battle is won.\n四周爆发出欢呼声，人们高举武器庆祝胜利。看来这场战斗打赢了。"

    old "The soldiers stay in formation, just in case another wave comes, but it seems that the attack has truly come to an end."
    new "The soldiers stay in formation, just in case another wave comes, but it seems that the attack has truly come to an end.\n士兵们仍保持着队形，以防再来一波进攻，但看来这场攻势确实已经结束。"

    old "I walk over to Hersilia's remains. Her body, having crumbled to dust moments before, has already blown away in the wind. All that remains is her sword."
    new "I walk over to Hersilia's remains. Her body, having crumbled to dust moments before, has already blown away in the wind. All that remains is her sword.\n我走到Hersilia的遗骸旁。她的躯体片刻前已化为尘土，此刻早已随风飘散。剩下的，只有她的剑。"

    old "I reach down to grab the sword."
    new "I reach down to grab the sword.\n我俯身去捡那把剑。"

    old "The sword vibrates in my hand, as if reacting to my touch with some kind of magical force. For a moment, I hear a voice in my ear, almost as if the sword is speaking to me, and I yelp and drop the sword in surprise."
    new "The sword vibrates in my hand, as if reacting to my touch with some kind of magical force. For a moment, I hear a voice in my ear, almost as if the sword is speaking to me, and I yelp and drop the sword in surprise.\n剑在我手中震颤，仿佛用某种魔法力量回应着我的触碰。有那么一瞬，我耳边响起一个声音，几乎就像剑在对我说话，我惊叫一声，把剑丢在了地上。"

    old "Captain Thomas walks over and examines the sword."
    new "Captain Thomas walks over and examines the sword.\nThomas队长走过来，端详起那把剑。"

    old "That's all that's left of her?"
    new "That's all that's left of her?\n她就剩下这点东西了？"

    old "Thomas reaches down to grab the sword, and fliches away."
    new "Thomas reaches down to grab the sword, and fliches away.\nThomas俯身去捡那把剑，又猛地缩回了手。"

    old "It's burning hot!"
    new "It's burning hot!\n它烫得厉害！"

    old "I reach down and grab the sword again."
    new "I reach down and grab the sword again.\n我再次俯身捡起那把剑。"

    old "How are you doing that?"
    new "How are you doing that?\n你是怎么做到的？"

    old "The sword seems to be reacting to me differently than it does to Thomas. Could it be recognizing something in me?"
    new "The sword seems to be reacting to me differently than it does to Thomas. Could it be recognizing something in me?\n这把剑对我的反应，似乎与对Thomas的不同。它会不会是在我身上认出了什么？"

    old "I hear a voice in my ear."
    new "I hear a voice in my ear.\n我耳边响起一个声音。"

    old "Are you my new master?"
    new "Are you my new master?\n你是我的新主人吗？"

    old "Hear what?"
    new "Hear what?\n听见什么？"

    old "I thought...I thought I heard a voice just now."
    new "I thought...I thought I heard a voice just now.\n我刚刚……我刚刚好像听见了一个声音。"

    old "Someone calling out to you? Well, there are a lot of people out here. Someone might have called your name."
    new "Someone calling out to you? Well, there are a lot of people out here. Someone might have called your name.\n有人在喊你？嗯，这里人很多。也许有人喊了你的名字。"

    old "It seems the voice is speaking only to me."
    new "It seems the voice is speaking only to me.\n看来那个声音只对我一个人说话。"

    old "Ah, you're not worthy, not yet! You're far too ripe. But one day...one day. Hold onto me, neonate. I think you and I may do great things together."
    new "Ah, you're not worthy, not yet! You're far too ripe. But one day...one day. Hold onto me, neonate. I think you and I may do great things together.\n啊，你还不配，还没到时候！你还太嫩了。但总有一天……总有一天。抓紧我吧，初生者。我想，你和我联手，将来也许能干出一番大事。"

    old "The sword...the sword is talking to me?"
    new "The sword...the sword is talking to me?\n这把剑……这把剑在跟我说话？"

    old "I whisper, trying to speak to it."
    new "I whisper, trying to speak to it.\n我低声细语，试图与它对话。"

    old "Neonate?"
    new "Neonate?\n初生者？"

    old "You haven't even turned yet. Why, you're barely initiated. The day approaches, and I grow weary of speaking. Call on me again when the moon is full."
    new "You haven't even turned yet. Why, you're barely initiated. The day approaches, and I grow weary of speaking. Call on me again when the moon is full.\n你甚至还没有转化。哎呀，你才刚刚入门。天快亮了，我也说累了。等月亮再圆时，再来召唤我吧。"

    old "Wait! I—"
    new "Wait! I—\n等等！我——"

    old "The sun starts to peak over the horizon, and the sword that was vibrating in my hand moments earlier becomes still."
    new "The sun starts to peak over the horizon, and the sword that was vibrating in my hand moments earlier becomes still.\n太阳开始从地平线探出头来，方才还在我手中震颤的剑，此刻归于静止。"

    old "This sword might be the source of the vampire captain's powers. It's clearly only meant to be wielded by other vampires. But I suppose I am one, too. A 'neonate,' as the sword called me."
    new "This sword might be the source of the vampire captain's powers. It's clearly only meant to be wielded by other vampires. But I suppose I am one, too. A 'neonate,' as the sword called me.\n这把剑也许就是那吸血鬼队长的力量之源。它显然只该由其他吸血鬼来使用。但我想，我也是其中之一——就像这把剑称呼我的那样，一个“初生者”。"

    old "I suppose that sword should, by all rights, be yours. Finders keepers, and you've more than earned it. Besides, I haven't the fortitude to hold such a thing."
    new "I suppose that sword should, by all rights, be yours. Finders keepers, and you've more than earned it. Besides, I haven't the fortitude to hold such a thing.\n我想，那把剑按理说该归你。谁捡到算谁的，何况你早已当之无愧。再说了，我可没那个胆魄去碰这样的东西。"

    old "I tuck the sword away."
    new "I tuck the sword away.\n我把剑收了起来。"

    old "The sword shudders for a moment under my touch, and I feel a burning sensation. I rip my hand away reflexively."
    new "The sword shudders for a moment under my touch, and I feel a burning sensation. I rip my hand away reflexively.\n剑在我触碰下颤抖了一瞬，我感到一阵灼烧。我本能地把手缩了回来。"

    old "What's wrong?"
    new "What's wrong?\n怎么了？"

    old "I lean down closer to the sword."
    new "I lean down closer to the sword.\n我凑近那把剑。"

    old "It appears to be pulsing with some kind of dark energy."
    new "It appears to be pulsing with some kind of dark energy.\n它似乎正随着某种黑暗能量脉动。"

    old "Ah, the vampire is dead, but some of her magic might still be in this sword. I'll make sure that we deal with this properly. This seems like work for mages to deal with. You can let us handle this."
    new "Ah, the vampire is dead, but some of her magic might still be in this sword. I'll make sure that we deal with this properly. This seems like work for mages to deal with. You can let us handle this.\n啊，吸血鬼死了，但她的一些魔法可能还残留在这把剑里。我会确保妥善处理。这看来该交给法师们处理。你可以把这事交给我们。"

    old "You probably have a report to deliver, don't you?"
    new "You probably have a report to deliver, don't you?\n你大概还有报告要交吧，不是吗？"

    old "Ah, that's right. The council will want a meeting."
    new "Ah, that's right. The council will want a meeting.\n啊，对。议会会想召见我的。"

    old "Well, I don't mean to chase you away, but you probably shouldn't keep them waiting. You'll have to celebrate later."
    new "Well, I don't mean to chase you away, but you probably shouldn't keep them waiting. You'll have to celebrate later.\n嗯，我不是要赶你走，但你大概不该让他们久等。庆功得留到之后再说了。"

    old "I certainly will try to make time for a proper celebration."
    new "I certainly will try to make time for a proper celebration.\n我一定会设法腾出时间，好好庆祝一番。"

    old "Apolimesho greets me at the door to the council chambers."
    new "Apolimesho greets me at the door to the council chambers.\nApolimesho在议会厅门口迎接我。"

    old "Well done, [protag]. You've done it again."
    new "Well done, [protag]. You've done it again.\n干得漂亮，[protag]。你又做到了。"

    old "I'm proud to have done my part in winning this battle."
    new "I'm proud to have done my part in winning this battle.\n能在赢得这场战斗中尽一份力，我很自豪。"

    old "Words aren't adequate to express the heroism you've shown on this day."
    new "Words aren't adequate to express the heroism you've shown on this day.\n言语不足以表达你今日展现出的英雄气概。"

    old "There were many soldiers defending the city last night. They fought just as hard as I did, and many of them suffered injuries far greater than my own. The victory belongs to them, not me."
    new "There were many soldiers defending the city last night. They fought just as hard as I did, and many of them suffered injuries far greater than my own. The victory belongs to them, not me.\n昨晚守城的士兵有很多。他们和我一样奋力拼杀，其中许多人的伤势远比我重。胜利属于他们，而不是我。"

    old "You're far too humble, [protag]. But that's also one of your best qualities."
    new "You're far too humble, [protag]. But that's also one of your best qualities.\n你实在太谦虚了，[protag]。不过，这也是你最可贵的品质之一。"

    old "I wish we had more time, but the council wants to speak with you immediately."
    new "I wish we had more time, but the council wants to speak with you immediately.\n我多希望时间能更充裕，但议会想立刻与你谈谈。"

    old "[protag]. You've done well in serving the interests of our domain."
    new "[protag]. You've done well in serving the interests of our domain.\n[protag]。你在为我们领地的利益效劳这件事上，做得很好。"

    old "Today was an important battle. We've proved our mettle against the vampire's attack. We've proved our superior strength."
    new "Today was an important battle. We've proved our mettle against the vampire's attack. We've proved our superior strength.\n今天是一场重要的战斗。面对吸血鬼的进攻，我们证明了自己的胆识，也证明了我们更胜一筹的力量。"

    old "The council has unilaterally decided that now is the time to turn this defensive success into an aggressive assault on castle N'Mar."
    new "The council has unilaterally decided that now is the time to turn this defensive success into an aggressive assault on castle N'Mar.\n议会已一致决定，现在正是把这场防守胜利转化为对N'Mar城堡主动进攻的时候。"

    old "Happening when?"
    new "Happening when?\n什么时候行动？"

    old "On the next full moon. One month from now."
    new "On the next full moon. One month from now.\n下个满月。也就是一个月后。"

    old "One month from now, then. Strike before they have a chance to rebuild their ranks. They've suffered losses, and we should take advantage of that."
    new "One month from now, then. Strike before they have a chance to rebuild their ranks. They've suffered losses, and we should take advantage of that.\n那就一个月后。趁他们还没机会重整旗鼓，先发制人。他们遭受了损失，我们应当抓住这一点。"

    old "That was our exact line of thinking."
    new "That was our exact line of thinking.\n这正是我们的思路。"

    old "One month? I question whether this city will really be ready for such an offensive in one month's time."
    new "One month? I question whether this city will really be ready for such an offensive in one month's time.\n一个月？我怀疑这座城市是否真的能在短短一个月内准备好发动这样的攻势。"

    old "We have already begun preparations."
    new "We have already begun preparations.\n我们已经开始筹备了。"

    old "There are men who have yet to return to their homes after the battle we just fought, and you've already made the decision to attack castle N'Mar. That must have been a very quick deliberation."
    new "There are men who have yet to return to their homes after the battle we just fought, and you've already made the decision to attack castle N'Mar. That must have been a very quick deliberation.\n刚刚打完这一仗，还有士兵没来得及回家，你们就已经决定攻打N'Mar城堡了。这番商议想必十分迅速。"

    old "Or there wasn't a deliberation at all. You made the decision to attack castle N'Mar before the battle at the city gates was even fought."
    new "Or there wasn't a deliberation at all. You made the decision to attack castle N'Mar before the battle at the city gates was even fought.\n又或者根本就没商议。在城门之战打响之前，你们就已经做出了攻打N'Mar城堡的决定。"

    old "Is that an objection?"
    new "Is that an objection?\n这是在表示反对吗？"

    old "If the council formulated plans with the assumption that we would win the battle as we did, that is quite an arrogant assumption to make."
    new "If the council formulated plans with the assumption that we would win the battle as we did, that is quite an arrogant assumption to make.\n如果议会是在假定我们能如此这般赢得战斗的前提下制定的计划，那这假定未免也太自负了。"

    old "Well, if you assumed we were going to win, it's a reasonable assumption to make. As one of the people who fought tonight, I appreciate your confidence in our ability to bring the city victory over the undead."
    new "Well, if you assumed we were going to win, it's a reasonable assumption to make. As one of the people who fought tonight, I appreciate your confidence in our ability to bring the city victory over the undead.\n嗯，如果你们假定我们会赢，那倒是个合理的假定。作为今晚参战的一员，我很感谢你们对我们战胜不死生物、为城市带来胜利的能力抱有信心。"

    old "The council is not so arrogant as to presume that we would win the battle. We had multiple contigencies, [protag]. We have had since the last full moon to develop plans on our next course of action."
    new "The council is not so arrogant as to presume that we would win the battle. We had multiple contigencies, [protag]. We have had since the last full moon to develop plans on our next course of action.\n议会还不至于自负到认定我们必赢。[protag]，我们准备了多套应急方案。自上个满月以来，我们一直在制定下一步行动的计划。"

    old "Our decision just now was simply a matter of determining which outcome had occurred so we would know which plan to follow. Had we lost the battle, we would be enacting a different set of plans."
    new "Our decision just now was simply a matter of determining which outcome had occurred so we would know which plan to follow. Had we lost the battle, we would be enacting a different set of plans.\n我们刚才的决定，不过是确定出现了哪种结果，好知道该执行哪套方案。若我们战败，就会启动另一套计划。"

    old "And you didn't include me in this planning."
    new "And you didn't include me in this planning.\n而你们没让我参与这些筹划。"

    old "You had your hands full with other matters. We didn't want to burden you with contemplating various possibilities of what might or might not happen."
    new "You had your hands full with other matters. We didn't want to burden you with contemplating various possibilities of what might or might not happen.\n你手头还有其他事忙得不可开交。我们不想再让你费神去琢磨种种可能发生或不会发生的情形。"

    old "You've called me here for a reason, I presume."
    new "You've called me here for a reason, I presume.\n我猜，你们把我叫来是有原因的。"

    old "Yes. We want you to help spearhead the assault on castle N'Mar in one month's time."
    new "Yes. We want you to help spearhead the assault on castle N'Mar in one month's time.\n是的。我们想让你帮忙牵头，一个月后对N'Mar城堡发起进攻。"

    old "You'd also be involved with the preparation as well."
    new "You'd also be involved with the preparation as well.\n你也将参与筹备工作。"

    old "Our plan involves the procurement of some resources from various neighboring cities. Of course, the responsibility of facilitating negotiations would fall on the council's emissary, a title that is still yours, should you choose to continue serving."
    new "Our plan involves the procurement of some resources from various neighboring cities. Of course, the responsibility of facilitating negotiations would fall on the council's emissary, a title that is still yours, should you choose to continue serving.\n我们的计划涉及从邻近各城采购一些资源。当然，促成谈判的责任要落到议会使者的肩上，而这个头衔仍属于你——只要你愿意继续效劳。"

    old "I suppose I should have expected this. We've come this far, but the battle won't be over until the evil lurking within castle N'Mar's walls is dealt with once and for all."
    new "I suppose I should have expected this. We've come this far, but the battle won't be over until the evil lurking within castle N'Mar's walls is dealt with once and for all.\n我想我早该料到。我们已走到这一步，但除非潜伏在N'Mar城堡墙内的邪恶被彻底铲除，否则战斗不会结束。"

    old "We've come this far. It won't end until we've gone all the way."
    new "We've come this far. It won't end until we've gone all the way.\n我们已走到这一步。不走到尽头，一切就不会结束。"

    old "We're glad to hear it. Apolimesho will continue to act as your handler. Meet with him to discuss your assignments in greater detail when you have the opportunity. In the meantime, I suggest that you get well-rested. You look exhausted."
    new "We're glad to hear it. Apolimesho will continue to act as your handler. Meet with him to discuss your assignments in greater detail when you have the opportunity. In the meantime, I suggest that you get well-rested. You look exhausted.\n听到你这么说，我们很高兴。Apolimesho将继续担任你的联络人。有机会时去找他，更详细地讨论你的各项任务。在此期间，我建议你好好休息。你看上去疲惫不堪。"

    old "Thank you. I think that I'm going to take a long sleep."
    new "Thank you. I think that I'm going to take a long sleep.\n谢谢。我想我要好好睡上一大觉。"

    old "I'll be waiting here when you're ready."
    new "I'll be waiting here when you're ready.\n等你准备好了，我会在这里等你。"

    old "Hey [protag], we kicked undead asses once again."
    new "Hey [protag], we kicked undead asses once again.\n嘿，[protag]，我们又狠狠教训了不死生物一顿。"

    old "Haha, indeed we did! Thank you for your help, Sylrissa."
    new "Haha, indeed we did! Thank you for your help, Sylrissa.\n哈哈，确实如此！谢谢你的帮助，Sylrissa。"

    old "Thank you for the help, Enok."
    new "Thank you for the help, Enok.\n谢谢你的帮助，Enok。"

    old "You're welcome. But truth to be told, I'm happy it's over."
    new "You're welcome. But truth to be told, I'm happy it's over.\n不客气。不过说真的，我很高兴这一切结束了。"

    old "You didn't look tired while fighting."
    new "You didn't look tired while fighting.\n你战斗时看起来一点也不累。"

    old "Oh no, not because of that. I can't wait to get back in the swamps to try some new cooking recipes!"
    new "Oh no, not because of that. I can't wait to get back in the swamps to try some new cooking recipes!\n哦不，不是因为这个。我是等不及要回沼泽去，试试几道新的烹饪食谱！"

    old "Haha, good, maybe I'll come visit you to try them then."
    new "Haha, good, maybe I'll come visit you to try them then.\n哈哈，好，也许到时我会去看你，尝尝那些菜。"

    old "Leena. Once again your help was invaluable."
    new "Leena. Once again your help was invaluable.\nLeena。你的帮助再一次显得弥足珍贵。"

    old "Thank you. I have to say that we built a good team. Everyone is...very motivated."
    new "Thank you. I have to say that we built a good team. Everyone is...very motivated.\n谢谢。我得说，我们组建了一支好队伍。每个人都……干劲十足。"

    old "And this is all your merit, [protag]. Remember it."
    new "And this is all your merit, [protag]. Remember it.\n而这都是你的功劳，[protag]。记住这一点。"

    old "Hey Jasper, you did a good job tonight."
    new "Hey Jasper, you did a good job tonight.\n嘿，Jasper，你今晚干得不错。"

    old "Why, you had any doubts about it?"
    new "Why, you had any doubts about it?\n怎么，你对此还有过怀疑？"

    old "Jasper winks at me."
    new "Jasper winks at me.\nJasper朝我眨了眨眼。"

    old "You know? You need to work on your modesty. Jokes apart, thank you again."
    new "You know? You need to work on your modesty. Jokes apart, thank you again.\n你知道吗？你可得好好改改你这不谦虚的毛病。玩笑归玩笑，再次谢谢你。"

    old "[protag], I'm going back in the desert but wanted to thank you first."
    new "[protag], I'm going back in the desert but wanted to thank you first.\n[protag]，我要回沙漠去了，但想先谢谢你。"

    old "I should be the one to thank you, Nuala."
    new "I should be the one to thank you, Nuala.\n该道谢的人是我，Nuala。"

    old "If you want to thank me, maybe you could come visit me again? I would like to spend more time with you."
    new "If you want to thank me, maybe you could come visit me again? I would like to spend more time with you.\n如果你想谢我，也许可以再来看看我？我想多和你待些时间。"

    old "I'm sure I'll find the time! Good night, Nuala."
    new "I'm sure I'll find the time! Good night, Nuala.\n我一定会抽出时间的！晚安，Nuala。"

    old "I have to congratulate with you, [protag]. You made the right choices and lead us to victory tonight."
    new "I have to congratulate with you, [protag]. You made the right choices and lead us to victory tonight.\n我得向你道贺，[protag]。你做出了正确的抉择，带领我们赢得了今晚的胜利。"

    old "Thank you, Larik. Coming from an experienced leader like you, it's a great compliment."
    new "Thank you, Larik. Coming from an experienced leader like you, it's a great compliment.\n谢谢你，Larik。出自你这样经验丰富的领袖之口，这是很高的赞誉。"

    old "Thank gods Grimoire didn't fall."
    new "Thank gods Grimoire didn't fall.\n谢天谢地，Grimoire没有陷落。"

    old "Yes, that would have been a disaster. All the people in here..."
    new "Yes, that would have been a disaster. All the people in here...\n是啊，那会是一场灾难。这里的所有人……"

    old "Thank you for bringing me with you. I couldn't just stand and watch while my new home was threatened like this."
    new "Thank you for bringing me with you. I couldn't just stand and watch while my new home was threatened like this.\n谢谢你带上我。当我的新家受到这样的威胁时，我无法只是袖手旁观。"

    old "Good job tonight, [protag]."
    new "Good job tonight, [protag].\n今晚干得漂亮，[protag]。"

    old "Thank you, Kusho. I can say the same to you."
    new "Thank you, Kusho. I can say the same to you.\n谢谢你，Kusho。你也不遑多让。"

    old "But let's not relax. I have fear that the biggest battle is yet to come. Goodnight, [protag]."
    new "But let's not relax. I have fear that the biggest battle is yet to come. Goodnight, [protag].\n但我们别松懈。我担心最大的战役还没到来。晚安，[protag]。"

    old "[protag]! Tonight was such an epic battle!"
    new "[protag]! Tonight was such an epic battle!\n[protag]！今晚真是一场史诗般的战斗！"

    old "You enjoyed it, it seems."
    new "You enjoyed it, it seems.\n看来你很享受。"

    old "Yes, I hate to say it, but I really liked fighting tonight. The best thing was that we fought undead, so I don't feel guilty for all the destruction I did."
    new "Yes, I hate to say it, but I really liked fighting tonight. The best thing was that we fought undead, so I don't feel guilty for all the destruction I did.\n是啊，虽然我不想承认，但我真的很喜欢今晚的战斗。最好的一点是，我们打的是不死生物，所以我对自己的大肆破坏毫无愧疚。"

    old "You're welcome, Galan!"
    new "You're welcome, Galan!\n不客气，Galan！"

    old "Dasyra? You look worried. What's up?"
    new "Dasyra? You look worried. What's up?\nDasyra？你看起来很担心。怎么了？"

    old "I was thinking what would have happened if we lost tonight. All the people in Grimoire, all the kids..."
    new "I was thinking what would have happened if we lost tonight. All the people in Grimoire, all the kids...\n我一直在想，要是今晚我们输了会怎样。Grimoire里的所有人，所有的孩子……"

    old "But we didn't lose."
    new "But we didn't lose.\n但我们没有输。"

    old "Yes, you're right. Maybe I should stop worrying and focus on the positive results we got!"
    new "Yes, you're right. Maybe I should stop worrying and focus on the positive results we got!\n是的，你说得对。也许我该停止担心，把注意力放在我们取得的积极成果上！"

    old "You should, Dasyra. Good night!"
    new "You should, Dasyra. Good night!\n你应该这样，Dasyra。晚安！"

    old "Hey, [protag]?"
    new "Hey, [protag]?\n嘿，[protag]？"

    old "You two again? It's kinda creepy."
    new "You two again? It's kinda creepy.\n又是你们俩？有点吓人啊。"

    old "My my. We're here only to thank you."
    new "My my. We're here only to thank you.\n哎呀呀。我们只是来谢谢你的。"

    old "The night has come. Tonight, we're going to conquer N'Mar."
    new "The night has come. Tonight, we're going to conquer N'Mar.\n夜幕已降临。今晚，我们要攻下N'Mar。"

    old "Senya and her pirate cohorts are leading the attack by sea. I can hear the sound of the ship cannons as they bombard N'Mar. The cannons aren't very accurate, but they'll manage to thin the undead ranks for sure. The vampires too. Even if they're undead, getting hit by a cannon ball ought to deal them some damage."
    new "Senya and her pirate cohorts are leading the attack by sea. I can hear the sound of the ship cannons as they bombard N'Mar. The cannons aren't very accurate, but they'll manage to thin the undead ranks for sure. The vampires too. Even if they're undead, getting hit by a cannon ball ought to deal them some damage.\nSenya和她的海盗同伙正从海上发起进攻。我能听见舰炮轰击N'Mar的声音。那些炮不算精准，但肯定能削薄不死大军的阵线，对吸血鬼也一样。即便他们是不死之身，挨上一发炮弹也该受点损伤。"

    old "The Empire soldiers shows their shiny steel weapons and armor. As they charge into battle, I see how much quicker their movements are. Supporting Lady Geraldine was probably a good idea."
    new "The Empire soldiers shows their shiny steel weapons and armor. As they charge into battle, I see how much quicker their movements are. Supporting Lady Geraldine was probably a good idea.\n帝国士兵们亮出锃亮的钢制武器和铠甲。当他们冲锋陷阵时，我看得出他们的动作敏捷了多少。支持Geraldine夫人也许是个好主意。"

    old "The Empire soldiers follow the veterans' orders and execute tactical maneuvers to take advantage of the terrain surrounding N'Mar. Even with the fog, the veterans experience proves invaluable in this fight. Sir Cedric was right, experience matters more than weapons and armor ever could."
    new "The Empire soldiers follow the veterans' orders and execute tactical maneuvers to take advantage of the terrain surrounding N'Mar. Even with the fog, the veterans experience proves invaluable in this fight. Sir Cedric was right, experience matters more than weapons and armor ever could.\n帝国士兵们听从老兵们的号令，执行战术机动，利用N'Mar周围的地形。即便有雾，老兵们的经验在这场战斗中依然弥足珍贵。Cedric爵士说得对，经验远比武器和铠甲更重要。"

    old "Of course, the Grand Mogul of Dingirra offered his help again, by sending more merchants to sell things to our army. I swear that those people have money flowing in their veins instead of blood."
    new "Of course, the Grand Mogul of Dingirra offered his help again, by sending more merchants to sell things to our army. I swear that those people have money flowing in their veins instead of blood.\n当然，Dingirra的大君主又伸出援手，派来更多商人向我们军队兜售货物。我发誓，那些人血管里流的是钱，不是血。"

    old "But in this case, I am happy to have the possibility to rest and restock my potions if needed."
    new "But in this case, I am happy to have the possibility to rest and restock my potions if needed.\n不过这一次，我很高兴有机会休整，并在需要时补充药剂。"

    old "I see two men approaching me, emerging from the mists."
    new "I see two men approaching me, emerging from the mists.\n我看到两个人从雾中走出，朝我靠近。"

    old "Sir Cedric! Captain Thomas!"
    new "Sir Cedric! Captain Thomas!\nCedric爵士！Thomas队长！"

    old "[protag], we're ready to commence the assault."
    new "[protag], we're ready to commence the assault.\n[protag]，我们已准备好发起进攻。"

    old "Good. But...Sir Cedric? I'm surprised to see you here."
    new "Good. But...Sir Cedric? I'm surprised to see you here.\n好。不过……Cedric爵士？在这里见到你，我很意外。"

    old "I couldn't miss it for anything in the world. Mind you, I won't be leading any army myself, but I simply wanted to be here. And offer any advice I can to help you."
    new "I couldn't miss it for anything in the world. Mind you, I won't be leading any army myself, but I simply wanted to be here. And offer any advice I can to help you.\n天大的事我也不会错过这一场。不过说清楚，我不会亲自领兵，我只是想在这里，尽我所能给你些建议、助你一臂之力。"

    old "Thank you. I could use some help indeed. What is the situation?"
    new "Thank you. I could use some help indeed. What is the situation?\n谢谢。我确实需要帮助。现在战况如何？"

    old "Our army is deployed and ready to strike. The vampires assumed a defensive position. They have the advantage, considering N'Mar's tricky terrain..."
    new "Our army is deployed and ready to strike. The vampires assumed a defensive position. They have the advantage, considering N'Mar's tricky terrain...\n我军已部署完毕，随时可以出击。吸血鬼摆出了防守阵势。考虑到N'Mar复杂的地形，他们占了优势……"

    old "The good news is that the mist seems to be retreating back to the castle too."
    new "The good news is that the mist seems to be retreating back to the castle too.\n好消息是，那雾似乎也在向城堡退去。"

    old "That's great news! We'll be able to see better what happens on the battlefield."
    new "That's great news! We'll be able to see better what happens on the battlefield.\n那真是太好了！我们就能更清楚地看到战场上的情况了。"

    old "Yes, but don't be too cocksure. It might also be a strategy. These vampires could be trying to trick us with a false sense of security, to strike us from behind. We must be vigilant."
    new "Yes, but don't be too cocksure. It might also be a strategy. These vampires could be trying to trick us with a false sense of security, to strike us from behind. We must be vigilant.\n是啊，但别太自以为是。这也可能是一种策略。这些吸血鬼也许想用虚假的安全感迷惑我们，好从背后偷袭。我们必须保持警惕。"

    old "I'll spare you the details, [protag], so you can focus on leading the battle on the larger scale. There are two things to consider: their defenses, and our army morale."
    new "I'll spare you the details, [protag], so you can focus on leading the battle on the larger scale. There are two things to consider: their defenses, and our army morale.\n细节我就不赘述了，[protag]，好让你专注于从更大层面指挥战斗。有两件事需要考虑：他们的防御，以及我军的士气。"

    old "The morale?"
    new "The morale?\n士气？"

    old "Sir Cedric is right. We outnumber the undead, but they keep coming out from the castle and rise from the ground surrounding it. We need to keep the momentum, we must keep pushing towards the castle, evade the enemy scare tactics."
    new "Sir Cedric is right. We outnumber the undead, but they keep coming out from the castle and rise from the ground surrounding it. We need to keep the momentum, we must keep pushing towards the castle, evade the enemy scare tactics.\nCedric爵士说得对。我们人数多于不死生物，但他们不断从城堡里涌出，也从城堡周围的地底升起。我们必须保持势头，不断向城堡推进，避开敌人的恐吓战术。"

    old "So one of our goals, beside destroying the castle defenses, is also to keep the army morale high. If terror starts spreading, even an army outnumbering the enemy could quickly collapse and retreat. Then all would be lost."
    new "So one of our goals, beside destroying the castle defenses, is also to keep the army morale high. If terror starts spreading, even an army outnumbering the enemy could quickly collapse and retreat. Then all would be lost.\n所以我们的目标之一，除了摧毁城堡防御之外，还要保持军队的高昂士气。一旦恐惧蔓延，即便是一支人数占优的军队，也可能迅速崩溃撤退。到那时，一切都完了。"

    old "All right, so what are our options?"
    new "All right, so what are our options?\n好吧，那我们有哪些选择？"

    old "There are several: you can go down the field yourself to thin their ranks. A successful victory will raise the army morale. Be careful though, a loss, while not deadly, would lower the morale."
    new "There are several: you can go down the field yourself to thin their ranks. A successful victory will raise the army morale. Be careful though, a loss, while not deadly, would lower the morale.\n有几个选择：你可以亲自下到战场上去削薄敌军阵线。一场胜仗会提振我军士气。不过要小心，一场败仗虽不致命，却会挫伤士气。"

    old "Since you already disposed of all the vampire lieutenants, that's one less thing to worry about."
    new "Since you already disposed of all the vampire lieutenants, that's one less thing to worry about.\n既然你已经除掉了所有吸血鬼副官，那我们就少了一桩心事。"

    old "However, we spotted some...giant undead. We have marked them as critical targets. Defeating one of those will obviously be harder but worth it. But I'm afraid they won't let you escape if you choose to fight them."
    new "However, we spotted some...giant undead. We have marked them as critical targets. Defeating one of those will obviously be harder but worth it. But I'm afraid they won't let you escape if you choose to fight them.\n不过，我们发现了一些……巨型不死生物。我们已将它们标记为关键目标。击败其中一个显然更难，但很值得。只是，你若选择与它们交战，恐怕它们不会放你逃脱。"

    old "There's still the problem of the remaining vampire lieutenants. Our scout spotted them here. They're ready to fight, and this time they won't retreat: any encounter with them will surely be a fight to the death, so don't wander in expecting anything less."
    new "There's still the problem of the remaining vampire lieutenants. Our scout spotted them here. They're ready to fight, and this time they won't retreat: any encounter with them will surely be a fight to the death, so don't wander in expecting anything less.\n还有剩下的吸血鬼副官这个麻烦。我们的斥候在这里发现了他们。他们已做好战斗准备，而且这次不会撤退：与他们任何一次遭遇，都必定是生死之战，所以别抱着侥幸的心思闯入。"

    old "And as if that weren't enough to deal with, we also spotted some...giant undead. We have marked them as critical targets together with the vampire lieutenants. Be careful if you decide to fight one of those."
    new "And as if that weren't enough to deal with, we also spotted some...giant undead. We have marked them as critical targets together with the vampire lieutenants. Be careful if you decide to fight one of those.\n而好像这还不够应付似的，我们还发现了一些……巨型不死生物。我们已把它们与吸血鬼副官一同标记为关键目标。你若决定与其中一只交战，务必小心。"

    old "As you can imagine, defeating a critical target will give a big boost in our army morale and will be a serious blow on the castle's defenses."
    new "As you can imagine, defeating a critical target will give a big boost in our army morale and will be a serious blow on the castle's defenses.\n你可以想象，击败一个关键目标，会大大提振我军士气，也会对城堡防御造成沉重打击。"

    old "Good. That's all I need to know."
    new "Good. That's all I need to know.\n好。我需要知道的就是这些。"

    old "One last thing, [protag]. Once the castle defenses are down, we can breach it, allowing our forces to enter. However, as you can imagine an army cannot march inside it without scouting first. We don't want them to wander into an ambush. We can't risk that many lives until we're sure that there isn't a trap waiting for them."
    new "One last thing, [protag]. Once the castle defenses are down, we can breach it, allowing our forces to enter. However, as you can imagine an army cannot march inside it without scouting first. We don't want them to wander into an ambush. We can't risk that many lives until we're sure that there isn't a trap waiting for them.\n最后一件事，[protag]。一旦城堡防御被击破，我们就能破门而入，让部队进去。不过，你可以想象，一支军队若不经侦察，是不能贸然开进去的。我们不想让他们走进伏击圈。在确认里面没有陷阱等着他们之前，我们不能拿那么多条命去冒险。"

    old "I'll be the first to enter the castle, together with my team. We'll make sure that there's nothing dangerous left inside. Once we secure the main hall, we'll give the signal and you can enter too."
    new "I'll be the first to enter the castle, together with my team. We'll make sure that there's nothing dangerous left inside. Once we secure the main hall, we'll give the signal and you can enter too.\n我会带着我的队伍率先进入城堡。我们会确保里面不再有任何危险。一旦守住主厅，我们就发信号，你们再进来。"

    old "Indeed. You take new territory, and the army will come in to defend it. Once we're inside, don't worry about watching your back; that's our job. Just concentrate on advancing the front line."
    new "Indeed. You take new territory, and the army will come in to defend it. Once we're inside, don't worry about watching your back; that's our job. Just concentrate on advancing the front line.\n确实。你夺取新的区域，军队就进来守住它。一旦我们进入，你就不必担心背后——那是我们的职责。你只需专心推进前线。"

    old "Good luck, [protag]."
    new "Good luck, [protag].\n祝你好运，[protag]。"

    old "We got reports that your... 'pirate friends' managed to kill a good amount of undead with their cannons!"
    new "We got reports that your... 'pirate friends' managed to kill a good amount of undead with their cannons!\n我们收到报告，说你的那些……“海盗朋友”用大炮杀死了不少不死生物！"

    old "{i}Castle Defenses decreased and Army Morale increased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Castle Defenses decreased and Army Morale increased!{/i}\n{i}城堡防御降低，军队士气提升！{/i}"

    old "Glad to hear it!"
    new "Glad to hear it!\n很高兴听到这个消息！"

    old "Thanks to the steel weapons, my men killed a few groups of undead too!"
    new "Thanks to the steel weapons, my men killed a few groups of undead too!\n多亏了那些钢制武器，我的弟兄们也杀掉了好几群不死生物！"

    old "{i}Castle Defenses decreased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Castle Defenses decreased!{/i}\n{i}城堡防御降低！{/i}"

    old "The help from Cedric's veteran friends is invaluable. They're keeping our army morale strong!"
    new "The help from Cedric's veteran friends is invaluable. They're keeping our army morale strong!\nCedric那些老兵朋友的帮助无比宝贵。他们让我军士气保持高昂！"

    old "{i}Army Morale increased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Army Morale increased!{/i}\n{i}军队士气提升！{/i}"

    old "Unfortunately, we got reports that the rest of the army lost several fights against undead."
    new "Unfortunately, we got reports that the rest of the army lost several fights against undead.\n不幸的是，我们收到报告，说其余部队与不死生物交手，输了好几场。"

    old "{i}Army Morale decreased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Army Morale decreased!{/i}\n{i}军队士气下降！{/i}"

    old "Unfortunately, we got reports that the rest of the army lost a few fights against undead."
    new "Unfortunately, we got reports that the rest of the army lost a few fights against undead.\n不幸的是，我们收到报告，说其余部队与不死生物交手，输了几场。"

    old "{i}Army Morale slightly decreased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Army Morale slightly decreased!{/i}\n{i}军队士气略有下降！{/i}"

    old "Unfortunately, we lost many men while you were fighting. This was a serious blow to our army's morale."
    new "Unfortunately, we lost many men while you were fighting. This was a serious blow to our army's morale.\n不幸的是，在你战斗期间，我们损失了许多弟兄。这对我军士气是沉重的打击。"

    old "{i}Army Morale greatly decreased!{/i}"
    new "{i}Army Morale greatly decreased!{/i}\n{i}军队士气大幅下降！{/i}"

    old "The undead army is dispersing! This is the opportunity we were waiting for!"
    new "The undead army is dispersing! This is the opportunity we were waiting for!\n不死大军正在溃散！这正是我们等待的机会！"

    old "We must strike now!"
    new "We must strike now!\n我们必须立即出击！"

    old "Men! Clear a path so that [protag] and [hisher] team can reach the castle's entrance!"
    new "Men! Clear a path so that [protag] and [hisher] team can reach the castle's entrance!\n弟兄们！清出一条路，让[protag]和[hisher]的队伍抵达城堡入口！"

    old "Uh, my apologies. I didn't mean to give orders to the army instead of you, Captain Thomas."
    new "Uh, my apologies. I didn't mean to give orders to the army instead of you, Captain Thomas.\n呃，抱歉。我不是有意越过你向军队发号施令的，Thomas队长。"

    old "It's fine. I can see why in the moment of excitement you might forgot who's in charge."
    new "It's fine. I can see why in the moment of excitement you might forgot who's in charge.\n没关系。我明白，人在兴奋关头是可能一时忘了谁才是发令的人。"

    old "Have you listened, men? Our goal is to clear a path through the undead army to let [protag]'s team inside!"
    new "Have you listened, men? Our goal is to clear a path through the undead army to let [protag]'s team inside!\n你们都听到了吗？我们的目标，是在不死大军中清出一条路，让[protag]的队伍进去！"

    old "The soldiers follow Thomas's orders and band together, clearing out a swath of the undead in the space between us and the castle. We quickly rush through the opening they've created to reach the castle entrance without being slowed down by writhing masses of undead."
    new "The soldiers follow Thomas's orders and band together, clearing out a swath of the undead in the space between us and the castle. We quickly rush through the opening they've created to reach the castle entrance without being slowed down by writhing masses of undead.\n士兵们听从Thomas的命令，集结起来，在我们与城堡之间清出了一大片不死生物。我们迅速穿过他们打开的缺口，冲向城堡入口，没有被那些翻滚蠕动的大群不死生物拖慢脚步。"

    old "We're inside Castle N'Mar, once again. There are a few lesser undead roaming around but we quickly dispose of them. I signal my team to follow me as I rush in the castle's main hall. I don't know why but I sense that someone is there."
    new "We're inside Castle N'Mar, once again. There are a few lesser undead roaming around but we quickly dispose of them. I signal my team to follow me as I rush in the castle's main hall. I don't know why but I sense that someone is there.\n我们再次进入了N'Mar城堡。周围游荡着几只低等不死生物，我们迅速解决了它们。我示意队伍跟上，冲进城堡主厅。不知为何，我感觉到有人在那里。"

    old "And indeed, my sixth sense was right."
    new "And indeed, my sixth sense was right.\n果然，我的第六感没错。"

    old "An enormous, muscular man shows in front of me. He's quite different from all the vampires I've seen before. He looks...massive."
    new "An enormous, muscular man shows in front of me. He's quite different from all the vampires I've seen before. He looks...massive.\n一个魁梧健壮的男人出现在我面前。他与我之前见过的所有吸血鬼都大不相同。他看起来……庞大得惊人。"

    old "So you think you have the rights to enter my new home uninvited? That's very rude of you. Unless, you're coming to be my dinner. In that case I forgive you."
    new "So you think you have the rights to enter my new home uninvited? That's very rude of you. Unless, you're coming to be my dinner. In that case I forgive you.\n所以你觉得，你有权不经邀请就闯进我的新家？你可真没礼貌。除非……你是来给我当晚餐的。那样的话，我原谅你。"

    old "I'm Sir Humbra."
    new "I'm Sir Humbra.\n我是Humbra爵士。"

    old "You're a knight?!"
    new "You're a knight?!\n你是个骑士？！"

    old "A former knight, and now a much more powerful shadowknight."
    new "A former knight, and now a much more powerful shadowknight.\n曾经是骑士，如今是强大得多的暗影骑士。"

    old "I shiver. I have heard many tales in my profession about shadowknights: they're deadly knights that specialize in dark magic. They're spoken about in whispers and vague rumors, as none have ever confronted one directly and lived to tell about it."
    new "I shiver. I have heard many tales in my profession about shadowknights: they're deadly knights that specialize in dark magic. They're spoken about in whispers and vague rumors, as none have ever confronted one directly and lived to tell about it.\n我不禁打了个寒颤。我在行当里听过许多关于暗影骑士的传说：他们是专精黑魔法的致命骑士。人们只在窃窃私语和模糊传闻中提到他们，因为从没有人正面对上过一个暗影骑士后还能活着讲述。"

    old "I see you trembling before me. Are you afraid, [protag]?"
    new "I see you trembling before me. Are you afraid, [protag]?\n我看你在我面前发抖。你害怕了吗，[protag]？"

    old "...!"
    new "...!\n……！"

    old "What, did you really think my friends didn't tell me your name? I know perfectly who you are. You disposed of my lieutenants. You killed Hersilia. You've been a decent opponent, after all."
    new "What, did you really think my friends didn't tell me your name? I know perfectly who you are. You disposed of my lieutenants. You killed Hersilia. You've been a decent opponent, after all.\n怎么，你真以为我的朋友们没把你的名字告诉我吗？我清楚得很你是谁。你除掉了我那些副官，还杀了Hersilia。说到底，你一直是个不错的对手。"

    old "Yes, friends. Why, do you think it's not possible for someone like me to have friends? Feelings? To love someone?"
    new "Yes, friends. Why, do you think it's not possible for someone like me to have friends? Feelings? To love someone?\n没错，朋友。怎么，你觉得像我这样的人，就不可能拥有朋友？不可能有感情？不可能去爱一个人？"

    old "He grins and clearly shows vampire teeth. So he is a vampire, and shadowknight. A formidable combination."
    new "He grins and clearly shows vampire teeth. So he is a vampire, and shadowknight. A formidable combination.\n他咧嘴一笑，清楚地露出吸血鬼的尖牙。原来他既是吸血鬼，又是暗影骑士。真是可怕至极的组合。"

    old "There's a sparkle in his eyes. This man, or vampire, or whatever he is, is driven by some powerful force. I know he won't stop until he reaches his goal. But what is his goal?"
    new "There's a sparkle in his eyes. This man, or vampire, or whatever he is, is driven by some powerful force. I know he won't stop until he reaches his goal. But what is his goal?\n他眼中闪过一丝光芒。这个男人，或者说这个吸血鬼，不管他究竟是什么，都被某种强大的力量驱动着。我知道，不达目的他不会罢休。可他的目的究竟是什么？"

    old "Five more vampires, lesser ones but still vampires, join his side. I need to gain time to plan a strategy. Make him talk. I have the feeling that if I attack him now, I would be quickly killed."
    new "Five more vampires, lesser ones but still vampires, join his side. I need to gain time to plan a strategy. Make him talk. I have the feeling that if I attack him now, I would be quickly killed.\n又有五个吸血鬼站到了他身边——是些较弱的，但终究还是吸血鬼。我需要争取时间来筹划策略。让他开口说话。我有种感觉，若此刻贸然进攻，我会很快被杀。"

    old "There's no need to fight. I only want you to leave. Here, take this gift as sign of my goodwill."
    new "There's no need to fight. I only want you to leave. Here, take this gift as sign of my goodwill.\n没必要动手。我只想让你离开。给，收下这份礼物，作为我善意的表示。"

    old "Puah! Keep your gifts for yourself! I don't care! I will never go away. Not until The Human Empire is destroyed!"
    new "Puah! Keep your gifts for yourself! I don't care! I will never go away. Not until The Human Empire is destroyed!\n呸！你的礼物自己留着吧！我不稀罕！我绝不会离开。除非人类帝国被摧毁！"

    old "But maybe your companions would like it?"
    new "But maybe your companions would like it?\n但也许你的同伴们会喜欢呢？"

    old "You seem a worthy foe. I don't know who of us will prevail in the end. But I think you deserve this."
    new "You seem a worthy foe. I don't know who of us will prevail in the end. But I think you deserve this.\n你看起来是个值得一战的对手。我不知道我们俩最终谁会胜出。但我想，你配得上这个。"

    old "A vial with my own blood. Seems fair to give you a taste since it's all you'll ever get from me."
    new "A vial with my own blood. Seems fair to give you a taste since it's all you'll ever get from me.\n一瓶我自己的血。让你尝尝也算公平，反正你从我这里能得到的，也就只有这个了。"

    old "Hahaha. I like your sense of humor. But I'm afraid I don't care about it. I'll get your blood directly from you."
    new "Hahaha. I like your sense of humor. But I'm afraid I don't care about it. I'll get your blood directly from you.\n哈哈哈。我喜欢你的幽默感。但恐怕我并不稀罕。我会直接从你身上取你的血。"

    old "Are you sure? Why don't you try it?"
    new "Are you sure? Why don't you try it?\n你确定？何不试试看？"

    old "What do I want? Hmm, let me think. I want Grimoire. And Lothark. And Horus. I want to see them all in ruin, and the whole Human Empire destroyed!"
    new "What do I want? Hmm, let me think. I want Grimoire. And Lothark. And Horus. I want to see them all in ruin, and the whole Human Empire destroyed!\n我想要什么？嗯，让我想想。我要Grimoire，还要Lothark，还要Horus。我要看着它们全部化为废墟，看着整个人类帝国被摧毁！"

    old "Damn, it looks like that parley with this one will be pointless. I won't be able to reach any compromise."
    new "Damn, it looks like that parley with this one will be pointless. I won't be able to reach any compromise.\n该死，看来和这家伙谈判是白费口舌。我根本不可能达成任何妥协。"

    old "The undead army is being routed. As we speak, the Empire Army is killing the few wandering undead left outside."
    new "The undead army is being routed. As we speak, the Empire Army is killing the few wandering undead left outside.\n不死大军正在溃败。就在我们说话的当口，帝国军队正在清剿外面剩下的少数游荡不死生物。"

    old "Interesting that you might be thinking this. Let me offer you another perspective instead. What if I willingly ordered the undead outside to let you pass?"
    new "Interesting that you might be thinking this. Let me offer you another perspective instead. What if I willingly ordered the undead outside to let you pass?\n你居然会这么想，真有意思。那我换个角度跟你说吧。如果是我主动命令外面的不死生物放你们进来的呢？"

    old "Your actions were disrupting our defenses and raising the Empire Army's morale. I couldn't risk going outside, so I simply allowed you to enter. So that I can fight you in my own terms. Instead of forcing me to come out and fight you, you've chosen to confront me here, in my inner sanctum. Do you really think that you have the advantage here?"
    new "Your actions were disrupting our defenses and raising the Empire Army's morale. I couldn't risk going outside, so I simply allowed you to enter. So that I can fight you in my own terms. Instead of forcing me to come out and fight you, you've chosen to confront me here, in my inner sanctum. Do you really think that you have the advantage here?\n你的行动扰乱了我们的防御，还提振了帝国军队的士气。我不敢冒险出去，于是干脆放你们进来。这样我就能按自己的方式来与你交战。你没有逼我出来迎战，而是选择在这里、在我的内殿与我正面对峙。你真的以为，在这里你能占到优势吗？"

    old "Haha, you're surprised? I can tell you this: once I kill you and your pathetic team here, nothing will be able to stop us from destroying the Empire's army."
    new "Haha, you're surprised? I can tell you this: once I kill you and your pathetic team here, nothing will be able to stop us from destroying the Empire's army.\n哈哈，你很惊讶？我可以告诉你：一旦我在这里杀了你和你们那支可怜的小队，就再没什么能阻止我们摧毁帝国军队了。"

    old "Uh? What about N'Mar?"
    new "Uh? What about N'Mar?\n嗯？那N'Mar呢？"

    old "Why did you choose to make this your center of operation?"
    new "Why did you choose to make this your center of operation?\n你为什么选择把这里当作你的行动中心？"

    old "Can you imagine a more ideal location? Far away from civilization, yet still close enough to go hunting during full moons. It is the ideal place for a vampire to live, don't you think?"
    new "Can you imagine a more ideal location? Far away from civilization, yet still close enough to go hunting during full moons. It is the ideal place for a vampire to live, don't you think?\n你能想象出更理想的地点吗？远离文明，却又近到能在满月时外出狩猎。这是吸血鬼栖身的理想之地，你不觉得吗？"

    old "And here I was, thinking you chose it to defend against possible attacks. It seems that was nothing but an unexpected benefit."
    new "And here I was, thinking you chose it to defend against possible attacks. It seems that was nothing but an unexpected benefit.\n我还以为你选这里，是为了抵御可能的进攻。看来那不过是意外之喜。"

    old "It was a happy little coincidence for us. I wouldn't have devoted all of my resources to this castle if I didn't think it was an ideal place to defend against an attack."
    new "It was a happy little coincidence for us. I wouldn't have devoted all of my resources to this castle if I didn't think it was an ideal place to defend against an attack.\n这对我们来说，是个令人愉快的小巧合。若不是觉得这里是抵御进攻的理想之地，我也不会把全部资源都投入到这座城堡上。"

    old "I thought so."
    new "I thought so.\n我想也是。"

    old "Are they with you?"
    new "Are they with you?\n他们和你是一伙的吗？"

    old "Who knows? They always show up when I less expect them. They could be following me even now."
    new "Who knows? They always show up when I less expect them. They could be following me even now.\n谁知道呢？他们总在我最意想不到的时候出现。说不定此刻也正跟着我。"

    old "Grah! First I'll take care of you, and then I'll take care of them!"
    new "Grah! First I'll take care of you, and then I'll take care of them!\n呃啊！我先解决你，再解决他们！"

    old "No surprise that he is not a friend of them. They've been plotting against N'Mar the whole time."
    new "No surprise that he is not a friend of them. They've been plotting against N'Mar the whole time.\n毫不意外，他不是他们的朋友。他们自始至终都在密谋对付N'Mar。"

    old "I throw the vial in their direction. The vial breaks on the floor, the blood coming out from it. One of the vampires can't resist and jumps on it, and starts licking the floor."
    new "I throw the vial in their direction. The vial breaks on the floor, the blood coming out from it. One of the vampires can't resist and jumps on it, and starts licking the floor.\n我把瓶子朝他们那边扔去。瓶子在地上碎裂，鲜血流了出来。其中一个吸血鬼按捺不住，扑了上去，开始舔地板。"

    old "I don't even have to give the signal: my companions hit the poor vampire with everything they have and it's killed in a few seconds."
    new "I don't even have to give the signal: my companions hit the poor vampire with everything they have and it's killed in a few seconds.\n我甚至不用发信号：我的同伴们倾尽全力攻击那个可怜的吸血鬼，几秒钟就把它结果了。"

    old "I flash a smile to Humbra, who is growing furious."
    new "I flash a smile to Humbra, who is growing furious.\n我朝Humbra露齿一笑，他已是怒不可遏。"

    old "I throw the vial in their direction. This time though, the other vampires stand still, probably knowing that Humbra didn't like what happened before."
    new "I throw the vial in their direction. This time though, the other vampires stand still, probably knowing that Humbra didn't like what happened before.\n我又把瓶子朝他们那边扔去。不过这一次，其他吸血鬼都站着一动不动，大概知道Humbra不喜欢刚才发生的那一幕。"

    old "Eventually though one of them moves towards the vial, but he's quickly killed by Humbra with a single slash of his sword!"
    new "Eventually though one of them moves towards the vial, but he's quickly killed by Humbra with a single slash of his sword!\n然而，最终还是有一个朝瓶子走去，Humbra挥剑一劈，眨眼就把他杀了！"

    old "Anyone else wants to disobey me tonight?"
    new "Anyone else wants to disobey me tonight?\n今晚还有谁想违抗我？"

    old "I swear the other vampires are trembling in fear in front of him. I didn't even know that this was possible."
    new "I swear the other vampires are trembling in fear in front of him. I didn't even know that this was possible.\n我发誓，其他吸血鬼都在他面前吓得瑟瑟发抖。我甚至不知道这种事竟然可能。"

    old "Enough talk! Prepare to die!"
    new "Enough talk! Prepare to die!\n废话少说！准备受死吧！"

    old "More vampires joined his side. However using the vials to take out his original allies must have made him weaker: the new ones are replacements anyway."
    new "More vampires joined his side. However using the vials to take out his original allies must have made him weaker: the new ones are replacements anyway.\n更多吸血鬼站到了他身边。不过，用血瓶除掉他原本的盟友，想必也削弱了他——反正新来的不过是替补罢了。"

    old "It's not over yet! No!"
    new "It's not over yet! No!\n还没结束！不！"

    old "Humbra gets back on his feet, and even if all his vampire allies are gone, he summons several zombies to assist him."
    new "Humbra gets back on his feet, and even if all his vampire allies are gone, he summons several zombies to assist him.\nHumbra重新站了起来，即便他所有的吸血鬼盟友都已不在，他还是召来了几只僵尸助阵。"

    old "Concentrate your attacks on him! If he's defeated, he can't control the undead anymore!"
    new "Concentrate your attacks on him! If he's defeated, he can't control the undead anymore!\n集中火力攻击他！一旦他倒下，就再也无法控制那些不死生物了！"

    old "But...why? You're one of us too... why did you fight me?"
    new "But...why? You're one of us too... why did you fight me?\n可……为什么？你也是我们中的一员啊……你为什么要与我为敌？"

    old "I needed your help to save Lisbeth..."
    new "I needed your help to save Lisbeth...\n我需要你的帮助去救Lisbeth……"

    old "No...Lisbeth...I failed..."
    new "No...Lisbeth...I failed...\n不……Lisbeth……我失败了……"

    old "Who's Lisbeth?"
    new "Who's Lisbeth?\nLisbeth是谁？"

    old "Is this the end? Yes. My love, I can see you now, through the light. Morte was wrong...we're together, again."
    new "Is this the end? Yes. My love, I can see you now, through the light. Morte was wrong...we're together, again.\n这就是尽头了吗？是的。我的爱人，透过那道光，我如今能看见你了。Morte错了……我们又在一起了。"

    old "The shadowknight collapses to the ground with a loud thump. Seconds later, his body vanishes and only ashes remain."
    new "The shadowknight collapses to the ground with a loud thump. Seconds later, his body vanishes and only ashes remain.\n那暗影骑士砰然一声倒地。几秒之后，他的身体消失，只剩下一堆灰烬。"

    old "Look outside the windows! The mist is completely gone!"
    new "Look outside the windows! The mist is completely gone!\n看窗外！那雾已经完全消失了！"

    old "We finally put an end to this evil magic! We did it !"
    new "We finally put an end to this evil magic! We did it !\n我们终于终结了这邪恶的魔法！我们做到了！"

    old "However, before I can answer my companions, from the four corners of the main hall, more shambling undead show up."
    new "However, before I can answer my companions, from the four corners of the main hall, more shambling undead show up.\n然而，我还没来得及回应同伴们，主厅的四角又冒出了更多蹒跚的不死生物。"

    old "More undead coming! Retreat to the battlements! They won't be able to surround us there!"
    new "More undead coming! Retreat to the battlements! They won't be able to surround us there!\n更多不死生物来了！撤到城垛上去！在那里它们没法包围我们！"

    old "We hastily make our way up to the battlement. We form two groups so that we can control the undead coming from both sides. But the narrow battlement gives us an advantage, the undead aren't able to overwhelm us."
    new "We hastily make our way up to the battlement. We form two groups so that we can control the undead coming from both sides. But the narrow battlement gives us an advantage, the undead aren't able to overwhelm us.\n我们匆忙撤上城垛，分成两组，好应对从两侧涌来的不死生物。而狭窄的城垛反倒给了我们优势，不死生物没法一拥而上压垮我们。"

    old "At least in theory, because after several minutes of fighting, there's no end in sight...I see the sun on the horizons and the beauty of the dawn is contrasting with the ugliness of the horde of undead attacking us."
    new "At least in theory, because after several minutes of fighting, there's no end in sight...I see the sun on the horizons and the beauty of the dawn is contrasting with the ugliness of the horde of undead attacking us.\n至少理论上如此，因为战斗持续了几分钟后，仍看不到尽头……我看到太阳升起在地平线上，黎明的美，与袭击我们的那丑陋的不死大群形成了鲜明对比。"

    old "This is it. Even with Humbra out of the picture, the undead are still too many. They are overwhelming us."
    new "This is it. Even with Humbra out of the picture, the undead are still too many. They are overwhelming us.\n就这样了吗。即便Humbra已不复存在，不死生物还是太多了。它们正要把我们淹没。"

    old "We should have won. We defeated every powerful adversary that came our way. No challenge was too great. But now...is this how it all ends? Overwhelmed by sheer numbers, of an undying army that knows no end?"
    new "We should have won. We defeated every powerful adversary that came our way. No challenge was too great. But now...is this how it all ends? Overwhelmed by sheer numbers, of an undying army that knows no end?\n我们本该赢的。我们击败了挡在面前的每一个强敌，没有什么挑战是我们跨不过去的。可现在……难道一切就以这种方式结束吗？被一支无穷无尽的不死大军以纯粹的数量压垮？"

    old "Suddenly, I hear sounds above us. Like the cry of giant birds flying over us. I look in the sky and the wonder before my eyes leaves me speechless."
    new "Suddenly, I hear sounds above us. Like the cry of giant birds flying over us. I look in the sky and the wonder before my eyes leaves me speechless.\n突然，我听到头顶上方传来声响，像是有巨鸟飞过时的鸣叫。我望向天空，眼前的奇景让我说不出话来。"

    old "Several amazons are riding griffons, led by queen Karen herself, launching an attack from the sky!"
    new "Several amazons are riding griffons, led by queen Karen herself, launching an attack from the sky!\n几个Amazon骑着狮鹫，由Karen女王亲自率领，从天空中发起了进攻！"

    old "The griffon riders are able to hit undead striking from above, like eagles, killing large swaths of undead on each strike. The tide of battle is rapidly changing in our favor!"
    new "The griffon riders are able to hit undead striking from above, like eagles, killing large swaths of undead on each strike. The tide of battle is rapidly changing in our favor!\n狮鹫骑手们如雄鹰般从上方俯冲攻击不死生物，每一次出击都能成片地消灭敌人。战局正迅速朝有利于我们的方向转变！"

    old "With the griffon riders thinning their ranks and drawing the attention of the undead, it's no trouble for us to finish off the stragglers by ourselves. The battle seems far from over, but a battle that seemed hopeless only moments ago now seems winnable."
    new "With the griffon riders thinning their ranks and drawing the attention of the undead, it's no trouble for us to finish off the stragglers by ourselves. The battle seems far from over, but a battle that seemed hopeless only moments ago now seems winnable.\n有了狮鹫骑手削薄敌阵、吸引不死生物的注意，我们自己收拾那些掉队的残兵就轻松多了。战斗看似远未结束，但片刻前还显得毫无希望的一战，如今已有了胜算。"

    old "I look at the faces of my companions, streaked with sweat and dirt and blood. But still they fight on, with a renewed sense of determination. No matter the challenge, no matter how relentless the assault, we will carry on."
    new "I look at the faces of my companions, streaked with sweat and dirt and blood. But still they fight on, with a renewed sense of determination. No matter the challenge, no matter how relentless the assault, we will carry on.\n我望着同伴们的脸，汗水、尘土和血迹斑驳。但他们仍继续战斗，带着焕然一新的决心。无论挑战多大，无论攻势多么凶猛，我们都会坚持下去。"

    old "We push forward, and the undead stop rising. At last, it seems that whatever force was animating them has dried out. After some minutes, the amazons land safely on the castle courtyard with their griffons."
    new "We push forward, and the undead stop rising. At last, it seems that whatever force was animating them has dried out. After some minutes, the amazons land safely on the castle courtyard with their griffons.\n我们向前推进，不死生物不再从地底升起。终于，驱动它们的某种力量似乎枯竭了。几分钟后，Amazon们骑着狮鹫安全降落在城堡庭院里。"

    old "Queen Karen comes forward to speak to me."
    new "Queen Karen comes forward to speak to me.\nKaren女王走上前来与我说话。"

    old "[protag]. Or should I call you, vampire [protag]? Did you choose another name yet?"
    new "[protag]. Or should I call you, vampire [protag]? Did you choose another name yet?\n[protag]。还是我该叫你“吸血鬼[protag]”呢？你给自己另起了名字吗？"

    old "Oh... you know."
    new "Oh... you know.\n哦……你都知道了。"

    old "Of course I know. Leena told me everything. I was unsure I swoop in and strike you down, too. But after considering everything we've been through to win this battle, I thought better of it."
    new "Of course I know. Leena told me everything. I was unsure I swoop in and strike you down, too. But after considering everything we've been through to win this battle, I thought better of it.\n我当然知道。Leena把一切都告诉我了。我一度拿不准，是否也该俯冲下来把你一并击倒。但在回想了我们为赢得这场战斗所经历的一切之后，我改了主意。"

    old "Save your breath, [protag]."
    new "Save your breath, [protag].\n省省吧，[protag]。"

    old "Queen Karen holds her hand forward. I slowly take it and shake her hand."
    new "Queen Karen holds her hand forward. I slowly take it and shake her hand.\nKaren女王伸出手。我缓缓握住，与她握手。"

    old "This will be the last time we met, [protag]. I think I know why you did it. To be more powerful. To increase the chances of victory."
    new "This will be the last time we met, [protag]. I think I know why you did it. To be more powerful. To increase the chances of victory.\n这将是我们最后一次见面了，[protag]。我想我明白你为什么要那么做。为了变得更强，为了增加胜利的机会。"

    old "This was wrong."
    new "This was wrong.\n这样做是错的。"

    old "True warriors never comes down to compromise their true self to win a battle. If they feel they're not up to the task, they train. They keep training until they're ready."
    new "True warriors never comes down to compromise their true self to win a battle. If they feel they're not up to the task, they train. They keep training until they're ready.\n真正的战士从不会为了赢得一场战斗，而妥协自己的本真。如果他们觉得自己还不够格，就会去训练，一直练到自己准备好为止。"

    old "What if there's no enough time to train?"
    new "What if there's no enough time to train?\n可要是没有足够的时间训练呢？"

    old "Then it means you weren't the right person for the job."
    new "Then it means you weren't the right person for the job.\n那就说明，你本不是这份差事的合适人选。"

    old "Goodbye, [protag]."
    new "Goodbye, [protag].\n再见了，[protag]。"

    old "As I watch Karen leaving, I have the certainty that I'll never see her again in my life. And that thought leaves me with a profound sense of sadness, as if she's taking an important part of me with her as she leaves."
    new "As I watch Karen leaving, I have the certainty that I'll never see her again in my life. And that thought leaves me with a profound sense of sadness, as if she's taking an important part of me with her as she leaves.\n望着Karen离去，我确信此生再也见不到她了。这个念头让我涌起一阵深沉的悲伤，仿佛她离去时，也带走了我身上重要的某一部分。"

    old "[protag]. Your efforts finally brought us to victory!"
    new "[protag]. Your efforts finally brought us to victory!\n[protag]。你的努力终于为我们带来了胜利！"

    old "And your efforts as well. You saved us, Karen. You turned the tide of a battle that seemed hopeless. It was the best surprise I could have hoped for. Nobody mentioned you'd be launching an assault from the sky."
    new "And your efforts as well. You saved us, Karen. You turned the tide of a battle that seemed hopeless. It was the best surprise I could have hoped for. Nobody mentioned you'd be launching an assault from the sky.\n也少不了你的努力。你救了我们，Karen。你扭转了一场看似毫无希望的战斗。这是我所能期盼的最好的惊喜。没人提过你会从天空发起进攻。"

    old "You have no idea how hard was to convince the Council of this. Even in this dire hour, they worried that we could scout their precious secrets of Horus and Lothark. Or that we would try to take the castle for ourselves."
    new "You have no idea how hard was to convince the Council of this. Even in this dire hour, they worried that we could scout their precious secrets of Horus and Lothark. Or that we would try to take the castle for ourselves.\n你根本不知道，说服议会同意这件事有多难。即便在这生死存亡的关头，他们仍担心我们会去窥探Horus和Lothark的那些宝贵秘密，或是想把城堡据为己有。"

    old "Of course, we have no ambitions of settling any place beyond our beloved citadel, and even if we did decide to move, it certainly wouldn't be to a dreadful place such as this."
    new "Of course, we have no ambitions of settling any place beyond our beloved citadel, and even if we did decide to move, it certainly wouldn't be to a dreadful place such as this.\n当然，我们没有任何在亲爱的Citadel之外定居的野心；即便真要搬迁，也绝不会搬到这么可怕的地方来。"

    old "In the end, we were lucky. Apolimesho managed to convince them. I'm sure he lost some friends and gained some enemies in the process. But enough of politics. The mission is over. Victory has been won."
    new "In the end, we were lucky. Apolimesho managed to convince them. I'm sure he lost some friends and gained some enemies in the process. But enough of politics. The mission is over. Victory has been won.\n最终，我们还是幸运的。Apolimesho设法说服了他们。我肯定，这一过程中他失去了一些朋友，也树了一些敌人。但政治就到此为止吧。任务结束了，胜利已经到手。"

    old "I feel... relieved. A sensation that I was missing since too long."
    new "I feel... relieved. A sensation that I was missing since too long.\n我感到……如释重负。这种感觉，我已经缺失太久了。"

    old "Karen smiles and pats me on the shoulder. I am surprised by such a show of camaraderie from Karen herself and remain speechless."
    new "Karen smiles and pats me on the shoulder. I am surprised by such a show of camaraderie from Karen herself and remain speechless.\nKaren微笑着拍了拍我的肩膀。Karen本人竟流露出这样的战友之情，让我惊讶得说不出话来。"

    old "Don't feel too relaxed. I'm sure when you get back to Grimoire, the council will have a new task for you. After all, you exceeded their expectations. Why wouldn't they take advantage of your skills again?"
    new "Don't feel too relaxed. I'm sure when you get back to Grimoire, the council will have a new task for you. After all, you exceeded their expectations. Why wouldn't they take advantage of your skills again?\n别太松懈。我敢肯定，等你回到Grimoire，议会又会有新任务交给你。毕竟你超出了他们的预期。他们又怎会不再借重你的本事呢？"

    old "As I watch Karen leaving, I secretly hope to see her again."
    new "As I watch Karen leaving, I secretly hope to see her again.\n望着Karen离去，我在心里暗暗希望还能再见她一面。"

    old "The others gathers around me. The first one to speak is Larik."
    new "The others gathers around me. The first one to speak is Larik.\n其他人围拢到我身边。第一个开口的是Larik。"

    old "[protag], are you... a vampire now?"
    new "[protag], are you... a vampire now?\n[protag]，你现在……是吸血鬼了吗？"

    old "Yes. I feel like one. I don't feel the hunger yet, but I could sense it approaching. It's probably best if you all go away from here."
    new "Yes. I feel like one. I don't feel the hunger yet, but I could sense it approaching. It's probably best if you all go away from here.\n是的。我感觉自己已经是了。我还没感到饥饿，但能察觉到它正在逼近。你们大家最好还是先离开这里。"

    old "Everyone leaves, except for [chosen_romance]. [Che] stands still in front of me, unsure what to do. I am unsure what to do either."
    new "Everyone leaves, except for [chosen_romance]. [Che] stands still in front of me, unsure what to do. I am unsure what to do either.\n所有人都离开了，除了[chosen_romance]。[Che]一动不动地站在我面前，不知所措。我也不知道该怎么办。"

    old "Finally, I move towards [chim]. [Che] looks scared, probably because my movements are already much faster than usual, being a vampire. I offer [chim] a word of reassurance:"
    new "Finally, I move towards [chim]. [Che] looks scared, probably because my movements are already much faster than usual, being a vampire. I offer [chim] a word of reassurance:\n最后，我朝[chim]走去。[Che]看起来有些害怕，大概是因为成了吸血鬼后，我的动作已经比平时快出许多。我向[chim]说了句安慰的话："

    old "[chosen_romance], my love. Don't say anything. I need to be alone for a while now. I need to learn to control myself. My new self. But I'm not abandoning you. I will find you again. We will meet again, [chosen_romance]. I swear it."
    new "[chosen_romance], my love. Don't say anything. I need to be alone for a while now. I need to learn to control myself. My new self. But I'm not abandoning you. I will find you again. We will meet again, [chosen_romance]. I swear it.\n[chosen_romance]，我的爱人。什么也别说。现在我需要独自待一阵子。我得学会控制自己，控制这个全新的自己。但我不会抛弃你。我会再找到你的。我们会再相见的，[chosen_romance]。我发誓。"

    old "[Che] says nothing but nods. Then, [che] leaves like the others."
    new "[Che] says nothing but nods. Then, [che] leaves like the others.\n[Che]什么也没说，只是点了点头，然后像其他人一样离开了。"

    old "Everyone leaves, except for [chosen_romance]. They stand still in front of me, unsure what to do. I am unsure what to do either."
    new "Everyone leaves, except for [chosen_romance]. They stand still in front of me, unsure what to do. I am unsure what to do either.\n所有人都离开了，除了[chosen_romance]。他们一动不动地站在我面前，不知所措。我也不知道该怎么办。"

    old "Finally, I move towards them. They look scared, probably because my movements are already much faster than usual, being a vampire. I offer them a word of reassurance:"
    new "Finally, I move towards them. They look scared, probably because my movements are already much faster than usual, being a vampire. I offer them a word of reassurance:\n最后，我朝他们走去。他们看起来有些害怕，大概是因为成了吸血鬼后，我的动作已经比平时快出许多。我向他们说了句安慰的话："

    old "They look at each other, saying nothing. Then, they nod and leave like the others."
    new "They look at each other, saying nothing. Then, they nod and leave like the others.\n他们彼此对视，什么也没说，然后点了点头，像其他人一样离开了。"

    old "Everyone leaves. Some of them slow down and look back at me, and in their faces, I see a sense of loss, as if this is the first time they're fully comprehending that they'll never see me again."
    new "Everyone leaves. Some of them slow down and look back at me, and in their faces, I see a sense of loss, as if this is the first time they're fully comprehending that they'll never see me again.\n所有人都离开了。其中几人放慢脚步，回头望向我，我在他们脸上看到一种失落，仿佛他们此刻才第一次真正意识到，再也见不到我了。"

    old "I feel a sense of loss as well, but it's not as intense as the feeling of loss I felt several days ago, and I wonder if these feelings will be but a lingering memory by the time several months have passed. Has being turned into a vampire made me more cynical, or have I always been this way?"
    new "I feel a sense of loss as well, but it's not as intense as the feeling of loss I felt several days ago, and I wonder if these feelings will be but a lingering memory by the time several months have passed. Has being turned into a vampire made me more cynical, or have I always been this way?\n我也感到一阵失落，却不及几天前那般强烈。我不禁想，几个月过去后，这些感受会不会只剩下一点残存的记忆。是变成吸血鬼让我变得更愤世嫉俗了，还是我本就是这样的人？"

    old "[protag] I think I can speak for everyone here when I say that you're a natural born leader. I wouldn't have been able to do a better job than you myself. And they say I'm a pretty good warchief."
    new "[protag] I think I can speak for everyone here when I say that you're a natural born leader. I wouldn't have been able to do a better job than you myself. And they say I'm a pretty good warchief.\n[protag]，我想我可以代表这里所有人说一句：你是天生的领袖。换作我自己，也不会做得比你更好。而他们都说我已经是个相当不错的酋长了。"

    old "[chosen_romance] steps forward, taking everyone by surprise. [Che] jumps on me and starts kissing me like if was the last thing [che] could do in life."
    new "[chosen_romance] steps forward, taking everyone by surprise. [Che] jumps on me and starts kissing me like if was the last thing [che] could do in life.\n[chosen_romance]走上前来，让大家吃了一惊。[Che]扑到我身上，开始亲吻我，仿佛这是[che]此生最后能做的一件事。"

    old "Enok and Sylrissa step forward, taking everyone by surprise. They jump on me, hugging and kissing me. I feel overwhelmed by their love but it's a pleasant feeling, even if I am a bit embarrassed since everyone else is looking at me."
    new "Enok and Sylrissa step forward, taking everyone by surprise. They jump on me, hugging and kissing me. I feel overwhelmed by their love but it's a pleasant feeling, even if I am a bit embarrassed since everyone else is looking at me.\nEnok和Sylrissa走上前来，让大家吃了一惊。他们扑到我身上，又是拥抱又是亲吻。我被他们的爱意淹没，但那是种愉快的感觉，尽管因为其他人都在看着我，我有些不好意思。"

    old "The others cheer and laugh, and then it's their turn to come close and talk."
    new "The others cheer and laugh, and then it's their turn to come close and talk.\n其他人欢呼着、大笑着，然后轮到了他们走近与我交谈。"

    old "[protag], we did it! Yes! Evil undead buried underground for good! Yay!"
    new "[protag], we did it! Yes! Evil undead buried underground for good! Yay!\n[protag]，我们做到了！没错！邪恶的不死生物被永远埋在地下了！耶！"

    old "This does call for a bit of celebration, doesn't it? Let's enjoy one last cheer together."
    new "This does call for a bit of celebration, doesn't it? Let's enjoy one last cheer together.\n这确实值得庆祝一下，不是吗？让我们最后一起欢呼一次吧。"

    old "Sylrissa and I tilt our heads back and let out a bellowing scream of joy as the others look on with varying expressions of amusement."
    new "Sylrissa and I tilt our heads back and let out a bellowing scream of joy as the others look on with varying expressions of amusement.\nSylrissa和我仰起头，发出响亮的欢叫，其他人则在一旁看着，脸上表情各异地乐在其中。"

    old "It's been a long ride, Sylrissa. I was glad to always have you by my side."
    new "It's been a long ride, Sylrissa. I was glad to always have you by my side.\n这一路走了很久，Sylrissa。有你一直陪在身边，我很高兴。"

    old "This has been the most interesting and intense experience of my life, [protag]."
    new "This has been the most interesting and intense experience of my life, [protag].\n这是我一生中最有趣、也最刻骨铭心的经历，[protag]。"

    old "Interesting is one word. I've got a whole list of words to describe it, but I'll spare you."
    new "Interesting is one word. I've got a whole list of words to describe it, but I'll spare you.\n“有趣”只是其中一个词。要形容它，我能列出一长串词，不过就饶了你吧。"

    old "It's been an incredible journey, Enok. And I couldn't have asked for better company."
    new "It's been an incredible journey, Enok. And I couldn't have asked for better company.\n这是一段不可思议的旅程，Enok。能有你作伴，我再好不过了。"

    old "I'll always remember the things we did together, [protag]. But this castle...this castle holds some kind of dark magic. I find myself more curious than I've ever been in my life before."
    new "I'll always remember the things we did together, [protag]. But this castle...this castle holds some kind of dark magic. I find myself more curious than I've ever been in my life before.\n我会永远记得我们一起做过的事，[protag]。但这座城堡……这座城堡里藏着某种黑暗魔法。我发现自己这一生还从没像现在这样好奇过。"

    old "Be careful, Enok. Not all paths lead to happy ends. I wouldn't want to have to fight a naga shadowknight one day."
    new "Be careful, Enok. Not all paths lead to happy ends. I wouldn't want to have to fight a naga shadowknight one day.\n小心点，Enok。不是所有道路都通往美满的结局。我可不想有朝一日，不得不与一个naga暗影骑士为敌。"

    old "Don't worry. I have found a good teacher. Bambara will teach me."
    new "Don't worry. I have found a good teacher. Bambara will teach me.\n别担心。我找到了一位好老师。Bambara会教我的。"

    old "Again with that person, he seems to be charmed by her. And I'm pretty sure he got her name wrong."
    new "Again with that person, he seems to be charmed by her. And I'm pretty sure he got her name wrong.\n又是那个人，他像是被她迷住了。而且我很确定，他把她的名字念错了。"

    old "Leena? You don't want to make Karen wait. I know your first loyalty is to your queen, not to me."
    new "Leena? You don't want to make Karen wait. I know your first loyalty is to your queen, not to me.\nLeena？你可不想让Karen久等。我知道你首要效忠的是你的女王，不是我。"

    old "My loyalty to you may not match my duty to the queen, but don't trivialize it, [protag]. I have more than a few moments to spare. We have time for a proper send-off."
    new "My loyalty to you may not match my duty to the queen, but don't trivialize it, [protag]. I have more than a few moments to spare. We have time for a proper send-off.\n我对你的忠诚，也许不及我对女王的职责，但别把它看得无足轻重，[protag]。我还有不止一点时间可耽搁。我们来得及好好道个别。"

    old "Besides, I have my own griffon waiting for me. Karen said I can go back anytime I want."
    new "Besides, I have my own griffon waiting for me. Karen said I can go back anytime I want.\n再说了，我还有自己的狮鹫在等我。Karen说我想什么时候回去都行。"

    old "Sounds like... you got a promotion?"
    new "Sounds like... you got a promotion?\n听起来……你升职了？"

    old "I'm already the royal guard captain. The only higher grade than this is... queen."
    new "I'm already the royal guard captain. The only higher grade than this is... queen.\n我早就是皇家卫队队长了。比这更高的，就只有……女王了。"

    old "Oops. Then I suppose you'd have to just be happy to be called 'the hero of N'Mar.'"
    new "Oops. Then I suppose you'd have to just be happy to be called 'the hero of N'Mar.'\n哎呀。那我想，你只好满足于“N'Mar的英雄”这个称号了。"

    old "It's not bad. I'll take it."
    new "It's not bad. I'll take it.\n这也不错。我接受。"

    old "It's one for the storybooks, Leena. Generations of amazons will remember what we did here today."
    new "It's one for the storybooks, Leena. Generations of amazons will remember what we did here today.\n这段事迹足以载入故事书了，Leena。一代代Amazon都会记得我们今天在这里所做的一切。"

    old "Leena smiles. I'm about to reach out to shake her hand when she hugs me."
    new "Leena smiles. I'm about to reach out to shake her hand when she hugs me.\nLeena笑了。我正要伸手与她握手，她却抱住了我。"

    old "Thank you [protag]. Come visit me at the citadel some time. I'm going to miss our talks."
    new "Thank you [protag]. Come visit me at the citadel some time. I'm going to miss our talks.\n谢谢你，[protag]。改天来Citadel看看我吧。我会想念我们之间的谈话的。"

    old "No promises, but if I have time, I will."
    new "No promises, but if I have time, I will.\n不敢保证，但只要我有时间，就会去。"

    old "Jasper. You seem relieved."
    new "Jasper. You seem relieved.\nJasper。你看起来如释重负。"

    old "Who wouldn't be? This threat is finally over."
    new "Who wouldn't be? This threat is finally over.\n谁能不呢？这个威胁终于结束了。"

    old "What will happen now? You'll be back...being a pirate?"
    new "What will happen now? You'll be back...being a pirate?\n接下来呢？你要回去……继续当海盗？"

    old "I think so. I haven't made my mind, to be honest. I need to talk with some people first."
    new "I think so. I haven't made my mind, to be honest. I need to talk with some people first.\n我想是吧。说实话，我还没拿定主意。我得先和一些人谈谈。"

    old "He doesn't say anything more, and I decide to not insist. If he didn't tell me any more details, it means he probably doesn't want to share."
    new "He doesn't say anything more, and I decide to not insist. If he didn't tell me any more details, it means he probably doesn't want to share.\n他没再多说什么，我也决定不再追问。他既然不肯透露更多细节，多半就是不想分享。"

    old "Well, maybe we'll see again, Jasper."
    new "Well, maybe we'll see again, Jasper.\n好吧，也许我们还会再见的，Jasper。"

    old "Oh, I'm sure we will, [protag]."
    new "Oh, I'm sure we will, [protag].\n哦，我肯定我们会的，[protag]。"

    old "[protag]! This is one of the happiest days of my life!"
    new "[protag]! This is one of the happiest days of my life!\n[protag]！这是我一生中最快乐的日子之一！"

    old "I like your enthusiasm, Nuala. I am happy as well."
    new "I like your enthusiasm, Nuala. I am happy as well.\n我喜欢你的热情，Nuala。我也很高兴。"

    old "Nuala runs up to hug me, but she leaps at me with such a force that pushes me on the ground."
    new "Nuala runs up to hug me, but she leaps at me with such a force that pushes me on the ground.\nNuala跑过来要抱我，可她朝我扑来的力道太大，把我撞倒在地。"

    old "Oh sorry! I-I only wanted to—"
    new "Oh sorry! I-I only wanted to—\n哦，抱歉！我、我只是想——"

    old "Ha ha! No need to apologize, Nuala. Just lend me a hand and help me back up."
    new "Ha ha! No need to apologize, Nuala. Just lend me a hand and help me back up.\n哈哈！不必道歉，Nuala。搭把手，拉我起来就行。"

    old "What will you do now, [protag]? Will we ever see each other again?"
    new "What will you do now, [protag]? Will we ever see each other again?\n你现在要做什么，[protag]？我们还能再见面吗？"

    old "I'm not sure yet, Nuala. But I promise that if I happen to wander around the Orcish Wastes, I'll pay a visit to the Dunemarchers again."
    new "I'm not sure yet, Nuala. But I promise that if I happen to wander around the Orcish Wastes, I'll pay a visit to the Dunemarchers again.\n我还不确定，Nuala。但我保证，如果碰巧在Orcish Wastes一带游荡，我一定会再去拜访Dunemarchers。"

    old "Finally, it's over. I don't sense the evil in the air like before anymore."
    new "Finally, it's over. I don't sense the evil in the air like before anymore.\n终于结束了。我不再像以前那样，从空气中感受到那股邪恶了。"

    old "Was it painful for you, Vaeril?"
    new "Was it painful for you, Vaeril?\n那对你来说很痛苦吧，Vaeril？"

    old "Yes. We druids have an innate sensibility to dark magic and everything that's evil. It's something that we can feel. A stirring deep inside of us. I never felt anything so strong in my life before."
    new "Yes. We druids have an innate sensibility to dark magic and everything that's evil. It's something that we can feel. A stirring deep inside of us. I never felt anything so strong in my life before.\n是的。我们德鲁伊对黑暗魔法和一切邪恶之物有着天生的感知。那是一种我们能感受到的东西，一种发自内心深处的不安。我这一生还从没感受过如此强烈的东西。"

    old "I guess you're extra glad that it's over then."
    new "I guess you're extra glad that it's over then.\n那我想，这一切结束了，你该格外高兴了。"

    old "For now, [protag]. Only for now."
    new "For now, [protag]. Only for now.\n眼下是这样，[protag]。只是眼下。"

    old "Without saying anything else, Vaeril moves away from me. I must admit I'm a little worried by what he just said. But I suppose Vaeril will always be aware of the darkness that lives in our world."
    new "Without saying anything else, Vaeril moves away from me. I must admit I'm a little worried by what he just said. But I suppose Vaeril will always be aware of the darkness that lives in our world.\nVaeril没再多说什么，从我身边走开了。我必须承认，他刚才的话让我有点担忧。但我想，Vaeril大概永远都会察觉到潜藏在我们这个世界里的黑暗。"

    old "It was a nice ride, [protag]. It gave me a lot to think about."
    new "It was a nice ride, [protag]. It gave me a lot to think about.\n这一路很愉快，[protag]。它让我思考了很多。"

    old "New ways to kill the undead? After all, you have a lot of experience about killing the living, but not much about killing the dead."
    new "New ways to kill the undead? After all, you have a lot of experience about killing the living, but not much about killing the dead.\n是想出了新的杀不死生物之法？毕竟，你在杀活人方面经验丰富，杀死人却没什么经验。"

    old "Very amusing, [protag]. No, I thought about the evil of this world, and what I am doing with my skills. I... might not want to be an assassin anymore."
    new "Very amusing, [protag]. No, I thought about the evil of this world, and what I am doing with my skills. I... might not want to be an assassin anymore.\n真会开玩笑，[protag]。不，我思考的是这个世界的邪恶，以及我该拿自己的本事去做什么。我……也许不想再当刺客了。"

    old "That's surprising, Kusho."
    new "That's surprising, Kusho.\n这倒让人意外，Kusho。"

    old "I have many talents. Maybe I was using them in the wrong way. Maybe... I should become an undead hunter or something."
    new "I have many talents. Maybe I was using them in the wrong way. Maybe... I should become an undead hunter or something.\n我有许多才能。也许我用错了地方。也许……我该去当个不死生物猎人之类的。"

    old "I'll believe it when I see it."
    new "I'll believe it when I see it.\n眼见为实，我才信。"

    old "Who knows. Maybe one day we'll fight undead together again. Goodbye, [protag]."
    new "Who knows. Maybe one day we'll fight undead together again. Goodbye, [protag].\n谁知道呢。也许有一天，我们还会一起并肩对抗不死生物。再见了，[protag]。"

    old "Nothing better than crushing some undead skulls, eh [protag]! Now I'm thirsty though."
    new "Nothing better than crushing some undead skulls, eh [protag]! Now I'm thirsty though.\n没什么比砸碎不死生物的脑壳更爽的了，对吧，[protag]！不过现在我渴了。"

    old "You deserve a pint of beer. Or maybe two."
    new "You deserve a pint of beer. Or maybe two.\n你该来一品脱啤酒，或许两品脱。"

    old "Let's make three then! I am not sure I'll be allowed to drink when I'm on Mount Kronos."
    new "Let's make three then! I am not sure I'll be allowed to drink when I'm on Mount Kronos.\n那就三品脱吧！等到了Mount Kronos，我还不一定能喝酒呢。"

    old "Mount Kronos?"
    new "Mount Kronos?\nMount Kronos？"

    old "Oh I didn't tell you about it already? I'm going to spend some time there. To... learn to control my temper. I spoke with a monk, a Master Of Truth. Name's Sauzer. He offered me his help, and I accepted."
    new "Oh I didn't tell you about it already? I'm going to spend some time there. To... learn to control my temper. I spoke with a monk, a Master Of Truth. Name's Sauzer. He offered me his help, and I accepted.\n哦，我还没跟你说过吗？我要去那里待上一阵子。去……学会控制我的脾气。我和一位僧侣谈过，一位真理大师，名叫Sauzer。他主动提出帮我，我接受了。"

    old "Looks interesting. Maybe I'll come visit you sometimes."
    new "Looks interesting. Maybe I'll come visit you sometimes.\n听起来挺有意思。也许我偶尔会去看看你。"

    old "You should. You might learn a thing or two too."
    new "You should. You might learn a thing or two too.\n你该来。也许你也能学到点东西。"

    old "Ha, why stop at only two? But I'll only have fun drinking if you're there with me, [protag]."
    new "Ha, why stop at only two? But I'll only have fun drinking if you're there with me, [protag].\n哈，何必只喝两品脱？但只有你在场陪我，喝酒才有意思，[protag]。"

    old "Of course I'd be happy to buy you a drink in person. What, did you think I was going to buy you a drink and then not stay around to enjoy it with you?"
    new "Of course I'd be happy to buy you a drink in person. What, did you think I was going to buy you a drink and then not stay around to enjoy it with you?\n我当然乐意当面请你喝一杯。怎么，你以为我会请你喝酒，然后自己却不在场陪你一起享用？"

    old "Sounds like we've got a night planned out, [protag]. I look forward to it! It will be a night to remember."
    new "Sounds like we've got a night planned out, [protag]. I look forward to it! It will be a night to remember.\n听起来我们已经把那一晚安排好了，[protag]。我很期待！那会是难忘的一夜。"

    old "Do you know what the future holds next?"
    new "Do you know what the future holds next?\n你知道接下来会怎样吗？"

    old "Ah, to be honest, I haven't given it much thought. Being busy with this N'Mar business has occupied most of my attention. I suppose my next great journey will be figuring out what to do with all of this free time!"
    new "Ah, to be honest, I haven't given it much thought. Being busy with this N'Mar business has occupied most of my attention. I suppose my next great journey will be figuring out what to do with all of this free time!\n啊，说实话，我还没怎么想过。忙着处理N'Mar这档子事，占去了我大部分心思。我想，我下一段了不起的旅程，就是琢磨怎么打发这大把的空闲时间！"

    old "Dasyra? You look sad. Why is that?"
    new "Dasyra? You look sad. Why is that?\nDasyra？你看起来很难过。怎么了？"

    old "Oh? It's nothing, it's just... now that all this is over... I won't see you and the others again, right? Of course I'm happy that we won, but it feels bittersweet, in a way. I got so used to seeing you almost every day... and now, what will happen?"
    new "Oh? It's nothing, it's just... now that all this is over... I won't see you and the others again, right? Of course I'm happy that we won, but it feels bittersweet, in a way. I got so used to seeing you almost every day... and now, what will happen?\n哦？没什么，只是……如今这一切都结束了……我再也见不到你和其他人了吧？我当然为我们获胜而高兴，但某种程度上，总有些苦乐参半。我已经习惯了几乎天天见到你……而现在，又会怎样呢？"

    old "Who knows? I spoke with some of them, and they seem to have interesting plans with their lives. However, in the immediate future, I think you'll still see many of us."
    new "Who knows? I spoke with some of them, and they seem to have interesting plans with their lives. However, in the immediate future, I think you'll still see many of us.\n谁知道呢？我和其中一些人聊过，他们对自己的人生似乎有着有趣的打算。不过，在接下来一段时间里，我想你仍会见到我们中的许多人。"

    old "For example, I'm going back to Grimoire with you right now. I have to talk with the Council about my future."
    new "For example, I'm going back to Grimoire with you right now. I have to talk with the Council about my future.\n比如，我现在就要和你一起回Grimoire。我得和议会谈谈我的未来。"

    old "That sounds fun."
    new "That sounds fun.\n听起来挺有意思。"

    old "We'll see, Dasyra. We'll see."
    new "We'll see, Dasyra. We'll see.\n走着瞧吧，Dasyra。走着瞧。"

    old "You can all go. I'll be with you in a moment. I only want to stay here and look at this castle one last time before I leave."
    new "You can all go. I'll be with you in a moment. I only want to stay here and look at this castle one last time before I leave.\n你们都可以走了。我一会儿就跟上。离开之前，我只想留在这里，最后再看一眼这座城堡。"

    old "Without thinking, I start wandering in the castle. It's odd, how just a few minutes ago it was writhing with undead and now it's empty. Even the remains of the undead have crumbled to dust. The silence is almost disturbing. I find myself in the throne room where I fought Humbra before, and spot the remains of his clothes."
    new "Without thinking, I start wandering in the castle. It's odd, how just a few minutes ago it was writhing with undead and now it's empty. Even the remains of the undead have crumbled to dust. The silence is almost disturbing. I find myself in the throne room where I fought Humbra before, and spot the remains of his clothes.\n我不假思索地开始在城堡里游荡。真是奇怪，几分钟前这里还挤满蠕动的不死生物，如今却空空荡荡。连不死生物的残骸都已化为尘土。这份寂静几乎令人不安。我来到先前与Humbra交战的那间王座厅，发现了他的衣服残骸。"

    old "I hear the sound of slow clapping behind me. I turn my head and somehow I'm not surprised by who I see."
    new "I hear the sound of slow clapping behind me. I turn my head and somehow I'm not surprised by who I see.\n我听到身后传来缓慢的鼓掌声。我转过头，不知为何，对眼前所见到的人，我竟并不感到意外。"

    old "You're my hero."
    new "You're my hero.\n你是我的英雄。"

    old "Well, hero maybe is a bit of an exaggeration. After all, if wasn't for Karen you'd be dead by now. But you did a good job nonetheless."
    new "Well, hero maybe is a bit of an exaggeration. After all, if wasn't for Karen you'd be dead by now. But you did a good job nonetheless.\n嗯，“英雄”也许有点夸张了。毕竟，要不是有Karen，你现在早死了。不过，你终究做得不错。"

    old "Just how long have you been lurking here, hidden in the darkness, observing me? Observing us?"
    new "Just how long have you been lurking here, hidden in the darkness, observing me? Observing us?\n你到底躲在这里多久了？藏在黑暗里，观察我？观察我们？"

    old "Try to understand, [protag]. We invested a lot in this little endeavor, and we wanted to be sure that you managed to fulfill it. Congratulations, you didn't disappoint."
    new "Try to understand, [protag]. We invested a lot in this little endeavor, and we wanted to be sure that you managed to fulfill it. Congratulations, you didn't disappoint.\n试着理解一下，[protag]。我们在这桩小事业上投入了很多，自然想确认你能把它完成。恭喜，你没让我们失望。"

    old "I have some questions."
    new "I have some questions.\n我有些问题要问。"

    old "Questions? About what?"
    new "Questions? About what?\n问题？关于什么的？"

    old "The shadowknight, before dying. He mentioned the names of Lisbeth and Morte. Who are they?"
    new "The shadowknight, before dying. He mentioned the names of Lisbeth and Morte. Who are they?\n那个暗影骑士，临死前，提到了Lisbeth和Morte的名字。他们是谁？"

    old "Sad story."
    new "Sad story.\n真是个悲伤的故事。"

    old "Oh yes, such a sad story. I'm sure you don't want to hear it."
    new "Oh yes, such a sad story. I'm sure you don't want to hear it.\n哦，是啊，真是个悲伤的故事。我相信你不会想听的。"

    old "Oh no. Don't give me that. I want to hear all the details, and if there's ever a time when you two owed me an explanation, it's now."
    new "Oh no. Don't give me that. I want to hear all the details, and if there's ever a time when you two owed me an explanation, it's now.\n哦，不。别跟我来这套。我想听所有的细节，而且，若说你们俩什么时候欠我一个解释，那就是现在。"

    old "Whatever. If you insist... Humbra, the shadowknight. Long time ago, he was a knight. A normal one, I mean. He served under king...what was his name, again? It's been a while, and the names of ancient kings can only survive so long. Perhaps it's written in a book somewhere. Anyway, the king who ruled Icesilia. You know Icesilia, right?"
    new "Whatever. If you insist... Humbra, the shadowknight. Long time ago, he was a knight. A normal one, I mean. He served under king...what was his name, again? It's been a while, and the names of ancient kings can only survive so long. Perhaps it's written in a book somewhere. Anyway, the king who ruled Icesilia. You know Icesilia, right?\n随你便。既然你坚持……Humbra，那个暗影骑士。很久以前，他是个骑士。我是说，普通的骑士。他效力于一位国王……那国王叫什么来着？已经过去很久了，古代国王的名字也就能存留那么久。也许哪里的一本书里记着。总之，是统治Icesilia的那位国王。你知道Icesilia，对吧？"

    old "Eastern coasts of Issanis. Go on."
    new "Eastern coasts of Issanis. Go on.\nIssanis的东海岸。继续。"

    old "Really, the details of this story are not important."
    new "Really, the details of this story are not important.\n说真的，这故事的细节并不重要。"

    old "I'll be the judge of that."
    new "I'll be the judge of that.\n重不重要，由我来判断。"

    old "It's a simple story, really. Knight falls in love with a poor young lady. Lisbeth was her name. Lisbeth, she was ill. Very sick. She dies. Humbra the knight falls into a deep sorrow. A once-great man, the first knight of Icesilia, is reduced to a slovenly drunkard whose mourning knows no end."
    new "It's a simple story, really. Knight falls in love with a poor young lady. Lisbeth was her name. Lisbeth, she was ill. Very sick. She dies. Humbra the knight falls into a deep sorrow. A once-great man, the first knight of Icesilia, is reduced to a slovenly drunkard whose mourning knows no end.\n这故事其实很简单。一位骑士爱上了一位贫穷的年轻女子。她的名字叫Lisbeth。Lisbeth，她病了，病得很重。她死了。骑士Humbra陷入深深的悲痛。一位曾经了不起的人、Icesilia的第一骑士，沦为了一个沉溺于无尽哀悼、邋遢潦倒的酒鬼。"

    old "One day, Humbra the mourning drunkard is visited by a benevolent vampire. A vampire who sees the potential within him, the strength that once made him the first knight of Icesilia. This vampire sees greatness in him, greatness that will be seen by others if only it is properly molded."
    new "One day, Humbra the mourning drunkard is visited by a benevolent vampire. A vampire who sees the potential within him, the strength that once made him the first knight of Icesilia. This vampire sees greatness in him, greatness that will be seen by others if only it is properly molded.\n有一天，一位仁慈的吸血鬼拜访了沉浸在哀悼中的酒鬼Humbra。这位吸血鬼看到了他内在的潜力，看到了那份曾让他成为Icesilia第一骑士的力量。这位吸血鬼在他身上看到了伟大——只要加以适当的塑造，这份伟大终会被世人看见。"

    old "I can guess how a vampire might 'mold' someone."
    new "I can guess how a vampire might 'mold' someone.\n我能猜到吸血鬼会怎样“塑造”一个人。"

    old "Yes, Humbra was transformed into...well, something quite special. It was a process that took time. Humbra behaved like a mad horse, at first. He found himself with new powers, and was not the most responsible steward of them. He traveled all across Aravorn, finding new friends along the way."
    new "Yes, Humbra was transformed into...well, something quite special. It was a process that took time. Humbra behaved like a mad horse, at first. He found himself with new powers, and was not the most responsible steward of them. He traveled all across Aravorn, finding new friends along the way.\n没错，Humbra被转化成了……嗯，某种相当特别的东西。那是个需要时间的过程。起初，Humbra表现得像匹疯马。他发现自己拥有了新的力量，却算不上这些力量最负责任的主人。他游历了整个Aravorn，沿途结识新的朋友。"

    old "The vampire lieutenants we encountered."
    new "The vampire lieutenants we encountered.\n就是那些我们遇到的吸血鬼副官。"

    old "Yes. This wandering band of misfits happened upon a decrepit old castle, located on a peninsula. A perfect place to call home, far away from the nearest town, yet close enough to go out hunting during full moons."
    new "Yes. This wandering band of misfits happened upon a decrepit old castle, located on a peninsula. A perfect place to call home, far away from the nearest town, yet close enough to go out hunting during full moons.\n是的。这群四处漂泊的怪人，偶然发现了一座破败的旧城堡，坐落在一处半岛上。那是安家的绝佳之地，离最近的城镇很远，却又近到能在满月时外出狩猎。"

    old "Castle N'Mar."
    new "Castle N'Mar.\nN'Mar城堡。"

    old "You keep interrupting my story."
    new "You keep interrupting my story.\n你总在打断我的故事。"

    old "I'm just confirming the details."
    new "I'm just confirming the details.\n我只是在确认细节。"

    old "Humbra and his friends called this castle home for...well, quite awhile. Years, centuries, they all sort of run together. Their lives, or undeath, rather, had no real meaning until someone important showed up."
    new "Humbra and his friends called this castle home for...well, quite awhile. Years, centuries, they all sort of run together. Their lives, or undeath, rather, had no real meaning until someone important showed up.\nHumbra和他的朋友们把这座城堡当成了家，住了……嗯，相当长一段时间。多少年、多少世纪，都混在一起分不清了。他们的生命，或者说他们的不死之身，一直毫无意义，直到某个重要人物出现。"

    old "Morte."
    new "Morte.\nMorte。"

    old "Yes, old mother Morte. A powerful being. A necromancer, perhaps. Strong, and manipulative. Morte works her way into Humbra's ear. Humbra, the man who is still, after all these years, mourning the loss of his precious Lisbeth."
    new "Yes, old mother Morte. A powerful being. A necromancer, perhaps. Strong, and manipulative. Morte works her way into Humbra's ear. Humbra, the man who is still, after all these years, mourning the loss of his precious Lisbeth.\n没错，老母亲Morte。一个强大的存在，也许是个死灵法师。强大，且善于操控人心。Morte一点一点地钻进Humbra的耳朵里。而Humbra，这个男人，即便过了这么多年，仍在为他心爱的Lisbeth之死而哀悼。"

    old "She makes him an offer he can't refuse."
    new "She makes him an offer he can't refuse.\n她向他开出了一个他无法拒绝的条件。"

    old "Yes, as all good necromancers do, Morte knows that Humbra's own existence is not as important to him as that of Lisbeth."
    new "Yes, as all good necromancers do, Morte knows that Humbra's own existence is not as important to him as that of Lisbeth.\n是的，正如所有出色的死灵法师那样，Morte知道，对Humbra来说，他自己的存在，远不如Lisbeth来得重要。"

    old "Morte can bring Lisbeth back from the Underrealm. That's what she claims, anyway."
    new "Morte can bring Lisbeth back from the Underrealm. That's what she claims, anyway.\nMorte能把Lisbeth从Underrealm带回来。反正她是这么声称的。"

    old "Can she?"
    new "Can she?\n她能吗？"

    old "Does it matter? What matters is that she has ways of persuading Humbra that she can bring Lisbeth back. And Humbra believes her. All she asks in exchange is a small favor. A minor task, really."
    new "Does it matter? What matters is that she has ways of persuading Humbra that she can bring Lisbeth back. And Humbra believes her. All she asks in exchange is a small favor. A minor task, really.\n这重要吗？重要的是，她有办法让Humbra相信她能带回Lisbeth，而Humbra也信了她。她索取的回报，只是一个小小的恩惠。真的只是件小事。"

    old "You say 'minor.' I'm willing to guess it isn't quite so minor."
    new "You say 'minor.' I'm willing to guess it isn't quite so minor.\n你说“小事”。我敢猜，这可没那么小。"

    old "All Morte wants in exchange for Lisbeth's soul is for Humbra to lead Morte's undead army to defeat the Human Empire."
    new "All Morte wants in exchange for Lisbeth's soul is for Humbra to lead Morte's undead army to defeat the Human Empire.\nMorte想用Lisbeth的灵魂换取的，就是让Humbra率领她的不死大军，去击败人类帝国。"

    old "Why would Morte want to destroy the Human Empire? Why humans, specifically?"
    new "Why would Morte want to destroy the Human Empire? Why humans, specifically?\nMorte为什么要摧毁人类帝国？为什么偏偏是人类？"

    old "Who knows? I am old, but only a few centuries. Morte must be older than I am. Something between her and the Empire must have happened centuries ago, and Morte seems like the sort to hold a grudge. Anyways: Humbra accepts, and thanks to Morte teachings, he becomes a shadowknight: a creature of darkness with powerful magical abilities."
    new "Who knows? I am old, but only a few centuries. Morte must be older than I am. Something between her and the Empire must have happened centuries ago, and Morte seems like the sort to hold a grudge. Anyways: Humbra accepts, and thanks to Morte teachings, he becomes a shadowknight: a creature of darkness with powerful magical abilities.\n谁知道呢？我虽老，但也只活了几百年。Morte肯定比我更年长。几个世纪前，她和帝国之间一定发生过什么，而Morte看上去正是那种会记仇的人。总之：Humbra接受了，在Morte的教导下，他成了暗影骑士——一个拥有强大魔法力量的黑暗生物。"

    old "The other vampires who disagree are either killed or thrown out from the castle. Humbra has only ears for Morte now. He doesn't care anymore about the others, even his long time friends."
    new "The other vampires who disagree are either killed or thrown out from the castle. Humbra has only ears for Morte now. He doesn't care anymore about the others, even his long time friends.\n其他不同意的吸血鬼，要么被杀，要么被赶出城堡。Humbra现在只听Morte一个人的话。他不再在乎其他人，哪怕是他多年的老友。"

    old "So, Humbra was only a pawn in all of this. Mother Morte was the one pulling the strings all along."
    new "So, Humbra was only a pawn in all of this. Mother Morte was the one pulling the strings all along.\n所以，Humbra在这整件事里不过是个棋子。自始至终在幕后操纵一切的，是Morte母亲。"

    old "Yes. Even the mist was her magic. I have to admit that that was a good idea. But I wouldn't worry too much. Though her powers are strong, she needs helpers. Morte, it would seem, is good at creating undead armies, but she can only furnish the raw material."
    new "Yes. Even the mist was her magic. I have to admit that that was a good idea. But I wouldn't worry too much. Though her powers are strong, she needs helpers. Morte, it would seem, is good at creating undead armies, but she can only furnish the raw material.\n是的。连那场雾都是她的魔法。我得承认，那确实是个好主意。不过我也不会太担心。虽然她的力量很强，但她需要帮手。Morte，看起来，很擅长制造亡灵大军，但她只能提供原材料。"

    old "When it comes to commanding undead, she needs the help of a shadowknight, or perhaps a vampire. That's why it was't until recently that she became a real threat. The vampires living in castle N'Mar may not have been the root cause of all of this, but they certainly catalyzed it."
    new "When it comes to commanding undead, she needs the help of a shadowknight, or perhaps a vampire. That's why it was't until recently that she became a real threat. The vampires living in castle N'Mar may not have been the root cause of all of this, but they certainly catalyzed it.\n说到指挥亡灵，她需要暗影骑士的帮助，或者也许是一个吸血鬼。这就是为什么直到最近她才成为真正的威胁。住在 N'Mar 城堡里的吸血鬼也许不是这一切的根源，但他们无疑起到了催化作用。"

    old "It is a recipe that requires three parts: Morte the necromancer can raise the dead, but evidently she cannot control them herself outside the castle. And vampires can command the dead, but not raise them. And vampires can control a limited number of undead, but to command an army required a number of vampires, all working toward a single common goal."
    new "It is a recipe that requires three parts: Morte the necromancer can raise the dead, but evidently she cannot control them herself outside the castle. And vampires can command the dead, but not raise them. And vampires can control a limited number of undead, but to command an army required a number of vampires, all working toward a single common goal.\n这道配方需要三样东西：死灵法师 Morte 能够唤醒死者，但显然她自己无法在城堡外控制它们。而吸血鬼能够指挥死者，却无法唤醒它们。而且吸血鬼能控制的亡灵数量有限，要指挥一支军队，就需要众多吸血鬼，全都朝着同一个共同目标努力。"

    old "It was only when the three intersected, when a shadowknight managed to gain the loyalty of some vampire 'friends,' and Morte managed to manipulate a shadowknight to do her bidding, that the Human Empire came to face an existential threat."
    new "It was only when the three intersected, when a shadowknight managed to gain the loyalty of some vampire 'friends,' and Morte managed to manipulate a shadowknight to do her bidding, that the Human Empire came to face an existential threat.\n只有当这三者交汇之时——当一个暗影骑士设法赢得了某些吸血鬼“朋友”的忠诚，而 Morte 又设法操纵一个暗影骑士为她效力时——人类帝国才真正面对了生死存亡的威胁。"

    old "What a sad story."
    new "What a sad story.\n多么悲伤的故事啊。"

    old "A sad story indeed. Morte preyed on Humbra's sorrows and turned him into her pawn. To think, all of this was because of Humbra's love for Lisbeth. He never finished mourning her death. And in the end, he lost everything. He lost the peace that he had managed to find in N'Mar. He lost the only friends who had ever cared about him."
    new "A sad story indeed. Morte preyed on Humbra's sorrows and turned him into her pawn. To think, all of this was because of Humbra's love for Lisbeth. He never finished mourning her death. And in the end, he lost everything. He lost the peace that he had managed to find in N'Mar. He lost the only friends who had ever cared about him.\n的确是个悲伤的故事。Morte 利用了 Humbra 的悲伤，把他变成了她的棋子。想想看，这一切都是因为 Humbra 对 Lisbeth 的爱。他始终没能走出她去世的哀痛。到最后，他失去了一切。他失去了在 N'Mar 好不容易找到的平静。他失去了唯一曾关心过他的朋友们。"

    old "Those friends wouldn't happen to be you, would they?"
    new "Those friends wouldn't happen to be you, would they?\n那些朋友，该不会就是你吧？"

    old "Smart. Very smart."
    new "Smart. Very smart.\n聪明。非常聪明。"

    old "Yes, [protag]. Of course you would figure it out. You see, I was the one who turned Humbra into a vampire. We came to N'Mar, and in the process of looking for more company, I turned Valery."
    new "Yes, [protag]. Of course you would figure it out. You see, I was the one who turned Humbra into a vampire. We came to N'Mar, and in the process of looking for more company, I turned Valery.\n没错，[protag]。你当然会想明白。你看，是我把 Humbra 变成了吸血鬼。我们来到 N'Mar，在寻找更多同伴的过程中，我把 Valery 也变成了吸血鬼。"

    old "You haven't yet earned an explanation of all the details, but suffice it to say, what we had together was something special. Humbra, for all of the anguish and grief that tormented him through the years, was a dear friend. And nothing made me sadder than the day when Mother Morte began to whisper foolish lies into Humbra's ear."
    new "You haven't yet earned an explanation of all the details, but suffice it to say, what we had together was something special. Humbra, for all of the anguish and grief that tormented him through the years, was a dear friend. And nothing made me sadder than the day when Mother Morte began to whisper foolish lies into Humbra's ear.\n你还没资格听到所有细节的解释，不过这么说就够了：我们曾经拥有的东西很特别。Humbra，尽管多年来被痛苦和悲伤所折磨，他仍是我亲爱的朋友。而最让我难过的，莫过于 Morte 母亲开始往 Humbra 耳朵里低语那些愚蠢谎言的那一天。"

    old "So you see, [protag], we never wanted any of this. All of this death and destruction. There was no reason behind it. But Humbra wouldn't listen to reason. His mind was corrupted by Morte, and there was no persuading him, or all of the stupid lesser vampires who followed him."
    new "So you see, [protag], we never wanted any of this. All of this death and destruction. There was no reason behind it. But Humbra wouldn't listen to reason. His mind was corrupted by Morte, and there was no persuading him, or all of the stupid lesser vampires who followed him.\n所以你明白了吧，[protag]，我们从来不想要这一切。所有这些死亡与毁灭。这一切背后没有任何理由。但 Humbra 不肯听劝。他的心被 Morte 腐蚀了，无论怎么劝都没用——劝不动他，也劝不动那些跟随他的愚蠢低阶吸血鬼。"

    old "When we first met, you made it sound as though you were part of some petty political squabble. I never realized that your relationship with Humbra ran so deep. That you were the one who created him. I never realized that I was part of a revenge plot."
    new "When we first met, you made it sound as though you were part of some petty political squabble. I never realized that your relationship with Humbra ran so deep. That you were the one who created him. I never realized that I was part of a revenge plot.\n我们第一次见面时，你把它说得像是卷入了一场微不足道的政治纠纷。我从没意识到你和 Humbra 的关系竟然如此之深。也从没意识到是你创造了他。我从没意识到，我成了一桩复仇阴谋的一部分。"

    old "Revenge? [protag], do you really believe that I wanted revenge against Humbra? Even now, seeing his unmaking brings me anguish."
    new "Revenge? [protag], do you really believe that I wanted revenge against Humbra? Even now, seeing his unmaking brings me anguish.\n复仇？[protag]，你真的以为我想对 Humbra 复仇吗？即使是现在，看着他走向毁灭也让我痛苦不堪。"

    old "But you lied to me."
    new "But you lied to me.\n可你骗了我。"

    old "I told you what I thought you needed to hear in order for your mission - for our mission - to be a success. Your people are safe. What do you have to complain about?"
    new "I told you what I thought you needed to hear in order for your mission - for our mission - to be a success. Your people are safe. What do you have to complain about?\n我只是把我觉得你需要听到的话告诉了你，好让你的任务——我们共同的任务——能够成功。你的人平安无事。你还有什么可抱怨的？"

    old "Or perhaps I should say...your former people? You're one of us now, after all."
    new "Or perhaps I should say...your former people? You're one of us now, after all.\n或者我该说……你从前的人民？毕竟，你现在是我们中的一员了。"

    old "What will you do now?"
    new "What will you do now?\n你现在打算做什么？"

    old "We're staying here. There's a vacant property, and I can't see anyone wanting to live here except us."
    new "We're staying here. There's a vacant property, and I can't see anyone wanting to live here except us.\n我们会留在这里。这里有一处空置的房产，而且除了我们，我看不出还有谁会想住在这儿。"

    old "But the real question is... what are YOU doing now, [protag]? Now you're a vampire too. You can't go back to Grimoire, they'd kill you on sight, no matter what you did for them. They will never trust you again."
    new "But the real question is... what are YOU doing now, [protag]? Now you're a vampire too. You can't go back to Grimoire, they'd kill you on sight, no matter what you did for them. They will never trust you again.\n但真正的问题是……[protag]，你现在打算做什么？现在你也是吸血鬼了。你回不去 Grimoire 了，他们一见到你就会杀了你，不管你为他们做过什么。他们永远不会再信任你了。"

    old "Don't worry. I have a special someone waiting for me."
    new "Don't worry. I have a special someone waiting for me.\n别担心。有个特别的人在等着我。"

    old "Very well. We'll let you go then, as token of gratitude for what you did. But don't dare to interfere with our plans or even come here again, uninvited."
    new "Very well. We'll let you go then, as token of gratitude for what you did. But don't dare to interfere with our plans or even come here again, uninvited.\n很好。那么我们就放你走，当作对你所做之事的感谢。但你可别胆敢干涉我们的计划，更别不请自来地再回到这里。"

    old "I won't, trust me. I have had enough of this place."
    new "I won't, trust me. I have had enough of this place.\n我不会的，相信我。我已经受够这个地方了。"

    old "Oh, isn't [heshe] cute, Valery?"
    new "Oh, isn't [heshe] cute, Valery?\n哦，Valery，[heshe] 是不是很可爱？"

    old "Very cute."
    new "Very cute.\n非常可爱。"

    old "That could be a possibility, yes..."
    new "That could be a possibility, yes...\n那倒是有可能，没错……"

    old "Friends are good to have."
    new "Friends are good to have.\n有朋友是件好事。"

    old "The other side?"
    new "The other side?\n另一边？"

    old "Over Everburn mountains. In the Forest Of Howlgrove perhaps. Or Icesilia, maybe. I haven't made my mind yet. But I'm not staying on this side of the continent."
    new "Over Everburn mountains. In the Forest Of Howlgrove perhaps. Or Icesilia, maybe. I haven't made my mind yet. But I'm not staying on this side of the continent.\n越过 Everburn 山脉。也许在 Forest Of Howlgrove。或者 Icesilia，说不定。我还没拿定主意。但我不打算留在大陆的这一边。"

    old "Afraid to be hunted down?"
    new "Afraid to be hunted down?\n害怕被追杀吗？"

    old "No, I'm afraid to hurt people I know."
    new "No, I'm afraid to hurt people I know.\n不，我是怕伤害到我认识的人。"

    old "You see, [protag], the thing is that what you want is not really important. What's important is what WE want."
    new "You see, [protag], the thing is that what you want is not really important. What's important is what WE want.\n你看，[protag]，问题在于你想要什么其实并不重要。重要的是我们想要什么。"

    old "And we have decided that you show a lot of potential. You must stay with us, here, on N'Mar. Yes you have a lot of potential, but such potential could be easily wasted. We'll teach you everything. How to avoid all the new dangers you'll have to face as vampire."
    new "And we have decided that you show a lot of potential. You must stay with us, here, on N'Mar. Yes you have a lot of potential, but such potential could be easily wasted. We'll teach you everything. How to avoid all the new dangers you'll have to face as vampire.\n而我们已经认定，你展现出很大的潜力。你必须和我们一起留在这里，留在 N'Mar。没错，你潜力很大，但这种潜力很容易被浪费。我们会把一切都教给你。教你如何避开作为吸血鬼将要面对的所有新危险。"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. You just turned. It's normal to feel confused. Now, you should start to feel hungry though..."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. You just turned. It's normal to feel confused. Now, you should start to feel hungry though...\n别担心，[protag]。你才刚刚转化。感到困惑是正常的。不过现在，你应该开始感到饿了……"

    old "I... yes...I've already started to feel it..."
    new "I... yes...I've already started to feel it...\n我……是的……我已经开始有感觉了……"

    old "Luckily we have taken care of your meal for you. Just this time."
    new "Luckily we have taken care of your meal for you. Just this time.\n幸运的是，我们已经替你准备好了晚餐。仅此一次。"

    old "What... who..."
    new "What... who...\n什么……谁……"

    old "Zachary brings forward an orc, with hands and legs tied. Despite his size, he is trembling in fear."
    new "Zachary brings forward an orc, with hands and legs tied. Despite his size, he is trembling in fear.\nZachary 带上来一个兽人，手脚都被绑着。尽管他块头不小，却吓得浑身发抖。"

    old "We thought to make it easy for you, since it's your first time. An evil orc, you see? He must have killed a lot of innocents around Horus. He deserves it, right?"
    new "We thought to make it easy for you, since it's your first time. An evil orc, you see? He must have killed a lot of innocents around Horus. He deserves it, right?\n我们想着让你轻松一点，毕竟这是你的第一次。一个邪恶的兽人，你看？他肯定在 Horus 一带杀害了很多无辜的人。他罪有应得，对吧？"

    old "Evil, evil orc. Nice meal for us."
    new "Evil, evil orc. Nice meal for us.\n邪恶的、邪恶的兽人。给我们的一顿美餐。"

    old "I... I... yes! It would be no different from killing an animal for its meat."
    new "I... I... yes! It would be no different from killing an animal for its meat.\n我……我……没错！这和杀一只动物取它的肉没什么两样。"

    old "Good! You need to hurry now, because Valery and I are hungry as well..."
    new "Good! You need to hurry now, because Valery and I are hungry as well...\n很好！你现在得快点，因为 Valery 和我也都饿了……"

    old "I join them as we feast over the orc, who screams in pain. In a few minutes everything is over. I only wanted to feed. That's all I was thinking of."
    new "I join them as we feast over the orc, who screams in pain. In a few minutes everything is over. I only wanted to feed. That's all I was thinking of.\n我加入他们，一起享用那个痛苦尖叫的兽人。几分钟后，一切都结束了。我只想进食。那是我脑子里唯一的念头。"

    old "Deep down, I knew that something like this was waiting for me. I was prepared to be freaked out by the idea of feeding as a vampire. But it doesn't seem to bother me at all, and perhaps that is the most disturbing thing of all."
    new "Deep down, I knew that something like this was waiting for me. I was prepared to be freaked out by the idea of feeding as a vampire. But it doesn't seem to bother me at all, and perhaps that is the most disturbing thing of all.\n内心深处，我知道这样的事在等着我。我本以为自己会因身为吸血鬼进食的想法而惊惧。但这似乎一点也不困扰我，而这或许才是最令人不安的地方。"

    old "And, I'm sorry to inform you that we have decided you must die, now."
    new "And, I'm sorry to inform you that we have decided you must die, now.\n另外，很抱歉地通知你，我们已经决定你必须死了，就现在。"

    old "You're too dangerous. You need to die."
    new "You're too dangerous. You need to die.\n你太危险了。你必须死。"

    old "As my beloved Valery said. You showed potential, a lot of potential. Too much. And you also disagree with us too often, we can't trust you. Can you see where this is going? We simply cannot allow a new, powerful vampire like you, to exist. You're a clear menace for both of us."
    new "As my beloved Valery said. You showed potential, a lot of potential. Too much. And you also disagree with us too often, we can't trust you. Can you see where this is going? We simply cannot allow a new, powerful vampire like you, to exist. You're a clear menace for both of us.\n正如我挚爱的 Valery 所说。你展现出了潜力，很大的潜力。太大了。而且你总是跟我们唱反调，我们没法信任你。你看得出来事情会往哪发展吗？我们绝不能允许像你这样崭新而强大的吸血鬼存在。对我们两个来说，你都是个明显的威胁。"

    old "You'll regret this choice!"
    new "You'll regret this choice!\n你们会后悔这个选择的！"

    old "Oh no, [protag]. You'll be the one to regret it."
    new "Oh no, [protag]. You'll be the one to regret it.\n哦不，[protag]。要后悔的人会是你。"

    old "I feel powerful, but still they're two against one. The odds are against me. Even if I'm a vampire now, I haven't forgot all the pragmatism that kept me alive before. So I decide to do the only sensible choice in this moment."
    new "I feel powerful, but still they're two against one. The odds are against me. Even if I'm a vampire now, I haven't forgot all the pragmatism that kept me alive before. So I decide to do the only sensible choice in this moment.\n我感到自己很强大，但他们毕竟是二对一。形势对我很不利。即使我现在成了吸血鬼，我也没有忘记从前让我活下来的那些务实之道。于是我决定做出此刻唯一明智的选择。"

    old "What? Stop! Where are you going?"
    new "What? Stop! Where are you going?\n什么？站住！你要去哪儿？"

    old "I run and jump against a window, destroying the glass and falling outside. I land in the waters below, and immediately I look up. They aren't following me."
    new "I run and jump against a window, destroying the glass and falling outside. I land in the waters below, and immediately I look up. They aren't following me.\n我跑起来，撞向一扇窗户，撞碎玻璃，跌落到外面。我落在下面的水里，随即抬头望去。他们没有追上来。"

    old "I start swimming, and once I'm on dry ground, I walk into a small forest. I start looking for some wildlife to feed, since I feel hungry."
    new "I start swimming, and once I'm on dry ground, I walk into a small forest. I start looking for some wildlife to feed, since I feel hungry.\n我开始游水，等到了干燥的陆地上，我便走进一片小森林。我开始寻找野生动物来进食，因为我感到饿了。"

    old "Time passes, and I remain careful, still on guard. But I can't see any trace of Zachary and Valery. Perhaps they decided to give up on me. It's unlikely, but that seems the case. Or maybe I'm far enough away that they don't know where to look for me. Perhaps they're convinced that I simply won't be able to survive on my own."
    new "Time passes, and I remain careful, still on guard. But I can't see any trace of Zachary and Valery. Perhaps they decided to give up on me. It's unlikely, but that seems the case. Or maybe I'm far enough away that they don't know where to look for me. Perhaps they're convinced that I simply won't be able to survive on my own.\n时间流逝，我依然小心翼翼，保持着警惕。但我看不到 Zachary 和 Valery 的任何踪迹。也许他们决定放弃我了。这不太可能，但看起来就是如此。又或者我已经走得足够远，他们不知道去哪里找我。也许他们认定我根本没法独自活下去。"

    old "I'd like to prove them wrong."
    new "I'd like to prove them wrong.\n我倒是很想证明他们错了。"

    old "Of course, I don't really approve that two new vampires are taking home in N'Mar again. But I'm too tired now, and I'm alone. I better play along with them."
    new "Of course, I don't really approve that two new vampires are taking home in N'Mar again. But I'm too tired now, and I'm alone. I better play along with them.\n当然，我其实并不赞同又有两个新吸血鬼在 N'Mar 安家。但我现在太累了，而且孤身一人。我最好还是顺着他们。"

    old "I see. Well, it's not my concern anymore. I did what the Council wanted me to do. And I suppose you won't be so foolish to start another war like Humbra tried to."
    new "I see. Well, it's not my concern anymore. I did what the Council wanted me to do. And I suppose you won't be so foolish to start another war like Humbra tried to.\n我明白了。好吧，这不再与我有关了。我做了议会要我做的事。而且我想，你们应该不会蠢到像 Humbra 那样再挑起一场战争。"

    old "Of course not! We're not stupid. We care about our survival. We will wait some time before settling here. I am sure the Empire will want to inspect this place well in the coming weeks. I don't know what they're hoping to find though."
    new "Of course not! We're not stupid. We care about our survival. We will wait some time before settling here. I am sure the Empire will want to inspect this place well in the coming weeks. I don't know what they're hoping to find though.\n当然不会！我们又不傻。我们在乎自己的生存。我们会等上一段时间再在这里定居。我相信未来几周里，帝国会想好好检查这个地方。不过我不知道他们指望能找到什么。"

    old "Well, this is where we say goodbye."
    new "Well, this is where we say goodbye.\n好了，我们就在此道别吧。"

    old "Goodbye [protag]. And thanks for your help."
    new "Goodbye [protag]. And thanks for your help.\n再见，[protag]。谢谢你帮忙。"

    old "Good bye. And good riddance."
    new "Good bye. And good riddance.\n再见。总算摆脱你们了。"

    old "The thought briefly crosses my mind that perhaps the Council would like to hear about Zachary and Valery. Should I tell them?"
    new "The thought briefly crosses my mind that perhaps the Council would like to hear about Zachary and Valery. Should I tell them?\n一个念头在我脑中一闪而过：也许议会会想听听关于 Zachary 和 Valery 的事。我要不要告诉他们呢？"

    old "The idea of being tasked by the council with killing these two doesn't seem like such an unpleasant outcome...I've gotten pretty good at killing vampires. Maybe I should plan on adding two more to the body count."
    new "The idea of being tasked by the council with killing these two doesn't seem like such an unpleasant outcome...I've gotten pretty good at killing vampires. Maybe I should plan on adding two more to the body count.\n被议会指派去杀掉这两个人，这样的结果似乎并不那么让人不快……我对杀吸血鬼已经相当在行了。也许我该打算着再把这两个也加进击杀名单。"

    old "I leave the castle with a bit of sadness. This will probably be the last time that I see Zachary and Valery. Even if they were using me every step of the way, in the end, they helped me in my mission. And as odd as our relationship has been, I can't help but feel that I'm going to miss those two."
    new "I leave the castle with a bit of sadness. This will probably be the last time that I see Zachary and Valery. Even if they were using me every step of the way, in the end, they helped me in my mission. And as odd as our relationship has been, I can't help but feel that I'm going to miss those two.\n我带着一丝伤感离开了城堡。这大概会是我最后一次见到 Zachary 和 Valery。即便他们一路都在利用我，到最后，他们还是在我的任务中帮了忙。而尽管我们的关系一直很古怪，我还是忍不住觉得，我会想念这两个人。"

    old "Was dealing with these two vampires the right thing to do? Perhaps I'll never know. They used me, and in a way, I used them. It was a relationship born out of convenience, out of mutual interest."
    new "Was dealing with these two vampires the right thing to do? Perhaps I'll never know. They used me, and in a way, I used them. It was a relationship born out of convenience, out of mutual interest.\n与这两个吸血鬼打交道是对的吗？也许我永远都不会知道。他们利用了我，而在某种意义上，我也利用了他们。这是一段因便利、因共同利益而生的关系。"

    old "I've heard it said that the enemy of my enemy is my friend. But without a common enemy to unite us any longer, it seems that it's time for my relationship with them to come to an end."
    new "I've heard it said that the enemy of my enemy is my friend. But without a common enemy to unite us any longer, it seems that it's time for my relationship with them to come to an end.\n我听过一句话：我敌人的敌人就是我的朋友。但如今既然不再有共同的敌人把我们团结在一起，看来是时候让我和他们的关系到此为止了。"

    old "I head to the hill memorial. Coming to see it now in person seems only right, considering the role that I played in its preservation."
    new "I head to the hill memorial. Coming to see it now in person seems only right, considering the role that I played in its preservation.\n我前往山丘纪念碑。考虑到我在保护它这件事上出过一份力，现在亲自来看看它，似乎再合适不过。"

    old "Cedric is at the tomb when I arrive."
    new "Cedric is at the tomb when I arrive.\n我到达时，Cedric 就在墓前。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Here to pay your respects?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Here to pay your respects?\n啊，[protag]。来吊唁的吗？"

    old "It seemed only right."
    new "It seemed only right.\n这似乎再合适不过。"

    old "If you came here hoping for some kind of enlightening or transcendent experience, you might walk away disappointed. There is nothing mystical about this site. It's just a symbol."
    new "If you came here hoping for some kind of enlightening or transcendent experience, you might walk away disappointed. There is nothing mystical about this site. It's just a symbol.\n如果你来这里，是希望获得某种启迪或超凡的体验，那你可能会失望而归。这个地方没有任何神秘之处。它只是一个象征。"

    old "Then why are you so adamant about defending its preservation?"
    new "Then why are you so adamant about defending its preservation?\n那你为什么如此坚决地捍卫它的存续？"

    old "The tomb doesn't need to be mystical to be powerful. You might not experience anything enlightening here, or transcendental."
    new "The tomb doesn't need to be mystical to be powerful. You might not experience anything enlightening here, or transcendental.\n这座墓不需要神秘才有力量。你在这里也许不会经历任何启迪，也不会有任何超凡的体验。"

    old "But I've seen soldiers come here and break down weeping. I've seen the families of soldiers, in some cases widows with their children, come and have the same powerful experience. It brings something out in people. There's nothing magical about it, but that doesn't mean those feelings aren't any less real."
    new "But I've seen soldiers come here and break down weeping. I've seen the families of soldiers, in some cases widows with their children, come and have the same powerful experience. It brings something out in people. There's nothing magical about it, but that doesn't mean those feelings aren't any less real.\n但我见过士兵们来到这里，泣不成声。我见过士兵们的家人，有些是带着孩子的寡妇，来到这里，同样经历那种强烈的情感。它会唤起人心中某些东西。这没有任何魔力，但这并不意味着那些情感就不真实。"

    old "So, the tomb isn't for people like me?"
    new "So, the tomb isn't for people like me?\n所以，这座墓不是为我这样的人准备的？"

    old "I didn't say that."
    new "I didn't say that.\n我可没这么说。"

    old "You see, the memorial serves another purpose. It is to remind us of the loss of life that comes with war. And I think it may be those who see no combat that need that reminder the most."
    new "You see, the memorial serves another purpose. It is to remind us of the loss of life that comes with war. And I think it may be those who see no combat that need that reminder the most.\n你看，这座纪念碑还有另一个用途。它是为了提醒我们，战争会带来生命的逝去。而我认为，或许最需要这种提醒的，恰恰是那些没有上过战场的人。"

    old "The soldier on the ground has no need for a structure to remind him of his own mortality. No, he faces that every day in combat."
    new "The soldier on the ground has no need for a structure to remind him of his own mortality. No, he faces that every day in combat.\n身处战场的士兵不需要一座建筑来提醒他自己的生命会消逝。不，他每天都在战斗中直面这一点。"

    old "It is the people at home. The loggers. The bakers. And even the metalworkers who coveted this hill so much they were willing to displace the memorial. This memorial is here to serve as a reminder to them, what exactly the cost of war is."
    new "It is the people at home. The loggers. The bakers. And even the metalworkers who coveted this hill so much they were willing to displace the memorial. This memorial is here to serve as a reminder to them, what exactly the cost of war is.\n需要提醒的是待在家里的人。是伐木工、面包师，甚至还有那些如此觊觎这座山、以至于愿意把纪念碑迁走的金属工匠。这座纪念碑立在这里，就是为了提醒他们，战争的代价究竟是什么。"

    old "This memorial commemorates the dead. It is a reminder to all of us that war is not something to stumble into wantonly. War is deadly. War is bloody. War is gruesome. War is heartbreaking. And sometimes, war is necessary."
    new "This memorial commemorates the dead. It is a reminder to all of us that war is not something to stumble into wantonly. War is deadly. War is bloody. War is gruesome. War is heartbreaking. And sometimes, war is necessary.\n这座纪念碑纪念逝者。它提醒我们所有人，战争不是可以轻率闯入的事。战争是致命的。战争是血腥的。战争是残酷的。战争令人心碎。而有时，战争又是必要的。"

    old "When people see this tomb, I hope they think of that. I hope they think of all of the men who died on the battlefield. And I hope that the pain and anguish of those lost lives registers for some of those observers."
    new "When people see this tomb, I hope they think of that. I hope they think of all of the men who died on the battlefield. And I hope that the pain and anguish of those lost lives registers for some of those observers.\n当人们看到这座墓时，我希望他们能想到这些。我希望他们能想到所有战死在沙场上的人。我也希望那些逝去生命所承受的痛苦与哀伤，能触动其中一些观者的心。"

    old "This memorial is not here to glorify war. The memorial is here to to remind us of war's immense cost."
    new "This memorial is not here to glorify war. The memorial is here to to remind us of war's immense cost.\n这座纪念碑不是来颂扬战争的。它立在这里，是为了提醒我们战争所付出的巨大代价。"

    old "That is why I fought so adamantly to see this memorial preserved. And I think that many men, especially those who know what it truly means to see their fellows sacrifice their lives in combat, will appreciate what you've done here. Those men want to know that their sacrifice will be acknowledged. That's what this memorial is here for."
    new "That is why I fought so adamantly to see this memorial preserved. And I think that many men, especially those who know what it truly means to see their fellows sacrifice their lives in combat, will appreciate what you've done here. Those men want to know that their sacrifice will be acknowledged. That's what this memorial is here for.\n这就是为什么我如此坚决地争取让这座纪念碑保留下来。而且我认为，许多人——尤其是那些真正懂得看着同伴在战斗中牺牲意味着什么的人——会感激你在这里所做的一切。那些人希望知道，他们的牺牲会被铭记。这就是这座纪念碑存在的意义。"

    old "The evil that lurks within N'Mar again demands that we ask our men to take up arms. Some of them will die for this cause. It is a worthy cause. But that shouldn't mean that our decision to go to war is an easy one."
    new "The evil that lurks within N'Mar again demands that we ask our men to take up arms. Some of them will die for this cause. It is a worthy cause. But that shouldn't mean that our decision to go to war is an easy one.\n潜伏在 N'Mar 中的邪恶再次要求我们让士兵们拿起武器。他们中的一些人会为这项事业而死。这是一项值得的事业。但这不应该意味着我们开战的决定是个轻松的决定。"

    old "I can't think of anything to say, so I bow my head in a nod of acknowledgment."
    new "I can't think of anything to say, so I bow my head in a nod of acknowledgment.\n我想不出该说什么，于是低下头，点头表示认同。"

    old "You've supported my cause, and now I can support yours. This will mostly come in the form of veteran leadership."
    new "You've supported my cause, and now I can support yours. This will mostly come in the form of veteran leadership.\n你支持过我的事业，现在我可以支持你的事业了。这种支持主要会以老练的领军之道体现出来。"

    old "I appreciate that."
    new "I appreciate that.\n我很感激。"

    old "I head to the site of the hill memorial. Builders have already begun tearing up the ground around the edges of the site, but the tomb itself still stands. A familiar man stands watching them, and he turns to face me."
    new "I head to the site of the hill memorial. Builders have already begun tearing up the ground around the edges of the site, but the tomb itself still stands. A familiar man stands watching them, and he turns to face me.\n我前往山丘纪念碑的所在地。工人们已经开始在场地边缘的地面上动土了，但墓本身依然屹立着。一个熟悉的人站在那里看着他们，随后转身面向我。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Come to pay your last respects?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Come to pay your last respects?\n啊，[protag]。来作最后的吊唁吗？"

    old "It seemed to be the proper thing to do, all things considered."
    new "It seemed to be the proper thing to do, all things considered.\n凡事考虑周全之后，这似乎是件该做的事。"

    old "I like that phrase. 'All things considered.' It's a powerful phrase. I hope you don't use it too carelessly."
    new "I like that phrase. 'All things considered.' It's a powerful phrase. I hope you don't use it too carelessly.\n我喜欢那句话。“凡事考虑周全。” 这是一句很有分量的话。我希望你不要太随意地用它。"

    old "I must admit, I've used it myself before without much thought. What about that phrase strikes you as so significant?"
    new "I must admit, I've used it myself before without much thought. What about that phrase strikes you as so significant?\n我必须承认，我自己以前也用过它，却没怎么多想。那句话有什么地方让你觉得如此意义重大？"

    old "'All things considered.' How often do we really have the time to consider {i}all{/i} of the things before us? Many issues are complex. Often, we avoid the details intentionally."
    new "'All things considered.' How often do we really have the time to consider {i}all{/i} of the things before us? Many issues are complex. Often, we avoid the details intentionally.\n“凡事考虑周全。” 我们究竟有多少次真正有时间去考虑摆在我们面前的{i}所有{/i}事情呢？许多问题都很复杂。很多时候，我们是故意回避细节的。"

    old "After all, when you consider 'all things,' most decisions become muddy things. There are pros and cons to every decision, even those which seem completely good and righteous. For example, suppose you spot an injured traveler by the side of the road, and stop to help him. To help him is right, surely, isn't it?"
    new "After all, when you consider 'all things,' most decisions become muddy things. There are pros and cons to every decision, even those which seem completely good and righteous. For example, suppose you spot an injured traveler by the side of the road, and stop to help him. To help him is right, surely, isn't it?\n毕竟，当你考虑“所有事情”时，大多数决定都会变得模糊不清。每一个决定都有利有弊，哪怕是那些看起来完全正确、完全正义的决定。比如说，假设你在路边发现一个受伤的旅人，然后停下来帮助他。帮助他是对的，当然没错，不是吗？"

    old "I would think so."
    new "I would think so.\n我想是这样。"

    old "But all things considered, there are some people who are really quite bad. People who don't deserve assistance. There are evil people in this world that would be better left to bleed out. Suppose that you help that injured traveler, and then a week later he kills a man. Was it really right to help him?"
    new "But all things considered, there are some people who are really quite bad. People who don't deserve assistance. There are evil people in this world that would be better left to bleed out. Suppose that you help that injured traveler, and then a week later he kills a man. Was it really right to help him?\n但凡事考虑周全之后，有些人确实相当坏。有些人不配得到帮助。这个世界上有些邪恶之人，倒不如让他们流血而亡。假设你帮助了那个受伤的旅人，而一周之后他杀了一个人。帮助他真的是对的吗？"

    old "I am, of course, agonizing over hypothetical possibilities. In that moment, you can really only consider the facts before you: the traveler is injured, and he needs help. So you help him. But if you had perfect knowledge of that man's future, you might approach it with a bit less confidence, even if you did come to the conclusion, as most would, that it's right to help him."
    new "I am, of course, agonizing over hypothetical possibilities. In that moment, you can really only consider the facts before you: the traveler is injured, and he needs help. So you help him. But if you had perfect knowledge of that man's future, you might approach it with a bit less confidence, even if you did come to the conclusion, as most would, that it's right to help him.\n当然，我这是在为假设出来的种种可能而纠结。在那一刻，你真正能考虑的只有摆在你面前的事实：这个旅人受伤了，他需要帮助。所以你帮助他。但如果你完全知晓那个人的未来，你或许就不会那么笃定了——即便你最终会像大多数人一样得出帮助他是对的这个结论。"

    old "So, I must presume that, all things considered, you decided that it was right to call for the removal of the memorial. You weighed all of the information before you, and you came to the conclusion that striking a deal with Geraldine and the metalworkers would produce the best outcome. Am I right?"
    new "So, I must presume that, all things considered, you decided that it was right to call for the removal of the memorial. You weighed all of the information before you, and you came to the conclusion that striking a deal with Geraldine and the metalworkers would produce the best outcome. Am I right?\n那么，我必须推测，凡事考虑周全之后，你认定要求拆除纪念碑是正确的。你权衡了面前的所有信息，然后得出结论：与 Geraldine 和金属工匠们达成协议，会带来最好的结果。我说得对吗？"

    old "And how could I fault you for doing what you determined to be the right thing?"
    new "And how could I fault you for doing what you determined to be the right thing?\n而我又怎能因为你做了自己认定正确的事而怪罪你呢？"

    old "So are you saying that you now agree with my decision?"
    new "So are you saying that you now agree with my decision?\n所以你是说，你现在同意我的决定了？"

    old "Agree with it? No. My stance now is the same as it was before. Only the future will tell which of us is right."
    new "Agree with it? No. My stance now is the same as it was before. Only the future will tell which of us is right.\n同意？不。我现在的立场和从前一样。只有未来才能证明我们谁是对的。"

    old "However, I want you to know that I understand why you did what you did. I am not one to harbor a grudge, which I'm told is uncharacteristic for a man of my profession. But I can't afford to be vindictive. The human empire needs you to succeed in your mission, and that means that I must do everything that I can to help you."
    new "However, I want you to know that I understand why you did what you did. I am not one to harbor a grudge, which I'm told is uncharacteristic for a man of my profession. But I can't afford to be vindictive. The human empire needs you to succeed in your mission, and that means that I must do everything that I can to help you.\n然而，我想让你知道，我理解你为什么会那么做。我不是那种心怀怨恨的人，据说这在我这一行的人身上并不常见。但我也不能斤斤计较、伺机报复。人类帝国需要你完成任务，而这意味着我必须尽我所能帮助你。"

    old "So you'll rally the support of the veterans?"
    new "So you'll rally the support of the veterans?\n所以你会去争取老兵们的支持？"

    old "I only hold so much sway. I don't hold a grudge, but many of them do, and I can't convince someone to follow you when he's convinced himself that you oppose everything he stands for."
    new "I only hold so much sway. I don't hold a grudge, but many of them do, and I can't convince someone to follow you when he's convinced himself that you oppose everything he stands for.\n我的影响力也有限。我不记仇，但他们中很多人记仇。而当一个人认定你与他所坚持的一切都对着干时，我没办法说服他追随你。"

    old "However."
    new "However.\n不过。"

    old "I'll do what I can. You'll still have an army, albeit one that lacks the veteran leadership an army like yours ought to have."
    new "I'll do what I can. You'll still have an army, albeit one that lacks the veteran leadership an army like yours ought to have.\n我会尽力而为。你仍会有一支军队，尽管它缺少一支像你这样的军队本该拥有的老兵领导。"

    old "I'd also like to do whatever I personally can to help you. I don't think I'm arrogant in saying this: I have significantly more combat experience than you do, and I would like to avail myself to you if you require guidance."
    new "I'd also like to do whatever I personally can to help you. I don't think I'm arrogant in saying this: I have significantly more combat experience than you do, and I would like to avail myself to you if you require guidance.\n我也想尽我个人的所能来帮你。我这么说并非自大：我的实战经验比你丰富得多，而如果你需要指点，我愿意为你效劳。"

    old "You're offering to become my mentor?"
    new "You're offering to become my mentor?\n你是要当我的导师吗？"

    old "You could call it that. If I were to become your mentor, what would you have me teach you about?"
    new "You could call it that. If I were to become your mentor, what would you have me teach you about?\n你可以这么说。如果我当你的导师，你想让我教你些什么？"

    old "Tell me what it means to be a soldier."
    new "Tell me what it means to be a soldier.\n告诉我，当一名士兵意味着什么。"

    old "Good question."
    new "Good question.\n问得好。"

    old "Tell me what it means to be a leader."
    new "Tell me what it means to be a leader.\n告诉我，当一名领袖意味着什么。"

    old "That's the wrong question."
    new "That's the wrong question.\n这个问题问错了。"

    old "I didn't think that there were 'wrong questions.'"
    new "I didn't think that there were 'wrong questions.'\n我还以为没有什么“问错了的问题”呢。"

    old "Your response betrays your over-eager attitude. Anything strong, anything that will last, needs to be built on a firm foundation. Leadership requires a firm foundation to stand upon, and you don't build it on a mountain of leadership."
    new "Your response betrays your over-eager attitude. Anything strong, anything that will last, needs to be built on a firm foundation. Leadership requires a firm foundation to stand upon, and you don't build it on a mountain of leadership.\n你的回答暴露了你过于急切的心态。任何强大的、能够长久存续的东西，都需要建立在牢固的基础上。领导力也需要一个牢固的基础来支撑，而它也不是靠堆砌领导力就能建成的。"

    old "What's the foundation that leadership is built on?"
    new "What's the foundation that leadership is built on?\n那领导力建立的基础是什么？"

    old "Now {i}that{/i} is the right question."
    new "Now {i}that{/i} is the right question.\n现在{i}这个{/i}才问对了。"

    old "Leadership is forged in the crucible of combat. You don't know what it means to be a soldier, but that doesn't mean you can't learn. You've done quite a bit of learning out in the field already, from what I've heard. One successful expedition into the halls of N'Mar."
    new "Leadership is forged in the crucible of combat. You don't know what it means to be a soldier, but that doesn't mean you can't learn. You've done quite a bit of learning out in the field already, from what I've heard. One successful expedition into the halls of N'Mar.\n领导力是在战斗的熔炉中锻造出来的。你不知道当一名士兵意味着什么，但这不代表你学不会。据我所知，你已经在战场上学到了不少东西。比如那次成功远征、深入 N'Mar 殿堂的行动。"

    old "All effective leaders start as followers. You were put in the unfortunate position of being robbed of that opportunity to learn."
    new "All effective leaders start as followers. You were put in the unfortunate position of being robbed of that opportunity to learn.\n所有卓有成效的领袖都是从追随者起步的。而你却被置于一种不幸的境地，被剥夺了这个学习的机会。"

    old "Most of the lessons you need to learn are things that I can't teach you. But I'll impart what I can."
    new "Most of the lessons you need to learn are things that I can't teach you. But I'll impart what I can.\n你需要学会的大部分东西，是我无法教你的。但我会尽我所能传授。"

    old "Are you going to train me?"
    new "Are you going to train me?\n你要训练我吗？"

    old "Train you? No. But I can offer you some wisdom amidst a whole lot of drivel and nonsense stories about the past."
    new "Train you? No. But I can offer you some wisdom amidst a whole lot of drivel and nonsense stories about the past.\n训练你？不。不过我可以在一大堆关于往事的废话和胡扯故事中间，给你一些智慧。"

    old "Come to my estate some time. My door is always open to you."
    new "Come to my estate some time. My door is always open to you.\n有空到我的宅邸来坐坐吧。我的门永远为你敞开。"

    old "Cedric greets me at the door and invites me in."
    new "Cedric greets me at the door and invites me in.\nCedric 在门口迎接我，并邀请我进去。"

    old "I'm having coffee, if you'd like to join me."
    new "I'm having coffee, if you'd like to join me.\n我正要喝咖啡，如果你愿意，可以一起。"

    old "Thank you for the invitation. I'd be glad to join you for a cup of coffee."
    new "Thank you for the invitation. I'd be glad to join you for a cup of coffee.\n谢谢你的邀请。我很乐意陪你喝一杯咖啡。"

    old "Cedric pours me a cup of brown liquid from a pot and hands it to me."
    new "Cedric pours me a cup of brown liquid from a pot and hands it to me.\nCedric 从壶里给我倒了一杯棕色的液体，递给我。"

    old "I take a sip of the liquid, and nearly gag on it. The coffee is thick and gritty, as if it hasn't been filtered."
    new "I take a sip of the liquid, and nearly gag on it. The coffee is thick and gritty, as if it hasn't been filtered.\n我抿了一口那液体，差点呛住。咖啡又浓又粗，好像根本没过滤过。"

    old "Ah, sorry, I should have warned you. It's not an ordinary pot of coffee. I understand it's not everyone's cup of tea, if you'll forgive the expression."
    new "Ah, sorry, I should have warned you. It's not an ordinary pot of coffee. I understand it's not everyone's cup of tea, if you'll forgive the expression.\n啊，抱歉，我本该先提醒你的。这不是一壶普通的咖啡。我知道它并不合每个人的口味，恕我用这个说法。"

    old "With a bit of willpower, I manage to swallow the liquid in my mouth."
    new "With a bit of willpower, I manage to swallow the liquid in my mouth.\n凭着一点毅力，我总算把嘴里的液体咽了下去。"

    old "Well? What do you think?"
    new "Well? What do you think?\n怎么样？你觉得如何？"

    old "It's rather disgusting."
    new "It's rather disgusting.\n相当难喝。"

    old "Ho ho! It's not often that civilians use such frank language around me."
    new "Ho ho! It's not often that civilians use such frank language around me.\n呵呵！平民在我身边很少说得这么直白。"

    old "I hope I haven't offended you."
    new "I hope I haven't offended you.\n希望我没有冒犯到你。"

    old "Not at all! I actually find it refreshing. I'll tell you this, I've heard many soldiers complain about this coffee in much stronger language."
    new "Not at all! I actually find it refreshing. I'll tell you this, I've heard many soldiers complain about this coffee in much stronger language.\n一点也不！我倒觉得这样很清新。我告诉你，我听过许多士兵用更难听的话抱怨这咖啡呢。"

    old "It's rather unique."
    new "It's rather unique.\n它相当独特。"

    old "Ah, so this is your first time having sock juice, eh?"
    new "Ah, so this is your first time having sock juice, eh?\n啊，这么说你是第一次喝袜子汁咯？"

    old "What is 'sock juice?'"
    new "What is 'sock juice?'\n什么是“袜子汁”？"

    old "It's like normal coffee, but filtered through a sock. A soldier has to make do with what he has. I use a clean sock, mind you, but it's not exactly the same kind of texture you'd get with a proper filter. Complaining about sock juice is a universal pastime amongst soldiers."
    new "It's like normal coffee, but filtered through a sock. A soldier has to make do with what he has. I use a clean sock, mind you, but it's not exactly the same kind of texture you'd get with a proper filter. Complaining about sock juice is a universal pastime amongst soldiers.\n它就像普通咖啡，只是用一只袜子过滤的。士兵只能用手头有的东西将就。我用的是干净袜子，听好了，不过它的口感和你用正经过滤器得到的并不完全一样。抱怨袜子汁是士兵们普遍的一种消遣。"

    old "If soldiers hate this stuff so much, why do you prepare it for yourself in the comfort of your own home?"
    new "If soldiers hate this stuff so much, why do you prepare it for yourself in the comfort of your own home?\n既然士兵们这么讨厌这东西，你又为什么要在自己舒适的家里为自己准备它？"

    old "Habit, partly. I make my own coffee, and I make it the way I learned to make it. But also, the texture has grown on me."
    new "Habit, partly. I make my own coffee, and I make it the way I learned to make it. But also, the texture has grown on me.\n一部分是习惯。我给自己煮咖啡，而且用的是我当初学会的那种煮法。不过，这种口感我也渐渐喜欢上了。"

    old "I don't think many people could come to like gritty coffee."
    new "I don't think many people could come to like gritty coffee.\n我觉得没有多少人能喜欢上这种粗糙的咖啡。"

    old "I guess that makes me unique, then. But more than habit or taste, I think the reason that I make this coffee is that grounds me. I used to be an ordinary footsoldier, you know."
    new "I guess that makes me unique, then. But more than habit or taste, I think the reason that I make this coffee is that grounds me. I used to be an ordinary footsoldier, you know.\n那我想这让我显得很特别了。但比起习惯或口味，我想我煮这种咖啡的原因，是它能让我脚踏实地。你知道，我曾经只是一名普通步兵。"

    old "And now look at you."
    new "And now look at you.\n而看看现在的你。"

    old "Yes, I've somehow become a bit of an aristocrat. This terrible coffee is one of the few things that connects me to the common man. Perhaps it's pretentious of me to think about it that way, but it does at least serve as a reminder of the life I used to live."
    new "Yes, I've somehow become a bit of an aristocrat. This terrible coffee is one of the few things that connects me to the common man. Perhaps it's pretentious of me to think about it that way, but it does at least serve as a reminder of the life I used to live.\n是啊，不知怎么的，我竟有点成了贵族。这难喝的咖啡是少数几样还能让我和普通人相连的东西之一。也许我这么想有些自命不凡，但它至少提醒着我过去过的是怎样的生活。"

    old "I've seen some aristocrats who engage in combat sports. Boxing, fencing, martial arts. Have you considered any of those?"
    new "I've seen some aristocrats who engage in combat sports. Boxing, fencing, martial arts. Have you considered any of those?\n我见过一些从事格斗运动的贵族。拳击、击剑、武术。你有考虑过其中哪一样吗？"

    old "No, and I don't think that I ever shall. A fencing match serves as a very poor facsimile of what a soldier's life is like."
    new "No, and I don't think that I ever shall. A fencing match serves as a very poor facsimile of what a soldier's life is like.\n没有，我想我也永远不会。一场击剑比赛，对于士兵真正的生活来说，不过是个拙劣的仿制品。"

    old "Ah, normal soldiers don't do much fighting with rapiers or bare hands?"
    new "Ah, normal soldiers don't do much fighting with rapiers or bare hands?\n啊，普通士兵不怎么会用细剑或赤手空拳来格斗？"

    old "It's not about the technique, [protag]. It's about the stakes. When a soldier raises his spear and charges into battle, his objective is to kill, and he risks his life. Neither of those are in play when two aristocrats don gloves to engage in a boxing match."
    new "It's not about the technique, [protag]. It's about the stakes. When a soldier raises his spear and charges into battle, his objective is to kill, and he risks his life. Neither of those are in play when two aristocrats don gloves to engage in a boxing match.\n关键不在于技巧，[protag]。而在于赌注。当一名士兵举起他的长矛冲入战场时，他的目标是杀人，他赌上的是自己的性命。而当两个贵族戴上手套打一场拳击比赛时，这两样都不存在。"

    old "Furthermore, very little of a soldier's life is about combat. War is, in a minuscule portion, absolute terror. And in much greater portions, it is a mix of boredom and anxiety."
    new "Furthermore, very little of a soldier's life is about combat. War is, in a minuscule portion, absolute terror. And in much greater portions, it is a mix of boredom and anxiety.\n更何况，士兵的生活只有极小一部分与战斗有关。战争，只在极小的部分里是绝对的恐怖。而在多得多的部分里，它是无聊与焦虑的混合。"

    old "Most battles are short. Even a long battle will often be over in less than an hour. For every hour that a soldier spends charging and swinging his weapon, he spends at least a hundred hours marching, waiting, preparing his weapons, setting up camp, or cursing the mud that his boots have become stuck in."
    new "Most battles are short. Even a long battle will often be over in less than an hour. For every hour that a soldier spends charging and swinging his weapon, he spends at least a hundred hours marching, waiting, preparing his weapons, setting up camp, or cursing the mud that his boots have become stuck in.\n大多数战斗都很短暂。即便是漫长的战斗，也往往不到一小时就结束了。士兵每花一小时冲锋、挥舞他的武器，就要至少花一百个小时去行军、等待、准备武器、扎营，或者咒骂那把他靴子陷进去的烂泥。"

    old "You will never experience any of those things in simulated combat. At least I'm drinking the same terrible coffee that those men did."
    new "You will never experience any of those things in simulated combat. At least I'm drinking the same terrible coffee that those men did.\n你在模拟战斗中永远体会不到这些。至少，我还喝着和那些人当年一样的难喝咖啡。"

    old "You said that war is a time of boredom and anxiety when it isn't terrifying. How can you experience both of those things simultaneously?"
    new "You said that war is a time of boredom and anxiety when it isn't terrifying. How can you experience both of those things simultaneously?\n你说战争在不那么恐怖的时候，就是一段无聊与焦虑交织的时光。人怎么能同时体验到这两种东西呢？"

    old "Well, different soldiers experience them in different proportions. Actually, a measure of what makes a good soldier is which one overtakes him or her faster."
    new "Well, different soldiers experience them in different proportions. Actually, a measure of what makes a good soldier is which one overtakes him or her faster.\n嗯，不同的士兵体验到它们的比例不同。事实上，衡量一个好士兵的标准之一，就是看哪一种情绪更快地压倒他或她。"

    old "I'll pose the question to you, [protag]. Suppose you are sent to hold down a location, such as an important hill. You set up camp, and establish a perimeter. You wait for the enemy army to come and attack. You wait a day, but the opposing army never comes."
    new "I'll pose the question to you, [protag]. Suppose you are sent to hold down a location, such as an important hill. You set up camp, and establish a perimeter. You wait for the enemy army to come and attack. You wait a day, but the opposing army never comes.\n我把这个问题抛给你，[protag]。假设你被派去守住一个地点，比如一座重要的山丘。你扎下营，设好防线。你等待敌军前来进攻。你等了一天，敌军却始终没来。"

    old "Yet, still you must stay on the hill to defend it when they do attack. So you stay there. For a day. And then another day. You still see no sign of the enemy, and yet you are told you must stay to defend the hill. At the end of the third day, which do you feel more strongly?"
    new "Yet, still you must stay on the hill to defend it when they do attack. So you stay there. For a day. And then another day. You still see no sign of the enemy, and yet you are told you must stay to defend the hill. At the end of the third day, which do you feel more strongly?\n然而，你仍必须守在这座山上，好在他们真的进攻时守住它。于是你继续待在那里。待了一天。又一天。你依旧看不到敌人的任何踪迹，却被告知必须留下来守住山丘。到了第三天结束时，你感受更强烈的是哪一种？"

    old "It would make me anxious more than bored."
    new "It would make me anxious more than bored.\n那会让我更多是焦虑，而非无聊。"

    old "Anxious, over nothing happening?"
    new "Anxious, over nothing happening?\n焦虑，就因为什么都没发生？"

    old "Yes. In fact, a situation where nothing happens would fill me with even more anxiety than a situation where things happen."
    new "Yes. In fact, a situation where nothing happens would fill me with even more anxiety than a situation where things happen.\n是的。事实上，什么都没发生的处境，比有事发生的处境更让我充满焦虑。"

    old "Isn't that something that's pretty widely understood? Think about words like 'nervous' and 'anxious.' Those are the kinds of things that you feel in moments of anticipation."
    new "Isn't that something that's pretty widely understood? Think about words like 'nervous' and 'anxious.' Those are the kinds of things that you feel in moments of anticipation.\n这不是很多人都明白的道理吗？想想“紧张”和“焦虑”这类词。它们都是你在满怀期待的瞬间才会感受到的东西。"

    old "When a dangerous-looking man approaches me, I feel nervous. When he pulls out a knife and charges at me, those feelings of nervousness are quickly replaced with things like the terror of combat."
    new "When a dangerous-looking man approaches me, I feel nervous. When he pulls out a knife and charges at me, those feelings of nervousness are quickly replaced with things like the terror of combat.\n当一个看起来危险的人走近我时，我会感到紧张。当他拔出刀向我冲来时，那种紧张感很快就会被战斗的恐怖之类的东西取代。"

    old "In fact, sometimes combat allows you to enter something like a flow state. When you're fighting for your life, it's very difficult to find the mental capacity for things like nervousness and existential dread."
    new "In fact, sometimes combat allows you to enter something like a flow state. When you're fighting for your life, it's very difficult to find the mental capacity for things like nervousness and existential dread.\n事实上，有时战斗会让你进入一种类似心流的状态。当你为性命而战时，很难再腾出心力去想紧张、生存恐惧之类的东西。"

    old "Dread, anxiousness, nervousness...those are all things I associate with someone who is contemplating some peril in the future, with nothing to distract them in the present. So yes, I would feel anxiety in that situation. Even if 'nothing' was happening."
    new "Dread, anxiousness, nervousness...those are all things I associate with someone who is contemplating some peril in the future, with nothing to distract them in the present. So yes, I would feel anxiety in that situation. Even if 'nothing' was happening.\n恐惧、焦虑、紧张……这些我都会和这样一个人联系在一起：他正在想着未来某种危险，而当下又没有任何东西能分散他的注意力。所以没错，在那种处境里我会感到焦虑。哪怕“什么”都没发生。"

    old "Interesting point, interesting point. I have to admit, I agree with most of what you say. In fact, there are soldiers who expressed many of those same ideas when they served with me."
    new "Interesting point, interesting point. I have to admit, I agree with most of what you say. In fact, there are soldiers who expressed many of those same ideas when they served with me.\n有意思的观点，有意思。我不得不承认，你说的我大部分都同意。事实上，有些士兵在和我并肩服役时，也表达过许多同样的想法。"

    old "I'd feel bored. That's the thing I most often feel when forced to do nothing, especially for days at a time."
    new "I'd feel bored. That's the thing I most often feel when forced to do nothing, especially for days at a time.\n我会感到无聊。那是我被迫无所事事时最常有的感受，尤其是连续好几天的时候。"

    old "You wouldn't feel fear?"
    new "You wouldn't feel fear?\n你不会感到恐惧吗？"

    old "I might feel fear initially. But if days happen without anything happening, that fear eventually gives way to boredom. It's hard to live in a constant state of terror for entire days at a time when nothing is happening to confirm that the fear is valid."
    new "I might feel fear initially. But if days happen without anything happening, that fear eventually gives way to boredom. It's hard to live in a constant state of terror for entire days at a time when nothing is happening to confirm that the fear is valid.\n起初我可能会感到恐惧。但如果一连好几天什么都没发生，那恐惧最终会让位给无聊。当没有任何事发生来印证这份恐惧有道理时，人很难一连数日都活在持续不断的恐怖之中。"

    old "Now, I might get a bit paranoid. I can see how, in that state of fear, I might begin to see illusory enemies. The idea of seeing movement on the horizon and being left to speculate whether it might be an approaching army...well, I can see how many might succumb to that fear."
    new "Now, I might get a bit paranoid. I can see how, in that state of fear, I might begin to see illusory enemies. The idea of seeing movement on the horizon and being left to speculate whether it might be an approaching army...well, I can see how many might succumb to that fear.\n当然，我可能会变得有些偏执。我能理解，在那种恐惧状态下，人可能会开始看到并不存在的敌人。在地平线上看到动静，然后只能去猜测那会不会是一支逼近的军队……嗯，我能理解许多人会屈从于那种恐惧。"

    old "It's more common than you might think. Different people handle the moments of silent differently. But one thing is universal in times of war: more than fighting, wartime is about spending many hours, days, sometimes weeks or months of time sitting quietly with your fellow soldiers, waiting for the moment when you are called to fight."
    new "It's more common than you might think. Different people handle the moments of silent differently. But one thing is universal in times of war: more than fighting, wartime is about spending many hours, days, sometimes weeks or months of time sitting quietly with your fellow soldiers, waiting for the moment when you are called to fight.\n这比你想象的更常见。不同的人以不同的方式应对那些沉寂的时刻。但战争时期有一点是共通的：比起战斗，战时更多是花上许多个小时、许多天、有时数周甚至数月的时间，和你的战友们静静坐在一起，等待被召唤去战斗的那一刻。"

    old "There are ways to make the time pass faster. Complaining about the quality of coffee is a common pastime. That kind of shared complaining builds strong bonds."
    new "There are ways to make the time pass faster. Complaining about the quality of coffee is a common pastime. That kind of shared complaining builds strong bonds.\n有办法让时间过得更快些。抱怨咖啡的质量就是一种常见的消遣。那种共同抱怨能建立起牢固的情谊。"

    old "But you strike me as the kind of person who knows quite a lot about building strong bonds with other fighters. You're a fighter, but you also know what it's like to be a soldier."
    new "But you strike me as the kind of person who knows quite a lot about building strong bonds with other fighters. You're a fighter, but you also know what it's like to be a soldier.\n但在我看来，你是那种很懂得与其他战士建立牢固情谊的人。你是个战士，但你也知道当一名士兵是什么滋味。"

    old "You know what it's like to exist in that interstitial time, the time between fights, when you have nothing to do but seek the companionship of the people who will be fighting alongside you in the next engagement."
    new "You know what it's like to exist in that interstitial time, the time between fights, when you have nothing to do but seek the companionship of the people who will be fighting alongside you in the next engagement.\n你知道活在那段间隙时光里是什么滋味——那是两场战斗之间的时光，你无事可做，只能去寻求那些将在下一场交战中与你并肩作战之人的陪伴。"

    old "Whether or not you were doing it intentionally, you've spent a lot of time preparing to be a soldier."
    new "Whether or not you were doing it intentionally, you've spent a lot of time preparing to be a soldier.\n不管你是不是有意为之，你已经花了很多时间为成为一名士兵做准备。"

    old "Cedric takes a long sip from his cup and sets it down. The cup is empty."
    new "Cedric takes a long sip from his cup and sets it down. The cup is empty.\nCedric 从杯子里长长地呷了一口，然后把杯子放下。杯子已经空了。"

    old "If you ever want to get to know someone better, brew a pot of sock juice for them. It might not be a pleasant experience, but I think you'll find it reveals a lot about their personality."
    new "If you ever want to get to know someone better, brew a pot of sock juice for them. It might not be a pleasant experience, but I think you'll find it reveals a lot about their personality.\n如果你哪天想更了解一个人，就给他们煮一壶袜子汁。这也许不是一次愉快的经历，但我想你会发现，它能透露出他们性格中的很多东西。"

    old "Cedric invites me into his den, and he takes a seat by the fireplace. I take the seat beside his."
    new "Cedric invites me into his den, and he takes a seat by the fireplace. I take the seat beside his.\nCedric 邀我进他的书房，然后他在壁炉旁坐下。我在他旁边的位子坐下。"

    old "Have you ever thought about how much you're like a general?"
    new "Have you ever thought about how much you're like a general?\n你有没有想过，你有多像一名将军？"

    old "No, I never really considered that before."
    new "No, I never really considered that before.\n没有，我以前还真没这么想过。"

    old "Yes, I have given it some thought, as a matter of fact."
    new "Yes, I have given it some thought, as a matter of fact.\n是的，事实上，我确实想过一些。"

    old "It's rather uncanny, just how much the Grimoire council has tried to sculpt your role to resemble that of a general, without ever giving you the military title before. Do you know why that is?"
    new "It's rather uncanny, just how much the Grimoire council has tried to sculpt your role to resemble that of a general, without ever giving you the military title before. Do you know why that is?\n说来也真是诡异，Grimoire 议会竟如此费力地把你的角色塑造成将军的样子，却从未给过你军衔。你知道这是为什么吗？"

    old "The council wants me to do things that a military officer can't. Things like gathering intelligence, for example. It would be scandalous if a military officer were to be snooping around the lands, gathering information about foreign governments. I think that's why my title tries to paint me in a more diplomatic role."
    new "The council wants me to do things that a military officer can't. Things like gathering intelligence, for example. It would be scandalous if a military officer were to be snooping around the lands, gathering information about foreign governments. I think that's why my title tries to paint me in a more diplomatic role.\n议会想让我去做军官做不了的事。比如收集情报。如果一名军官在各地暗中打探、收集外国政府的情报，那会成为丑闻。我想这就是为什么我的头衔试图把我塑造成一个更偏外交的角色。"

    old "Astute observation, [protag]. The truth is, you will never know some of the worst parts of being a military officer."
    new "Astute observation, [protag]. The truth is, you will never know some of the worst parts of being a military officer.\n敏锐的观察，[protag]。事实是，当军官最糟糕的一些方面，你永远不会知道。"

    old "Helplessness. Being in military leadership is about learning to live with helplessness."
    new "Helplessness. Being in military leadership is about learning to live with helplessness.\n无力感。身处军队领导之位，就是学着与无力感共处。"

    old "I think the council is intentionally limiting my powers. If I were a military officer, I'd have more authority."
    new "I think the council is intentionally limiting my powers. If I were a military officer, I'd have more authority.\n我觉得议会是在故意限制我的权力。如果我是军官，我的权力会更大。"

    old "It's interesting you'd say that, [protag]. Actually, I think the opposite may be true. If you went down the route of becoming a recognized military officer, I think you'd find yourself with fewer powers than you might imagine."
    new "It's interesting you'd say that, [protag]. Actually, I think the opposite may be true. If you went down the route of becoming a recognized military officer, I think you'd find yourself with fewer powers than you might imagine.\n你会这么说倒很有意思，[protag]。实际上，我认为事实可能恰恰相反。如果你走上成为正式军官这条路，我想你会发现自己拥有的权力比你想象的要少。"

    old "The dirty truth of the matter is that military officers have surprisingly little decision-making power. And one of the most difficult things I've had to do as an officer myself is to learn how to live with a constant sense of helplessness."
    new "The dirty truth of the matter is that military officers have surprisingly little decision-making power. And one of the most difficult things I've had to do as an officer myself is to learn how to live with a constant sense of helplessness.\n这事的肮脏真相是，军官拥有的决策权少得惊人。而我自己身为军官，做过最难的事情之一，就是学会如何与一种持续不断的无力感共处。"

    old "In what ways are military officers 'helpless?'"
    new "In what ways are military officers 'helpless?'\n军官在哪些方面是“无力的”？"

    old "For one immediate thing, the members of the military don't have the power to declare war. Only the civilian council can do that."
    new "For one immediate thing, the members of the military don't have the power to declare war. Only the civilian council can do that.\n首先最直接的一点，军人没有宣战的权力。只有文官议会才能宣战。"

    old "Sadly, this is a fact that many people seem to be unaware of. One of the other difficulties of being a military officer is constantly being blamed for things that you had no part in doing, but also had no power to prevent."
    new "Sadly, this is a fact that many people seem to be unaware of. One of the other difficulties of being a military officer is constantly being blamed for things that you had no part in doing, but also had no power to prevent.\n可悲的是，这似乎是许多人都不知道的事实。当军官的另一重困难是，你不断为那些你没有参与、却也没有权力阻止的事情而受指责。"

    old "In some cases, I have actively argued against certain actions, and then been forced to carry them out anyway, accepting the responsibility that came with following those general orders. Their is a chain of command, but the top of the command structure isn't the generals. It's the council."
    new "In some cases, I have actively argued against certain actions, and then been forced to carry them out anyway, accepting the responsibility that came with following those general orders. Their is a chain of command, but the top of the command structure isn't the generals. It's the council.\n在某些情况下，我曾极力反对某些行动，却还是被迫执行，并承担了服从那些上级命令所带来的责任。指挥链是存在的，但指挥结构的顶端并不是将军们。而是议会。"

    old "When we go to war, and things turn out poorly, when we lose battles or find ourselves morally challenged when we discover that our enemies are not so evil as our leaders have made them out to be, the leaders of the military are blamed."
    new "When we go to war, and things turn out poorly, when we lose battles or find ourselves morally challenged when we discover that our enemies are not so evil as our leaders have made them out to be, the leaders of the military are blamed.\n当我们开战而战事不利时，当我们吃了败仗，或者当我们发现敌人并不像我们的领袖所描绘的那么邪恶、从而在道义上陷入两难时，军队的领导者们就会受到指责。"

    old "After all, a man carrying a sword and shield and shouting as he charges toward the enemy is the manifestation of war for most people. But that man made no choice to be here. No, he only fights in the battles. He only obeys orders."
    new "After all, a man carrying a sword and shield and shouting as he charges toward the enemy is the manifestation of war for most people. But that man made no choice to be here. No, he only fights in the battles. He only obeys orders.\n毕竟，对大多数人来说，一个手持剑盾、呐喊着冲向敌人的人，就是战争的化身。但那个人并没有选择来到这里。不，他只是参与了战斗。他只是服从命令。"

    old "People who think about it for one moment longer might think to blame the captains, the generals, and the military officers that strategize how best to fight the war. The military leadership is often blamed for disasters of war."
    new "People who think about it for one moment longer might think to blame the captains, the generals, and the military officers that strategize how best to fight the war. The military leadership is often blamed for disasters of war.\n多想一想的人，可能会把责任归到队长、将军，以及那些谋划如何作战的军官头上。军事领导层常常因战争带来的灾难而受指责。"

    old "And it is true that generals are given the highest decision-making authority in times of war. But the generals lack authority in one area: they themselves cannot declare war."
    new "And it is true that generals are given the highest decision-making authority in times of war. But the generals lack authority in one area: they themselves cannot declare war.\n而且，将军在战时确实被授予最高的决策权。但将军们有一个领域没有权力：他们自己不能宣战。"

    old "No, before the plans can be drawn and the battles can be fought, we need a declaration of war. And who is it that declares war? Certainly not the footsoldier on the front lines, nor the experienced military general."
    new "No, before the plans can be drawn and the battles can be fought, we need a declaration of war. And who is it that declares war? Certainly not the footsoldier on the front lines, nor the experienced military general.\n不，在能够制定计划、开打战役之前，我们需要一份宣战声明。而宣战的又是谁呢？当然不是前线的步兵，也不是经验丰富的将军。"

    old "No, ironically, people of the military lack the ability to make the most important decision when it comes to war, which is answering the question of whether we instigate it or not. The only group with the power to declare war is the council."
    new "No, ironically, people of the military lack the ability to make the most important decision when it comes to war, which is answering the question of whether we instigate it or not. The only group with the power to declare war is the council.\n不，讽刺的是，军人恰恰没有能力在战争问题上做出那个最重要的决定，也就是回答我们是否要主动开战这个问题。唯一有权宣战的，只有议会。"

    old "The civilian council decides that war has started, and then they send the men in uniform off to fight it. You might think that the council would value the input of officers, or people who have at least served on the battlefield. And they do, nominally."
    new "The civilian council decides that war has started, and then they send the men in uniform off to fight it. You might think that the council would value the input of officers, or people who have at least served on the battlefield. And they do, nominally.\n文官议会认定战争开始了，然后派那些穿军装的人上阵作战。你也许会以为议会会重视军官、或至少上过战场的人的意见。名义上，他们确实如此。"

    old "Every now and again, I will be called to testify before the council and be asked to provide my input on how I believe the empire's interests would best be served. But someone like me will never hold a seat on the council. When the question of whether we go to war comes up, I'll never be the one to cast the ballot."
    new "Every now and again, I will be called to testify before the council and be asked to provide my input on how I believe the empire's interests would best be served. But someone like me will never hold a seat on the council. When the question of whether we go to war comes up, I'll never be the one to cast the ballot.\n时不时地，我会被召到议会前作证，被要求就我心目中帝国利益如何得到最佳维护提供意见。但像我这样的人永远无法在议会中占有一席之地。当是否开战的问题被提出时，我永远不会是投出那一票的人。"

    old "It would be easy to fill the council with people who have military experience. After all, with the way conscription works, nearly half of the adults in our country have, at some time or another, held a weapon and been called into service."
    new "It would be easy to fill the council with people who have military experience. After all, with the way conscription works, nearly half of the adults in our country have, at some time or another, held a weapon and been called into service.\n让有从军经验的人填满议会是很容易的。毕竟，按照征兵制度运作的方式，我国近一半的成年人，都曾在某个时候拿起过武器、被征召服役。"

    old "Very few of them have seen battle, but at least most of them know what it is to march in formation and follow an officer's orders. They understand the basic concepts of military discipline."
    new "Very few of them have seen battle, but at least most of them know what it is to march in formation and follow an officer's orders. They understand the basic concepts of military discipline.\n他们中很少有人真正上过战场，但至少大多数人都知道列队行进、服从军官命令是什么滋味。他们理解军纪的基本概念。"

    old "So you might think, at the very least, that a number of the council's members would have that experience of knowing what it's like to put on armor and carry a weapon. If the council were a representation of the empire that they govern over, then perhaps half of the council's active members would have that experience."
    new "So you might think, at the very least, that a number of the council's members would have that experience of knowing what it's like to put on armor and carry a weapon. If the council were a representation of the empire that they govern over, then perhaps half of the council's active members would have that experience.\n所以你至少会以为，议会中有一部分成员会有这种经验——知道穿上盔甲、拿起武器是什么感觉。如果议会真能代表它所治理的帝国，那么也许议会里有一半的现任成员都该有过这种经验。"

    old "But in reality, fewer than a tenth of them do. I can count the number of veterans with council seats on one finger."
    new "But in reality, fewer than a tenth of them do. I can count the number of veterans with council seats on one finger.\n但现实中，他们中这么做的人不到十分之一。议席上的退伍军人，我用一根手指就数得清。"

    old "Why the disparity?"
    new "Why the disparity?\n为什么会差这么多？"

    old "Because holding a seat on the council requires connections. Many of them come from wealthy families, others simply have a talent for politics and talking their way into positions of power. And talking your way into positions of power is a trait you commonly find in people who manage to find ways to avoid conscription."
    new "Because holding a seat on the council requires connections. Many of them come from wealthy families, others simply have a talent for politics and talking their way into positions of power. And talking your way into positions of power is a trait you commonly find in people who manage to find ways to avoid conscription.\n因为要在议会中占有一席之地，需要有人脉。他们中许多人出身富裕家庭，另一些人则只是有政治天赋，能靠嘴皮子钻营到权力之位。而靠嘴皮子钻营到权力之位，恰恰是你常能在那些设法逃避征兵的人身上找到的特质。"

    old "It's the cruelest of life's ironies, that the people with the greatest authority in times of war are the people who have the least amount of direct experience waging it. Time was, the city elders would be respected community members."
    new "It's the cruelest of life's ironies, that the people with the greatest authority in times of war are the people who have the least amount of direct experience waging it. Time was, the city elders would be respected community members.\n这是人生最残酷的讽刺之一：战时拥有最大权力的人，恰恰是亲历战争经验最少的人。想当年，城中的长老们都是受人敬重的社区成员。"

    old "You might see people who were stone masons, or farmers serving among the members of the voting council. But now, they are all professional politicians."
    new "You might see people who were stone masons, or farmers serving among the members of the voting council. But now, they are all professional politicians.\n你或许能看到石匠、农夫列席于投票议会成员之中。可如今，他们全都是职业政客了。"

    old "Cedric stares into the fire with sullen eyes. He appears to be lost in thought."
    new "Cedric stares into the fire with sullen eyes. He appears to be lost in thought.\nCedric 目光郁郁地凝视着炉火。他看上去陷入了沉思。"

    old "Do you ever regret becoming a soldier?"
    new "Do you ever regret becoming a soldier?\n你可曾后悔当过兵？"

    old "Good question. I think many soldiers ask themselves that at one point or another in their careers."
    new "Good question. I think many soldiers ask themselves that at one point or another in their careers.\n问得好。我想许多士兵在职业生涯的某个时刻，都会这样问自己。"

    old "And what answer have you come up with?"
    new "And what answer have you come up with?\n那你得出的答案是什么？"

    old "I don't regret it, not at all. Even if I've had to do regrettable things."
    new "I don't regret it, not at all. Even if I've had to do regrettable things.\n我不后悔，一点都不。即便我不得不做过一些令人遗憾的事。"

    old "I don't understand. You feel like you've had to do regrettable things, and yet you don't regret doing them? That doesn't make sense."
    new "I don't understand. You feel like you've had to do regrettable things, and yet you don't regret doing them? That doesn't make sense.\n我不明白。你觉得你不得不做了些令人遗憾的事，却又不后悔做过它们？这讲不通啊。"

    old "Certain individual actions may have been regrettable. But you asked me about the decision to be a soldier. That isn't something that I regret at all."
    new "Certain individual actions may have been regrettable. But you asked me about the decision to be a soldier. That isn't something that I regret at all.\n个别行动也许令人遗憾。但你问的是当兵这个决定。这我可一点都不后悔。"

    old "I'm having trouble seeing the distinction."
    new "I'm having trouble seeing the distinction.\n我看不出这有什么区别。"

    old "Imagine that you made the decision to be a father. In the process of raising a child to adulthood, you're bound to have some regrets. You'll make some mistakes in parenting. But at the end of it, even in spite of all the mistakes, would you regret your decision to become a father? Those are two different questions. Just because something is not perfect does not mean that it is regrettable."
    new "Imagine that you made the decision to be a father. In the process of raising a child to adulthood, you're bound to have some regrets. You'll make some mistakes in parenting. But at the end of it, even in spite of all the mistakes, would you regret your decision to become a father? Those are two different questions. Just because something is not perfect does not mean that it is regrettable.\n想象一下，你决定当一名父亲。在把孩子抚养到成年的过程中，你难免会有一些遗憾。你会在养育孩子时犯下一些错误。但到最后，尽管有种种错误，你会后悔自己当父亲的决定吗？这是两个不同的问题。一件事不完美，并不意味着它就令人遗憾。"

    old "Imagine that you made the decision to be a mother. In the process of raising a child to adulthood, you're bound to have some regrets. You'll make some mistakes in parenting. But at the end of it, even in spite of all the mistakes, would you regret your decision to become a mother? Just because something is not perfect does not mean that it is regrettable."
    new "Imagine that you made the decision to be a mother. In the process of raising a child to adulthood, you're bound to have some regrets. You'll make some mistakes in parenting. But at the end of it, even in spite of all the mistakes, would you regret your decision to become a mother? Just because something is not perfect does not mean that it is regrettable.\n想象一下，你决定当一名母亲。在把孩子抚养到成年的过程中，你难免会有一些遗憾。你会在养育孩子时犯下一些错误。但到最后，尽管有种种错误，你会后悔自己当母亲的决定吗？只是，一件事不完美，并不意味着它就令人遗憾。"

    old "My decision to make military service my life's work is much the same way."
    new "My decision to make military service my life's work is much the same way.\n我决定把军旅当作毕生事业，也是同样的道理。"

    old "I gave up some of my own agency so that I could be used as an instrument of good in the world. The cost of that is that I've also fashioned myself as someone who can be used as an agent of destruction. But you can't have one without the other. A soldier who pledges his loyalty conditionally is no soldier at all."
    new "I gave up some of my own agency so that I could be used as an instrument of good in the world. The cost of that is that I've also fashioned myself as someone who can be used as an agent of destruction. But you can't have one without the other. A soldier who pledges his loyalty conditionally is no soldier at all.\n我放弃了自己的一部分自主，好让自己能成为世间行善的工具。代价是，我也把自己塑造成了一个可以被当作毁灭工具的人。但这两者是无法只取其一的。一个有条件地宣誓效忠的士兵，根本算不上士兵。"

    old "Do you think we can win the war?"
    new "Do you think we can win the war?\n你觉得我们能打赢这场战争吗？"

    old "That's a disconcerting question to hear from you. It feels like I should be the one asking you that."
    new "That's a disconcerting question to hear from you. It feels like I should be the one asking you that.\n从你口中听到这个问题，真让我不安。感觉这话本该是我问你才对。"

    old "After all, you're far more intimately connected with the war efforts than I am. You surely know more about our combat readiness. So why do you come to me and ask this question?"
    new "After all, you're far more intimately connected with the war efforts than I am. You surely know more about our combat readiness. So why do you come to me and ask this question?\n毕竟，你和战事的关联远比我紧密。你对我们的战备情况肯定更了解。那你为什么来找我问这个问题？"

    old "Because you have experience. You know what it takes to win a war, and you know what it means to fight both winning and losing battles."
    new "Because you have experience. You know what it takes to win a war, and you know what it means to fight both winning and losing battles.\n因为你有经验。你知道赢得一场战争需要什么，你也知道打赢的仗和打输的仗各是什么滋味。"

    old "Well, [protag], let me tell you what my experience has taught me. The people of the empire will survive."
    new "Well, [protag], let me tell you what my experience has taught me. The people of the empire will survive.\n好吧，[protag]，让我告诉你我的经验教会了我什么。帝国的人民会活下去的。"

    old "Grimoire will survive?"
    new "Grimoire will survive?\nGrimoire 会挺过去吗？"

    old "I didn't say that. I said its people will survive."
    new "I didn't say that. I said its people will survive.\n我可没这么说。我说的是它的人民会活下去。"

    old "One thing I've learned in all my years is that people will always surprise you with their tenacity. Even if their soldiers die, even if their cities are overrun, even if they are forced to flee the lands their ancestors have inhabited for countless generations, life finds a way."
    new "One thing I've learned in all my years is that people will always surprise you with their tenacity. Even if their soldiers die, even if their cities are overrun, even if they are forced to flee the lands their ancestors have inhabited for countless generations, life finds a way.\n我这些年来学到的一件事是，人们总会以他们的坚韧让你惊讶。即使他们的士兵战死，即使他们的城市被攻陷，即使他们被迫逃离祖先世世代代居住的土地，生命总会找到出路。"

    old "I'm not saying that the city of Grimoire will still be standing after all this is over. Hell, the human empire itself may be in jeopardy. Other neighboring nations, too. Who can say? But I know that no matter what happens, there will be those who persevere. And with their perseverance, and what remains after the dust has settled, we will rebuild."
    new "I'm not saying that the city of Grimoire will still be standing after all this is over. Hell, the human empire itself may be in jeopardy. Other neighboring nations, too. Who can say? But I know that no matter what happens, there will be those who persevere. And with their perseverance, and what remains after the dust has settled, we will rebuild.\n我并不是说这一切结束后，Grimoire 城仍会屹立不倒。见鬼，人类帝国本身都可能岌岌可危。其他邻国也一样。谁说得准呢？但我知道，无论发生什么，总会有坚持下去的人。靠着他们的坚持，以及尘埃落定后剩下的东西，我们会重建一切。"

    old "So when you ask if I think that we can win the war, I can't give you an answer yes or no. What I can tell you is that regardless of the war's outcome, we will survive. Maybe not you or I, for either of us may perish at any moment. But the spirit of the people will live on."
    new "So when you ask if I think that we can win the war, I can't give you an answer yes or no. What I can tell you is that regardless of the war's outcome, we will survive. Maybe not you or I, for either of us may perish at any moment. But the spirit of the people will live on.\n所以，当你问我是否觉得我们能打赢这场战争时，我给不了你是或否的答案。我能告诉你的是，无论战争结果如何，我们都会活下去。也许活下来的不是你或我，因为我们中任何一个人都可能随时丧命。但人民的精神会延续下去。"

    old "Cedric turns back to the fire and takes a puff of his pipe."
    new "Cedric turns back to the fire and takes a puff of his pipe.\nCedric 转回炉火前，抽了一口他的烟斗。"

    old "I'm not sure that's the answer that you were looking for."
    new "I'm not sure that's the answer that you were looking for.\n我不确定这是不是你想听的答案。"

    old "Cedric sighs and gazes away wistfully."
    new "Cedric sighs and gazes away wistfully.\nCedric 叹了口气，怅然地望向远方。"

    old "My, this conversation turned somber. I hope you didn't come here hoping for me to entertain you."
    new "My, this conversation turned somber. I hope you didn't come here hoping for me to entertain you.\n哎呀，这谈话变得沉重起来了。我希望你不是抱着让我逗你开心的期待来的。"

    old "I appreciate your time. I feel like you've given me a lot to ponder."
    new "I appreciate your time. I feel like you've given me a lot to ponder.\n感激你抽出时间。我觉得你给了我许多值得思考的东西。"

    old "And what a burden that is. I hope you can still shoulder it with all of your other responsibilities. I understand if you'd rather not dwell on such things, but please, stop by again if you ever find yourself in the mood to be lectured at about weighty topics."
    new "And what a burden that is. I hope you can still shoulder it with all of your other responsibilities. I understand if you'd rather not dwell on such things, but please, stop by again if you ever find yourself in the mood to be lectured at about weighty topics.\n那可是个不小的负担啊。我希望你在肩负其他所有责任的同时，还担得起它。如果你想先不纠缠这些事，我能理解。但请你随时再来坐坐，如果你哪天有心情听人对着严肃话题说教的话。"

    old "[protag], the next time we speak, I don't expect that conversation to be as frivolous as this one. Do you know what I mean?"
    new "[protag], the next time we speak, I don't expect that conversation to be as frivolous as this one. Do you know what I mean?\n[protag]，等下次我们再谈时，我想那番谈话就不会像今天这般轻松了。你明白我的意思吗？"

    old "I'm not sure that I do, Cedric."
    new "I'm not sure that I do, Cedric.\n我不太确定，Cedric。"

    old "Well, you will soon enough."
    new "Well, you will soon enough.\n嗯，你很快就会明白了。"

    old "[protag], welcome back. I'm surprised that you still have interest in hearing what I have to say."
    new "[protag], welcome back. I'm surprised that you still have interest in hearing what I have to say.\n[protag]，欢迎回来。我很惊讶你居然还有兴趣听我说这些话。"

    old "Should I be surprised that you still willingly invite me into your home?"
    new "Should I be surprised that you still willingly invite me into your home?\n你仍然愿意邀我进你家门，我该为此惊讶吗？"

    old "You are the rising star, the up-and-comer. I'm the old washed-up veteran whose best days are behind him."
    new "You are the rising star, the up-and-comer. I'm the old washed-up veteran whose best days are behind him.\n你是冉冉升起的新星，是后起之秀。我则是个过气的老兵，最好的日子已经过去了。"

    old "But perhaps you disagree, [protag]. Who would you say has more social influence, me or you?"
    new "But perhaps you disagree, [protag]. Who would you say has more social influence, me or you?\n不过也许你不同意，[protag]。你觉得谁的社会影响力更大，我还是你？"

    old "Speaking frankly? I think that I'm in a better position than you are, Cedric. You're right. I'm a rising star."
    new "Speaking frankly? I think that I'm in a better position than you are, Cedric. You're right. I'm a rising star.\n直说的话？我觉得我的处境比你好，Cedric。你说得对。我是颗冉冉升起的新星。"

    old "You're not humble, but you are realistic. It's best to have both, but given the choice between the two qualities, I'd say that realism will serve you better."
    new "You're not humble, but you are realistic. It's best to have both, but given the choice between the two qualities, I'd say that realism will serve you better.\n你不谦逊，但很务实。两者兼备最好，但若要在两种品质间做选择，我会说务实对你更有用。"

    old "I'd say that you have more social influence, Cedric. Do you remember when we first met? There was a reason that I came to you looking for support, and not the other way around."
    new "I'd say that you have more social influence, Cedric. Do you remember when we first met? There was a reason that I came to you looking for support, and not the other way around.\n我会说你的社会影响力更大，Cedric。你还记得我们第一次见面吗？我之所以来找你寻求支持，而不是反过来，是有原因的。"

    old "True, true. I do have some connections to offer you. But connections mean nothing if they go unused..."
    new "True, true. I do have some connections to offer you. But connections mean nothing if they go unused...\n也对，也对。我确实有一些人脉可以给你。但人脉如果不用，就毫无意义……"

    old "Anyway, I think we have matters of more significance to discuss."
    new "Anyway, I think we have matters of more significance to discuss.\n总之，我想我们有更重要的事情要谈。"

    old "And what matters would those be?"
    new "And what matters would those be?\n那会是什么事情？"

    old "I want to know what kind of leader you are, [protag]. I want to know where your loyalties lie."
    new "I want to know what kind of leader you are, [protag]. I want to know where your loyalties lie.\n我想知道你是什么样的领袖，[protag]。我想知道你的忠诚在何处。"

    old "Are you questioning my loyalties?"
    new "Are you questioning my loyalties?\n你在质疑我的忠诚吗？"

    old "It sounds like a bad thing, doesn't it? I would say that loyalty is a matter of degree. You have many loyalties. I think it's best to know which ones are strongest. I thought I would pose the question to you."
    new "It sounds like a bad thing, doesn't it? I would say that loyalty is a matter of degree. You have many loyalties. I think it's best to know which ones are strongest. I thought I would pose the question to you.\n听起来像是坏事，对吧？我会说忠诚是有程度之分的。你有很多份忠诚。我想最好弄清楚哪一份最重。所以我想把这个问题抛给你。"

    old "You are assembling a team of fighters to help you take N'Mar. These people, I imagine, have become close comrades of yours, both on and off the battlefield. But you've assembled them for a reason. You serve a higher calling, as it were. You're serving the interests of the people of Grimoire."
    new "You are assembling a team of fighters to help you take N'Mar. These people, I imagine, have become close comrades of yours, both on and off the battlefield. But you've assembled them for a reason. You serve a higher calling, as it were. You're serving the interests of the people of Grimoire.\n你正在召集一支战士队伍来帮你攻下 N'Mar。我想，这些人已经成了你的亲密战友，无论战场内外。但你召集他们是有原因的。可以说，你在履行一种更高的使命。你在为 Grimoire 人民的利益效劳。"

    old "So, here is my question. Which of those obligations is more important? The obligation that you have to serve Grimoire, or the bond that you share with your comrades in arms?"
    new "So, here is my question. Which of those obligations is more important? The obligation that you have to serve Grimoire, or the bond that you share with your comrades in arms?\n那么，我的问题来了。这些义务中哪一个更重要？是你为 Grimoire 效力的义务，还是你与并肩作战的战友之间共享的情谊？"

    old "My greatest loyalty is to the people who fight alongside me."
    new "My greatest loyalty is to the people who fight alongside me.\n我最大的忠诚，属于那些与我并肩作战的人。"

    old "I'd like to hear you justify that answer, [protag]. Suppose you have fighting companions. You're taking them into dangerous situations. Surely, if you valued their lives and safety above all else, you wouldn't summon them to follow you into battle."
    new "I'd like to hear you justify that answer, [protag]. Suppose you have fighting companions. You're taking them into dangerous situations. Surely, if you valued their lives and safety above all else, you wouldn't summon them to follow you into battle.\n我想听听你如何为这个答案辩护，[protag]。假设你有并肩作战的同伴。你正把他们带进危险的境地。当然，如果你把他们的生命与安全看得高于一切，你就不会召唤他们跟着你上战场。"

    old "We've forged a bond together that is based on our willingness to enter battle together. I do not force them to fight. They've joined me of their own volition. They each fight for their own reasons."
    new "We've forged a bond together that is based on our willingness to enter battle together. I do not force them to fight. They've joined me of their own volition. They each fight for their own reasons.\n我们共同铸就的情谊，是建立在我们愿意并肩作战的基础上的。我没有强迫他们战斗。他们是自愿加入我的。他们每个人都为自己而战。"

    old "And if it became apparent that the success of your mission required you to betray your allies?"
    new "And if it became apparent that the success of your mission required you to betray your allies?\n而如果有一天，你的任务要成功，似乎就必须背叛你的盟友呢？"

    old "As I said, the bond I share with my combat comrades is most important. If they act to break that bond, I will punish that betrayal, but I will not betray my friends out of convenience."
    new "As I said, the bond I share with my combat comrades is most important. If they act to break that bond, I will punish that betrayal, but I will not betray my friends out of convenience.\n正如我说的，我与战友们共享的情谊最为重要。如果他们做出破坏这份情谊的事，我会惩罚那种背叛，但我不会出于方便而背叛我的朋友。"

    old "So what you're saying is that the lives of the people you fight next to are more important than the orders that you receive from the council."
    new "So what you're saying is that the lives of the people you fight next to are more important than the orders that you receive from the council.\n所以你的意思是，与你并肩作战之人的性命，比议会下达给你的命令更重要。"

    old "Yes, that's exactly what I'm saying."
    new "Yes, that's exactly what I'm saying.\n对，这正是我的意思。"

    old "Those are dangerous words, [protag]. Some might even call them treasonous. They sound like the words of a rogue or a renegade."
    new "Those are dangerous words, [protag]. Some might even call them treasonous. They sound like the words of a rogue or a renegade.\n这些话很危险，[protag]。有些人甚至会说这是叛国之言。它们听起来像是一个流氓或叛逆者说的话。"

    old "But those words are the truth."
    new "But those words are the truth.\n但那些话是事实。"

    old "Cedric places his palms together and breathes deeply."
    new "Cedric places his palms together and breathes deeply.\nCedric 双掌合十，深深地吸了一口气。"

    old "Those treasonous thoughts you've just shared...I've thought them many times myself."
    new "Those treasonous thoughts you've just shared...I've thought them many times myself.\n你刚才说出的那些叛逆念头……我自己也想过很多次。"

    old "Cedric?"
    new "Cedric?\nCedric？"

    old "A man of the military must respect the chain of command. The private is subordinate to the corporal. The corporal is subordinate to the sergeant. And so on, all the way until I became a general, and I answered directly to the orders of the council."
    new "A man of the military must respect the chain of command. The private is subordinate to the corporal. The corporal is subordinate to the sergeant. And so on, all the way until I became a general, and I answered directly to the orders of the council.\n军人必须尊重指挥链。列兵服从下士。下士服从中士。依此类推，一直到我自己当上将军，直接听命于议会的命令。"

    old "Well, the council has blind spots. The council is imperfect. They don't see things the way that soldiers see them."
    new "Well, the council has blind spots. The council is imperfect. They don't see things the way that soldiers see them.\n可是，议会有盲区。议会并不完美。他们看事情的方式和士兵不一样。"

    old "I never erred in my duty to the council. I always followed their instructions, even when I disagreed with them. Disobeying them, committing the ultimate act of insubordination, was never necessary. However, for a long time I considered what I might do if it did become necessary."
    new "I never erred in my duty to the council. I always followed their instructions, even when I disagreed with them. Disobeying them, committing the ultimate act of insubordination, was never necessary. However, for a long time I considered what I might do if it did become necessary.\n我从未在对议会的职责上出过差错。即使我不同意他们的指示，我也总是照做。违抗他们、犯下最极端的抗命之举，从来都没有必要。然而，很长一段时间里，我都在想，如果有一天它真的变得必要，我会怎么做。"

    old "The Grimoire council is the highest authority in all the land. But there needs to be a group capable of questioning the council's authority in times of dire need. And using my network of military contacts, I've assembled a loose coalition of others like myself, ready to commit to action if the circumstances ever demand it."
    new "The Grimoire council is the highest authority in all the land. But there needs to be a group capable of questioning the council's authority in times of dire need. And using my network of military contacts, I've assembled a loose coalition of others like myself, ready to commit to action if the circumstances ever demand it.\nGrimoire 议会是这片土地上的最高权威。但需要有一个团体，能在万分危急之时质疑议会的权威。而借助我的军中关系网，我召集起了一个由我这样的人组成的松散联盟，一旦局势需要，随时准备付诸行动。"

    old "Cedric, it sounds like you are talking about a revolution."
    new "Cedric, it sounds like you are talking about a revolution.\nCedric，听起来你像是在说一场革命。"

    old "I have no plans of overthrowing the government. But if it one day becomes necessary...what side would you find yourself on, [protag]? Would you take the council's side, unquestioningly, in all circumstances, or might you be persuaded to join me and the coalition of soldiers whose greatest loyalty is to each other, the comrades that they forged in the fires of combat?"
    new "I have no plans of overthrowing the government. But if it one day becomes necessary...what side would you find yourself on, [protag]? Would you take the council's side, unquestioningly, in all circumstances, or might you be persuaded to join me and the coalition of soldiers whose greatest loyalty is to each other, the comrades that they forged in the fires of combat?\n我没有推翻政府的计划。但若有一天这变得必要……[protag]，你会站在哪一边？你会在任何情况下都不加质疑地站到议会一边，还是说，你有可能被说服，加入我和那个士兵联盟——他们最大的忠诚属于彼此，属于那些在战火中铸就的战友？"

    old "I would not be so selfish as to demand an answer from you immediately. Right now, your preoccupations are with the business around N'Mar. That is one area in which my interests and the interests of the council are closely aligned."
    new "I would not be so selfish as to demand an answer from you immediately. Right now, your preoccupations are with the business around N'Mar. That is one area in which my interests and the interests of the council are closely aligned.\n我不会自私到要你现在就给我答案。眼下，你操心的是 N'Mar 周边的事务。那正是我的利益与议会的利益高度一致的一个领域。"

    old "However, when your mission concludes, I would appreciate an answer. And I'm well aware that the answer to that question might happen to be 'no.'"
    new "However, when your mission concludes, I would appreciate an answer. And I'm well aware that the answer to that question might happen to be 'no.'\n不过，等你任务结束时，我会很感激你能给我一个答案。而且我很清楚，那个问题的答案也许会是“不”。"

    old "Why are you telling me all of this so openly? Aren't you worried I might decide to reveal your conspiracy?"
    new "Why are you telling me all of this so openly? Aren't you worried I might decide to reveal your conspiracy?\n你为什么把这些事这么公开地告诉我？你不担心我会决定揭发你的密谋吗？"

    old "As of now, there's nothing to reveal. Just a series of handshakes between like-minded people."
    new "As of now, there's nothing to reveal. Just a series of handshakes between like-minded people.\n就目前而言，没什么可揭发的。不过是志同道合之人之间的一连串握手罢了。"

    old "Anyway, think about it, will you? Well, I know you will think about it, whether or not I tell you to."
    new "Anyway, think about it, will you? Well, I know you will think about it, whether or not I tell you to.\n总之，你考虑一下吧，好吗？嗯，我知道你会考虑的，不管我有没有让你去考虑。"

    old "Goodbye, [protag]. We'll talk again. Later."
    new "Goodbye, [protag]. We'll talk again. Later.\n再见，[protag]。我们以后再谈。回头见。"

    old "My greatest loyalty is to the people of this land. Of course the interests of the greater good prevail over the interests of a few fighters."
    new "My greatest loyalty is to the people of this land. Of course the interests of the greater good prevail over the interests of a few fighters.\n我最大的忠诚，属于这片土地的人民。当然，大局的利益要胜过少数战士的利益。"

    old "After all, the entire reason that band of fighters is assembled is so that they can cooperate to accomplish what needs to be done for the greater good. If I valued the lives of my companions above everything else, I might not be so casual about leading them into N'Mar. But there is a mission that must be done, and so we will do it, even if it requires some sacrifice."
    new "After all, the entire reason that band of fighters is assembled is so that they can cooperate to accomplish what needs to be done for the greater good. If I valued the lives of my companions above everything else, I might not be so casual about leading them into N'Mar. But there is a mission that must be done, and so we will do it, even if it requires some sacrifice.\n毕竟，召集这群战士的全部原因，就是为了让他们协作完成那些为大局而必须做的事。如果我把同伴的性命看得高于一切，我或许就不会那么随意地领他们进 N'Mar 了。但有一项必须完成的使命，所以我们就会去做，哪怕需要付出一些牺牲。"

    old "So, you carry out the will of the council."
    new "So, you carry out the will of the council.\n所以，你是在执行议会的意志。"

    old "The council represents the interests of the people of the empire. That's how government works, Cedric. I serve the people by serving the council."
    new "The council represents the interests of the people of the empire. That's how government works, Cedric. I serve the people by serving the council.\n议会代表帝国人民的利益。政府就是这么运作的，Cedric。我通过为议会服务来为人民服务。"

    old "As well a proper soldier should."
    new "As well a proper soldier should.\n这才是一名合格士兵该有的样子。"

    old "Cedric nods and pats me on the shoulder."
    new "Cedric nods and pats me on the shoulder.\nCedric 点点头，拍了拍我的肩膀。"

    old "You've become a fine leader, [protag]. I'm not sure that I have anything to teach you. Whatever needs to be done, I'll trust that you'll do it. The fate of many rests on your shoulders, but you seem well-equipped to handle the burden. But perhaps I can lighten the burden for you."
    new "You've become a fine leader, [protag]. I'm not sure that I have anything to teach you. Whatever needs to be done, I'll trust that you'll do it. The fate of many rests on your shoulders, but you seem well-equipped to handle the burden. But perhaps I can lighten the burden for you.\n你已经成为一名出色的领袖了，[protag]。我不确定我还有什么能教你的。无论需要做什么，我都相信你会去做。许多人的命运压在你的肩上，但你看上去足以担起这副担子。不过，也许我能为你减轻一点负担。"

    old "Cedric looks up at the ceiling of the manor, as if appraising his own dwelling."
    new "Cedric looks up at the ceiling of the manor, as if appraising his own dwelling.\nCedric 抬头望向庄园的天花板，仿佛在审视自己的居所。"

    old "This mansion seems like a poor place for a man like me to be spending his days. I shouldn't be sitting here, sitting in front of a fire place. I should be in a war room, looking at a map, dictating troop movements."
    new "This mansion seems like a poor place for a man like me to be spending his days. I shouldn't be sitting here, sitting in front of a fire place. I should be in a war room, looking at a map, dictating troop movements.\n这栋宅子，对我这样的人来说，似乎是个蹉跎岁月的不合适之所。我不该坐在这里，坐在壁炉前。我该待在作战室里，看着地图，指挥军队的调动。"

    old "I think I shall leave this estate behind. I think that my days would be better spent in the council chambers. I've already used as much of my influence as I can for the cause, but being a social influencer was never my strong suit. So whatever skill I have as a military strategist that I have that the council can make use of, I'll offer it up."
    new "I think I shall leave this estate behind. I think that my days would be better spent in the council chambers. I've already used as much of my influence as I can for the cause, but being a social influencer was never my strong suit. So whatever skill I have as a military strategist that I have that the council can make use of, I'll offer it up.\n我想我该离开这处庄园了。我想我的日子还是更适合在议会议事厅里度过。为了这项事业，我已尽我所能用掉了自己的影响力，但当一个左右舆论的人从来不是我的强项。所以，作为军事战略家，凡是我拥有、议会又用得上的本事，我都会献出来。"

    old "Does that mean we'll be seeing more of each other?"
    new "Does that mean we'll be seeing more of each other?\n那是不是说我们以后见面的机会会更多？"

    old "Probably less, actually. You don't strike me as the type who spends much time in the council chambers. You're the type of soldier who marches into battle, and now I'm the type who stays home and decides how the marching best ought to be done."
    new "Probably less, actually. You don't strike me as the type who spends much time in the council chambers. You're the type of soldier who marches into battle, and now I'm the type who stays home and decides how the marching best ought to be done.\n其实，多半会更少。你给我的印象，不像是会常在议会议事厅里久留的人。你是那种开赴战场的士兵，而现在，我是那种留守后方、决定这仗该怎么打的类型。"

    old "Well, you command an autonomous unit, but there are other troops who aren't so autonomous. So I'll be behind closed doors, figuring out how best to command them."
    new "Well, you command an autonomous unit, but there are other troops who aren't so autonomous. So I'll be behind closed doors, figuring out how best to command them.\n嗯，你指挥的是一支自主行动的队伍，但还有其他不那么自主的部队。所以我会闭门不出，琢磨如何最好地指挥他们。"

    old "I feel a bit too old to be doing this. But seeing you...it's filled me with a desire to serve. And so I shall, with everything I can."
    new "I feel a bit too old to be doing this. But seeing you...it's filled me with a desire to serve. And so I shall, with everything I can.\n我觉得自己有点太老了，做不了这些了。但看到你……我心中又燃起了效力的渴望。所以我会去做的，倾尽我所能。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. Thank you for giving me hope for our country's future. Let's make it a good one."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. Thank you for giving me hope for our country's future. Let's make it a good one.\n谢谢你，[protag]。谢谢你给了我对这个国家未来的希望。让我们把它变成一个好未来吧。"

    old "Before I leave the mansion, Cedric calls out to me."
    new "Before I leave the mansion, Cedric calls out to me.\n在我离开宅邸之前，Cedric 叫住了我。"

    old "[protag], wait! Before you go, I... I would like you to take this."
    new "[protag], wait! Before you go, I... I would like you to take this.\n[protag]，等等！在你走之前，我……我想让你收下这个。"

    old "An old amulet. It was a gift from the Queen of Flowervale, Magesta."
    new "An old amulet. It was a gift from the Queen of Flowervale, Magesta.\n一枚旧护身符。这是 Flowervale 的女王 Magesta 送的礼物。"

    old "Flowervale? That's far away from here. I'm curious, How did you two meet?"
    new "Flowervale? That's far away from here. I'm curious, How did you two meet?\nFlowervale？那离这儿可远了。我很好奇，你们俩是怎么认识的？"

    old "Actually, we've never met. She sent this amulet to me as a gift many years ago for saving an elven noble from Triberg. I didn't know it at the time, but the young lady was actually Magesta's niece, Trixi."
    new "Actually, we've never met. She sent this amulet to me as a gift many years ago for saving an elven noble from Triberg. I didn't know it at the time, but the young lady was actually Magesta's niece, Trixi.\n其实，我们从未见过面。多年前，我从 Triberg 救下了一位精灵贵族，她便把这枚护身符当作礼物寄给了我。当时我并不知道，那位年轻小姐其实正是 Magesta 的侄女 Trixi。"

    old "Triberg, huh? It looks like your time in the army took you all over Aravorn."
    new "Triberg, huh? It looks like your time in the army took you all over Aravorn.\nTriberg，是吗？看来你的军旅生涯带你走遍了 Aravorn。"

    old "It did, [protag]. It did. Maybe we can sit down and swap more stories some day. For now though, take this with you. I'm too old to fight so I have little use for it. Perhaps it can serve you or someone on your team instead."
    new "It did, [protag]. It did. Maybe we can sit down and swap more stories some day. For now though, take this with you. I'm too old to fight so I have little use for it. Perhaps it can serve you or someone on your team instead.\n确实如此，[protag]。确实如此。也许哪一天我们可以坐下来，多交换些故事。不过眼下，你把这个带上吧。我太老了，打不动仗了，所以它对我没什么用处。也许它能为你或你队伍里的某个人派上用场。"

    old "Are you sure you want me to take this?"
    new "Are you sure you want me to take this?\n你确定要我把这个带走吗？"

    old "I... yes. This amulet brings back a lot of memories, but in times like these everyone needs to make sacrifices. This is the least I can do. Now please, [protag], take it before I change my mind."
    new "I... yes. This amulet brings back a lot of memories, but in times like these everyone needs to make sacrifices. This is the least I can do. Now please, [protag], take it before I change my mind.\n我……是的。这枚护身符会勾起许多回忆，但在这样的时局里，每个人都需要做出牺牲。这是我能做的最起码的事了。现在，请吧，[protag]，趁我还没改变主意，快把它拿走。"

    old "Thank you, Sir Cedric. This amulet is an amazing gift. We'll put it to good use."
    new "Thank you, Sir Cedric. This amulet is an amazing gift. We'll put it to good use.\n谢谢你，Cedric 爵士。这枚护身符是份了不起的礼物。我们会好好利用它的。"

    old "[protag], you've returned. Are you ready to revisit the tomb?"
    new "[protag], you've returned. Are you ready to revisit the tomb?\n[protag]，你回来了。准备好再次造访那座墓了吗？"

    old "I'm ready. Are you prepared?"
    new "I'm ready. Are you prepared?\n我准备好了。你呢，准备好了吗？"

    old "Yes. As is Nuala."
    new "Yes. As is Nuala.\n是的。Nuala 也准备好了。"

    old "I've been overwhelmed with excitement ever since Larik told me of your findings. If we're going to the tomb, then let's be quick about it."
    new "I've been overwhelmed with excitement ever since Larik told me of your findings. If we're going to the tomb, then let's be quick about it.\n自从 Larik 把你的发现告诉我之后，我就一直激动得不得了。要是我们要去那座墓，那就快点动身吧。"

    old "Ha! Nuala's enthusiasm is unmatched, as you can see. Though, I too find myself brimming with curiosity."
    new "Ha! Nuala's enthusiasm is unmatched, as you can see. Though, I too find myself brimming with curiosity.\n哈！如你所见，Nuala 的热情无人能比。不过，我也满心好奇。"

    old "I hope you brought a few friends with you. The three of us might not be enough for the trials of the Tomb Of Urd."
    new "I hope you brought a few friends with you. The three of us might not be enough for the trials of the Tomb Of Urd.\n希望你还带了几位朋友。就凭我们三个，恐怕不足以应对 Tomb Of Urd 的考验。"

    old "Don't worry, I have."
    new "Don't worry, I have.\n别担心，我带了。"

    old "We set out in the direction of the tomb. As we walk, to pass the time..."
    new "We set out in the direction of the tomb. As we walk, to pass the time...\n我们朝那座墓的方向出发。一路上，为了打发时间……"

    old "Nuala, you said you've been overwhelmed with excitement for this investigation. What exactly has you so excited?"
    new "Nuala, you said you've been overwhelmed with excitement for this investigation. What exactly has you so excited?\nNuala，你说你对这次调查激动得不得了。究竟是什么让你这么兴奋？"

    old "Urd's legendary weapons may be inside. I'd very much like to see them for myself."
    new "Urd's legendary weapons may be inside. I'd very much like to see them for myself.\nUrd 的传奇武器也许就在里面。我很想亲眼看看。"

    old "Is there a reason that your people have never ventured into the tomb to try and find the weapons?"
    new "Is there a reason that your people have never ventured into the tomb to try and find the weapons?\n你们的人从未冒险进入那座墓去寻找武器，是有什么原因吗？"

    old "Legend is that Urd preserved his weapons for times of need. They are not something to be used wantonly."
    new "Legend is that Urd preserved his weapons for times of need. They are not something to be used wantonly.\n传说 Urd 把他的武器保存下来，是为了危急之时。它们不是可以随意使用的东西。"

    old "So what has changed?"
    new "So what has changed?\n那么，现在有什么变了？"

    old "Wouldn't you say we're now in times of need? The creeping corrosion of whatever infested Urd's tomb still lurks in the lands of Aravorn. If we don't end it at the source, it may return again."
    new "Wouldn't you say we're now in times of need? The creeping corrosion of whatever infested Urd's tomb still lurks in the lands of Aravorn. If we don't end it at the source, it may return again.\n你不觉得我们现在正处在危急之时吗？那侵染了 Urd 之墓的、缓缓蔓延的腐化之物，仍潜伏在 Aravorn 的土地上。如果我们不从根源上消灭它，它可能还会卷土重来。"

    old "Besides, Baneslayer and Benediction were made for battling. They're weapons to be used in battle, not some ancient treasure to be forever preserved underground."
    new "Besides, Baneslayer and Benediction were made for battling. They're weapons to be used in battle, not some ancient treasure to be forever preserved underground.\n况且，Baneslayer 和 Benediction 生来就是为战斗而造的。它们是用来在战场上使用的武器，不是什么该永远埋在地底保存的古代珍宝。"

    old "So, just how much do you believe from the tales of Baneslayer and Benediction?"
    new "So, just how much do you believe from the tales of Baneslayer and Benediction?\n那么，关于 Baneslayer 和 Benediction 的故事，你相信多少？"

    old "I believe all the stories, though I only repeat the good ones."
    new "I believe all the stories, though I only repeat the good ones.\n我相信所有的故事，只不过我只转述那些好的。"

    old "What's a 'good' story?"
    new "What's a 'good' story?\n什么是“好”故事？"

    old "A good story has a beginning, a middle, and an end."
    new "A good story has a beginning, a middle, and an end.\n一个好故事，有开头、有中段、有结尾。"

    old "I would think that all of the stories of Urd would have those."
    new "I would think that all of the stories of Urd would have those.\n我原以为 Urd 的所有故事都该具备这些。"

    old "You might think. But there are some stories that tease you with a promising beginning and an exciting middle, only to leave you wanting when you discover that the story's ending is not known."
    new "You might think. But there are some stories that tease you with a promising beginning and an exciting middle, only to leave you wanting when you discover that the story's ending is not known.\n你也许会这么想。但有些故事，先用一个充满希望的开头和激动人心的中段吊你胃口，最后却让你怅然若失，因为你发现故事的结局无人知晓。"

    old "Could you give an example?"
    new "Could you give an example?\n能举个例子吗？"

    old "The battle in which Urd banished the lich, the spirit of an ancient and evil king who fused his essence to a reanimated corpse in a mad quest for immortality."
    new "The battle in which Urd banished the lich, the spirit of an ancient and evil king who fused his essence to a reanimated corpse in a mad quest for immortality.\n就是 Urd 放逐巫妖的那场战斗——那巫妖是一位古老邪恶国王的亡魂，他为了疯狂地追寻永生，把自己的精魂与一具复活的尸骸融为一体。"

    old "Actually, in most versions of the story, the lich was just a mad magician. Not a king."
    new "Actually, in most versions of the story, the lich was just a mad magician. Not a king.\n其实，在这个故事的大多数版本里，那巫妖只是一个疯狂的魔法师。并不是国王。"

    old "Yes, but the version of the story about the mad and evil king sounds better, so that's the version I always choose to repeat."
    new "Yes, but the version of the story about the mad and evil king sounds better, so that's the version I always choose to repeat.\n是的，但那个关于疯狂邪恶国王的版本听起来更精彩，所以我总是选择转述那个版本。"

    old "Anyway, the story goes that Urd used his axe and rod to slay the minions of the lich. It's at this point in the story that you would expect to hear how Urd defeated the lich."
    new "Anyway, the story goes that Urd used his axe and rod to slay the minions of the lich. It's at this point in the story that you would expect to hear how Urd defeated the lich.\n总之，故事讲到 Urd 用他的斧头和法杖斩杀了巫妖的爪牙。讲到这个节骨眼上，你自然会期待听到 Urd 是如何击败巫妖的。"

    old "But..."
    new "But...\n但是……"

    old "But none of the versions of this story I've heard explain how Urd defeated the lich. Only that he reigned victorious, and ended the terror of the lich."
    new "But none of the versions of this story I've heard explain how Urd defeated the lich. Only that he reigned victorious, and ended the terror of the lich.\n但我听过的这个故事的每一个版本，都没有解释 Urd 是如何击败巫妖的。只说他最终得胜，终结了巫妖的恐怖统治。"

    old "None of the versions have a real ending?"
    new "None of the versions have a real ending?\n所有版本都没有一个真正的结局？"

    old "None of them."
    new "None of them.\n一个都没有。"

    old "You would think that with all the different versions of this story that exist, at some point a storyteller might have come up with a better ending..."
    new "You would think that with all the different versions of this story that exist, at some point a storyteller might have come up with a better ending...\n你会以为，既然这个故事存在这么多不同版本，总该有某个说书人在什么时候编出过一个更好的结局……"

    old "It is not a storyteller's place to 'come up' with a better ending. They simply report the story as they observed it, or as it was told to them."
    new "It is not a storyteller's place to 'come up' with a better ending. They simply report the story as they observed it, or as it was told to them.\n编造一个更好的结局，可不是说书人该做的事。他们只是如实讲述故事——要么按他们亲见的样子，要么按别人讲给他们的样子。"

    old "So you believe all the stories are true, then."
    new "So you believe all the stories are true, then.\n所以，你是相信所有这些故事都是真的了。"

    old "How is it that you can believe all of the stories are true while multiple versions of them exist?"
    new "How is it that you can believe all of the stories are true while multiple versions of them exist?\n既然这些故事存在多个版本，你怎么还能相信它们全都是真的呢？"

    old "You mean, how is it that I can hear a story of a lich king, and a lich magician, and believe both of them when they seem to contradict each other?"
    new "You mean, how is it that I can hear a story of a lich king, and a lich magician, and believe both of them when they seem to contradict each other?\n你是说，我怎么能一边听着巫妖国王的故事，一边听着巫妖魔法师的故事，明明两者看似互相矛盾，我却两个都信？"

    old "Yes, that would be one example."
    new "Yes, that would be one example.\n对，那就是个例子。"

    old "Those two stories aren't necessarily contradictory."
    new "Those two stories aren't necessarily contradictory.\n这两个故事未必互相矛盾。"

    old "Please, explain."
    new "Please, explain.\n请说说看。"

    old "There might have been a lich who was formerly a king who also practiced magic. If that were the case, then the story which reported the lich as being a magician and the story of the lich who was a king would both be correct."
    new "There might have been a lich who was formerly a king who also practiced magic. If that were the case, then the story which reported the lich as being a magician and the story of the lich who was a king would both be correct.\n也许有那么一个巫妖，原本是国王，也修习魔法。若是如此，那么把巫妖说成魔法师的故事，和把巫妖说成国王的故事，就都是对的。"

    old "It could also be that they are not two versions of the same story, but two different stories altogether.After all, Urd lived a long life. It is possible that he fought more than one lich during his travels."
    new "It could also be that they are not two versions of the same story, but two different stories altogether.After all, Urd lived a long life. It is possible that he fought more than one lich during his travels.\n也有可能，它们并不是同一个故事的两个版本，而是两个完全不同的故事。毕竟 Urd 活了很久。他在旅途中与不止一个巫妖交过手，也是可能的。"

    old "To me, it sounds like you are going to great lengths to justify how both stories might be true..."
    new "To me, it sounds like you are going to great lengths to justify how both stories might be true...\n在我听来，你这是在费尽心机地论证这两个故事可能都是真的……"

    old "Isn't it more likely that one of the stories is made up? Or perhaps both of them are."
    new "Isn't it more likely that one of the stories is made up? Or perhaps both of them are.\n更有可能的，难道不是其中一个故事是编造的？又或者两个都是。"

    old "I suppose you're right. Just because two stories seem to differ doesn't necessarily mean that they're contradictory."
    new "I suppose you're right. Just because two stories seem to differ doesn't necessarily mean that they're contradictory.\n我想你说得对。两个故事看起来不同，并不一定就意味着它们互相矛盾。"

    old "Regardless, whether or not we choose to believe the stories doesn't change the past. Whatever happened, happened. What we choose to do with the information we are given is up to us."
    new "Regardless, whether or not we choose to believe the stories doesn't change the past. Whatever happened, happened. What we choose to do with the information we are given is up to us.\n无论如何，我们选择信不信这些故事，都改变不了过去。发生过的，就是发生过了。而拿到这些信息后选择怎么做，取决于我们自己。"

    old "Actually, the fact that I believe all of the stories makes me somewhat unique."
    new "Actually, the fact that I believe all of the stories makes me somewhat unique.\n其实，正因为我所有的故事都信，我多少显得有些与众不同。"

    old "For example, Larik doesn't believe all of the stories."
    new "For example, Larik doesn't believe all of the stories.\n比如说，Larik 就不会所有的故事都信。"

    old "I don't believe all of the stories unquestioningly. But I think all of them contain good lessons, even if those lessons are simply providing us with a heroic figure to believe in."
    new "I don't believe all of the stories unquestioningly. But I think all of them contain good lessons, even if those lessons are simply providing us with a heroic figure to believe in.\n我并非不加质疑地相信所有故事。但我认为它们都蕴含着有益的教诲，哪怕那些教诲只是给了我们一个可以信奉的英雄形象。"

    old "And we oftentimes find that the answers to our own mysteries are hidden in the stories of the past."
    new "And we oftentimes find that the answers to our own mysteries are hidden in the stories of the past.\n而且我们常常发现，我们自己那些谜题的答案，就藏在往昔的故事里。"

    old "What is it that they say? A smart man learns from his experiences. A wise man learns from the experiences of others."
    new "What is it that they say? A smart man learns from his experiences. A wise man learns from the experiences of others.\n那句话是怎么说的来着？聪明人从自己的经历中学习。智者从他人的经历中学习。"

    old "And in the end, that's what stories are."
    new "And in the end, that's what stories are.\n说到底，故事的本质就是这样。"

    old "Larik, you said you were brimming with curiosity. What exactly are you hoping to discover?"
    new "Larik, you said you were brimming with curiosity. What exactly are you hoping to discover?\nLarik，你说你满心好奇。你究竟希望发现什么？"

    old "For myself? I'd like to learn more about the lore of Urd."
    new "For myself? I'd like to learn more about the lore of Urd.\n就我而言？我想更多地了解 Urd 的传说。"

    old "You seem to be quite an enthusiast. You've already shared several stories of Urd with me."
    new "You seem to be quite an enthusiast. You've already shared several stories of Urd with me.\n你似乎相当热衷于此。你已经跟我分享过好几个 Urd 的故事了。"

    old "And I could share many more."
    new "And I could share many more.\n而我还能分享更多。"

    old "Tell me a story about Urd, then. What story is the most unique?"
    new "Tell me a story about Urd, then. What story is the most unique?\n那就给我讲一个 Urd 的故事吧。哪个故事最独特？"

    old "The most unique story? That would be the tale of the lich."
    new "The most unique story? That would be the tale of the lich.\n最独特的故事？那要数巫妖的故事了。"

    old "Lich?"
    new "Lich?\n巫妖？"

    old "The lich was a sorcerer who combined his intellect with the power of the undead to grant himself immortality."
    new "The lich was a sorcerer who combined his intellect with the power of the undead to grant himself immortality.\n那巫妖是个术士，他将自己的智慧与亡灵之力结合，好让自己获得永生。"

    old "Urd confronted the lich. Baneslayer in one hand, Benediction in the other."
    new "Urd confronted the lich. Baneslayer in one hand, Benediction in the other.\nUrd 与巫妖对峙。一手握着 Baneslayer，另一手握着 Benediction。"

    old "The lich summoned corpses from the ground to fight on his behalf. Urd swung his axe, and decapitated the walking corpses. However, as he removed each individual limb, he discovered something disturbing."
    new "The lich summoned corpses from the ground to fight on his behalf. Urd swung his axe, and decapitated the walking corpses. However, as he removed each individual limb, he discovered something disturbing.\n巫妖从地里召出尸体为他而战。Urd 挥动他的战斧，将那些行走的尸体斩首。然而，当他砍下每一截残肢时，他发现了某种令人不安的事情。"

    old "The limbs continued to move, even after being separated from their body. The lich was puppeting the limbs in exactly the same way he puppeted the corpses."
    new "The limbs continued to move, even after being separated from their body. The lich was puppeting the limbs in exactly the same way he puppeted the corpses.\n那些残肢即使与躯体分离后，仍在继续活动。巫妖操控这些残肢的方式，与他操控尸体时如出一辙。"

    old "Urd held aloft the staff of Benediction, and called upon the light of heaven. The shambling corpses and parts immediately disintegrated as the light shone on them."
    new "Urd held aloft the staff of Benediction, and called upon the light of heaven. The shambling corpses and parts immediately disintegrated as the light shone on them.\nUrd 高举 Benediction 之杖，呼唤天堂之光。蹒跚的尸体和残肢一经光芒照到，立刻灰飞烟灭。"

    old "The lich summoned more minions, but they too were dispatched. The battle continued for days, until eventually Urd defeated the lich."
    new "The lich summoned more minions, but they too were dispatched. The battle continued for days, until eventually Urd defeated the lich.\n巫妖召来更多爪牙，但也被一一消灭。战斗持续了数日，直到最终 Urd 击败了巫妖。"

    old "Um...how exactly did Urd defeat the lich?"
    new "Um...how exactly did Urd defeat the lich?\n呃……Urd 究竟是怎么击败巫妖的？"

    old "No one knows."
    new "No one knows.\n没有人知道。"

    old "That's the end of the story? No explanation of how Urd triumphed over his immortal foe?"
    new "That's the end of the story? No explanation of how Urd triumphed over his immortal foe?\n故事就这么结束了？没有解释 Urd 是如何战胜他那不死之敌的？"

    old "As I said, no one knows."
    new "As I said, no one knows.\n正如我说的，没人知道。"

    old "You would think that oral tradition would fill in the gaps. I think it would make for a better story if Urd had devised some cunning method for slaying the lich. Hasn't anyone come up with a better ending for the story?"
    new "You would think that oral tradition would fill in the gaps. I think it would make for a better story if Urd had devised some cunning method for slaying the lich. Hasn't anyone come up with a better ending for the story?\n你会以为口耳相传的传统会把这些空白补上。我想，要是 Urd 设计出了某种杀死巫妖的巧妙方法，这故事会精彩得多。难道就没人给这个故事编出过更好的结局吗？"

    old "How exactly would you kill an immortal foe?"
    new "How exactly would you kill an immortal foe?\n你究竟要怎么杀死一个不死的敌人？"

    old "I don't know. But I would think that the storyteller would figure it out. What about the light of heaven? Isn't that lethal to a lich?"
    new "I don't know. But I would think that the storyteller would figure it out. What about the light of heaven? Isn't that lethal to a lich?\n我不知道。但我想说书人总该能想出办法。那天堂之光呢？那对巫妖来说难道不是致命的吗？"

    old "No. Immortality isn't exactly immortality if it's so fragile that it can be ended with exposure to sunlight, don't you think?"
    new "No. Immortality isn't exactly immortality if it's so fragile that it can be ended with exposure to sunlight, don't you think?\n不。如果永生脆弱到被阳光一照就会终结，那它也就不算什么真正的永生了，你不觉得吗？"

    old "I suppose so. Still..."
    new "I suppose so. Still...\n我想也是。不过……"

    old "Maybe we'll find more answers etched in the stone."
    new "Maybe we'll find more answers etched in the stone.\n也许我们能在刻在石头上的铭文里找到更多答案。"

    old "It seems we've arrived. Look, if you focus your gaze between those two dunes, you can see the tomb from here."
    new "It seems we've arrived. Look, if you focus your gaze between those two dunes, you can see the tomb from here.\n看来我们到了。看，你把目光集中在那两座沙丘之间，就能从这里望见那座墓。"

    old "Oh, now this is exciting."
    new "Oh, now this is exciting.\n哦，这下可让人兴奋起来了。"

    old "Just seeing the tomb in the distance is enough to excite you?"
    new "Just seeing the tomb in the distance is enough to excite you?\n光是远远望见那座墓，就足够让你兴奋了？"

    old "It's been a long time since I've been here."
    new "It's been a long time since I've been here.\n我已经很久没来过这里了。"

    old "Well, what's life without a bit of excitement?"
    new "Well, what's life without a bit of excitement?\n嗯，生活要是没有一点兴奋，那还叫什么生活？"

    old "Tomb? You didn't tell me I needed to go inside a tomb! A tomb buried in the desert sands!"
    new "Tomb? You didn't tell me I needed to go inside a tomb! A tomb buried in the desert sands!\n墓？你可没告诉我要钻进一座墓里去！一座埋在沙漠黄沙下的墓！"

    old "Hey, Dasyra, calm down. We're going in all together."
    new "Hey, Dasyra, calm down. We're going in all together.\n嘿，Dasyra，冷静点。我们大家会一起进去的。"

    old "Not reassuring. Not at all."
    new "Not reassuring. Not at all.\n这可没让人安心。一点也没有。"

    old "What is it, Leena? You think entering a tomb might upset the Gods?"
    new "What is it, Leena? You think entering a tomb might upset the Gods?\n怎么了，Leena？你觉得进入一座墓会触怒众神吗？"

    old "We amazons don't have Gods. We have Great-Mothers."
    new "We amazons don't have Gods. We have Great-Mothers.\n我们 Amazons 没有神明。我们有伟大之母。"

    old "Which are past Queens."
    new "Which are past Queens.\n也就是历代女王。"

    old "...how do you know it?"
    new "...how do you know it?\n……你是怎么知道的？"

    old "Well, I spoke with Apolimesho one time I visited Grimoire. I was curious about the Gods and ancestors that other culture choose to worship."
    new "Well, I spoke with Apolimesho one time I visited Grimoire. I was curious about the Gods and ancestors that other culture choose to worship.\n嗯，有一次我去 Grimoire 时，和 Apolimesho 聊过。我对其他文化所选择崇拜的神明和祖先很好奇。"

    old "And for what it's worth, I think it's really good that you take in such consideration your past Queens."
    new "And for what it's worth, I think it's really good that you take in such consideration your past Queens.\n而且不管怎么说，我觉得你们如此敬重历代女王，真的很好。"

    old "...thanks."
    new "...thanks.\n……谢谢。"

    old "Wait, does it means that... future generations will worship Karen? I mean, not that she isn't worth respect, but..."
    new "Wait, does it means that... future generations will worship Karen? I mean, not that she isn't worth respect, but...\n等等，那岂不是说……未来的后代会崇拜 Karen？我是说，倒不是说她不值得尊敬，但……"

    old "I think we should enter the tomb. Now."
    new "I think we should enter the tomb. Now.\n我想我们该进墓了。就现在。"

    old "Finally we've arrived."
    new "Finally we've arrived.\n我们终于到了。"

    old "What, you're not used to walking?"
    new "What, you're not used to walking?\n怎么，你不习惯走路？"

    old "I have no problem to walk, swim, run. But in the desert..."
    new "I have no problem to walk, swim, run. But in the desert...\n走路、游泳、跑步，我都没问题。但在沙漠里……"

    old "True, that was a bit exhausting for me as well. At least inside the tomb we can get a break from the desert sun."
    new "True, that was a bit exhausting for me as well. At least inside the tomb we can get a break from the desert sun.\n确实，那对我也有些累人。至少进了墓里，我们能躲开沙漠的烈日歇一歇。"

    old "What's up Vaeril?"
    new "What's up Vaeril?\n怎么了，Vaeril？"

    old "I'm not sure, but I can sense something."
    new "I'm not sure, but I can sense something.\n我不确定，但我能感应到什么。"

    old "And from your face, nothing good."
    new "And from your face, nothing good.\n而从你的表情看，不是什么好事。"

    old "No. This place is full of evil energy."
    new "No. This place is full of evil energy.\n不。这地方充满了邪恶的能量。"

    old "Are you going to be OK?"
    new "Are you going to be OK?\n你没事吧？"

    old "Don't worry [protag], I'm eager to get inside and find out what is it."
    new "Don't worry [protag], I'm eager to get inside and find out what is it.\n别担心，[protag]，我急着进去一探究竟。"

    old "I hope all this sand and wind won't ruin my skin."
    new "I hope all this sand and wind won't ruin my skin.\n希望这些沙子和风不会毁了我的皮肤。"

    old "Your skin? That's what you're worrying about?"
    new "Your skin? That's what you're worrying about?\n你的皮肤？你担心的就是这个？"

    old "Not only that. Clothes and jewelry too."
    new "Not only that. Clothes and jewelry too.\n不止这个。还有衣服和首饰。"

    old "I was kidding this time, [protag]."
    new "I was kidding this time, [protag].\n我这次是开玩笑的，[protag]。"

    old "Don't worry. I wont let my giddiness get in the way of our mission. I'm as alert and ready for action as ever."
    new "Don't worry. I wont let my giddiness get in the way of our mission. I'm as alert and ready for action as ever.\n别担心。我不会让我的兴奋劲儿妨碍到我们的任务。我和往常一样警觉，随时准备行动。"

    old "Then let's get to it."
    new "Then let's get to it.\n那我们就动手吧。"

    old "[protag], look."
    new "[protag], look.\n[protag]，看。"

    old "But... we killed the Emperor Scorpion!"
    new "But... we killed the Emperor Scorpion!\n可是……我们已经杀死了 Emperor Scorpion 啊！"

    old "They look... undead."
    new "They look... undead.\n它们看起来……是亡灵。"

    old "Undead scorpions? Now I've seen it all."
    new "Undead scorpions? Now I've seen it all.\n亡灵蝎子？这下我真是大开眼界了。"

    old "Look, there's also more of those black sand monsters."
    new "Look, there's also more of those black sand monsters.\n看，那边还有更多那种黑沙怪物。"

    old "No time to talk, they're attacking now!"
    new "No time to talk, they're attacking now!\n没时间说话了，它们攻过来了！"

    old "What was that...black thing?"
    new "What was that...black thing?\n那……黑色的东西是什么？"

    old "It's the same thing [protag] and I fought the first time we came searching for the tomb."
    new "It's the same thing [protag] and I fought the first time we came searching for the tomb.\n就是 [protag] 和我第一次来找这座墓时交手过的同一种东西。"

    old "But you said the corruption was gone?"
    new "But you said the corruption was gone?\n可你不是说腐化已经消失了吗？"

    old "Several days have passed since then. Might have returned."
    new "Several days have passed since then. Might have returned.\n从那以后已经过了好几天了。也许又回来了。"

    old "Yes, this kind of corruption needs to be stopped at its source."
    new "Yes, this kind of corruption needs to be stopped at its source.\n没错，这种腐化必须从根源上被遏制。"

    old "Otherwise, it will always slowly return."
    new "Otherwise, it will always slowly return.\n否则，它总会慢慢地卷土重来。"

    old "Curious."
    new "Curious.\n有意思。"

    old "What is it, Enok?"
    new "What is it, Enok?\n怎么了，Enok？"

    old "Those undead scorpions. Takes a lot of skills in necromancy to do it."
    new "Those undead scorpions. Takes a lot of skills in necromancy to do it.\n那些亡灵蝎子。要做到这一点，需要很高的死灵法术造诣。"

    old "Whoever or whatever did that, is a powerful dark magic user."
    new "Whoever or whatever did that, is a powerful dark magic user.\n不管是谁、是什么东西做的，那都是个强大的黑暗魔法使用者。"

    old "Hopefully not too powerful for us. We need to stop this."
    new "Hopefully not too powerful for us. We need to stop this.\n希望对我们来说不至于强得过头。我们必须阻止这一切。"

    old "That's why I am here."
    new "That's why I am here.\n这正是我在这里的原因。"

    old "The way seems clear. Let's head inside the tomb now."
    new "The way seems clear. Let's head inside the tomb now.\n路看起来畅通了。我们进墓吧。"

    old "Larik leads the way into the tomb. The others, Nuala and I follow behind him."
    new "Larik leads the way into the tomb. The others, Nuala and I follow behind him.\nLarik 领头走进墓中。其余的人——Nuala 和我——跟在他身后。"

    old "The symbols we found the last time we entered this tomb seemed to imply that we might need your talents, Nuala. Be ready."
    new "The symbols we found the last time we entered this tomb seemed to imply that we might need your talents, Nuala. Be ready.\n我们上次进这座墓时发现的符号，似乎暗示我们可能会用到你的本事，Nuala。做好准备。"

    old "Are you all ready?"
    new "Are you all ready?\n你们都准备好了吗？"

    old "I'm more than ready. Let's get to it."
    new "I'm more than ready. Let's get to it.\n我岂止是准备好了。我们开始吧。"

    old "Take us into the catacombs, Larik."
    new "Take us into the catacombs, Larik.\n带我们进地穴吧，Larik。"

    old "I nod to Larik, and he begins walking down the tomb's dark passageway. Nuala taps her staff against the wall and it begins emitting a faint light, barely enough to see by, but enough to prevent us from stumbling in the darkness."
    new "I nod to Larik, and he begins walking down the tomb's dark passageway. Nuala taps her staff against the wall and it begins emitting a faint light, barely enough to see by, but enough to prevent us from stumbling in the darkness.\n我朝 Larik 点点头，他便开始沿着墓中黑暗的通道走下去。Nuala 用她的法杖敲了敲墙壁，法杖开始发出微弱的光，虽只勉强够看清，却足以让我们不在黑暗中绊倒。"

    old "That's a handy trick."
    new "That's a handy trick.\n这招真方便。"

    old "Hopefully I'll be doing more than just serving as your torch-bearer."
    new "Hopefully I'll be doing more than just serving as your torch-bearer.\n希望我不只是给你当个举火把的。"

    old "Eventually, the passageway ends, and Larik begins running his hands over the surface of the wall in front of us."
    new "Eventually, the passageway ends, and Larik begins running his hands over the surface of the wall in front of us.\n终于，通道到了尽头，Larik 开始用手在面前墙壁的表面摸索。"

    old "Dead end?"
    new "Dead end?\n死路？"

    old "It appears that way. But some things aren't quite what they seem. Nuala, can you illuminate this part of the wall for me?"
    new "It appears that way. But some things aren't quite what they seem. Nuala, can you illuminate this part of the wall for me?\n看起来是这样。但有些东西并不完全是看上去的样子。Nuala，你能帮我把这面墙的这一部分照亮吗？"

    old "Nuala raises her staff aloft, and the wall above our heads lights up, showing symbols carved into the wall."
    new "Nuala raises her staff aloft, and the wall above our heads lights up, showing symbols carved into the wall.\nNuala 高举她的法杖，我们头顶上方的墙壁亮了起来，现出刻在墙上的符号。"

    old "Larik, can you read this?"
    new "Larik, can you read this?\nLarik，你能读懂这个吗？"

    old "Let's see...this says 'door, concealed. sunlight, reveal.'"
    new "Let's see...this says 'door, concealed. sunlight, reveal.'\n让我看看……这上面写的是“门，隐匿。阳光，显现”。"

    old "So there's a hidden door."
    new "So there's a hidden door.\n所以有一扇暗门。"

    old "And it's revealed by sunlight."
    new "And it's revealed by sunlight.\n而这扇门要靠阳光显现。"

    old "How are we supposed to get sunlight in here? Do we need to dismantle the tomb to get further."
    new "How are we supposed to get sunlight in here? Do we need to dismantle the tomb to get further.\n我们在这底下要怎么弄到阳光？难道要把整座墓拆了才能继续前进？"

    old "Sunlight could break the seal...but I think a flash of radiance will do in a pinch."
    new "Sunlight could break the seal...but I think a flash of radiance will do in a pinch.\n阳光或许能破除封印……但我想，关键时刻，一道闪光应该也能奏效。"

    old "A flash of radiance?"
    new "A flash of radiance?\n一道闪光？"

    old "You two might want to close your eyes for this."
    new "You two might want to close your eyes for this.\n你们俩最好闭上眼睛。"

    old "I close my eyes, and not a moment later, I hear Nuala's voice."
    new "I close my eyes, and not a moment later, I hear Nuala's voice.\n我闭上眼睛，没过一会儿，就听到 Nuala 的声音。"

    old "Rah!"
    new "Rah!\n哈！"

    old "Even through my closed eyelids, I can see the brilliant flash of light as I hear the sound of Nuala's staff striking stone."
    new "Even through my closed eyelids, I can see the brilliant flash of light as I hear the sound of Nuala's staff striking stone.\n即使隔着紧闭的眼皮，我也能看到那道耀眼的光芒，同时听到 Nuala 的法杖击打石头的声响。"

    old "I hear the sound of moving stone, and a cool draft begins flowing through the tomb."
    new "I hear the sound of moving stone, and a cool draft begins flowing through the tomb.\n我听到石头移动的声音，一股凉风开始穿过墓室。"

    old "I open my eyes, and it takes a few moments for them to re-adjust to the darkness. I can make out the shape of Nuala's grinning face in the dim light of her staff."
    new "I open my eyes, and it takes a few moments for them to re-adjust to the darkness. I can make out the shape of Nuala's grinning face in the dim light of her staff.\n我睁开眼睛，花了好一会儿才重新适应黑暗。在法杖的微光中，我能辨认出 Nuala 咧嘴而笑的脸庞轮廓。"

    old "Blinding light from the inside of a completely dark tomb. I guess that was enough to open the passage. Nice trick, Nuala."
    new "Blinding light from the inside of a completely dark tomb. I guess that was enough to open the passage. Nice trick, Nuala.\n在这漆黑一片的墓室里迸出一道炫目的光。我想这足以打开通道了。漂亮的一招，Nuala。"

    old "Thanks, I thought so too."
    new "Thanks, I thought so too.\n谢谢，我也这么觉得。"

    old "Nuala...next time you do something that could blind me, maybe give me more than a moment's notice, okay?"
    new "Nuala...next time you do something that could blind me, maybe give me more than a moment's notice, okay?\nNuala……下次你要做这种可能闪瞎我眼的事，能不能提前多给我一点时间提醒，好吗？"

    old "Alright, alright. But it does seem to have worked."
    new "Alright, alright. But it does seem to have worked.\n好啦，好啦。不过看起来确实管用了。"

    old "Larik presses forward, and as we progress further, the walls of the corridor seem to close in around us."
    new "Larik presses forward, and as we progress further, the walls of the corridor seem to close in around us.\nLarik 继续向前，而随着我们越走越深，走廊两侧的墙壁似乎向我们逼拢过来。"

    old "The passage is getting narrower. Be careful."
    new "The passage is getting narrower. Be careful.\n通道越来越窄了。小心。"

    old "Eventually, the passageway becomes too narrow for Larik to face forward with his broad shoulders, and he turns sideways and begins sliding down the passage with his back to one of the walls."
    new "Eventually, the passageway becomes too narrow for Larik to face forward with his broad shoulders, and he turns sideways and begins sliding down the passage with his back to one of the walls.\n终于，通道窄得让 Larik 无法用他那宽阔的肩膀正身向前，于是他侧过身子，背贴着一面墙，开始慢慢往下挪。"

    old "Are you okay, Larik?"
    new "Are you okay, Larik?\n你没事吧，Larik？"

    old "I'm feeling a bit uneasy about what will happen if we encounter some kind of foe here, but I can back up and exit this passage the same way that I entered it."
    new "I'm feeling a bit uneasy about what will happen if we encounter some kind of foe here, but I can back up and exit this passage the same way that I entered it.\n要是我们在这儿遇上什么敌人会怎样，我有点不安，但我可以后退，按原路退出这条通道。"

    old "So you're not worried about getting stuck?"
    new "So you're not worried about getting stuck?\n所以你并不担心会被卡住？"

    old "Ha! It'll take more than these narrow walls to trap me. Don't worry, [protag]. As long as it's just us here, I feel perfectly safe."
    new "Ha! It'll take more than these narrow walls to trap me. Don't worry, [protag]. As long as it's just us here, I feel perfectly safe.\n哈！光凭这几面窄墙还困不住我。别担心，[protag]。只要这里只有我们自己人，我就觉得十分安全。"

    old "Well, for once I feel I'm of the right size for the job."
    new "Well, for once I feel I'm of the right size for the job.\n嗯，这回我总算觉得自己的体型正适合这差事了。"

    old "Hah. You can say it, Dasyra."
    new "Hah. You can say it, Dasyra.\n哈。你可以直说，Dasyra。"

    old "Still, this place gives me the shivers."
    new "Still, this place gives me the shivers.\n不过，这地方还是让我直打寒颤。"

    old "Narrow? What do you mean narrow? It's just fine!"
    new "Narrow? What do you mean narrow? It's just fine!\n窄？你什么意思窄？这挺好的！"

    old "Don't brag, Galan. What if I need to climb some walls later?"
    new "Don't brag, Galan. What if I need to climb some walls later?\n别吹牛，Galan。要是待会儿我得爬墙怎么办？"

    old "Hmpf. I can climb just fine. You've seen me already doing it."
    new "Hmpf. I can climb just fine. You've seen me already doing it.\n哼。我爬墙可没问题。你已经见过我爬了。"

    old "Let's keep going, then."
    new "Let's keep going, then.\n那我们继续走吧。"

    old "Let's stop and listen. If there is anyone down here besides us, we should be able to hear them. And I'd prefer to hear them before we see them."
    new "Let's stop and listen. If there is anyone down here besides us, we should be able to hear them. And I'd prefer to hear them before we see them.\n我们停下来听一听。如果这下面除了我们还有别人，我们应该能听到。而且我宁愿先听到他们，再看到他们。"

    old "I lean against the wall to steady myself and listen. I hear...nothing. A few moments later, I hear a light pounding inside of my head, matching the rhythmic beat of my own pulse."
    new "I lean against the wall to steady myself and listen. I hear...nothing. A few moments later, I hear a light pounding inside of my head, matching the rhythmic beat of my own pulse.\n我靠在墙上稳住自己，侧耳倾听。我听到……什么也没有。过了片刻，我听到脑袋里传来轻轻的砰砰声，与我自己的脉搏节奏相合。"

    old "For a moment there, it was so quiet in here that I could hear my own heartbeat."
    new "For a moment there, it was so quiet in here that I could hear my own heartbeat.\n有那么一会儿，这里静得能让我听见自己的心跳。"

    old "I think that means we're alone."
    new "I think that means we're alone.\n我想这意味着这里只有我们自己。"

    old "I guess that means it's safe to keep going. At the very least, we're probably not at risk of being ambushed."
    new "I guess that means it's safe to keep going. At the very least, we're probably not at risk of being ambushed.\n我想这意味着继续前进是安全的。至少，我们大概没有被埋伏的危险。"

    old "We arrive in another chamber. It's very dark."
    new "We arrive in another chamber. It's very dark.\n我们来到另一个房间。里面非常黑。"

    old "This darkness... seems almost a sort of dark fog."
    new "This darkness... seems almost a sort of dark fog.\n这黑暗……几乎像是某种黑雾。"

    old "I agree, something it's not right here."
    new "I agree, something it's not right here.\n我同意，这里有什么不对劲。"

    old "Did you hear it? What was that sound?"
    new "Did you hear it? What was that sound?\n你听到了吗？那是什么声音？"

    old "I think you found your answer, [protag]."
    new "I think you found your answer, [protag].\n我想你找到答案了，[protag]。"

    old "From all around us, skeletons begins to rise from the ground. We're completely surrounded."
    new "From all around us, skeletons begins to rise from the ground. We're completely surrounded.\n骷髅开始从我们四周的地面升起。我们被彻底包围了。"

    old "Fall back! Let's reorganize and strike back!"
    new "Fall back! Let's reorganize and strike back!\n后撤！我们重新集结，再反击！"

    old "Phew. That was all of them?"
    new "Phew. That was all of them?\n呼。全都解决了吗？"

    old "Let me look around... I see 3 more in that corner."
    new "Let me look around... I see 3 more in that corner.\n让我看看四周……我看到那个角落里还有 3 个。"

    old "One of them is not a skeleton. It's bigger and-"
    new "One of them is not a skeleton. It's bigger and-\n其中一个不是骷髅。它更大，而且——"

    old "Bwwaahh!"
    new "Bwwaahh!\n哇啊！"

    old "A giant mummy!?"
    new "A giant mummy!?\n一具巨型木乃伊！？"

    old "The dark fog...it faded ?"
    new "The dark fog...it faded ?\n那黑雾……消散了？"

    old "Yes. It seems that killing that mummy disrupted the dark magic in this place."
    new "Yes. It seems that killing that mummy disrupted the dark magic in this place.\n是的。看来杀死那具木乃伊，搅乱了此地的黑暗魔法。"

    old "I believe it's safe to go forward now."
    new "I believe it's safe to go forward now.\n我相信现在可以继续前进了。"

    old "Wait. This last fight was tough. I'm not sure it's wise to keep going."
    new "Wait. This last fight was tough. I'm not sure it's wise to keep going.\n等等。刚才那场战斗很艰难。我不确定继续前进是否明智。"

    old "But the path is clear now."
    new "But the path is clear now.\n但现在路已经畅通了。"

    old "We thought there was nobody even before we stumbled into this room. I understand your desire to explore further, and I am eager too."
    new "We thought there was nobody even before we stumbled into this room. I understand your desire to explore further, and I am eager too.\n就连闯进这个房间之前，我们都以为这里没人。我理解你想进一步探索的渴望，我也一样急切。"

    old "But I must think about the team, I can't put them all at risk."
    new "But I must think about the team, I can't put them all at risk.\n但我必须为队伍着想，我不能让所有人一起冒险。"

    old "Oh? What do you propose?"
    new "Oh? What do you propose?\n哦？你有什么提议？"

    old "They wait outside and recover, and the three of us go on."
    new "They wait outside and recover, and the three of us go on.\n他们留在外面休整，我们三个继续前进。"

    old "We asked their help to reach the tomb's inner chamber. We got it."
    new "We asked their help to reach the tomb's inner chamber. We got it.\n我们请他们帮忙，是为了到达墓的内室。我们已经到这儿了。"

    old "I agree. Nuala and I have a personal interest in this. It's not fair to ask for even more help."
    new "I agree. Nuala and I have a personal interest in this. It's not fair to ask for even more help.\n我同意。Nuala 和我在这件事上都有私人的牵挂。再要求更多帮助，就不公平了。"

    old "Are you sure [protag]?"
    new "Are you sure [protag]?\n你确定吗，[protag]？"

    old "I'm not looking forward to stay here any longer, but...[protag] are you sure it's a good idea?"
    new "I'm not looking forward to stay here any longer, but...[protag] are you sure it's a good idea?\n我并不想在这里多待，但是……[protag]，你确定这是个好主意吗？"

    old "This place is still full of dark energy, even if... not as strong as before. Perhaps you'll be safe even without our help."
    new "This place is still full of dark energy, even if... not as strong as before. Perhaps you'll be safe even without our help.\n这地方仍充满黑暗能量，即使……没有之前那么强了。也许就算没有我们的帮助，你们也会安全。"

    old "What? Just when I was starting to have fun!"
    new "What? Just when I was starting to have fun!\n什么？我正开始觉得好玩呢！"

    old "Well, if nothing else, if you need help we can run inside the tomb and reach you in a few minutes."
    new "Well, if nothing else, if you need help we can run inside the tomb and reach you in a few minutes.\n好吧，别的先不说，如果你需要帮忙，我们可以冲进墓里，几分钟就能赶到你身边。"

    old "I'm not going anywhere!"
    new "I'm not going anywhere!\n我哪儿也不去！"

    old "Galan..."
    new "Galan...\nGalan……"

    old "Don't worry, we'll be fine. Then it's decided: Larik, Nuala and I will move forward, you go outside and rest."
    new "Don't worry, we'll be fine. Then it's decided: Larik, Nuala and I will move forward, you go outside and rest.\n别担心，我们会没事的。那就这么定了：Larik、Nuala 和我继续前进，你们到外面去休息。"

    old "We continue forward until Larik runs against another wall with symbols on it."
    new "We continue forward until Larik runs against another wall with symbols on it.\n我们继续前进，直到 Larik 撞上另一面刻着符号的墙。"

    old "Another trick door?"
    new "Another trick door?\n又一道机关门？"

    old "This says, 'first door, second door, unity.' The first door and the second are the same, it seems."
    new "This says, 'first door, second door, unity.' The first door and the second are the same, it seems.\n这上面写的是“第一道门，第二道门，合一”。看来第一道门和第二道门是一样的。"

    old "Sounds like it's time for another dose of radiance."
    new "Sounds like it's time for another dose of radiance.\n听起来又该来一剂闪光了。"

    old "Wait a minute. There's another bit here. It begins with the symbol, 'beware,' or 'warning,' the same one that we saw in the main chamber."
    new "Wait a minute. There's another bit here. It begins with the symbol, 'beware,' or 'warning,' the same one that we saw in the main chamber.\n等一下。这里还有一点。它以一个符号开头——“当心”，或者“警告”，就是我们在主室看到过的那个。"

    old "What exactly do we need to be wary of?"
    new "What exactly do we need to be wary of?\n我们到底要提防什么？"

    old "The symbols are arranged in two patterns. Two paths. One with the symbol of light, and the other with the symbol of darkness."
    new "The symbols are arranged in two patterns. Two paths. One with the symbol of light, and the other with the symbol of darkness.\n这些符号排成两种图样。两条路。一条带光明符号，另一条带黑暗符号。"

    old "What does the part under the pattern for the light path say?"
    new "What does the part under the pattern for the light path say?\n光明之路那图样下面的部分写了什么？"

    old "Perhaps it's wrong to describe them as 'light path' and 'dark path.' This one actually says, 'light heart' or 'light spirit.' It seems to imply some kind of spiritual meaning, rather than a physical one."
    new "Perhaps it's wrong to describe them as 'light path' and 'dark path.' This one actually says, 'light heart' or 'light spirit.' It seems to imply some kind of spiritual meaning, rather than a physical one.\n也许把它们说成“光明之路”和“黑暗之路”并不准确。这一个实际写的是“光明之心”，或者说“光明之灵”。它似乎暗示某种精神层面的含义，而非物质层面的。"

    old "So it's not actually talking about a well-lit path and a path hidden from the light."
    new "So it's not actually talking about a well-lit path and a path hidden from the light.\n所以它说的并不是一条光照良好的路和一条避光而藏的路。"

    old "No. It seems more like, 'this is the path of a person with a heart of darkness,' and 'this is the path of a person with a heart of light.'"
    new "No. It seems more like, 'this is the path of a person with a heart of darkness,' and 'this is the path of a person with a heart of light.'\n不。它更像是说，“这是怀有黑暗之心的人之路”，以及“这是怀有光明之心的人之路”。"

    old "Which of those do you think describes you, [protag]?"
    new "Which of those do you think describes you, [protag]?\n你觉得哪一种说的是你，[protag]？"

    old "The light heart, I would hope."
    new "The light heart, I would hope.\n我希望是光明之心。"

    old "Larik, you said that each of the headings had a set of symbols under it. Can you read that part?"
    new "Larik, you said that each of the headings had a set of symbols under it. Can you read that part?\nLarik，你说每个标题下面都有一组符号。你能读读那部分吗？"

    old "Yes, of course. I presume you'll want to hear both of these. Which should I start with?"
    new "Yes, of course. I presume you'll want to hear both of these. Which should I start with?\n是的，当然。我想这两部分你都会想听。我先从哪一个开始？"

    old "Tell me what it says about the path of those with a heart of light."
    new "Tell me what it says about the path of those with a heart of light.\n告诉我关于怀有光明之心者之路的那部分写了什么。"

    old "It says, 'beginning, companion, outcome, triumph.'"
    new "It says, 'beginning, companion, outcome, triumph.'\n上面写着：“起始，同伴，结果，凯旋”。"

    old "Beginning with companions results in triumph?"
    new "Beginning with companions results in triumph?\n以同伴起始，结果便是凯旋？"

    old "That seems like a reasonable interpretation."
    new "That seems like a reasonable interpretation.\n这似乎是个合理的解读。"

    old "What about the other part? The part about the path of the heart of darkness."
    new "What about the other part? The part about the path of the heart of darkness.\n那另一部分呢？关于黑暗之心之路的那部分。"

    old "It's similar to the other one. 'Beginning, strength, outcome, triumph.'"
    new "It's similar to the other one. 'Beginning, strength, outcome, triumph.'\n和另一个类似。“起始，力量，结果，凯旋”。"

    old "So, those who enter with a heart of darkness will triumph through strength?"
    new "So, those who enter with a heart of darkness will triumph through strength?\n所以，怀有黑暗之心进入的人，会凭力量获胜？"

    old "That also sounds like a correct interpretation."
    new "That also sounds like a correct interpretation.\n这听起来也是个正确的解读。"

    old "Tell me what it says about the path of those with a heart of darkness."
    new "Tell me what it says about the path of those with a heart of darkness.\n告诉我关于怀有黑暗之心者之路的那部分写了什么。"

    old "It says, 'beginning, strength, outcome, triumph.'"
    new "It says, 'beginning, strength, outcome, triumph.'\n上面写着：“起始，力量，结果，凯旋”。"

    old "Beginning with strength results in triumph?"
    new "Beginning with strength results in triumph?\n以力量起始，结果便是凯旋？"

    old "That sounds like a reasonable interpretation."
    new "That sounds like a reasonable interpretation.\n这听起来是个合理的解读。"

    old "What about the other part, about the heart of light?"
    new "What about the other part, about the heart of light?\n那另一部分呢，关于光明之心的？"

    old "Same structure as the other one. 'Beginning companions, outcome, triumph.'"
    new "Same structure as the other one. 'Beginning companions, outcome, triumph.'\n和另一个结构一样。“起始，同伴，结果，凯旋”。"

    old "So, those who enter with a heart of light will triumph with companions?"
    new "So, those who enter with a heart of light will triumph with companions?\n所以，怀有光明之心进入的人，会与同伴一同获胜？"

    old "I guess so."
    new "I guess so.\n我想是吧。"

    old "I just noticed something. Hold on for a moment."
    new "I just noticed something. Hold on for a moment.\n我刚注意到一件事。稍等一下。"

    old "Larik reaches down and rubs the surface with his hand."
    new "Larik reaches down and rubs the surface with his hand.\nLarik 俯下身，用手擦了擦那表面。"

    old "There's another set of symbols here, under each of the headings. One symbol for each side. Under the 'heart of darkness' side, it says 'boon.' Under the 'heart of light' side, it says 'survival.'"
    new "There's another set of symbols here, under each of the headings. One symbol for each side. Under the 'heart of darkness' side, it says 'boon.' Under the 'heart of light' side, it says 'survival.'\n每个标题下面还有另一组符号。每一边各有一个符号。在“黑暗之心”那一边，写的是“恩赐”。在“光明之心”那一边，写的是“生还”。"

    old "I wonder what might be meant by 'person with a heart of darkness.'"
    new "I wonder what might be meant by 'person with a heart of darkness.'\n我在想，“怀有黑暗之心的人”会是什么意思。"

    old "The vampires I encountered earlier. Zachary and Valery were their names. Could the passage be referring to...vampires? Or the undead?"
    new "The vampires I encountered earlier. Zachary and Valery were their names. Could the passage be referring to...vampires? Or the undead?\n我之前遇到的那些吸血鬼。他们叫 Zachary 和 Valery。这段文字指的会不会是……吸血鬼？或者是亡灵？"

    old "It could be that what lies ahead is a test of one's purity of will."
    new "It could be that what lies ahead is a test of one's purity of will.\n也许前方所设的，是对一个人意志纯净度的考验。"

    old "That could be true..."
    new "That could be true...\n这倒有可能……"

    old "I am not so sure. I think it could be that what lies ahead are two paths, one path by which [heshe] who enters will be tested on the basis of fellowship, and one by which [heshe] who enters will be tested by strength."
    new "I am not so sure. I think it could be that what lies ahead are two paths, one path by which [heshe] who enters will be tested on the basis of fellowship, and one by which [heshe] who enters will be tested by strength.\n我不太确定。我想，前方也许是两条路，一条是让进入的[heshe]以情谊为基准接受考验，另一条则是考验[heshe]的力量。"

    old "Perhaps the tablet is asking what metric one wishes to be judged by."
    new "Perhaps the tablet is asking what metric one wishes to be judged by.\n也许这块碑文是在问，你希望自己被以什么标准评判。"

    old "The symbols said 'boon' and 'survival.' Could it be that by choosing your trial, you also choose your reward?"
    new "The symbols said 'boon' and 'survival.' Could it be that by choosing your trial, you also choose your reward?\n符号写的是“恩赐”和“生还”。会不会是，你选择了自己的考验，也就同时选择了自己的回报？"

    old "[HeShe] who chooses to be tested by fellowship will survive. But [heshe] who is tested by strength could win a great boon. Is that what you mean?"
    new "[HeShe] who chooses to be tested by fellowship will survive. But [heshe] who is tested by strength could win a great boon. Is that what you mean?\n选择接受情谊考验的[HeShe]会生还。而接受力量考验的[heshe]则可能赢得丰厚的恩赐。你是这个意思吗？"

    old "I suppose that could be true."
    new "I suppose that could be true.\n我想这也可能说得通。"

    old "It could also be that we're completely misinterpreting the symbols, trying to attach meaning to etchings that were meant for someone else, or that describe something completely different."
    new "It could also be that we're completely misinterpreting the symbols, trying to attach meaning to etchings that were meant for someone else, or that describe something completely different.\n也有可能我们完全曲解了这些符号，硬要把含义附会到那些本是写给别人、或是在描述完全不同事物的刻痕上。"

    old "There's something almost proverb-like about this. It seems to be describing philosophy more than giving any kind of concrete direction."
    new "There's something almost proverb-like about this. It seems to be describing philosophy more than giving any kind of concrete direction.\n这些文字几乎带点谚语的味道。它更像是在阐述哲理，而非给出任何具体指引。"

    old "That may be. But I would not dismiss them outright. Many trials test one's resolve and spiritual fortitude. Philosophical advice could come in quite handy."
    new "That may be. But I would not dismiss them outright. Many trials test one's resolve and spiritual fortitude. Philosophical advice could come in quite handy.\n也许吧。但我不会全然不理会它们。许多考验，考验的是一个人的决心和精神毅力。哲理性的建议说不定会非常有用。"

    old "Hypothetically, which path would you choose to walk? A trial of fellowship, or a trial of strength?"
    new "Hypothetically, which path would you choose to walk? A trial of fellowship, or a trial of strength?\n假设一下，你会选择走哪条路？情谊的考验，还是力量的考验？"

    old "Not to deny the value of companions and fellowship, but if I'm going to bet on anything, I want to bet on strength. Larik, Nuala, I trust both of you. We have a bond. But more importantly, I know that you're both strong and capable. Things like bonds and trust mean nothing if you don't have strength to back them up."
    new "Not to deny the value of companions and fellowship, but if I'm going to bet on anything, I want to bet on strength. Larik, Nuala, I trust both of you. We have a bond. But more importantly, I know that you're both strong and capable. Things like bonds and trust mean nothing if you don't have strength to back them up.\n我倒不是否定同伴与情谊的价值，但如果要让我押注，我想押在力量上。Larik，Nuala，我信任你们俩。我们之间有情谊。但更重要的是，我知道你们俩都很强、很有本事。若是没有力量作后盾，情谊和信任这类东西就毫无意义。"

    old "Well said, [protag]."
    new "Well said, [protag].\n说得好，[protag]。"

    old "I'm flattered that you think of me as someone who's 'strong.'"
    new "I'm flattered that you think of me as someone who's 'strong.'\n你把我当作“强大”的人，我受宠若惊。"

    old "Let's get in there, and not waste any more time. Nuala, do your thing."
    new "Let's get in there, and not waste any more time. Nuala, do your thing.\n我们进去吧，别再浪费时间了。Nuala，露一手吧。"

    old "Your wish is my command."
    new "Your wish is my command.\n你的愿望就是我的命令。"

    old "I close my eyes, and Nuala unleashes radiance, flooding the passage with light. I hear the sound of stone moving, and Larik begins moving forward."
    new "I close my eyes, and Nuala unleashes radiance, flooding the passage with light. I hear the sound of stone moving, and Larik begins moving forward.\n我闭上眼睛，Nuala 释放出光辉，让光芒灌满通道。我听到石头移动的声音，Larik 开始向前走去。"

    old "The passage is open. Let's go."
    new "The passage is open. Let's go.\n通道开了。我们走吧。"

    old "If we're going to be challenged and tested on the basis of fellowship, I think we're well-equipped for the challenge. Between you, me, and Nuala, I think we have a solid team. We trust each other, and bonds of trust are important in trying times."
    new "If we're going to be challenged and tested on the basis of fellowship, I think we're well-equipped for the challenge. Between you, me, and Nuala, I think we have a solid team. We trust each other, and bonds of trust are important in trying times.\n如果我们要以情谊为基准接受挑战和考验，我想我们完全足以应对。你、我，再加上 Nuala，我们是一支扎实的队伍。我们彼此信任，而在艰难时期，信任的纽带十分重要。"

    old "I feel that way too, [protag]. In a sense, Nuala and I have already pledged our loyalty to you. And that's because you've earned it by serving the interests of our people."
    new "I feel that way too, [protag]. In a sense, Nuala and I have already pledged our loyalty to you. And that's because you've earned it by serving the interests of our people.\n我也这么觉得，[protag]。从某种意义上说，Nuala 和我早已向你宣誓效忠。而那是因为你通过为我们人民的利益效劳，赢得了这份忠诚。"

    old "So, are we going to go?"
    new "So, are we going to go?\n那么，我们走吗？"

    old "Yes, let's. Nuala, I think you know what to do. Show us your radiance."
    new "Yes, let's. Nuala, I think you know what to do. Show us your radiance.\n好，走吧。Nuala，我想你知道该怎么做。给我们看看你的光辉。"

    old "I thought you'd never ask. Remember, keep your eyes shut for this."
    new "I thought you'd never ask. Remember, keep your eyes shut for this.\n我还以为你永远不会开口呢。记住，接下来把眼睛闭好。"

    old "I close my eyes, and Nuala floods the corridor with light. I hear the sound of stone moving, and Larik steps forward."
    new "I close my eyes, and Nuala floods the corridor with light. I hear the sound of stone moving, and Larik steps forward.\n我闭上眼睛，Nuala 让光芒灌满走廊。我听到石头移动的声音，Larik 迈步向前。"

    old "Let's go."
    new "Let's go.\n我们走。"

    old "If we're going to be challenged and tested on the basis of fellowship, I think we're well-equipped for the challenge. I think we have a solid team. We trust each other, and bonds of trust are important in trying times."
    new "If we're going to be challenged and tested on the basis of fellowship, I think we're well-equipped for the challenge. I think we have a solid team. We trust each other, and bonds of trust are important in trying times.\n如果我们要以情谊为基准接受挑战和考验，我想我们完全足以应对。我想我们有一支扎实的队伍。我们彼此信任，而在艰难时期，信任的纽带十分重要。"

    old "However, when it comes to tests of strength...I am not so sure."
    new "However, when it comes to tests of strength...I am not so sure.\n然而，说到力量的考验……我就不那么有把握了。"

    old "Could the Zachary and Valery know more about this? They were slinking about here. If I decide to trust in strength over bonds of fellowship, perhaps I'd do better to consult them..."
    new "Could the Zachary and Valery know more about this? They were slinking about here. If I decide to trust in strength over bonds of fellowship, perhaps I'd do better to consult them...\nZachary 和 Valery 会不会对此知道得更多？他们曾在这里鬼鬼祟祟地出没。如果我决定相信力量胜过情谊，也许我最好去请教他们……"

    old "Let's keep going. I think we're ready for the trials that wait ahead."
    new "Let's keep going. I think we're ready for the trials that wait ahead.\n我们继续吧。我想我们已经准备好迎接前方等待的考验了。"

    old "Nuala, you want to give us another dose of radiance?"
    new "Nuala, you want to give us another dose of radiance?\nNuala，再给我们来一剂光辉如何？"

    old "I was hoping you'd say that. Close your eyes."
    new "I was hoping you'd say that. Close your eyes.\n我就盼着你说这句呢。闭上眼睛。"

    old "I shut my eyes, and Nuala's radiance floods the corridor with what I can only assume is a blinding light. The stone in front of us begins moving, and I open my eyes."
    new "I shut my eyes, and Nuala's radiance floods the corridor with what I can only assume is a blinding light. The stone in front of us begins moving, and I open my eyes.\n我闭上眼，Nuala 的光辉灌满走廊，那想必是炫目至极的光芒。我们面前的石头开始移动，我睁开了眼睛。"

    old "The passage is open."
    new "The passage is open.\n通道打开了。"

    old "Larik, Nuala, I'm sorry to cut our journey short, but I feel that we need more information before going further."
    new "Larik, Nuala, I'm sorry to cut our journey short, but I feel that we need more information before going further.\nLarik，Nuala，抱歉要中断我们的行程了，但我觉得在继续深入之前，我们需要更多信息。"

    old "You'd like to do research?"
    new "You'd like to do research?\n你想去做些调查？"

    old "In a manner of speaking, yes. I know others who might understand the nature of this tomb better than any of us. I'd like the chance to talk to them before we go any further."
    new "In a manner of speaking, yes. I know others who might understand the nature of this tomb better than any of us. I'd like the chance to talk to them before we go any further.\n可以这么说，是的。我认识一些人，他们或许比我们任何人都更了解这座墓的本质。我想在继续深入之前，先有机会和他们谈谈。"

    old "Very well. If you think that others may know something we do not, then it seems wise to consult them."
    new "Very well. If you think that others may know something we do not, then it seems wise to consult them.\n很好。如果你认为别人可能知道我们所不知道的事，那么去请教他们似乎是个明智之举。"

    old "Nuala begins backing out of the tomb, and Larik and I follow her out."
    new "Nuala begins backing out of the tomb, and Larik and I follow her out.\nNuala 开始退出墓室，Larik 和我跟着她一起出来。"

    old "I hope to come back to this tomb soon."
    new "I hope to come back to this tomb soon.\n我希望很快能再回到这座墓。"

    old "I hope so too, [protag]. Then next time you come back to the desert, let's see what's really lurking behind that door."
    new "I hope so too, [protag]. Then next time you come back to the desert, let's see what's really lurking behind that door.\n我也希望如此，[protag]。那么下次你回到沙漠时，让我们看看那扇门后到底潜伏着什么。"

    old "Next time we'll go the three of us alone. The way now is clear."
    new "Next time we'll go the three of us alone. The way now is clear.\n下次就我们三个单独去。现在路已经通了。"

    old "I return to the desert. Nuala and Larik are waiting for me when I arrive."
    new "I return to the desert. Nuala and Larik are waiting for me when I arrive.\n我回到沙漠。到达时，Nuala 和 Larik 正在等我。"

    old "Are you ready to return to the tomb?"
    new "Are you ready to return to the tomb?\n你准备好回到那座墓了吗？"

    old "Of course. That is, assuming you two are ready."
    new "Of course. That is, assuming you two are ready.\n当然。也就是说，假设你们俩都准备好了。"

    old "I've been waiting for this. Let's do it."
    new "I've been waiting for this. Let's do it.\n我一直盼着这一天。我们出发吧。"

    old "Any reports of strange creatures in front of the tomb?"
    new "Any reports of strange creatures in front of the tomb?\n墓前有出现什么奇怪生物的报告吗？"

    old "No, everything looks clear now."
    new "No, everything looks clear now.\n没有，现在一切看起来都清静了。"

    old "Good. Let's go."
    new "Good. Let's go.\n好。我们走。"

    old "I walk to Urd's tomb with Nuala and Larik, and we make our way back to the passage we stopped at last time."
    new "I walk to Urd's tomb with Nuala and Larik, and we make our way back to the passage we stopped at last time.\n我与 Nuala 和 Larik 一同走向 Urd 之墓，然后回到上次停下的那条通道。"

    old "Now, if I recall, this door called for a certain thing to be opened...Nuala, why don't you show us how it's done?"
    new "Now, if I recall, this door called for a certain thing to be opened...Nuala, why don't you show us how it's done?\n现在，如果我没记错的话，这扇门需要某样东西才能打开……Nuala，你何不给我们演示一下该怎么做？"

    old "I thought you'd never ask. Remember, eyes closed, unless you want to find yourself temporarily blind."
    new "I thought you'd never ask. Remember, eyes closed, unless you want to find yourself temporarily blind.\n我还以为你永远不会开口呢。记住，闭上眼睛，除非你想让自己暂时失明。"

    old "I shut my eyes, and Nuala's radiance floods the corridor. I hear the sound of moving footsteps as Larik continues forward."
    new "I shut my eyes, and Nuala's radiance floods the corridor. I hear the sound of moving footsteps as Larik continues forward.\n我闭上眼，Nuala 的光辉灌满走廊。我听到 Larik 继续向前时移动的脚步声。"

    old "I follow Larik into a large chamber. Unlit torches line the walls."
    new "I follow Larik into a large chamber. Unlit torches line the walls.\n我跟着 Larik 走进一间大厅。未点燃的火把沿墙排列。"

    old "Nuala steps into the chamber after me and breathes a sigh of relief."
    new "Nuala steps into the chamber after me and breathes a sigh of relief.\nNuala 跟着我走进大厅，如释重负地舒了口气。"

    old "Were you getting claustrophobic?"
    new "Were you getting claustrophobic?\n你刚才是犯幽闭恐惧了吗？"

    old "Afraid of tight spaces? No, never. But that doesn't mean I'm fond of them."
    new "Afraid of tight spaces? No, never. But that doesn't mean I'm fond of them.\n害怕狭窄的空间？不，从来不怕。但那并不代表我喜欢它们。"

    old "Nuala takes a moment to stretch as I survey the room."
    new "Nuala takes a moment to stretch as I survey the room.\n在我打量房间时，Nuala 趁机伸了个懒腰。"

    old "Do you think it's safe to light those torches?"
    new "Do you think it's safe to light those torches?\n你觉得点燃那些火把安全吗？"

    old "If you're worried about starting a fire in here, I don't see what the danger is. We're surrounded by stone and sand. At worst, the torches just burn out."
    new "If you're worried about starting a fire in here, I don't see what the danger is. We're surrounded by stone and sand. At worst, the torches just burn out.\n如果你担心在这里引起火灾，我看不出有什么危险。我们四周都是石头和沙子。最糟的情况，也不过是火把烧尽而已。"

    old "Nuala, can you light those torches for us?"
    new "Nuala, can you light those torches for us?\nNuala，能帮我们点燃那些火把吗？"

    old "Nuala takes her staff and taps each of the torches, giving them just enough of a spark to set them burning."
    new "Nuala takes her staff and taps each of the torches, giving them just enough of a spark to set them burning.\nNuala 拿起她的法杖，逐一点了点火把，只给它们一点火星，便让它们燃烧起来。"

    old "Once the torches are lit, I turn my attention to the center of the room. The floor is composed of stone tiles, and three tiles near the center of the room have symbols carved in them."
    new "Once the torches are lit, I turn my attention to the center of the room. The floor is composed of stone tiles, and three tiles near the center of the room have symbols carved in them.\n火把一点亮，我便把注意力转向房间中央。地面由石砖铺成，靠近房间中央的三块石砖上刻着符号。"

    old "Larik, are you ready for some reading?"
    new "Larik, are you ready for some reading?\nLarik，准备好读点什么了吗？"

    old "Each of these tiles starts with the same symbol. 'Underneath.'"
    new "Each of these tiles starts with the same symbol. 'Underneath.'\n这些石砖每一块都以同一个符号开头。“下方”。"

    old "What else to they say?"
    new "What else to they say?\n它们还写了什么？"

    old "The first one says, 'dark chaser.' The last one says 'light bringer.'"
    new "The first one says, 'dark chaser.' The last one says 'light bringer.'\n第一块写的是“黑暗追逐者”。最后一块写的是“光明使者”。"

    old "What about the middle one?"
    new "What about the middle one?\n那中间那块呢？"

    old "I...I'm not sure. I don't recognize this symbol."
    new "I...I'm not sure. I don't recognize this symbol.\n我……我不确定。我不认得这个符号。"

    old "I examine the symbol on the middle slate. It appears to be shaped like a skull."
    new "I examine the symbol on the middle slate. It appears to be shaped like a skull.\n我仔细端详中间那块石板上的符号。它看起来像是个骷髅头。"

    old "You're sure that skull doesn't mean death?"
    new "You're sure that skull doesn't mean death?\n你确定那个骷髅头不是死亡的意思？"

    old "That would be a reasonable interpretation. However, it seems odd. All of the other symbols have been, well, symbolic. They're images that have meaning attached. This is the only image that appears to be so...literal."
    new "That would be a reasonable interpretation. However, it seems odd. All of the other symbols have been, well, symbolic. They're images that have meaning attached. This is the only image that appears to be so...literal.\n那会是个合理的解读。不过，这似乎有点怪。其他所有符号都是，嗯，象征性的。它们是带有寓意的图像。只有这个图像看起来如此……直白。"

    old "This appears to be as deep as the tomb goes, unless there's another hidden door here. And I don't see any writing on the walls to indicate that."
    new "This appears to be as deep as the tomb goes, unless there's another hidden door here. And I don't see any writing on the walls to indicate that.\n这里似乎已经是这座墓的最深处了，除非此处还有另一道暗门。而我在墙上也看不到任何能表明这一点的文字。"

    old "Larik, you said all of the floor tiles have a symbol in common. What did it say?"
    new "Larik, you said all of the floor tiles have a symbol in common. What did it say?\nLarik，你说这些地砖都有一个共同的符号。那写的是什么？"

    old "'Underneath.' Or 'beneath.' Seems like we're already underground."
    new "'Underneath.' Or 'beneath.' Seems like we're already underground.\n“下方”。或者“地底”。看来我们已经在地下了。"

    old "I kneel down and examine the etched floor tiles, the one Larik described as 'light bringer.' I pick up a rock and pound it into the floor, and the tile cracks a bit."
    new "I kneel down and examine the etched floor tiles, the one Larik described as 'light bringer.' I pick up a rock and pound it into the floor, and the tile cracks a bit.\n我跪下来，仔细查看那些刻字的地砖，尤其是 Larik 形容为“光明使者”的那一块。我捡起一块石头砸向地面，石砖裂开了一点。"

    old "[protag], what are you doing?"
    new "[protag], what are you doing?\n[protag]，你在干什么？"

    old "Just testing a hunch. Any objections?"
    new "Just testing a hunch. Any objections?\n只是在验证一个猜想。有人反对吗？"

    old "I don't think we need to worry about defiling the tomb. I think we're well past that point."
    new "I don't think we need to worry about defiling the tomb. I think we're well past that point.\n我想我们不必担心亵渎这座墓了。我想我们早就过了那个阶段。"

    old "I continue pounding the tile until it breaks in two, collapsing and revealing a small cavity in the floor under it. I pick out the broken bits of tile. A glint of metal flashes through the sandy debris."
    new "I continue pounding the tile until it breaks in two, collapsing and revealing a small cavity in the floor under it. I pick out the broken bits of tile. A glint of metal flashes through the sandy debris.\n我继续砸那石砖，直到它裂成两半，塌陷下去，露出下方地面里的一个小凹洞。我捡出碎砖块。沙土碎屑间闪过一道金属的光芒。"

    old "Need a hand?"
    new "Need a hand?\n需要帮忙吗？"

    old "Please."
    new "Please.\n麻烦你了。"

    old "Nuala kneels next to me, and we both dig at the dust and broken tile until a metal rod is exposed. Nuala lifts the rod out of the floor cavity."
    new "Nuala kneels next to me, and we both dig at the dust and broken tile until a metal rod is exposed. Nuala lifts the rod out of the floor cavity.\nNuala 在我身旁跪下，我们俩一起扒开尘土和碎砖，直到一根金属杖露了出来。Nuala 把那根杖从地洞中取出。"

    old "It appears to be silver. And I'll be damned if that doesn't have the appearance of a wizard's rod."
    new "It appears to be silver. And I'll be damned if that doesn't have the appearance of a wizard's rod.\n它看起来是银制的。而且我敢说，它怎么看都像是一根巫师的法杖。"

    old "This rod...I can feel it pulsing in my hand. There's something rhythmic about it. Almost like it's trying to attune itself to my biorhythm. I feel...I feel like I could enact my will through this rod."
    new "This rod...I can feel it pulsing in my hand. There's something rhythmic about it. Almost like it's trying to attune itself to my biorhythm. I feel...I feel like I could enact my will through this rod.\n这根杖……我能感觉到它在手中搏动。它带着某种节奏，几乎像是想与我的生命节律调谐。我觉得……我觉得自己可以通过这根杖施展意志。"

    old "Sounds magical to me."
    new "Sounds magical to me.\n我听着挺神奇的。"

    old "If that tile was covering a magical rod, then..."
    new "If that tile was covering a magical rod, then...\n如果那块石砖下盖着一根魔法杖，那么……"

    old "We all look toward the first floor tile, the one marked 'dark chaser.'"
    new "We all look toward the first floor tile, the one marked 'dark chaser.'\n我们全都看向第一块地砖——那块标着“黑暗追逐者”的。"

    old "[protag], may I?"
    new "[protag], may I?\n[protag]，我来？"

    old "Larik takes his axe and drives it, blunt end first, into the center of the floor tile. The slate shatters under the blow, and he reaches down and claws at the broken slate debris and dust until he exposes a handle."
    new "Larik takes his axe and drives it, blunt end first, into the center of the floor tile. The slate shatters under the blow, and he reaches down and claws at the broken slate debris and dust until he exposes a handle.\nLarik 拿起他的战斧，以钝头朝下，猛砸进那块地砖中央。石板在重击下碎裂，他俯下身，扒开碎石板和尘土，直到露出一只握柄。"

    old "Could this be..."
    new "Could this be...\n这该不会是……"

    old "Larik grabs the handle and lifts, tearing a silver weapon from the sand."
    new "Larik grabs the handle and lifts, tearing a silver weapon from the sand.\nLarik 抓住握柄向上提，从沙土里拔出一件银色武器。"

    old "A silver axe."
    new "A silver axe.\n一把银斧。"

    old "Baneslayer. This must be Urd's legendary axe."
    new "Baneslayer. This must be Urd's legendary axe.\nBaneslayer。这一定是 Urd 的传奇战斧。"

    old "And I must be holding his rod, Benediction."
    new "And I must be holding his rod, Benediction.\n而我手里握着的，一定是他的法杖，Benediction。"

    old "We all turn our attention to the middle floor tile, the one with a skull-like symbol."
    new "We all turn our attention to the middle floor tile, the one with a skull-like symbol.\n我们全都把注意力转向中间那块地砖——带着骷髅状符号的那一块。"

    old "So...what lies here?"
    new "So...what lies here?\n那么……这里藏着什么？"

    old "We've destroyed two of the tiles and been rewarded for it. We may as well see what's under the third one."
    new "We've destroyed two of the tiles and been rewarded for it. We may as well see what's under the third one.\n我们已经砸开两块石砖，还都得到了回报。不如再看看第三块下面有什么。"

    old "Very well. Let's hope your sense of optimism isn't punished."
    new "Very well. Let's hope your sense of optimism isn't punished.\n很好。但愿你的乐观不会被惩罚。"

    old "Even if there is something dangerous under that tile, isn't it better to know what it is, rather than remain ignorant?"
    new "Even if there is something dangerous under that tile, isn't it better to know what it is, rather than remain ignorant?\n就算那块石砖下面有什么危险的东西，弄明白它是什么，总比一无所知要强，不是吗？"

    old "Perhaps you are right. [protag], would you like me to do the honors?"
    new "Perhaps you are right. [protag], would you like me to do the honors?\n也许你说得对。[protag]，你愿意让我来动手吗？"

    old "Do it, Larik."
    new "Do it, Larik.\n动手吧，Larik。"

    old "Larik brings his axe down in the center of the tile, cleaving it in two, and I reach down to pull out the slate, revealing the cavity underneath."
    new "Larik brings his axe down in the center of the tile, cleaving it in two, and I reach down to pull out the slate, revealing the cavity underneath.\nLarik 一斧砍在石砖中央，把它劈成两半，我伸手抽出石板，露出下面的凹洞。"

    old "Look. It's the handle of another silver weapon."
    new "Look. It's the handle of another silver weapon.\n看。是另一件银色武器的握柄。"

    old "Looks like a blade of some kind. Or the hilt of one."
    new "Looks like a blade of some kind. Or the hilt of one.\n看起来像是某种刀刃。或者是剑柄。"

    old "I reach down and grasp the sword hilt, but feel a wave of energy pulse out of the ground. I feel a sharp punch to my gut, and I fly back, thrown across the room until I hit the wall."
    new "I reach down and grasp the sword hilt, but feel a wave of energy pulse out of the ground. I feel a sharp punch to my gut, and I fly back, thrown across the room until I hit the wall.\n我伸手握住剑柄，却感到一股能量波从地里喷涌而出。我只觉腹部被狠狠一击，整个人倒飞出去，被抛过房间，直到撞上墙壁。"

    old "Are you alright?"
    new "Are you alright?\n你没事吧？"

    old "I get up and dust myself off."
    new "I get up and dust myself off.\n我爬起来，拍了拍身上的灰。"

    old "Apart from some bruising, I think I'm fine. But that blade..."
    new "Apart from some bruising, I think I'm fine. But that blade...\n除了一些淤青，我想我没事。但那把剑……"

    old "It seemed to have a life of its own. When I touched it, I felt it pushing back, as though it were violently rejecting me. Something about that weapon feels...sinister."
    new "It seemed to have a life of its own. When I touched it, I felt it pushing back, as though it were violently rejecting me. Something about that weapon feels...sinister.\n它似乎有自己的生命。当我碰到它时，我感觉到它在抗拒，仿佛在猛烈地拒绝我。那件武器有种……邪恶的感觉。"

    old "Nuala kneels down next to the hole in the ground and reaches down."
    new "Nuala kneels down next to the hole in the ground and reaches down.\nNuala 在洞口旁跪下，伸手下去。"

    old "Careful. You don't want to wind up thrown against the wall."
    new "Careful. You don't want to wind up thrown against the wall.\n小心。你可不想被甩到墙上。"

    old "Incredible. Even without touching it, I can feel some kind of malevolent energy pulsing from it. This sword...it's nothing like Baneslayer or Benediction."
    new "Incredible. Even without touching it, I can feel some kind of malevolent energy pulsing from it. This sword...it's nothing like Baneslayer or Benediction.\n难以置信。即使不去碰它，我也能感觉到它散发出的某种恶意能量。这把剑……它和 Baneslayer、Benediction 完全不一样。"

    old "[protag], I think you need to see this. Look...look at what else is inside this hole in the ground."
    new "[protag], I think you need to see this. Look...look at what else is inside this hole in the ground.\n[protag]，我想你得看看这个。看……看看这地洞里还有什么。"

    old "I crawl over to the hole and peer in."
    new "I crawl over to the hole and peer in.\n我爬过去，往洞里张望。"

    old "Is that...a skeleton?"
    new "Is that...a skeleton?\n那是……一具骷髅？"

    old "I think the other holes contain partial skeletons as well, though I think we crushed them to dust when we broke through the floor. They must be centuries old."
    new "I think the other holes contain partial skeletons as well, though I think we crushed them to dust when we broke through the floor. They must be centuries old.\n我想其他洞里也藏着残缺的骷髅，尽管我们砸穿地面时，恐怕已把它们碾成了灰。它们一定有几百年历史了。"

    old "Just what kind of place is this?"
    new "Just what kind of place is this?\n这到底是个什么地方？"

    old "It's a tomb. A tomb is where they bury the dead, right?"
    new "It's a tomb. A tomb is where they bury the dead, right?\n这是一座墓。墓不就是埋葬死者的地方吗？"

    old "Then...could one of these skeletons belong to Urd? But what about the others?"
    new "Then...could one of these skeletons belong to Urd? But what about the others?\n那么……这些骷髅里会不会有一具属于 Urd？可其他的呢？"

    old "I might be paranoid, but something about that tile seems very...foreboding. Perhaps we should leave it alone."
    new "I might be paranoid, but something about that tile seems very...foreboding. Perhaps we should leave it alone.\n也许是我多疑，但那块石砖有种……不祥的感觉。也许我们该别去碰它。"

    old "I share your sense of caution, [protag]. There's nothing else in the tomb remotely like this. Something about it strikes me as...otherworldly."
    new "I share your sense of caution, [protag]. There's nothing else in the tomb remotely like this. Something about it strikes me as...otherworldly.\n我和你一样心存谨慎，[protag]。整座墓里没有别的东西和它有一丁点相像。它有种……非人间之物的感觉。"

    old "Some mysteries are best left unsolved, I suppose."
    new "Some mysteries are best left unsolved, I suppose.\n我想，有些谜团最好还是留着不解开。"

    old "While we're on the subject of unsolved mysteries...[protag], does something about these floor cavities strike you as strange?"
    new "While we're on the subject of unsolved mysteries...[protag], does something about these floor cavities strike you as strange?\n说到未解之谜……[protag]，这些地洞有没有什么地方让你觉得奇怪？"

    old "They're deceptively large. Very long, large enough to contain the entire length of this axe handle, or the entire length of that rod. Almost as tall as...as a man."
    new "They're deceptively large. Very long, large enough to contain the entire length of this axe handle, or the entire length of that rod. Almost as tall as...as a man.\n它们大得出乎意料。非常长，长得足以容纳这整个斧柄的长度，或那整根法杖的长度。差不多有……一个人那么高。"

    old "Look at this dust. At first, I thought it was sand, but it has an almost splintery texture to it. Almost like..."
    new "Look at this dust. At first, I thought it was sand, but it has an almost splintery texture to it. Almost like...\n看看这灰。一开始我以为它是沙，但它几乎有种碎屑般的质感。几乎像是……"

    old "Like bone."
    new "Like bone.\n像骨头。"

    old "I look down at the holes in the ground, and lean down next to one of them. In the dim torchlight, I can see what looks like bone fragments."
    new "I look down at the holes in the ground, and lean down next to one of them. In the dim torchlight, I can see what looks like bone fragments.\n我低头看向地上的洞，俯身凑近其中一个。在昏暗的火把光下，我能看到像是碎骨的东西。"

    old "This looks like part of a skeleton."
    new "This looks like part of a skeleton.\n这看起来像是一具骷髅的一部分。"

    old "And the dust must be what remains of the rest of it."
    new "And the dust must be what remains of the rest of it.\n而这些灰，想必就是其余部分所剩下的东西。"

    old "We came here searching for the legendary weapons, right? And it seems we've found them. Can we leave now?"
    new "We came here searching for the legendary weapons, right? And it seems we've found them. Can we leave now?\n我们来这里是为了寻找传奇武器，对吧？看来我们已经找到了。现在可以走了吗？"

    old "Suddenly, the room begins to shake, and I feel the floor giving out from under me."
    new "Suddenly, the room begins to shake, and I feel the floor giving out from under me.\n突然，房间开始震动，我感觉脚下的地面塌了下去。"

    old "I feel myself sinking, and I grab at a rock outcropping as I fall, but it snaps in my hand and I sink into the ground."
    new "I feel myself sinking, and I grab at a rock outcropping as I fall, but it snaps in my hand and I sink into the ground.\n我感觉到自己在往下陷，坠落时伸手去抓一块突出的岩石，可它在我手中折断，我便陷进了地里。"

    old "I land on my back, and several small rocks fall around me. I feel one of them strike my shoulder, and all I can think of is how grateful I am that it didn't hit my head."
    new "I land on my back, and several small rocks fall around me. I feel one of them strike my shoulder, and all I can think of is how grateful I am that it didn't hit my head.\n我仰面落地，几块小石头落在我周围。我感觉到其中一块砸中我的肩膀，而我满脑子只想着庆幸它没砸到我的头。"

    old "I sit up and try to get my bearings. I hear Nuala and Larik's voices above me."
    new "I sit up and try to get my bearings. I hear Nuala and Larik's voices above me.\n我坐起来，努力辨明方位。我听到头顶上方传来 Nuala 和 Larik 的声音。"

    old "Are you alright? What's down there?"
    new "Are you alright? What's down there?\n你没事吧？下面有什么？"

    old "I squint my eyes, trying to see in the dim torchlight from the chamber above."
    new "I squint my eyes, trying to see in the dim torchlight from the chamber above.\n我眯起眼睛，借着上方房间透下的昏暗火光努力张望。"

    old "It looks like I'm in another room. Another hidden passageway, perhaps. How are things up there?"
    new "It looks like I'm in another room. Another hidden passageway, perhaps. How are things up there?\n我好像落进了另一个房间。也许是另一条隐秘通道。上面情况怎么样？"

    old "The floor underneath us still seems to be stable. It's a small hole. You just happened to be standing in the wrong spot when the floor gave way."
    new "The floor underneath us still seems to be stable. It's a small hole. You just happened to be standing in the wrong spot when the floor gave way.\n我们脚下的地面似乎还稳固。这只是个小洞。地板塌陷时，你只是恰好站在了错误的位置。"

    old "Larik and Nuala both lean over the hole, reaching down."
    new "Larik and Nuala both lean over the hole, reaching down.\nLarik 和 Nuala 都俯身在洞口，把手伸下来。"

    old "[protag], can you grab my hand?"
    new "[protag], can you grab my hand?\n[protag]，你能抓住我的手吗？"

    old "I try to get to my feet, but I collapse under my own weight as I try to stand."
    new "I try to get to my feet, but I collapse under my own weight as I try to stand.\n我试着站起来，却在自己的体重下倒了下去。"

    old "[protag]! Are you alright?"
    new "[protag]! Are you alright?\n[protag]！你没事吧？"

    old "I'm feeling a bit shaky on my legs."
    new "I'm feeling a bit shaky on my legs.\n我的腿有点发软。"

    old "I'm coming down to help you."
    new "I'm coming down to help you.\n我下来帮你。"

    old "Nuala, please. You should stay up here while I check on [himher]."
    new "Nuala, please. You should stay up here while I check on [himher].\nNuala，拜托。你留在上面，我去看看[himher]的情况。"

    old "Larik, stay up there. Nuala and I might need your help in getting back up."
    new "Larik, stay up there. Nuala and I might need your help in getting back up.\nLarik，留在上面。我和 Nuala 待会儿可能需要你帮忙上去。"

    old "Alright. Stay safe, Nuala."
    new "Alright. Stay safe, Nuala.\n好吧。注意安全，Nuala。"

    old "I'll be fine."
    new "I'll be fine.\n我会没事的。"

    old "Nuala leaps down the hole, and lands on her hands and knees next to me."
    new "Nuala leaps down the hole, and lands on her hands and knees next to me.\nNuala 跃下洞口，双手双膝着地，落在我身旁。"

    old "You pounce like a cat."
    new "You pounce like a cat.\n你扑下来真像只猫。"

    old "I always land on my feet. Can you stand on yours?"
    new "I always land on my feet. Can you stand on yours?\n我总能稳稳落地。你能靠自己的脚站起来吗？"

    old "Nuala reaches down, and I take her hand. She hoists me off the ground."
    new "Nuala reaches down, and I take her hand. She hoists me off the ground.\nNuala 伸出手，我握住她的手。她把我从地上拽了起来。"

    old "I stumble for a moment, and Nuala supports me while I catch my balance."
    new "I stumble for a moment, and Nuala supports me while I catch my balance.\n我踉跄了一下，Nuala 扶住我，让我稳住平衡。"

    old "Are you hurt anywhere? Twisted ankle? Injured foot?"
    new "Are you hurt anywhere? Twisted ankle? Injured foot?\n你有没有哪里受伤？扭到脚踝？伤了脚？"

    old "I'm just feeling a bit woozy, I think. The impact from that fall really knocked the wind out of me."
    new "I'm just feeling a bit woozy, I think. The impact from that fall really knocked the wind out of me.\n我想我只是有点头晕。那一摔的冲击真把我撞得喘不过气。"

    old "A cool draft rushes past us."
    new "A cool draft rushes past us.\n一股凉风从我们身边掠过。"

    old "Chilling."
    new "Chilling.\n真冷。"

    old "I felt it, too. Where could that have come from? We're underground, so it couldn't be wind..."
    new "I felt it, too. Where could that have come from? We're underground, so it couldn't be wind...\n我也感觉到了。这会是从哪来的？我们在地下，所以不可能是风……"

    old "A shriek ripples through the room, so loud that hurts my ears to hear it. Nuala and I both wince in pain and look into the darkness, toward the source of the sound."
    new "A shriek ripples through the room, so loud that hurts my ears to hear it. Nuala and I both wince in pain and look into the darkness, toward the source of the sound.\n一声尖啸荡过房间，响得刺痛我的耳朵。Nuala 和我都痛得皱起脸，望向黑暗之中、声音传来的方向。"

    old "I don't think we're alone down here."
    new "I don't think we're alone down here.\n我想这下面并非只有我们。"

    old "Not alone. Yes, finally, not alone..."
    new "Not alone. Yes, finally, not alone...\n不是独自一人。是的，终于，不是独自一人了……"

    old "I make out the shape of a figure sitting against the wall. His skin is a sickly pale shade, and he has the appearance of a corpse. A talking corpse."
    new "I make out the shape of a figure sitting against the wall. His skin is a sickly pale shade, and he has the appearance of a corpse. A talking corpse.\n我辨认出一个靠墙而坐的人影。他的皮肤是一种病态的苍白，他看上去就像一具尸体。一具会说话的尸体。"

    old "Who...what are you?"
    new "Who...what are you?\n你……你是什么？"

    old "Two questions. I'll begin by answering the first one. My name is King Nimaeus. Perhaps you've heard of me."
    new "Two questions. I'll begin by answering the first one. My name is King Nimaeus. Perhaps you've heard of me.\n两个问题。我先回答第一个。我叫 King Nimaeus。也许你听说过我。"

    old "Well, I've never heard of you."
    new "Well, I've never heard of you.\n嗯，我从来没听说过你。"

    old "Neither have I."
    new "Neither have I.\n我也没有。"

    old "Well, you'll be familiar with my name soon enough. Tell me...who sent you? Are you disciples of Urd? Has she become too cowardly to do the job himself?"
    new "Well, you'll be familiar with my name soon enough. Tell me...who sent you? Are you disciples of Urd? Has she become too cowardly to do the job himself?\n嗯，你们很快就会熟悉我的名字了。告诉我……是谁派你们来的？你们是 Urd 的门徒吗？难道她胆怯到不敢亲自来做这件事了？"

    old "Urd died hundreds of years ago."
    new "Urd died hundreds of years ago.\nUrd 几百年前就死了。"

    old "Nimaeus lets out a raspy laugh."
    new "Nimaeus lets out a raspy laugh.\nNimaeus 发出一声嘶哑的笑。"

    old "Has it been that long? Damn that woman. I suppose I had the last word after all."
    new "Has it been that long? Damn that woman. I suppose I had the last word after all.\n已经过去那么久了吗？该死的那个女人。看来最终还是我笑到了最后。"

    old "Woman?"
    new "Woman?\n女人？"

    old "Yes. Urd is the one who left me to rot here."
    new "Yes. Urd is the one who left me to rot here.\n没错。Urd 就是那个把我留在这里腐烂的人。"

    old "Urd was a woman?"
    new "Urd was a woman?\nUrd 是个女人？"

    old "Do you people know nothing? Of course Urd was a woman. But I suppose you've had several hundred years to forget. Few stories can endure for six or more generations."
    new "Do you people know nothing? Of course Urd was a woman. But I suppose you've had several hundred years to forget. Few stories can endure for six or more generations.\n你们这些人什么都不知道吗？Urd 当然是个女人。不过我想，你们有几百年的时间去遗忘。很少有故事能流传六代甚至更久。"

    old "Nimaeus raises his hands."
    new "Nimaeus raises his hands.\nNimaeus 举起双手。"

    old "This body is weak with age, but it will do. And you've so generously come along to serve as new minions. Together, we might just conquer the world."
    new "This body is weak with age, but it will do. And you've so generously come along to serve as new minions. Together, we might just conquer the world.\n这具身体因年迈而虚弱，但也够用了。而你们还如此慷慨地送上门来，充当新的爪牙。我们联手，说不定就能征服世界。"

    old "I doubt that."
    new "I doubt that.\n我对此表示怀疑。"

    old "Ah, I can see why you might think it unlikely, but allow me to explain. As I said, I'm King Nimaeus. Though, apparently my name has been forgotten, so I'll have to reclaim the title somehow. Urd and her companions left me trapped in my old body to rot. It's probably all faded to dust by now. Perhaps you've seen it."
    new "Ah, I can see why you might think it unlikely, but allow me to explain. As I said, I'm King Nimaeus. Though, apparently my name has been forgotten, so I'll have to reclaim the title somehow. Urd and her companions left me trapped in my old body to rot. It's probably all faded to dust by now. Perhaps you've seen it.\n啊，我能理解你为什么觉得这不太可能，但请容我解释。正如我所说，我是 King Nimaeus。只不过，我的名字显然已被遗忘，所以我得想办法夺回这个头衔。Urd 和她的同伴们把我困在旧躯壳里任其腐烂。如今它大概早已化为尘土。也许你们已经见过它了。"

    old "The skeletons..."
    new "The skeletons...\n那些骷髅……"

    old "Yes, Urd did have a cruel sense of humor, didn't she? For years, I stayed trapped in that rotting corpse, until it at last decayed, finally setting me free. And now I've found a fresh body. It was mostly drained of blood, but it's serving me well enough now."
    new "Yes, Urd did have a cruel sense of humor, didn't she? For years, I stayed trapped in that rotting corpse, until it at last decayed, finally setting me free. And now I've found a fresh body. It was mostly drained of blood, but it's serving me well enough now.\n没错，Urd 确实很有一种残酷的幽默感，不是吗？多年来，我一直被困在那具腐烂的尸体里，直到它终于彻底腐朽，才把我释放出来。而现在，我找到了一具新鲜的躯体。它大半的血都被抽干了，但如今用起来也还算趁手。"

    old "A fresh corpse drained of blood...could vampires be responsible?"
    new "A fresh corpse drained of blood...could vampires be responsible?\n一具被抽干血的新鲜尸体……会不会是吸血鬼干的？"

    old "You're a lich?"
    new "You're a lich?\n你是巫妖？"

    old "Yes, yes. Separating my soul from my mortal body was quite an ordeal, but such is the price of immortality."
    new "Yes, yes. Separating my soul from my mortal body was quite an ordeal, but such is the price of immortality.\n没错，没错。把我的灵魂与凡躯分离，着实是场磨难，但这就是永生的代价。"

    old "Now that I'm back, will you help me conquer the world yet again? Of course the answer is yes, but I'm curious as to whether or not you'll do it willingly. Servants who submit willingly are easier to handle, and it seems like a happier life, don't you think? And sometimes, trying to possess the weak-willed turns out to be quite fatal for them."
    new "Now that I'm back, will you help me conquer the world yet again? Of course the answer is yes, but I'm curious as to whether or not you'll do it willingly. Servants who submit willingly are easier to handle, and it seems like a happier life, don't you think? And sometimes, trying to possess the weak-willed turns out to be quite fatal for them.\n现在我回来了，你们愿不愿意再帮我征服一次世界？答案当然会是“愿意”，但我很好奇你们是否心甘情愿。自愿臣服的仆人更好使唤，日子似乎也更舒心，你们不觉得吗？而且有时候，试图占据那些意志薄弱的人，对他们来说反倒会致命。"

    old "So, will you submit to me? Or will I have to turn you into soulless drones?"
    new "So, will you submit to me? Or will I have to turn you into soulless drones?\n那么，你们是要臣服于我？还是要我不得不把你们变成没有灵魂的行尸？"

    old "Submit to you? Never!"
    new "Submit to you? Never!\n臣服于你？休想！"

    old "Very well, you seem strong-willed enough to survive my possession."
    new "Very well, you seem strong-willed enough to survive my possession.\n很好，你似乎意志坚定，足以挺过我的占据。"

    old "Nimaeus raises his hands, and a dark energy begins to build around him. Nuala charges at him, but Nimaeus unfurls the blast of energy, knocking both me and Nuala to our feet."
    new "Nimaeus raises his hands, and a dark energy begins to build around him. Nuala charges at him, but Nimaeus unfurls the blast of energy, knocking both me and Nuala to our feet.\nNimaeus 举起双手，一股黑暗能量开始在他周身凝聚。Nuala 向他冲去，但 Nimaeus 释放出那股能量冲击，把我和 Nuala 都掀翻在地。"

    old "No...how..."
    new "No...how...\n不……怎么会……"

    old "I try to stand, but find myself pinned to the ground. No, not pinned...it's as if my limbs aren't responding. Every muscle in my body is completely frozen."
    new "I try to stand, but find myself pinned to the ground. No, not pinned...it's as if my limbs aren't responding. Every muscle in my body is completely frozen.\n我试着站起来，却发现自己被按在地上动弹不得。不，不是被按住……而是我的四肢仿佛不听使唤。我全身每一块肌肉都僵住了。"

    old "Quiet, child. Just be still and let the darkness take you."
    new "Quiet, child. Just be still and let the darkness take you.\n安静，孩子。别动，让黑暗带走你吧。"

    old "Nimaeus claps his hands and begins chanting."
    new "Nimaeus claps his hands and begins chanting.\nNimaeus 一拍双手，开始念咒。"

    old "I hear the sound of footsteps behind me."
    new "I hear the sound of footsteps behind me.\n我听到身后传来脚步声。"

    old "Die, fiend!"
    new "Die, fiend!\n去死吧，恶魔！"

    old "I watch as Larik charges forward toward Nimaeus, raising the silver axe aloft."
    new "I watch as Larik charges forward toward Nimaeus, raising the silver axe aloft.\n我看着 Larik 高举银斧，朝 Nimaeus 冲了过去。"

    old "No. You—"
    new "No. You—\n不。你——"

    old "Larik yells as he swings the axe down, and the lich lets out a shriek as his body collapses to the floor, pinned in place by the blade of the axe."
    new "Larik yells as he swings the axe down, and the lich lets out a shriek as his body collapses to the floor, pinned in place by the blade of the axe.\nLarik 大喝一声，挥斧劈下，那巫妖的身体被斧刃钉在原地、瘫倒在地时，发出了一声尖啸。"

    old "Son of Urd...it can't be..."
    new "Son of Urd...it can't be...\nUrd 之子……不可能……"

    old "Nuala stands up, and I find myself in control of my own body once again. I stand up beside Larik."
    new "Nuala stands up, and I find myself in control of my own body once again. I stand up beside Larik.\nNuala 站起身来，我发现自己又能掌控身体了。我在 Larik 身旁站起来。"

    old "Kill...me..."
    new "Kill...me...\n杀……了我……"

    old "I was planning on doing exactly that."
    new "I was planning on doing exactly that.\n我正打算这么做呢。"

    old "Larik grabs the axe handle, but I stop him before he pulls it out of the lich's chest."
    new "Larik grabs the axe handle, but I stop him before he pulls it out of the lich's chest.\nLarik 抓住斧柄，但在他把斧头从巫妖胸口拔出之前，我拦住了他。"

    old "Larik, wait."
    new "Larik, wait.\nLarik，等等。"

    old "Wait for what? This fiend needs to die."
    new "Wait for what? This fiend needs to die.\n等什么？这恶魔必须死。"

    old "He's immortal. If we kill him, we'll just be freeing his soul to haunt and take control of some other corpse."
    new "He's immortal. If we kill him, we'll just be freeing his soul to haunt and take control of some other corpse.\n他是不死之身。如果我们杀了他，只会放出他的灵魂，让它去缠上并占据别的尸体。"

    old "So what do we do?"
    new "So what do we do?\n那我们该怎么办？"

    old "Look at him. He seems incapacitated. I think you put the head of the axe right through his spine."
    new "Look at him. He seems incapacitated. I think you put the head of the axe right through his spine.\n看看他。他似乎已经动弹不得了。我想你的斧刃正好贯穿了他的脊椎。"

    old "A lich should be able to recover from that kind of blow, though. Unless...could this be the power of Baneslayer?"
    new "A lich should be able to recover from that kind of blow, though. Unless...could this be the power of Baneslayer?\n不过，巫妖本该能从那种重创中恢复的。除非……这会是 Baneslayer 的力量吗？"

    old "It's the silver. He can't recover with a silver weapon separating his spine."
    new "It's the silver. He can't recover with a silver weapon separating his spine.\n是银子。有件银器把他的脊椎截断，他就无法恢复了。"

    old "If we kill him now, we free his soul. But if we leave him like this, his soul will be trapped in this corpse."
    new "If we kill him now, we free his soul. But if we leave him like this, his soul will be trapped in this corpse.\n如果我们现在杀了他，就会放出他的灵魂。但如果我们让他保持这样，他的灵魂就会被困在这具尸体里。"

    old "Eventually, the corpse will rot away."
    new "Eventually, the corpse will rot away.\n最终，这具尸体会腐烂殆尽。"

    old "Yes, eventually this body will completely decay, freeing his soul once again. But that might be a hundred years or more from now."
    new "Yes, eventually this body will completely decay, freeing his soul once again. But that might be a hundred years or more from now.\n没错，最终这具躯体会彻底腐烂，再次放出他的灵魂。但那可能是一百年甚至更久以后的事了。"

    old "Can we really leave our children to face this same curse?"
    new "Can we really leave our children to face this same curse?\n我们真的能让我们的后代去面对同样的诅咒吗？"

    old "Yes. That seems to be exactly what Urd did. Urd couldn't kill the immortal lich. So she did the next best thing: she trapped him here. I think she figured that when the time came, others would come along to do again what she once did before. And I think we've proved her right."
    new "Yes. That seems to be exactly what Urd did. Urd couldn't kill the immortal lich. So she did the next best thing: she trapped him here. I think she figured that when the time came, others would come along to do again what she once did before. And I think we've proved her right.\n没错。这似乎正是 Urd 当年的做法。Urd 杀不死这不死的巫妖。于是她退而求其次：把他困在这里。我想她料定，等时候到了，自会有后来人再来做一遍她当年做过的事。而我想，我们已经证明她想得没错。"

    old "How can we be sure that our descendants will be able to live up to the challenge?"
    new "How can we be sure that our descendants will be able to live up to the challenge?\n我们怎么能确定，我们的后代能担当起这个挑战？"

    old "How is that we know of the accomplishments of Urd? We can preserve this information through stories. Even if we sometimes get certain details wrong, like the exact nature of Urd's identity, perhaps enough of the details will endure that when the time comes, our children's children's children can put this lich to rest once again."
    new "How is that we know of the accomplishments of Urd? We can preserve this information through stories. Even if we sometimes get certain details wrong, like the exact nature of Urd's identity, perhaps enough of the details will endure that when the time comes, our children's children's children can put this lich to rest once again.\n我们又是怎么知道 Urd 的功绩的？我们可以通过故事来保存这些信息。即使我们有时会把某些细节搞错，比如 Urd 身份的确切情况，也许仍有足够多的细节能流传下去，等到时候到了，我们子孙的子孙能再一次让这巫妖安息。"

    old "I look down at Nimaeus."
    new "I look down at Nimaeus.\n我低头看着 Nimaeus。"

    old "I'm right, aren't I?"
    new "I'm right, aren't I?\n我说得没错，对吧？"

    old "Damn...you..."
    new "Damn...you...\n该死的……你……"

    old "You've claimed immortality, and I don't think that we can take that away from you. But a hundred years from now, as you spend your days trapped down here, waiting for the day when your corpse finally expires, perhaps immortality won't seem like such a blessing."
    new "You've claimed immortality, and I don't think that we can take that away from you. But a hundred years from now, as you spend your days trapped down here, waiting for the day when your corpse finally expires, perhaps immortality won't seem like such a blessing.\n你宣称自己得到了永生，而我想我们也夺不走它。但一百年后，当你日复一日被困在这下面，等着你的尸体最终消亡的那一天，也许永生就不显得是什么福分了。"

    old "In fact, when I look at you, lying helplessly on the ground, it seems like a curse that I wouldn't wish on anyone. But in a way, you wished it on yourself."
    new "In fact, when I look at you, lying helplessly on the ground, it seems like a curse that I wouldn't wish on anyone. But in a way, you wished it on yourself.\n事实上，看着你无助地躺在地上，这倒像是一个我不愿加诸任何人的诅咒。但从某种意义上说，这是你自找的。"

    old "Nuala, stay up there. Larik and I might need your help in getting back up."
    new "Nuala, stay up there. Larik and I might need your help in getting back up.\nNuala，留在上面。Larik 和我可能需要你帮忙上去。"

    old "Be careful, Larik. If anything happens down there..."
    new "Be careful, Larik. If anything happens down there...\n小心点，Larik。如果下面出了什么事……"

    old "Larik slides down the hole after me."
    new "Larik slides down the hole after me.\nLarik 跟着我滑下洞口。"

    old "Lucky for us, it looks like the ceiling is low enough for me to reach up. Now, can you stand?"
    new "Lucky for us, it looks like the ceiling is low enough for me to reach up. Now, can you stand?\n我们运气不错，看来天花板低得我伸手就能够到。现在，你能站起来吗？"

    old "Larik offers me a hand, and lifts me to my feet."
    new "Larik offers me a hand, and lifts me to my feet.\nLarik 向我伸出手，把我拉了起来。"

    old "Yeah, I think I'm fine, actually. I don't think I'm injured, just a little bit dazed."
    new "Yeah, I think I'm fine, actually. I don't think I'm injured, just a little bit dazed.\n嗯，其实我想我没事。我不觉得自己受了伤，只是有点头晕。"

    old "Did you feel that?"
    new "Did you feel that?\n你感觉到了吗？"

    old "Yes. Where could that have come from? We're underground, so it couldn't be wind..."
    new "Yes. Where could that have come from? We're underground, so it couldn't be wind...\n感觉到了。这会是从哪来的？我们在地下，所以不可能是风……"

    old "A shriek ripples through the room, so loud that hurts my ears to hear it. Larik and I both wince in pain and look into the darkness, toward the source of the sound."
    new "A shriek ripples through the room, so loud that hurts my ears to hear it. Larik and I both wince in pain and look into the darkness, toward the source of the sound.\n一声尖啸荡过房间，响得刺痛我的耳朵。Larik 和我都痛得皱起脸，望向黑暗之中、声音传来的方向。"

    old "I've never heard the name before. I turn to Larik, and he shakes his head, as if to say, 'I've never heard of him either.'"
    new "I've never heard the name before. I turn to Larik, and he shakes his head, as if to say, 'I've never heard of him either.'\n我从没听过这个名字。我转向 Larik，他摇摇头，仿佛在说：“我也从没听说过他。”"

    old "Urd...Urd has been dead for over two hundred years."
    new "Urd...Urd has been dead for over two hundred years.\nUrd……Urd 已经死了两百多年了。"

    old "What...what are you?"
    new "What...what are you?\n你……你是什么？"

    old "Ah, that was your other question, wasn't it? Well, I suppose I ought to explain myself to you. As I said, I'm King Nimaeus. Though, apparently my name has been forgotten, so I'll have to reclaim the title somehow. Urd and her companions left me trapped in my old body to rot. Perhaps you've seen it."
    new "Ah, that was your other question, wasn't it? Well, I suppose I ought to explain myself to you. As I said, I'm King Nimaeus. Though, apparently my name has been forgotten, so I'll have to reclaim the title somehow. Urd and her companions left me trapped in my old body to rot. Perhaps you've seen it.\n啊，那是你的另一个问题，对吧？好吧，我想我是该向你们解释一下。正如我所说，我是 King Nimaeus。只不过，我的名字显然已被遗忘，所以我得想办法夺回这个头衔。Urd 和她的同伴们把我困在旧躯壳里任其腐烂。也许你们已经见过它了。"

    old "You're...a lich."
    new "You're...a lich.\n你是……一个巫妖。"

    old "We'll never submit to the likes of you!"
    new "We'll never submit to the likes of you!\n我们绝不会臣服于你这种人！"

    old "Nimaeus raises his hands, and a dark energy begins to build around him. Larik charges at him, but Nimaeus unfurls the blast of energy, knocking both me and Larik to our feet."
    new "Nimaeus raises his hands, and a dark energy begins to build around him. Larik charges at him, but Nimaeus unfurls the blast of energy, knocking both me and Larik to our feet.\nNimaeus 举起双手，一股黑暗能量开始在他周身凝聚。Larik 向他冲去，但 Nimaeus 释放出那股能量冲击，把我和 Larik 都掀翻在地。"

    old "Can't...move..."
    new "Can't...move...\n动不了……"

    old "Die, monster!"
    new "Die, monster!\n去死吧，怪物！"

    old "I watch as Nuala charges forward, pointing the silver staff at Nimaeus."
    new "I watch as Nuala charges forward, pointing the silver staff at Nimaeus.\n我看着 Nuala 向前冲去，把银色法杖对准 Nimaeus。"

    old "Nuala yells as she forces the glowing staff into the chest of Nimaeus, and he shrieks as she forces the staff through him, pinning him to the floor."
    new "Nuala yells as she forces the glowing staff into the chest of Nimaeus, and he shrieks as she forces the staff through him, pinning him to the floor.\nNuala 大喝一声，把发光的法杖插进 Nimaeus 的胸口，她用力将法杖刺穿他、把他钉在地板上时，他发出一声尖啸。"

    old "Daughter of Urd...it can't be..."
    new "Daughter of Urd...it can't be...\nUrd 之女……不可能……"

    old "Larik stands up, and I find myself in control of my own body once again. I stand up beside Nuala."
    new "Larik stands up, and I find myself in control of my own body once again. I stand up beside Nuala.\nLarik 站起身来，我发现自己又能掌控身体了。我在 Nuala 身旁站起来。"

    old "Sounds like a good idea."
    new "Sounds like a good idea.\n听起来是个好主意。"

    old "Nuala grabs hold of the staff, and I place a hand on her shoulder."
    new "Nuala grabs hold of the staff, and I place a hand on her shoulder.\nNuala 抓住法杖，我把一只手搭在她肩上。"

    old "Nuala, wait."
    new "Nuala, wait.\nNuala，等等。"

    old "What is it? Are we going to kill him or not?"
    new "What is it? Are we going to kill him or not?\n怎么了？我们到底要不要杀了他？"

    old "Look at him. He seems incapacitated. I think you put the rod right through his spine."
    new "Look at him. He seems incapacitated. I think you put the rod right through his spine.\n看看他。他似乎已经动弹不得了。我想你的法杖正好贯穿了他的脊椎。"

    old "A lich should be able to recover from that kind of blow, though. Unless...could this be the power of Benediction?"
    new "A lich should be able to recover from that kind of blow, though. Unless...could this be the power of Benediction?\n不过，巫妖本该能从那种重创中恢复的。除非……这会是 Benediction 的力量吗？"

    old "Nuala and Larik follow me back to the hole in the ceiling where I fell through. Larik bends down and lifts me and Nuala out of the hole, then Nuala and I reach down and pull Larik up after us."
    new "Nuala and Larik follow me back to the hole in the ceiling where I fell through. Larik bends down and lifts me and Nuala out of the hole, then Nuala and I reach down and pull Larik up after us.\nNuala 和 Larik 跟着我回到天花板上那个我跌落下来的洞口。Larik 弯下腰，把我和 Nuala 托出洞外，然后我和 Nuala 再伸手把 Larik 拉了上来。"

    old "We exit the tomb in the same way that we came, and Larik pushes the rock back into place, sealing the tomb once again."
    new "We exit the tomb in the same way that we came, and Larik pushes the rock back into place, sealing the tomb once again.\n我们沿着来时的路走出墓室，Larik 把石头推回原位，重新封住了墓穴。"

    old "We meet with the others, who are happy that we made out alive."
    new "We meet with the others, who are happy that we made out alive.\n我们与其他人会合，他们很高兴我们活着出来了。"

    old "After a short talk, everyone leaves, except for Nuala and Larik who are still talking. I decide to approach them."
    new "After a short talk, everyone leaves, except for Nuala and Larik who are still talking. I decide to approach them.\n简短交谈之后，大家都离开了，只有 Nuala 和 Larik 还在说话。我决定过去找他们。"

    old "The tomb of Urd..."
    new "The tomb of Urd...\nUrd 之墓……"

    old "Quite the deceptive name, don't you think?"
    new "Quite the deceptive name, don't you think?\n这名字挺有迷惑性的，你不觉得吗？"

    old "All this time, I assumed that this is where Urd was buried. But the more I think about it, the more it seems like this tomb was built not {i}for{/i} Urd, but {i}by{/i} Urd, to contain a threat that he—that she couldn't vanquish."
    new "All this time, I assumed that this is where Urd was buried. But the more I think about it, the more it seems like this tomb was built not {i}for{/i} Urd, but {i}by{/i} Urd, to contain a threat that he—that she couldn't vanquish.\n一直以来，我都以为 Urd 就埋葬在这里。但我越想越觉得，这座墓不是{i}为{/i} Urd 而建，而是{i}由{/i} Urd 所建，用来困住一个他——一个她无法消灭的威胁。"

    old "Do you think Urd really was a woman?"
    new "Do you think Urd really was a woman?\n你觉得 Urd 真的是个女人吗？"

    old "Who do you think we should trust? Storytellers, who have had hundreds and multiple generations to get the details wrong? Or someone who met with Urd face to face?"
    new "Who do you think we should trust? Storytellers, who have had hundreds and multiple generations to get the details wrong? Or someone who met with Urd face to face?\n你觉得我们该信谁？是那些有数百年、历经好几代人、很可能把细节讲错的说书人？还是那个与 Urd 面对面见过的人？"

    old "I'm not sure I can trust a lich."
    new "I'm not sure I can trust a lich.\n我不确定我能信任一个巫妖。"

    old "Neither am I. And yet, I can't imagine why he would have lied to us. Man, woman, who knows? Either way, it seems like a great story."
    new "Neither am I. And yet, I can't imagine why he would have lied to us. Man, woman, who knows? Either way, it seems like a great story.\n我也不能。然而，我想象不出他为什么要对我们撒谎。男人，女人，谁知道呢？不管怎样，这倒像是个精彩的故事。"

    old "I'm glad that we were able to seal away a threat. Though, I think that my people should come back here soon, to re-seal the tomb."
    new "I'm glad that we were able to seal away a threat. Though, I think that my people should come back here soon, to re-seal the tomb.\n我很高兴我们能封印住一个威胁。不过，我想我的人应该很快再回来，重新封住这座墓。"

    old "Good idea. Close the doors we opened, and maybe write a warning message to future generations. Carving symbols into stone seems like a good way to do this."
    new "Good idea. Close the doors we opened, and maybe write a warning message to future generations. Carving symbols into stone seems like a good way to do this.\n好主意。把我们打开的门封上，也许再给后世留一句警示。把符号刻进石头，似乎是个好办法。"

    old "Larik hefts the silver axe."
    new "Larik hefts the silver axe.\nLarik 掂了掂那柄银斧。"

    old "It seems somehow wrong to take it with me."
    new "It seems somehow wrong to take it with me.\n把它带走，总觉得有些不对。"

    old "Why not? This axe was crafted to seal away the undead, but in the end, Benediction was enough to do the job. Why not reintroduce Baneslayer to the world, and show it the undead horrors that now wander around N'Mar?"
    new "Why not? This axe was crafted to seal away the undead, but in the end, Benediction was enough to do the job. Why not reintroduce Baneslayer to the world, and show it the undead horrors that now wander around N'Mar?\n为什么不呢？这把斧头本就是为封印亡灵而打造的，但到头来，Benediction 就足以完成这件事了。何不让 Baneslayer 重新现世，让它去见识见识如今在 N'Mar 一带游荡的亡灵恐怖呢？"

    old "Perhaps one day, the undead menaces of N'Mar will also be laid to rest, and Baneslayer can be returned to Urd's tomb."
    new "Perhaps one day, the undead menaces of N'Mar will also be laid to rest, and Baneslayer can be returned to Urd's tomb.\n也许有一天，N'Mar 的亡灵威胁也会被平息，届时 Baneslayer 就能归还到 Urd 之墓。"

    old "Yes, one day, perhaps. I'd like to see that day very much."
    new "Yes, one day, perhaps. I'd like to see that day very much.\n是啊，也许会有那么一天。我非常想看到那一天。"

    old "So would I."
    new "So would I.\n我也一样。"

    old "Then let's fight to make it happen."
    new "Then let's fight to make it happen.\n那我们就为让那一天到来而战吧。"

    old "Nuala hefts the silver staff she took from the tomb."
    new "Nuala hefts the silver staff she took from the tomb.\nNuala 掂了掂她从墓中取出的那根银杖。"

    old "If we're right, this is Benediction, Urd's legendary staff. It seems somehow wrong to take it with me."
    new "If we're right, this is Benediction, Urd's legendary staff. It seems somehow wrong to take it with me.\n如果我们没猜错，这就是 Benediction，Urd 的传奇法杖。把它带走，总觉得有些不对。"

    old "Why not? That rod was made for fighting. It belongs in the hands of a warrior, not buried in a tomb. At one time, Urd must have used it to seal away an undead beast, but it seems that Baneslayer alone was enough to accomplish that."
    new "Why not? That rod was made for fighting. It belongs in the hands of a warrior, not buried in a tomb. At one time, Urd must have used it to seal away an undead beast, but it seems that Baneslayer alone was enough to accomplish that.\n为什么不呢？那根杖生来就是为战斗而造的。它属于战士之手，而不该被埋在墓里。当年，Urd 一定曾用它封印过一头亡灵怪物，但看来单凭 Baneslayer 就足以办到了。"

    old "Then I'll use Benediction, and use it to vanquish the undead menace that plagues the lands around N'Mar. But one day, when that threat is gone, I'll come back to this tomb, and return Urd's rod to the place where she left it."
    new "Then I'll use Benediction, and use it to vanquish the undead menace that plagues the lands around N'Mar. But one day, when that threat is gone, I'll come back to this tomb, and return Urd's rod to the place where she left it.\n那我就使用 Benediction，用它去消灭肆虐于 N'Mar 周边的亡灵威胁。但有一天，当那个威胁消失后，我会回到这座墓，把 Urd 的法杖放回她当初留下它的地方。"

    old "I stare at the skull symbol, and feel myself almost drawn in by the tile. No, it's not the tile itself. It's what's under the tile."
    new "I stare at the skull symbol, and feel myself almost drawn in by the tile. No, it's not the tile itself. It's what's under the tile.\n我凝视着那个骷髅符号，感觉自己几乎被那块石砖吸了进去。不，不是石砖本身。而是石砖下面的东西。"

    old "My hand forms a fist and punches through the tile, breaking it in half."
    new "My hand forms a fist and punches through the tile, breaking it in half.\n我的手攥成拳头，一拳砸穿石砖，把它打成两半。"

    old "I...I'm not sure. Something just came over me."
    new "I...I'm not sure. Something just came over me.\n我……我不确定。刚刚有什么东西控制了我。"

    old "Is your hand okay?"
    new "Is your hand okay?\n你的手没事吧？"

    old "It seems fine."
    new "It seems fine.\n看起来没事。"

    old "I pick at the broken bits of floor tile, revealing what looks like the hilt of a sword."
    new "I pick at the broken bits of floor tile, revealing what looks like the hilt of a sword.\n我扒开破碎的地砖，露出一个看似剑柄的东西。"

    old "Larik, do you want to help me dig this out?"
    new "Larik, do you want to help me dig this out?\nLarik，你愿意帮我把它挖出来吗？"

    old "Larik kneels down next to me, and we both begin digging at the sand and detritus around the sword hilt. Suddenly, Larik snaps back. His body flies into the air, and he lands on his back several feet away."
    new "Larik kneels down next to me, and we both begin digging at the sand and detritus around the sword hilt. Suddenly, Larik snaps back. His body flies into the air, and he lands on his back several feet away.\nLarik 在我身旁跪下，我们俩开始扒剑柄周围的沙土和碎屑。突然，Larik 猛地向后弹开。他的身体飞向空中，然后仰面摔落在几尺之外。"

    old "Larik!"
    new "Larik!\nLarik！"

    old "I'm fine. But that sword..."
    new "I'm fine. But that sword...\n我没事。但那把剑……"

    old "I just touched it. That sword...it seems to have a life of its own. As my finger touched it, I felt it pushing back, as though it were rejecting me."
    new "I just touched it. That sword...it seems to have a life of its own. As my finger touched it, I felt it pushing back, as though it were rejecting me.\n我刚碰到它。那把剑……它似乎有自己的生命。我的手指一碰到它，就感到它在往回推，仿佛在拒绝我。"

    old "I'd like to see."
    new "I'd like to see.\n我想看看。"

    old "Nuala kneels down next to the hole and waves her hand over it."
    new "Nuala kneels down next to the hole and waves her hand over it.\nNuala 在洞口旁跪下，把手在洞上方挥了挥。"

    old "I can feel some sort of energy pulsing from it. Some sort of dark force is possessing this blade."
    new "I can feel some sort of energy pulsing from it. Some sort of dark force is possessing this blade.\n我能感觉到某种能量从它身上脉动而出。有某种黑暗力量寄宿在这把剑里。"

    old "I lean down and grab the sword by its hilt."
    new "I lean down and grab the sword by its hilt.\n我俯下身，抓住剑柄。"

    old "Careful!"
    new "Careful!\n小心！"

    old "I tighten my grip on the hilt, and pull it from the floor. Dust and bits of broken rock brush off the blade as I pull it out."
    new "I tighten my grip on the hilt, and pull it from the floor. Dust and bits of broken rock brush off the blade as I pull it out.\n我攥紧剑柄，把它从地里拔出。拔出的过程中，尘土和碎石屑纷纷从剑身上抖落。"

    old "This blade...there's something special about it."
    new "This blade...there's something special about it.\n这把剑……它有些特别之处。"

    old "I think we'd all established that. But there seems to be something particularly special about {i}you{/i}."
    new "I think we'd all established that. But there seems to be something particularly special about {i}you{/i}.\n我想我们大家都已经认定了这一点。但似乎特别的地方在{i}你{/i}身上。"

    old "Could this be the power that Zachary told me about? A silver edge, crafted for vampires? But why a silver blade, if its use was to be wielded by a vampire? A sword like this seems like it would be better used as a weapon against the undead, not for them."
    new "Could this be the power that Zachary told me about? A silver edge, crafted for vampires? But why a silver blade, if its use was to be wielded by a vampire? A sword like this seems like it would be better used as a weapon against the undead, not for them.\n这会不会就是 Zachary 告诉过我的那种力量？一件为吸血鬼打造的银刃？可如果它是给吸血鬼使用的，又为什么是银刃？这样一把剑，似乎更适合用来对付亡灵，而不是为亡灵所用。"

    old "I feel the blade turn, and my hand turns with it."
    new "I feel the blade turn, and my hand turns with it.\n我感觉到剑在转动，我的手也跟着它转。"

    old "I'm...not. The blade is moving by itself."
    new "I'm...not. The blade is moving by itself.\n不……不是我。是剑在自己动。"

    old "The sword points toward the ground, and plunges into the floor underneath me. I feel the floor give way, and the tile I'm standing on crumbles as I fall."
    new "The sword points toward the ground, and plunges into the floor underneath me. I feel the floor give way, and the tile I'm standing on crumbles as I fall.\n剑指向地面，插进我脚下的地板。我感到地板塌陷，我站着的那块石砖随之碎裂，我便坠了下去。"

    old "After a moment of sheer terror, I hit the ground, somehow miraculously landing on my feet. I'm in...another hidden chamber?"
    new "After a moment of sheer terror, I hit the ground, somehow miraculously landing on my feet. I'm in...another hidden chamber?\n在片刻纯粹的惊恐之后，我摔到地上，竟奇迹般地双脚着地。我这是在……另一间密室里？"

    old "Yes, I'm fine."
    new "Yes, I'm fine.\n是的，我没事。"

    old "What's down there? Should we follow you?"
    new "What's down there? Should we follow you?\n下面有什么？我们要跟下去吗？"

    old "Hold on. Let me see what's down here."
    new "Hold on. Let me see what's down here.\n等一下。让我看看这下面有什么。"

    old "I scan the chamber. It's unlit, but a bit of the torchlight from the chamber above bleeds through the hole that I fell through, and in the dim illumination I can make out the form of a corpse resting against the wall."
    new "I scan the chamber. It's unlit, but a bit of the torchlight from the chamber above bleeds through the hole that I fell through, and in the dim illumination I can make out the form of a corpse resting against the wall.\n我扫视这间密室。里面没有灯，但上方房间的火光从我跌落的洞口透进来一点，借着这昏暗的光，我能辨认出靠墙躺着的一具尸体轮廓。"

    old "Ah, at last you've come."
    new "Ah, at last you've come.\n啊，你终于来了。"

    old "A talking corpse?"
    new "A talking corpse?\n一具会说话的尸体？"

    old "What are you?"
    new "What are you?\n你是什么？"

    old "What am I? I am a king. King Nimaeus, they called me. Though I suppose my throne is gone by now."
    new "What am I? I am a king. King Nimaeus, they called me. Though I suppose my throne is gone by now.\n我是什么？我是一位国王。人们称我为 King Nimaeus。不过我想，我的王位如今早已不在了。"

    old "I've never head of a King Nimaeus."
    new "I've never head of a King Nimaeus.\n我从没听说过 King Nimaeus 这号人物。"

    old "That's the problem with immortality. I keep living, but the world's kingdoms and borders continue to shift."
    new "That's the problem with immortality. I keep living, but the world's kingdoms and borders continue to shift.\n这就是永生的问题。我一直在活着，可世间的王国与疆界却不断变迁。"

    old "Immortality?"
    new "Immortality?\n永生？"

    old "Yes, it was quite an ordeal, and it's had some unpleasant side-effects as well. For example, I had to attach my soul to this corpse, the most recent in a line of many corpses that have held my soul over the centuries. But great power always comes at great cost."
    new "Yes, it was quite an ordeal, and it's had some unpleasant side-effects as well. For example, I had to attach my soul to this corpse, the most recent in a line of many corpses that have held my soul over the centuries. But great power always comes at great cost.\n没错，那着实是场磨难，还带来了一些令人不快的副作用。比如，我不得不把自己的灵魂附在这具尸体上——几个世纪以来，盛放我灵魂的诸多尸体中，这是最新的一具。但巨大的力量总要付出巨大的代价。"

    old "You're a lich."
    new "You're a lich.\n你是个巫妖。"

    old "That is what they called me, yes. A creature born of the earth. Though, aren't we all? The only thing that separates me is that I continue to reborn through the death of others."
    new "That is what they called me, yes. A creature born of the earth. Though, aren't we all? The only thing that separates me is that I continue to reborn through the death of others.\n没错，他们是这样称呼我的。一个从大地中诞生的造物。不过，我们谁又不是呢？我唯一不同的地方，只是我靠着别人的死亡不断重生。"

    old "But enough about me. Tell me, did you come to serve me? Or are you another of Urd's disciples, drawn here out of some misguided desire to seal me in the ground once more?"
    new "But enough about me. Tell me, did you come to serve me? Or are you another of Urd's disciples, drawn here out of some misguided desire to seal me in the ground once more?\n不过，关于我就说到这儿吧。告诉我，你是来为我效劳的吗？还是说，你又是 Urd 的门徒之一，怀着某种误入歧途的念头，被吸引到这里，想再把我封进地里一次？"

    old "I came to serve you."
    new "I came to serve you.\n我是来为你效劳的。"

    old "And yet you seem to have no idea who I am. I think you are a poor liar. But, whether you desire it or not, you'll be my servant soon enough."
    new "And yet you seem to have no idea who I am. I think you are a poor liar. But, whether you desire it or not, you'll be my servant soon enough.\n可你似乎根本不知道我是谁。我看你是个蹩脚的骗子。不过，不管你愿不愿意，你很快就会成为我的仆人了。"

    old "Urd once came at me with an army, you know. A group of adventurers who were foolish enough to follow her into battle."
    new "Urd once came at me with an army, you know. A group of adventurers who were foolish enough to follow her into battle.\n你知道，Urd 当年曾带着一支军队来讨伐我。那是一群愚蠢到肯跟着她上战场的冒险者。"

    old "Her?"
    new "Her?\n她？"

    old "Yes, Urd found many disciples who were willing to do her bidding. Something about that woman's acts of heroism must have inspired them. Though, in the end, their devotion to Urd was what killed them."
    new "Yes, Urd found many disciples who were willing to do her bidding. Something about that woman's acts of heroism must have inspired them. Though, in the end, their devotion to Urd was what killed them.\n没错，Urd 找到了许多愿意听她差遣的门徒。那个女人的种种英雄壮举，一定有什么地方鼓舞了他们。只不过，到头来，他们对 Urd 的忠诚正是害死他们的原因。"

    old "Or most of them. The weak-willed ones, they died instantly. The strong-willed ones, they survived. They're always the most useful."
    new "Or most of them. The weak-willed ones, they died instantly. The strong-willed ones, they survived. They're always the most useful.\n或者说，是其中大部分人。意志薄弱的那些，当场就死了。意志坚定的那些，活了下来。而他们总是最有用的。"

    old "I am a disciple of Urd."
    new "I am a disciple of Urd.\n我是 Urd 的门徒。"

    old "Urd must be dead by now. It must be at least a hundred years since we last met. Tell me, how did the woman die?"
    new "Urd must be dead by now. It must be at least a hundred years since we last met. Tell me, how did the woman die?\nUrd 现在一定已经死了。我们上次见面，至少是一百年前的事了。告诉我，那个女人是怎么死的？"

    old "What woman?"
    new "What woman?\n哪个女人？"

    old "Urd. How did she die?"
    new "Urd. How did she die?\nUrd。她是怎么死的？"

    old "Ah, so it seems you are not a disciple of Urd after all. You are a very poor liar indeed."
    new "Ah, so it seems you are not a disciple of Urd after all. You are a very poor liar indeed.\n啊，看来你终究不是 Urd 的门徒。你确实是个蹩脚透顶的骗子。"

    old "I serve no one but myself."
    new "I serve no one but myself.\n我不为任何人效力，只为自己。"

    old "Funny, Urd spoke those exact words to me, right before she left me here to rot. Did you come here hoping to emulate that woman's success?"
    new "Funny, Urd spoke those exact words to me, right before she left me here to rot. Did you come here hoping to emulate that woman's success?\n有趣，就在 Urd 把我留在这里腐烂之前，她对我说过一模一样的话。你来这里，是想效仿那个女人的成功吗？"

    old "Yes, Urd inspired many disciples. Whether it was her charisma or acts of heroism that did it, I'll not know. But I prefer to claim my followers through more...magical means."
    new "Yes, Urd inspired many disciples. Whether it was her charisma or acts of heroism that did it, I'll not know. But I prefer to claim my followers through more...magical means.\n没错，Urd 激励了许多门徒。究竟是她的魅力还是她的英雄壮举起了作用，我无从知晓。但我更喜欢用更……魔法的方式去收服我的追随者。"

    old "You deny being one of Urd's disciples, but when I see that defiant look in your eye..."
    new "You deny being one of Urd's disciples, but when I see that defiant look in your eye...\n你否认自己是 Urd 的门徒，可当我看到你眼中那种桀骜不驯的神情……"

    old "Gah, these half-dead eyes must be playing tricks on me."
    new "Gah, these half-dead eyes must be playing tricks on me.\n啊，这双半死不活的眼睛一定是在跟我开玩笑。"

    old "You will serve me. Whether it's willingly or not is up to you. To be honest, mindless thralls are more convenient, but I thought I'd do you the courtesy of offering a choice."
    new "You will serve me. Whether it's willingly or not is up to you. To be honest, mindless thralls are more convenient, but I thought I'd do you the courtesy of offering a choice.\n你会为我效劳的。是自愿还是被迫，由你决定。老实说，没有心智的奴仆用起来更方便，但我想出于礼貌，还是给你一个选择的机会。"

    old "I'd never serve someone like you."
    new "I'd never serve someone like you.\n我绝不会为你这种人效劳。"

    old "Very well, then."
    new "Very well, then.\n那好吧。"

    old "Nimaeus raises his hand and summons dark energy, then unfurls it. I feel a wave of coldness wash over me."
    new "Nimaeus raises his hand and summons dark energy, then unfurls it. I feel a wave of coldness wash over me.\nNimaeus 举起手，召唤出黑暗能量，然后将其释放。我感到一股寒意袭遍全身。"

    old "Are you done?"
    new "Are you done?\n你完了吗？"

    old "Wh-what? How are you still standing? You should be—"
    new "Wh-what? How are you still standing? You should be—\n什……什么？你怎么还能站着？你应该——"

    old "I should be what?"
    new "I should be what?\n我应该怎样？"

    old "You should be dead or possessed."
    new "You should be dead or possessed.\n你应该已经死了，或者被附身了。"

    old "I see. Your magic possesses the minds of the strong-willed, and shatters the minds of the weak-willed, is that it? That's how you gather your army of followers?"
    new "I see. Your magic possesses the minds of the strong-willed, and shatters the minds of the weak-willed, is that it? That's how you gather your army of followers?\n我明白了。你的魔法能占据意志坚定者的心智，又能击碎意志薄弱者的心智，是这样吗？这就是你召集追随者大军的方式？"

    old "It seems that you've discovered the limitations of your power. Nimaeus, you are not so powerful."
    new "It seems that you've discovered the limitations of your power. Nimaeus, you are not so powerful.\n看来你已经发现了自己力量的局限。Nimaeus，你没那么强大。"

    old "I raise the silver edge and point it toward the lich, then charge forward."
    new "I raise the silver edge and point it toward the lich, then charge forward.\n我举起银刃，指向巫妖，然后冲了上去。"

    old "He raises his arms, trying to summon more dark energies, and he releases several more blasts of magic. I feel the waves of darkness pass over me as I continue to charge forward."
    new "He raises his arms, trying to summon more dark energies, and he releases several more blasts of magic. I feel the waves of darkness pass over me as I continue to charge forward.\n他举起双臂，试图召唤更多黑暗能量，接着又释放出几波魔法冲击。我继续向前冲，感觉那一波波黑暗从我身上掠过。"

    old "I thrust the silver edge into his abdomen, pushing it further and further until it pierces the wall behind him."
    new "I thrust the silver edge into his abdomen, pushing it further and further until it pierces the wall behind him.\n我将银刃刺进他的腹部，越推越深，直到它刺穿他身后的墙壁。"

    old "It's going to take more than that to kill me."
    new "It's going to take more than that to kill me.\n光凭这个可杀不死我。"

    old "You're right, it would take more than that to kill you. You are immortal, after all."
    new "You're right, it would take more than that to kill you. You are immortal, after all.\n你说得对，要杀死你可不止这点手段。毕竟，你是不死之身。"

    old "But I don't need to kill you. You see, this sword has severed your spine, and as long as the silver stays lodged in your body, your spine will remain split."
    new "But I don't need to kill you. You see, this sword has severed your spine, and as long as the silver stays lodged in your body, your spine will remain split.\n但我不需要杀死你。你看，这把剑已经斩断了你的脊椎，只要这银子还嵌在你体内，你的脊椎就会一直断着。"

    old "Nimaeus, there are fates worse than death. I'm not going to kill you. No, I'm just going to leave you here, paralyzed, to spend the next few centuries rotting away."
    new "Nimaeus, there are fates worse than death. I'm not going to kill you. No, I'm just going to leave you here, paralyzed, to spend the next few centuries rotting away.\nNimaeus，有些命运比死亡更可怕。我不会杀你。不，我只会把你留在这里，瘫痪着，用接下来的几个世纪慢慢腐烂。"

    old "Eventually, your flesh may crumble to dust, and at that point you may find another body to possess. But that is a problem for the people of a hundred years to face. And this world has a habit of producing worthy heroes when the need arises."
    new "Eventually, your flesh may crumble to dust, and at that point you may find another body to possess. But that is a problem for the people of a hundred years to face. And this world has a habit of producing worthy heroes when the need arises.\n最终，你的血肉也许会化为尘土，到那时，你也许能找到另一具身体来占据。但那是百年之后的人们要面对的问题。而这个世界，总习惯在需要的时候造就出称职的英雄。"

    old "I think that your next attempt at grandeur will end very much like this: pinned to the ground, buried underground, left to rot for several hundred years until the next adventurer comes along to defeat you."
    new "I think that your next attempt at grandeur will end very much like this: pinned to the ground, buried underground, left to rot for several hundred years until the next adventurer comes along to defeat you.\n我想，你下一次图谋伟业的尝试，结局也会和这次差不多：被钉在地上，埋在地下，腐烂几百年，直到下一个冒险者前来把你击败。"

    old "Perhaps in a thousand years, you'll wish that you had chosen death instead."
    new "Perhaps in a thousand years, you'll wish that you had chosen death instead.\n也许千年之后，你会后悔当初没有选择死亡。"

    old "How...how did you survive my magic?"
    new "How...how did you survive my magic?\n你……你是怎么从我的魔法中活下来的？"

    old "Nimaeus coughs with a raspy voice, barely willing his lungs to speak."
    new "Nimaeus coughs with a raspy voice, barely willing his lungs to speak.\nNimaeus 用嘶哑的声音咳嗽着，几乎连肺腑都不听使唤，说不出话。"

    old "Blood magic, that's the way you control, your thralls, isn't it? Those with strong constitution can be animated according to your will. Those with weak constitution will have their blood vessels ruptured."
    new "Blood magic, that's the way you control, your thralls, isn't it? Those with strong constitution can be animated according to your will. Those with weak constitution will have their blood vessels ruptured.\n血魔法，这就是你控制你那些奴仆的方式，对吧？体魄强健的人能按你的意志被驱使。体魄孱弱的人则会血管爆裂。"

    old "I lean in and whisper into his ear."
    new "I lean in and whisper into his ear.\n我凑上前，在他耳边低语。"

    old "Blood doesn't work so well when your victims have no blood."
    new "Blood doesn't work so well when your victims have no blood.\n当你的受害者没有血时，血魔法就不那么好使了。"

    old "You're...a vampire?"
    new "You're...a vampire?\n你……是吸血鬼？"

    old "Now you understand."
    new "Now you understand.\n现在你明白了。"

    old "I turn around. Nimaeus tries to yell at me, but it only comes out as high-pitched wheezing. I walk back to the hole in the ceiling and climb out, leaving the lich behind."
    new "I turn around. Nimaeus tries to yell at me, but it only comes out as high-pitched wheezing. I walk back to the hole in the ceiling and climb out, leaving the lich behind.\n我转过身。Nimaeus 想朝我大喊，可发出的只有尖利的喘息声。我走回天花板上的洞口，爬了出去，把巫妖留在了身后。"

    old "I think our work here is done. Let's get out of here."
    new "I think our work here is done. Let's get out of here.\n我想我们在这里的活儿干完了。我们离开这儿吧。"

    old "What happened down there?"
    new "What happened down there?\n下面发生了什么？"

    old "I learned a few things about Urd."
    new "I learned a few things about Urd.\n我了解到了一些关于 Urd 的事。"

    old "Well, Urd was a woman."
    new "Well, Urd was a woman.\n嗯，Urd 是个女人。"

    old "An immortal lich told me."
    new "An immortal lich told me.\n一个不死的巫妖告诉我的。"

    old "You saw a lich down there?"
    new "You saw a lich down there?\n你在下面见到了一个巫妖？"

    old "Yes, apparently that story was true."
    new "Yes, apparently that story was true.\n是的，看来那个故事是真的。"

    old "Did you kill the lich?"
    new "Did you kill the lich?\n你杀了那巫妖吗？"

    old "If the stories are true, and I think they are, then the lich is immortal. But I incapacitated the lich, and I don't think you or your people will have to worry about him again for a very, very long time."
    new "If the stories are true, and I think they are, then the lich is immortal. But I incapacitated the lich, and I don't think you or your people will have to worry about him again for a very, very long time.\n如果那些故事是真的——而我认为它们是真的——那么这巫妖是不死的。但我已经让他动弹不得了，而且我想，你和你的人民在非常、非常长的时间里，都不用再为他担心了。"

    old "How long is very long?"
    new "How long is very long?\n非常长是有多长？"

    old "How long ago was it that Urd first fought the lich?"
    new "How long ago was it that Urd first fought the lich?\nUrd 第一次与那巫妖交手，是多久以前的事了？"

    old "Hundreds of years."
    new "Hundreds of years.\n几百年前。"

    old "I think it will be about that long before you see the lich again. When your children's children's children's children have to deal with him one day, they should know what they're dealing with."
    new "I think it will be about that long before you see the lich again. When your children's children's children's children have to deal with him one day, they should know what they're dealing with.\n我想，要再过差不多那么久，你才会再见到那巫妖。等有一天，你子孙的子孙的子孙不得不对付他时，他们应当知道自己在对付什么。"

    old "How do you suppose we should achieve that?"
    new "How do you suppose we should achieve that?\n你觉得我们该怎么做到这一点？"

    old "Stories seem to be one thing that endure through the centuries. Some of them may be recast as legends, but I think that a good story will serve the test of time."
    new "Stories seem to be one thing that endure through the centuries. Some of them may be recast as legends, but I think that a good story will serve the test of time.\n故事似乎是少数能历经数百年而不衰的东西之一。其中一些也许会被改写成传奇，但我想，一个好故事经得起时间的考验。"

    old "Then I'd like to hear everything that happened down there."
    new "Then I'd like to hear everything that happened down there.\n那我愿意听听下面发生的一切。"

    old "I'll tell you everything as soon as we get out of here."
    new "I'll tell you everything as soon as we get out of here.\n我们一离开这里，我就把一切都告诉你。"

    old "I lead Larik and Nuala back to the entrance of tomb, and stop just short of the entrance. It feels like someone is watching me..."
    new "I lead Larik and Nuala back to the entrance of tomb, and stop just short of the entrance. It feels like someone is watching me...\n我领着 Larik 和 Nuala 回到墓的入口，在离入口不远的地方停下。感觉好像有人在盯着我……"

    old "You to go on out. I'd like to spend a few moments alone in here, if you don't mind."
    new "You to go on out. I'd like to spend a few moments alone in here, if you don't mind.\n你们俩先出去吧。我想在这里独自待一会儿，如果你们不介意的话。"

    old "You want us to seal you inside?"
    new "You want us to seal you inside?\n你想让我们把你封在里面？"

    old "Yes, I'll let you know when I want to be let out."
    new "Yes, I'll let you know when I want to be let out.\n是的，等我想要出来时，我会告诉你们。"

    old "Larik and Nuala walk out, and they roll the stone back into place, sealing me inside."
    new "Larik and Nuala walk out, and they roll the stone back into place, sealing me inside.\nLarik 和 Nuala 走了出去，他们把石头滚回原位，把我封在了里面。"

    old "You can come out now."
    new "You can come out now.\n你们现在可以出来了。"

    old "Zachary and Valery appear before me."
    new "Zachary and Valery appear before me.\nZachary 和 Valery 出现在我面前。"

    old "My, [protag]. You're getting quite sharp."
    new "My, [protag]. You're getting quite sharp.\n哎呀，[protag]。你越来越敏锐了。"

    old "It must be these vampiric senses."
    new "It must be these vampiric senses.\n一定是这些吸血鬼的感官。"

    old "Only partially turned, and yet you've already shown such power..."
    new "Only partially turned, and yet you've already shown such power...\n只是部分转化，你却已经展现出如此的力量……"

    old "Were you watching?"
    new "Were you watching?\n你们一直在看着？"

    old "No, unfortunately. But I did see the aftermath. Nimaeus was in bad shape. Poor chap, the man just can't seem to catch a break."
    new "No, unfortunately. But I did see the aftermath. Nimaeus was in bad shape. Poor chap, the man just can't seem to catch a break.\n不，很不幸。不过我确实看到了后果。Nimaeus 的情况糟透了。可怜的家伙，这人似乎就是走背运。"

    old "You know Nimaeus?"
    new "You know Nimaeus?\n你认识 Nimaeus？"

    old "You could say that we were acquaintances, once upon a time. He and I...well, we never really got along."
    new "You could say that we were acquaintances, once upon a time. He and I...well, we never really got along.\n可以说，我们曾经是熟人。他和我……嗯，我们从来没真正合得来。"

    old "It's a small world."
    new "It's a small world.\n这世界真小。"

    old "The world seems small when you live for centuries."
    new "The world seems small when you live for centuries.\n当你活上几个世纪时，世界就显得很小了。"

    old "When I was talking with Nimaeus, I noticed something."
    new "When I was talking with Nimaeus, I noticed something.\n我和 Nimaeus 交谈时，注意到了一件事。"

    old "Oh? What might that be?"
    new "Oh? What might that be?\n哦？那会是什么？"

    old "He had a fresh corpse. That corpse didn't come from nowhere."
    new "He had a fresh corpse. That corpse didn't come from nowhere.\n他有一具新鲜的尸体。那具尸体不会凭空出现。"

    old "I sense an accusatory tone in your voice."
    new "I sense an accusatory tone in your voice.\n我从你的语气里听出了一丝指责。"

    old "Maybe I'm casting accusations, maybe I'm just curious. Some questions are meant to cast doubt, other questions are meant to resolve it."
    new "Maybe I'm casting accusations, maybe I'm just curious. Some questions are meant to cast doubt, other questions are meant to resolve it.\n也许我是在指责，也许我只是好奇。有些问题是为了抛出怀疑，另一些问题则是为了消除怀疑。"

    old "If you're suspecting that I'm the one who left the corpse there, then yes, it was me."
    new "If you're suspecting that I'm the one who left the corpse there, then yes, it was me.\n如果你怀疑是我把尸体留在那儿的，那么没错，就是我。"

    old "You don't strike me as the sort of person who does things like leave a corpse somewhere by accident."
    new "You don't strike me as the sort of person who does things like leave a corpse somewhere by accident.\n你给我的印象，不像是会意外把尸体留在某处的那种人。"

    old "No, you're right."
    new "No, you're right.\n不，你说得对。"

    old "So, you wanted Nimaeus to have a new body?"
    new "So, you wanted Nimaeus to have a new body?\n所以，你是想让 Nimaeus 得到一具新的身体？"

    old "Yes. He was a disembodied soul searching for a new corpse. So I gave it to him. I figured it would be better than leaving things up to chance."
    new "Yes. He was a disembodied soul searching for a new corpse. So I gave it to him. I figured it would be better than leaving things up to chance.\n没错。他是一个游荡的灵魂，正在寻找一具新尸体。于是我就给了他。我想这总比把事情交给偶然要好。"

    old "And yet, when I found him, he seemed to be quite in control of his faculties."
    new "And yet, when I found him, he seemed to be quite in control of his faculties.\n然而，我找到他的时候，他似乎对自己的神智掌控得相当好。"

    old "Yes, but you managed to subdue him, didn't you?"
    new "Yes, but you managed to subdue him, didn't you?\n没错，但你设法制服了他，不是吗？"

    old "But what if I hadn't?"
    new "But what if I hadn't?\n可万一我没有呢？"

    old "Then the gods would have intervened. Or, if not the gods, then someone like me."
    new "Then the gods would have intervened. Or, if not the gods, then someone like me.\n那样神就会出手干预了。又或者，即便不是神，也会有像我这样的人。"

    old "You left Nimaeus like that because you wanted to test me."
    new "You left Nimaeus like that because you wanted to test me.\n你把 Nimaeus 弄成那样，是因为你想考验我。"

    old "And you seem to have proven yourself quite capably. I knew I was right to set my eyes on you, [protag]. You and I are going to do great things together. Your display of capability in dealing with Nimaeus only proves that further."
    new "And you seem to have proven yourself quite capably. I knew I was right to set my eyes on you, [protag]. You and I are going to do great things together. Your display of capability in dealing with Nimaeus only proves that further.\n而你也似乎已经相当出色地证明了自己。我就知道我看上你是对的，[protag]。你和我将会一起成就一番大事业。你在对付 Nimaeus 时展现出的能力，只会更进一步证明这一点。"

    old "I don't appreciate being tested like that."
    new "I don't appreciate being tested like that.\n我可不喜欢被那样考验。"

    old "Really? But you dealt with things so capably."
    new "Really? But you dealt with things so capably.\n是吗？可你把事情处理得那么出色。"

    old "So capably!"
    new "So capably!\n那么出色！"

    old "You were toying with me, Zachary. And I'm not someone who likes being toyed with. I hope today was the last time."
    new "You were toying with me, Zachary. And I'm not someone who likes being toyed with. I hope today was the last time.\n你是在耍我，Zachary。而我不是那种喜欢被人耍的人。我希望今天是最后一次。"

    old "Of course, of course. You've shown yourself more than deserving of my respect."
    new "Of course, of course. You've shown yourself more than deserving of my respect.\n当然，当然。你已经证明自己，远不止配得上我的尊重。"

    old "You don't need to test me like that again."
    new "You don't need to test me like that again.\n你不必再那样考验我了。"

    old "Yes, of course. You've proven yourself more than deserving of my respect. But little tests like this are such fun, don't you think?"
    new "Yes, of course. You've proven yourself more than deserving of my respect. But little tests like this are such fun, don't you think?\n是啊，当然。你已经证明自己，远不止配得上我的尊重。不过像这样的小小考验，真的很有趣，你不觉得吗？"

    old "'Fun' is not the word I'd use."
    new "'Fun' is not the word I'd use.\n“有趣”可不是我会用的词。"

    old "Well then, my apologies."
    new "Well then, my apologies.\n那么，我道歉。"

    old "Any other questions? Or are we done here? I wouldn't want to keep your friends waiting."
    new "Any other questions? Or are we done here? I wouldn't want to keep your friends waiting.\n还有别的问题吗？还是我们到此为止？我可不想让你的朋友们久等。"

    old "I think we're done here."
    new "I think we're done here.\n我想我们到此为止吧。"

    old "Then goodbye, [protag]. I bid you adieu."
    new "Then goodbye, [protag]. I bid you adieu.\n那么再会了，[protag]。我向你道别。"

    old "Adieu."
    new "Adieu.\n再会。"

    old "Zachary and Valery vanish from sight, and I go back to the tomb entrance and pound on the rock."
    new "Zachary and Valery vanish from sight, and I go back to the tomb entrance and pound on the rock.\nZachary 和 Valery 从眼前消失，我回到墓的入口，用力敲击那块石头。"

    old "I'm all done in here!"
    new "I'm all done in here!\n我在里面的事都办完了！"

    old "The stone rolls to the side, and I step out."
    new "The stone rolls to the side, and I step out.\n石头滚到一旁，我走了出去。"

    old "[protag], while you were inside, Nuala and I have been thinking a bit about Urd's weapons."
    new "[protag], while you were inside, Nuala and I have been thinking a bit about Urd's weapons.\n[protag]，你在里面的时候，Nuala 和我一直在琢磨 Urd 的武器。"

    old "Larik holds the silver axe in both hands, and Nuala presents the silver rod."
    new "Larik holds the silver axe in both hands, and Nuala presents the silver rod.\nLarik 双手握着银斧，Nuala 则亮出银杖。"

    old "Do you think it's alright for us to abscond with them like this? It seems like they were left in here for a reason."
    new "Do you think it's alright for us to abscond with them like this? It seems like they were left in here for a reason.\n你觉得我们就这样把它们带走合适吗？它们被留在这里，似乎是有原因的。"

    old "I think what bothers me more is that we seem to have misunderstood so much about Urd. To discover, after hundreds of years, that Urd was a woman..."
    new "I think what bothers me more is that we seem to have misunderstood so much about Urd. To discover, after hundreds of years, that Urd was a woman...\n我想更让我困扰的是，我们似乎对 Urd 有那么多误解。几百年后才发现，Urd 竟然是个女人……"

    old "That seems like a small detail, compared to the nature of this tomb. For so long, we assumed that this was where Urd was buried."
    new "That seems like a small detail, compared to the nature of this tomb. For so long, we assumed that this was where Urd was buried.\n与这座墓的性质相比，那似乎只是个小细节。长久以来，我们都以为 Urd 就埋葬在这里。"

    old "The tomb of Urd."
    new "The tomb of Urd.\nUrd 之墓。"

    old "Yet it seems that this tomb was created, not {i}for{/i} Urd, but {i}by{/i} Urd, to seal away some kind of evil."
    new "Yet it seems that this tomb was created, not {i}for{/i} Urd, but {i}by{/i} Urd, to seal away some kind of evil.\n然而看来，这座墓不是{i}为{/i} Urd 而建，而是{i}由{/i} Urd 所建，用来封印某种邪恶。"

    old "Perhaps Urd's silver weapons played a role in that."
    new "Perhaps Urd's silver weapons played a role in that.\n也许 Urd 的银色武器在其中起了作用。"

    old "Perhaps. But I think this time, Baneslayer and Benediction weren't needed to finish the job. That lich isn't going anywhere."
    new "Perhaps. But I think this time, Baneslayer and Benediction weren't needed to finish the job. That lich isn't going anywhere.\n也许吧。但我想，这一次，要了结这件事并不需要 Baneslayer 和 Benediction。那巫妖哪儿也去不了了。"

    old "I don't think Urd will mind us borrowing her weapons. Especially if we're using them to vanquish the undead menace at N'Mar. I think that Urd would approve of that."
    new "I don't think Urd will mind us borrowing her weapons. Especially if we're using them to vanquish the undead menace at N'Mar. I think that Urd would approve of that.\n我想 Urd 不会介意我们借用她的武器。尤其是我们用它们去消灭 N'Mar 的亡灵威胁。我想 Urd 会赞许这样做的。"

    old "When we're done, we can return the weapons to where we found them."
    new "When we're done, we can return the weapons to where we found them.\n等事情了结后，我们可以把武器放回我们找到它们的地方。"

    old "On the day when undead nightmares no longer haunt N'Mar, I will happily lay Baneslayer to rest once more. But until then...I think I'd like to use this axe to split some zombie skulls."
    new "On the day when undead nightmares no longer haunt N'Mar, I will happily lay Baneslayer to rest once more. But until then...I think I'd like to use this axe to split some zombie skulls.\n等到不死噩梦不再纠缠 N'Mar 的那一天，我会很乐意让 Baneslayer 再次安息。但在那之前……我想用这把斧头劈开一些僵尸的脑壳。"

    old "And I'd like to use this rod to punish some vampires."
    new "And I'd like to use this rod to punish some vampires.\n而我想用这根法杖去惩戒一些吸血鬼。"

    old "I think the weapons are in good hands. After several hundred years, they're probably itching for a chance to see the battlefield once again."
    new "I think the weapons are in good hands. After several hundred years, they're probably itching for a chance to see the battlefield once again.\n我想这些武器落到了可靠的人手里。经过几百年，它们多半正渴望着能再有机会重返战场。"

    old "Fool. You think you can make demands? I am the one who does!"
    new "Fool. You think you can make demands? I am the one who does!\n蠢货。你以为你有资格提要求？提要求的是我！"

    old "I am done trying to reason with you. Submit or die."
    new "I am done trying to reason with you. Submit or die.\n我已经懒得再跟你讲道理了。要么臣服，要么死。"

    old "Your tricks don't work with me, [protag]. You should have accepted my deal."
    new "Your tricks don't work with me, [protag]. You should have accepted my deal.\n你的把戏对我没用，[protag]。你本该接受我的条件。"

    old "Yes, keep talking, keep talking."
    new "Yes, keep talking, keep talking.\n对，继续说，继续说。"

    old "All right, all right! We surrender! We accept your offer."
    new "All right, all right! We surrender! We accept your offer.\n好，好！我们投降！我们接受你的提议。"

    old "I nod to my companion, who takes advantage of the distraction and hits King Nimaeus."
    new "I nod to my companion, who takes advantage of the distraction and hits King Nimaeus.\n我朝同伴点头示意，同伴趁对方分神之际，击中了 King Nimaeus。"

    old "Pah! You fooled me once, but now you will pay!"
    new "Pah! You fooled me once, but now you will pay!\n呸！你骗过我一次，但现在你要付出代价了！"

    old "For the rest of the battle my talents won't work anymore, but at least thanks to my distraction, my companion was able to inflict a critical strike on him."
    new "For the rest of the battle my talents won't work anymore, but at least thanks to my distraction, my companion was able to inflict a critical strike on him.\n这场战斗余下的时间里，我的本事再也发挥不出来了，但至少多亏我分散了对方的注意力，同伴才得以对他打出一记重击。"

    old "I walk to Geraldine's estate with a sense of trepidation, clutching the paper invitation in my hand. She invites me into the manor without any show of ceremony."
    new "I walk to Geraldine's estate with a sense of trepidation, clutching the paper invitation in my hand. She invites me into the manor without any show of ceremony.\n我攥着手中的纸质请柬，怀着几分忐忑走向 Geraldine 的宅邸。她没有任何繁文缛节，直接把我请进了庄园。"

    old "Ah, [protag], you've arrived. Please, come in. I hope you're not busy. I think that you and I have much to talk about."
    new "Ah, [protag], you've arrived. Please, come in. I hope you're not busy. I think that you and I have much to talk about.\n啊，[protag]，你到了。请进。希望你不忙。我想你和我有很多话要谈。"

    old "You must be happy about my decision."
    new "You must be happy about my decision.\n你肯定为我的决定感到高兴。"

    old "Of course I am. But do not think I am happy because you supported my cause. I also think the army will be much more efficient with the steel weapons coming out that facility."
    new "Of course I am. But do not think I am happy because you supported my cause. I also think the army will be much more efficient with the steel weapons coming out that facility.\n我当然高兴。不过别以为我高兴是因为你支持了我的事业。我还认为，有了从那个设施里产出的钢铁武器，军队会高效得多。"

    old "However, I invited you here to talk about future."
    new "However, I invited you here to talk about future.\n不过，我邀请你来，是想谈谈未来。"

    old "What business is there to talk about? The decision to preserve the memorial is over and done with."
    new "What business is there to talk about? The decision to preserve the memorial is over and done with.\n还有什么可谈的？保留纪念碑的决定早已尘埃落定。"

    old "Yes, I understand that. But I've never been one to hold a grudge. I hoped to have you on my side for this decision, and so I made an appeal. An offer of sorts. You declined. That's fine, that deal is over and done with. But it doesn't preclude the possibility of us working together in the future."
    new "Yes, I understand that. But I've never been one to hold a grudge. I hoped to have you on my side for this decision, and so I made an appeal. An offer of sorts. You declined. That's fine, that deal is over and done with. But it doesn't preclude the possibility of us working together in the future.\n是的，我理解。但我从来不是个记仇的人。我当时希望你能站在我这边，于是提出了请求。算是一种开价。你拒绝了。没关系，那桩交易已经结束。但这并不排除我们将来合作的可能。"

    old "What future deal do you have in mind?"
    new "What future deal do you have in mind?\n你心里想的是什么样的未来交易？"

    old "At the moment? None. But I find it helpful to have friends in a variety of places, and all the better if they happen to be friends in high places."
    new "At the moment? None. But I find it helpful to have friends in a variety of places, and all the better if they happen to be friends in high places.\n眼下？没有。但我发现，在形形色色的地方都有朋友是件好事，如果他们恰好是身居高位的朋友，那就更好了。"

    old "What about me is so special?"
    new "What about me is so special?\n我有什么特别之处？"

    old "Quite frankly, many of the friends I've made were not special at all. For example, there's one fruit vendor I happen to do business with quite regularly. He's not a fruit vendor in the same sense that I am a weapons vendor, you understand. He's a street vendor. He sells pieces of fruit to passing pedestrians. But he's someone that I keep quite close. Do you know why?"
    new "Quite frankly, many of the friends I've made were not special at all. For example, there's one fruit vendor I happen to do business with quite regularly. He's not a fruit vendor in the same sense that I am a weapons vendor, you understand. He's a street vendor. He sells pieces of fruit to passing pedestrians. But he's someone that I keep quite close. Do you know why?\n坦白说，我结交的许多朋友一点都不特别。比如，有个水果贩子，我碰巧经常和他做生意。你明白，他不是像我这样的军火商。他是个街头小贩，把一块块水果卖给路过的行人。但我却和他走得相当近。你知道为什么吗？"

    old "I presume because you provide him with fruit. Or maybe he provides you with fruit."
    new "I presume because you provide him with fruit. Or maybe he provides you with fruit.\n我猜是因为你给他提供水果。或者是他给你提供水果。"

    old "The only time he has provided me with fruit are on the occasions when I stop to visit him, and he provides me with a single apple or plum to enjoy as we speak."
    new "The only time he has provided me with fruit are on the occasions when I stop to visit him, and he provides me with a single apple or plum to enjoy as we speak.\n他给我提供水果，仅有的几次，是我顺路去拜访他时，他会给我一个苹果或李子，让我们边聊边吃。"

    old "No, the main reason I am friends with him is that his small fruit cart sits directly across from the estate of one of my biggest business rivals. This small fruit vendor watches the front of his gate every day, and he happens to notice whoever comes and goes from the estate. I pay him for that information."
    new "No, the main reason I am friends with him is that his small fruit cart sits directly across from the estate of one of my biggest business rivals. This small fruit vendor watches the front of his gate every day, and he happens to notice whoever comes and goes from the estate. I pay him for that information.\n不，我和他交好的主要原因，是他的小水果摊正好摆在我最大的商业对手之一的宅邸对面。这个小小的水果贩子每天盯着他家大门，碰巧就会注意到进出宅邸的都是些什么人。我为这些情报付他钱。"

    old "Doesn't sound like much of a friendship."
    new "Doesn't sound like much of a friendship.\n这听上去可不像什么友谊。"

    old "Well, it's hard to buy information from someone in the absence of trust, and when trust becomes mutual it starts to resemble a friendship. And sometimes when a relationship closely resembles a friendship, you call that a friendship."
    new "Well, it's hard to buy information from someone in the absence of trust, and when trust becomes mutual it starts to resemble a friendship. And sometimes when a relationship closely resembles a friendship, you call that a friendship.\n嗯，在缺乏信任的情况下，很难从某人那里买到情报，而当信任变成相互的，它就开始像友谊了。而有时，当一段关系酷似友谊时，你就把它称作友谊。"

    old "So, you want something from me."
    new "So, you want something from me.\n所以，你想从我这里得到点什么。"

